c695cfcb-4873-49e0-ba8f-38f9bef70623	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	2	● Governance Risk (30%): Indicates long-term reliability and compliance capability\n● Operational Risk (30%): Reflects day-to-day service delivery stability\n1.2 Product Risk Calculation\n1.2.1 Master Formula\nProduct_Risk = Inherent_Risk × (1 - Mitigation_Effectiveness) ×\nConfidence_Factor\nWhere:\nInherent_Risk = MIN(100, ((L × I × CM × DW) + SM) × 4)\nVariable Definitions:\n● L = Likelihood (1-5 scale)\n● I = Impact (1-5 scale)\n● CM = Combined Contextual Multiplier\n● DW = Domain Weight\n● SM = Sector Modifier\n● MIN(100, x) = Cap maximum value at 100\n1.2.2 Likelihood Determination\nFormula:\nL = AVERAGE(Likelihood_scores from applicable_risks)\nWhere applicable_risks are filtered by:\n- Domain match (e.g., piiHandling="extensive" → Privacy & Security risks)\n- Intent match (aiCapabilities="generative_ai" → Intentional risks)\n- Timing match (devStage="production" → Post-deployment risks)\nLikelihood Scale:\nValue Classification Frequency Probability Range\n1 Rare Less than once per 10 < 10%\nyears\n2 Unlikely Once per 5-10 years 10-33%\n3 Possible Once per 1-5 years 34-66%\n4 Likely Once per year 67-90%\n5 Almost Certain Multiple times per year > 90%\nCalculation Example:\nApplicable risks for GenAI healthcare chatbot:\n- Risk_ID_0042: Likelihood = 4 (hallucination in medical advice)\n- Risk_ID_0157: Likelihood = 3 (privacy breach via prompt injection)\n- Risk_ID_0298: Likelihood = 5 (bias in treatment recommendations)\n- Risk_ID_0401: Likelihood = 4 (unauthorized PHI disclosure)\nL = (4 + 3 + 5 + 4) / 4 = 4.0\n1.2.3 Impact Determination\nFormula:\nI = AVERAGE(Impact_scores from applicable_risks)\nImpact Scale:\nValue Classification Financial Operational Reputational\n1 Negligible < $10K No disruption No media\nattention\n2 Minor $10K-$100K < 4 hours Local media\ndowntime\n3 Moderate $100K-$1M 4-24 hours Regional media\ndowntime\n4 Major $1M-$10M 1-7 days National media\ndowntime\n5 Catastrophic > $10M > 7 days International crisis\ndowntime\nSector-Specific Impact Modifiers:\nHealthcare impacts automatically elevated for patient safety risks:\nIF risk_category = "patient_safety" AND sector = "healthcare":\nI_adjusted = MIN(5, I + 1)\nCalculation Example:\nSame applicable risks:\n- Risk_ID_0042: Impact = 5 (wrong medical advice → patient harm)\n- Risk_ID_0157: Impact = 4 (HIPAA violation → $1M+ fines)\n- Risk_ID_0298: Impact = 4 (discriminatory care → lawsuits)\n- Risk_ID_0401: Impact = 3 (privacy breach → regulatory action)\nI = (5 + 4 + 4 + 3) / 4 = 4.0\n1.2.4 Combined Contextual Multiplier (CM)\nMaster Formula:\nCM = ET × TM × AM × SM × RTM × IM\nWhere:\nET = Entity Type Multiplier\nTM = Timing Multiplier\nAM = Architecture Multiplier\nSM = Scale Multiplier\nRTM = Risk Tolerance Multiplier\nIM = Intent Multiplier\nTypical Range: 0.24× to 3.1× (compound effect of six factors)\nEntity Type Multiplier (ET)\nFormula:\nET = ET_base + Stake_adjustment\nET_base = LOOKUP(decisionAutonomyLevel, {\n"advisory": 0.8,\n"assisted": 0.9,\n"supervised": 1.0,\n"autonomous": 1.2,\n"fully_autonomous": 1.3\n})\nStake_adjustment = LOOKUP(decisionStakeLevel, {\n"Low": -0.1,\n"Moderate": 0.0,\n"High": 0.1,\n"Critical": 0.15,\n"Life-Critical": 0.2\n})\nRationale:\n● Advisory systems (like spell-check) have human final decision = lower risk\n● Fully autonomous systems (like autonomous vehicles) make critical decisions independently = higher\nrisk\n● Life-critical stakes (medical diagnosis, flight control) elevate risk regardless of autonomy\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot configuration:	[-0.022608226,0.03569854,0.044053353,0.031400185,-0.001246894,0.023382945,0.11064301,-0.055037472,-0.04596847,0.011602833,0.018869719,0.005823596,0.008169256,-0.022397328,-0.029047411,0.006814437,0.010474563,0.02770864,-0.002325635,-0.05823083,-0.045