99e0772b-8d3b-493c-8517-ab115df4988b	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	3	risk\n● Life-critical stakes (medical diagnosis, flight control) elevate risk regardless of autonomy\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot configuration:\n- decisionAutonomyLevel = "assisted" → ET_base = 0.9\n- decisionStakeLevel = "High" (medical advice impacts health) → Stake = 0.1\nET = 0.9 + 0.1 = 1.0\nTiming Multiplier (TM)\nFormula:\nTM = TM_base + Phase_adjustment\nTM_base = LOOKUP(devStage, {\n"design": 0.75,\n"development": 0.80,\n"testing": 0.85,\n"staging": 0.95,\n"production": 1.30\n})\nPhase_adjustment = LOOKUP(assessmentPhase, {\n"pre_procurement": -0.05,\n"vendor_evaluation": -0.03,\n"pilot": 0.0,\n"scaling": 0.05,\n"mature_deployment": 0.10\n})\nRationale (Risk Backwards Methodology):\n● Earlier assessment stages receive favorable multipliers (incentivize early risk evaluation)\n● Production systems carry maximum risk (errors affect real users)\n● Mature deployments add incremental risk (technical debt, dependency lock-in)\nCalculation Example:\nProduction chatbot during vendor self-attestation:\n- devStage = "production" → TM_base = 1.30\n- assessmentPhase = "vendor_evaluation" → Phase = -0.03\nTM = 1.30 + (-0.03) = 1.27\nArchitecture Multiplier (AM)\nFormula:\nAM = AM_base + Integration_adj + Hosting_adj\nAM_base = LOOKUP(customizationLevel, {\n"off_the_shelf": 0.70,\n"lightly_customized": 0.85,\n"moderately_customized": 1.00,\n"heavily_customized": 1.20,\n"fully_custom": 1.40\n})\nIntegration_adj = LOOKUP(integrationComplexity, {\n"standalone": 0.00,\n"simple_api": 0.05,\n"moderate_integration": 0.10,\n"complex_integration": 0.15,\n"legacy_systems": 0.20\n})\nHosting_adj = LOOKUP(hostingType, {\n"cloud_hosted": 0.00,\n"on_premise": 0.05,\n"hybrid": 0.08,\n"edge_devices": 0.10\n})\nRationale:\n● Off-the-shelf products = well-tested, mature code = lower risk\n● Fully custom = unproven code, potential bugs = higher risk\n● Legacy integration = compatibility issues, data format challenges = increased risk\n● Edge/on-premise = limited monitoring, harder updates = elevated risk\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot architecture:\n- customizationLevel = "lightly_customized" → AM_base = 0.85\n- integrationComplexity = "moderate_integration" (EHR + billing) → Integration\n= 0.10\n- hostingType = "cloud_hosted" → Hosting = 0.00\nAM = 0.85 + 0.10 + 0.00 = 0.95\nScale Multiplier (SM)\nFormula:\nSM = (Employee_base × Geographic_factor) + Data_volume_adj\nEmployee_base = LOOKUP(employeeCount, {\n"1-10": 0.70,\n"11-50": 0.75,\n"51-200": 0.80,\n"201-1000": 0.90,\n"1001-5000": 1.00,\n"5001-10000": 1.10,\n"10000+": 1.20\n})\nGeographic_factor = LOOKUP(geographicRegions, {\n"single_location": 1.00,\n"regional": 1.05,\n"national": 1.10,\n"multi_national": 1.15,\n"global": 1.20\n})\nData_volume_adj = LOOKUP(dataVolumeScale, {\n"minimal": 0.00,\n"moderate": 0.03,\n"large": 0.06,\n"very_large": 0.09,\n"petabyte_scale": 0.12\n})\nRationale:\n● Larger deployments = more users affected by failures = higher risk\n● Geographic distribution = regulatory complexity, latency issues = increased risk\n● Massive data volumes = privacy exposure, processing errors = elevated risk\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare vendor scale:\n- employeeCount = "51-200" → Employee_base = 0.80\n- geographicRegions = "national" → Geographic = 1.10\n- dataVolumeScale = "large" (millions of patient records) → Data_volume = 0.06\nSM = (0.80 × 1.10) + 0.06 = 0.88 + 0.06 = 0.94\nRisk Tolerance Multiplier (RTM)\nFormula:\nRTM = LOOKUP(aiRiskAppetite, {\n"aggressive": 0.85,\n"moderate": 1.00,\n"conservative": 1.15,\n"risk_averse": 1.25\n})\nRationale:	[-0.0030798912,0.035343233,0.06621932,0.026997063,0.06819221,0.026376748,0.07561517,-0.02656506,-0.021418104,0.059105992,-0.061054897,0.020298097,0.0062756105,-0.007400991,-0.040885735,-0.0128705455,-0.028491717,-