27cdd4df-e178-40ff-944c-c40a8440a146	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	4	SM = (0.80 × 1.10) + 0.06 = 0.88 + 0.06 = 0.94\nRisk Tolerance Multiplier (RTM)\nFormula:\nRTM = LOOKUP(aiRiskAppetite, {\n"aggressive": 0.85,\n"moderate": 1.00,\n"conservative": 1.15,\n"risk_averse": 1.25\n})\nRationale:\n● Organizations with conservative risk appetite require lower absolute risk scores\n● Multiplier adjusts inherent risk upward for conservative contexts\n● Ensures same AI system evaluated differently based on organizational risk tolerance\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare organization risk appetite:\n- aiRiskAppetite = "conservative" (patient safety paramount)\nRTM = 1.15\nIntent Multiplier (IM)\nFormula:\nIM = MAJORITY_VOTE(Risk_intent from applicable_risks)\nWhere MAJORITY_VOTE returns:\n- 1.2 if > 60% of applicable risks classified as "Intentional"\n- 0.7 if > 60% of applicable risks classified as "Unintentional"\n- 1.0 otherwise (mixed intent profile)\nIntent Classification Logic:\nIntentional risks include:\n- Adversarial attacks (prompt injection, jailbreaking)\n- Malicious use (weaponization, fraud)\n- Deliberate misuse by authorized users\nUnintentional risks include:\n- System errors (hallucinations, drift)\n- Design flaws (bias, privacy leaks)\n- Operational failures (downtime, data loss)\nRationale:\n● Intentional risks (adversarial) harder to mitigate = higher multiplier\n● Unintentional risks (system errors) more predictable and controllable = lower multiplier\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot applicable risks:\n- 132 risks classified as "Unintentional" (63% - hallucinations, bias, errors)\n- 78 risks classified as "Intentional" (37% - prompt injection, data\nexfiltration)\nMajority = Unintentional (63% > 60% threshold)\nIM = 0.7\nCombined Contextual Multiplier Result\nFormula:\nCM = ET × TM × AM × SM × RTM × IM\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot combined multiplier:\nCM = 1.0 × 1.27 × 0.95 × 0.94 × 1.15 × 0.7\nCM = 0.9167\nInterpretation: Contextual factors reduce base risk by ~8% due to:\n- Assisted autonomy (not fully autonomous)\n- Unintentional risk profile (system errors more controllable)\n- Lightly customized architecture (proven code base)\n1.2.5 Domain Weight (DW)\nFormula:\nDW = WEIGHTED_AVERAGE(Domain_weights for applicable_domains)\nDomain_weights = {\n"Privacy & Security": 1.20,\n"AI System Safety": 1.20,\n"Fairness & Non-discrimination": 1.15,\n"Transparency & Explainability": 1.10,\n"Human Oversight": 1.10,\n"Accountability & Governance": 1.00,\n"Socioeconomic Impact": 0.90\n}\nDomain Selection Logic:\nApplicable domains determined by assessment fields:\nIF piiHandling IN ["moderate", "extensive", "critical"]:\nINCLUDE "Privacy & Security"\nIF biasTestingMethodology != "none":\nINCLUDE "Fairness & Non-discrimination"\nIF adversarialTestingCompleted = "yes":\nINCLUDE "AI System Safety"\nIF explainabilityRequirement IN ["required", "critical"]:\nINCLUDE "Transparency & Explainability"\nIF humanOversightCapabilities != "none":\nINCLUDE "Human Oversight"\nIF aiGovernanceBoard = "yes" OR aiEthicsPolicy != "none":\nINCLUDE "Accountability & Governance"\nIF employeeCount > 1000 OR customerImpact = "high":\nINCLUDE "Socioeconomic Impact"\nWeight Calculation:\nIF multiple domains apply:\nDW = SUM(Domain_weights × Risk_count_per_domain) /\nSUM(Risk_count_per_domain)\nELSE:\nDW = Single_applicable_domain_weight\nRationale:\n● Privacy & Security (1.20): Direct regulatory liability, customer trust impact\n● AI System Safety (1.20): Physical or health consequences possible\n● Fairness (1.15): Legal discrimination risk, reputational damage	[0.019253235,-0.003658471,0.040416274,0.072032474,0.053127665,0.039910126,0.07757912,-0.00622553,0.027773688,0.030751964,-0.02911546,0.033538092,0.0092927115,-0.018197887,-0.0553017,0.018138058,-0.04119907,-0.0011074761,0.0023826754,-0.021767067