ba27f288-4e5c-431f-8d40-2599b932e472	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	5	Rationale:\n● Privacy & Security (1.20): Direct regulatory liability, customer trust impact\n● AI System Safety (1.20): Physical or health consequences possible\n● Fairness (1.15): Legal discrimination risk, reputational damage\n● Transparency (1.10): Regulatory requirement (EU AI Act), customer demand\n● Human Oversight (1.10): Reduces autonomous system risk\n● Governance (1.00): Baseline—good governance expected universally\n● Socioeconomic (0.90): Important but typically lower immediate business impact\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot domain analysis:\n- Privacy & Security: 85 applicable risks\n- AI System Safety: 38 applicable risks\n- Fairness: 42 applicable risks\n- Transparency: 27 applicable risks\n- Human Oversight: 18 applicable risks\nDW = [(1.20 × 85) + (1.20 × 38) + (1.15 × 42) + (1.10 × 27) + (1.10 × 18)] /\n210\nDW = [102 + 45.6 + 48.3 + 29.7 + 19.8] / 210\nDW = 245.4 / 210 = 1.17\n1.2.6 Sector Modifier (SM)\nFormula:\nSM = SM_base + Use_case_adjustment\nSM_base = LOOKUP(sector, {\n"Healthcare": RANGE(3, 8),\n"Financial Services": RANGE(2, 7),\n"Autonomous Vehicles": RANGE(4, 8),\n"Government": RANGE(3, 7),\n"E-Commerce": RANGE(1, 5),\n"Technology": RANGE(0, 3),\n"Other": RANGE(0, 2)\n})\nHealthcare Sector Detailed Breakdown:\nSM_base (Healthcare):\nIF aiCapabilityType = "diagnostic" OR aiCapabilityType =\n"treatment_recommendation":\nBase = 8 (life-critical decisions)\nELSE IF aiCapabilityType = "patient_communication":\nBase = 6 (health advice without diagnosis)\nELSE IF aiCapabilityType = "administrative":\nBase = 4 (billing, scheduling—PHI handling only)\nELSE IF aiCapabilityType = "research":\nBase = 3 (lower stakes, controlled environment)\nELSE:\nBase = 5 (default healthcare baseline)\nUse_case_adjustment:\nIF piiHandling = "critical" (PHI):\n+2 points\nIF regulatoryComplexity INCLUDES "FDA_clearance":\n+1 point\nIF deploymentScale = "multi_hospital_system":\n+1 point\nIF patientDemographic = "pediatric" OR "elderly":\n+1 point (vulnerable populations)\nRationale:\n● Healthcare = Patient safety + HIPAA + FDA oversight = highest baseline modifier\n● Financial = Fair lending + market manipulation + consumer protection = high modifier\n● Autonomous vehicles = Physical safety + ISO 26262 ASIL levels = very high modifier\n● Government = Constitutional rights + equal protection + public trust = high modifier\n● E-Commerce = Consumer protection + GDPR/CCPA = moderate modifier\n● Technology = Innovation-focused, lighter regulation = minimal modifier\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot sector modifier:\n- sector = "Healthcare" → Base range 3-8\n- aiCapabilityType = "patient_communication" → Base = 6\n- piiHandling = "critical" (PHI) → +2\n- regulatoryComplexity includes "HIPAA_BAA" (not FDA) → +0\n- deploymentScale = "single_hospital" → +0\n- patientDemographic = "general_adult" → +0\nSM = 6 + 2 = 8\n1.2.7 Inherent Risk Assembly\nMaster Formula:\nInherent_Risk = MIN(100, ((L × I × CM × DW) + SM) × 4)\nStep-by-Step Calculation:\n1. Base Risk = L × I\n2. Contextual Risk = Base Risk × CM\n3. Domain-Weighted Risk = Contextual Risk × DW\n4. Sector-Adjusted Risk = Domain-Weighted Risk + SM\n5. Normalized Risk = Sector-Adjusted Risk × 4\n6. Capped Risk = MIN(100, Normalized Risk)\nNormalization Factor (× 4) Rationale:\n● Maximum theoretical pre-normalization: (5 × 5 × 3.1 × 1.2) + 8 = 101\n● Multiply by 4 spreads scores across 0-100 range\n● Without normalization, most scores cluster in 10-30 range (poor discrimination)\n● With normalization, achieves healthy distribution across full scale	[-0.023436444,0.05646694,0.041452438,0.033490654,0.006281538,0.027088117,0.12040285,-0.022187043,-0.0080261575,0.059073023,0.032629777,0.013766349,-0.028061235,-0.04242855,-0.012049967,-0.0032019182,-0.02543589,-0.0141288