47631939-6a21-4c8f-ab05-c3de5a100a01	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	8	● Self-reported unverified (1.10): No verification increases uncertainty, elevates final risk\n● Evidence adjustments: Objective artifacts (pen test reports, SOC2) reduce uncertainty\nConfidence Factor vs Confidence in Score:\n● Lower factor (< 1.0) = Higher confidence = Lower final risk score\n● Higher factor (> 1.0) = Lower confidence = Higher final risk score\n● Factor adjusts for assessment quality, not risk level\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot vendor attestation:\nBase assessment method:\n- assessmentMethod = "third_party_review" → 0.93\nEvidence availability:\n- compliance_documentation_complete = "yes" → ×0.98\n- penetration_test_report_available = "yes" → ×0.97\n- soc2_type2_current = "yes" → ×0.95\nConfidence_Factor = 0.93 × 0.98 × 0.97 × 0.95\n= 0.843\nInterpretation: High confidence due to third-party review + strong evidence\nLower confidence factor (0.843) will reduce final Product Risk\n1.2.10 Final Product Risk\nMaster Formula:\nProduct_Risk = Inherent_Risk × (1 - Mitigation_Effectiveness) ×\nConfidence_Factor\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot product risk:\nProduct_Risk = 100.0 × (1 - 0.74) × 0.843\n= 100.0 × 0.26 × 0.843\n= 21.92\nRounded: 22.0 (out of 100)\nInterpretation:\n● Started with maximum inherent risk (100)\n● Vendor's controls reduced risk by 74% (to 26)\n● High confidence in assessment reduced risk further by 15.7% (to 22)\n● Final Product Risk: 22/100 (Low-Medium)\nRisk Reduction Analysis:\nRisk reduction path:\n100 (inherent) → 26 (post-mitigation) → 22 (confidence-adjusted)\nTotal reduction: 78 points (78% risk reduction)\n- Mitigation contribution: 74 points (74% of original risk)\n- Confidence contribution: 4 points (15.7% of residual risk)\n1.3 Governance Risk Calculation\n1.3.1 Master Formula\nGovernance Risk operates as inverse scoring (higher points = better governance):\nGovernance_Score = Certifications_Score + Assessment_Quality_Score +\nPolicy_Score + Operational_Controls_Score +\nMaturity_Adjustment\nGovernance_Risk = 100 - Governance_Score\nMaximum Possible Score: 100 points Rationale: Mature governance reduces risk, so we invert the score\n1.3.2 Certifications Score\nFormula:\nCertifications_Score = SOC2_points + ISO_points + HIPAA_points +\nIndustry_specific_points\nWhere:\nSOC2_points = LOOKUP(soc2Certification, {\n"Type 2 (current)": 20,\n"Type 1 (current)": 12,\n"Type 2 (expired < 1 year)": 8,\n"None": 0\n})\nISO_points = LOOKUP(isoCertifications, {\n"ISO 27001 + ISO 42001": 25,\n"ISO 27001 only": 15,\n"ISO 42001 only": 12,\n"ISO 9001": 5,\n"None": 0\n})\nHIPAA_points = IF sector = "Healthcare":\nLOOKUP(hipaaCertification, {\n"HIPAA BAA + HITRUST": 20,\n"HIPAA BAA only": 15,\n"HIPAA self-attestation": 8,\n"None": 0\n})\nELSE: 0\nIndustry_specific_points = SECTOR_SPECIFIC_LOOKUP\nMaximum Certifications Score: 50 points\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot vendor certifications:\nSOC2_points:\n- soc2Certification = "Type 2 (current)" → 20 points\nISO_points:\n- isoCertifications = "ISO 27001 only" → 15 points\nHIPAA_points (healthcare sector):\n- hipaaCertification = "HIPAA BAA + HITRUST" → 20 points\n- Exceeds max, capped at 15 for HIPAA category\nCertifications_Score = 20 + 15 + 15 = 50 points\n1.3.3 Assessment Quality Score\nFormula:\nAssessment_Quality_Score = LOOKUP(assessmentMethod, {\n"third_party_audit": 20,\n"third_party_review": 15,\n"internal_audit": 10,\n"internal_review": 8,\n"self_assessment": 3,\n"none": 0\n}) + Audit_frequency_bonus\nAudit_frequency_bonus = IF assessmentMethod INCLUDES "audit":\nLOOKUP(auditFrequency, {\n"annual": 5,	[0.020027395,-0.018169327,0.055866033,0.042441748,0.010096263,-0.0025735416,0.06129886,-0.06728283,-0.017056853,0.026361357,0.04565988,-0.016896887,-0.008602938,-0.026500965,0.031731322,-0.011320514,-0.018350566,