4884fd64-a648-41e5-92be-2686512eca74	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	12	Expertise:\n- technicalAccountManager = "dedicated_tam" → 5 points\nSupport_Score = 10 + 5 + 5 = 20 points\n1.4.7 Final Operational Risk\nFormula:\nOperational_Score = SLA + Incident_Management + Deployment_Maturity +\nStability + Support\nOperational_Score = MIN(100, calculated_score)\nOperational_Risk = 100 - Operational_Score\nCalculation Example:\nHealthcare chatbot operational calculation:\nOperational_Score = 33 + 30 + 30 + 22 + 20\n= 135 points\nCapped: MIN(100, 135) = 100\nOperational_Risk = 100 - 100 = 0\nInterpretation: Maximum operational maturity\nZero operational risk indicates:\n- Excellent SLA (99.95% uptime)\n- Mature incident management\n- Production-ready at enterprise scale\n- Established company with strong retention\n- Comprehensive 24/7 support\n1.5 Final Vendor Trust Score\n1.5.1 Master Formula\nVendor_Trust_Score = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) +\n(Governance_Risk × 0.30) +\n(Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\nWeight Rationale:\n● Product Risk (40%): Core offering—the AI system customers are actually buying\n● Governance Risk (30%): Indicates long-term partnership viability and compliance capability\n● Operational Risk (30%): Day-to-day reliability and support quality\n1.5.2 Comprehensive Calculation Example\nFormula:\nVTS = 100 - [(22 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\n= 100 - [8.8 + 0 + 0]\n= 100 - 8.8\n= 91.2\nRounded: VTS = 91\n1.5.3 Trust Score Interpretation Framework\nGrade Score Range Classification Vendor Profile Recommended\nAction\nA 90-100 Exceptional Market leader; Fast-track\nVendor comprehensive procurement;\ncontrols; proven minimal additional\ntrack record due diligence\nB 80-89 Trusted Vendor Strong Standard\ncapabilities; procurement\nmature process; focus on\ngovernance; use-case fit\nreliable operations\nC 70-79 Acceptable Moderate Enhanced due\nVendor capabilities; some diligence; require\ngaps; growing mitigation\noperations roadmap\nD 60-69 Review Significant gaps; Extensive\nRecommended immature validation;\nprocesses; limited consider\ntrack record alternatives; pilot\nonly\nF 0-59 Review Required Critical Reject; only\ndeficiencies; consider for\nunproven low-stakes\ncapabilities; high non-production\nrisk use\nThe A-through-F grading scale uses uniform 10-point bands for grades A through D, with F absorbing the\nfull 0-59 range. The 70-point threshold for a passing grade (C) reflects enterprise buyer expectations in\nregulated industries. Grades D and F use action-oriented language (Review Recommended, Review\nRequired) rather than negative vendor classifications.\n1.5.4 Healthcare Chatbot Vendor Final Assessment\nComplete Score Breakdown:\nProduct Risk Calculation:\n├─ Inherent Risk: 100.0 (maximum due to PHI + production + healthcare)\n├─ Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.74 (strong controls, minor gaps)\n├─ Confidence Factor: 0.843 (third-party audit + evidence)\n└─ Product Risk: 22.0\nGovernance Risk Calculation:\n├─ Certifications: 50 points (SOC2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 + HIPAA)\n├─ Assessment Quality: 25 points (third-party annual audit)\n├─ Policies: 45 points (complete framework)\n├─ Operational Controls: 40 points (mature automation)\n├─ Maturity Adjustment: 15 points (established company)\n├─ Governance Score: 100 (capped)\n└─ Governance Risk: 0\nOperational Risk Calculation:\n├─ SLA: 33 points (99.95% uptime)\n├─ Incident Management: 30 points (automated + tested)\n├─ Deployment Maturity: 30 points (enterprise multi-tenant)\n├─ Stability: 22 points (8-year company, profitable)\n├─ Support: 20 points (24/7 dedicated support)\n├─ Operational Score: 100 (capped)	[-0.03014712,0.037445977,0.028877715,0.04423008,0.0060936715,0.026737407,0.091135144,-0.04527697,0.0010020362,-0.023817517,0.026250895,0.014029251,-0.006101518,-0.031321883,-0.012595066,-0.043066267,-0.0069656875,-0.009715281,-