7fd58480-1f48-4922-a0db-9764d8cd0335	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	13	├─ Incident Management: 30 points (automated + tested)\n├─ Deployment Maturity: 30 points (enterprise multi-tenant)\n├─ Stability: 22 points (8-year company, profitable)\n├─ Support: 20 points (24/7 dedicated support)\n├─ Operational Score: 100 (capped)\n└─ Operational Risk: 0\nFinal Vendor Trust Score:\nVTS = 100 - [(22 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\n= 100 - 8.8\n= 91.2 ≈ 91\nClassification: Exceptional Vendor (90-100 range)\nVendor Strengths:\n14. Exceptional Governance (0 risk): Best-in-class certifications, policies, and controls\n15. Exceptional Operations (0 risk): Proven reliability, mature deployment, strong support\n16. Managed Product Risk (22/100): High inherent risk mitigated by comprehensive controls\nResidual Concerns:\n17. Mitigation Coverage Gaps: Missing Post-Deployment Monitoring and Human Oversight categories\n18. Recommendation: Require vendor to implement continuous model drift monitoring and clinical\nreview workflow before deployment\nProcurement Recommendation: APPROVED FOR FAST-TRACK PROCUREMENT\n● Vendor demonstrates market-leading capabilities\n● Risk profile acceptable for healthcare PHI handling\n● Require mitigation gap closure as contract condition\nAssessment Type 2: COTS Vendor Side (Sales Enablement)\n2.1 Assessment Overview\nObjective: Quantify vendor confidence in closing a specific sales opportunity.\nPrimary Users: AI vendors evaluating prospective customer deals\nOutput Metric: Sales Confidence Score (SCS) = 0-100 (higher = stronger deal)\nFormula Structure:\nSCS = 100 - [(Customer_Friction_Risk × 0.35) +\n(Implementation_Risk × 0.35) +\n(Competitive_Risk × 0.30)]\nRationale for Weights:\n● Customer Friction (35%): Complex requirements are hardest to overcome\n● Implementation (35%): Deployment failure kills deals post-sale\n● Competitive (30%): Even with competition, superior solution can win\nScale Alignment Note: The Sales Confidence Score is structurally aligned with the Vendor Trust Score\n(Assessment Type 1). Both use the pattern: Score = 100 - [weighted risk components]. Higher scores\nindicate stronger outcomes across all assessment types.\n2.2 Customer Friction Risk Calculation\n2.2.1 Master Formula\nCustomer_Friction_Risk = Regulatory_Complexity +\nData_Sensitivity_Friction +\nRisk_Tolerance_Friction +\nCustomer_Specific_Risk_Friction\nCFR = MIN(100, sum_of_components)\n2.2.2 Regulatory Complexity\nFormula:\nRegulatory_Complexity = COUNT(customerRegulatoryRequirements) ×\nComplexity_multiplier\nComplexity_multiplier = LOOKUP(sector, {\n"Healthcare": 6,\n"Financial_Services": 5,\n"Government": 5,\n"Autonomous_Systems": 7,\n"E_Commerce": 3,\n"Technology": 2\n})\nRationale:\n● Each additional regulatory framework adds procurement steps, documentation requirements, and\napproval cycles\n● Sector multiplier reflects regulatory burden density\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance regulatory landscape:\ncustomerRegulatoryRequirements = ["HIPAA", "SOC2", "State Insurance\nRegulations"]\nCOUNT = 3\nsector = "Healthcare" → Complexity_multiplier = 6\nRegulatory_Complexity = 3 × 6 = 18 points\n2.2.3 Data Sensitivity Friction\nFormula:\nData_Sensitivity_Friction = LOOKUP(customerDataSensitivity, {\n"Critical (Life-safety, National security)": 30,\n"High (PHI, Financial data, PII)": 20,\n"Medium (Business confidential)": 10,\n"Low (Public or anonymized)": 5\n}) + Compliance_documentation_burden\nCompliance_documentation_burden = IF sector IN ["Healthcare",\n"Financial_Services"]:\nCOUNT(customerRegulatoryRequirements) × 3\nELSE:	[-0.033851888,0.006417811,0.013835026,0.0042804065,-0.028950674,0.022629926,0.031567488,-0.012900965,0.0036985604,0.0055135353,-0.002935971,-0.0057578795,-0.041308988,-0.022711154,-0.0151611585,-0.021255199,-0.007945969,-0.0024249568,-0.036828335,0.0280358