066741b9-264a-401d-ad5d-917a3aff9e33	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	16	= (9 / 12) × 40\n= 0.75 × 40\n= 30 points\n2.3.7 Total Implementation Risk\nFormula:\nImplementation_Risk = MIN(100, Integration + Customization +\nTimeline + Feature_Gap + Mitigation_Gap)\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance implementation risk:\nIR = MIN(100, 22 + 39 + 12 + 24 + 30)\n= MIN(100, 127)\n= 100 (capped at maximum)\nInterpretation: Maximum implementation complexity\nCritical challenges:\n- Legacy mainframe integration (35-point complexity)\n- Extensive customization required (39 points)\n- Large mitigation gap (9 of 12 required mitigations missing)\n- Critical feature gaps (prior auth, state appeals)\n2.4 Competitive Risk Calculation\n2.4.1 Master Formula\nCompetitive_Risk = Competitive_Alternatives +\nBudget_Constraint +\nCompetitive_Advantage +\nVendor_Maturity_Gap\nCR = MAX(0, sum_of_components) // Can go negative if strong advantages\n2.4.2 Competitive Alternatives\nFormula:\nCompetitive_Alternatives = Base_competition + Build_option_penalty\nBase_competition = LOOKUP(competitorCount, {\n"0 (sole source)": 0,\n"1 competitor": 10,\n"2-3 competitors": 20,\n"4+ competitors": 25\n})\nBuild_option_penalty = IF customer_considering_build_vs_buy = "yes":\nLOOKUP(customer_technical_capability, {\n"Strong (can build)": 20,\n"Moderate (difficult build)": 10,\n"Weak (unlikely to build)": 5\n})\nELSE: 0\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance competitive landscape:\ncompetitorCount = "2-3 competitors" → 20 points\nBuild option:\n- customer_considering_build_vs_buy = "yes"\n- customer_technical_capability = "Moderate" (have data scientists but limited\nAI experience) → 10 points\nCompetitive_Alternatives = 20 + 10 = 30 points\n2.4.3 Budget Constraint\nFormula:\nBudget_Constraint = LOOKUP(budgetMidpoint, {\n"< $100K": 35,\n"$100K-$250K": 25,\n"$250K-$500K": 15,\n"$500K-$1M": 10,\n"$1M-$5M": 5,\n"> $5M": 0\n}) + Budget_approval_complexity\nBudget_approval_complexity = LOOKUP(approvalLevels, {\n"VP_and_below": 0,\n"C_suite_single": 3,\n"C_suite_multiple": 8,\n"Board_approval": 15\n})\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance budget:\nbudgetMidpoint = "$500K-$1M" → 10 points\nApproval complexity:\n- approvalLevels = "C_suite_multiple" (CFO + CTO approval) → 8 points\nBudget_Constraint = 10 + 8 = 18 points\n2.4.4 Competitive Advantage (Negative Points = Better)\nFormula:\nCompetitive_Advantage = -(Unique_differentiators × Differentiator_value) -\nIndustry_expertise_bonus\nDifferentiator_value = LOOKUP_PER_ADVANTAGE(advantage_type, {\n"Regulatory_certification": 10,\n"Proven_customer_in_sector": 8,\n"Faster_deployment": 5,\n"Lower_TCO": 7,\n"Superior_feature_set": 6,\n"Domain_expertise": 8,\n"Technology_leadership": 5\n})\nIndustry_expertise_bonus = IF years_in_customer_sector >= 5: -10 ELSE: 0\nCalculation Example:\nVendor's competitive advantages vs. HealthFirst:\nUnique differentiators:\n1. HIPAA certification + HITRUST (competitors don't have both) → -10\n2. 15+ healthcare customers (proven track record) → -8\n3. Claims processing domain expertise → -8\nCompetitive_Advantage = -(10 + 8 + 8) = -26 points\nIndustry expertise:\n- years_in_customer_sector = 8 years in healthcare\n- Bonus = -10 points\nTotal_Advantage = -26 + (-10) = -36 points\n2.4.5 Vendor-Buyer Maturity Gap\nFormula:\nVendor_Maturity_Gap = LOOKUP(vendor_stage, customer_type_pairing, {\n("startup", "Enterprise"): 25,\n("startup", "Mid_market"): 15,\n("startup", "SMB"): 5,\n("growth", "Enterprise"): 15,\n("growth", "Mid_market"): 5,\n("growth", "SMB"): 0,\n("established", "Enterprise"): 5,\n("established", "Mid_market"): 0,\n("established", "SMB"): 0,	[-0.025736721,0.016248561,-0.0017437534,0.00076198974,0.041156992,0.015572387,0.07296809,-0.020786561,0.027647357,0.05565737,-0.005193191,-0.029235968,-0.033221334,0.007922885,0.010986817,-0.0093867