59083458-0804-4323-b6a6-1054e53acef3	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf	17	("startup", "Mid_market"): 15,\n("startup", "SMB"): 5,\n("growth", "Enterprise"): 15,\n("growth", "Mid_market"): 5,\n("growth", "SMB"): 0,\n("established", "Enterprise"): 5,\n("established", "Mid_market"): 0,\n("established", "SMB"): 0,\n("mature", any): 0\n}) + Expectation_mismatch_penalty\nExpectation_mismatch_penalty = IF customer_expects_features_of_larger_vendor =\n"yes":\nMIN(15, (customer_employee_count / vendor_employee_count) × 3)\nELSE: 0\nCalculation Example:\nVendor-HealthFirst maturity analysis:\nVendor stage: "growth" (Series B, 150 employees)\nCustomer type: "Enterprise" (5,000+ employees)\nBase gap = 15 points\nExpectation mismatch:\n- customer_expects_features_of_larger_vendor = "yes" (wants enterprise SLAs,\ndedicated support)\n- customer_employee_count = 5000\n- vendor_employee_count = 150\n- Penalty = MIN(15, (5000/150) × 3) = MIN(15, 100) = 15 points\nVendor_Maturity_Gap = 15 + 15 = 30 points\n2.4.6 Total Competitive Risk\nFormula:\nCompetitive_Risk = MAX(0, Alternatives + Budget + Advantage + Maturity_Gap)\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance competitive risk:\nCR = MAX(0, 30 + 18 + (-36) + 30)\n= MAX(0, 42)\n= 42 points\nInterpretation: Moderate-High competitive pressure\nAnalysis:\n- Strong competitive advantages (-36) offset other friction\n- HIPAA+HITRUST certification is powerful differentiator\n- Maturity gap (growth vendor vs. enterprise customer) adds significant risk\n- Build-vs-buy consideration adds uncertainty\n2.5 Final Sales Confidence Score\n2.5.1 Master Formula\nSales_Confidence_Score = 100-[(Customer_Friction_Risk × 0.35) +\n(Implementation_Risk × 0.35) +\n(Competitive_Risk × 0.30)]\n2.5.2 Comprehensive Calculation\nFormula:\nSCS = 100 - [(100 × 0.35) + (100 × 0.35) + (42 × 0.30)]\n= 100 - [35 + 35 + 12.6]\n= 17.4 ≈ 17\n2.5.3 Sales Confidence Interpretation Framework\nScore Range Classification Deal Profile Recommended Action\n90-100 High Low friction; strong fit; Standard sales process; focus on value\nConfidence weak competition demonstration\nDeal\n80-89 Favorable Deal Minor friction; good fit; Standard sales process; executive\nmanageable competition sponsorship helpful\n70-79 Moderate Some friction; gaps Extended sales cycle; custom proposal with\nDeal present; competitive mitigation roadmap\npressure\n60-69 Review Deal High friction; notable gaps; Executive engagement required; review\nStrategy strong competition resource investment before pursuing\n0-59 Reassess Critical friction; major Reassess deal viability; only pursue if\nOpportunity gaps; intense competition strategically critical\n2.5.4 HealthFirst Insurance Sales Assessment\nComplete Score Breakdown:\nCustomer Friction Risk: 100\n├─ Regulatory Complexity: 18 (HIPAA + SOC2 + State)\n├─ Data Sensitivity: 29 (PHI + compliance burden)\n├─ Risk Tolerance: 24 (Conservative + proof requirements)\n└─ Specific Risks: 51 (Legacy integration + unique state requirements)\nImplementation Risk: 100\n├─ Integration: 22 (Mainframe + Salesforce + Azure avg)\n├─ Customization: 39 (Healthcare workflows + industry requirements)\n├─ Timeline: 12 (4-month target with regulatory deadline)\n├─ Feature Gap: 24 (15% gap + 2 critical missing features)\n└─ Mitigation Gap: 30 (9 of 12 required mitigations missing)\nCompetitive Risk: 42\n├─ Alternatives: 30 (2-3 competitors + build option)\n├─ Budget: 18 ($500K-$1M + C-suite approval)\n├─ Advantage: -36 (HIPAA+HITRUST + healthcare expertise)\n└─ Maturity Gap: 30 (Growth vendor vs. Enterprise customer)\nSales_Confidence_Score = 100 - [(100 × 0.35) + (100 × 0.35) + (42 × 0.30)]	[-0.017596023,-0.0116633745,0.02798025,0.0075790556,0.0046855486,-0.0075552897,0.019388003,-0.041152515,0.03071548,0.037889317,-0.01239973,-0.03558873,0.006645047,0.0042541935,0.046473738,-0.008464831,-0.03771093,-0.0116263