ab634601-dd1e-4fb2-83d7-7c2dce9988c7	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	0	AI EVAL Platform Risk Scoring Methodology\nPart 2\nTable of Contents - Part 2\nTable of Contents - Part 2 1\nAssessment Type 3: COTS Buyer Side (Implementation Risk) 2\n3.1 Assessment Overview 3\n3.2 Vendor Risk Calculation 3\n3.2.1 Master Formula 3\n3.2.2 Base Vendor Risk 4\n3.2.3 Vendor-Buyer Maturity Gap Risk 5\n3.2.4 Certification Gap Risk 6\n3.2.5 Reference Check Risk 7\n3.2.6 Financial Stability Risk 8\n3.2.7 Total Vendor Risk 9\n3.3 Organizational Readiness Gap Calculation 10\n3.3.1 Master Formula 10\n3.3.2 AI Governance Maturity Gap 10\n3.3.3 Data Governance Maturity Gap 11\n3.3.4 Skills Gap Risk 13\n3.3.5 Change Management Risk 14\n3.3.6 Budget Adequacy Risk 16\n3.3.7 Total Organizational Readiness Gap 18\n3.4 Integration Risk Calculation 19\n3.4.1 Master Formula 19\n3.4.2 Technical Integration Complexity 19\n3.4.3 Feature Gap Risk 21\n3.4.4 Data Interoperability Risk 22\n3.4.5 Vendor Lock-in Risk 23\n3.4.6 Rollback Capability Risk 24\n3.4.7 Scaling Risk 25\n3.4.8 Total Integration Risk 26\n3.5 Final Implementation Risk Score 27\n3.5.1 Master Formula 27\n3.5.2 Comprehensive Calculation 27\n3.5.3 Implementation Risk Interpretation Framework 28\n3.5.4 HealthFirst Insurance Implementation Assessment 28\n3.5.5 Decision Recommendation 29\nAssessment Type 4: Custom AI Build 32\n4.1 Assessment Overview 32\n4.2 Technical Risk Calculation 33\n4.2.1 Master Formula 33\n4.2.2 Team Capability Gap 34\n4.2.3 Architecture Complexity Risk 35\n4.2.4 Model Development Risk 36\n4.2.5 Infrastructure Risk 37\n4.2.6 Maintenance Burden Risk 38\n4.2.7 Total Technical Risk 40\n4.3 Governance Risk Calculation 40\n4.3.1 Master Formula 40\n4.3.2 AI Governance Maturity Gap 41\n4.3.3 Ethics Oversight Gap 42\n4.3.4 Risk Management Gap 43\n4.3.5 Compliance Capability Gap 44\n4.3.6 Total Governance Risk 45\n4.4 Data Risk Calculation 45\n4.4.1 Master Formula 45\n4.4.2 Training Data Availability 46\n4.4.3 Data Quality Risk 47\n4.4.4 Data Governance Risk 48\n4.4.5 Labeling Effort Risk 49\n4.4.6 Total Data Risk 50\n4.5 Final Build Risk Score 51\n4.5.1 Master Formula 51\n4.5.2 Comprehensive Calculation 51\n4.5.3 Build Risk Interpretation Framework 51\n4.5.4 HealthFirst Custom Build Assessment 52\n4.5.5 Build vs. Buy Decision Analysis 52\nOverview\nThis document (Part 2) defines two downstream evaluations in the AI EVAL platform: Assessment Type 3\n(COTS Buyer Side), which produces an Implementation Readiness Score (IRS, 0-100, higher = more ready)\nby inverting the weighted combination of Vendor Risk (35%), Organizational Readiness Gap (35%), and\nIntegration Risk (30%) and translating the result into clear readiness guidance, and Assessment Type 4\n(Custom AI Build), which produces a Build Readiness Score (BRS, 0-100, higher = more viable) by\ninverting the weighted combination of Technical Risk (40%), Governance Risk (30%), and Data Risk (30%),\nwith a parallel decision framework from "Build Ready" through "Build Reassessment Required." It also\nshows how assessments integrate across the suite, e.g., Assessment Type 3 can pull the Vendor Trust\nScore from Assessment Type 1 (or fall back to buyer evaluation/default logic) to compute base vendor\nrisk, and Assessment Type 4 reuses implementation context (such as integration/architecture\ncomplexity) to inform build feasibility and supports a build-vs-buy comparison against the IRS outcome.\nAssessment Type 3: COTS Buyer Side (Implementation Risk)\n3.1 Assessment Overview\nObjective: Quantify an organization's readiness to implement a commercial off-the-shelf	[0.0022288428,0.012210237,0.04491829,0.033005673,0.026554842,0.012468278,0.098362915,-0.023418233,0.0047901054,0.060681026,0.048523426,0.046000354,-0.0028694607,-0.009702098,0.0074897967,-0.03036581,-0.06351217,-0.016405376,0.018496463,0.0061422866,0.02