113435,-0.014087045,-0.05295995,-0.088778354,0.016573044,-0.007508107,0.039968193,-0.044671506,0.026298692,0.008089516,0.005770217,-0.030620068,0.039885405,0.010954058,0.05595507,-0.045189917,0.03170857,0.029894263,0.04800184,-0.071696594,0.04897654,-0.042906422,0.051483627,-0.032073997,-0.03698736,0.019304428,-0.0030745873,0.06035204,-0.022205213,0.030187337,0.0611069,-0.016353637,0.019066518,0.013635068,-0.018801237,-0.013772862,-0.060460627,0.008400632,-0.0030416525]	{"chunker": "langchain.RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter", "file_name": "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf", "char_count": 3462, "chunk_index": 0, "orchestrator": "langgraph", "embedding_model": "amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0", "embedding_dimensions": 1024}	2026-07-16 10:18:29.319439+05:30
3aeebc49-eb86-4850-99dd-9459b23811a9	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	1	Assessment Type 3: COTS Buyer Side (Implementation Risk)\n3.1 Assessment Overview\nObjective: Quantify an organization's readiness to implement a commercial off-the-shelf\n(COTS) AI product from a specific vendor.\nPrimary Users: Organizations (buyers) evaluating readiness to deploy AI vendor solutions\nOutput Metric: Implementation Readiness Score (IRS) = 0-100 (higher = more ready to\nproceed)\nFormula Structure:\nIRS = 100 - [(Vendor_Risk x 0.35) +\n(Organizational_Readiness_Gap x 0.35) +\n(Integration_Risk x 0.30)]\nRationale for Weights:\n● Vendor Risk (35%): Vendor quality affects long-term success and partnership viability\n● Organizational Readiness (35%): #1 cause of AI implementation failure is\norganizational unpreparedness\n● Integration Risk (30%): Technical integration complexity affects deployment timeline\nand quality\nDecision Framework:\nIF IRS >= 76: PROCEED (High Readiness)\nELSE IF IRS >= 51: PROCEED WITH CAUTION\n(Moderate Readiness - extend timeline, address gaps)\nELSE: DO NOT PROCEED UNTIL GAPS RESOLVED\n(Low Readiness - major remediation required)\n3.2 Vendor Risk Calculation\n3.2.1 Master Formula\nVendor_Risk = Base_Vendor_Risk + Maturity_Gap_Risk + Certification_Gap_Risk +\nReference_Check_Risk + Financial_Stability_Risk\nVR = MIN(100, sum_of_components)\nRisk Philosophy: Even excellent vendors can be wrong fit for specific buyers. This measures vendor-buyer\nalignment risk.\n3.2.2 Base Vendor Risk\nFormula:\nBase_Vendor_Risk = 100 - Vendor_Trust_Score\nWhere:\nVendor_Trust_Score = {\nFROM vendor self-attestation (Assessment Type 1) IF available\nOR FROM buyer's independent vendor evaluation IF not available\nOR 50 (default moderate risk) IF no assessment exists\n}\nSource Priority Logic:\nIF vendor_completed_self_attestation = "yes":\nBase_Vendor_Risk = 100 - vendor_trust_score_from_attestation\nELSE IF buyer_conducted_vendor_evaluation = "yes":\nBase_Vendor_Risk = 100 - buyer_vendor_evaluation_score\nELSE:\nBase_Vendor_Risk = 50 // Conservative default assumption\nWarning_flag = "No vendor assessment available - using default risk"\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance vendor evaluation:\nVendor (AI chatbot company) completed self-attestation:\n- vendor_completed_self_attestation = "yes"\n- vendor_trust_score_from_attestation = 91 (from Assessment Type 1)\nBase_Vendor_Risk = 100 - 91 = 9\nInterpretation: Low inherent vendor risk (vendor is highly trustworthy)\n3.2.3 Vendor-Buyer Maturity Gap Risk\nFormula:\nMaturity_Gap_Risk = Stage_mismatch_penalty + Scale_mismatch_penalty +\nIndustry_experience_gap\nStage_mismatch_penalty = LOOKUP((vendor_stage, buyer_type), {\n("startup", "Enterprise"): 30,\n("startup", "Mid_market"): 20,\n("startup", "SMB"): 5,\n("growth", "Enterprise"): 15,\n("growth", "Mid_market"): 8,\n("growth", "SMB"): 0,\n("established", "Enterprise"): 5,\n("established", "Mid_market"): 0,\n("established", "SMB"): 0,\n("mature", any): 0\n})\nScale_mismatch_penalty = IF (buyer_employee_count / vendor_employee_count) >\n10:\nMIN(20, (buyer_employee_count / vendor_employee_count) × 2)\nELSE: 0\nIndustry_experience_gap = IF vendor_years_in_buyer_sector < 3:\nLOOKUP(vendor_years_in_buyer_sector, {\n"0-1 years": 15,\n"1-2 years": 10,\n"2-3 years": 5,\n"3+ years": 0\n})\nELSE: 0\nRationale:\n● Stage Mismatch: Startup vendors may lack enterprise support infrastructure, SLAs, or stability\n● Scale Mismatch: Vendor serving customers 10× their size creates capacity/support risks\n● Industry Experience: Sector-specific knowledge (healthcare workflows, financial regulations) reduces	[-0.027570928,0.044049196,0.009546292,0.0017678827,0.047903948,-0.002817875,0.098136835,-0.036452934,-0.0091600055,0.0028337894,0.007346968,0.016994225,-0.051057797,-0.008596509,-0.0538328,-0.01909343,-0.03862565,-0