ce7c37e5-6c03-4695-8b3e-5d11bbee3640	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	2	● Scale Mismatch: Vendor serving customers 10× their size creates capacity/support risks\n● Industry Experience: Sector-specific knowledge (healthcare workflows, financial regulations) reduces\nimplementation friction\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance maturity analysis:\nVendor profile:\n- vendor_stage = "growth" (Series B, 150 employees, 8 years old)\n- vendor_employee_count = 150\n- vendor_years_in_buyer_sector = 8 (healthcare)\nBuyer profile:\n- buyer_type = "Enterprise"\n- buyer_employee_count = 5,000\nStage mismatch:\n- ("growth", "Enterprise") → 15 points\nScale mismatch:\n- buyer_employee_count / vendor_employee_count = 5000 / 150 = 33.3\n- 33.3 > 10 → triggers penalty\n- MIN(20, 33.3 × 2) = MIN(20, 66.6) = 20 points\nIndustry experience:\n- vendor_years_in_buyer_sector = 8 years (> 3 threshold) → 0 points\nMaturity_Gap_Risk = 15 + 20 + 0 = 35 points\n3.2.4 Certification Gap Risk\nFormula:\nCertification_Gap_Risk = COUNT(missing_required_certifications) ×\nCertification_weight\nCertification_weight = LOOKUP(certification_type, {\n"SOC2_Type_2": 20,\n"ISO_27001": 15,\n"ISO_42001": 12,\n"HIPAA_BAA": 20,\n"HITRUST": 18,\n"FedRAMP": 25,\n"PCI_DSS": 18,\n"State_Privacy_Laws": 10\n})\nRequired_certifications = SECTOR_SPECIFIC_REQUIREMENTS(buyer_sector,\nbuyer_regulatory_environment)\nSector-Specific Requirements:\nHealthcare requirements = ["SOC2_Type_2", "HIPAA_BAA"]\nFinancial Services requirements = ["SOC2_Type_2", "ISO_27001"]\nGovernment requirements = ["FedRAMP"] (if federal) OR ["SOC2_Type_2"] (if\nstate/local)\nE-Commerce requirements = ["SOC2_Type_2"] (if > $10M revenue)\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance certification requirements:\nRequired certifications (Healthcare sector):\n1. SOC2_Type_2 (weight: 20)\n2. HIPAA_BAA (weight: 20)\nVendor has:\n- SOC2_Type_2: ✓\n- HIPAA_BAA: ✓\n- ISO_27001: ✓ (bonus, not required)\n- HITRUST: ✓ (bonus, not required)\nMissing required certifications: 0\nCertification_Gap_Risk = 0 × 20 = 0 points\nInterpretation: No certification gap—vendor exceeds requirements\n3.2.5 Reference Check Risk\nFormula:\nReference_Check_Risk = Base_reference_risk - Reference_quality_bonus\nBase_reference_risk = LOOKUP(reference_availability, {\n"No references provided": 25,\n"1-2 references": 15,\n"3-4 references": 8,\n"5+ references": 3\n})\nReference_quality_bonus = SUM(quality_adjustments_per_reference)\nQuality_adjustment_per_reference = {\nIF reference_in_same_sector AS buyer: -5\nIF reference_similar_size AS buyer: -3\nIF reference_similar_use_case AS buyer: -4\nIF reference_deployed_production > 1_year: -2\n}\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance reference check:\nVendor provided 4 references:\nReference 1: BlueCross BlueShield (Healthcare insurer)\n- Same sector: -5\n- Similar size (4,500 employees vs 5,000): -3\n- Similar use case (claims automation): -4\n- Production 18 months: -2\n- Reference 1 bonus: -14\nReference 2: UnitedHealth (Healthcare insurer)\n- Same sector: -5\n- Larger size (350,000 employees): 0\n- Similar use case: -4\n- Production 2 years: -2\n- Reference 2 bonus: -11\nReference 3: Aetna (Healthcare insurer)\n- Same sector: -5\n- Similar size (6,000 employees): -3\n- Different use case (customer service): 0\n- Production 9 months: 0\n- Reference 3 bonus: -8\nReference 4: Kaiser Permanente (Healthcare provider - different subsector)\n- Different sector: 0\n- Much larger: 0\n- Different use case (clinical decision support): 0\n- Production 6 months: 0\n- Reference 4 bonus: 0\nBase_reference_risk = 8 (for 3-4 references)	[-0.027616452,-0.028641213,-0.0012457706,0.034435395,0.009087643,0.018383631,0.049864292,-0.04443356,0.039767407,0.024284624,0.0048416504,-0.017753929,-0.07042436,-0.021206867,0.047242153,-0.019447505,-0.04146011,-0.024623076,-0.03198084,-