46ad90c4-f514-4b26-9bca-c719847e2a67	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	3	- Different sector: 0\n- Much larger: 0\n- Different use case (clinical decision support): 0\n- Production 6 months: 0\n- Reference 4 bonus: 0\nBase_reference_risk = 8 (for 3-4 references)\nReference_quality_bonus = -14 + -11 + -8 + 0 = -33\nReference_Check_Risk = 8 - 33 = -25\nCapped at 0: Reference_Check_Risk = MAX(0, -25) = 0\nInterpretation: Exceptional references—vendor proven in similar deployments\nBonus exceeded base risk, resulting in zero reference risk\n3.2.6 Financial Stability Risk\nFormula:\nFinancial_Stability_Risk = Base_financial_risk - Stability_indicators_bonus\nBase_financial_risk = LOOKUP(vendor_financial_status, {\n"Publicly_traded": 0,\n"Profitable_3plus_years": 3,\n"Profitable_1_to_3_years": 5,\n"Break_even": 8,\n"Funded_24plus_months_runway": 10,\n"Funded_12_to_24_months_runway": 15,\n"Funded_6_to_12_months_runway": 25,\n"Funded_under_6_months_runway": 40,\n"Unknown_financial_status": 20\n})\nStability_indicators_bonus = {\nIF annual_recurring_revenue > $10M: -5\nIF revenue_growth_rate > 50% YoY: -3\nIF customer_retention_rate > 90%: -4\nIF enterprise_customer_count > 20: -3\n}\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance vendor financial analysis:\nVendor financial status:\n- vendor_financial_status = "Profitable_1_to_3_years" → 5 points\nStability indicators:\n- annual_recurring_revenue = $12M → -5\n- revenue_growth_rate = 75% YoY → -3\n- customer_retention_rate = 93% → -4\n- enterprise_customer_count = 15 → 0 (< 20 threshold)\nFinancial_Stability_Risk = 5 - (5 + 3 + 4 + 0) = 5 - 12 = -7\nCapped at 0: Financial_Stability_Risk = MAX(0, -7) = 0\nInterpretation: Strong financial position reduces vendor risk to zero\n3.2.7 Total Vendor Risk\nFormula:\nVendor_Risk = (MIN(100, Base_Vendor_Risk) x 0.35) +\n(MIN(100, Maturity_Gap_Risk) x 0.25) +\n(MIN(100, Certification_Gap_Risk) x 0.20) +\n(MIN(100, Reference_Check_Risk) x 0.10) +\n(MIN(100, Financial_Stability_Risk) x 0.10)\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance total vendor risk:\nVR = (9 x 0.35) + (35 x 0.25) + (0 x 0.20) + (0 x 0.10) + (0 x 0.10)\n= 3.15 + 8.75 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 11.9 ~ 12\nInterpretation: Low vendor risk. Primary concern: Maturity gap (35 raw, 8.75\nweighted).\nRecommendation: Require dedicated technical account manager and enterprise SLA\nWeight Rationale:\nComponent Weight Rationale\nBase Vendor Risk 0.35 Core vendor quality is the strongest signal of\npartnership viability\nMaturity Gap Risk 0.25 Vendor-buyer maturity mismatch causes real support\nand scaling problems\nCertification Gap Risk 0.20 Missing certifications create compliance blockers in\nregulated industries\nReference Check Risk 0.10 Supporting signal; references confirm but rarely\noverride other factors\nFinancial Stability Risk 0.10 Supporting signal; relevant for long-term viability\nassessment\n3.3 Organizational Readiness Gap Calculation\n3.3.1 Master Formula\nReadiness Gap measures internal organizational preparedness:\nOrganizational_Readiness_Gap = AI_Governance_Maturity_Gap +\nData_Governance_Maturity_Gap +\nSkills_Gap_Risk +\nChange_Management_Risk +\nBudget_Adequacy_Risk\nORG = MIN(100, sum_of_components)\nCore Principle: Organizations unprepared for AI deployment experience 60-80% higher failure rates\nregardless of vendor quality.\n3.3.2 AI Governance Maturity Gap\nFormula:\nAI_Governance_Maturity_Gap = (Required_level - Current_level) × Level_penalty +\nDocumentation_gap_penalty +\nApproval_process_gap_penalty\nLevel_penalty = 15 points per maturity level gap\nRequired_level = LOOKUP((risk_tolerance, business_criticality), {	[0.008675906,0.050832596,-0.015930565,0.009910033,0.017417526,0.025193542,0.10171718,-0.08833421,0.008953799,0.019932797,-0.014670972,0.028290877,-0.04535605,-0.030148901,-0.020924777,-0.027506985,-0.030486643,-0.00068116985,-0.006322