s_Engineer: 0\nAI_Product_Manager: 1\nIntegration_Specialist: 0\n}\nGap calculation:\n- Data_Scientists: (3 - 2) = 1 × 10 = 10 points\n- ML_Engineers: (2 - 1) = 1 × 10 = 10 points\n- MLOps_Engineer: (1 - 0) = 1 × 8 = 8 points\n- AI_Product_Manager: (1 - 1) = 0 × 7 = 0 points\n- Integration_Specialist: (1 - 0) = 1 × 8 = 8 points\nHeadcount gap total = 10 + 10 + 8 + 0 + 8 = 36 points\nTraining gaps:\n- existing_staff_ai_training = "basic" (attended workshops) → +8 (partial)\n- executive_team_ai_literacy = "medium" (understand concepts) → +5 (partial)\n- end_user_training_plan = "draft" (in development) → +4 (partial)\n- Training penalty = 17 points\nExternal dependency:\n- plan_to_use_consultants_indefinitely = "no" (transition plan exists)\n- no_knowledge_transfer_plan = "no" (documented handoff)\n- External dependency = 0 points\nSkills_Gap_Risk = 36 + 17 + 0 = 53 points\n3.3.5 Change Management Risk\nFormula:\nChange_Management_Risk = (Change_impact_scale / Change_capability) ×\nScale_factor -\nStakeholder_engagement_bonus\nChange_impact_scale = Impacted_employees + (Impacted_customers / 1000) +\n(Business_process_changes × 50)\nChange_capability = LOOKUP(change_management_maturity, {\n"None": 0,\n"Ad_hoc": 3,\n"Basic": 10,\n"Moderate": 20,\n"Mature": 35,\n"Excellence": 50\n})\nScale_factor = 100 // Normalization constant\nStakeholder_engagement_bonus = {\nIF executive_sponsor_committed = "yes": -10\nIF user_representatives_in_design = "yes": -8\nIF communication_plan_defined = "yes": -5\nIF pilot_user_group_identified = "yes": -4\n}\nChange_Management_Risk = MIN(60, calculated_value) // Cap at 60 to leave room\nfor other gaps\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance change impact assessment:\nImpact scale:\n- Impacted_employees = 250 (claims processors)	[-0.020148763,0.020174216,0.04407888,0.010343262,0.0066944924,0.0061757886,0.019743746,-0.062083837,0.015068422,0.034064505,-0.011162401,-0.028837198,0.026202643,0.010232756,0.0137381945,-0.03898403,0.029463895