054085143,0.0072480347,-0.0073305303,-0.017890735,-0.042710725,-0.081113376,-0.0155952955,0.018139612,0.0017114185,0.025847962,-0.0020490352,0.043221552,0.012253512,0.023478216,0.02830257,0.00436798,0.055078227,-0.0013047511,0.032527283,0.007322825,0.07938102,-0.00231454,-0.0140509065,0.051530454,-0.013311344,0.031054761,-0.026368795,0.012632643,-0.014105437,0.0071399673,0.031847473,0.045500062,0.0034539674,-0.036472544,0.059735626,0.043575667,-0.005607407,0.028506113,-0.039518412,-0.04830285,-0.014682376,0.0044277594]	{"chunker": "langchain.RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter", "file_name": "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf", "char_count": 3488, "chunk_index": 5, "orchestrator": "langgraph", "embedding_model": "amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0", "embedding_dimensions": 1024}	2026-07-16 10:18:29.319439+05:30
6a5c8db0-9a27-46bf-904c-90488b84f0ce	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	6	}\nChange_Management_Risk = MIN(60, calculated_value) // Cap at 60 to leave room\nfor other gaps\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance change impact assessment:\nImpact scale:\n- Impacted_employees = 250 (claims processors)\n- Impacted_customers = 500,000 (policyholders)\n- Business_process_changes = 4 (claims intake, review, authorization, appeals)\nChange_impact_scale = 250 + (500,000 / 1000) + (4 × 50)\n= 250 + 500 + 200\n= 950\nChange capability:\n- change_management_maturity = "Moderate" → 20\nRisk calculation:\n- (950 / 20) × 100 = 47.5 × 100 = 4,750\n- Scale_factor adjustment: 4,750 / 100 = 47.5\nStakeholder engagement:\n- executive_sponsor_committed = "yes" (COO championing) → -10\n- user_representatives_in_design = "yes" (3 senior claims processors) → -8\n- communication_plan_defined = "yes" (detailed rollout communications) → -5\n- pilot_user_group_identified = "yes" (20-person pilot team) → -4\n- Engagement bonus = -27\nChange_Management_Risk = 47.5 - 27 = 20.5\nCapped: MIN(60, 20.5) = 20.5 ≈ 21 points\nInterpretation: Moderate change risk\nStrong stakeholder engagement (-27 bonus) significantly reduces risk\nLarge scale (950 impact score) managed by solid change capability\n3.3.6 Budget Adequacy Risk\nFormula:\nBudget_Adequacy_Risk = Budget_shortfall_percentage × Shortfall_multiplier +\nHidden_cost_risk +\nFunding_uncertainty_penalty\nBudget_shortfall_percentage = MAX(0, ((Estimated_total_cost - Allocated_budget)\n/\nEstimated_total_cost) × 100)\nShortfall_multiplier = 0.5 // Convert percentage to risk points (50% shortfall\n= 25 points)\nEstimated_total_cost = {\nVendor_license_fees +\nImplementation_services +\nInternal_labor_costs +\nInfrastructure_costs +\nTraining_costs +\nOngoing_maintenance_costs (Year 1)\n}\nHidden_cost_risk = {\nIF customization_costs_not_estimated = "yes": +10\nIF integration_costs_underestimated = "yes": +8\nIF change_management_costs_not_budgeted = "yes": +7\n}\nFunding_uncertainty_penalty = {\nIF budget_not_fully_approved = "yes": +15\nIF funding_source_uncertain = "yes": +12\nIF contingency_reserve < 15%: +8\n}\nEstimation Methodology:\nVendor license fees = Vendor_quoted_price × (1 + Negotiation_buffer)\nNegotiation_buffer = 0.05 // Assume 5% price variance\nImplementation_services = {\nVendor_professional_services +\nThird_party_consultants +\nIntegration_partners\n}\nInternal_labor_costs = SUM(Required_FTE × Average_loaded_cost × Months)\nInfrastructure_costs = {\nCloud_compute_costs +\nStorage_costs +\nNetwork_bandwidth +\nSecurity_tools\n}\nTraining_costs = {\n(End_user_count × Hours_per_user × Hourly_cost) +\nExecutive_training +\nAdministrator_training +\nTraining_material_development\n}\nOngoing_maintenance = {\nVendor_support_fees +\nInternal_support_staffing +\nModel_monitoring_tools +\nContinuous_improvement_budget\n}\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance budget analysis:\nEstimated total cost breakdown:\n1. Vendor license fees:\n- Vendor quoted: $500K annually\n- Negotiation buffer: $500K × 1.05 = $525K\n2. Implementation services:\n- Vendor professional services: $150K\n- Third-party consultants (integration): $200K\n- Total implementation: $350K\n3. Internal labor costs:\n- 3 staff × $150K loaded × 0.75 years = $337.5K\n4. Infrastructure costs:\n- Azure compute: $75K annually\n- Storage: $25K annually\n- Security tools: $50K annually\n- Total infrastructure: $150K\n5. Training costs:\n- 250 end users × 8 hours × $75/hr = $150K\n- Executive training: $25K\n- Administrator training: $30K\n- Materials development: $15K\n- Total training: $220K	[-0.011920788,-0.0013608956,0.05553919,-0.030285222,0.017614152,0.0193015,0.040388606,-0.06933941,-0.036159378,0.0573972,-0.011949853,-0.03995572,0.0059823357,0.01358813,0.0033244498,0.009105775,0.030587172,-0.0014678147,