Data quality and management directly impact AI\nsystem performance\nSkills Gap 0.25 People are the primary constraint; missing roles block\nall downstream work\nChange Management 0.15 Important for adoption but more addressable than\nstructural gaps\nBudget Adequacy 0.15 Budget enables execution but is typically the most\nnegotiable dimension\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance organizational readiness:\nORG = (48 x 0.25) + (29 x 0.20) + (53 x 0.25) + (21 x 0.15) + (39 x 0.15)\n= 12 + 5.8 + 13.25 + 3.15 + 5.85 = 40.05 ~ 40\nInterpretation: Moderate organizational readiness gap\nPriority remediation order:\n1. Skills Gap: 53 raw (13.25 weighted)\n2. AI Governance: 48 raw (12 weighted)\n3. Budget Adequacy: 39 raw (5.85 weighted)\n4. Data Governance: 29 raw (5.8 weighted)\n5. Change Management: 21 raw (3.15 weighted)\nRecommended actions before proceeding:\n● Hire MLOps Engineer and Integration Specialist immediately\n● Establish AI Governance Board with defined charter\n● Secure additional $328K budget + 15% contingency ($319K)\n● Advance data governance to Optimized level\n● Extend implementation timeline from 6 to 12 months\n3.4 Integration Risk Calculation\n3.4.1 Master Formula\nIntegration_Risk = Technical_Integration_Complexity +\nFeature_Gap_Risk +\nData_Interoperability_Risk +\nVendor_Lock_in_Risk +\nRollback_Capability_Risk +\nScaling_Risk\nIR = MIN(100, sum_of_components)\n3.4.2 Technical Integration Complexity\nFormula:\nTechnical_Integration_Complexity = AVERAGE(Integration_point_scores) +\nSystem_count_penalty +\nReal_time_requirement_penalty\nIntegration_point_score = LOOKUP(system_architecture, {\n"Legacy_mainframe": 35,\n"Legacy_client_server": 28,\n"Monolithic_application": 22,\n"Microservices": 15,\n"Cloud_native": 10,\n"SaaS_API": 5	[0.0011452821,0.04428394,-0.01719481,-0.032546137,-0.0027937253,0.021790266,0.056650158,-0.0339001,0.024630899,0.022097724,-0.034961466,0.043195844,0.02531084,0.013267467,-0.046665225,-0.052918926,0.060143355,0.0