2714c6f0-f8c3-4a26-97bb-f8b9b5cf2951	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	10	→ 3 points\nContract flexibility:\n- minimum_term = 1 year (< 2 year threshold) → 0\n- auto_renewal_without_opt_out = "no" (90-day notice to cancel) → 0\n- early_termination_penalty = 25% (< 50% threshold) → 0\n- no_migration_assistance_clause = "yes" (vendor won't help migrate off) → +7\n- Contract penalty = 7 points\nVendor_Lock_in_Risk = 32 + 3 + 7 = 42 points\n3.4.6 Rollback Capability Risk\nFormula:\nRollback_Capability_Risk = Rollback_mechanism_gap +\nRollback_testing_gap +\nBusiness_continuity_gap\nRollback_mechanism_gap = LOOKUP(rollback_capability, {\n"No_rollback_plan": 30,\n"Manual_rollback_undocumented": 22,\n"Manual_rollback_documented": 15,\n"Semi_automated_rollback": 8,\n"Fully_automated_rollback": 2\n})\nRollback_testing_gap = {\nIF rollback_never_tested = "yes": +15\nIF rollback_test_over_1_year_ago = "yes": +8\nIF rollback_test_within_year = "yes": 0\n}\nBusiness_continuity_gap = {\nIF no_fallback_process = "yes": +20\nIF manual_fallback_process = "yes": +10\nIF automated_fallback_system = "yes": 0\n}\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance rollback planning:\nRollback mechanism:\n- rollback_capability = "Manual_rollback_documented" (runbook exists) → 15\npoints\nRollback testing:\n- rollback_never_tested = "yes" (plan exists but never executed) → +15\nBusiness continuity:\n- manual_fallback_process = "yes" (can route claims back to human reviewers) →\n+10\nRollback_Capability_Risk = 15 + 15 + 10 = 40 points\nInterpretation: High rollback risk\nRecommendation: Test rollback procedure during pilot phase before production\nEnsure human review capacity can handle 100% claims volume if rollback needed\n3.4.7 Scaling Risk\nFormula:\nScaling_Risk = Pilot_to_production_gap +\nPerformance_uncertainty +\nInfrastructure_capacity_gap\nPilot_to_production_gap = LOG10(Production_scale / Pilot_scale) × Scale_penalty\nScale_penalty = 10 points per order of magnitude\nPerformance_uncertainty = {\nIF load_testing_not_completed = "yes": +15\nIF stress_testing_not_completed = "yes": +12\nIF production_volume_unknown = "yes": +10\n}\nInfrastructure_capacity_gap = {\nIF infrastructure_not_sized = "yes": +15\nIF auto_scaling_not_configured = "yes": +10\nIF monitoring_alerts_not_defined = "yes": +8\n}\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance scaling assessment:\nPilot to production gap:\n- Pilot_scale = 50 claims/day × 30 days = 1,500 claims\n- Production_scale = 5,000 claims/day × 30 days = 150,000 claims\n- Ratio = 150,000 / 1,500 = 100×\n- LOG10(100) = 2 (two orders of magnitude)\n- Pilot_to_production_gap = 2 × 10 = 20 points\nPerformance uncertainty:\n- load_testing_not_completed = "no" (vendor tested at 10,000 claims) → 0\n- stress_testing_not_completed = "yes" (not tested at 150,000 scale) → +12\n- production_volume_unknown = "no" (historical data available) → 0\n- Performance penalty = 12 points\nInfrastructure capacity:\n- infrastructure_not_sized = "no" (Azure sizing calculated) → 0\n- auto_scaling_not_configured = "yes" (manual scaling initially) → +10\n- monitoring_alerts_not_defined = "yes" (alerts TBD) → +8\n- Infrastructure penalty = 18 points\nScaling_Risk = 20 + 12 + 18 = 50 points\nInterpretation: High scaling risk\n100× scale jump from pilot to production\nRecommendation:\n1. Phased rollout: 10% → 25% → 50% → 100% of volume\n2. Configure auto-scaling before production\n3. Conduct stress test at 200,000 claims (133% of expected peak)\n3.4.8 Total Integration Risk\nFormula:\nIntegration_Risk = (MIN(100, Technical_Integration) x 0.15) +\n(MIN(100, Feature_Gap) x 0.25) +	[0.008916096,0.026705872,-0.0083470745,-0.020135637,0.031763297,0.0123344865,0.033941902,-0.04749918,-0.0041801487,0.0038937107,-0.018817548,-0.015182628,-0.028845655,-0.013839215,-0.03800373,-0.040716693,-0.017021049,-0.021760197,0.02476095