21a26e13-021b-4e4e-84e5-5da82ac9fc34	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	13	● Require vendor delivery of missing features before pilot\n● Executive checkpoint at Month 6 before pilot proceeds\nSuccess Criteria for Month 6 Checkpoint:\n4. All 3 critical positions hired and onboarded\n5. AI Governance Board operational with 3+ meetings held\n6. Data governance advanced to Optimized (verified by audit)\n7. Vendor demonstrates prior auth + state appeals features\n8. Budget fully approved and allocated\nIf Success Criteria Not Met → Abort and Re-Evaluate\nAssessment Type 4: Custom AI Build\n4.1 Assessment Overview\nObjective: Evaluate the feasibility and readiness of building a custom AI solution\nin-house rather than purchasing a commercial product.\nPrimary Users: Organizations considering whether to build custom AI capabilities internally\nOutput Metric: Build Readiness Score (BRS) = 0-100 (higher = more viable to build)\nFormula Structure:\nBRS = 100 - [(Technical_Risk x 0.40) +\n(Governance_Risk x 0.30) +\n(Data_Risk x 0.30)]\nRationale for Weights:\n• Technical Risk (40%): Building AI requires specialized expertise; technical challenges are\nthe primary blocker\n• Governance Risk (30%): Internal builds require robust governance to prevent unchecked\ndeployment\n• Data Risk (30%): Custom AI is only as good as training data; quality/availability is critical\nDecision Framework:\nIF BRS >= 76: BUILD RECOMMENDED (Strong capability)\nELSE IF BRS >= 51: BUILD FEASIBLE (Gaps to address; extended timeline)\nELSE IF BRS >= 26: REVIEW BUILD DECISION (COTS preferred)\nELSE: REASSESS APPROACH (Major blockers; COTS strongly preferred)\n4.2 Technical Risk Calculation\n4.2.1 Master Formula\nTechnical_Risk = Team_Capability_Gap +\nArchitecture_Complexity_Risk +\nModel_Development_Risk +\nInfrastructure_Risk +\nMaintenance_Burden_Risk\nTR = MIN(100, sum_of_components)\n4.2.2 Team Capability Gap\nFormula:\nTeam_Capability_Gap = Required_expertise_gap +\nExperience_gap +\nRetention_risk\nRequired_expertise_gap = SUM(Missing_role_count × Role_criticality)\nRole_criticality = LOOKUP(role_type, {\n"ML_Research_Scientist": 12,\n"Senior_ML_Engineer": 10,\n"MLOps_Engineer": 9,\n"Data_Engineer": 8,\n"AI_Product_Manager": 7,\n"ML_Platform_Engineer": 8,\n"AI_Safety_Researcher": 10\n})\nExperience_gap = LOOKUP(team_average_ai_experience, {\n"< 1 year": 15,\n"1-2 years": 10,\n"2-4 years": 5,\n"4+ years": 0\n}) + Project_complexity_penalty\nProject_complexity_penalty = IF project_complexity IN ["High", "Very_High"]:\nLOOKUP(team_prior_similar_projects, {\n"0 projects": 10,\n"1-2 projects": 5,\n"3+ projects": 0\n})\nELSE: 0\nRetention_risk = LOOKUP(team_stability, {\n"High_turnover (>20% annually)": 15,\n"Moderate_turnover (10-20%)": 8,\n"Stable (<10%)": 0\n})\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst Insurance custom build team assessment:\nRequired team for GenAI chatbot build:\n- ML Research Scientists: Need 2, Have 0 → Gap: 2 × 12 = 24\n- Senior ML Engineers: Need 3, Have 1 → Gap: 2 × 10 = 20\n- MLOps Engineers: Need 2, Have 0 → Gap: 2 × 9 = 18\n- Data Engineers: Need 2, Have 1 → Gap: 1 × 8 = 8\n- AI Product Managers: Need 1, Have 0 → Gap: 1 × 7 = 7\nRequired_expertise_gap = 24 + 20 + 18 + 8 + 7 = 77 points\nExperience assessment:\n- team_average_ai_experience = "1-2 years" → 10 points\n- project_complexity = "Very_High" (GenAI + healthcare)\n- team_prior_similar_projects = "0 projects" → 10 points\n- Experience_gap = 10 + 10 = 20 points\nRetention:\n- team_stability = "Moderate_turnover" (15% annual in tech roles) → 8 points\nTeam_Capability_Gap = 77 + 20 + 8 = 105 points\nCapped: MIN(100, 105) = 100	[0.016757648,0.053557258,0.030097682,0.011879847,0.020712445,0.012751618,0.062085208,-0.03130513,0.06246922,0.06970813,0.013482038,0.09335943,-0.0004774655,-0.0064472076,0.040717352,-0.03258155,-0.0028362072,0.0028108093,-0.014056999,-0.