5e7ec65d-300d-4e19-b9a6-eda37ce9b7c7	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	16	Interpretation: VERY HIGH ongoing maintenance\nMonthly retraining = 2-3 FTE dedicated to model ops\nTechnical debt from inexperienced team = future refactoring costs\nCritical API dependencies = vendor lock-in risk\nHIPAA documentation = ongoing compliance burden\n4.2.7 Total Technical Risk\nFormula:\nTechnical_Risk = (MIN(100, Team_Capability_Gap) x 0.25) +\n(MIN(100, Architecture_Complexity) x 0.20) +\n(MIN(100, Model_Development_Risk) x 0.25) +\n(MIN(100, Infrastructure_Risk) x 0.15) +\n(MIN(100, Maintenance_Burden) x 0.15)\nWeight Rationale:\nComponent Weight Rationale\nTeam Capability Gap 0.25 People are the primary constraint for custom AI builds\nArchitecture Complexity 0.20 Architectural decisions have long-term cost and risk\nimplications\nModel Development 0.25 Core technical challenge; model quality determines\nRisk viability\nInfrastructure Risk 0.15 Important but typically the most\npurchasable/outsourceable\nMaintenance Burden 0.15 Long-term cost driver but lower urgency than\nbuild-phase risks\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst custom build technical assessment:\nTR = (100 x 0.25) + (76 x 0.20) + (55 x 0.25) + (50 x 0.15) + (52 x 0.15)\n= 25 + 15.2 + 13.75 + 7.5 + 7.8 = 69.25 ~ 69\nInterpretation: High technical risk. Team Capability is the dominant blocker.\n- Team: 100 raw (25 weighted) - missing 8 positions\n- Architecture: 76 raw (15.2 weighted) - GenAI + PHI + mainframe\n- Model Dev: 55 raw (13.75 weighted) - clinical validation + bias\n- Infrastructure: 50 raw (7.5 weighted) - no MLOps platform\n- Maintenance: 52 raw (7.8 weighted) - monthly retrain + debt\n4.3 Governance Risk Calculation\n4.3.1 Master Formula\nGovernance_Risk = AI_Governance_Maturity_Gap +\nEthics_Oversight_Gap +\nRisk_Management_Gap +\nCompliance_Capability_Gap\nGR = MIN(100, sum_of_components)\n4.3.2 AI Governance Maturity Gap\nFormula:\nAI_Governance_Maturity_Gap = (Required_Build_Governance - Current_Governance) ×\nLevel_weight\nRequired_Build_Governance = Required_Governance_Level_from_Assessment_Type_3 +\nBuild_penalty\nBuild_penalty = 1 // Building requires 1 additional maturity level vs. buying\nLevel_weight = 20 // Higher than Assessment Type 3 (15) due to build\ncomplexity\nRationale: Building AI requires MORE mature governance than buying:\n● Buying: Vendor handles product governance, buyer focuses on deployment governance\n● Building: Organization responsible for BOTH product development governance AND deployment\ngovernance\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst governance for custom build:\nFrom Assessment Type 3:\n- Required_Governance_Level = 4 (Optimized)\n- Current_Governance_Level = 2 (Basic Policies)\nFor custom build:\n- Required_Build_Governance = 4 + 1 = 5 (Data-Driven Culture)\n[Building requires excellence-level governance]\n- Current_Governance_Level = 2 (unchanged)\nAI_Governance_Maturity_Gap = (5 - 2) × 20\n= 3 × 20\n= 60 points\nInterpretation: CRITICAL governance gap for custom build\nNeed to advance 3 maturity levels (24-36 months minimum)\nBuilding without Level 5 governance = high probability of deployment failures\n4.3.3 Ethics Oversight Gap\nFormula:\nEthics_Oversight_Gap = Ethics_board_gap +\nEthics_review_process_gap +\nStakeholder_engagement_gap\nEthics_board_gap = LOOKUP(ai_ethics_board_status, {\n"Established_operational_>2years": 0,\n"Established_operational_<2years": 10,\n"Established_inactive": 20,\n"Planned": 25,\n"None": 30\n})\nEthics_review_process_gap = LOOKUP(ethics_review_process, {\n"Mandatory_for_all_AI_projects": 0,\n"Mandatory_for_high_risk_only": 8,\n"Optional": 15,\n"None": 20	[0.004694817,0.06181434,0.019469948,0.006842931,0.014095184,0.028434178,0.07214032,-0.066219576,0.020018222,0.016432555,0.0025110652,0.0160667,0.013270839,0.011230076,-0.0055116424,-0.0056265215,0.026201218,-0.0071