5cd12a46-2123-48b9-8f7b-dfc29454c372	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	18	Interpretation: MAXIMUM compliance gap\nNo AI regulatory expertise, no audit capability, no certifications\nBuilding requires achieving same compliance as COTS vendors\nEstimated compliance program: 18-24 months, $1.5M+\n4.3.6 Total Governance Risk\nFormula:\nGovernance_Risk = (MIN(100, AI_Governance_Maturity_Gap) x 0.30) +\n(MIN(100, Ethics_Oversight_Gap) x 0.25) +\n(MIN(100, Risk_Management_Gap) x 0.25) +\n(MIN(100, Compliance_Capability_Gap) x 0.20)\nWeight Rationale:\nComponent Weight Rationale\nAI Governance Maturity 0.30 Foundation for all other governance dimensions\nEthics Oversight 0.25 Critical for responsible AI in regulated industries\nRisk Management 0.25 Ongoing risk identification and response capability\nCompliance Capability 0.20 Regulatory necessity; often the most outsourceable\nfunction\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst custom build governance assessment:\nGR = (60 x 0.30) + (65 x 0.25) + (70 x 0.25) + (70 x 0.20)\n= 18 + 16.25 + 17.5 + 14 = 65.75 ~ 66\nInterpretation: High governance risk\n- AI Governance: 60 raw (18 weighted) - need 3 maturity levels\n- Ethics: 65 raw (16.25 weighted) - no board, no process\n- Risk Mgmt: 70 raw (17.5 weighted) - no identification/response\n- Compliance: 70 raw (14 weighted) - no expertise or audits\n4.4 Data Risk Calculation\n4.4.1 Master Formula\nData_Risk = Training_Data_Availability +\nData_Quality_Risk +\nData_Governance_Risk +\nLabeling_Effort_Risk\nDR = MIN(100, sum_of_components)\n4.4.2 Training Data Availability\nFormula:\nTraining_Data_Availability = Volume_gap +\nDiversity_gap +\nRecency_gap\nVolume_gap = ((Required_samples - Available_samples) / Required_samples) ×\nVolume_penalty\nVolume_penalty = 30\nRequired_samples = LOOKUP(model_type, {\n"Rule_based": 0,\n"Traditional_ML": 10_000,\n"Deep_learning": 100_000,\n"Generative_AI (fine_tune)": 500_000,\n"Generative_AI (pretrain)": 10_000_000\n})\nDiversity_gap = LOOKUP(data_coverage, {\n"Comprehensive (all scenarios)": 0,\n"Good (90% scenarios)": 5,\n"Partial (70% scenarios)": 12,\n"Limited (50% scenarios)": 20,\n"Narrow (<30% scenarios)": 25\n})\nRecency_gap = LOOKUP(data_freshness, {\n"< 1 year old": 0,\n"1-2 years old": 3,\n"2-3 years old": 6,\n"3-5 years old": 10,\n"> 5 years old": 15\n})\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst training data assessment:\nVolume analysis:\n- model_type = "Generative_AI (fine_tune)" → Required = 500,000 samples\n- Available_samples = 350,000 claims (10 years history)\n- Volume_gap = ((500,000 - 350,000) / 500,000) × 30\n= (150,000 / 500,000) × 30\n= 0.30 × 30\n= 9 points\nDiversity:\n- data_coverage = "Partial (70% scenarios)"\n[Missing: complex appeals, rare conditions, certain geographies]\n- Diversity_gap = 12 points\nRecency:\n- data_freshness = "2-3 years old" (most recent data from 2022-2023)\n- Recency_gap = 6 points\nTraining_Data_Availability = 9 + 12 + 6 = 27 points\nInterpretation: MODERATE data availability risk\nVolume 70% adequate but gap exists\nDiversity limited (missing 30% of real-world scenarios)\nRecency acceptable but not ideal for current patterns\n4.4.3 Data Quality Risk\nFormula:\nData_Quality_Risk = Accuracy_issues +\nCompleteness_issues +\nConsistency_issues +\nBias_in_data\nAccuracy_issues = LOOKUP(data_accuracy_rate, {\n"> 99%": 0,\n"95-99%": 8,\n"90-95%": 15,\n"85-90%": 22,\n"< 85%": 30\n})\nCompleteness_issues = LOOKUP(missing_data_rate, {\n"< 1%": 0,\n"1-5%": 5,\n"5-10%": 12,\n"10-20%": 20,\n"> 20%": 25\n})\nConsistency_issues = LOOKUP(data_standardization, {\n"Fully_standardized": 0,\n"Mostly_standardized": 6,\n"Partially_standardized": 12,\n"Not_standardized": 20	[-0.009720081,0.035027552,0.04689197,0.0038250936,0.009221504,0.0064624012,-0.01684022,-0.09987669,-0.008258504,0.04944862,-0.01624948,-0.025630014,-0.022970961,0.02765749,0.022089222,-0.02