9ae0cd8f-a147-4fd5-8350-c2925b6c567f	\N	C:\\2026\\AI-Q\\Jul2026\\14July2026_bkp\\AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf	20	- Labeling_cost = $1,750,000 / $100,000 = 17.5 ≈ 18 points\nExpertise requirement:\n- required_labeler_expertise = "Expert (clinical/legal)"\n[Medical necessity labeling requires clinical judgment]\n- Expertise requirement = 20 points\nTime requirement:\n- 350K labels at 50 labels/day/expert = 7,000 expert-days\n- With 10 clinical experts = 700 days / 20 working days/month = 35 months\n- estimated_labeling_duration = "> 12 months" → 25 points\nLabeling_Effort_Risk = 18 + 20 + 25 = 63 points\nInterpretation: CRITICAL labeling effort risk\n$1.75M cost + 35 months timeline = major blocker\nRequires 10 clinical experts dedicated for 3 years\nAlternative: Use vendor product with pre-labeled training data\n4.4.6 Total Data Risk\nFormula:\nData_Risk = (MIN(100, Training_Data_Availability) x 0.25) +\n(MIN(100, Data_Quality_Risk) x 0.30) +\n(MIN(100, Data_Governance_Risk) x 0.20) +\n(MIN(100, Labeling_Effort_Risk) x 0.25)\nWeight Rationale:\nComponent Weight Rationale\nTraining Data Availability 0.25 Volume and diversity set the performance ceiling\nData Quality Risk 0.30 Highest-impact dimension; poor quality = poor models\nData Governance Risk 0.20 Provenance and lineage; important but more\nprocess-oriented\nLabeling Effort Risk 0.25 Major cost and timeline driver; often the gating\nconstraint\nCalculation Example:\nHealthFirst custom build data assessment:\nDR = (27 x 0.25) + (64 x 0.30) + (45 x 0.20) + (63 x 0.25)\n= 6.75 + 19.2 + 9.0 + 15.75 = 50.7 ~ 51\nInterpretation: Moderate-High data risk. Data Quality is the dominant concern.\n- Data Quality: 64 raw (19.2 weighted)\n- Labeling: 63 raw (15.75 weighted) - $1.75M, 35 months\n- Data Governance: 45 raw (9.0 weighted)\n- Training Data: 27 raw (6.75 weighted)\n4.5 Final Build Risk Score\n4.5.1 Master Formula\nBuild_Risk_Score = 100 - (Technical_Risk × 0.40) +\n(Governance_Risk × 0.30) +\n(Data_Risk × 0.30)\n4.5.2 Comprehensive Calculation\nFormula:\nBRS = 100 - [(69 x 0.40) + (66 x 0.30) + (51 x 0.30)]\n= 100 - [27.6 + 19.8 + 15.3]\n= 100 - 62.7\n= 37.3\nRounded: BRS = 37\n4.5.3 Build Risk Interpretation Framework\nScore Classification Build Viability Recommended Action\nRange\n76-100 Build Ready Strong organizational Build recommended; proceed\ncapability; team, data, with standard development\nand governance in place timeline\n51-75 Build Feasible Viable with targeted gaps; Build possible; address gaps\npreparation needed first; 24-36 month timeline\n26-50 Build Review Significant gaps across Review build decision; COTS\nRecommended multiple dimensions preferred unless strategic\nimperative\n0-25 Build Reassessment Major gaps; insufficient Reassess approach; COTS\nRequired capability for custom strongly preferred\ndevelopment\n4.5.4 HealthFirst Custom Build Assessment Example\nComplete Score Breakdown:\nTechnical Risk: 69\nTeam Capability: 100 x 0.25 = 25\nArchitecture Complexity: 76 x 0.20 = 15.2\nModel Development: 55 x 0.25 = 13.75\nInfrastructure: 50 x 0.15 = 7.5\nMaintenance Burden: 52 x 0.15 = 7.8\nGovernance Risk: 66\nAI Governance Maturity: 60 x 0.30 = 18\nEthics Oversight: 65 x 0.25 = 16.25\nRisk Management: 70 x 0.25 = 17.5\nCompliance Capability: 70 x 0.20 = 14\nData Risk: 51\nTraining Data: 27 x 0.25 = 6.75\nData Quality: 64 x 0.30 = 19.2\nData Governance: 45 x 0.20 = 9.0\nLabeling Effort: 63 x 0.25 = 15.75\nBRS = 100 - [(69 x 0.40) + (66 x 0.30) + (51 x 0.30)]\n= 100 - [27.6 + 19.8 + 15.3]\n= 100 - 62.7 = 37.3 ~ 37\nThe BRS of 37 correctly shows building is not recommended but communicates\nwhy: Technical Risk (69) is the primary blocker, followed closely by	[-0.016043277,0.07070467,0.022896675,-0.027030282,0.00636004,0.03063532,0.043294072,-0.060035754,0.027576057,0.023425246,0.024160914,0.020960238,0.05482468,-0.010737792,-0.0476768,-0.007899343,-0.0012871925,0.00