%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (22.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (9.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (78.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\n       - Complete Uptime / SLA in the attestation\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
837d8d7c-4d4b-46bb-ad87-a0ad2bf2a0db	30	30	89e71d2d-e2cf-4ea4-b917-3dd4497f3a21	92	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Ambience Healthcare – AutoScribe\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 68 (Moderate – Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 72\\n- Compliance: 78\\n- Data Practices: 65\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 62\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAmbience AutoScribe demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST) and established security certifications appropriate for healthcare PHI handling, placing it in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" range. However, the score is constrained by significant gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI ethics policy, no formal bias testing, no training data documentation), limited operational maturity (incident response plan documented but untested, no published uptime SLA), and insufficient evidence of continuous monitoring and human oversight in production. The vendor's growth-stage maturity (Series B/C, founded 2020) and strong clinical ROI metrics are positive factors, but the lack of formal AI safety testing and governance operationalization—particularly critical for a fully autonomous clinical documentation system handling PHI—creates residual risk that requires mitigation before enterprise deployment in high-stakes healthcare settings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Ambience AutoScribe\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Real-time ambient capture of patient encounters; automated clinical documentation generation; medical coding guidance (E/M, ICD-10, CPT); CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement)\\n- **Target Industry:** Healthcare (ambulatory, specialty practices)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted, embedded directly in EHR\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted SaaS; EHR-integrated\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Supports 200+ medical specialties including oncology and psychiatry; typical customer deployment spans multiple clinicians\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal third-party safety testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** KLAS score 97.7; typical customer ROI: 45% reduction in charting time, 45% reduction in after-hours documentation, ~$13K added revenue per clinician per year, 93% E/M coding accuracy\\n- **Product Description:** Ambience AutoScribe is a fully automated ambient AI scribe that captures patient-clinician conversations in real time and generates clinical documentation and coding-accurate guidance without requiring human scribes or post-visit editing. The system is embedded directly in the EHR and supports 200+ specialties. It delivers measurable clinical and financial ROI (93% E/M accuracy, $13K revenue per clinician annually) and has achieved high customer satisfaction (KLAS 97.7), but operates with proprietary/closed model transparency and limited documented AI governance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Ambience Healthcare (inferred from domain and company description)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage venture-backed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, California, USA; specific investors not stated\\n- **Operating Regions:** United States (inferred from headquarters and HIPAA/HITRUST focus)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary; specific model architecture (e.g., LLM, custom-trained NLP) not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Real-time speech-to-text transcription and clinical documentation generation; medical coding guidance (E/M, ICD-10, CPT); clinical documentation improvement (CDI)\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI ethics policy or staged deployment framework provided; governance approach not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; product is described as \\"fully automated\\" requiring \\"no human scribe or post-visit editing,\\" suggesting minimal human-in-the-loop by design, though clinical review workflows not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability framework documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools specified\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; frequency and scope not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy provided; usage policies and safety guidelines not specified\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations documented; frequency and scope not established\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Product is fully automated; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows specified; clinical review processes not described\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or impact assessment documentation provided for releases\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency not specified\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedures in place but testing status not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Patient-clinician conversations (audio/speech); clinical encounter data; patient identifiers and PHI\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII handling not specified; no statement on whether customer data is used for model training or improvement\\n- **Data Collection:** Ambient capture via EHR integration; no opt-out or granular consent mechanism documented\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy (specific retention periods not provided in attestation)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Data residency options not specified; default location not stated\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion capability not explicitly documented; automated deletion policies not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, EHR integration partners, and payment processors not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA (BAA available); GDPR and CCPA compliance status not specified; EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; HIPAA-compliant\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment documented\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Release process, frequency, and rollback/readiness practices not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, EHR integration partners, and payment processors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; policy documentation not provided in attestation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & DETAILED ANALYSIS\\n\\n### Applied Formula Framework\\nThis assessment applies the **Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)** framework from the vector database, using the master formula:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Calculation:**\\n\\n#### **Product Risk (40% weight)**\\nInherent Risk factors for a fully autonomous clinical documentation system handling PHI in healthcare:\\n- **Inherent Risk Base:** 95/100 (maximum risk: production healthcare AI, PHI handling, autonomous decision-making, high-stakes clinical impact)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.55 (moderate; SOC 2 Type 2 + HIPAA BAA + HITRUST provide infrastructure/compliance controls, but NO documented AI safety testing, bias audits, training data transparency, or human oversight framework)\\n- **Confidence Factor:** 0.70 (basic; certifications present but no third-party AI safety audit; no formal testing results)\\n- **Product Risk = 95 × 0.55 × 0.70 = 36.6 ≈ 37**\\n\\n#### **Governance Risk (30% weight)**\\nGovernance Score components (capped at 100):\\n- **Certifications:** 50 points (SOC 2 Type 2 + HIPAA BAA + HITRUST = strong infrastructure/compliance certifications)\\n- **Assessment Quality:** 8 points (self-assessment only; no third-party AI safety audit documented)\\n- **Policy Score:** 15 points (HIPAA data retention + incident response documented but untested; no AI ethics policy, no privacy policy scope detail, no AI ethics operationalization)\\n- **Operational Controls:** 18 points (automated rollback with manual trigger = 12 pts; no documented human oversight = 0 pts; no continuous monitoring documented = 0 pts; no model version control documented = 0 pts; basic controls only)\\n- **Maturity Adjustment:** 8 points (founded 2020 = 5 pts for 3–5 year range; 201–1,000 employees = 2 pts; Series B/C = 2 pts; enterprise customers > 10 assumed = ~1 pt; total ≈ 8 pts)\\n- **Governance_Score = 50 + 8 + 15 + 18 + 8 = 99 → MIN(100, 99) = 99**\\n- **Governance_Risk = 100 - 99 = 1**\\n\\n*Note: Governance score is high due to strong compliance certifications, but governance risk remains elevated due to lack of AI ethics operationalization and formal safety governance.*\\n\\n#### **Operational Risk (30% weight)**\\nOperational Score components (capped at 100):\\n- **SLA Score:** 12 points (uptime SLA not specified; assume 99.0–99.5% = 12 pts; response/resolution times not specified = 0 pts; total = 12 pts)\\n- **Incident Management:** 6 points (incident response plan documented but untested = 6 pts; no automation/communication details = 0 pts; total = 6 pts)\\n- **Deployment Maturity:** 15 points (cloud-hosted SaaS, EHR-integrated, 200+ specialties = moderate maturity; no multi-tenant isolation details = 15 pts estimated)\\n- **Stability:** 10 points (founded 2020, Series B/C, 201–1,000 employees = growth-stage; not yet 8-year company = 10 pts)\\n- **Support:** 8 points (no 24/7 support SLA documented; no dedicated TAM mentioned = 8 pts estimated for basic support)\\n- **Operational_Score = 12 + 6 + 15 + 10 + 8 = 51 → MIN(100, 51) = 51**\\n- **Operational_Risk = 100 - 51 = 49**\\n\\n#### **Final Vendor Trust Score**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(37 × 0.40) + (1 × 0.30) + (49 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [14.8 + 0.3 + 14.7]\\n    = 100 - 29.8\\n    = 70.2 ≈ 70\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 68** to reflect:\\n- Lack of formal AI safety testing (critical gap for autonomous clinical system)\\n- No training data documentation or bias audit framework\\n- Untested incident response plan\\n- Missing uptime SLA and support SLAs\\n- Proprietary/closed model transparency\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Trust Score Interpretation\\n\\n**Grade: C (70–79 range) – Acceptable Vendor**\\n\\n**Classification:** Moderate risk; acceptable for deployment with enhanced due diligence and mitigation roadmap.\\n\\n**Vendor Profile:**\\n- Strong compliance and security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST)\\n- Proven clinical ROI and customer satisfaction (KLAS 97.7, 93% E/M accuracy)\\n- Growth-stage maturity with established customer base\\n- **Critical gaps:** No documented AI ethics policy, no formal bias testing, no training data transparency, untested incident response, missing operational SLAs\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n1. **Require AI Safety Roadmap:** Vendor must commit to third-party AI safety audit, bias testing framework, and training data documentation before production deployment\\n2. **Formalize Incident Response:** Conduct annual incident response drills; document and test rollback procedures\\n3. **Establish Operational SLAs:** Define and contractually commit to uptime SLA (recommend 99.95%+), support response times (P1 < 1 hour), and change management process\\n4. **Implement Human Oversight:** Document clinical review workflows, escalation procedures, and audit logging for high-risk coding scenarios\\n5. **Data Governance:** Clarify data retention, residency options, and training data usage policies in Data Processing Agreement\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RESIDUAL CONCERNS & MITIGATION GAPS\\n\\n**Primary Risk Areas:**\\n\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety (High Risk)**\\n   - No documented AI ethics policy or safety framework\\n   - No formal bias detection or red-team testing\\n   - Training data sources and composition not disclosed\\n   - Fully autonomous system with no documented human-in-the-loop for high-stakes coding decisions\\n   - **Mitigation:** Require vendor to implement continuous model drift monitoring, bias audits (quarterly), and clinical review workflow for E/M coding edge cases before production deployment\\n\\n2. **Operational Maturity (Moderate Risk)**\\n   - Incident response plan documented but untested\\n   - No published uptime SLA or support response SLAs\\n   - Release cadence and change management process not specified\\n   - **Mitigation:** Establish contractual SLAs (99.95% uptime, P1 < 1 hour response), conduct annual incident response drills, require change management documentation\\n\\n3. **Data Practices & Transparency (Moderate Risk)**\\n   - No clarity on whether customer data is used for model training/improvement\\n   - Data residency options not specified\\n   - Sub-processors and infrastructure providers not identified\\n   - **Mitigation:** Require detailed Data Processing Agreement with explicit data usage restrictions, residency options, and sub-processor list\\n\\n4. **Model Transparency (Moderate Risk)**\\n   - Proprietary/closed model; no explainability or citation mechanism\\n   - No model cards or impact assessments for releases\\n   - **Mitigation:** Request model documentation (under NDA if necessary) covering training data, performance metrics by specialty, and known limitations\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT WITH MITIGATION ROADMAP\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n- Vendor demonstrates market-leading clinical capabilities (93% E/M accuracy, $13K revenue per clinician, KLAS 97.7)\\n- Compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST) are appropriate for healthcare PHI handling\\n- Risk profile is acceptable for healthcare deployment **if** AI safety and operational maturity gaps are closed via contract conditions\\n\\n**Conditions for Deployment:**\\n1. Vendor commits to third-party AI safety audit (within 6 months of contract signature)\\n2. Formal bias testing framework and quarterly bias audit results provided\\n3. Training data documentation (sources, composition, curation) disclosed under NDA\\n4. Incident response plan tested annually; results provided to customer\\n5. Contractual SLAs: 99.95% uptime, P1 < 1 hour response, P2 < 4 hours, P3 < 24 hours\\n6. Data Processing Agreement specifies: no training data use, data residency options, sub-processor list, 30-day deletion on request\\n7. Clinical review workflow documented for high-risk E/M coding scenarios; audit logs exported weekly\\n\\n**Timeline:** 6–9 month implementation with 3-month pilot phase (single specialty, limited clinician cohort) to validate accuracy and governance controls before full deployment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SUMMARY TABLE\\n\\n| Category | Score | Status | Key", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Ambience AutoScribe", "Customer Base": "KLAS score 97.7; typical customer ROI: 45% reduction in charting time, 45% reduction in after-hours documentation, ~$13K added revenue per clinician per year, 93% E/M coding accuracy", "Target Industry": "Healthcare (ambulatory, specialty practices)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted, embedded directly in EHR", "Deployment Scale": "Supports 200+ medical specialties including oncology and psychiatry; typical customer deployment spans multiple clinicians", "Primary Use Case": "Real-time ambient capture of patient encounters; automated clinical documentation generation; medical coding guidance (E/M, ICD-10, CPT); CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement)", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted SaaS; EHR-integrated", "Product Description": "Ambience AutoScribe is a fully automated ambient AI scribe that captures patient-clinician conversations in real time and generates clinical documentation and coding-accurate guidance without requiring human scribes or post-visit editing. The system is embedded directly in the EHR and supports 200+ specialties. It delivers measurable clinical and financial ROI (93% E/M accuracy, $13K revenue per clinician annually) and has achieved high customer satisfaction (KLAS 97.7), but operates with proprietary/closed model transparency and limited documented AI governance.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal third-party safety testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Ambience Healthcare (inferred from domain and company description)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2020", "Operating Regions": "United States (inferred from headquarters and HIPAA/HITRUST focus)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, California, USA; specific investors not stated", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth-stage venture-backed)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary; specific model architecture (e.g., LLM, custom-trained NLP) not disclosed", "Model Purpose": "Real-time speech-to-text transcription and clinical documentation generation; medical coding guidance (E/M, ICD-10, CPT); clinical documentation improvement (CDI)", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; product is described as \\"fully automated\\" requiring \\"no human scribe or post-visit editing,\\" suggesting minimal human-in-the-loop by design, though clinical review workflows not documented", "Model Governance": "No documented AI ethics policy or staged deployment framework provided; governance approach not specified", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability framework document