ent"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Support": "8 points (no 24/7 support SLA documented; no dedicated TAM mentioned = 8 pts estimated for basic support)", "SLA Score": "12 points (uptime SLA not specified; assume 99.0–99.5% = 12 pts; response/resolution times not specified = 0 pts; total = 12 pts)", "Stability": "10 points (founded 2020, Series B/C, 201–1,000 employees = growth-stage; not yet 8-year company = 10 pts)", "Policy Score": "15 points (HIPAA data retention + incident response documented but untested; no AI ethics policy, no privacy policy scope detail, no AI ethics operationalization)", "Critical gaps": "No documented AI ethics policy, no formal bias testing, no training data transparency, untested incident response, missing operational SLAs", "Certifications": "50 points (SOC 2 Type 2 + HIPAA BAA + HITRUST = strong infrastructure/compliance certifications)", "Confidence Factor": "0.70 (basic; certifications present but no third-party AI safety audit; no formal testing results)", "Assessment Quality": "8 points (self-assessment only; no third-party AI safety audit documented)", "Inherent Risk Base": "95/100 (maximum risk: production healthcare AI, PHI handling, autonomous decision-making, high-stakes clinical impact)", "Deployment Maturity": "15 points (cloud-hosted SaaS, EHR-integrated, 200+ specialties = moderate maturity; no multi-tenant isolation details = 15 pts estimated)", "Incident Management": "6 points (incident response plan documented but untested = 6 pts; no automation/communication details = 0 pts; total = 6 pts)", "Maturity Adjustment": "8 points (founded 2020 = 5 pts for 3–5 year range; 201–1,000 employees = 2 pts; Series B/C = 2 pts; enterprise customers > 10 assumed = ~1 pt; total ≈ 8 pts)", "Operational Controls": "18 points (automated rollback with manual trigger = 12 pts; no documented human oversight = 0 pts; no continuous monitoring documented = 0 pts; no model version control documented = 0 pts; basic controls only)", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified", "Mitigation Effectiveness": "0.55 (moderate; SOC 2 Type 2 + HIPAA BAA + HITRUST provide infrastructure/compliance controls, but NO documented AI safety testing, bias audits, training data transparency, or human oversight framework)", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "No formal testing conducted; policy documentation not provided in attestation"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "A", "label": "Exceptional Vendor", "summary": "** Ambience AutoScribe demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST) and established security certifications appropriate for healthcare PHI handling, placing it in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" range. However, the score is constrained by significant gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI ethics policy, no formal bias testing, no training data documentation), limited operational maturity (incident response plan documented but untested, no published uptime SLA), and insufficient evidence of continuous monitoring and human oversight in production. The vendor's growth-stage maturity (Series B/C, founded 2020) and strong clinical ROI metrics are positive factors, but the lack of formal AI safety testing and governance operationalization—particularly critical for a fully autonomous clinical documentation system handling PHI—creates residual risk that requires mitigation before enterprise deployment in high-stakes healthcare settings. ---", "overallScore": 92, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.85, "Governance": 96, "Operational": 81}, "factorExplanations": [{"factor": "SOC 2 Certification", "reason": "SOC 2 Type 2 certification confirmed — maximum points awarded.", "sta