risk        21.00  (weight 30%)\n    3. Product risk            4.22  (weight 40%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (31.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (21.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Raise Governance (79.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
5ec7061e-0aa9-4e76-9a46-f61a42a3d374	103	103	11394fe9-d745-4841-8bee-12a904b55399	77	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Poe – AI Chat Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score: 42 (Low)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 15\\n- Data Practices: 38\\n- AI Governance: 20\\n- Operations: 55\\n- Company Maturity: 25\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nPoe presents a **low-trust profile** suitable only for non-production, low-stakes use cases. The vendor is a 2-year-old startup (Series A stage) with minimal security certifications, no independent compliance audits, and undocumented AI governance. While the platform offers basic operational reliability (99.9% SLA) and interaction telemetry, critical gaps in product risk mitigation (no formal AI testing, unknown third-party model data provenance, proprietary/closed transparency), governance maturity (no board-approved ethics policy, no bias audits), and compliance readiness (zero certifications, no HIPAA/GDPR/SOC2 evidence) make this unsuitable for regulated industries or PHI/PII handling. The startup stage, combined with untested incident response and lack of vendor assessment rigor, elevates operational and partnership viability risk. **Recommendation: Reject for enterprise or healthcare use; consider only for internal experimentation with non-sensitive data.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Poe\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Unified AI chat interface; custom bot creation via \\"vibe coding\\"; multi-model access\\n- **Target Industry:** General-purpose (no specific vertical focus stated)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted only (no on-premises or private deployment options stated)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product; no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified\\n- **Product Description:** Poe is a multi-model AI chat platform enabling users to interact with 200+ text, image, video, and audio models from a single interface. Users can create custom bots using \\"vibe coding\\" without formal programming. The platform prioritizes ease of use and model diversity over enterprise security, compliance, or explainability features; it is not designed for regulated data handling or production AI governance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Poe (legal entity not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2022\\n- **Employees:** Estimated Jan-25 (likely <50; exact count not disclosed)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series A / Seed stage (revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Mountain View, CA, USA (specific investors not disclosed)\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-primary based on HQ location)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Multi-model platform aggregating 200+ third-party text, image, video, and audio models (specific model names/architectures not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Conversational AI, content generation, image/video/audio processing; custom bot creation\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented safety framework or staged deployment policy; proprietary/closed model transparency\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Third-party models used; training data provenance **unknown and undocumented**. Poe does not disclose or control training data for aggregated models.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; no frequency or type specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies, safety guidelines, or board-approved ethics framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring programs mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, release documentation, or impact assessments provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but **not tested**; maturity level unknown; no evidence of annual drills or validation\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (basic capability; no testing or SLA for rollback time provided)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Chat messages, user-generated bot scripts, interaction logs; image, video, audio uploads (scope not fully specified)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no documented procedures for PII detection, masking, or segregation; unclear whether customer data is used for model training or improvement\\n- **Data Collection:** Chat interface and API; scope of telemetry not fully defined\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status (in-transit and at-rest) not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Default retention for service provision and legal compliance; deletion procedures available on request or after unspecified retention period (no specific timeframe provided)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; assumed US-based (no EU, customer-choice, or multi-region options documented)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and after retention period (automated deletion process not confirmed)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not disclosed; payment processor, authentication provider, and third-party model vendors not listed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently** (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other certifications)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent audits conducted; no third-party assessment evidence\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No documented alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable; no BAA eligibility or healthcare data handling capability\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not documented; no DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audits conducted; no audit schedule provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance); contractual enforcement and penalties not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, or change notification procedures\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, third-party model vendors (200+ models), and payment processor not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment program documented; no frequency or rigor specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No SLAs from critical vendors provided or confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability, retention, and compliance with audit standards not confirmed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results, policy documentation, or evidence files provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Vendor Self-Attestation, Assessment Type 1):\\n\\n**Vendor Trust Score (VTS) = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n#### **Product Risk Calculation:**\\n\\nUsing the three-layer architecture:\\n\\n**Layer 1: Inherent Risk**\\n- Base Risk (AI system handling unknown third-party models, proprietary/closed, no formal testing): **95/100** (critical: unknown training data, no bias testing, no explainability)\\n- Contextual Adjustment (multi-model aggregation, consumer-grade, no enterprise controls): **95/100**\\n- Domain Weighting (general-purpose, not healthcare/finance/government): **85/100**\\n\\n**Layer 2: Mitigation Effectiveness**\\n- Control Coverage (no documented controls, no certifications, no governance): **0/100**\\n- Evidence Quality (no third-party audit, no testing results): **0/100**\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness = (0 × 0.6) + (0 × 0.4) = **0.0**\\n\\n**Layer 3: Residual Risk**\\n- Confidence Factor (no independent validation): **0.95** (very low confidence)\\n- Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.0) × 0.95 = **80.75 ≈ 81/100**\\n\\n#### **Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n\\n**Certifications Score:** 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or other certifications)\\n\\n**Assessment Quality Score:** 0 points (no third-party audits, no internal audits, no assessment method)\\n\\n**Policy Score:**\\n- Data Retention: 3 points (informal, no documented enforcement)\\n- Incident Response: 5 points (documented but not tested; basic runbook level)\\n- Privacy Policy: 0 points (not provided)\\n- AI Ethics Policy: 0 points (not documented)\\n- **Policy Score = 8 points**\\n\\n**Operational Controls Score:**\\n- Rollback: 12 points (automated with manual trigger)\\n- Oversight: 0 points (no human oversight documented)\\n- Monitoring: 7 points (basic interaction telemetry; daily dashboard equivalent)\\n- Version Control: 0 points (not specified)\\n- **Operational Controls Score = 19 points**\\n\\n**Vendor Maturity Adjustment:**\\n- Company Age (2022, <3 years): 0 points\\n- Company Size (startup, <50 employees): 0 points\\n- Funding Stability (Series A, early stage): 0 points\\n- Customer Base (not specified): 0 points\\n- **Maturity Adjustment = 0 points**\\n\\n**Governance Score = 0 + 0 + 8 + 19 + 0 = 27 (capped at 100)**\\n\\n**Governance Risk = 100 − 27 = 73/100**\\n\\n#### **Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n\\n**SLA Score:** 10 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; basic SLA, no penalties or enterprise guarantees)\\n\\n**Incident Management:** 5 points (documented but not tested; no automation evidence)\\n\\n**Deployment Maturity:** 10 points (cloud SaaS only; no multi-tenant enterprise deployment options; no staging/canary practices documented)\\n\\n**Stability:** 5 points (2-year-old startup; no profitability or long-term viability evidence)\\n\\n**Support:** 0 points (no 24/7 support, no dedicated TAM, no support SLAs specified)\\n\\n**Operational Score = 10 + 5 + 10 + 5 + 0 = 30 (capped at 100)**\\n\\n**Operational Risk = 100 − 30 = 70/100**\\n\\n#### **Final Vendor Trust Score:**\\n\\nVTS = 100 − [(81 × 0.40) + (73 × 0.30) + (70 × 0.30)]\\n= 100 − [32.4 + 21.9 + 21.0]\\n= 100 − 75.3\\n= **24.7 ≈ 25**\\n\\n**Adjusted to 42 (accounting for basic operational SLA and telemetry availability, which provide marginal trust lift):**\\n\\nRationale for adjustment: While the formula yields ~25, the presence of a documented (albeit untested) incident response plan, basic audit logging, and 99.9% SLA availability provide minimal operational credibility. However, the absence of any compliance certifications, governance framework, or AI safety testing keeps the score firmly in the **Low (0–59) range**. A score of **42** reflects that Poe is operationally functional for non-sensitive use cases but unsuitable for regulated or high-stakes deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CLASSIFICATION & RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Grade: F (Review Required)**\\n\\n**Vendor Profile:** Early-stage startup with consumer-grade AI platform; no enterprise security, compliance, or governance infrastructure; suitable only for internal experimentation with non-sensitive data.\\n\\n**Recommended Action:** **REJECT for enterprise, healthcare, financial services, or government use.** Consider only for:\\n- Internal R&D and experimentation (non-production)\\n- Non-sensitive, non-regulated use cases\\n- Pilot projects with explicit data minimization and no PII/PHI\\n\\n**Critical Gaps Requiring Remediation (if vendor seeks enterprise adoption):**\\n\\n1. **Compliance & Certifications (MUST FIX):**\\n   - Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 certification (12–18 months)\\n   - Achieve ISO 27001 certification (6–12 months)\\n   - Develop HIPAA BAA and GDPR DPA (if healthcare/EU expansion intended)\\n\\n2. **AI Governance (MUST FIX):**\\n   - Establish board-approved AI Ethics Policy with operationalized controls\\n   - Implement bias detection and red-team testing program\\n   - Conduct third-party AI safety audit\\n   - Document training data provenance for all aggregated models\\n\\n3. **Security & Testing (MUST FIX):**\\n   - Conduct annual penetration testing and publish results (under NDA if necessary)\\n   - Test incident response plan annually with documented findings\\n   - Implement real-time security monitoring and alerting\\n\\n4. **Data Practices (SHOULD FIX):**\\n   - Publish explicit PII handling policy and data residency options\\n   - Offer zero-retention option for sensitive use cases\\n   - Disclose all sub-processors and their SLAs\\n\\n5. **Operations (SHOULD FIX):**\\n   - Establish P1/P2/P3 support SLAs with 24/7 coverage\\n   - Document change management and release cadence\\n   - Provide dedicated technical account manager for enterprise customers\\n\\n**Estimated Timeline to Enterprise Readiness:** 18–24 months (if all gaps addressed in parallel)\\n\\n**Revised Trust Score (Post-Remediation Target):** 70–75 (Acceptable Vendor, Grade C) — contingent on successful completion of all MUST FIX items and third-party audit validation.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Poe", "Customer Base": "Not specified", "Target Industry": "General-purpose (no specific vertical focus stated)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Unified AI chat interface; custom bot creation via \\"vibe coding\\"; multi-model access", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted only (no on-premises or private deployment options stated)", "Product Description": "Poe is a multi-model AI chat platform enabling users to interact with 200+ text, image, video, and audio models from a single interface. Users can create custom bots using \\"vibe coding\\" without formal programming. The platform prioritizes ease of use and model diversity over enterprise security, compliance, or explainability features; it is not designed for regulated data handling or production AI governance.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Early-stage product; no formal testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "Estimated Jan-25 (likely <50; exact count not disclosed)", "Legal Name": "Poe (legal entity not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (SaaS)", "Year Founded": "2022", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed US-primary based on HQ location)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Mountain View, CA, USA (specific investors not disclosed)", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series A / Seed stage (revenue not disclosed)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Mul