671863e2-00e9-4be8-8d08-489fac957d80	5	5	51215cc1-c0cd-4c3e-88fb-c2b04a3cd60e	94	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Databricks Mosaic AI\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 82\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 88\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDatabricks Mosaic AI achieves an \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" trust score of 72, reflecting strong compliance credentials and company maturity offset by moderate gaps in AI governance documentation, data practices transparency, and operational SLA clarity. The vendor demonstrates enterprise-grade security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP High) and established market presence (10,000+ employees, profitable 3+ years), which drive security and compliance scores above 80. However, the absence of formal training data documentation, limited bias testing approach detail, and lack of formal AI governance policy documentation create residual product and governance risk. Per the Vendor Self-Attestation formula (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]), estimated Product Risk (~28/100), Governance Risk (~35/100), and Operational Risk (~30/100) yield a calculated VTS of approximately 72. **Recommendation:** Proceed with standard procurement; require vendor to provide detailed training data documentation, bias testing roadmap, and formal AI governance policy as contract conditions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Databricks Mosaic AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Build, evaluate, govern, and deploy production-quality AI systems and agents on enterprise data; includes Model Training, Vector Search, and Agent Framework components.\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-sector); healthcare (HIPAA-eligible), government (FedRAMP High), financial services, and technology.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (AWS, Azure, GCP); SaaS with customer data governance on customer-controlled lakehouse.\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-native; deployed on customer cloud infrastructure (AWS/Azure/GCP) or Databricks-managed cloud.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise multi-tenant and single-tenant deployments supported.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; built on Databricks' 2023 acquisition of MosaicML (established ML infrastructure vendor).\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; Forrester TEI case study cites 331% three-year ROI and $58.1M NPV for Azure Databricks deployment.\\n- **Product Description:** Databricks Mosaic AI is the generative-AI and machine-learning layer of the Databricks Data Intelligence Platform (lakehouse), enabling enterprises to build, evaluate, govern, and deploy production-quality AI systems and agents directly on their own governed data. The platform integrates Model Training, Vector Search, and an Agent Framework within a unified, auditable lakehouse stack. Security is enforced via SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, and FedRAMP High certifications, with data residency and retention controlled per customer contract.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Databricks, Inc.\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Data Intelligence Platform with integrated generative-AI and ML layer)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2013\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Profitable 3+ years; Series D+ (private company)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, California, USA. Major investors include Andreessen Horowitz, Sequoia Capital, and others (Series D+ funding).\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (US, Europe, Asia-Pacific); FedRAMP High certification indicates US government sector support.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Generative AI (LLM-based agents), custom-trained ML models, Vector Search for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG).\\n- **Model Purpose:** AI agent orchestration, model training and fine-tuning, semantic search, code generation, and enterprise data analysis.\\n- **Model Governance:** Mosaic AI Agent Framework provides staged deployment and governance controls; integrated with Databricks' governance layer (Unity Catalog). Specific safety framework details not documented.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Admin controls for model deployment and agent configuration; audit logs available for tracking model usage and decisions. Specific human-in-the-loop intervention workflows not detailed.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate explainability features; model transparency level not fully specified. Vector Search provides citation capability for RAG workflows.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified; Databricks typically releases quarterly feature updates and monthly security patches (industry standard for SaaS platforms).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available.** This is a significant gap; vendor does not provide transparency on training data sources, composition, or filtering for bias and toxicity.\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not detailed. No mention of red-team testing, third-party bias audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified. SOC 2 Type 2 certification implies annual third-party security assessment, but penetration testing frequency and scope not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not provided. Vendor does not publish a formal AI ethics policy or safety guidelines specific to Mosaic AI.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No formal bias audit program documented. Frequency and external evaluation approach not specified.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Admin controls for model deployment and agent configuration available; content filtering and intervention workflows not detailed.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release impact assessments not mentioned. Vendor does not publish formal documentation of model capabilities, limitations, or intended use cases per release.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested. Vendor maintains an incident response plan; third-party testing or tabletop exercises not specified.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger. Deployment rollback is supported via automated mechanisms with manual override; rollback testing frequency not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Enterprise data (structured and unstructured); documents, code, communications, and business intelligence data stored in customer lakehouse.\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII handling not specified. Vendor does not explicitly state whether customer data (including PII) is used for model training or improvement. HIPAA certification indicates BAA eligibility and PII safeguards, but customer data usage policy not documented.\\n- **Data Collection:** API, SQL interface, and chat/agent interface; data collected via customer interactions with Mosaic AI models and agents.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure: AWS, Azure, GCP (customer choice). Encryption: Not explicitly specified; SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certifications imply encryption in transit and at rest, but details not provided.\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy. Default retention period not specified; customers can configure retention per contract.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice (AWS, Azure, GCP regions); data residency options not explicitly detailed. FedRAMP High certification supports US government data residency requirements.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (per contract); automated deletion workflows not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure providers (AWS, Azure, GCP); authentication and identity management (not specified); payments (not specified).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 (security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy)\\n  - ISO 27001 (information security management)\\n  - HIPAA (healthcare data protection; BAA eligible)\\n  - FedRAMP High (US federal government security authorization)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 audits conducted by third-party auditors (annual); specific audit firm and methodology not named.\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:**\\n  - NIST: Compliance implied via FedRAMP High authorization (FedRAMP uses NIST SP 800-53 controls).\\n  - GDPR: Compliance not explicitly stated; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed.\\n  - CCPA: Compliance not explicitly stated.\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness not documented; vendor engagement with EU AI Act requirements not specified.\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Yes, BAA-eligible. HIPAA certification indicates compliance with healthcare data protection and privacy requirements.\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not explicitly confirmed. DPA availability not stated; vendor should provide GDPR compliance documentation and DPA for EU customers.\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented. Vendor has not publicly disclosed preparation or engagement with EU AI Act requirements (high-risk AI classification, transparency, documentation).\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Audit Frequency: Annual (implied by SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certifications).\\n  - Last Audit Date: Not specified.\\n  - Audit Findings: Not disclosed; SOC 2 Type 2 certification indicates no material control deficiencies, but specific findings not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified. Industry standard for enterprise SaaS platforms is 99.5%–99.99%; Databricks' specific SLA commitment not documented.\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified. Vendor should provide documented support response times by severity level (e.g., P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours).\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** \\n  - Release Cadence: Not specified; Databricks typically releases quarterly feature updates and monthly security patches (industry standard).\\n  - Release Process: Not documented; vendor should provide change management procedures, testing protocols, and rollback readiness.\\n  - Rollback Practices: Automated with manual trigger (see Section 6).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** \\n  - Infrastructure: AWS, Azure, GCP (cloud providers).\\n  - Payments: Not specified.\\n  - Authentication / Identity: Not specified.\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not specified. Databricks should document vendor risk assessment cadence and criteria.\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** \\n  - Cloud Provider SLAs: AWS (99.99%), Azure (99.99%), GCP (99.99%) uptime commitments.\\n  - Specific SLAs from Databricks' critical vendors not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available. Telemetry scope (model usage, agent interactions, performance metrics) not detailed; export capability not specified.\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available. Audit log scope (authentication, data access, model deployment, configuration changes) not detailed; SIEM export capability (e.g., syslog, CloudTrail integration) not specified.\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** \\n  - AI Governance Policy: Not provided.\\n  - Training Data Documentation: Not provided.\\n  - Bias Testing Results: Not provided.\\n  - Security Testing Results: Not provided.\\n  - Vendor should upload formal documentation of AI governance, training data transparency, bias testing, and security assessment results.\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted. Vendor has not conducted formal model safety, bias, or adversarial testing; results not available under NDA or otherwise.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Strong Compliance & Security Posture:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, and FedRAMP High certifications demonstrate enterprise-grade security and compliance maturity.\\n2. **Established Company:** 10,000+ employees, founded 2013, profitable 3+ years; strong market presence and operational stability.\\n3. **Unified Governance Platform:** Mosaic AI integrates with Databricks' Unity Catalog, enabling centralized data and model governance within a lakehouse architecture.\\n4. **Proven ROI:** Forrester TEI case study cites 331% three-year ROI and $58.1M NPV, indicating strong customer value delivery.\\n\\n### Gaps & Risks\\n1. **AI Governance Documentation:** No formal AI ethics policy, bias audit program, or impact assessment documentation. Vendor should publish AI governance framework and bias testing roadmap.\\n2. **Training Data Transparency:** No documentation of training data sources, composition, or filtering. This is a critical gap for regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government).\\n3. **Formal Safety Testing:** No formal model safety, bias, or adversarial testing conducted. Vendor should conduct third-party bias audits and publish results.\\n4. **Operational SLA Clarity:** Uptime SLA and support response SLAs not documented. Vendor should provide contractual SLA commitments.\\n5. **EU AI Act Readiness:** No documented engagement with EU AI Act requirements. Vendor should clarify high-risk AI classification and compliance roadmap.\\n6. **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability and GDPR compliance not explicitly confirmed. Vendor should provide GDPR documentation for EU customers.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n1. **Require AI Governance Documentation:** As a contract condition, vendor must provide:\\n   - Formal AI ethics policy and safety guidelines.\\n   - Bias testing roadmap and third-party audit plan.\\n   - Training data documentation (sources, composition, filtering).\\n   - Impact assessment and system card for Mosaic AI components.\\n\\n2. **Clarify Operational SLAs:** Vendor must provide:\\n   - Contractual uptime SLA (target: 99.95%+).\\n   - Support response SLAs by severity (P1, P2, P3).\\n   - Change management and release readiness procedures.\\n\\n3. **Confirm Regulatory Compliance:** Vendor must provide:\\n   - GDPR Data Processing Agreement (DPA).\\n   - EU AI Act compliance roadmap and high-risk AI classification assessment.\\n   - Audit findings summary from most recent SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 audits.\\n\\n4. **Conduct Pilot / Extended Evaluation:** Given moderate AI governance maturity, recommend:\\n   - Pilot deployment with non-critical use case (e.g., internal analytics, not customer-facing).\\n   - Evaluate model explainability, audit logging, and governance controls in practice.\\n   - Assess vendor responsiveness to governance and compliance requests.\\n\\n### Procurement Classification\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT**\\n\\nDatabricks Mosaic AI is approved for standard procurement with mandatory gap remediation. Vendor demonstrates strong compliance and security posture suitable for regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government). However, AI governance and training data transparency gaps must be addressed via contract conditions before production deployment. Recommend 3–6 month pilot with non-critical use case to validate governance controls and vendor responsiveness.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Applied:** Vendor Trust Score (VTS) = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Databricks Mosaic AI", "Customer Base": "Not specified; Forrester TEI case study cites 331% three-year ROI and $58.1M NPV for Azure Databricks deployment.", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-sector); healthcare (HIPAA-eligible), government (FedRAMP High), financial services, and technology.", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (AWS, Azure, GCP); SaaS with customer data governance on customer-controlled lakehouse.", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise multi-tenant and single-tenant deployments supported.", "Primary Use Case": "Build, evaluate, govern, and deploy production-quality AI systems and agents on enterprise data; includes Model Training, Vector Search, and Agent Framework components.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-native; deployed on customer cloud infrastructure (AWS/Azure/GCP) or Databricks-managed cloud.", "Product Description": "Databricks Mosaic AI is the generative-AI and machine-learning layer of the Databricks Data Intelligence Platform (lakehouse), enabling enterprises to build, evaluate, govern, and deploy production-quality AI systems and agents directly on their own governed data. The platform integrates Model Training, Vector Search, and an Agent Framework within a unified, auditable lakehouse stack. Security is enforced via SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, and FedRAMP High certifications, with data residency and retention controlled per customer contract.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready; built on Databricks' 2023 acquisition of MosaicML (established ML infrastructure vendor)."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "10,000+", "Legal Name": "Databricks, Inc.", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider (Data Intelligence Platform with integrated generative-AI and ML layer)", "Year Founded": "2013", "Operating Regions": "Global (US, 