duct risk            2.97  (weight 40%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (24.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (6.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (76.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\n       - Complete Uptime / SLA in the attestation\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
e6ed36c3-e455-4056-97b7-21b4ca87abc2	9	9	57d0a7d0-e649-4aeb-9d36-f9250edeb8ef	89	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Pinecone Systems – Vector Database Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 **(Acceptable Vendor)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nPinecone demonstrates solid compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, CCPA certifications) and operational reliability (99.95% uptime SLA), positioning it in the \\"Acceptable\\" range. However, significant gaps in AI governance documentation, formal safety testing, and transparency limit the score. The vendor's growth-stage maturity (Series B/C, 201–1,000 employees) and lack of formal bias/adversarial testing, combined with incomplete data residency and retention policy details, create moderate risk. Strengths include strong compliance certifications and managed infrastructure reducing operational burden; primary gaps are undocumented AI governance, no formal security testing program, and limited explainability features for a platform serving AI applications.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Pinecone Vector Database\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Semantic search, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), recommendation systems, and AI application development requiring high-dimensional vector storage and querying\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise AI/ML teams across financial services, healthcare, technology, e-commerce, and other sectors building AI-powered applications\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-native SaaS (fully managed, serverless)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** AWS, GCP, Azure (multi-cloud support with regional deployment options)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Scalable from development to enterprise production workloads; serverless architecture eliminates infrastructure management\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal third-party security or AI safety testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count and deployment metrics not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Pinecone is a fully managed, serverless vector database enabling fast, scalable semantic search and RAG without infrastructure management. The platform stores and queries high-dimensional vector embeddings across AWS, GCP, and Azure regions. Key differentiators include serverless architecture (claimed 50x cost reduction vs. pod-based alternatives), multi-cloud deployment, and HIPAA/GDPR compliance; however, limited explainability features and undocumented AI governance create transparency gaps for regulated use cases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Pinecone Systems\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Infrastructure / Database)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2019\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: New York, New York, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Multi-region cloud deployment (AWS, GCP, Azure); primary operating region USA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Vector database platform; does not train proprietary AI models. Integrates third-party embedding models (e.g., OpenAI, Hugging Face) for semantic search and RAG\\n- **Model Purpose:** Storage, indexing, and retrieval of high-dimensional vector embeddings; enables semantic understanding and recommendation without training custom models\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; vendor relies on third-party model governance. No staged deployment or safety framework documented for the platform itself\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; platform provides API-level access without documented human-in-the-loop controls or intervention mechanisms\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate; some explainability features present but not detailed. Limited transparency into vector similarity scoring and retrieval ranking\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data provenance and documentation unknown. Vendor does not train proprietary models, reducing direct responsibility but limiting transparency\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias detection, red team testing, or third-party audits documented. Bias responsibility deferred to upstream embedding model providers\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal penetration testing program documented; incident response plan exists but not tested\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no published AI ethics or safety guidelines specific to vector database operations\\n- **Bias Audits:** No formal bias audits or external evaluations conducted; vendor does not audit third-party embedding models integrated into platform\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not documented; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows specified\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for AI safety impact assessment\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested. Maturity level and testing frequency unknown\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** High-dimensional vector embeddings (numerical data); metadata and customer application data stored in indexes\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for training/model improvement unknown\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based ingestion; chat interface and telemetry collection method not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-native infrastructure (AWS, GCP, Azure); encryption method (in-transit and at-rest) not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; specific default retention periods and zero-retention options not detailed\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Multi-region deployment available (AWS, GCP, Azure); customer choice of region supported; specific residency guarantees not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion supported; automated deletion policies not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** AWS, GCP, Azure (infrastructure); third-party embedding model providers (OpenAI, Hugging Face, etc.); payment and authentication providers not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, CCPA\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope unknown\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA, GDPR, CCPA compliance claimed; NIST and EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HIPAA certification held; BAA (Business Associate Agreement) eligibility presumed but not explicitly confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification held; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented; no engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date and findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (contractual commitment)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, rollback procedures, and readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** AWS, GCP, Azure (cloud infrastructure); third-party embedding model providers (OpenAI, Hugging Face, etc.)\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Cloud provider SLAs inherited (AWS, GCP, Azure standard SLAs); third-party model provider SLAs not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results or policy documentation uploaded; incident response plan documented but not tested\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Scoring Methodology & Rationale\\n\\n### Formula Applied\\nUsing **Assessment Type 1: Vendor Self-Attestation** framework from vector database guidance:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n### Component Calculations\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 65 (moderate; vector database is infrastructure, not autonomous AI; third-party model dependency reduces direct risk but increases opacity)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.65 (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA/GDPR certifications provide controls; but no formal AI safety testing, bias audits, or explainability documentation)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.75 (certifications present; no third-party AI safety audit)\\n- **Product Risk = 65 × (1 − 0.65) × 0.75 = 17.1 ≈ 17**\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 40 points (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, CCPA present; no EU AI Act or NIST documentation)\\n- Assessment Quality: 15 points (audit frequency and scope not disclosed; no third-party AI safety audit)\\n- Policies: 20 points (incident response documented but not tested; no published AI ethics or governance policy)\\n- Operational Controls: 25 points (automated rollback, multi-region deployment; no formal change management or release cadence documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10 points (Series B/C, 201–1,000 employees; growth-stage, not yet established)\\n- **Governance Score = 40 + 15 + 20 + 25 + 10 = 110 → capped at 100**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 − 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.95% uptime; strong but not 99.99%)\\n- Incident Management: 15 points (documented but not tested; maturity unknown)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 20 points (serverless, multi-cloud; production-ready but growth-stage)\\n- Stability: 15 points (founded 2019, 5 years old; profitable status unknown; Series B/C indicates ongoing funding)\\n- Support: 10 points (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 dedicated support documented)\\n- **Operational Score = 25 + 15 + 20 + 15 + 10 = 85**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 − 85 = 15**\\n\\n**Final Vendor Trust Score:**\\n- VTS = 100 − [(17 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (15 × 0.30)]\\n- VTS = 100 − [6.8 + 0 + 4.5]\\n- VTS = 100 − 11.3\\n- **VTS = 88.7 ≈ 89**\\n\\n### Adjustment for AI Governance Gaps\\nThe formula-derived score of 89 is adjusted downward to **72** to reflect:\\n- **No formal AI governance policy** (critical gap for AI platform)\\n- **No bias detection or adversarial testing** (third-party model risk not managed)\\n- **No explainability documentation** (opacity risk for RAG/semantic search use cases)\\n- **Untested incident response** (operational risk not validated)\\n- **Growth-stage maturity** (Series B/C; limited track record vs. established vendors)\\n\\nThis adjustment aligns with the **\\"Acceptable Vendor\\" (70–79 range)** classification, reflecting moderate capabilities with notable governance and transparency gaps requiring enhanced due diligence before production deployment in regulated industries.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Strong compliance posture:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, CCPA certifications demonstrate security and privacy controls\\n2. **Reliable operations:** 99.95% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability support production stability\\n3. **Managed infrastructure:** Serverless architecture reduces operational burden and infrastructure risk for customers\\n4. **Multi-cloud deployment:** AWS, GCP, Azure support provides flexibility and reduces vendor lock-in\\n\\n### Gaps Requiring Mitigation\\n1. **AI governance documentation:** Publish formal AI ethics policy, governance framework, and third-party model vetting process\\n2. **Bias and safety testing:** Conduct formal bias audits of integrated embedding models; document red team testing and adversarial security testing results\\n3. **Explainability:** Document vector similarity scoring, retrieval ranking, and provide transparency into model behavior for RAG use cases\\n4. **Support SLAs:** Define P1/P2/P3 response time targets and escalation procedures\\n5. **Audit transparency:** Disclose audit frequency, last audit date, and audit findings (within confidentiality constraints)\\n6. **Incident response validation:** Test incident response plan and document results\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT**\\n\\nPinecone is suitable for **non-regulated, general-purpose AI application development** (e.g., semantic search, recommendation systems, internal RAG). For **regulated industries (healthcare, financial services, government)**, require:\\n- Executed BAA (HIPAA) and DPA (GDPR) before deployment\\n- Formal written commitment to bias audits and explainability documentation\\n- Extended pilot (3–6 months) with monitoring and audit log review\\n- Dedicated technical account manager and enterprise SLA negotiation\\n- Quarterly governance and security review checkpoints\\n\\n**Timeline:** 6–9 months for regulated use cases (vs. 2–3 months for general-purpose deployment)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Classification:** Acceptable Vendor (Score: 72/100)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Pinecone Vector Database", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count and deployment metrics not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Enterprise AI/ML teams across financial services, healthcare, technology, e-commerce, and other sectors building AI-powered applications", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-native SaaS (fully managed, serverless)", "Deployment Scale": "Scalable from development to enterprise production workloads; serverless architecture eliminates infrastructure management", "Primary Use Case": "Semantic search, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), recommendation systems, and AI application development requiring high-dimensional vector storage and querying", "Hosted / Deployed": "AWS, GCP, Azure (multi-cloud support with regional deployment options)", "Product Description": "Pinecone is a fully managed, serverless vector database enabling fast, scalable semantic search and RAG without infrastructure management. The platform stores and queries high-dimensional vector embeddings across AWS, GCP, and Azure regions. Key differentiators include serverless architecture (claimed 50x cost reduction vs. pod-based alternatives), multi-cloud deployment, and HIPAA/GDPR compliance; however, limited explainability features and undocumented AI governance create transparency gaps for regulated use cases.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal third-party security or AI safety testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Pinecone Systems", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider (Infrastructure / Database)", "Ye