c5185e56-c897-47d9-91fe-52cea50be6a5	10	10	01d9b26f-a8fa-43ed-8101-f50017eeb36b	92	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Moveworks AI Assistant\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 72\\n- Company Maturity: 80\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nMoveworks demonstrates solid enterprise-grade compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001 family, ISO 42001) and strong company maturity as an established vendor acquired by ServiceNow. However, the Trust Score reflects meaningful gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and formal safety testing that are critical for autonomous workplace AI handling sensitive employee data. The vendor's proprietary/closed model approach and lack of documented bias testing or adversarial security testing create residual product risk despite strong operational and governance certifications. Strengths include robust security certifications and acquisition by a mature enterprise software leader; primary gaps are AI transparency, formal testing evidence, and human-oversight documentation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Moveworks AI Assistant\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Autonomous resolution of employee workplace requests (IT help-desk tickets, HR inquiries, finance requests, facilities management) across enterprise communication and ticketing platforms.\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (all sectors); primary use cases in IT operations, HR service delivery, and finance operations.\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted); integrates with existing enterprise tools (Slack, Microsoft Teams, ServiceNow).\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted SaaS; on-premises deployment options not specified.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale; typical deployments serve 1,000+ employees per customer.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years); no formal testing results documented.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not disclosed); case studies reference significant L1 help-desk time savings (40% agent capacity freed, 1,000 hours/year per customer).\\n- **Product Description:** Moveworks is an enterprise-grade conversational AI assistant that autonomously resolves employee workplace requests using natural language understanding and machine learning. The system integrates into existing workplace tools (Slack, Teams, ServiceNow) to handle IT, HR, finance, and facilities requests without manual escalation. The product is now part of ServiceNow's portfolio following acquisition in December 2025, providing enterprise-grade security (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001 family) and compliance infrastructure.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Moveworks, Inc. (acquired by ServiceNow, December 2025)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (Enterprise SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Established / Profitable 3+ years (Series D+ prior to acquisition); current revenue not disclosed.\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Acquired by ServiceNow (December 2025); Headquarters: Mountain View, California, USA.\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; assumed US-based with potential global reach via ServiceNow infrastructure post-acquisition.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/Closed; specific model architecture (LLM, custom-trained NLP, or hybrid) not disclosed.\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding, machine learning, and automation for employee request classification, routing, and autonomous resolution across IT, HR, finance, and facilities domains.\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment framework, safety gates, or model versioning policy specified.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; autonomous decision-making capability implied (resolves requests without manual escalation), but admin controls, content filtering, and intervention workflows not documented.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability documentation available.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools specified.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; incident response plan documented but not tested.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework specified.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations documented; no frequency or audit schedule provided.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not documented; no admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows specified despite autonomous decision-making capability.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation available; no formal impact assessment process specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency not specified.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; rollback testing and validation procedures not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Employee workplace requests (IT tickets, HR inquiries, finance requests, facilities requests); communication data (Slack, Teams messages); potentially PII and sensitive employee information.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed.\\n- **Data Collection:** API integration with Slack, Microsoft Teams, ServiceNow; chat interface interaction; collection scope and granularity not specified.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards not documented.\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period and zero-retention options not specified.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice for data residency not documented.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied via privacy policy); automated deletion procedures not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payment processors, authentication providers, and third-party vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2\\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security Controls)\\n  - ISO 27018 (PII Protection in Cloud)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management System)\\n  - CSA STAR Level 2\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit scope, frequency, and most recent audit date not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management System) indicates AI governance framework alignment.\\n  - NIST, GDPR, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness: Not specified.\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not documented.\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability not documented.\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; engagement or preparation status not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit schedule and findings not available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; contractual uptime commitment not documented.\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response targets by severity not documented.\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, and deployment validation procedures not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** \\n  - Infrastructure: Not specified (assumed AWS/Azure/GCP via ServiceNow post-acquisition, but not confirmed).\\n  - Payments: Not specified.\\n  - Authentication: Not specified.\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments of sub-processors not documented.\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure and service vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified.\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified.\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** \\n  - Security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001 family, ISO 42001, CSA STAR Level 2) available.\\n  - AI governance policy, training data documentation, bias testing results, and formal safety testing: **Not available**.\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Strong Compliance Posture:** Comprehensive security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001 family, ISO 42001, CSA STAR Level 2) demonstrate enterprise-grade security and AI governance framework alignment.\\n2. **Established Vendor Maturity:** Founded 2016, profitable 3+ years, acquired by ServiceNow (December 2025); strong operational stability and access to enterprise infrastructure.\\n3. **Clear Enterprise Value:** Documented ROI (40% L1 help-desk capacity savings, 1,000 hours/year per customer) and integration with widely-used workplace tools (Slack, Teams, ServiceNow).\\n\\n### Key Gaps & Residual Risks\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency (Critical):** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, or formal safety testing; proprietary/closed model limits explainability and audit capability.\\n2. **Training Data Documentation (Critical):** No disclosure of training data sources, composition, or curation practices; unclear whether customer data is used for model training.\\n3. **Human Oversight & Autonomy (High):** Autonomous decision-making capability not paired with documented human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows; risk of uncontrolled autonomous actions on sensitive employee data.\\n4. **Operational SLAs (High):** Uptime SLA, support response SLAs, and change management procedures not specified; difficult to assess operational reliability commitments.\\n5. **Data Practices Transparency (High):** PII handling extent, data residency options, default retention periods, and sub-processor disclosure not available; creates compliance and privacy risk for regulated industries.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED**\\n\\nMoveworks is acceptable for enterprise deployment **IF** the following conditions are met before contract execution:\\n\\n#### Must-Fix (Before Proceeding)\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety Documentation:**\\n   - Provide documented AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, and formal safety testing results (or commit to third-party audit within 90 days of deployment).\\n   - Disclose training data sources, composition, and whether customer data is used for model training.\\n   - Document human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, and escalation workflows for autonomous decisions.\\n\\n2. **Operational SLAs:**\\n   - Define contractual uptime SLA (recommend 99.5% minimum for enterprise IT operations).\\n   - Specify support response SLAs by severity (P1/P2/P3).\\n   - Document change management process, release cadence, and rollback validation procedures.\\n\\n3. **Data Practices & Privacy:**\\n   - Clarify PII handling scope and whether customer data is retained for model training.\\n   - Provide data residency options (US, EU, customer choice) and default retention periods.\\n   - Disclose sub-processors (infrastructure, payments, authentication) and their SLAs.\\n   - Confirm GDPR DPA availability and HIPAA BAA eligibility (if applicable).\\n\\n#### Should-Fix (Reduces Residual Risk)\\n4. **Formal Testing & Audit:**\\n   - Commit to annual third-party bias audit and adversarial security testing.\\n   - Provide model card or system card documenting model capabilities, limitations, and known risks.\\n\\n5. **Incident Response & Rollback:**\\n   - Test incident response plan and document results.\\n   - Validate automated rollback capability with documented test cases.\\n\\n### Risk Classification\\n- **Product Risk:** 28/100 (Moderate-High) — Autonomous AI with limited transparency and untested safety controls.\\n- **Governance Risk:** 18/100 (Low) — Strong certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 42001) but gaps in AI ethics documentation.\\n- **Operational Risk:** 28/100 (Moderate) — Established vendor with acquisition backing, but SLAs and change management not specified.\\n\\n**Estimated Trust Score (Post-Remediation):** 78–82 (Trusted Vendor) if conditions are met.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Framework:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Methodology (VTS = 100 − [Product Risk × 0.40 + Governance Risk × 0.30 + Operational Risk × 0.30])", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Moveworks AI Assistant", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer co