weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (21.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (3.1) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (79.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\\n       - Complete Uptime / SLA in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation"}	2026-07-28 14:04:25.159381+05:30	** Moveworks demonstrates solid enterprise-grade compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001 family, ISO 42001) and strong company maturity as an established vendor acquired by ServiceNow. However, the Trust Score reflects meaningful gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and formal safety testing that are critical for autonomous workplace AI handling sensitive employee data. The vendor's proprietary/closed model approach and lack of documented bias testing or adversarial security testing create residual product risk despite strong operational and governance certifications. Strengths include robust security certifications and acquisition by a mature enterprise software leader; primary gaps are AI transparency, formal testing evidence, and human-oversight documentation. ---	3.136	0	21	7.5544	A	Exceptional Vendor	{"llm": {"error": null, "label": "Exceptional Vendor", "summary": "** Moveworks demonstrates solid enterprise-grade compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001 family, ISO 42001) and strong company maturity as an established vendor acquired by ServiceNow. However, the Trust Score reflects meaningful gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and formal safety testing that are critical for autonomous workplace AI hand