e Data residency in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
c5500cd6-3263-4e12-a626-149ccf3f227e	14	14	8c408ab9-df5b-4e16-803c-25f39a0188be	94	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Dataiku Enterprise AI Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 82\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDataiku demonstrates solid foundational trust through established company maturity (13 years, Series D+, profitable), strong security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001/27701), and documented incident response capability. However, the vendor exhibits notable gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing, no training data documentation) and operational clarity (SLAs not specified, support response times undefined, release cadence not documented). The score of 72 reflects an \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" classification per the rubric (70–79 range): moderate capabilities with some governance and operational gaps that require enhanced due diligence and contractual clarity before deployment in regulated or high-stakes environments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Dataiku (The Enterprise AI Platform)\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise analytics, machine learning operationalization, generative/agentic AI deployment, data preparation through model lifecycle management\\n- **Target Industry:** Cross-industry (financial services, healthcare, technology, manufacturing, retail)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (AWS, Azure, GCP supported); on-premises options available\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** SaaS and self-hosted deployment options\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise multi-tenant (typical deployment: 50–500+ users per organization)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; used by established enterprises\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not publicly disclosed (enterprise customer base implied)\\n- **Product Description:** Dataiku is a unified enterprise AI platform that consolidates analytics, machine learning, and generative/agentic AI capabilities into a single governed system. It provides both visual and code-based interfaces to serve technical and business users across the full AI lifecycle—from data preparation through model deployment and agent orchestration. The platform emphasizes governance controls embedded across all stages, enabling organizations to operationalize AI at scale while maintaining compliance and transparency.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Dataiku (registered entity: Dataiku SAS / Dataiku Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (unified analytics, ML, and generative AI)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2013\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: New York, New York, USA; investors include Sapphire Ventures, Bessemer Venture Partners, and others (Series D+)\\n- **Operating Regions:** North America, Europe, Asia-Pacific (global operations)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** LLM integration (generative AI), custom-trained ML models (supervised/unsupervised), NLP, time-series forecasting, classification, regression\\n- **Model Purpose:** Data understanding, feature engineering, model training, generative text/code generation, agentic AI orchestration, predictive analytics\\n- **Model Governance:** Governance embedded across the platform lifecycle; staged deployment supported through project/environment controls; no formal documented AI governance policy provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Visual workflow builder with human-in-the-loop capability; model monitoring and alerts available; audit logs present; autonomous agent orchestration with governance guardrails (specifics not detailed)\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** High model transparency (feature importance, confidence scores reported); model cards and documentation available within platform; explainability level: feature-level and prediction-level insights\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; vendor does not provide public training data provenance or composition details for embedded models\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits or third-party bias evaluations reported\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy provided; governance controls embedded in platform (content filtering, model monitoring) but formal ethics framework not disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** No formal bias audit program documented; no external bias evaluation or audit frequency specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Visual workflow builder enables human review of model decisions; model monitoring and alerting available; audit logs support intervention and review; specific intervention workflows not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or formal impact assessment documentation provided; release notes available but no pre-release impact assessments disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented; however, not tested or validated through tabletop exercises or third-party assessment\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated rollback with manual trigger option; deployment rollback supported; specifics on rollback testing frequency not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Structured data (databases, data warehouses), unstructured data (documents, images), code, communications, time-series data, logs\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII handling not specified; no explicit statement on whether customer data is used for training or model improvement\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based integration, web interface, file upload; telemetry collection (basic metrics available)\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud infrastructure (AWS, Azure, GCP) with encryption in transit and at rest (standard); on-premises storage option available\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; no explicit zero-retention or data minimization option documented\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of cloud region (US, EU, APAC); on-premises deployment available for data residency control\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion supported; automated deletion policies not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Cloud infrastructure providers (AWS, Azure, GCP); authentication providers; payment processors (not detailed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 1 Type 2, SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, ISO 9001\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted by external auditor (annual or biennial, frequency not specified); ISO certifications maintained through external certification bodies\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST alignment implied through ISO 27001; GDPR compliance framework in place (ISO 27701 privacy extension); CCPA compliance not explicitly stated; EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligibility not explicitly stated; healthcare use cases supported but HIPAA certification not confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA (Data Processing Agreement) available; ISO 27701 certification indicates privacy-by-design; GDPR compliance framework in place\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No formal engagement or preparation statement provided; governance controls present but EU AI Act alignment not documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment disclosed\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response times by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Release cadence not specified; rollback/readiness practices include automated rollback with manual trigger; formal change management process not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Cloud infrastructure providers (AWS, Azure, GCP); authentication and identity providers; payment processors\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified; vendor SLAs inherited from cloud providers (AWS, Azure, GCP standard SLAs)\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Dependent on selected cloud provider SLAs; no Dataiku-specific vendor SLA commitments documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; telemetry scope limited to usage analytics (not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; SIEM export capability not explicitly confirmed; audit log retention and export format not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Incident response plan documented but not tested; no formal security testing results provided; no policy documentation uploaded\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Strengths\\n\\n1. **Established Company Maturity:** 13-year-old company, Series D+ funded, profitable for 3+ years; strong market presence and stability\\n2. **Strong Security Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, ISO 9001 demonstrate security and privacy controls\\n3. **High Model Transparency:** Feature importance and confidence scores provide explainability; visual workflow builder enables human oversight\\n4. **Flexible Deployment:** Multi-cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP) and on-premises options support diverse data residency requirements\\n5. **Governance-First Architecture:** Governance controls embedded across the AI lifecycle; audit logs and monitoring available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Gaps & Risks\\n\\n1. **Undocumented AI Governance Policy:** No formal AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, or training data documentation; governance controls present but not formally articulated\\n2. **Operational Clarity Gaps:** Uptime SLA, support response SLAs, and release cadence not specified; limits contractual clarity for enterprise deployments\\n3. **No Formal AI Safety Testing:** No bias audits, red-team assessments, or adversarial testing documented; incident response plan not tested\\n4. **PII and Training Data Transparency:** No explicit statement on customer data usage for model training; PII handling extent not specified\\n5. **EU AI Act Readiness Unknown:** No documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance; governance controls present but regulatory alignment not confirmed\\n6. **Limited Audit Transparency:** Audit frequency, last audit date, and findings not disclosed; limits buyer confidence in control effectiveness\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recommended Actions for Procurement\\n\\n1. **Require Contractual SLA Clarity:** Negotiate explicit uptime SLA (e.g., 99.9% or 99.95%), support response SLAs by severity (P1/P2/P3), and change management process documentation\\n2. **Request AI Governance Documentation:** Obtain formal AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, training data documentation, and model card templates\\n3. **Validate Incident Response:** Request tabletop exercise results or third-party incident response assessment; confirm rollback testing frequency\\n4. **Clarify Data Practices:** Obtain explicit statement on customer data usage (no training/improvement without consent), PII handling procedures, and data retention options\\n5. **Assess Regulatory Readiness:** Confirm HIPAA BAA eligibility if healthcare use case; request EU AI Act readiness assessment and timeline\\n6. **Audit Transparency:** Request most recent SOC 2 Type 2 audit report (executive summary), audit frequency, and any open findings\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Classification & Recommendation\\n\\n**Grade: C (Acceptable Vendor)**  \\n**Recommended Action:** Standard procurement process with enhanced due diligence on AI governance, operational SLAs, and data practices.\\n\\n**Conditional Approval:** Proceed with Dataiku for non-regulated, moderate-risk AI use cases (e.g., internal analytics, business intelligence, non-critical ML). For regulated industries (healthcare, financial services) or high-stakes deployments (autonomous decision-making, customer-facing AI), require gap remediation on AI governance documentation, formal bias testing, and regulatory compliance confirmation before contract signature.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Dataiku (The Enterprise AI Platform)", "Customer Base": "Not publicly disclosed (enterprise customer base implied)", "Target Industry": "Cross-industry (financial services, healthcare, technology, manufacturing, retail)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (AWS, Azure, GCP supported); on-premises options available", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise multi-tenant (typical deployment: 50–500+ users per organization)", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise analytics, machine learning operationalization, generative/agentic AI deployment, data preparation through model lifecycle management", "Hosted / Deployed": "SaaS and self-hosted deployment options", "Product Description": "Dataiku is a unified enterprise AI platform that consolidates analytics, machine learning, and generative/agentic AI capabilities into a single governed system. It provides both visual and code-based interfaces to serve technical and business users across the full AI lifecycle—from data preparation through model deployment and agent orchestration. The platform emphasizes governance controls embedded across all stages, enabling organizations to operationalize AI at scale while maintaining compliance and transparency.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready; used by established enterprises"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Dataiku (registered entity: Dataiku SAS / Dataiku Inc.)", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider (unified analytics, ML, and generative AI)", "Year Founded": "2013", "Operating Regions": "North America, Europe, Asia-Pacific (global operations)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: New York, New York, USA; investors include Sapphire Ventures, Bessemer Venture Partners, and others (Series D+)", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "LLM integration (generative AI), custom-trained ML models (supervised/unsupervised), NLP, time-series forecasting, classification, regression", "Model Purpose": "Data understanding, feature engineering, model training, generative text/code generation, agentic AI orchestration, predictive analytics", "Human Oversight": "Visual workflow builder with human-in-the-loop capability; model monitoring and alerts available; audit logs present; autonomous agent orchestration with governance guardrails (specifics not detailed)", "Model Governance": "Governance embedded across the platform lifecycle; staged deployment supported through project/environment controls; no formal documented AI governance policy provided", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "High model transparency (feature importance, confidence scores reported); model cards and documentation available wi