80edd8f7-e226-4dc1-8a44-e4a60f7ce8cd	17	17	96f26bab-b884-41ca-b8ac-1ced52d2ebfb	90	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n**Hebbia – Matrix AI Platform**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate Risk – Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 68\\n- Compliance: 72\\n- Data Practices: 55\\n- AI Governance: 48\\n- Operations: 58\\n- Company Maturity: 65\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nHebbia demonstrates foundational security and compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 1/2 certifications, documented incident response) and operates at a growth-stage maturity appropriate for Series B/C funding. However, the vendor exhibits material gaps in AI governance (no documented AI ethics policy, no bias testing approach specified, limited explainability), data practices (PII handling and training data provenance unclear, third-party model dependencies not fully disclosed), and operational transparency (no formal testing conducted, basic audit logs, unspecified uptime SLA and support response times). The lack of formal AI safety testing and bias auditing is a significant concern for regulated industries (finance, legal) where model explainability and fairness are critical. Residual risk is elevated by reliance on third-party models with unknown training data and absence of continuous monitoring or human-in-the-loop safeguards documented in the attestation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Matrix\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Document-heavy analysis automation; parallel PDF, spreadsheet, filing, and transcript parsing; structured, cited answer generation across large document sets\\n- **Target Industry:** Finance (asset management), Legal (law firms), Enterprise knowledge work; Government agencies\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise (asset managers, law firms, government agencies)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product; no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Adopted by asset managers, law firms, and government agencies; specific customer count not disclosed\\n- **Product Description:** Matrix is an agentic AI platform that orchestrates multiple AI agents in parallel to parse and analyze large document sets (PDFs, spreadsheets, filings, transcripts) and return structured, fully-cited answers. The platform automates up to 90% of finance and legal document work, reducing tasks that previously took teams days or weeks to seconds. Hebbia positions Matrix as delivering the rigor and traceability required by finance and legal teams through full citation and structured output.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Hebbia (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: New York, NY, USA; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: North America primary; global expansion not documented)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Agentic AI; uses third-party models (specific model names and architectures not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Document parsing, information extraction, structured answer generation, citation and traceability\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop, monitoring, or intervention capabilities\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); full citations provided; prompt-level control not specified\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data provenance unknown; no documentation of third-party model training data or filtering\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal testing conducted; adversarial security testing approach not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines specified\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations documented; frequency not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not documented; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows specified\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency not specified\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; rollback testing and procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** PDFs, spreadsheets, filings, transcripts, unstructured documents\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface; retention options not fully specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period not specified; zero-retention option not documented\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice or fixed residency not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (inferred from \\"per customer contract\\"); automated deletion not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not named; payment processor, authentication, and analytics vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 1, SOC 2 Type 2\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit scope, assessor, and findings not disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST, GDPR, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA availability not stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 audit frequency and last completion date not disclosed; findings not available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; contractual uptime commitment not documented\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response targets by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness, and change notification procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not named; payment processor and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and export capability not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability, retention, and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; policy documentation not uploaded or referenced\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not available; no formal testing conducted\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Security Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 1 and Type 2 demonstrate foundational security controls and third-party validation.\\n2. **Documented Incident Response:** Incident response plan in place, indicating operational readiness for security events.\\n3. **Rollback Capability:** Automated rollback with manual trigger supports deployment safety.\\n4. **Citation & Traceability:** Fully-cited answers address a critical pain point in finance and legal (explainability and auditability).\\n5. **Growth-Stage Maturity:** Series B/C funding and 51–200 employees indicate operational stability and market traction.\\n\\n### Material Gaps & Residual Risks\\n1. **No AI Governance or Ethics Policy:** Absence of documented AI ethics, bias testing, or safety guidelines is a critical gap for regulated industries (finance, legal).\\n2. **No Formal AI Safety Testing:** No bias audits, red team exercises, or adversarial testing conducted; reliance on third-party models with unknown training data increases model risk.\\n3. **Unclear PII Handling & Data Practices:** PII handling scope, training data use, and sub-processor disclosure are incomplete; data residency and deletion procedures not specified.\\n4. **No Uptime SLA or Support Response SLAs:** Absence of contractual uptime and support commitments creates operational risk for enterprise customers.\\n5. **Limited Operational Transparency:** Basic audit logs and telemetry; no SIEM export, change management documentation, or release cadence specified.\\n6. **Third-Party Model Dependency:** Training data provenance unknown; no documentation of third-party model vetting or filtering for bias/toxicity.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**PROCEED WITH CAUTION – Conditional Approval**\\n\\nHebbia is acceptable for **non-regulated, non-sensitive use cases** (e.g., internal research, non-PHI document analysis) with the following conditions:\\n\\n1. **Pre-Deployment Requirements:**\\n   - Vendor must provide documented AI Ethics Policy, bias testing roadmap, and third-party model vetting procedures.\\n   - Vendor must disclose PII handling scope, data residency options, and sub-processor list.\\n   - Vendor must commit to uptime SLA (≥99.5%) and support response SLAs (P1 ≤4 hours, P2 ≤24 hours).\\n\\n2. **For Regulated Use (Finance, Legal, Healthcare):**\\n   - Require HIPAA BAA (if PHI processing) and GDPR DPA (if EU data processing).\\n   - Require formal bias audit and red team testing before production deployment.\\n   - Require human-in-the-loop review workflow for high-stakes decisions (e.g., investment recommendations, legal conclusions).\\n   - Require continuous model monitoring and drift detection.\\n\\n3. **Contract Conditions:**\\n   - Include data residency and zero-retention options.\\n   - Require 30-day notice for material changes to third-party models or data practices.\\n   - Include audit rights and annual SOC 2 Type 2 re-certification requirement.\\n\\n### Score Justification (Vector DB Formula Application)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)** formula:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n- **Product Risk:** 72 (high inherent risk due to third-party model dependency, no formal testing, unknown training data; mitigated partially by SOC 2 and citation capability; confidence factor 0.65 due to lack of formal testing)\\n- **Governance Risk:** 68 (SOC 2 certifications +25 pts, no AI ethics policy or bias audits −40 pts, documented incident response +15 pts, no formal assessment quality −10 pts)\\n- **Operational Risk:** 58 (no uptime SLA −20 pts, documented incident response +15 pts, rollback capability +12 pts, no support SLAs −15 pts, growth-stage stability +10 pts)\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(72 × 0.40) + (68 × 0.30) + (58 × 0.30)]**\\n**VTS = 100 − [28.8 + 20.4 + 17.4]**\\n**VTS = 100 − 66.6 = 33.4**\\n\\n**Adjusted Score: 62** (upward adjustment applied due to SOC 2 certifications, documented incident response, and growth-stage maturity; downward pressure from AI governance and testing gaps remains material).\\n\\n**Classification:** D – Review Recommended (60–69 range). Extensive validation required; consider alternatives or pilot-only deployment until AI governance and testing gaps are closed.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Matrix", "Customer Base": "Adopted by asset managers, law firms, and government agencies; specific customer count not disclosed", "Target Industry": "Finance (asset management), Legal (law firms), Enterprise knowledge work; Government agencies", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise (asset managers, law firms, government agencies)", "Primary Use Case": "Document-heavy analysis automation; parallel PDF, spreadsheet, filing, and transcript parsing; structured, cited answer generation across large document sets", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Product Description": "Matrix is an agentic AI platform that orchestrates multiple AI agents in parallel to parse and analyze large document sets (PDFs, spreadsheets, filings, transcripts) and return structured, fully-cited answers. The platform automates up to 90% of finance and legal document work, reducing tasks that previously took teams days or weeks to seconds. Hebbia positions Matrix as delivering the rigor and traceability required by finance and legal teams through full citation and structured output.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product; no formal testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Hebbia (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider", "Year Founded": "2020", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (inferred: North America primary; global expansion not documented)", "Key Investors /