iles": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.4542}, "Data Governance & Privacy Controls": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.4202}}, "attestation_similarities": {"Human Oversight Mechanisms": 0.3475, "Model Security & Integrity": 0.4737, "Post-Deployment Monitoring": 0.4399, "Incident Response & Recovery": 0.4218, "Transparency & Documentation": 0.4693, "Testing & Auditing Procedures": 0.5674, "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence": 0.5115, "Access Management & Authentication": 0.4747, "Data Governance & Privacy Controls": 0.4738}}, "from_vector": ["Data Governance & Privacy Controls", "Model Security & Integrity", "Access Management & Authentication", "Testing & Auditing Procedures", "Post-Deployment Monitoring", "Incident Response & Recovery", "Transparency & Documentation", "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence"], "coverage_ratio": 0.8889, "required_count": 9, "from_attestation": ["Data Governance & Privacy Controls", "Model Security & Integrity", "Access Management & Authentication", "Post-Deployment Monitoring", "Incident Response & Recovery", "Transparency & Documentation", "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence"], "implemented_count": 8, "evidence_blob_chars": 303}}	vts-formula-1.0	VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\n========================================================================\n\nRESULT\n  Trust score:   91 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\n  Grade:         A - Exceptional Vendor\n  Next step:     Fast-track procurement; minimal additional due diligence\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\n\nHOW WE GOT HERE\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\n\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\n    1. Operational risk       24.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\n    2. Product risk            2.90  (weight 40%)\n    3. Governance risk         1.00  (weight 30%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (24.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Product risk (2.9) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (76.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\n       - Complete Uptime / SLA in the attestation\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
1a2cd888-9821-447d-84ed-cc302329a4e7	19	19	382a70d9-9c0b-44a2-a369-a1da98869551	90	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: RUNWAY (GEN-4)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate / Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 65\\n- Compliance: 55\\n- Data Practices: 58\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 60\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nRunway demonstrates moderate trustworthiness with established company maturity (Series E, profitable, 201–1,000 employees) and foundational security controls (SOC 2 Type 2), but significant gaps in AI governance, transparency, and compliance documentation limit enterprise readiness—particularly for regulated use cases. The vendor lacks documented AI governance policies, formal bias testing, training data documentation, and comprehensive compliance frameworks (no HIPAA BAA, GDPR DPA, or EU AI Act readiness stated). While the company is operationally mature and incident response is documented, the absence of formal AI safety testing, explainability controls, and human-in-the-loop mechanisms, combined with proprietary/closed model transparency, places this vendor in the \\"Review Recommended\\" category (60–69 range per VTS rubric). Strengths include SOC 2 Type 2 certification and automated rollback capability; primary gaps are AI governance maturity, bias auditing, and regulatory compliance readiness for high-stakes deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Runway (Gen-4)\\n- **Version:** Gen-4 (latest generation video model)\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Generative video creation and editing; text-to-video, image-to-video, and video-to-video synthesis with physics simulation and scene consistency.\\n- **Target Industry:** Creative studios, filmmaking, enterprise content production, marketing, VFX.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted via Runway platform; API access available for enterprise integrations.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise and individual creator scale; typical deployments range from single-user creative workflows to multi-user studio environments.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; Gen-4 is the latest released model with active user base.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor (not publicly disclosed in attestation data).\\n- **Customer Base:** Filmmakers, creative studios, enterprises; specific customer count or revenue metrics not disclosed.\\n- **Product Description:** Runway Gen-4 is a state-of-the-art generative video model enabling creators to produce and edit cinematic video from text, image, or video prompts. The model simulates real-world physics and maintains scene consistency, reducing production time and cost. Deployed as a cloud SaaS platform with SOC 2 Type 2 security certification; however, the model operates as a proprietary/closed system with limited transparency into training data, bias controls, or governance frameworks.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Runway (legal entity not specified; operating as Runway ML)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2018\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series E funding round at $5.3B valuation; vendor maturity classified as Established (Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years).\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters in New York, NY, USA; Series E valuation $5.3B (specific investors not listed in attestation).\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to be global via cloud SaaS platform.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary generative video model (Gen-4); closed-source architecture.\\n- **Model Purpose:** Video generation and editing; text-to-video synthesis, image-to-video synthesis, video-to-video editing, physics simulation, scene consistency maintenance.\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment framework, safety gates, or governance policy stated.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of advisory controls, autonomous decision gates, monitoring dashboards, or audit logs for model outputs.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control documentation, citation mechanisms, or explainability framework disclosed. Users cannot inspect model reasoning or training data sources.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified; inferred to be periodic based on Gen-series versioning (Gen-1 through Gen-4 released over product lifecycle).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; vendor does not disclose training data sources, composition, or curation methodology.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing not specified; no frequency or scope of penetration testing disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit program, frequency, or external evaluation methodology stated.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, admin intervention mechanisms, or approval workflows documented.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release impact documentation provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; formal incident response procedures exist but lack evidence of tabletop exercises, simulations, or validation.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; vendor can roll back deployments automatically or via manual intervention, supporting rapid incident recovery.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Video, images, text prompts; user-generated creative content.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no disclosure of whether personally identifiable information (PII) is processed, retained, or used for model training or improvement.\\n- **Data Collection:** API and web interface (Runway platform); data collection scope and granularity not detailed.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure not specified; encryption status (in transit / at rest) not disclosed.\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; specific retention periods and defaults not provided in attestation.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no disclosure of data residency options (US, EU, customer choice, etc.).\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (inferred from \\"per customer contract\\"); automated deletion timelines not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, authentication vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2 (security and availability controls audited and validated).\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted by third-party auditor; specific audit firm, scope, and last audit date not provided.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No documented alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act frameworks stated.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** No HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement) eligibility stated; vendor does not appear to support healthcare PHI handling.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance framework documented.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement, preparation, or risk classification (unacceptable, high, limited, minimal) stated.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 audit frequency and last audit date not disclosed; audit findings not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment (e.g., 99.9%, 99.95%) disclosed.\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response time targets provided.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, or change advisory board (CAB) procedures disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication vendors not disclosed.\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no frequency or methodology for assessing critical vendor risk stated.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; no SLA commitments from critical infrastructure or service vendors provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics; vendor collects and can provide basic usage telemetry (e.g., API calls, session counts) but detailed interaction data not specified.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging; audit logs are available but export capability and SIEM integration not detailed.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; no uploaded evidence files, policy documents, or compliance artifacts provided.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no safety testing results, bias reports, or adversarial robustness evaluations available (even under NDA).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established Company Maturity:** Series E funding ($5.3B valuation), 201–1,000 employees, founded 2018, profitable 3+ years—demonstrates financial stability and operational longevity.\\n2. **SOC 2 Type 2 Certification:** Third-party validated security and availability controls; foundational for enterprise trust.\\n3. **Incident Response & Rollback:** Documented incident response plan and automated rollback capability support operational resilience.\\n4. **Production-Ready Technology:** Gen-4 model actively deployed with established user base; technology maturity is high.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **AI Governance Vacuum:** No documented AI ethics policy, governance framework, or safety guidelines; no human-in-the-loop controls or impact assessments.\\n2. **Bias & Safety Testing:** No formal bias detection, red-team audits, or adversarial testing; training data documentation absent.\\n3. **Regulatory Compliance:** No HIPAA BAA, GDPR DPA, or EU AI Act readiness; unsuitable for regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government).\\n4. **Transparency & Explainability:** Proprietary/closed model with no training data disclosure, explainability framework, or audit trail for model decisions.\\n5. **Operational SLAs:** No uptime SLA, support response SLAs, or change management documentation; enterprise operational commitments undefined.\\n\\n### Risk Classification (per VTS Rubric)\\n**Grade: D (Review Recommended, 60–69 range)**\\n- **Product Risk:** High (proprietary model, no bias testing, no training data documentation, no governance framework).\\n- **Governance Risk:** High (no AI ethics policy, no impact assessments, no compliance framework).\\n- **Operational Risk:** Moderate (SOC 2 Type 2, incident response documented but untested, no SLAs).\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n\\n**For Creative / Non-Regulated Use Cases (Low Risk):**\\n- Runway Gen-4 is acceptable for creative studios, filmmaking, and marketing content production where regulatory compliance is not required.\\n- Recommend standard procurement process with focus on data residency and retention terms in contract negotiation.\\n\\n**For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Finance, Government):**\\n- **NOT RECOMMENDED** without major remediation.\\n- Vendor must provide: HIPAA BAA, GDPR DPA, formal bias audit, training data documentation, and AI governance policy.\\n- Estimated remediation timeline: 6–12 months.\\n\\n**For Enterprise Deployments (Any Industry):**\\n- **CONDITIONAL APPROVAL** with contract requirements:\\n  1. Define uptime SLA (recommend 99.9% minimum).\\n  2. Establish support response SLAs (P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours).\\n  3. Require change management documentation and release notes for each Gen-series update.\\n  4. Negotiate data residency options (US, EU, or customer choice).\\n  5. Clarify PII handling and data retention defaults in Data Processing Agreement.\\n  6. Request SOC 2 Type 2 audit report (last audit date, scope, findings).\\n\\n**For High-Stakes AI Deployments (Autonomous Decision-Making, Content Moderation, etc.):**\\n- **DEFER** until vendor implements:\\n  - Formal bias detection and continuous monitoring.\\n  - Training data documentation and transparency framework.\\n  - Human-in-the-loop controls and audit logging.\\n  - AI governance policy and ethics review process.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation:** **APPROVED FOR CREATIVE USE CASES; CONDITIONAL FOR ENTERPRISE; DEFER FOR REGULATED INDUSTRIES**", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor (not publicly disclosed in attestation data).", "Version": "Gen-4 (latest generation video model)", "Product Name": "Runway (Gen-4)", "Customer Base": "Filmmakers, creative studios, enterprises; specific customer count or revenue metrics not disclosed.", "Target Industry": "Creative studios, filmmaking, enterprise content production, marketing, VFX.", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise and individual creator scale; typical deployments range from single-user creative workflows to multi-user studio environments.", "Primary Use Case": "Generative video creation and editing; text-to-video, image-to-video, and video-to-video synthesis with physics simulation and scene consistency.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted via Runway platform; API access available for enterprise integrations.", "Product Description": "Runway Gen-4 is a state-of-the-art generative video model enabling creators to produce and edit cinematic video from text, image, or video prompts. The model simulates real-world physics and maintains scene consistency, reducing production time and cost. Deployed as a cloud SaaS platform with SOC 2 Type 2 security certification; however, the model operates as a proprietary/closed system with limited transparency into training data, bias controls, or governance frameworks.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready; Gen-4 is the latest released model with active user base."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Runway (legal entity not specified; operating as Runway ML)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2018", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; inferred to be global via cloud SaaS platform.", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters in New York, NY, USA; Series E valuation $5.3B (specific investors not listed in attestation).", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series E funding round at $5.3B valuation; vendor maturity classified as Established (Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years)."}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary generative video model (Gen-4); closed-source architecture.", "Model Purpose": "Video generation and editing; text-to-video synthesis, image-to-video synthesis, video-to-video editing, physics simulation, scene consistency maintenance.", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no evidence of advisory controls, autonomous decision gates, monitoring dashboards, or audit logs for model outputs.", "Model Governance": "Not documented; no staged deployment framework, safety gates, or governance policy stated.", "Update Frequency": "Not specified; inferred to be periodic based on Gen-series versioning (Gen-1 through Gen-4 released over product lif