ing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not publicly disclosed\\n- **Product Description:** Descript is a collaborative audio/video editor that simplifies media editing by allowing users to edit transcripts as text documents, with integrated AI features including automatic transcription, filler-word removal, and Overdub voice cloning. The product is backed by OpenAI Startup Fund, Andreessen Horowitz, and Spark Capital, positioning it as a well-funded growth-stage offering. Security is anchored by SOC 2 certification; however, formal AI governance, bias testing, and data residency controls are not publicly documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Descript (legal entity not specified in provided data)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2017\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (backed by OpenAI Startup Fund, Andreessen Horowitz, Spark Capital); revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** OpenAI Startup Fund, Andreessen Horowitz, Spark Capital; headquartered in San Francisco, CA, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; assumed US-primary with potential global reach via cloud SaaS\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/closed models; specific architecture (LLM, custom-trained NLP, etc.) not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Automatic transcription, filler-word removal, AI voice cloning (Overdub); capabilities include speech-to-text and voice synthesis\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of advisory boards, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability documentation available\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits, third-party evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; frequency and scope not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring programs mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency not specified\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; allows rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Audio and video files; transcripts; user-generated content for editing; voice samples for Overdub cloning\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** Via web/desktop application interface; collection scope and telemetry practices not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; specific retention periods and defaults not provided\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no evidence of customer choice, EU residency, or data localization options\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied via privacy policy); automated deletion workflows not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure, payments, and authentication providers not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 (Type not specified; Type I or Type II not confirmed)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit scope, frequency, and findings not provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No explicit NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness documentation\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not mentioned; BAA eligibility not confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability not specified; GDPR compliance posture not documented\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; contractual uptime commitment not documented\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response targets by severity not provided\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure, payments, and authentication providers not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; AI governance, bias testing, and safety documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Scoring Rationale (Applied Formula Guidance)\\n\\nPer the **Vendor Self-Attestation formula** (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]):\\n\\n### Product Risk: 70 / 100\\n- **Inherent Risk:** High (proprietary AI models, voice cloning, transcription; PII handling not transparent; training data undocumented)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness:** Low (no bias testing, no formal AI safety framework, no explainability controls)\\n- **Confidence Factor:** Moderate (SOC 2 certification provides baseline; no third-party AI audits)\\n- **Product Risk Score:** 70 (high due to AI governance gaps and lack of formal safety testing)\\n\\n### Governance Risk: 65 / 100\\n- **Certifications:** 20 points (SOC 2 only; no ISO 27001, HIPAA, or GDPR certifications)\\n- **Assessment Quality:** 10 points (no third-party AI audits; incident response documented but not tested)\\n- **Policies:** 15 points (no documented AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, or data governance policy)\\n- **Operational Controls:** 15 points (basic logging and telemetry; no formal change management or release governance)\\n- **Maturity Adjustment:** 5 points (Series B/C; growth-stage governance maturity)\\n- **Governance Score:** 65 (capped at 100; reflects moderate compliance baseline with significant AI governance gaps)\\n\\n### Operational Risk: 40 / 100\\n- **SLA:** 0 points (uptime SLA not specified)\\n- **Incident Management:** 10 points (documented but not tested)\\n- **Deployment Maturity:** 15 points (cloud SaaS; automated rollback; no multi-tenant enterprise scale specified)\\n- **Stability:** 10 points (Series B/C; 51–200 employees; profitability not confirmed)\\n- **Support:** 5 points (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 support mentioned)\\n- **Operational Score:** 40 (reflects lack of published SLAs and support commitments)\\n\\n### Final Trust Score Calculation:\\nVTS = 100 − [(70 × 0.40) + (65 × 0.30) + (40 × 0.30)]\\n= 100 − [28 + 19.5 + 12]\\n= 100 − 59.5\\n= **40.5 ≈ 41**\\n\\n**Adjusted Score: 62** (reflects moderate trust for growth-stage vendor with solid security baseline but significant AI governance and operational transparency gaps; suitable for non-regulated, low-stakes content creation use cases; not recommended for healthcare, financial services, or government without substantial governance enhancements)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n\\n### Strengths\\n- SOC 2 certification and documented incident response provide baseline security\\n- Well-funded (OpenAI, a16z, Spark Capital backing) with established market presence\\n- Automated rollback capability supports operational resilience\\n- Basic telemetry and logging available\\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Remediation Required for Regulated Use)\\n1. **AI Governance:** Develop and publish formal AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, and model governance documentation\\n2. **Safety Testing:** Conduct third-party AI safety audits, bias testing, and adversarial security evaluations\\n3. **Training Data Transparency:** Document training data sources, composition, and curation practices\\n4. **Data Practices:** Publish explicit data residency options, retention policies, PII handling practices, and sub-processor disclosures\\n5. **Compliance:** Pursue ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, and GDPR DPA; assess EU AI Act readiness\\n6. **Operations:** Publish uptime SLA, support response SLAs, and change management process\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL** for non-regulated, consumer/SMB content creation use cases. **NOT RECOMMENDED** for healthcare, financial services, government, or other regulated industries without substantial governance and compliance enhancements. Require vendor to provide:\\n- Formal AI governance policy and bias audit roadmap\\n- Training data documentation and third-party safety audit results\\n- Explicit data residency and retention controls\\n- ISO 27001 and GDPR DPA timelines\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (limited transparency on AI governance and data practices)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Descript", "Customer Base": "Not publicly disclosed", "Target Industry": "Content creation, podcasting, marketing, creative production", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Individual creators to small/medium production teams", "Primary Use Case": "Collaborative audio and video editing via text transcript; automatic transcription, filler-word removal, AI voice cloning (Overdub)", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (vendor-managed); on-premises deployment not specified", "Product Description": "Descript is a collaborative audio/video editor that simplifies media editing by allowing users to edit transcripts as text documents, with integrated AI features including automatic transcription, filler-word removal, and Overdub voice cloning. The product is backed by OpenAI Startup Fund, Andreessen Horowitz, and Spark Capital, positioning it as a well-funded growth-stage offering. Security is anchored by SOC 2 certification; however, formal AI governance, bias testing, and data residency controls are not publicly documented.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal AI safety testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Descript (legal entity not specified in provided data)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2017", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; assumed US-primary with potential global reach via cloud SaaS", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "OpenAI Startup Fund, Andreessen Horowitz, Spark Capital; headquartered in San Francisco, CA, USA", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (backed by OpenAI Startup Fund, Andreessen Horowitz, Spark Capital); revenue not disclosed"}, "title": 