product; no formal third-party safety testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not publicly disclosed\\n- **Product Description:** Tabnine is an enterprise AI code assistant that differentiates on privacy and data sovereignty, offering deployment options (VPC, on-premises, air-gapped) where proprietary code never leaves the customer network. The product provides code completion, generation, and code-review/test agents with moderate explainability features. It addresses compliance and data residency concerns for organizations restricted from using public cloud AI coding tools.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Tabnine (formerly Codota)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2013\\n- **Employees:** 11–50\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); annual revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Tel Aviv, Israel; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to include North America and Europe based on GDPR compliance and enterprise customer base\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; inferred to include transformer-based code models (LLM-adjacent) for completion and generation tasks\\n- **Model Purpose:** Code understanding, code generation, code completion, code review, test generation\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no published AI safety framework or staged deployment policy\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop controls, monitoring alerts, or audit log integration mentioned\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate; some explainability features available; no prompt-level control or citation mechanisms documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available.** Significant gap: training data sources, composition, filtering, and bias mitigation are not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing or penetration testing program documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no published AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework available\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted or planned; no external evaluations mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but **not tested**; maturity level unknown; no evidence of annual testing or tabletop exercises\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; allows rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Source code, development artifacts, code review inputs, test specifications\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; unclear whether customer code (which may contain embedded credentials, API keys, or sensitive identifiers) is filtered or anonymized\\n- **Data Collection:** API and IDE plugin interfaces; collection scope not fully documented\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status (in transit and at rest) not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period not specified; zero-retention option availability not confirmed\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** **Core differentiator:** On-premises, VPC, and air-gapped deployments ensure code remains on customer infrastructure; cloud SaaS option available but data residency not specified for multi-tenant offering\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion supported; automated deletion policy not documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider(s), payment processor, and authentication services not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, GDPR compliance claimed\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted (third-party audit); audit frequency and last audit date not specified\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliance claimed; NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not mentioned; BAA eligibility unknown\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification claimed; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented; no evidence of EU AI Act compliance assessment or preparation\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** **Not published.** Critical gap for enterprise deployment; no contractual uptime commitment specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** **Not specified.** No documented support response targets by severity level\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not documented; release frequency, testing practices, and rollback readiness procedures not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider(s), payment processor, and authentication services not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not documented\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited; no formal AI safety testing results, no published AI ethics policy, no model cards or system cards\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (VTS Formula Applied)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from the vector database:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Inherent Risk: 75 (code generation + deployment autonomy + no formal safety testing = elevated inherent risk)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.50 (on-premises/air-gapped deployment mitigates data exfiltration risk; no bias testing or safety controls documented)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.70 (SOC 2 Type 2 provides some assurance; no third-party AI safety audit)\\n- **Product Risk = 75 × 0.50 × 0.70 = 26.25 ≈ 26**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n- Certifications: 20 points (SOC 2 Type 2 + GDPR; missing HIPAA, FedRAMP, EU AI Act readiness)\\n- Assessment Quality: 8 points (SOC 2 Type 2 audit = third-party review; frequency unknown; no AI safety audit)\\n- Policies: 15 points (data retention policy documented; no AI ethics policy, no incident response testing, no bias audit policy)\\n- Operational Controls: 12 points (automated rollback with manual trigger; no documented human oversight, monitoring, or version control)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 8 points (11-year company history; Series B/C funding stage = moderate maturity)\\n- **Governance Score = 20 + 8 + 15 + 12 + 8 = 63 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 63 = 37**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n- SLA: 0 points (no published uptime SLA)\\n- Incident Management: 8 points (documented but not tested)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 18 points (multi-deployment options; no published release cadence or change management process)\\n- Stability: 12 points (11-year company; Series B/C stage; profitability not confirmed)\\n- Support: 0 points (no published support SLAs)\\n- **Operational Score = 0 + 8 + 18 + 12 + 0 = 38**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 38 = 62**\\n\\n**Final VTS:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(26 × 0.40) + (37 × 0.30) + (62 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [10.4 + 11.1 + 18.6]\\n    = 100 - 40.1\\n    = 59.9 ≈ 60\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 62** based on data residency/privacy differentiator and SOC 2 Type 2 certification providing moderate confidence uplift.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CLASSIFICATION & RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Grade: D (Review Recommended)**  \\n**Score Range: 60–69**  \\n**Vendor Profile:** Significant gaps in AI governance, operational maturity, and transparency; growth-stage company with proven privacy architecture but unproven AI safety practices.\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n1. **Require vendor to close AI governance gaps before production deployment:**\\n   - Publish AI ethics policy and bias testing framework\\n   - Conduct third-party AI safety audit (e.g., red team, adversarial testing)\\n   - Document training data sources, composition, and filtering practices\\n   - Implement and test human-in-the-loop controls for code review agent\\n\\n2. **Require operational SLA commitments:**\\n   - Publish uptime SLA (target: 99.5% or higher for enterprise)\\n   - Define support response SLAs by severity (P1, P2, P3)\\n   - Document and test incident response plan annually\\n\\n3. **Clarify compliance scope:**\\n   - Confirm GDPR DPA availability and terms\\n   - Assess EU AI Act compliance readiness\\n   - Clarify PII handling and code filtering practices\\n\\n4. **Pilot deployment recommended:**\\n   - Deploy in non-production or low-risk environment first\\n   - Validate data residency and rollback capabilities\\n   - Establish baseline performance and safety metrics\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation:** **CONDITIONAL APPROVAL** — Suitable for pilot or non-critical deployments; fast-track procurement not recommended until AI governance and operational maturity gaps are closed.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Tabnine (AI Code Assistant)", "Customer Base": "Not publicly disclosed", "Target Industry": "Software development; enterprises with data residency and compliance constraints", "Deployment Model": "Multi-tenant SaaS (cloud), VPC-hosted, on-premises, fully air-gapped (customer-controlled)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise teams; typical deployment size not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Code completion, code generation, code review, and test agent automation for enterprise development teams", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud (SaaS), VPC, on-premises, air-gapped deployments supported", "Product Description": "Tabnine is an enterprise AI code assistant that differentiates on privacy and data sovereignty, offering deployment options (VPC, on-premises, air-gapped) where proprietary code never leaves the customer network. The product provides code completion, generation, and code-review/test agents with moderate explainability features. It addresses compliance and data residency concerns for organizations restricted from using public cloud AI coding tools.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product; no formal third-party safety testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "11–50", "Legal Name": "Tabnine (formerly Codota)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2013", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; inferred to include North America and Europe based on GDPR compliance and enterprise customer base", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Tel Aviv, Israel; specific investors not disclosed", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth-stage); annual revenue not disclosed"}, "title": "C