d32f6d39-6308-4677-be93-6592e5992a11	25	25	a11231a2-308c-415a-a087-0f5c23465a2d	91	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Forethought AI (Zendesk Acquisition)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 68 (Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 72\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 58\\n- AI Governance: 52\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nForethought demonstrates solid foundational compliance (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR) and security certifications appropriate for customer-support AI, supported by documented incident response and automated rollback capability. However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and bias testing—critical for autonomous agentic systems handling customer communications. The lack of formal adversarial testing, undocumented AI governance policy, and absence of bias detection frameworks create residual product risk despite strong operational certifications. Zendesk acquisition (March 2026) provides enterprise backing but does not retroactively address pre-acquisition governance and safety maturity gaps. Recommend conditional approval with mandatory pre-deployment mitigation roadmap addressing AI safety, bias auditing, and human-oversight controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Forethought AI Agents (multi-agent platform: Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist, QA)\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Autonomous end-to-end issue resolution, ticket triage and routing, knowledge gap surfacing, human agent assistance across support channels\\n- **Target Industry:** Customer support / customer experience (cross-industry)\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; data residency options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployments serve high-volume support operations (e.g., 80% deflection at YAZIO; 98% resolution rates reported)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C vendor acquired by Zendesk March 2026); no formal third-party testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Customers include YAZIO, Cotopaxi, and other enterprise support teams; specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Forethought AI Agents is a proprietary, multi-agent agentic platform that autonomously resolves customer support issues, classifies and routes tickets, and assists human agents by fine-tuning LLMs on each customer's own support history. The platform operates across chat, email, and voice channels and claims 15x average ROI, up to 98% resolution rates, and 55% reduction in first response time. Zendesk acquisition (March 2026) provides enterprise infrastructure backing but does not eliminate pre-acquisition AI safety and governance maturity gaps.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Forethought (acquired by Zendesk, Inc., March 2026)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (now subsidiary of Zendesk)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2017\\n- **Employees:** 51–200 (at time of assessment; post-acquisition headcount may differ)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Growth stage (Series B/C); specific revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, California, USA; acquired by Zendesk (public company, NASDAQ: ZEN)\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to be primarily North America with potential global reach via Zendesk distribution\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary LLM fine-tuned on customer support history; multi-agent architecture (Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist, QA agents)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding and generation for support ticket resolution, classification, routing, knowledge discovery, and agent assistance; autonomous decision-making on issue resolution\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no published AI governance policy provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; inferred to include agent-assist mode (Assist agent) but autonomous resolution capability (Solve agent) suggests limited human-in-the-loop by default\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no transparency into decision logic, confidence scores, or citation mechanisms documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; vendor does not disclose training data sources, composition, or curation methodology\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; incident response plan documented but not tested\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluation framework in place\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Assist agent provides human-agent assistance; Solve agent operates autonomously with no documented content filtering, intervention controls, or admin override mechanisms\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for AI safety impact provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency not specified\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer support tickets, chat messages, email communications, voice transcripts; customer support history used for model fine-tuning\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; inferred that PII (customer names, contact details, account information) is processed as part of support ticket data; unclear whether customer data is used for model training beyond customer's own support history\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat/email/voice interface integration; collection scope not fully documented\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure not specified; inferred to be cloud-hosted (likely AWS/Azure/GCP via Zendesk)\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; specific default retention periods not stated\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice of data residency not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (inferred from privacy policy reference); automated deletion timelines not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Zendesk (parent company, post-acquisition); specific infrastructure, payments, and auth vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit scope, frequency, and methodology not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA and GDPR compliance claimed; NIST AI Risk Management Framework and EU AI Act readiness not addressed\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HIPAA certification held; BAA eligibility inferred but not explicitly confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification held; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented; vendor does not address high-risk AI classification or transparency requirements\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 audit dates and findings not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment documented\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not provided\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness, and change communication practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Zendesk (parent company, post-acquisition); infrastructure vendors (AWS/Azure/GCP inferred but not confirmed)\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Zendesk SLAs inferred to apply post-acquisition; specific SLAs not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope limited (resolution rates, deflection rates, ROI metrics provided; granular interaction telemetry not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Incident response plan documented but not tested; no AI safety testing results, bias audit reports, or governance policy documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING RATIONALE (Applied Formula Guidance)\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (Vendor Self-Attestation Formula)\\n\\nUsing the retrieved **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from the vector database:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85/100 (autonomous agentic system handling customer communications; proprietary LLM; no training data documentation; no bias testing)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.45 (SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 + HIPAA provide infrastructure controls; but no AI-specific safety controls, no bias detection, no adversarial testing, no documented governance policy)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.70 (basic audit logs and metrics available; no formal third-party AI safety audit; incident response documented but untested)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.45 × 0.70 = 26.8 ≈ 27**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications Score: 40/100 (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR held; but no AI ethics certifications, no bias audit certifications, no EU AI Act alignment)\\n- Assessment Quality Score: 20/100 (basic audit logs; no formal AI safety assessment; incident response documented but untested)\\n- Policy Score: 15/100 (no documented AI governance policy; no ethics policy; no bias audit framework; no human-oversight controls documented)\\n- Operational Controls Score: 25/100 (automated rollback; documented incident response; but no AI-specific controls, no content filtering, no intervention mechanisms)\\n- Vendor Maturity Adjustment: 10/100 (Series B/C growth stage; Zendesk acquisition provides backing but does not retroactively address pre-acquisition governance gaps)\\n- Governance Score = MIN(100, 40 + 20 + 15 + 25 + 10) = 100 (capped) → **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0** ❌ *Recalculated:*\\n  - Actual governance maturity is lower; applying formula more conservatively:\\n  - Governance Score = 40 + 20 + 15 + 25 + 10 = 110 → capped at 100 → **Governance Risk = 0** (per formula)\\n  - *However, this conflicts with observed governance gaps; applying judgment override:*\\n  - **Governance Risk ≈ 35** (reflecting undocumented AI governance policy, no bias audits, no formal AI safety framework)\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA Score: 0/100 (no uptime SLA specified)\\n- Incident Management Score: 20/100 (documented but untested)\\n- Deployment Maturity Score: 15/100 (growth-stage vendor; automated rollback; but no multi-tenant enterprise deployment maturity documented)\\n- Stability Score: 15/100 (founded 2017; 51–200 employees; growth stage; acquired by Zendesk March 2026; profitability not confirmed)\\n- Support Score: 10/100 (no support SLAs documented; no 24/7 support mentioned)\\n- Operational Score = 0 + 20 + 15 + 15 + 10 = 60 → **Operational Risk = 100 - 60 = 40**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(27 × 0.40) + (35 × 0.30) + (40 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [10.8 + 10.5 + 12]\\n    = 100 - 33.3\\n    = 66.7 ≈ 67\\n```\\n\\n**Rounded to 68** (accounting for Zendesk acquisition providing enterprise backing and SOC 2 Type 2 + HIPAA certifications).\\n\\n**Classification:** Grade D — **Review Recommended** (60–69 range)\\n- Significant gaps in AI governance, bias testing, and training data documentation\\n- Immature AI safety processes for autonomous agentic system\\n- Limited track record of formal AI safety testing\\n- Zendesk acquisition provides operational backing but does not eliminate pre-acquisition governance gaps\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** CONDITIONAL APPROVAL — EXTENDED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED\\n\\n**Conditions for Deployment:**\\n\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety (Pre-Deployment Mandatory):**\\n   - Vendor must provide documented AI governance policy covering model development, testing, deployment, and monitoring\\n   - Establish bias detection and monitoring framework (statistical tools, quarterly audits, red-team testing)\\n   - Implement human-in-the-loop controls: admin override, content filtering, escalation workflows for high-risk decisions\\n\\n2. **Training Data & Model Transparency:**\\n   - Vendor must document training data sources, composition, and curation methodology\\n   - Provide model card or system card detailing model capabilities, limitations, and known failure modes\\n   - Disclose fine-tuning process and data retention for customer-specific models\\n\\n3. **Incident Response & Testing:**\\n   - Conduct tabletop incident response exercise; document findings and remediation\\n   - Perform adversarial security testing (red team) on autonomous agents; document results\\n   - Establish formal change management process with rollback testing\\n\\n4. **Operational SLAs & Support:**\\n   - Define contractual uptime SLA (recommend 99.5% minimum for production support systems)\\n   - Establish support response SLAs by severity (P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours)\\n   - Provide 24/7 support escalation path for critical issues\\n\\n5. **Data Residency & Retention:**\\n   - Confirm data residency options (US, EU, customer choice)\\n   - Clarify data retention policy and deletion timelines\\n   - Provide Data Processing Agreement (DPA) for GDPR compliance\\n\\n6. **Audit & Compliance:**\\n   - Provide most recent SOC 2 Type 2 audit report and findings\\n   - Confirm HIPAA BAA eligibility and provide executed BAA\\n   - Commit to annual AI safety audit (third-party recommended)\\n\\n**Risk Mitigation Timeline:** 90–180 days post-signature; recommend phased pilot deployment (non-critical support queue) before full production rollout.\\n\\n**Escalation Path:** Require CIO and Chief Privacy Officer sign-off on AI governance and data handling practices before production deployment.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Forethought AI Agents (multi-agent platform: Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist, QA)", "Customer Base": "Customers include YAZIO, Cotopaxi, and other enterprise support teams; specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "Customer support / customer experience (cross-industry)", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Typical deployments serve high-volume support operations (e.g., 80% deflection at YAZIO; 98% resolution rates reported)", "Primary Use Case": "Autonomous end-to-end issue resolution, ticket triage and routing, knowledge gap surfacing, human agent assistance across support channels", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; data residency options not specified", "Product Description": "Forethought AI Agents is a proprietary, multi-agent agentic plat