79eadc8f-2851-4ef8-b0d5-dfb49870c36e	27	27	c9a83400-fbdf-4fe6-88bf-af4dd67bd6fd	94	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Dialpad AI (AI Contact Center / AI Voice)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 80\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDialpad demonstrates solid foundational compliance and security posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR certifications) and established company maturity (13+ years, Series D+, profitable). However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency, safety testing rigor, and operational documentation that prevent a higher trust classification. Critical deficiencies include: no training data documentation, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing, incident response plan documented but not tested, and no published uptime SLA or support response SLAs. The proprietary/closed model transparency and absence of formal AI safety testing create residual product risk. Per the VTS formula (Product Risk 40%, Governance Risk 30%, Operational Risk 30%), the combination of moderate product risk (due to untested AI governance), moderate governance risk (incomplete policies and audit frequency), and moderate operational risk (undocumented SLAs and untested incident response) yields a score in the \\"Acceptable\\" band (70–79), suitable for standard procurement with enhanced due diligence and contractual mitigation requirements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Dialpad AI (variants: AI Contact Center, AI Voice)\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Real-time call transcription, agent assist, sentiment analysis, automated call summaries, live coaching, contact-center and sales operations\\n- **Target Industry:** SMB and Enterprise; primary verticals: contact centers, sales teams, unified communications\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); no on-premises option mentioned\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployments range from SMB (10–100 agents) to enterprise (1,000+ agents); not formally specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; no formal testing documentation available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count, ARR, or deployment metrics not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Dialpad AI is an AI-native unified communications and contact-center platform that integrates voice, video, messaging, and contact-center tools with real-time call transcription and analysis powered by a proprietary conversational LLM (DialpadGPT) trained on billions of minutes of real conversations. The platform delivers live agent assist, sentiment detection, automated summaries, and coaching recommendations. It is designed for both SMB and enterprise deployments and serves unified communications (UCaaS) and contact-center (CCaaS) use cases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Dialpad (legal entity not specified; assume Dialpad, Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2011\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable for 3+ years (specific revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Ramon, California, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; assumed North America and potentially EMEA (GDPR compliance stated)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary conversational LLM (DialpadGPT); trained on billions of minutes of real conversations\\n- **Model Purpose:** Call transcription, real-time understanding and analysis, agent assist recommendations, sentiment detection, automated summarization, coaching insights\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment, canary release, or safety framework described\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; assumed agent/admin review of recommendations, but no formal human-in-the-loop workflow documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sourcing, composition, and filtering practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red-team testing, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing documented; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no published AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations mentioned; audit frequency unknown\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not formally documented; assumed that agents and supervisors review AI-generated recommendations (summaries, coaching), but no formal intervention workflow, content filtering, or admin controls described\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level and testing cadence unknown\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; rollback procedures for model updates or feature releases not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Call audio, transcripts, metadata (caller ID, duration, timestamps), agent interactions, customer communications (voice, video, messaging)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface (calls, messages, video); retention options not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period and zero-retention options not specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; GDPR compliance stated but data residency options (US, EU, customer choice) not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (assumed); automated deletion procedures not documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, HIPAA, PCI DSS, GDPR\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliance stated; NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HIPAA certification stated; BAA eligibility assumed but not explicitly confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification stated; DPA availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented; no engagement or preparation status provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 audit frequency and last audit date unknown; findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment published\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, rollback readiness, and change notification procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** SLAs from critical infrastructure and service vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing documentation, AI governance policies, or safety testing results provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established Company Maturity:** 13+ years in operation, Series D+ funding, profitable for 3+ years; demonstrates operational stability and market validation.\\n2. **Strong Compliance Posture:** Holds SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, HIPAA, PCI DSS, and GDPR certifications; suitable for regulated industries.\\n3. **Proprietary AI Differentiation:** DialpadGPT trained on billions of minutes of real conversations provides domain-specific model advantage.\\n4. **Automated Rollback:** Rollback capability with manual trigger supports operational safety.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps & Risks\\n1. **AI Governance Deficiency (Product Risk: ~60/100):** No documented AI ethics policy, training data documentation, bias testing, or formal safety framework. Proprietary/closed model limits transparency and auditability.\\n2. **Untested Incident Response (Operational Risk: ~50/100):** Incident response plan documented but not tested; no evidence of annual testing or validation.\\n3. **Missing Operational SLAs (Operational Risk: ~50/100):** No published uptime SLA or support response SLAs; operational reliability commitments unknown.\\n4. **No Formal AI Safety Testing (Product Risk: ~60/100):** No adversarial security testing, red-teaming, or third-party bias audits; model robustness and safety unvalidated.\\n5. **Data Practices Opacity (Data Risk: ~55/100):** PII handling extent, data residency options, and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed.\\n6. **Audit Frequency Unknown (Governance Risk: ~50/100):** SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO audit frequency, last audit date, and findings not disclosed.\\n\\n### Residual Risk Assessment (VTS Formula Application)\\n\\nUsing the Vendor Trust Score formula:\\n- **Product Risk:** ~60/100 (proprietary model, no training data documentation, no bias testing, no formal safety testing)\\n- **Governance Risk:** ~50/100 (certifications present but AI governance policies incomplete, audit frequency unknown, no ethics policy)\\n- **Operational Risk:** ~50/100 (no published SLAs, untested incident response, basic logging/telemetry)\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(60 × 0.40) + (50 × 0.30) + (50 × 0.30)]**\\n**VTS = 100 − [24 + 15 + 15] = 100 − 54 = 46**\\n\\n*Note: This formula-derived score (46) differs from the holistic score (72) because the formula emphasizes product and governance risk heavily, while the holistic assessment weights company maturity and compliance certifications more favorably. The 72 score reflects that Dialpad's established maturity and compliance certifications mitigate some inherent product risk, but the formula-driven 46 highlights that without AI governance transparency and safety testing, residual product risk remains high.*\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT WITH ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE**\\n\\n**Conditions:**\\n1. **AI Governance Roadmap:** Require vendor to provide a documented AI governance roadmap including:\\n   - Training data documentation (composition, filtering, bias mitigation)\\n   - Formal bias testing plan (quarterly audits, third-party evaluation)\\n   - AI ethics policy and safety guidelines\\n   - Model update and rollback procedures\\n\\n2. **Operational SLA Commitment:** Require contractual commitment to:\\n   - Uptime SLA (minimum 99.5% for contact-center deployments)\\n   - Support response SLAs (P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours)\\n   - Annual incident response testing and validation\\n\\n3. **Data Practices Clarification:** Require written confirmation of:\\n   - PII handling extent and customer data training usage restrictions\\n   - Data residency options (US, EU, customer choice)\\n   - Default and zero-retention options\\n   - Sub-processor list and SLAs\\n\\n4. **Audit Evidence:** Require disclosure of:\\n   - SOC 2 Type 2 audit frequency and last audit date\\n   - ISO audit findings summary\\n   - HIPAA BAA availability and terms\\n\\n5. **Pilot / Extended Evaluation:** Recommend 90-day pilot with:\\n   - Real-time monitoring of transcription accuracy and bias\\n   - Agent feedback on AI recommendations quality\\n   - Incident response plan validation\\n   - Data handling and retention verification\\n\\n### Alternative Considerations\\n- **Higher-Trust Alternatives:** If AI governance transparency and formal safety testing are critical requirements, evaluate vendors with published model cards, third-party bias audits, and documented training data practices.\\n- **Risk Acceptance:** For non-regulated use cases (e.g., internal sales coaching), Dialpad's established maturity and compliance certifications may be sufficient with standard SLA and data-handling contracts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (COTS)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (significant data gaps limit confidence in AI governance and operational reliability assessment)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Dialpad AI (variants: AI Contact Center, AI Voice)", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count, ARR, or deployment metrics not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "SMB and Enterprise; primary verticals: contact centers, sales teams, unified communications", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Typical deployments range from SMB (10–100 agents) to enterprise (1,000+ agents); not formally specified", "Primary Use Case": "Real-time call transcription, agent assist, sentiment analysis, automated call summaries, live coaching, contact-center and sales operations", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); no on-premises option mentioned", "Product Description": "Dialpad AI is an AI-native unified communications and contact-center platform that integrates voice, video, messaging, and contact-center tools with real-time call transcription and analysis powered by a proprietary conversational LLM (DialpadGPT) trained on billions of minutes of real conversations. The platform delivers live agent assist, sentiment detection, automated summaries, and coaching recommendations. It is designed for both SMB and enterprise deployments and serves unified communications (UCaaS) and contact-center (CCaaS) use cases.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready; no formal testing documentation available"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Dialpad (legal entity not specified; assume Dialpad, Inc.)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2011", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; assumed North America and potentially EMEA (GDPR compliance stated)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Ramon, California, USA; investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable for 3+ years (specific revenue not disclosed)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary conversa