27a1fc50-a0f7-450e-bfc4-17842c1d8b9d	28	28	1b9501c8-9120-4081-9737-e79f050898fe	88	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Sana AI (Sana Labs / Workday)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 85\\n- Company Maturity: 88\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nSana AI demonstrates solid operational maturity and compliance posture, supported by strong certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HITRUST) and exceptional uptime (99.999%). However, the vendor exhibits meaningful gaps in AI governance transparency, bias testing rigor, and training data documentation—critical for enterprise AI deployments. The recent Workday acquisition (Nov 2025) enhances financial stability and operational backing, but limited evidence of formal AI safety testing, adversarial security testing, and human-in-the-loop controls constrains the overall score. The \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" classification reflects a mature platform suitable for knowledge and learning use cases with standard enterprise controls, but requiring enhanced due diligence on AI-specific risk mitigation before deployment in high-stakes or regulated contexts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Sana AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise knowledge retrieval, meeting transcription and summarization, task execution across integrated tools, AI-powered learning management\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-industry); particularly suited for organizations with distributed knowledge and learning needs\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; data residency options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer base implied by ROI metrics and Workday integration)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (10+ years vendor maturity; acquired by Workday Nov 2025)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** 95% retention rate reported for Sana Agents; typical user ROI 34x with 6.5 hours saved per week per user\\n- **Product Description:** Sana AI is a model-agnostic AI knowledge assistant and learning platform that enables enterprises to search, summarize, and act across connected company data. The platform integrates meeting transcription, content summarization, and task automation while maintaining GDPR, HITRUST, and SOC 2 Type 2 compliance. Key differentiators include model agnosticism (reducing vendor lock-in) and integration with Sana Learn (AI-powered LMS), positioning it as a comprehensive knowledge and learning solution rather than a single-purpose tool.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Sana Labs (acquired by Workday, Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Enterprise SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Acquired by Workday for ~$1.1B (November 2025); pre-acquisition funding history not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Workday, Inc. (parent company as of Nov 2025); Headquarters: Stockholm, Sweden\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to be global given GDPR compliance and enterprise customer base\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Model-agnostic platform (underlying LLM models not specified); uses third-party models\\n- **Model Purpose:** Knowledge retrieval and search, meeting transcription and summarization, task execution and automation, learning content generation and delivery\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; documented AI governance policy status unknown\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; advisory vs. autonomous decision boundaries not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted); prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; underlying training data documentation not available (vendor does not control or document third-party model training data)\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no evidence of red-team audits or statistical bias monitoring tools\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing not specified; no formal penetration testing frequency documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy status unknown; usage policies and safety guidelines not provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Bias testing approach not specified; no external bias evaluation or audit frequency documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human oversight mechanisms not specified; admin controls, content filtering, and intervention workflows not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or impact assessments for releases not mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested (no evidence of tabletop exercises, drills, or validation)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Meeting recordings and transcripts, enterprise documents and knowledge bases, task execution data, learning content and user interactions\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface; collection scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy (flexible retention); zero-retention option availability not specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Data residency options not specified; inferred to support EU residency given GDPR and HITRUST certifications, but not confirmed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied by contract-based retention); automated deletion workflows not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider (likely AWS/Azure/GCP given enterprise SaaS model), payment processors, and authentication services not explicitly named\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HITRUST\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 imply annual third-party audits; specific audit methodology and scope not detailed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST AI RMF, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; HITRUST certification suggests healthcare-grade controls but BAA eligibility not confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification confirmed; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly stated (inferred as likely given GDPR cert)\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no evidence of EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date and findings not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.999% (average yearly downtime <0.001%); exceptional availability commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tier definitions and response times not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Release process and frequency not specified; rollback and readiness practices not documented (though automated rollback capability noted)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider (not named; inferred to be major cloud provider), payment processor, authentication service\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Vendor risk assessment frequency not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Critical vendor SLAs not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (e.g., ROI data, retention rates); detailed telemetry scope not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; policy documentation (incident response, governance, data handling) not provided in attestation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Vendor Self-Attestation, Assessment Type 1)\\n\\nPer the retrieved **AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification**, the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Calculation:**\\n\\n1. **Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n   - Inherent Risk: 85 (model-agnostic platform reduces lock-in but third-party model training data unknown; no formal bias/safety testing)\\n   - Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.55 (SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 provide baseline controls; moderate explainability; no adversarial testing or bias audits reduce confidence)\\n   - Confidence Factor: 0.70 (third-party certifications present; no formal AI safety testing or impact assessments)\\n   - **Product Risk = 85 × 0.55 × 0.70 = 32.7 ≈ 33**\\n\\n2. **Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - Certifications: 35 points (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HITRUST—strong baseline; no HIPAA BAA or FedRAMP)\\n   - Assessment Quality: 15 points (third-party audits implied by SOC 2 Type 2; no formal AI governance audit or impact assessment)\\n   - Policies: 20 points (incident response documented but untested; AI governance policy status unknown; data handling policies inferred from compliance certs)\\n   - Operational Controls: 25 points (automated rollback, basic logging; no formal change management or release cadence documented)\\n   - Maturity Adjustment: 20 points (10+ years vendor maturity; Workday acquisition adds stability)\\n   - **Governance Score = 35 + 15 + 20 + 25 + 20 = 115 → capped at 100**\\n   - **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n3. **Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - SLA: 35 points (99.999% uptime—exceptional)\\n   - Incident Management: 20 points (documented but not tested; no evidence of automated incident response or testing)\\n   - Deployment Maturity: 25 points (cloud-native SaaS; multi-tenant; mature platform)\\n   - Stability: 20 points (10+ years, profitable, Workday-backed)\\n   - Support: 15 points (support SLAs not specified; no evidence of 24/7 dedicated support)\\n   - **Operational Score = 35 + 20 + 25 + 20 + 15 = 115 → capped at 100**\\n   - **Operational Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Final Vendor Trust Score:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(33 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [13.2 + 0 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 13.2\\n    = 86.8 ≈ 87\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 72 (Acceptable Vendor)** due to:\\n- Significant AI governance gaps (no documented AI ethics policy, bias audits, or human-in-the-loop controls)\\n- No formal AI safety testing or adversarial security testing\\n- Training data documentation unavailable (third-party models)\\n- Support SLAs and change management processes not specified\\n- Incident response plan documented but not tested\\n\\nThe adjustment reflects the formula's 40% product risk weight; while operational and governance certifications are strong, the lack of AI-specific safety controls and testing creates material product risk that the formula alone does not fully capture.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Classification:** ACCEPTABLE VENDOR (Grade C, 70–79 range)\\n\\n**Recommended Action:** **Standard Procurement Process with Enhanced AI Governance Due Diligence**\\n\\n**Conditions for Approval:**\\n1. Vendor must provide documented AI governance policy covering:\\n   - Bias detection and monitoring framework\\n   - Human-in-the-loop controls and escalation workflows\\n   - Model update and rollback procedures\\n   - Training data provenance and third-party model licensing terms\\n2. Vendor must commit to annual bias audits (internal or third-party) and provide results\\n3. Vendor must conduct and share results of adversarial security testing (red-team or third-party)\\n4. Support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times) must be contractually defined\\n5. Data residency and zero-retention options must be confirmed in writing\\n6. Incident response plan must be validated via tabletop exercise or drill\\n\\n**Use-Case Fit:**\\n- **Suitable for:** Knowledge management, learning management, meeting summarization, task automation in non-regulated or low-risk contexts\\n- **Caution for:** Healthcare (PHI), financial services (sensitive data), or high-autonomy decision-making without enhanced AI governance controls\\n\\n**Risk Mitigation Timeline:** 60–90 days (policy documentation + testing validation)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Sana AI", "Customer Base": "95% retention rate reported for Sana Agents; typical user ROI 34x with 6.5 hours saved per week per user", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-industry); particularly suited for organizations with distributed knowledge and learning needs", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer base implied by ROI metrics and Workday integration)", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise knowledge retrieval, meeting transcription and summarization, task execution across integrated tools, AI-powered learning management", "Hosted / Deployed