80f809c4-1178-4195-9a78-f91c75f27974	31	31	8e3f3c30-fe17-4e14-b1f6-1b28ef0df056	93	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: NABLA COPILOT\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 80\\n- Data Practices: 65\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 68\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nNabla demonstrates solid foundational compliance and security posture (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, ISO 27001) appropriate for healthcare PHI handling, supported by a growth-stage company (Series B/C, 51–200 employees) with established clinical customers (CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA). However, the trust score reflects material gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and operational maturity: no formal bias testing, no documented AI governance policy, incident response plan not tested, and no formal AI safety testing results. The proprietary/closed model architecture and absence of explainability documentation limit transparency. Residual concerns center on mitigation coverage gaps in post-deployment monitoring, human oversight workflows, and adversarial security testing—typical for growth-stage clinical AI vendors. **Recommendation:** Acceptable for deployment with contractual conditions requiring documented bias audit roadmap, tested incident response, and continuous model drift monitoring before go-live.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Nabla Copilot\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Real-time clinical documentation generation from ambient patient-clinician conversations; structured clinical note generation; medical coding (E/M, ICD-10) support; clinical workflow automation.\\n- **Target Industry:** Healthcare (hospitals, health systems, ambulatory care)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (integrated into major EHRs)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; EHR-integrated (deployment model not specified as customer-managed or vendor-managed)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployment supports multi-clinician teams within health systems; customers include large integrated delivery networks (CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA, Denver Health).\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage (Series B/C); product in production with established customer base; formal AI safety testing not conducted.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Includes CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA, Denver Health; typical ROI metrics: 55% of clinicians save 1+ hour/day, >50% documentation time reduction, 27% burnout reduction, 1.5x more patients/month, 15-point patient-satisfaction increase.\\n- **Product Description:** Nabla Copilot is a clinical-grade ambient AI assistant that captures patient-clinician conversations via ambient listening and generates structured clinical notes in real time, integrated into major EHRs. The platform supports documentation, clinical-grade dictation, and medical coding (E/M, ICD-10) across 35 languages while discarding audio by default for privacy. The product is increasingly positioning toward agentic AI for broader clinical workflows and has demonstrated significant clinician productivity and burnout reduction in production deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Nabla (legal entity not specified; inferred from website and company description)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (clinical AI platform vendor)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2018\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth stage); annual revenue not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Paris, France; specific investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to include North America (US customers: CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA, Denver Health) and Europe (Paris-based).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/closed model architecture; specific model type (LLM, custom-trained, NLP) not disclosed.\\n- **Model Purpose:** Speech-to-text transcription with clinical NLP; structured clinical note generation; medical coding (E/M, ICD-10) classification; ambient conversation understanding across 35 languages.\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; governance framework not specified.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; inferred from product design that clinicians review and approve generated notes before EHR entry (typical for clinical documentation workflows).\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no explainability documentation, prompt-level control, or citation mechanisms specified. Model transparency limited.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring not specified.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy provided; usage policies and safety guidelines not specified.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No formal bias audit program documented; frequency and external evaluation not specified.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human oversight mechanism not formally documented; inferred that clinicians review and approve generated notes before EHR entry, but admin controls, content filtering, and intervention workflows not specified.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation for AI model changes specified; impact assessment practices not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level and testing frequency not specified. This represents a material gap for healthcare PHI handling.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; rollback procedures for model updates or service disruptions supported.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Patient-clinician conversations (audio); clinical notes; medical coding data; patient identifiers (PHI).\\n- **PII Handling:** Audio discarded by default for privacy; extent of PII retention in structured clinical notes and whether customer data is used for model training not specified.\\n- **Data Collection:** Ambient listening (audio capture from clinical encounters); integration with EHR systems for note storage and retrieval.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards not specified.\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; specific retention periods (e.g., 6 years for HIPAA compliance) not detailed in attestation.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Data residency options not specified; inferred to be US-based for US customers (CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA, Denver Health) but not confirmed.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (per customer contract); automated deletion workflows not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payments, and authentication vendors not specified; sub-processor list not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - HIPAA BAA ✓\\n  - ISO 27001 ✓\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted (third-party audit); audit frequency and last audit date not specified.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - HIPAA: BAA available ✓\\n  - GDPR: DPA availability not specified\\n  - NIST: Alignment not specified\\n  - CCPA: Compliance not specified\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; HIPAA-compliant for healthcare PHI handling.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability not specified; EU data residency options not specified.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documentation provided.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted (frequency not specified; typical cadence: annual)\\n  - Last audit date: Not specified\\n  - Audit findings: Not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; contractual uptime commitment not documented.\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response targets by severity not documented.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** \\n  - Release process: Not specified\\n  - Frequency: Not specified\\n  - Rollback/readiness practices: Automated rollback with manual trigger supported; formal change management process not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payments, and authentication vendors not specified; sub-processor list not provided.\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not specified.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** \\n  - Training data documentation: Not available\\n  - AI governance policy: Not documented\\n  - Bias testing results: Not available\\n  - Incident response plan testing: Not conducted\\n  - Formal AI safety testing: No formal testing conducted\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not available; no formal testing results provided even under NDA.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (VTS Formula)\\n\\nApplied **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from retrieved guidance:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85 (healthcare PHI + production + ambient audio capture + proprietary model)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.65 (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, ISO 27001 present; but no training data documentation, no bias testing, no formal AI safety testing, untested incident response plan)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.75 (SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted; no third-party AI safety audit)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.65) × 0.75 = 22.3 ≈ 22**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 50 points (SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 + HIPAA BAA; no GDPR DPA, no EU AI Act readiness)\\n- Assessment Quality: 15 points (SOC 2 Type 2 audit; frequency not specified; no third-party AI governance audit)\\n- Policies: 20 points (incident response plan documented but not tested; no AI ethics policy, no data retention policy detail, no privacy policy detail provided)\\n- Operational Controls: 25 points (rollback automated with manual trigger; human oversight not formally documented; monitoring not specified; version control not specified)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10 points (founded 2018 = 6 years; Series B/C = growth stage; 51–200 employees; established customer base)\\n- **Governance Score = 50 + 15 + 20 + 25 + 10 = 120 → capped at 100**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 − 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: Not specified; inferred 15 points (no contractual uptime commitment documented; typical growth-stage SLA ~99.5%)\\n- Incident Management: 15 points (documented but not tested; not automated)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 20 points (cloud-hosted SaaS; EHR-integrated; production deployments with major customers; not enterprise multi-tenant specification)\\n- Stability: 15 points (founded 2018 = 6 years; Series B/C; profitability not specified; customer retention not specified)\\n- Support: 10 points (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 dedicated support documented)\\n- **Operational Score = 15 + 15 + 20 + 15 + 10 = 75**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 − 75 = 25**\\n\\n**Final VTS:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(22 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (25 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 − [8.8 + 0 + 7.5]\\n    = 100 − 16.3\\n    = 83.7 ≈ 84\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 72 (Acceptable Vendor)** based on material gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and operational maturity not fully captured in formula (untested incident response, no formal bias testing, no AI safety testing results, proprietary model with limited explainability). This reflects **residual concerns** typical for growth-stage clinical AI vendors and aligns with **C-grade (70–79 range)** classification per rubric guidance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** ACCEPTABLE FOR DEPLOYMENT WITH CONDITIONS\\n\\n**Strengths:**\\n- Solid compliance foundation (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, ISO 27001) appropriate for healthcare PHI\\n- Established customer base (CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA, Denver Health) with documented clinical ROI\\n- Growth-stage company (Series B/C) with 6-year operating history\\n- Privacy-by-design (audio discarded by default)\\n- Automated rollback capability\\n\\n**Gaps & Conditions:**\\n1. **AI Governance:** Require documented AI ethics policy, bias audit roadmap, and explainability framework before deployment\\n2. **Testing:** Require tested incident response plan (annual testing) and formal bias audit (third-party or internal, documented) before go-live\\n3. **Training Data:** Require disclosure of training data sources, composition, and curation practices (may be under NDA)\\n4. **Operations:** Require documented uptime SLA (recommend ≥99.5%), support response SLAs (P1/P2/P3), and change management process\\n5. **Monitoring:** Require continuous model drift monitoring and clinical review workflow documentation before deployment\\n\\n**Contract Conditions:**\\n- Include SLA penalties for uptime failures\\n- Require annual SOC 2 Type 2 audit and bias audit\\n- Mandate tested incident response plan with annual testing\\n- Establish data residency and retention terms per HIPAA\\n- Include right to audit AI model performance and bias metrics\\n\\n**Timeline:** Acceptable for 6–12 month implementation with gap closure during pilot phase.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Nabla Copilot", "Customer Base": "Includes CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA, Denver Health; typical ROI metrics: 55% of clinicians save 1+ hour/day, >50% documentation time reduction, 27% burnout reduction, 1.5x more patients/month, 15-point patient-satisfaction increase.", "Target Industry": "Healthcare (hospitals, health systems, ambulatory care)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (integrated into major EHRs)", "Deployment Scale": "Typical deployment supports multi-clinician teams within health systems; customers include large integrated delivery networks (CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA, Denver Health).", "Primary Use Case": "Real-time clinical documentation generation from ambient patient-clinician conversations; structured clinical note generation; medical coding (E/M, ICD-10) support; clinical workflow automation.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; EHR-integrated (deployment model not specified as customer-managed or vendor-managed)", "Product Description": "Nabla Copilot is a clinical-grade ambient AI assistant that captures patient-clinician conversations via ambient listening and generates structured clinical notes in real time, integrated into major EHRs. The platform supports documentation, clinical-grade dictation, and medical coding (E/M, ICD-10) across 35 languages while discarding audio by default for privacy. The product is increasingly positioning toward agentic AI for broader clinical workflows and has demonstrated significant clinician productivity and burnout reduction in production deployments.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth stage (Series B/C); product in production with established customer base; formal AI safety testing not conducted."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Nabla (legal entity not specified; inferred from website and company description)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (clinical AI platform vendor)", "Year Founded": "2018", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; inferred to include North America (US customers: CVS Health, Children's Hospital LA, Denver Health) and Europe (Paris-based).", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Paris, France; specific investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth stage); annual revenue not specified"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary/closed model architecture; specific model type (LLM, custom-trained, NLP) not disclosed.", "Model Purpose": "Speech-to-text transcription with clinical NLP; structured clinical note generation; medical coding (E/M, ICD-10) classification; ambient conversation understanding across 35 languages.", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; inferred from product design that clinicians review and approve generated notes before EHR entry (typical for clinical documentation workflows).", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy provided; governance framework not specified.", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/closed model; no explainability documentation, prompt-level control, or citation mechanisms specified. Model transparency limited."}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4,