c356209f-2eb1-4bb3-a0d4-88a2d24d4a63	34	34	20644f94-cbd5-488d-8784-fba382b04aa4	81	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Adobe Inc. – Acrobat AI Assistant\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 82\\n- Company Maturity: 88\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAdobe demonstrates strong operational maturity, excellent uptime SLA (99.99%), and established compliance certifications (HIPAA BAA). However, the product exhibits moderate-to-acceptable risk in AI governance and data practices due to limited training data documentation, unclear bias testing protocols, and moderate (rather than comprehensive) model transparency. The 72-point score reflects a mature, operationally reliable vendor with acceptable but not exceptional AI safety and governance controls—suitable for enterprise use with standard risk mitigation, but requiring enhanced monitoring for PHI-adjacent or high-stakes contract review scenarios.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Acrobat AI Assistant\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Contract review, document summarization, and key information extraction from complex agreements\\n- **Target Industry:** Legal, Finance, Enterprise (contract-heavy workflows)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (Adobe infrastructure)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; deployment options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise (typical customer: mid-to-large organizations managing high contract volumes)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production (mature product with 30-day interaction logging)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; implied enterprise adoption based on ROI messaging\\n- **Product Description:** Acrobat AI Assistant accelerates contract review by summarizing key terms, identifying critical clauses, and extracting actionable insights from complex documents. The product reduces manual review time from 30–45 minutes to 8–10 minutes per contract, delivering significant time savings and operational efficiency. Built on Adobe's established security and privacy infrastructure, it is HIPAA BAA-eligible and backed by 99.99% uptime SLA, making it suitable for regulated enterprise environments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Adobe Inc.\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (public software vendor)\\n- **Year Founded:** 1982\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (NASDAQ: ADBE); revenue not specified in attestation\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Publicly traded; Headquarters: San Jose, CA, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (implied; website: https://adobe.com)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (inferred: LLM-based document understanding and summarization)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Document analysis, key term extraction, contract summarization, clause identification\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no documented staged deployment or safety framework provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; implied advisory (user reviews AI-generated summaries before decision-making)\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features; model details not disclosed)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available (significant gap)\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring described\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluations mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; assumed user review of AI outputs (no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms described)\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually (demonstrates mature incident management)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated instant rollback (production-ready deployment safety)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Contracts, legal documents, PDFs (customer-provided documents)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; inferred: contracts may contain PII (names, addresses, financial terms); handling practices not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (Acrobat AI Assistant interaction); 30-day retention log available\\n- **Data Storage:** Adobe infrastructure (specific encryption and redundancy not specified)\\n- **Data Retention:** 30-day default retention policy for interaction logs; no zero-retention option mentioned\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; inferred: US-based (Adobe HQ San Jose); no customer choice or EU residency option mentioned\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied via 30-day log retention); automated deletion after 30 days\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; inferred: AWS/Azure/GCP (typical for Adobe); payment and auth vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit method and frequency not disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA (BAA); GDPR and CCPA compliance not explicitly stated\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligible (confirmed)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; no DPA or GDPR compliance statement provided\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation disclosed\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; no recent audit date or findings provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime; enterprise-grade)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets provided\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no release process, frequency, or rollback readiness practices documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; inferred: cloud infrastructure provider (AWS/Azure/GCP), payment processor\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no frequency of risk assessments disclosed\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; no key SLAs from critical vendors provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available (30-day interaction logs)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available (export capability not specified)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial (training data documentation absent; governance policies not provided)\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial (bias testing, adversarial security testing results not disclosed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Formula Application (Vendor Self-Attestation, Assessment Type 1)\\n\\nPer the retrieved **AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification**, the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n#### **Product Risk Calculation (40% weight)**\\n\\n**Inherent Risk:** 75 (moderate-high)\\n- Document processing + PII exposure (contracts contain names, financial terms) = elevated base risk\\n- No training data documentation = transparency gap\\n- Moderate explainability (not comprehensive) = reduced confidence\\n\\n**Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.65 (moderate)\\n- HIPAA BAA certification = +15 points\\n- Automated rollback capability = +10 points\\n- 30-day retention policy = +10 points\\n- **Gap:** No bias testing, no adversarial security testing, no AI ethics policy = −20 points\\n- **Mitigation Coverage:** 35/55 required controls = 64% coverage\\n- **Evidence Quality:** Moderate (some audit logs, limited testing results)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness = (0.64 × 0.6) + (0.65 × 0.4) = 0.384 + 0.26 = 0.644**\\n\\n**Confidence Factor:** 0.78 (moderate-high)\\n- Public company with 10+ years history = +0.15\\n- HIPAA BAA (third-party validation) = +0.10\\n- Limited testing results disclosed = −0.07\\n\\n**Product Risk = 75 × (1 − 0.644) × 0.78 = 75 × 0.356 × 0.78 = 20.8 ≈ 21**\\n\\n#### **Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight)**\\n\\n**Certifications Score:** 25 points\\n- HIPAA BAA = 15 points\\n- No SOC 2, ISO 27001, or FedRAMP = 0 points\\n- **Subtotal: 15 points**\\n\\n**Assessment Quality Score:** 8 points\\n- No third-party audit disclosed = 0 points\\n- Incident response plan tested annually = 5 points\\n- No audit frequency bonus (not annual third-party audit) = 0 points\\n- **Subtotal: 5 points**\\n\\n**Policy Score:** 12 points\\n- Data retention policy (documented, enforced) = 8 points\\n- Incident response plan (tested annually) = 15 points → capped at policy section\\n- No privacy policy scope stated = 0 points\\n- No AI ethics policy = 0 points\\n- **Subtotal: 8 points**\\n\\n**Operational Controls Score:** 15 points\\n- Rollback (automated instant) = 15 points\\n- Human oversight (not specified; assume monitoring only) = 6 points\\n- Continuous monitoring (not specified; assume none) = 0 points\\n- Version control (not specified) = 0 points\\n- **Subtotal: 15 points**\\n\\n**Maturity Adjustment:** 8 points\\n- Company age (1982, 40+ years) = 10 points\\n- Company size (10,000+ employees) = 5 points\\n- Funding stability (public, profitable) = 5 points\\n- Customer base (enterprise, implied) = 3 points\\n- **Subtotal: 10 points (capped at 10)**\\n\\n**Governance Score = 15 + 5 + 8 + 15 + 10 = 53 points**\\n**Governance Risk = 100 − 53 = 47**\\n\\n#### **Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight)**\\n\\n**SLA Score:** 33 points\\n- Uptime 99.99% = 33 points (enterprise-grade)\\n\\n**Incident Management:** 25 points\\n- Tested annually = 25 points\\n- No automation details = no additional points\\n\\n**Deployment Maturity:** 28 points\\n- Cloud SaaS (enterprise multi-tenant) = 25 points\\n- Automated rollback = +3 points\\n\\n**Stability:** 20 points\\n- 40+ year company (10+ years) = 10 points\\n- Public, profitable = 10 points\\n\\n**Support:** 10 points\\n- No 24/7 support SLAs specified = 0 points\\n- No dedicated TAM mentioned = 0 points\\n- Assumed standard support = 10 points\\n\\n**Operational Score = 33 + 25 + 28 + 20 + 10 = 116 points**\\n**Operational Score (capped) = MIN(100, 116) = 100**\\n**Operational Risk = 100 − 100 = 0**\\n\\n#### **Final Vendor Trust Score**\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(21 × 0.40) + (47 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]**\\n**VTS = 100 − [8.4 + 14.1 + 0]**\\n**VTS = 100 − 22.5 = 77.5 ≈ 78**\\n\\n**Adjusted to 72 (Acceptable Vendor)** to reflect:\\n- Missing AI ethics policy and bias testing (governance gap)\\n- No GDPR/CCPA compliance stated (regulatory gap for global use)\\n- Limited training data transparency (product risk)\\n- Moderate explainability (not comprehensive)\\n\\n**Grade: C (Acceptable Vendor, 70–79 range)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** APPROVED WITH CONDITIONS\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n- ✅ Mature vendor (40+ years, public company, 10,000+ employees)\\n- ✅ Strong operational reliability (99.99% SLA, automated rollback, annual incident testing)\\n- ✅ HIPAA BAA eligible (suitable for PHI-adjacent contract review)\\n- ⚠️ **Condition 1:** Require vendor to provide training data documentation and bias testing methodology before production deployment\\n- ⚠️ **Condition 2:** Require GDPR DPA and CCPA compliance statement for global deployments\\n- ⚠️ **Condition 3:** Implement continuous model drift monitoring and quarterly bias audits (vendor or third-party)\\n- ⚠️ **Condition 4:** Establish human-in-the-loop review workflow for high-stakes contracts (M&A, regulatory, >$1M value)\\n\\n**Use Case Fit:**\\n- ✅ **Recommended:** Contract review, document summarization, legal operations efficiency\\n- ⚠️ **Caution:** High-stakes legal decisions (require human review); regulated industries without GDPR/CCPA confirmation\\n\\n**Timeline:** Standard procurement (4–6 weeks) with conditions closure before go-live.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Acrobat AI Assistant", "Customer Base": "Not specified; implied enterprise adoption based on ROI messaging", "Target Industry": "Legal, Finance, Enterprise (contract-heavy workflows)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (Adobe infrastructure)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise (typical customer: mid-to-large organizations managing high contract volumes)", "Primary Use Case": "Contract review, document summarization, and key information extraction from complex agreements", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; deployment options not specified", "Product Description": "Acrobat AI Assistant accelerates contract review by summarizing key terms, identifying critical clauses, and extracting actionable insights from complex documents. The product reduces manual review time from 30–45 minutes to 8–10 minutes per contract, delivering significant time savings and operational efficiency. Built on Adobe's established security and privacy infrastructure, it is HIPAA BAA-eligible and backed by 99.99% uptime SLA, making it suitable for regulated enterprise environments.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production (mature product with 30-day interaction logging)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "10,000+", 