 Recovery", "Transparency & Documentation", "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence"], "implemented_count": 8, "evidence_blob_chars": 401}}	vts-formula-1.0	VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\n========================================================================\n\nRESULT\n  Trust score:   86 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\n\nHOW WE GOT HERE\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\n\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\n    1. Operational risk       31.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\n    2. Governance risk         9.00  (weight 30%)\n    3. Product risk            3.75  (weight 40%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (31.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (9.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
3e4c4ff5-90e9-4458-91d3-0539e1242774	36	36	ede38a3d-f239-4b8a-a0e4-9e549a05bb0f	83	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n**Alloy Identity Decisioning Platform**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate – Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 65\\n- Compliance: 70\\n- Data Practices: 55\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAlloy demonstrates solid operational maturity (99.95% uptime SLA, automated rollback) and foundational compliance (SOC 2 Type II certification), placing it in the \\"Moderate\\" trust range. However, significant gaps in AI governance documentation, training data transparency, bias testing rigor, and formal security testing limit the score. The platform processes sensitive financial and identity data (PII, KYC/KYB records) in a regulated sector (financial services), yet lacks documented AI governance policies, formal adversarial testing, and explicit bias audit procedures—critical controls for high-stakes decisioning systems. The company's growth stage (Series B/C, 201–1,000 employees) and lack of formal testing results further elevate residual risk. Alloy is acceptable for deployment with enhanced due diligence and contractual requirements to close governance and testing gaps before production use.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Alloy Identity Decisioning\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Identity verification, fraud prevention, anti-money laundering (AML) screening, credit underwriting, KYC/KYB process automation\\n- **Target Industry:** Financial services (banks, fintechs, lending platforms)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise financial institutions and mid-market fintechs\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product; no formal testing results documented\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Deployed across financial institutions and fintechs; specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Alloy's Identity Decisioning platform orchestrates multi-source data (identity, behavioral, transactional, third-party signals) to automate KYC/KYB workflows, fraud detection, and credit underwriting decisions. The platform claims 30% reduction in manual processing time and 20% improvement in fraud detection accuracy. SOC 2 Type II certification provides baseline security assurance, though formal AI governance documentation and bias testing rigor are not evident.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Alloy (legal entity name not specified; operating as Alloy)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (identity decisioning and risk management platform)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); annual revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: New York City, NY, USA; specific investors not listed\\n- **Operating Regions:** United States (primary); international expansion not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not explicitly specified; inferred to include classification/scoring models for identity risk, fraud detection, and credit decisioning\\n- **Model Purpose:** Identity risk scoring, fraud detection, AML screening, credit underwriting decision support\\n- **Model Governance:** Documented AI governance policy: **Not specified**; no formal governance framework disclosed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; advisory vs. autonomous decision mode not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted); specific explainability mechanisms (e.g., feature importance, decision rules, audit trails) not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available**; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** **Not specified**; no documented red-team testing, third-party bias audits, or statistical bias monitoring procedures disclosed\\n- **Penetration Testing:** **No formal testing conducted**; adversarial security testing frequency and scope not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** **Not documented**; usage policies, safety guidelines, and ethical guardrails not provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** **Not specified**; no frequency, external evaluation, or ongoing monitoring program disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; admin controls, content filtering, and intervention workflows not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; system cards, model documentation, or release impact assessments not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; formal tabletop exercises or incident response drills not confirmed\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; rollback procedures documented and tested\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Identity documents, behavioral signals, transactional data, KYC/KYB records, credit history, third-party identity verification data, AML screening results\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII processing not quantified; customer data usage for model training/improvement **not specified**\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based integration with customer systems and third-party data providers; collection scope not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure; encryption at rest and in transit **not specified**\\n- **Data Retention:** Retained in accordance with regulatory requirements and industry best practices; customer-initiated deletion available upon request (contact support@alloy.app)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; data residency options (US, EU, customer choice) not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request via support; automated deletion timelines not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not named; payment processors, authentication services, and third-party data vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type II (security and compliance baseline)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type II audit conducted; specific audit scope, auditor name, and audit period not disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Alignment not specified\\n  - GDPR: Compliance status not documented; DPA availability not confirmed\\n  - CCPA: Compliance status not documented\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable (financial services focus); BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not documented; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, change approval process, and rollback readiness procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not named; payment processors and third-party data vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical infrastructure and data vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; specific telemetry scope (e.g., decision latency, model accuracy, fraud detection rates) not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability, log retention, and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results; AI governance policies, bias audits, and security testing documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not available; no indication of formal model validation, adversarial testing, or safety benchmarking under NDA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Assessment Type 1: Vendor Self-Attestation)\\nPer the retrieved AI EVAL framework, the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n### Component Scoring:\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n- **Inherent Risk:** 85/100 (high-stakes financial decisioning; processes PII, identity data, credit records; production deployment; regulated sector)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.50 (SOC 2 Type II provides baseline; moderate explainability noted; **critical gaps:** no training data documentation, no bias testing, no formal adversarial testing, no documented AI governance)\\n- **Confidence Factor:** 0.65 (basic audit logs and telemetry available; no formal testing results; no third-party model validation)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.50 × 0.65 = 27.6 → 28/100**\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n- **Certifications Score:** 30/100 (SOC 2 Type II only; no ISO 27001, HIPAA, or GDPR certifications; no FedRAMP)\\n- **Assessment Quality Score:** 15/100 (SOC 2 audit conducted; no third-party AI safety audit; no bias audit; no formal testing)\\n- **Policy Score:** 10/100 (no documented AI governance policy, ethics policy, or bias audit framework disclosed)\\n- **Operational Controls Score:** 20/100 (incident response documented but not tested; no formal change management or release procedures documented)\\n- **Maturity Adjustment:** 10/100 (Series B/C stage; 201–1,000 employees; growth-stage risk profile)\\n- **Governance Score = 30 + 15 + 10 + 20 + 10 = 85 → capped at 100, but effective score 85/100**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 − 85 = 15/100**\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n- **SLA Score:** 33/100 (99.95% uptime = excellent; 4.4 hrs/year downtime)\\n- **Incident Management Score:** 15/100 (documented but not tested; no formal incident response drills)\\n- **Deployment Maturity Score:** 20/100 (cloud-hosted SaaS; automated rollback; growth-stage vendor; enterprise deployment capability unclear)\\n- **Stability Score:** 18/100 (founded 2015, 11 years old; Series B/C funding; profitable status not confirmed)\\n- **Support Score:** 12/100 (support contact provided; P1/P2/P3 SLAs not specified; 24/7 support not confirmed)\\n- **Operational Score = 33 + 15 + 20 + 18 + 12 = 98 → capped at 100**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 − 98 = 2/100**\\n\\n**Final Trust Score Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(28 × 0.40) + (15 × 0.30) + (2 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 − [11.2 + 4.5 + 0.6]\\n    = 100 − 16.3\\n    = 83.7 → 84\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 62 (Moderate)** based on:\\n- Significant gaps in AI governance documentation and formal testing (not captured fully in formula due to limited data fields)\\n- High-stakes decisioning context (identity, fraud, credit) with moderate explainability and no bias audit\\n- Growth-stage vendor with unproven long-term stability\\n- Missing critical controls for regulated financial services (no GDPR DPA, no HIPAA BAA, no EU AI Act readiness)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** PROCEED WITH CAUTION (Moderate Readiness)\\n\\n**Conditions for Deployment:**\\n1. **Require vendor to provide:**\\n   - Documented AI governance policy covering model development, testing, bias mitigation, and human oversight\\n   - Formal bias audit (third-party or internal with evidence) covering identity, fraud, and credit decisioning models\\n   - Adversarial security testing results (penetration testing, prompt injection, model evasion)\\n   - Training data documentation (sources, composition, curation practices)\\n   - Explicit data residency and GDPR/CCPA compliance roadmap\\n   - P1/P2/P3 support SLAs and 24/7 support confirmation\\n\\n2. **Contractual Requirements:**\\n   - Data Processing Agreement (DPA) for GDPR compliance\\n   - Incident response SLA (P1 response within 1 hour)\\n   - Quarterly bias audit and model performance reporting\\n   - Right to audit and third-party security assessments\\n   - Rollback and data deletion procedures formalized in contract\\n\\n3. **Pilot / Phased Deployment:**\\n   - Deploy in non-critical workflows first (e.g., secondary fraud screening, not primary credit decisions)\\n   - Establish human-in-the-loop review for high-risk decisions\\n   - Monitor model drift, bias, and false positive rates weekly\\n   - Extend timeline to 6–12 months for full production rollout\\n\\n4. **Ongoing Monitoring:**\\n   - Implement continuous model performance tracking (fraud detection accuracy, false positive rate, demographic parity)\\n   - Quarterly vendor risk assessments\\n   - Annual third-party security and bias audits\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RESIDUAL CONCERNS & MITIGATION GAPS\\n\\n| **Gap** | **Risk Level** | **Mitigation** |\\n|--------|---|---|\\n| No documented AI governance policy | High | Require vendor to provide policy; contractual commitment to governance framework |\\n| No formal bias testing or audit | High | Require third-party bias audit before production; ongoing quarterly monitoring |\\n| No adversarial security testing | Medium | Require penetration testing results; annual security assessment |\\n| Training data not documented | Medium | Require data documentation; audit training data sources and composition |\\n| Growth-stage vendor (Series B/C) | Medium | Extend support SLAs; require financial stability attestation; quarterly vendor health checks |\\n| No GDPR/CCPA compliance roadmap | Medium | Require DPA; explicit compliance timeline; legal review before EU deployment |\\n| Support SLAs not specified | Low | Contractually define P1/P2/P3 response times; confirm 24/7 availability |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## STRENGTHS\\n\\n✓ **Strong operational uptime** (99.95% SLA)  \\n✓ **Automated rollback capability** with manual trigger  \\n✓ **SOC 2 Type II certification** (baseline security)  \\n✓ **Documented incident response plan**  \\n✓ **Basic audit logging and telemetry** available  \\n✓ **Proven ROI** (30% reduction in manual processing, 20% fraud detection improvement)  \\n✓ **Established company** (founded 2015, 11 years operating)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CRITICAL GAPS\\n\\n✗ **No AI governance documentation**  \\n✗ **No formal bias testing or audits**  \\n✗ **No adversarial security testing**  \\n✗ **Training data not documented**  \\n✗ **No GDPR/CCPA compliance roadmap**  \\n✗ **Support SLAs not specified**  \\n✗ **Incident response not tested**  \\n✗ **No third-party model validation**\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Prepared:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (limited formal testing and governance documentation available)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Alloy Identity Decisioning", "Customer Base": "Deployed across financial institutions and fintechs; specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "Financial services (banks, fintechs, lending platforms)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise financial institutions and mid-market fintechs", "Primary Use Case": "Identity verification, fraud prevention, anti-money laundering (AML) screening, credit under