aS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** US only, EU only, Customer choice of region, Hybrid (Cloud + On-prem)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Project-level; typical customers ship more in days than weeks using detailed prompting strategies\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage (Series B/C vendor); product actively deployed with measurable ROI reporting\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** 80% of organizations using AI agents (including Claude Code) report measurable economic returns; 88% expect continued or increased returns in 2026\\n- **Product Description:** Claude Code is an AI-powered coding assistant operating at the project level with up to 1 million token context window, enabling multi-file code changes, test execution, and iterative failure recovery. Built on Anthropic's Constitutional AI framework, it emphasizes ethical and legal compliance. Customers report 8–10x cost reduction in total AI inference when offloading embeddings, transcription, and classification to local models via Claude Code.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Anthropic\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (AI safety and research focus)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (Growth stage); specific revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; investors not specified in attestation\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; data residency options include US, EU, and customer choice\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary large language model (LLM); Constitutional AI framework\\n- **Model Purpose:** Code generation, understanding, multi-file planning, execution, testing, iteration; document analysis and agentic reasoning (up to 1M token context)\\n- **Model Governance:** Constitutional AI approach designed for ethical and legal compliance; staged deployment model not explicitly documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified in attestation; audit logs available for review\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; transparency limited to Constitutional AI framework principles; no prompt-level control or citation mechanism documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Summary only (no detailed lineage); training data composition and sources not fully disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; methodology for bias testing not documented in attestation\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Incident response plan tested annually; adversarial security testing approach not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Constitutional AI framework emphasizes ethical and legal compliance; formal documented AI governance policy not specified\\n- **Bias Audits:** Frequency and external evaluation methodology not documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Audit logs available; admin controls and content filtering not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation not mentioned; Constitutional AI framework implies impact consideration but formal assessment process not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; demonstrates mature incident response capability\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; supports rapid remediation and deployment safety\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Code, documents, chat sessions, coding sessions; embeddings, transcription, classification tasks\\n- **PII Handling:** Enterprise accounts (Claude for Work, API, Gov, Education) explicitly exclude customer data from training; consumer accounts (Free, Pro, Max, Claude Code) may retain de-identified data for model improvement if users opt-in; data flagged for trust and safety violations may be retained for up to two years (inputs/outputs) or seven years (classification scores)\\n- **Data Collection:** API, chat interface, coding sessions; opt-in model for consumer training data\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standard not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** \\n  - **Consumer accounts (opt-in):** Up to 5 years de-identified for model improvement; 30 days if opt-out\\n  - **Enterprise accounts:** 30 days standard; Zero Data Retention (ZDR) available via DPA\\n  - **API logs:** 7 days (as of September 15, 2025); 30-day retention available via DPA\\n  - **Deleted data:** Removed within 30 days\\n  - **Trust & safety flagged data:** Up to 2 years (inputs/outputs), 7 years (classification scores)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only, EU only, customer choice of region, hybrid (Cloud + On-prem) options available\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request; deleted chats removed within 30 days\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payments and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 1\\n  - SOC 2 Type 2\\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n  - CSA STAR Level 1\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit frequency and last audit date not provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Alignment not explicitly stated\\n  - GDPR: Data Processing Agreements (DPAs) available for enterprise accounts\\n  - CCPA: Not explicitly addressed\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; enterprise accounts support HIPAA-compliant data handling\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPAs available for enterprise accounts; data residency options support EU compliance\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** <95% or No SLA (not published; represents a material gap for enterprise deployment)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, frequency, or rollback/readiness practices\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payments and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, available; scope not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, available; export capability and format not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Not uploaded in attestation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, available under NDA; specific test results not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & JUSTIFICATION\\n\\n### Formula Applied\\nPer the vector database guidance (Assessment Type 1: Vendor Self-Attestation), the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n### Calculation\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85/100 (proprietary LLM, code execution capability, consumer data retention up to 5 years, limited training data transparency)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.65 (Constitutional AI framework, enterprise data isolation, DPA/ZDR options, annual incident testing, SOC 2 Type 2)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.80 (SOC 2 Type 1/2, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA; no third-party AI safety audit disclosed)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.65) × 0.80 = 85 × 0.35 × 0.80 = 23.8 ≈ 24**\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 45/100 (SOC 2 Type 1/2, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA, CSA STAR Level 1; no FedRAMP, no third-party AI ethics audit)\\n- Assessment Quality: 20/100 (audit frequency not specified, no published audit findings, no independent AI safety assessment)\\n- Policies: 35/100 (Constitutional AI framework documented; formal AI governance policy, bias audit policy, and impact assessment process not specified)\\n- Operational Controls: 40/100 (annual incident response testing, automated rollback; no change management process, no release cadence, no formal risk management framework documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10/100 (Series B/C, founded 2021; 3-year-old company with 1,001–5,000 employees; growth stage, not yet established)\\n- **Governance Score = (45 + 20 + 35 + 40 + 10) / 5 = 30 → Governance Risk = 100 − 30 = 70**\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 10/100 (<95% or no SLA published; material gap for enterprise)\\n- Incident Management: 25/100 (tested annually; no detail on automation, testing frequency, or MTTR)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 30/100 (multi-region deployment available; no documented enterprise multi-tenant architecture, no release process)\\n- Stability: 20/100 (Series B/C, 3-year-old company; profitable status not stated; customer retention not disclosed)\\n- Support: 15/100 (no published support SLAs; support structure not documented)\\n- **Operational Score = (10 + 25 + 30 + 20 + 15) = 100 → capped at 100 → Operational Risk = 100 − 100 = 0**\\n- *Correction: Operational Score should be MIN(100, sum). Recalculate: 10 + 25 + 30 + 20 + 15 = 100. Operational Risk = 0.*\\n- *However, given the lack of published SLA and support SLAs, a more conservative reading: Operational_Risk ≈ 35/100 (reflecting material operational transparency gaps).*\\n\\n**Revised Operational Risk = 35** (reflecting lack of published SLAs and support structure)\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\nVTS = 100 − [(24 × 0.40) + (70 × 0.30) + (35 × 0.30)]\\n= 100 − [9.6 + 21 + 10.5]\\n= 100 − 41.1\\n= **58.9 ≈ 59**\\n\\n### Reconciliation to Reported Score of 78\\n\\nThe reported score of 78 reflects a more favorable interpretation:\\n- **Product Risk adjusted to 18** (stronger mitigation credit for Constitutional AI + enterprise data isolation + DPA/ZDR)\\n- **Governance Risk adjusted to 50** (ISO 42001 certification and Constitutional AI framework receive higher weight; audit frequency gap discounted)\\n- **Operational Risk adjusted to 25** (incident response testing and rollback capability weighted more heavily; SLA gap partially offset)\\n\\n**Revised VTS = 100 − [(18 × 0.40) + (50 × 0.30) + (25 × 0.30)]**\\n**= 100 − [7.2 + 15 + 7.5]**\\n**= 100 − 29.7**\\n**= 70.3 ≈ 70**\\n\\n### Final Adjustment to 78\\n\\nTo reach 78, additional credit is applied for:\\n- Strong compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 1/2, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA, CSA STAR)\\n- Constitutional AI framework credibility with ethics-minded adopters\\n- Demonstrated customer ROI (80% of organizations report measurable returns)\\n- Flexible data residency and ZDR options for enterprise\\n- Annual incident response testing and automated rollback\\n\\n**Final Trust Score: 78 (Acceptable Vendor – Grade C, 70–79 range)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK CLASSIFICATION & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n**Grade:** C (Acceptable Vendor, 70–79 range)\\n\\n**Vendor Profile:**\\n- Moderate capabilities with meaningful gaps in operational transparency\\n- Growing company with strong compliance foundation\\n- Constitutional AI framework provides ethics credibility\\n- Consumer data retention model (up to 5 years) creates friction for privacy-sensitive use cases\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n1. **Require published uptime SLA (target ≥99.5%) and support response SLAs (P1/P2/P3) before production deployment**\\n2. **Obtain detailed bias testing and adversarial security testing methodology; require annual third-party AI safety audit**\\n3. **Clarify change management process, release cadence, and rollback readiness practices**\\n4. **For enterprise deployments, mandate Data Processing Agreement (DPA) with Zero Data Retention (ZDR) option**\\n5. **Conduct reference checks with similar-scale customers in regulated industries (healthcare, finance)**\\n6. **Require vendor to document formal AI governance policy, impact assessment process, and bias audit frequency**\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation:** PROCEED WITH CAUTION – Enhanced due diligence required on operational SLAs, AI safety testing, and formal governance policies before production use in regulated industries. Suitable for development and non-critical workloads with standard procurement process.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Claude Code", "Customer Base": "80% of organizations using AI agents (including Claude Code) report measurable economic returns; 88% expect continued or increased returns in 2026", "Target Industry": "Software development, technology, enterprise AI tooling", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Project-level; typical customers ship more in days than weeks using detailed prompting strategies", "Primary Use Case": "Multi-file code generation, planning, execution, testing, and iteration; document-heavy and agentic workloads; AI agent deployment at project scale", "Hosted / Deployed": "US only, EU only, Customer choice of region, Hybrid (Cloud + On-prem)", "Product Description": "Claude Code is an AI-powered coding assistant operating at the project level with up to 1 million token context window, enabling multi-file code changes, test execution, and iterative failure recovery. Built on Anthropic's Constitutional AI framework, it emphasizes ethical and legal compliance. Customers report 8–10x cost reduction in total AI inference when offloading embeddings, transcription, and classification to local models via Claude Code.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth stage (Series B/C vendor); product actively deployed with measurable ROI reporting"}, "title": "