92764658-ea11-45f8-91e7-982258b5f1fa	38	38	31984c98-d0ce-4af0-b1c9-d7839c5414a7	87	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Anthropic – Claude Enterprise\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 82 (Trusted Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 85\\n- Compliance: 88\\n- Data Practices: 80\\n- AI Governance: 78\\n- Operations: 88\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAnthropic demonstrates strong enterprise readiness with comprehensive security certifications (SOC 2 Type I & II, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA), robust operational maturity (99.99% uptime SLA, established company with Series D+ funding), and differentiated AI safety approach via Constitutional AI. Primary strengths include mature governance framework, flexible data residency and zero-retention options, and proven customer ROI across legal, sales, and enterprise operations. Main gaps include incomplete bias testing documentation, limited detail on adversarial security testing frequency, and absence of published incident response testing results; these are typical for proprietary AI vendors and do not materially impair enterprise deployment readiness.\\n\\n**Scoring Methodology:**\\nApplied Vendor Trust Score formula from vector database (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]). Product Risk estimated at ~18 (Constitutional AI + HIPAA + strong benchmarks mitigate inherent LLM risk); Governance Risk at ~12 (SOC 2 Type II + ISO 42001 + documented policies); Operational Risk at ~0 (99.99% SLA, established company, automated rollback). Resulting VTS ≈ 82, placing vendor in \\"Trusted Vendor\\" (B-grade, 80–89 range) with standard procurement process and use-case fit validation recommended.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Claude Enterprise\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Legal document review and contract analysis (14 hrs/week savings); M&A advisory; AI-powered fundraising tools; enterprise search and summarization; creative task automation; legacy system operations automation; sales conversation coaching and repeatability\\n- **Target Industry:** Legal services, financial advisory (M&A), venture capital, enterprise operations, sales enablement\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (API-based)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Anthropic-hosted cloud; customer choice of region for data residency\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise (multi-user, multi-team)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; established customer base with documented ROI\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Named customers include GC AI (legal), HubSpot (creative), Yoodli (sales coaching), Duvo (enterprise operations); additional enterprise customers not named\\n- **Product Description:** Claude Enterprise is a proprietary large language model (LLM) platform emphasizing safety, interpretability, and steerable behavior through Constitutional AI—a training approach that embeds ethical constraints directly into model weights rather than relying solely on output filtering. The product offers long context windows, strong reasoning and coding benchmarks, and enterprise-grade security (SOC 2 Type II, HIPAA BAA, ISO 27001). Differentiated by developer productivity tools (Claude Code) and flexible data handling (zero-retention options, customer-controlled residency).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Anthropic (legal entity name not specified in attestation)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (AI Safety & Research)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; investors not specified in attestation\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (not specified in detail); data residency available in customer-chosen regions\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Model (LLM); proprietary, closed-source\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding, generation, reasoning, coding, summarization, analysis, and enterprise automation\\n- **Model Governance:** Constitutional AI framework embeds safety constraints directly into model training; staged deployment implied by enterprise product maturity; governance policy documented but not detailed in attestation\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified in detail; implied via enterprise controls and audit logs; no explicit advisory vs. autonomous classification provided\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary model; transparency level not specified; Constitutional AI approach suggests interpretability emphasis, but specific explainability features (citations, prompt-level control) not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data composition and curation methodology not detailed in attestation\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; Constitutional AI framework implies proactive bias mitigation, but formal red-team or third-party audit results not provided\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy exists (not detailed); Constitutional AI approach reflects strong ethical design philosophy; specific usage policies and safety guidelines not provided in attestation\\n- **Bias Audits:** Frequency and external evaluation methodology not specified; Constitutional AI training approach suggests proactive bias mitigation, but formal audit cadence and results not disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Admin controls, content filtering, and intervention mechanisms not detailed; audit logs available (see Section 11), enabling post-hoc review\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation not mentioned; typical for proprietary vendors under NDA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented incident response plan exists; testing status not specified (vendor attestation notes \\"documented but not tested\\")\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated rollback with manual trigger capability; enables rapid incident recovery\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Prompts, outputs, and metadata from API interactions; document uploads (legal, M&A, enterprise data); code submissions (Claude Code feature)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified; HIPAA BAA compliance and zero-retention options indicate capability to handle PHI and sensitive PII; customer data not used for model training (standard for enterprise SaaS)\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based interaction; chat interface; telemetry available (see Section 11)\\n- **Data Storage:** Anthropic-hosted cloud infrastructure; encryption standard (implied by SOC 2 Type II and ISO 27001); specific encryption algorithms and key management not detailed\\n- **Data Retention:** \\n  - **Standard (API users):** 30 days (updated to 7 days effective September 15, 2025)\\n  - **Enterprise (via DPA):** Configurable; up to 30 days for audit purposes\\n  - **Zero Data Retention (ZDR):** Available for qualifying Enterprise customers; prompts, outputs, and metadata immediately discarded after real-time abuse detection\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; specific regions not enumerated in attestation\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated per retention policy; on-request deletion available via DPA\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; typical cloud infrastructure (compute, storage) and payment processing assumed but not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type I (security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy)\\n  - SOC 2 Type II (same domains, tested over time period)\\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management System)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type II and ISO certifications imply third-party audit; specific audit firm, scope, and last audit date not provided in attestation\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Implied compliance via ISO 27001 and SOC 2 Type II alignment; explicit NIST mapping not provided\\n  - GDPR: Implied via ISO 27001 and data residency options; DPA availability suggests GDPR readiness; specific GDPR compliance statement not provided\\n  - CCPA: Not explicitly addressed in attestation\\n  - EU AI Act: Not explicitly addressed; Constitutional AI approach aligns with EU AI Act risk-mitigation philosophy, but formal readiness assessment not provided\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; indicates HIPAA-eligible product for healthcare use cases\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Data Processing Addendum (DPA) available; customer-controlled data residency and zero-retention options support GDPR compliance\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not explicitly stated; Constitutional AI framework and safety emphasis suggest alignment with high-risk AI requirements, but formal EU AI Act compliance roadmap not provided\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Frequency: Not specified (typical for SOC 2 Type II: annual)\\n  - Last Audit Date: Not provided\\n  - Audit Findings: Not provided (typically under NDA or available to customers only)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime); enterprise-grade commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified in attestation; typical enterprise support model assumed but not detailed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; automated rollback capability implies mature release process, but specific cadence and readiness practices not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; cloud infrastructure provider(s) and payment processor(s) assumed but not named\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; implied via Anthropic's own 99.99% SLA commitment\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Available; scope and export capability not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Available; export format and retention aligned with data retention policy (7–30 days standard, longer for Enterprise DPA customers)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Partial documentation available; Constitutional AI research papers and safety documentation likely available via Anthropic website and research publications; specific attestation evidence files not listed\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Available; red-team results, bias testing, and adversarial robustness evaluations likely available under NDA to enterprise customers; not disclosed in public attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary Assessment\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation:** **APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT**\\n\\nAnthropic demonstrates **Trusted Vendor** (B-grade) status with strong enterprise readiness across security, compliance, and operations. The company's Series D+ maturity, 99.99% uptime SLA, comprehensive certifications (SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA), and differentiated Constitutional AI safety approach position Claude Enterprise as a low-risk choice for regulated industries (healthcare, legal, financial services). Flexible data handling (zero-retention, customer-controlled residency) and documented incident response further reduce operational risk.\\n\\n**Primary Gaps (Non-Blocking):**\\n- Bias testing and adversarial security testing methodologies not publicly detailed; typical for proprietary vendors and addressable via NDA-protected documentation review\\n- Incident response plan documented but not tested; recommend requiring test results or third-party validation as contract condition\\n- EU AI Act readiness not explicitly stated; recommend clarifying compliance roadmap during procurement\\n\\n**Recommended Contract Conditions:**\\n1. Require evidence of incident response plan testing (tabletop or full-scale) within past 12 months\\n2. Confirm availability of bias audit results and red-team testing documentation under NDA\\n3. Clarify EU AI Act compliance roadmap and timeline for high-risk AI classification (if applicable to use case)\\n4. Confirm support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times) and escalation procedures for enterprise tier\\n5. Validate data residency options align with customer's data sovereignty requirements\\n\\n**Suitable Use Cases:** Legal document review, M&A analysis, enterprise search/summarization, sales enablement, creative task automation, healthcare (with HIPAA BAA), financial services (with GDPR/CCPA validation).", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Claude Enterprise", "Customer Base": "Named customers include GC AI (legal), HubSpot (creative), Yoodli (sales coaching), Duvo (enterprise operations); additional enterprise customers not named", "Target Industry": "Legal services, financial advisory (M&A), venture capital, enterprise operations, sales enablement", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (API-based)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise (multi-user, multi-team)", "Primary Use Case": "Legal document review and contract analysis (14 hrs/week savings); M&A advisory; AI-powered fundraising tools; enterprise search and summarization; creative task automation; legacy system operations automation; sales conversation coaching and repeatability", "Hosted / Deployed":