1b984d08-d447-4829-9141-0d4b0f6cd888	38	38	5c63e968-b38c-47dc-9e5c-d6424ee060d7	81	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Anthropic – Claude Team\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 75\\n- Compliance: 78\\n- Data Practices: 70\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 68\\n- Company Maturity: 72\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAnthropic demonstrates solid foundational capabilities in compliance (HIPAA BAA, data residency options) and security posture, placing it in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" range (70–79 per the rubric). However, the vendor exhibits moderate gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented governance policy, summary-only training data documentation), operational maturity (99.0% SLA is below enterprise standard of 99.95%, incident response untested), and limited evidence of bias testing or adversarial security testing. The company's growth-stage maturity (Series B/C, founded 2021) and strong focus on AI safety principles (Claude's Constitution) are strengths, but the lack of detailed governance documentation, tested incident response, and comprehensive bias audits prevent a higher score. Recommended action: Standard procurement process with enhanced due diligence on governance and incident response testing before production deployment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Claude Team\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise collaboration, legal workflows, M&A advisory, AI-powered agent building, bug fixing, enterprise operations automation, sales enablement\\n- **Target Industry:** Legal services, financial advisory, software development, enterprise operations, sales\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; customer choice of data residency region\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Team-based collaboration; supports shared projects and workplace connectors\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C vendor)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified\\n- **Product Description:** Claude Team is an AI-powered collaboration platform featuring a 200K context window for processing long documents, an \\"Artifacts\\" feature for generating standalone code and documents, and enterprise-grade data handling with HIPAA BAA eligibility. The product emphasizes AI safety through Anthropic's \\"Claude's Constitution\\" framework and offers flexible data residency and retention options, including Zero Data Retention (ZDR) for qualifying customers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Anthropic (legal entity name not specified in attestation)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth stage); revenue not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not listed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (implied: North America and potentially international via cloud regions)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary large language model (Claude); closed-source architecture\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding, code generation, document analysis, long-context reasoning (200K token context window), content generation (Artifacts feature)\\n- **Model Governance:** Guided by \\"Claude's Constitution\\" framework emphasizing AI safety and ethical compliance; staged deployment implied but not detailed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; Artifacts feature enables user review and editing of generated content\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary model; transparency limited to user-facing features (Artifacts, context window visibility); no detailed model card or explainability framework documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Summary only; no detailed lineage, source attribution, or composition breakdown provided\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no evidence of red-team testing, third-party bias audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type of adversarial security testing documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** \\"Claude's Constitution\\" framework guides safety and ethical compliance; specific usage policies and safety guidelines not detailed in attestation\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluation schedule documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Admin controls and content filtering not detailed; user-level review via Artifacts feature; no documented intervention workflows or escalation procedures\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards, model cards, or release impact documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level unclear\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; deployment rollback capability confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Documents, code, conversations, structured workflows, enterprise communications (via workplace connectors)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; HIPAA BAA eligibility indicates PII handling capability, but extent of PII processing and safeguards not detailed\\n- **Data Collection:** API, chat interface, workplace connectors; collection scope not fully specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure; encryption status not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** \\n  - Consumer products: up to 5 years if used for model improvement; otherwise 30 days\\n  - Enterprise API logs: standard 30-day retention\\n  - Zero Data Retention (ZDR): available for qualifying customers\\n  - Long-term storage: 2–7 years for policy-flagged prompts and compliance analytics\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (specific regions not listed)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied); automated deletion for standard retention periods\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and frequency not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA compliance confirmed; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; compliance scope and audit evidence not detailed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documentation provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; no audit schedule or results provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.0% (3.7 days/year downtime allowed); below enterprise standard (99.95%)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no release process, frequency, or readiness practices documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no frequency of risk assessments or vendor SLA reviews documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; no SLAs from critical vendors provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Available; scope and export capability not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Available; export format and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Not provided in attestation; governance policies and testing results not uploaded\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Available; specific results and NDA terms not disclosed in attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Classification:** **ACCEPTABLE VENDOR – Standard Procurement with Enhanced Due Diligence**\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\nAnthropic's Claude Team scores in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" range (70–79) due to solid compliance foundations (HIPAA BAA, flexible data residency) and documented security capabilities (automated rollback, incident response plan). However, the vendor exhibits material gaps in:\\n\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency** (65/100): No documented governance policy, bias audit schedule, or detailed training data lineage\\n2. **Operational Maturity** (68/100): 99.0% SLA is below enterprise standard; incident response untested\\n3. **Adversarial Testing** (not scored): No evidence of red-teaming or penetration testing\\n4. **Regulatory Readiness** (partial): HIPAA BAA confirmed, but GDPR, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n\\n**Recommended Actions Before Deployment:**\\n\\n1. **Require vendor to provide:**\\n   - Documented AI governance policy with bias audit schedule and methodology\\n   - Evidence of incident response plan testing (tabletop or full-scale exercise)\\n   - Training data composition summary and bias testing results (under NDA if necessary)\\n   - GDPR Data Processing Agreement (DPA) and EU AI Act compliance roadmap\\n\\n2. **Negotiate contract conditions:**\\n   - Upgrade SLA to 99.5% minimum (or 99.95% for production use cases)\\n   - Define support response SLAs by severity (P1/P2/P3)\\n   - Require quarterly compliance attestations and annual third-party audit\\n\\n3. **Pilot approach:**\\n   - Deploy in non-production environment first (e.g., legal document review, non-PHI use cases)\\n   - Monitor for 60 days; validate data retention and deletion processes\\n   - Escalate to production only after governance gaps are closed\\n\\n**Pass/Fail Criteria:**\\n- **PASS:** Vendor provides tested incident response plan, documented bias audit schedule, and GDPR DPA within 30 days\\n- **FAIL:** Vendor unable to provide governance documentation or refuses to upgrade SLA; consider alternative vendors (e.g., OpenAI, Google Vertex AI) with higher operational maturity\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessor Notes:** This assessment is based on vendor self-attestation data. Independent verification of compliance certifications, audit results, and security controls is recommended before contract execution.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Claude Team", "Customer Base": "Not specified", "Target Industry": "Legal services, financial advisory, software development, enterprise operations, sales", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Team-based collaboration; supports shared projects and workplace connectors", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise collaboration, legal workflows, M&A advisory, AI-powered agent building, bug fixing, enterprise operations automation, sales enablement", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; customer choice of data residency region", "Product Description": "Claude Team is an AI-powered collaboration platform featuring a 200K context window for processing long documents, an \\"Artifacts\\" feature for generating standalone code and documents, and enterprise-grade data handling with HIPAA BAA eligibility. The product emphasizes AI safety through Anthropic's \\"Claude's Constitution\\" framework and offers flexible data residency and retention options, including Zero Data Retention (ZDR) for qualifying customers.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C vendo