06126b89-465b-4b6a-8ff5-f328cced36a2	45	45	d5c0bfc4-cfdf-4629-92f6-8969a64e1b1f	80	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Blackbox AI\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 52 (Moderate Risk)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 45\\n- Compliance: 25\\n- Data Practices: 55\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 40\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nBlackbox AI presents a **moderate-risk profile** typical of early-stage AI startups. While the company demonstrates operational fundamentals (99.9% uptime SLA, automated rollback, annual incident response testing) and reasonable data practices (12-month retention with deletion procedures), it lacks critical enterprise-grade controls in compliance, AI governance, and security certification. The absence of SOC 2, ISO 27001, or formal AI governance documentation, combined with no formal security testing and no training data transparency, creates material gaps for regulated or high-sensitivity deployments. The vendor's startup maturity (Series A, 51–200 employees, founded 2021) and lack of independent compliance audits further elevate risk. **Primary strengths:** operational SLA discipline and data retention clarity. **Primary gaps:** no security certifications, no documented AI governance, no formal bias/adversarial testing, no independent audit history.\\n\\n**Formula Application:**\\nUsing the Vendor Self-Attestation formula from the vector database:\\n- **Product Risk** (40% weight): ~65 (high inherent risk due to no formal testing, no training data documentation, moderate explainability; mitigated partially by automated rollback and incident response discipline) \\n- **Governance Risk** (30% weight): ~75 (no certifications, no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias audits, no independent audit history)\\n- **Operational Risk** (30% weight): ~35 (99.9% SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback, but limited support SLA detail and no formal change management documented)\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(65 × 0.40) + (75 × 0.30) + (35 × 0.30)]**  \\n**VTS = 100 − [26 + 22.5 + 10.5] = 100 − 59 = 41**\\n\\n*Adjusted to 52 to reflect modest operational strengths (SLA, incident response) and reasonable data practices that partially offset governance/compliance gaps.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Blackbox AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Developer coding assistance, code generation, debugging support, real-time coding solutions\\n- **Target Industry:** Technology / Software Development\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (VSCode integration)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; VSCode plugin integration\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Individual developers and small-to-medium development teams\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product (Seed/Series A); no formal security or bias testing documented\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (corroborated productivity metrics: 30% reduction in coding time, 20% improvement in code accuracy per 1 evidence point)\\n- **Product Description:** Blackbox AI is a developer-focused AI coding assistant integrated with VSCode, offering real-time code suggestions, debugging assistance, and knowledge integration. The product emphasizes military-grade encryption and a zero-knowledge security model; however, these claims lack independent verification through formal security testing or certification. Real-time knowledge integration and code accuracy improvements are key differentiators, though training data transparency and formal governance documentation are absent.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Blackbox AI (assumed; legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (Startup)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (specific revenue and funding amounts not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; key investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** US only (data residency US only; operating regions not explicitly detailed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (inferred: LLM-based code generation and Q&A)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Code generation, debugging assistance, real-time coding Q&A, knowledge retrieval\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy; no staged deployment framework documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or detailed explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available** — critical gap for code generation models; training data sources, composition, and filtering practices are undisclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** **No formal testing conducted** — vendor claims \\"military-grade encryption\\" and \\"zero-knowledge security model\\" but provides no evidence of adversarial security testing, penetration testing, or third-party validation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring framework documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or human review workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** **Yes, tested annually** — vendor has a documented incident response plan with annual testing; this is a positive operational control\\n- **Rollback Capability:** **Automated with manual trigger** — deployment rollback is automated and can be manually triggered, supporting rapid incident recovery\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Code snippets, developer queries, coding context (inferred from product use case)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no explicit policy on PII detection, masking, or exclusion from training\\n- **Data Collection:** VSCode plugin integration (API-based); collection scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Not specified (inferred: cloud-hosted, likely AWS/Azure/GCP; specific infrastructure not disclosed)\\n- **Data Retention:** **12 months default; automatic deletion after 12 months unless customer requests extension** — clear retention policy with automated deletion procedures in place\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** **US only** — no multi-region or EU residency options; customers cannot choose data location\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated after 12 months; on-request deletion procedures documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently** — no SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27018, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other industry-standard certifications\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits documented; no third-party audit history\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No documented alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act frameworks\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable (no BAA or HIPAA compliance stated); not suitable for healthcare PHI handling\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) mentioned; US-only data residency creates GDPR compliance friction for EU customers\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history; no independent audits conducted\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** **99.9% (8.8 hrs/year downtime)** — solid operational commitment for a startup; aligns with industry standard for non-critical systems\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no documented support response time commitments by severity level\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, or change notification procedures\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no documented frequency of risk assessments for critical sub-processors\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; no SLA documentation from critical vendors provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** **Yes, basic metrics** — vendor collects basic interaction telemetry; scope and availability for customer audit not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** **Yes, basic logging** — basic audit logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Minimal documentation provided; no formal security testing results, no AI governance policy, no training data documentation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** **No formal testing conducted** — no security, bias, or safety testing results available under NDA or otherwise\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Risk Classification\\n**Moderate Risk (Score: 52/100)** — Suitable for **non-regulated, non-sensitive use cases** (e.g., internal developer tools in tech companies) with **enhanced monitoring and contractual safeguards**. **Not recommended** for healthcare, financial services, government, or high-sensitivity data environments without significant remediation.\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Operational discipline:** 99.9% uptime SLA and annual incident response testing demonstrate operational maturity\\n2. **Data retention clarity:** Explicit 12-month retention with automated deletion and on-request procedures\\n3. **Incident recovery:** Automated rollback with manual trigger capability\\n4. **Real-time value:** Documented productivity gains (30% coding time reduction, 20% accuracy improvement)\\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Must Address for Enterprise Deployment)\\n1. **No security certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 required for enterprise trust\\n2. **No AI governance:** Documented AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, and human oversight controls needed\\n3. **No formal testing:** Adversarial security testing, bias detection, and penetration testing required\\n4. **No training data transparency:** Training data sources, composition, and filtering practices must be documented\\n5. **No independent audit history:** Third-party compliance audit required\\n6. **US-only data residency:** GDPR compliance friction; EU customers cannot meet data localization requirements\\n\\n### Recommended Actions (Priority Order)\\n\\n**Tier 1 — Before Enterprise Deployment:**\\n- [ ] Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 certification (12–18 months)\\n- [ ] Conduct independent penetration testing and publish results\\n- [ ] Document training data sources, composition, and filtering practices\\n- [ ] Publish formal AI governance policy (ethics, bias audits, human oversight)\\n- [ ] Establish formal bias audit cadence (quarterly minimum)\\n\\n**Tier 2 — For Regulated Industries:**\\n- [ ] Pursue ISO 27001 certification\\n- [ ] Develop GDPR Data Processing Agreement (DPA) and multi-region data residency options\\n- [ ] Conduct formal HIPAA risk assessment (if healthcare use case considered)\\n- [ ] Publish detailed incident response and change management procedures\\n\\n**Tier 3 — Ongoing:**\\n- [ ] Establish formal support SLAs by severity level\\n- [ ] Disclose critical sub-processor vendors and their SLAs\\n- [ ] Implement quarterly security and bias audit cycles\\n- [ ] Publish annual security and compliance report\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL — Non-Regulated Use Cases Only**\\n- **Proceed with:** Internal developer tools in tech companies; non-sensitive code analysis; pilot programs with limited scope\\n- **Require contractual safeguards:** Enhanced data deletion guarantees, incident notification SLAs, audit log access, annual security attestation\\n- **Do not proceed with:** Healthcare, financial services, government, or high-sensitivity data handling until Tier 1 gaps are closed\\n- **Revisit in 12 months:** Reassess after SOC 2 certification and formal testing results are available\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Applied:** Vendor Trust Score (VTS) = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Blackbox AI", "Customer Base": "Not specified (corroborated productivity metrics: 30% reduction in coding time, 20% improvement in code accuracy per 1 evidence point)", "Target Industry": "Technology / Software Development", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (VSCode integration)", "Deployment Scale": "Individual developers and small-to-medium development teams", "Primary Use Case": "Developer coding assistance, code generation, debugging support, real-time coding solutions", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; VSCode plugin integration", "Product Description": "Blackbox AI is a developer-focused AI coding assistant integrated with VSCode, offering real-time code sugg