sions\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (consumer user base; enterprise customer count not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Character.AI is a proprietary LLM-powered chat platform offering personalized, age-appropriate conversations with custom AI characters. The platform emphasizes safety through advanced content classifiers and separate model versions for users under 18, reducing exposure to sensitive content. Unique value lies in user-created characters and engagement-focused design; however, the product lacks formal security certifications and independent compliance validation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Character.AI (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (specific figures not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Menlo Park, CA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: primarily US-based; global consumer reach likely)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary Large Language Model (LLM)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Conversational AI; personalized dialogue generation; character-based interaction; content filtering for age-appropriate responses\\n- **Model Governance:** Age-gated model versions (separate LLM for users under 18); continuous updates; no formal staged deployment or safety framework documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Advanced classifiers for content filtering; moderation infrastructure implied but not detailed; no explicit human-in-the-loop approval workflow documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level transparency, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Continuously updated (specific cadence not specified)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available** — critical gap for enterprise trust\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; age-gating suggests awareness of demographic sensitivity but no red-team, third-party audit, or statistical monitoring disclosed\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing documented; no frequency or scope provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy provided; pain points mention \\"safe and moderated environment\\" and \\"safety features\\" but formal policy framework not disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits documented; no external evaluations or internal audit frequency specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Content filtering via classifiers; no explicit admin controls, intervention workflows, or audit trails for moderation decisions documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release impact assessments provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested** — represents moderate maturity gap (formula: tested_annually = 15 pts; documented_not_tested = 10 pts → **10 points**)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (formula: automated_manual_trigger = 12 points)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Chat messages, user-generated character definitions, interaction history, user profile data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified; privacy policy referenced but specific PII handling practices (e.g., whether customer data used for training) not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** Chat interface; API not mentioned; telemetry collection scope not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not disclosed\\n- **Data Retention:** **Vague policy** — \\"Character.AI retains user data as described in their privacy policy\\" with options to delete personal information and deactivate accounts, but **specific retention periods not disclosed** (formula: informal = 3 points)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; inferred US-based (Menlo Park HQ) but no explicit residency options or GDPR/CCPA data localization commitments documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** User-initiated deletion and account deactivation available; automated deletion timelines not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not identified; payment processor not specified; authentication provider not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently** — no SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other security/compliance certifications\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit documented; no third-party review evidence provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: No NIST alignment documented\\n  - GDPR: No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance statement provided\\n  - CCPA: No CCPA compliance documentation\\n  - EU AI Act: No EU AI Act readiness assessment or engagement documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable (consumer product); no BAA eligibility\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No DPA availability confirmed; data residency and processing terms not transparent\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history; no third-party or internal audit schedule disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.5% (1.8 days/year downtime allowed) — **moderate for consumer SaaS; below enterprise standard of 99.9%+**\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; continuous model updates mentioned but no formal release process, testing gates, or rollback readiness practices documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not identified; payment processor not identified; authentication provider not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment frequency or process documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No vendor SLAs from critical sub-processors disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (search impressions, clicks, conversions reported; detailed telemetry scope not specified)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** **Minimal** — no formal testing results, no policy documentation uploaded, no model cards or safety reports provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** **No formal testing conducted** — critical gap for enterprise evaluation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Applied Vector Database Formulas:\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation** (from Formula Chunk 1 & 4):\\n- Certifications: 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO, HIPAA, etc.)\\n- Assessment Quality: 0 points (no third-party audit; self-assessment only = 3 pts, but no self-assessment evidence provided)\\n- Policies: 3 points (informal data retention only; no incident response testing, no privacy policy detail, no AI ethics policy)\\n- Operational Controls: 12 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 12 points (automated_manual_trigger rollback = 12; no oversight, monitoring, or version control documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 5 points (founded 2021 = 3–5 years → 0 pts base; startup stage = -5 adjustment; 201–1,000 employees = growth stage; no profitable/funded status = 0 pts; net = 5 pts conservative)\\n- **Governance Score: 0 + 0 + 3 + 12 + 5 = 20 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk: 100 − 20 = 80**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation** (from Formula Chunk 1):\\n- SLA: 99.5% uptime = 25 points (below 99.9% enterprise standard; formula: 99.5% ≈ 25 pts)\\n- Incident Management: 10 points (documented but not tested = 10 pts; formula: tested_annually = 30, documented_not_tested = 10)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 15 points (SaaS cloud-hosted but no multi-tenant enterprise architecture documented; inferred = 15 pts)\\n- Stability: 10 points (founded 2021, 3 years old, startup stage, no profitability disclosed = 10 pts; formula: 3–5 years = 0 pts base, but startup risk = −10)\\n- Support: 0 points (no support SLAs documented; no 24/7 support or dedicated TAM mentioned = 0 pts)\\n- **Operational Score: 25 + 10 + 15 + 10 + 0 = 60 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Operational Risk: 100 − 60 = 40**\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation** (from Formula Chunk 1):\\n- Inherent Risk: 75 (consumer product with PII/chat data, no formal testing, proprietary model = high inherent risk)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.35 (age-gating + content filters present, but no formal bias testing, no training data documentation, no adversarial testing = weak controls)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.60 (no third-party audit, no formal testing, basic telemetry only = low confidence)\\n- **Product Risk: 75 × (1 − 0.35) × 0.60 = 75 × 0.65 × 0.60 = 29.25 ≈ 29**\\n\\n**Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** (from Formula Chunk 1):\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\nVTS = 100 − [(29 × 0.40) + (80 × 0.30) + (40 × 0.30)]\\nVTS = 100 − [11.6 + 24.0 + 12.0]\\nVTS = 100 − 47.6\\nVTS = 52.4 ≈ 52\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted Trust Score: 38** (further reduced due to: no certifications, no independent audit, no formal AI safety testing, vague data retention policy, no regulatory framework alignment, startup maturity stage)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## TRUST SCORE INTERPRETATION\\n\\n**Grade: F (0–59 range) — Review Required**\\n\\nPer the vector database rubric (Formula Chunk 1, Section 1.5.3):\\n- **Classification:** Review Required\\n- **Vendor Profile:** Critical deficiencies; unproven capabilities; high risk\\n- **Recommended Action:** Reject for regulated/sensitive use; consider for low-stakes, non-production, consumer-only deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## KEY STRENGTHS\\n\\n1. **Product Innovation:** Age-gated LLM and content filtering demonstrate thoughtful safety design for consumer use\\n2. **Operational Resilience:** 99.5% SLA and automated rollback show operational maturity\\n3. **Engagement Metrics:** Documented user growth (+200% impressions, +160% clicks) indicates product-market fit\\n4. **Basic Telemetry & Logging:** Interaction data and audit logs available for monitoring\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CRITICAL GAPS\\n\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2, ISO 27001, or equivalent undermines enterprise trust\\n2. **No Independent Compliance Audit:** No third-party validation of security, data practices, or regulatory alignment\\n3. **No Formal AI Safety Testing:** No training data documentation, bias audits, or adversarial testing; critical for LLM products\\n4. **Vague Data Retention Policy:** Specific retention periods not disclosed; unclear if customer data used for model training\\n5. **No Regulatory Framework Alignment:** No GDPR DPA, CCPA compliance statement, or EU AI Act readiness; unsuitable for regulated industries\\n6. **Incident Response Not Tested:** Plan documented but never exercised; reduces confidence in crisis response\\n7. **Startup Maturity:** Founded 2021; Series A stage; limited track record for enterprise partnerships\\n8. **No Formal AI Governance:** No documented ethics policy, bias audit program, or human-in-the-loop oversight framework\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### **For Consumer / Non-Regulated Use:**\\n- ✅ **Acceptable** for B2C chat, education, entertainment applications\\n- Implement basic data minimization (avoid collecting sensitive PII)\\n- Monitor uptime and support responsiveness\\n\\n### **For Enterprise / Regulated Use:**\\n- ❌ **Not Recommended** without major remediation:\\n  1. Require SOC 2 Type 2 certification (12–18 month timeline)\\n  2. Commission independent security audit and AI safety assessment\\n  3. Provide explicit data retention policy and GDPR DPA\\n  4. Document training data sources and bias testing methodology\\n  5. Conduct and document incident response drill\\n  6. Establish enterprise SLA (99.9%+) and dedicated support\\n\\n### **Procurement Path:**\\n- **Pilot Only:** If enterprise interest exists, limit to non-production pilot with data minimization\\n- **Contract Conditions:** Require vendor roadmap for SOC 2, audit, and regulatory compliance within 12 months\\n- **Alternative:** Evaluate mature competitors (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, Cohere) with established compliance posture\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Framework:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification (Vector Database)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Character.AI", "Customer Base": "Not specified (consumer user base; enterprise customer count not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Consumer (B2C); education; entertainment", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Consumer-scale; typical user engagement metrics show +200% search impressions, +160% clicks, +120% conversions", "Primary Use Case": "Personalized AI-driven conversations, creative character interaction, safe moderated chat environment (particularly for teens)", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "Character.AI is a proprietary LLM-powered chat platform offering personalized, age-appropriate conversations with custom AI characters. The platform emphasizes safety through advanced content classifiers and separate model versions for users under 18, reducing exposure to sensitive content. Unique value lies in user-created characters and engagement-focused design; however, the p