y, support\n  2. Governance risk (21.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Raise Governance (79.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
021f1e83-96ce-431c-9f9b-14715fea5d8f	54	54	0438a3c8-9dc6-44dc-9d47-2693d181c496	89	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Clari Copilot\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 74\\n- Company Maturity: 82\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nClari Copilot scores in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" range (70–79) due to solid foundational security and compliance posture, established company maturity (11+ years, Series D+, profitable), and reasonable operational reliability (99.9% SLA). However, significant gaps in AI governance, training data transparency, and bias testing limit the score. The vendor demonstrates moderate security controls (ISO 27001, SOC 2 Type 2) and GDPR compliance, but lacks documented AI ethics policies, formal bias audits, and adversarial testing—critical for enterprise AI deployments. Data practices are acceptable but limited to US residency with no customer choice. The absence of formal AI safety testing and training data documentation represents the primary risk driver; these gaps must be addressed via contract conditions before deployment in regulated or high-stakes revenue operations contexts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Clari Copilot\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Revenue operations optimization; real-time forecasting, predictive analytics, and operational efficiency across sales, marketing, customer success, and finance teams.\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise B2B SaaS, financial services, and organizations with complex revenue operations.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (vendor-managed); US-only data residency.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise multi-tenant (typical customer: mid-market to enterprise revenue teams).\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Product stage not specified; interaction data available (basic metrics); no formal testing conducted.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; typical ROI cited as 30% improvement in forecasting accuracy and 20% reduction in manual processing time.\\n- **Product Description:** Clari Copilot is a cloud-native AI-powered revenue operations platform that integrates with CRM and ERP systems to provide real-time big data analytics and predictive insights. The product aligns sales, marketing, customer success, and finance teams through unified visibility and automated forecasting. It offers moderate explainability features and is GDPR-compliant with ISO 27001 and SOC 2 Type 2 certifications, though formal AI safety testing and bias audits are not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Clari (legal entity name not specified; operating as Clari Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2012\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Sunnyvale, CA, USA; specific investors not listed.\\n- **Operating Regions:** US-based; data residency US-only; global customer reach implied but not detailed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; vendor describes \\"big data analytics and predictive insights\\" but does not disclose underlying model architecture (LLM, custom-trained, ensemble, etc.).\\n- **Model Purpose:** Predictive analytics (forecasting), real-time insights generation, operational pattern recognition across revenue data.\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not disclosed.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of advisory vs. autonomous decision modes, monitoring workflows, or intervention capabilities.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate explainability features noted; prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available. This is a significant gap for enterprise AI deployments.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; frequency and type not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits documented; frequency and external evaluations not available.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human oversight capabilities not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, release documentation, or impact assessments provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested. Maturity level unclear; annual testing recommended before enterprise deployment.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger. Deployment rollback is supported but requires manual intervention; instant automated rollback not available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Revenue operations data (sales pipeline, forecasts, customer success metrics, finance data); specific data types (documents, communications, structured records) not detailed.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed.\\n- **Data Collection:** API and integration-based collection (CRM/ERP systems); specific collection mechanisms not detailed.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards not disclosed.\\n- **Data Retention:** Data is not retained after account termination (zero-retention option available by default).\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only; no customer choice for data residency or multi-region deployment.\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automatic deletion upon account termination; on-request deletion not explicitly stated.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 (Security, Availability, Processing Integrity, Confidentiality, Privacy)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - CSA STAR Level 1 (Cloud Security Alliance)\\n  - GDPR Compliant\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - GDPR: Compliant (stated)\\n  - NIST: Not mentioned\\n  - CCPA: Not mentioned\\n  - EU AI Act Readiness: Not mentioned\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not mentioned; BAA eligibility not stated. (Not applicable for revenue operations use case unless processing healthcare financial data.)\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes, stated as GDPR-compliant; Data Protection Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed.\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not mentioned; no engagement or preparation documented.\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit frequency and most recent audit date not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance). This is a standard enterprise SLA; no enhanced SLA tiers mentioned.\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not provided.\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, change approval process, and rollback readiness practices not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified.\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical sub-processors not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and export capabilities not detailed.\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified.\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; AI governance, bias testing, and training data documentation not available.\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established Company:** 11+ years in operation, Series D+ funding, profitable 3+ years—demonstrates stability and market viability.\\n2. **Solid Security Baseline:** ISO 27001, SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27701, and CSA STAR Level 1 certifications indicate mature security controls.\\n3. **GDPR Compliance:** Stated compliance with GDPR and data deletion upon account termination reduce privacy risk.\\n4. **Reasonable Uptime:** 99.9% SLA meets enterprise expectations for non-critical revenue operations.\\n5. **Automated Rollback:** Deployment rollback capability (automated with manual trigger) supports operational safety.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **No AI Safety Testing:** Absence of formal bias testing, adversarial security testing, and training data documentation is a significant risk for enterprise AI deployments.\\n2. **Missing AI Governance:** No documented AI ethics policy, human-in-the-loop workflows, or impact assessments.\\n3. **Untested Incident Response:** Incident response plan is documented but not tested; annual testing required before production deployment.\\n4. **Limited Data Residency:** US-only data location with no customer choice; may not meet regulatory requirements for EU or APAC customers.\\n5. **Incomplete Vendor Transparency:** Sub-processor details, support SLAs, and release cadence not disclosed.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT** with mandatory contract conditions:\\n\\n1. **AI Safety Roadmap:** Require vendor to provide a documented roadmap for implementing bias testing, adversarial security testing, and training data documentation within 6 months of contract execution.\\n2. **Incident Response Testing:** Mandate annual incident response plan testing with results provided to customer.\\n3. **Enhanced Support SLAs:** Negotiate explicit P1/P2/P3 response time commitments (e.g., P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours).\\n4. **Data Residency Flexibility:** Negotiate multi-region deployment or EU data residency option for GDPR-sensitive customers.\\n5. **Audit Access:** Require SOC 2 Type 2 audit report (most recent) and commitment to annual audits with findings disclosure.\\n6. **Sub-processor Disclosure:** Request list of critical infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors with their SLAs.\\n\\n### Risk Mitigation\\n- **Pilot Deployment:** Consider a 3–6 month pilot with a single revenue team before enterprise-wide rollout.\\n- **Monitoring:** Implement continuous monitoring of forecast accuracy and model drift; establish escalation procedures for anomalies.\\n- **Governance:** Assign a dedicated data steward to oversee data handling and compliance with retention policies.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Methodology:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification (VTS formula applied with product, governance, and operational risk weights)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "