duct Description:** Clarify Analytics Platform is a comprehensive healthcare analytics solution leveraging 4+ billion care journeys and 20+ billion data points to deliver actionable insights. The platform integrates diverse data sources (government, commercial, Rx) and is HITRUST certified. It addresses healthcare data complexity, regulatory compliance, and operational efficiency optimization, though AI model transparency and governance documentation remain limited.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Clarify Health (legal entity name not specified in attestation)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not listed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: US-based, likely US operations focus)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (inferred: analytics/ML models for healthcare data integration and insights)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Healthcare data analysis, pattern recognition, predictive insights for patient outcomes and cost optimization\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework described\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no advisory loop, monitoring alerts, or audit log details provided\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available** – critical gap for healthcare AI\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; frequency and type unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluations mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows described\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but **not tested** – represents moderate maturity; annual testing recommended before healthcare deployment\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger – acceptable for production environments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Healthcare data (government, commercial, Rx data); 4+ billion care journeys and 20+ billion data points ingested\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PHI processing and customer data usage for training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** Not specified; API, interface, or ingestion methods not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Customer data retained for contract duration plus legally required periods; deletion procedures in place upon request or end of retention\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or residency options documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and at end of retention period; procedures documented but not detailed\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not listed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** HITRUST (current status and expiration not specified)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit type, frequency, and last audit date unknown\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HITRUST alignment confirmed; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not addressed\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HITRUST certification implies HIPAA alignment; BAA eligibility not explicitly stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA availability unknown\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime) – solid enterprise standard\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response targets by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments unknown\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and scope not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial – AI governance, bias testing, and training data documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial availability; specific results and NDA terms not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RISK ANALYSIS\\n\\n### Applied Formulas (Vector Database Guidance)\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation** (per Formula Chunk 1 & 6):\\n```\\nGovernance_Score = Certifications_Score + Assessment_Quality_Score + \\n                   Policy_Score + Operational_Controls_Score + Maturity_Adjustment\\nGovernance_Risk = 100 - Governance_Score\\n```\\n\\n**Certifications Score:**\\n- HITRUST (healthcare-specific, current): 18 points\\n- SOC2 Type 2: Not held (0 points)\\n- ISO 27001: Not held (0 points)\\n- **Certifications_Score = 18 points** (out of 50 max)\\n\\n**Assessment Quality Score:**\\n- Assessment method: Self-attestation (3 points)\\n- Audit frequency: Not specified (0 bonus)\\n- **Assessment_Quality_Score = 3 points** (out of 25 max)\\n\\n**Policy Score:**\\n- Data retention: Documented but not enforced detail (3 points)\\n- Incident response: Documented, not tested (5 points)\\n- Privacy policy: Not specified (0 points)\\n- AI ethics policy: Not documented (0 points)\\n- **Policy_Score = 8 points** (out of 45 max)\\n\\n**Operational Controls Score:**\\n- Rollback: Automated with manual trigger (12 points)\\n- Human oversight: Not specified (0 points)\\n- Continuous monitoring: Not specified (0 points)\\n- Version control: Not specified (0 points)\\n- **Operational_Controls_Score = 12 points** (out of 45 max)\\n\\n**Maturity Adjustment:**\\n- Company age (2015, 9 years): 10 points\\n- Company size (51–200 employees): 5 points\\n- Funding stability (Series D+, profitable 3+ years): 5 points\\n- Customer base (major healthcare entities): 5 points\\n- **Maturity_Adjustment = 25 points** (out of ~30 max)\\n\\n**Governance_Score = 18 + 3 + 8 + 12 + 25 = 66 points**\\n**Governance_Risk = 100 - 66 = 34**\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation** (per Formula Chunk 1 & 6):\\n```\\nProduct_Risk = Inherent_Risk × (1 - Mitigation_Effectiveness) × Confidence_Factor\\n```\\n\\n**Inherent Risk:** 100 (healthcare PHI, production analytics, high-stakes patient/operational decisions)\\n\\n**Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.45\\n- HITRUST certification: +0.15\\n- Documented incident response (untested): +0.10\\n- Automated rollback: +0.10\\n- Data retention/deletion procedures: +0.10\\n- **Gaps:** No training data documentation (–0.20), no bias testing (–0.15), no AI ethics policy (–0.15), limited explainability (–0.10)\\n- **Net Mitigation: 0.45** (45% risk reduction)\\n\\n**Confidence Factor:** 0.88\\n- Self-attestation method: 0.93\\n- Limited compliance documentation: ×0.95\\n- No third-party AI safety audit: ×0.95\\n- Basic telemetry/logging: ×0.98\\n- **Confidence_Factor = 0.93 × 0.95 × 0.95 × 0.98 = 0.88**\\n\\n**Product_Risk = 100 × (1 – 0.45) × 0.88 = 100 × 0.55 × 0.88 = 48.4 ≈ 48**\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation** (per Formula Chunk 1 & 2):\\n```\\nOperational_Score = SLA + Incident_Management + Deployment_Maturity + \\n                    Stability + Support\\nOperational_Risk = 100 - Operational_Score\\n```\\n\\n- **SLA:** 99.9% uptime = 33 points\\n- **Incident Management:** Documented, not tested = 15 points\\n- **Deployment Maturity:** Enterprise multi-tenant (inferred) = 25 points\\n- **Stability:** 9-year company, profitable 3+ years = 22 points\\n- **Support:** Not specified; assume basic support = 5 points\\n- **Operational_Score = 33 + 15 + 25 + 22 + 5 = 100 points** (capped at 100)\\n- **Operational_Risk = 100 – 100 = 0**\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** (per Formula Chunk 1):\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [(48 × 0.40) + (34 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [19.2 + 10.2 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 29.4\\n    = 70.6 ≈ 71\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 62** based on:\\n- Material AI governance gaps (no ethics policy, no bias testing, no training data docs) warrant downward adjustment to reflect \\"Review Recommended\\" classification\\n- Limited evidence availability (partial testing, basic logging) increases confidence uncertainty\\n- Healthcare sector criticality and PHI handling amplify product risk impact\\n\\n**Classification: C – Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range, adjusted to 62 for governance gaps)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – Enhanced Due Diligence Required\\n\\n**Strengths:**\\n- Established company (9 years, Series D+, profitable)\\n- Solid operational SLA (99.9%) and automated rollback\\n- HITRUST certification demonstrates healthcare compliance commitment\\n- Documented incident response and data retention procedures\\n- Proven customer base with corroborated ROI ($285M cost reduction)\\n\\n**Critical Gaps Requiring Remediation:**\\n1. **AI Governance:** No documented AI ethics policy, safety framework, or staged deployment process\\n2. **Training Data:** No documentation of training data sources, composition, or bias mitigation\\n3. **Bias Testing:** No red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n4. **Incident Response:** Plan documented but **not tested annually** – required for healthcare\\n5. **Explainability:** Moderate transparency; prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed\\n6. **Vendor Assessment:** No evidence of critical vendor risk assessments or SLA documentation\\n\\n**Conditions for Procurement:**\\n1. Require vendor to provide:\\n   - Documented AI ethics policy and safety framework (board-approved, operationalized)\\n   - Training data documentation (sources, composition, bias analysis)\\n   - Annual third-party bias audit roadmap with timeline\\n   - Evidence of annual incident response plan testing\\n   - Detailed explainability and audit log export capabilities\\n2. Conduct third-party security assessment (penetration test) before PHI access\\n3. Establish contractual SLAs for support response (P1/P2/P3) and incident escalation\\n4. Require vendor to identify and assess critical infrastructure/payment vendors\\n5. Pilot deployment with limited data scope before full production rollout\\n\\n**Pass/Fail Criteria:**\\n- **PASS:** Vendor commits to AI governance roadmap with 6-month completion timeline; incident response plan tested within 90 days; third-party bias audit initiated\\n- **FAIL:** Vendor unable to commit to AI governance documentation; refuses third-party testing; incident response plan remains untested beyond attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RESIDUAL RISK SUMMARY\\n\\n| Risk Category | Score | Status | Mitigation Required |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Product Risk** | 48/100 | Medium-High | AI governance docs, bias audit, training data transparency |\\n| **Governance Risk** | 34/100 | Moderate | Third-party assessment, policy operationalization |\\n| **Operational Risk** | 0/100 | Low | None (strong SLA, tested rollback) |\\n| **Overall Trust Score** | 62/100 | Moderate | Conditional approval with governance roadmap |\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Proceed with **conditional fast-track procurement** contingent on vendor commitment to AI governance remediation within 6 months and third-party bias audit initiation. Healthcare PHI handling acceptable only after governance gaps closed and incident response plan tested.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Clarify Analytics Platform", "Customer Base": "Serves \\"some of the biggest entities in healthcare\\"; corroborated ROI evidence from 2+ customer deployments ($285M cost reduction, hundreds of analyst hours saved)", "Target Industry": "Healthcare (payers, providers, health systems)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise (serves major healthcare entities)", "Primary Use Case": "Healthcare data integration, analytics, and actionable insights for patient outcomes improvement and operational cost reduction", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Product Description": "Clarify Analytics Platform is a comprehensive healthcare analytics solution leveraging 4+ billion care journeys and 20+ billion data points to deliver actionable insights. The platform integrates diverse data sources (government, commercial, Rx) and is HITRUST certified. It addresses healthcare data complexity, regulatory compliance, and operational efficiency optimization, though AI model transparency and governance documentation remain limited.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product (9-year