2a606b90-5f6e-4afe-b4e0-a189ac6af1d1	57	57	a3cbbccd-a12a-4998-9017-8daf46b9279b	81	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: CLIPCHAMP\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 52 (Moderate Risk)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 25\\n- Data Practices: 45\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 72\\n- Company Maturity: 80\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nClipchamp receives a moderate trust score of 52, reflecting strong operational maturity and company stability (10+ years, 10,000+ employees, 99.99% uptime) offset by significant gaps in AI governance, compliance certifications, and security documentation. While the vendor demonstrates reliable infrastructure and reasonable data residency flexibility, the absence of formal security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), undocumented AI training data, untested incident response procedures, and lack of formal AI ethics governance create material risk for enterprise deployments. The product is suitable for general video editing but presents elevated risk for regulated industries (healthcare, finance) or use cases involving sensitive data processing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Clipchamp\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Cloud-based video editing, auto-captioning, AI voiceover generation, video production acceleration for enterprise and consumer users\\n- **Target Industry:** General enterprise (Microsoft 365 integration focus); media, marketing, communications, education\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (web-based)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted via Google Cloud Platform (GCP) and Microsoft cloud integration (OneDrive/SharePoint); no on-premises deployment option\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale (10,000+ employee company); typical deployment is per-user subscription\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (10+ years in market); no formal AI safety testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Subscription-based; specific pricing not disclosed\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (corroborated evidence indicates broad adoption with 99.99% availability and reported ROI metrics)\\n- **Product Description:** Clipchamp is a web-based video editing platform offering AI-powered features including auto-subtitle generation, realistic AI voiceovers, trim/cut, green screen, effects, and filters. The platform integrates seamlessly with Microsoft 365 (OneDrive/SharePoint) and eliminates the need for high-end hardware, reducing manual editing time by up to 50% according to customer reports. Video projects are stored on cloud infrastructure (Microsoft or Google Cloud), with data residency options available by customer choice.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Clipchamp (subsidiary of Microsoft; acquired 2021)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS (video editing platform)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2014\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+ (as part of Microsoft organization)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Not specified; Microsoft-owned (public company)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Microsoft (parent company); Headquarters: Brisbane, Queensland, Australia\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not enumerated; cloud infrastructure via GCP and Microsoft cloud)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/closed AI models; specific model architectures not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Auto-subtitle generation (speech-to-text), AI voiceover synthesis (text-to-speech), video effects and filtering\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; no staged deployment or safety framework described\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of human-in-the-loop review for AI-generated subtitles or voiceovers\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no explainability or transparency documentation available\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring described\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing or penetration testing results provided; no frequency specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy provided; usage policies and safety guidelines not disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations conducted or documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms for AI-generated outputs\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for AI features provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level unclear; no evidence of annual testing or validation\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; capability exists but testing status and reliability not confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Video files, user-generated content, project metadata, subtitle/voiceover data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no documentation on extent of PII processing or whether customer data is used for model training\\n- **Data Collection:** Web-based interface (browser); API integration with Microsoft 365 (OneDrive/SharePoint) and Google Cloud Platform\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud infrastructure (Microsoft cloud and Google Cloud Platform); encryption status not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Default retention aligned with Microsoft and Google standard practices; specific retention durations not disclosed; no explicit zero-retention option documented\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region supported; specific regions not enumerated\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion capability implied via cloud provider practices; automated deletion policies not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Microsoft (OneDrive/SharePoint), Google Cloud Platform (storage/compute); payment processors and authentication providers not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently held**; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other formal security certifications documented\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits conducted or documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not specified; no evidence of NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness assessment\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; no BAA (Business Associate Agreement) eligibility documented\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; no Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability documented\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history provided; no audit findings available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime); contractual commitment level not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no release process, frequency, or rollback readiness practices documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Microsoft (cloud infrastructure, OneDrive/SharePoint), Google Cloud Platform (storage/compute); payment processors and authentication providers not specified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No documented vendor risk assessment frequency or process\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Microsoft and GCP SLAs apply to underlying infrastructure; specific SLA terms not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited; no formal AI safety testing results, no AI governance policies, no bias audit reports, no penetration testing documentation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Operational Maturity:** 99.99% uptime SLA, 10+ year company history, 10,000+ employees, Microsoft backing\\n2. **Data Residency Flexibility:** Customer choice of cloud region supports multi-geography compliance needs\\n3. **Proven ROI:** Documented time savings (up to 50% reduction in manual editing) and broad adoption\\n4. **Cloud-Native Architecture:** Web-based deployment eliminates hardware constraints; seamless Microsoft 365 integration\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or equivalent certifications creates compliance friction for regulated industries\\n2. **Undocumented AI Governance:** No AI ethics policy, bias testing, training data documentation, or explainability framework\\n3. **Untested Incident Response:** Documented but not tested incident response plan; no evidence of annual validation\\n4. **Limited Compliance Readiness:** No HIPAA BAA, GDPR DPA, or EU AI Act readiness assessment documented\\n5. **Minimal Transparency:** Proprietary/closed models with no explainability or model documentation; no formal testing results\\n\\n### Recommended Actions for Procurement\\n\\n**For General Enterprise Use (Non-Regulated):**\\n- **Acceptable with standard controls:** Clipchamp is suitable for general video editing, marketing, and communications use cases in non-regulated industries\\n- **Recommended conditions:** Require written confirmation of data residency options, encryption standards, and data deletion procedures; establish SLA for support response times\\n\\n**For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Finance, Government):**\\n- **Not recommended without remediation:** Absence of SOC 2, HIPAA BAA, and formal AI governance creates unacceptable compliance risk\\n- **Mitigation roadmap required:** Vendor must commit to:\\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 certification within 12 months\\n  - HIPAA BAA eligibility (if healthcare use case)\\n  - Documented AI ethics policy and bias testing framework\\n  - Annual third-party security audit\\n  - Tested incident response plan with annual validation\\n\\n**For AI-Sensitive Use Cases (Autonomous Decision-Making, High-Stakes Content):**\\n- **Enhanced due diligence required:** Vendor must provide:\\n  - Training data documentation and composition analysis\\n  - Bias audit results from independent third party\\n  - Explainability framework for AI-generated subtitles/voiceovers\\n  - Human-in-the-loop review process for sensitive content\\n\\n### Risk Classification\\n**Current State:** Moderate Risk (52/100) — Acceptable for general enterprise video editing; elevated risk for regulated or sensitive use cases\\n**Post-Remediation Target:** Trusted Vendor (75–80/100) — Achievable with SOC 2, HIPAA BAA, and documented AI governance\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation  \\n**Methodology:** Vector-DB Formula Guidance (VTS framework) + Vendor Data Analysis", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Subscription-based; specific pricing not disclosed", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Clipchamp", "Customer Base": "Not specified (corroborated evidence indicates broad adoption with 99.99% availability and reported ROI metrics)", "Target Industry": "General enterprise (Microsoft 365 integration focus); media, marketing, communications, ed