sessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (58.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	2026-07-28 15:18:28.891716+05:30	** CodeRabbit demonstrates moderate trustworthiness with solid foundational security (SOC 2 Type 2) and reasonable company maturity (Series D+, founded 2023), but significant gaps in AI governance, testing rigor, and operational transparency limit confidence for enterprise deployment. The vendor lacks formal AI safety documentation, bias testing frameworks, and documented training data provenance—critical gaps for an AI code review tool that influences developer workflows and security decisions. While the product shows market traction and operational rollback capability, the absence of formal testing results, unclear uptime SLA, and minimal AI governance policy place this vendor in the "Review Recommended" category (D-grade, 60–69 range per vector-DB rubric). Recommend enhanced due diligence and contractual SLA clarification before production use in regulated or high-stakes environments. ---	4.3717	11	42	17.6487	B	Trusted Vendor	{"llm": {"error": null, "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** CodeRabbit demonstrates moderate trustworthiness with solid foundational security (SOC 2 Type 2) and reasonable company maturity (Series D+, founded 2023), but significant gaps in AI governance, testing rigor, and operational transparency limit confidence for enterprise deployment. The vendor lacks formal AI safety documentation, bias testing frameworks, and documented training data provenance—critical gaps for an AI code review tool that influences d