sistant designed to improve medical decision-making and triage accuracy during patient interactions and emergency calls. The product claims 30% reduction in manual processing time and 2x improvement in triage accuracy. However, the product lacks documented training data provenance, formal bias testing, and independent security/compliance validation, limiting its suitability for regulated healthcare environments without significant remediation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Corti.com (independent publication)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** August 2024\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth stage); revenue not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Copenhagen K, Denmark; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified\\n- **Model Purpose:** Medical decision-support, triage accuracy, automated documentation generation\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of advisory workflows, monitoring alerts, or audit trail integration\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); specific mechanisms not documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools specified\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring framework specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested (untested plan carries elevated risk)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Medical records, emergency call transcripts, patient interaction data (inferred from use case)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no documentation on extent of PII processing or whether customer data is used for model training/improvement\\n- **Data Collection:** Not specified (API, chat interface, or other collection method not documented)\\n- **Data Storage:** Not specified; encryption standard and infrastructure not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** General policy states data retained \\"only as long as necessary\\" for stated purposes and legal compliance; Usage Data retained for shorter periods or longer if used to improve security/functionality or legally required. No zero-retention or customer-configurable retention options specified.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or regional residency guarantees documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied by retention policy); automated deletion not confirmed\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently held\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit conducted\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No evidence of NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness assessment\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** No BAA (Business Associate Agreement) eligibility documented; vendor does not appear to meet HIPAA compliance requirements\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance documentation provided\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audits conducted; vendor is too early-stage for established audit cadence\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, rollback readiness practices, or change notification procedures\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment program documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available (export capability and SIEM integration not confirmed)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Minimal; no formal testing results, AI governance policies, or compliance documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Risk Factors\\n\\n1. **Extreme Immaturity:** Vendor founded August 2024 (< 6 months old); insufficient operational history for enterprise healthcare deployment\\n2. **Zero Compliance Posture:** No SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, or GDPR DPA; ineligible for regulated healthcare use without major remediation\\n3. **No AI Safety Framework:** Undocumented training data, no bias testing, no adversarial security testing, no formal AI governance policy\\n4. **Untested Incident Response:** Documented but not tested incident response plan carries elevated operational risk\\n5. **Opaque Data Practices:** PII handling, data residency, sub-processor relationships, and training data usage not disclosed\\n6. **Limited Transparency:** Moderate explainability claims unsupported by technical documentation\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**REJECT for healthcare PHI handling.** Vendor does not meet minimum compliance, security, or AI safety standards for regulated healthcare environments. Consider only for non-regulated, non-PHI pilot use cases with explicit risk acceptance and data isolation.\\n\\n### Remediation Path (if vendor pursues healthcare market)\\n\\n1. **Immediate (0–3 months):**\\n   - Achieve SOC 2 Type 2 certification\\n   - Publish comprehensive AI governance policy and bias testing framework\\n   - Conduct third-party penetration testing and document results\\n   - Provide complete training data documentation and bias audit results\\n\\n2. **Short-term (3–6 months):**\\n   - Obtain HIPAA BAA eligibility and execute DPA for GDPR compliance\\n   - Implement formal change management and tested incident response procedures\\n   - Establish vendor risk assessment program for critical sub-processors\\n   - Publish model card and system impact assessment\\n\\n3. **Medium-term (6–12 months):**\\n   - Achieve ISO 27001 certification\\n   - Conduct independent third-party compliance audit\\n   - Demonstrate 12+ months of stable operations and customer references\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Low (significant data gaps; many fields not specified by vendor)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Corti AI for Healthcare", "Customer Base": "Not specified", "Target Industry": "Healthcare (emergency services, hospitals, primary care)", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Medical decision-support during patient i