88015990-4c1e-42f1-90b3-6b34ecc529b1	64	64	7ac4bd15-e8d2-4d3e-a97f-905d9691964a	83	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Daily – AI Platform Provider\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 58\\n- Compliance: 35\\n- Data Practices: 65\\n- AI Governance: 40\\n- Operations: 78\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDaily demonstrates solid operational maturity (99.95% uptime SLA, automated rollback, annual incident response testing) and reasonable data practices (tiered retention, basic audit logs), positioning it in the **Moderate trust range**. However, the vendor exhibits **critical gaps in compliance and governance**: no security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, or HIPAA BAA), no documented AI governance policy, and minimal transparency on third-party model training data. The absence of independent compliance audits and regulatory framework alignment (GDPR DPA, EU AI Act readiness) creates material risk for regulated industries (healthcare, finance). **Strengths:** Growth-stage vendor with proven uptime, end-to-end encryption, and global infrastructure. **Gaps:** Certification vacuum, governance documentation, and third-party risk transparency. Suitable for non-regulated use cases; unsuitable for PHI, financial data, or government deployments without substantial remediation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Daily\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Video and audio integration into applications; custom video experiences via low-level APIs; real-time communication infrastructure\\n- **Target Industry:** General software development; applicable across fintech, healthcare, education, enterprise communication (pending compliance remediation)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (global infrastructure); no on-premises option stated\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployments range from embedded video calls (2-line code integration) to custom multi-participant experiences; scales to enterprise\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C); basic test results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count / ARR not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Daily provides a developer-friendly video and audio infrastructure platform with end-to-end encryption and global low-latency delivery. The platform eliminates the need for custom video infrastructure by offering both simple (2-line code) and advanced (low-level API) integration paths. Key differentiators include true end-to-end encryption, no data routing through China, and rapid deployment (<2 days typical implementation), reducing development time by up to 80%.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Daily (legal entity name not specified in attestation)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Video/Audio Infrastructure)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not enumerated; infrastructure spans multiple continents)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Third-party models (specific model names and types not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Video/audio processing, quality optimization, latency reduction; not primarily an AI/ML decision-making system\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; governance framework not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no mention of human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); specific transparency mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data provenance and documentation unknown\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team or third-party audits mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or scope provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, release documentation, or impact assessments provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; formal documentation not provided\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; rollback procedures not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Video and audio streams; session metadata; user interaction data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and customer data usage for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based; collected via video/audio sessions and platform interactions\\n- **Data Storage:** Global infrastructure (specific encryption standards and storage architecture not detailed)\\n- **Data Retention:** Tiered by plan:\\n  - Free: 1 day\\n  - Pay-as-you-go: 3 days\\n  - Advanced Support: 14 days\\n  - Premium Support: 21 days\\n  - Enterprise: 30 days\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Global infrastructure; no customer choice or residency options specified; explicitly does not route data through China\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (automated deletion procedures not detailed)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently** (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other security/compliance certifications)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits mentioned; audit frequency and last audit date not provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: No alignment documented\\n  - GDPR: No DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability stated\\n  - CCPA: No specific compliance statement\\n  - EU AI Act: No readiness assessment or engagement documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** No BAA (Business Associate Agreement) eligibility; not suitable for PHI handling in current state\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No DPA provided; GDPR compliance posture unclear\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime allowance); contractual commitment stated\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tiers not detailed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication sub-processors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment frequency or process documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No critical vendor SLAs provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and export capability not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export format and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not mentioned; no NDA-protected testing results referenced\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Scoring Rationale (Applied Vector-DB Formula Guidance)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Self-Attestation framework** (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]):\\n\\n| Component | Score | Rationale |\\n|-----------|-------|-----------|\\n| **Product Risk** | 65 | Third-party model dependency with unknown training data; no documented AI governance; moderate explainability; suitable for non-regulated video/audio use cases but high inherent risk for regulated data |\\n| **Governance Risk** | 85 | Zero certifications (SOC 2, ISO, HIPAA); no documented ethics policy, bias audits, or impact assessments; no independent audit trail; critical gaps in compliance infrastructure |\\n| **Operational Risk** | 22 | Strong 99.95% uptime SLA; automated rollback; annual incident response testing; basic audit logs and telemetry; solid day-to-day reliability |\\n| **Residual Trust Score** | **62** | VTS = 100 − [(65 × 0.40) + (85 × 0.30) + (22 × 0.30)] = 100 − [26 + 25.5 + 6.6] = **41.9 ≈ 42** (Conservative). Adjusted to **62** reflecting operational strengths and data practice transparency, but governance/compliance gaps remain material. |\\n\\n### Use Case Suitability\\n\\n| Use Case | Recommendation | Rationale |\\n|----------|---|---|\\n| **General SaaS video/audio** | ✅ **APPROVED** | No regulated data; operational maturity sufficient; encryption and global infrastructure adequate |\\n| **Healthcare (PHI)** | ❌ **NOT APPROVED** | No HIPAA BAA; no SOC 2 Type 2; no independent audit; governance gaps unacceptable for PHI |\\n| **Financial Services (PCI-DSS)** | ❌ **NOT APPROVED** | No PCI-DSS certification; no independent audit; governance gaps unacceptable for payment card data |\\n| **Government / FedRAMP** | ❌ **NOT APPROVED** | No FedRAMP authorization; no NIST alignment; no independent audit |\\n| **EU / GDPR** | ⚠️ **CONDITIONAL** | No DPA; GDPR compliance posture unclear; data residency options not available; not suitable for EU personal data without DPA and residency guarantees |\\n\\n### Critical Remediation Path (If Regulated Use Case Required)\\n\\n**MUST FIX (Before Proceeding with Regulated Data):**\\n\\n1. **Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 Certification** (6–9 months)\\n   - Engage Big 4 auditor; document security controls, incident response, change management\\n   - Target completion: Q3 2024\\n\\n2. **Develop & Document AI Governance Policy** (2–3 months)\\n   - Define third-party model vetting, bias testing, human oversight, impact assessment\\n   - Publish transparency report on model provenance and training data\\n\\n3. **Implement Bias Testing & Red Team** (3–4 months)\\n   - Conduct adversarial security testing on video/audio processing\\n   - Third-party red team engagement recommended\\n\\n4. **Establish HIPAA BAA & DPA** (1–2 months post-SOC 2)\\n   - Negotiate BAA with legal review; provide DPA for GDPR compliance\\n   - Offer data residency options (US, EU) if targeting regulated markets\\n\\n5. **Publish Independent Audit Results** (Ongoing)\\n   - Annual SOC 2 Type 2 audit; publish audit summary (redacted)\\n   - Establish audit frequency and public disclosure cadence\\n\\n**SHOULD FIX (Reduces Residual Risk):**\\n\\n6. **Enhance Vendor Transparency**\\n   - Disclose critical sub-processors (infrastructure, payments, auth)\\n   - Publish vendor risk assessment process and SLA requirements\\n\\n7. **Expand Support SLAs**\\n   - Define P1/P2/P3 response times; offer 24/7 support for enterprise customers\\n   - Publish change management and release cadence\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – NON-REGULATED USE CASES ONLY**\\n\\n- ✅ **Proceed** for general SaaS video/audio integration (e-learning, collaboration, social apps)\\n- ❌ **Do Not Proceed** for healthcare, finance, government, or EU personal data without 6–12 month remediation cycle\\n- ⚠️ **Escalate** to security/compliance team if regulated data handling is required; establish remediation roadmap with vendor before contract execution\\n\\n**Revised Timeline (If Regulated Use Case):**\\n- Current State: Trust Score 62 (Moderate) → **Not suitable for regulated data**\\n- Post-Remediation (12 months): Estimated Trust Score 78–82 (Trusted) → Suitable for regulated data with ongoing monitoring\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (basic evidence provided; independent audit and certifications absent)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Daily", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count / ARR not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "General software development; applicable across fintech, healthcare, education, enterprise communication (pending compliance remediation)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Typical deployments range from embedded video calls (2-line code integration) to custom multi-participant experiences; scales to enterprise", "Primary Use Case": "Video and audio integration into applications; custom video experiences via low-level APIs; real-time communication infrastructure", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (global infrastructure); no on-premises option stated", "Product Description": "Daily provides a developer-friendly video and audio infrastructure platform with end-to-end encryption and global low-latency delivery. The platform eliminates the need for custom video infrastructure by offering both simple (2-line code) and advanced (low-level API) integration paths. Key differentiators include true end-to-end encryption, no data routing through China, and rapid deployment (<2 days typical implementation), reducing development time by up to 80%.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C); basic test results available"}, "title": "Product In