9ad37825-7f3c-4466-9c16-4b9912d2af24	69	69	5c24452b-2607-4c4e-a07e-97af34c0b0db	78	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## DeepSeek Chat\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 42 (Low)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 15\\n- Data Practices: 25\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 40\\n- Company Maturity: 45\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDeepSeek Chat scores in the Low trust range (42/100) due to significant gaps across governance, compliance, and operational maturity. While the vendor demonstrates transparency through open-source models and cost efficiency, critical deficiencies in security certifications, data retention policies, incident response readiness, and formal AI governance frameworks present material risk for enterprise deployment. The startup stage (founded 2023, 51–200 employees) and absence of independent compliance audits, SLA commitments, and documented bias testing further constrain confidence. Strengths include open-model architecture and basic logging capability; primary gaps are lack of formal certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA), undefined data retention practices, and immature operational controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** DeepSeek Chat\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Cost-effective AI conversational and analytical tasks; operational cost reduction; high-performance language model inference\\n- **Target Industry:** Technology, Finance, Healthcare (cost-sensitive segments); enterprises seeking AGI-aligned research partnerships\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (vendor-operated); open-source model weights available for self-hosted deployment\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Vendor-hosted cloud platform; self-hosted via open-source weights\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified; typical deployments range from pilot (single team) to enterprise-wide\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product (vendor founded 2023); limited third-party validation\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor (cost-effective positioning; 40% operational cost reduction claimed vs. competitors)\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; metrics not disclosed\\n- **Product Description:** DeepSeek Chat is an open-source AI language model offering full transparency and high customization capability. The platform delivers performance comparable to or exceeding established competitors while reducing operational costs by up to 40% and manual processing time by 30%. Open-source architecture enables on-premises deployment and model fine-tuning; however, data retention practices remain ambiguous and formal security/compliance certifications are absent.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** DeepSeek (registered in 杭州 [Hangzhou], China)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (model developer and SaaS provider)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2023\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Not specified; Seed/Series A stage inferred from employee count and founding date\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: 杭州 (Hangzhou), China; investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** China (primary); global access via web platform; regional data residency options not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Model (LLM); open-source weights; transformer-based architecture (inferred)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding, generation, reasoning, and code analysis; positioned as AGI-research-aligned\\n- **Model Governance:** Focused on AGI research and development; formal safety framework and staged deployment policy not documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop review, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Full transparency via open weights; model architecture and training approach disclosed; prompt-level explainability and citation mechanisms not specified\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified; release cadence and model versioning practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training corpus composition, sources, and filtering practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools not mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not available; usage policies and safety guidelines not disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit program documented; frequency and external evaluation partners not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No documented admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows; autonomous decision-making scope not defined\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards, model documentation, or release impact assessments not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** In development; formal incident response procedures, escalation paths, and communication protocols not yet mature\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Manual rollback with documented procedures available; automated rollback or canary deployment practices not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Chat logs, user prompts, model outputs; code, documents, and structured data via API (inferred from conversational AI use case)\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII processing not specified; no explicit policy on whether customer data is used for model training; significant ambiguity noted\\n- **Data Collection:** Web chat interface and API; collection scope and opt-out mechanisms not documented\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** **Critical Gap:** Data retention practices are not explicitly defined. User data (chat logs) may be retained indefinitely and could be used for model training unless explicitly deleted by users. No default zero-retention option or automated purge policy documented\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Primary operations in China (Hangzhou); customer choice of data residency not specified; EU/US data residency options not available\\n- **Data Deletion:** User-initiated deletion available; automated deletion on request not specified; deletion confirmation and audit trail not documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider(s) not disclosed; payment processor, authentication provider, and third-party analytics vendors not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently held.** No SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, FedRAMP, HIPAA, HITRUST, or equivalent certifications documented\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit conducted; vendor self-assessment only\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST AI Risk Management Framework: Engagement not specified\\n  - GDPR: Compliance status unclear; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) not available\\n  - CCPA: Compliance status not specified\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness and engagement not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not HIPAA-eligible; BAA not available; healthcare data handling not authorized\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA not available; data residency in China creates compliance friction for EU customers; adequacy determination unclear\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No documented engagement with EU AI Act requirements; high-risk classification likely (general-purpose LLM); compliance roadmap not provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No independent audits conducted; vendor maturity (founded 2023) and startup stage preclude established audit history\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** <95% or no formal SLA; uptime commitment not contractually defined; reliability targets not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response times by severity not documented; support availability (24/7 vs. business hours) not stated\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Release process and frequency not documented; rollback readiness practices not specified; change communication procedures not defined\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider(s), payment processor, and authentication services not disclosed; vendor dependencies not transparent\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified; vendor SLA monitoring and audit practices not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** SLAs from critical infrastructure and service vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope (user counts, query volume, latency, error rates) not detailed; export capability not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; log retention period, export format, and SIEM integration not specified; audit trail completeness not documented\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial; formal security policies, compliance documentation, and testing results not provided; evidence files not uploaded\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial; third-party model evaluation results, safety benchmarks, or adversarial robustness testing not available; NDA-protected results not offered\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Must Address Before Enterprise Deployment)\\n\\n1. **Compliance & Certifications (Severity: Critical)**\\n   - No SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or equivalent security certifications\\n   - Not HIPAA-eligible; unsuitable for healthcare PHI handling\\n   - GDPR compliance unclear; DPA not available; China data residency creates legal friction\\n   - Recommendation: Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 audit within 12 months; provide GDPR DPA; clarify EU AI Act compliance roadmap\\n\\n2. **Data Retention & PII Handling (Severity: Critical)**\\n   - Indefinite data retention by default; ambiguity on model training use\\n   - No explicit opt-out or zero-retention policy\\n   - Recommendation: Publish explicit data retention policy; offer customer-controlled deletion and zero-retention options; provide audit trail for data handling\\n\\n3. **Incident Response & Operational Maturity (Severity: High)**\\n   - Incident response plan in development; not yet mature\\n   - No formal SLA commitments; uptime <95% or undefined\\n   - Recommendation: Complete and document incident response procedures; commit to 99.5%+ uptime SLA with penalties; establish 24/7 support escalation\\n\\n4. **AI Governance & Safety Testing (Severity: High)**\\n   - No documented bias testing, red-teaming, or adversarial security evaluation\\n   - Training data composition not disclosed; no impact assessments\\n   - Recommendation: Conduct third-party bias audit; publish training data documentation; establish formal AI safety review board\\n\\n### Moderate Gaps (Address Before Production Deployment)\\n\\n5. **Security Certifications & Vendor Transparency**\\n   - Infrastructure providers and sub-processors not disclosed\\n   - Encryption practices (at rest, in transit) not documented\\n   - Recommendation: Disclose critical vendor dependencies; document encryption standards (AES-256, TLS 1.3); provide vendor SLA summaries\\n\\n6. **Support & Change Management**\\n   - Support SLAs by severity not defined\\n   - Release cadence and rollback procedures not documented\\n   - Recommendation: Define P1/P2/P3 response times; publish release notes and rollback procedures; establish change advisory board\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – PILOT ONLY (Not Recommended for Production)**\\n\\n- **Current State:** DeepSeek Chat is suitable for **low-risk, non-regulated pilot use cases only** (e.g., internal R&D, cost-optimization experiments, non-PHI data analysis)\\n- **Restrictions:** Do not deploy with regulated data (healthcare PHI, financial PII, government classified); do not use in customer-facing production until compliance gaps are closed\\n- **Path to Production:**\\n  1. **Months 1–3:** Vendor completes SOC 2 Type 2 audit; publishes GDPR DPA and data retention policy\\n  2. **Months 4–6:** Vendor conducts third-party bias audit; documents training data and AI safety framework\\n  3. **Months 7–9:** Vendor commits to 99.5%+ uptime SLA; establishes 24/7 support with defined response times\\n  4. **Month 10+:** Re-evaluate for production deployment; consider phased rollout with extended monitoring\\n\\n- **Timeline to Production-Ready:** 10–12 months (subject to vendor remediation)\\n- **Residual Risk (Post-Remediation):** Moderate (50–60/100) due to startup stage and China-based operations; ongoing monitoring required\\n\\n### Alternative Considerations\\n\\n- **For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Finance, Government):** Recommend established vendors with proven compliance track records (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI) until DeepSeek achieves SOC 2 Type 2 and HIPAA eligibility\\n- **For Cost-Sensitive, Non-Regulated Use Cases:** DeepSeek Chat is a strong candidate; leverage open-source model for on-premises deployment to mitigate data residency concerns\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Analyst Assessment Level:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confidence in Score:** Moderate (limited independent verification; reliance on vendor-provided data and public disclosures)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor (cost-effective positioning; 40% operational cost reduction 