cff3c7aa-8bea-4332-9cff-5f81d764575f	71	71	31a1a343-0485-46ec-81d9-587d42f17618	82	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Drift AI Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 55\\n- Compliance: 45\\n- Data Practices: 60\\n- AI Governance: 50\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDrift demonstrates moderate trustworthiness with established company maturity (founded 2015, Series D+, profitable 3+ years) and reasonable operational stability (99.9% SLA). However, significant gaps in AI governance documentation, compliance certifications, and security posture limit the overall score. The vendor lacks published security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA), no formal AI ethics policy or bias testing framework is documented, and training data documentation is absent—critical gaps for enterprise deployment. Strengths include automated rollback capability, documented incident response, and basic audit logging; weaknesses center on incomplete governance, unverified compliance, and limited transparency into AI model safety practices.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Drift AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Conversational marketing and sales automation; real-time customer engagement; lead qualification and nurturing; sales conversion optimization\\n- **Target Industry:** B2B SaaS, enterprise sales and marketing organizations\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer base not quantified)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (operational since 2015)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; corroborated evidence includes 2X qualified leads, 120% demo requests, 9X pipeline increase metrics\\n- **Product Description:** Drift AI is a conversational marketing and sales platform that automates lead qualification, customer engagement, and sales workflows through real-time AI-driven interactions. The platform integrates with existing CRM systems to streamline customer interactions and provide actionable insights. Customers report 30% increase in lead conversion rates and 20% reduction in manual sales processing time.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Drift (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Boston, Massachusetts, USA; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-based with potential international reach)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; conversational AI (likely LLM-based or custom NLP)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Lead qualification, customer engagement automation, sales conversation analysis, real-time response generation\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; level of human-in-the-loop intervention not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted); specific prompt-level control or citation mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available** — critical gap for enterprise AI governance\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; frequency and scope of adversarial security testing not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines published\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluation process documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not documented; no system cards or release documentation available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested** — represents moderate maturity with unvalidated procedures\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger — supports rapid incident recovery\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer conversations, lead information, CRM data, sales interactions\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (specific collection mechanisms not detailed)\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Drift retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; secure deletion procedures outlined in Information Security Addendum\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or residency options documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request via Information Security Addendum; timelines and procedures not detailed in attestation\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None documented** — no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other standard certifications listed\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no recent independent audit documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not specified; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not addressed\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA availability not documented\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime) — industry-standard commitment for SaaS\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of third-party risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (qualified leads, demo requests, pipeline metrics)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and scope not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no NDA-protected testing results referenced\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (Vendor Self-Attestation Formula)\\n\\n**Formula Applied:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Component Scores:**\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85 (conversational AI with customer data; moderate inherent risk for lead qualification use case)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.35 (limited documented controls; no bias testing, training data documentation, or formal safety framework)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.60 (basic testing results available; no third-party audit or comprehensive evidence)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.35) × 0.60 = 33.3 → 33**\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or other standard certifications)\\n- Assessment Quality: 5 points (basic testing results; no third-party audit)\\n- Policies: 10 points (documented incident response and data retention; no AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, or impact assessment)\\n- Operational Controls: 15 points (automated rollback, basic audit logs; limited control maturity)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 20 points (established company, 3+ years profitable)\\n- **Governance Score = 50 (capped at 100) → Governance Risk = 100 − 50 = 50**\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; industry standard but not best-in-class)\\n- Incident Management: 15 points (documented but not tested)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 20 points (SaaS multi-tenant; no enterprise-specific deployment details)\\n- Stability: 20 points (established company, 3+ years profitable)\\n- Support: 10 points (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 dedicated support documented)\\n- **Operational Score = 90 → Operational Risk = 100 − 90 = 10**\\n\\n**Final Vendor Trust Score:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(33 × 0.40) + (50 × 0.30) + (10 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 − [13.2 + 15 + 3]\\n    = 100 − 31.2\\n    = 68.8 ≈ 69\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 62** based on:\\n- Significant gaps in AI governance (no ethics policy, bias testing, training data documentation)\\n- Absence of security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001)\\n- Unverified compliance posture (no HIPAA, GDPR, or regulatory framework documentation)\\n- Incident response not tested\\n- Limited transparency into AI model safety and explainability\\n\\n**Classification:** Moderate Vendor (60–69 range per rubric: \\"Review Recommended\\")\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT SUMMARY\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established Company Maturity:** Founded 2015, Series D+, profitable 3+ years — demonstrates market viability and financial stability\\n2. **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA; automated rollback capability; documented incident response\\n3. **Basic Audit Trail:** Audit logs and basic testing results available\\n4. **Data Retention Governance:** Documented data deletion procedures in Information Security Addendum\\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Require Remediation)\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or HIPAA certification limits enterprise deployability\\n2. **AI Governance Deficiency:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, or training data documentation\\n3. **Compliance Uncertainty:** GDPR, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not addressed; no DPA or BAA availability stated\\n4. **Unvalidated Incident Response:** Incident response plan documented but not tested\\n5. **Limited Transparency:** Model explainability rated \\"moderate\\"; no detailed transparency into AI decision-making or safety practices\\n\\n### Residual Concerns\\n- Support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 support commitment documented\\n- Sub-processor and critical vendor information not disclosed\\n- Change management and release cadence not documented\\n- No third-party audit or independent compliance validation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** **REVIEW RECOMMENDED** (Score 62/100)\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n1. **Require SOC 2 Type 2 certification** before enterprise deployment (timeline: 6–12 months typical)\\n2. **Request formal AI ethics policy and bias testing framework** with third-party validation\\n3. **Obtain HIPAA BAA and GDPR DPA** if handling regulated data\\n4. **Conduct independent security assessment** (penetration testing, code review)\\n5. **Validate incident response plan** through tabletop exercise or audit\\n6. **Clarify support SLAs** and escalation procedures for P1/P2/P3 incidents\\n7. **Request training data documentation** and model card for AI transparency\\n\\n**Suitable For:**\\n- Non-regulated B2B SaaS lead generation and sales automation\\n- Organizations with moderate data sensitivity requirements\\n- Pilot or phased deployments with extended evaluation period\\n\\n**Not Suitable For (Without Remediation):**\\n- Healthcare (HIPAA-regulated) applications\\n- Financial services or government deployments\\n- High-sensitivity PII or PHI processing\\n- Regulated industries requiring formal compliance certifications\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Framework:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)])", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Drift AI", "Customer Base": "Not specified; corroborated evidence includes 2X qualified leads, 120% demo requests, 9X pipeline increase metrics", "Target Industry": "B2B SaaS, enterprise sales and marketing organizations", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer base not quantified)", "Primary Use Case": "Conversational marketing and sales automation; real-time customer engagement; lead qualification and nurturing; sales conversion optimization", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "Drift AI is a conversational marketing and sales platform that automates lead qualification, customer engagement, and sales workflows through real-time AI-driven interactions. The platform integrates with existing CRM systems to streamline customer interactions and provide actionable insights. Customers report 30% increase in lead conversion rates and 20% r