tes clinical documentation for behavioral health providers, reducing documentation time by over 70% and enabling compliance with HIPAA and related regulations. The platform leverages a large database of real-world behavioral health sessions and supports multilingual documentation. It is SOC 2 Type II certified and HITRUST compliant, positioning it as a security-conscious solution for regulated healthcare environments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Eleos Health (legal entity name not specified; inferred from domain and branding)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (specific revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Boston, MA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: United States; international regions not disclosed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (inferred: NLP/speech-to-text for documentation automation; specific model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Clinical documentation generation, compliance checking, behavioral health insights extraction\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no formal staged deployment or safety framework documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; level of clinician review and intervention not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features available; specific prompt-level control or citation mechanisms not documented)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data provenance, composition, and bias analysis not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no formal red team, third-party bias audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; frequency and scope of adversarial security testing not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified; no documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no formal bias audit schedule or external evaluation results disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; clinician review workflows, content filtering, and intervention mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards or release impact documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; formal incident response procedures are in place and validated through annual testing\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback is supported via automated processes with manual initiation option\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Clinical documentation (audio, text), behavioral health session notes, patient identifiers (PHI)\\n- **PII Handling:** HIPAA BAA eligible; PII (PHI) is processed as part of clinical documentation; specific restrictions on customer data use for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and clinical interface (inferred from SaaS deployment); collection mechanism not fully specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly documented\\n- **Data Retention:** After a predefined period, information can be de-identified or deleted upon request, based on applicable laws. De-identified audio data may be retained to improve system accuracy.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; data residency options (US, EU, customer choice) not disclosed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and automated based on retention policy; de-identification option available\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type II (security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy)\\n  - HITRUST (healthcare information security)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type II audit (third-party audit); HITRUST certification (third-party assessment); specific audit firm and scope not disclosed\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - HIPAA (Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act)\\n  - State behavioral health regulations (implied; specific frameworks not listed)\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligible; HIPAA compliance demonstrated via BAA availability\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability not disclosed; EU data residency not confirmed\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Incident response plan tested annually\\n  - SOC 2 Type II audit frequency not specified (typical: annual)\\n  - Last audit date not disclosed\\n  - Audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; contractual uptime commitment (e.g., 99.9%, 99.95%) not disclosed\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not documented\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** \\n  - Release frequency not specified\\n  - Rollback/readiness practices: Automated rollback with manual trigger available\\n  - Formal change management process not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers (cloud, hosting), payment processors, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of third-party vendor risk assessments not documented\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure or service vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity of telemetry not detailed\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** \\n  - Basic test results available\\n  - Partial training data documentation available\\n  - Formal policy documentation (AI ethics, data governance, incident response) not provided\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; availability of detailed model safety testing results under NDA not confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Healthcare-Specific Compliance:** SOC 2 Type II, HITRUST, and HIPAA BAA demonstrate serious commitment to regulated healthcare environments.\\n2. **Documented Incident Response:** Annual testing of incident response plan indicates operational maturity.\\n3. **Proven Clinical ROI:** 70%+ documentation time reduction corroborated by 12 evidence points; strong user satisfaction (92% UX rating).\\n4. **Automated Rollback:** Deployment rollback capability reduces operational risk.\\n5. **Growth-Stage Stability:** 201–1,000 employees and Series B/C funding suggest operational sustainability.\\n\\n### Gaps & Risks\\n1. **AI Governance Opacity:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, or human oversight framework; limits confidence in model safety.\\n2. **Incomplete Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation insufficient for regulatory scrutiny or third-party validation.\\n3. **Missing Operational SLAs:** No published uptime SLA or support response times; limits buyer confidence in operational reliability.\\n4. **Limited Transparency on Model Architecture:** AI model types, decision autonomy, and explainability mechanisms not detailed.\\n5. **GDPR / International Readiness:** No DPA, data residency options, or EU AI Act preparation documented; limits international deployment.\\n6. **Vendor Sub-processor Disclosure:** Critical infrastructure and payment vendors not disclosed; limits supply chain risk visibility.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions for Procurement\\n- **Require:** Formal AI ethics policy, documented bias testing methodology, and human oversight workflow before contract execution.\\n- **Require:** Published uptime SLA (recommend ≥99.9%) and support response time SLAs (P1/P2/P3).\\n- **Require:** Complete training data documentation (composition, sources, bias analysis) or third-party model audit.\\n- **Require:** GDPR DPA and data residency options if international deployment is planned.\\n- **Require:** Disclosure of critical sub-processors and their SLAs.\\n- **Recommended:** Pilot deployment with single behavioral health clinic to validate ROI claims and operational stability before enterprise rollout.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Current Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Classification:** Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range) — Proceed with enhanced due diligence; require mitigation of AI governance and operational transparency gaps as contract conditions.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Eleos Health", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Behavioral health / Mental health care", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Behavioral health documentation automation, compliance management, and clinical insights for mental health providers", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; specific cloud provider not specified", "Product Description": "Eleos Health is an AI-enabled SaaS platform that automates 