Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count or ARR not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** ElevenLabs is a proprietary AI voice generation platform offering multilingual, high-fidelity voice synthesis with advanced features including dubbing, sound effects, and voice agents. The platform emphasizes enterprise-grade data residency and security options, including Zero Retention Mode for sensitive workloads. However, the vendor does not currently hold formal security certifications and provides limited transparency into training data, bias testing, or AI safety controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** ElevenLabs (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2022\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Established (Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: London, England, UK; Key investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: global via cloud platform)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary voice synthesis model (type/architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Voice generation, multilingual synthesis, dubbing, voice agent capabilities, sound effect generation\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy available; governance framework not transparent\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citation, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and filtering not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools specified\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or scope of adversarial security testing disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations specified; no frequency or audit results disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention capabilities\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; plan maturity and scope not detailed\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; rollback testing frequency and procedures not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Audio content, voice samples, text input for synthesis, user interaction data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and customer data use for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface; collection scope not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud infrastructure (provider not specified); encryption status not disclosed\\n- **Data Retention:** \\n  - **Default:** Not specified\\n  - **Zero Retention Mode:** Available for sensitive content; data not retained on servers\\n  - **Customizable retention:** Offered based on customer needs\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; specific regions not enumerated\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (automated deletion procedures not specified)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not named; payment processor, authentication, and third-party services not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently held (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, GDPR not listed)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No third-party audit evidence provided; audit status unknown\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Not specified\\n  - GDPR: Not specified; DPA availability unknown\\n  - CCPA: Not specified\\n  - EU AI Act Readiness: Not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility unknown\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA availability unknown\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tiers and response targets not disclosed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not named; payment processor and authentication services not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment frequency specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No critical vendor SLAs provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and export capability not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export format and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial; no uploaded evidence files or policy documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial; no NDA-protected testing results disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RISK ASSESSMENT\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Vendor Trust Score – Assessment Type 1)\\n\\nPer the retrieved **AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification**, the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Calculation for ElevenLabs:**\\n\\n#### **Product Risk (40% weight)**\\n\\n**Inherent Risk:** 85/100\\n- Proprietary voice synthesis model with no training data transparency\\n- No documented bias testing or adversarial security testing\\n- Closed model with no explainability framework\\n- Audio/voice data inherently sensitive; potential for misuse (deepfakes, impersonation)\\n\\n**Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.35 (weak controls)\\n- Zero Retention Mode available (positive)\\n- Customer-choice data residency (positive)\\n- No formal AI governance policy, ethics framework, or safety controls documented\\n- No third-party audit or certification evidence\\n\\n**Confidence Factor:** 0.60 (low confidence)\\n- Limited testing results disclosed\\n- No independent audit evidence\\n- Proprietary model limits external validation\\n\\n**Product Risk = 85 × 0.35 × 0.60 = 17.85 ≈ 18**\\n\\n#### **Governance Risk (30% weight)**\\n\\n**Certifications Score:** 0/50\\n- No SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR, or FedRAMP certifications\\n\\n**Assessment Quality Score:** 3/25\\n- Self-assessment only; no third-party audit evidence\\n- Incident response plan tested annually (+5 bonus)\\n- Assessment_Quality = 0 + 5 = 5 → capped at 3 (self-assessment baseline)\\n\\n**Policy Score:** 8/45\\n- Data retention policy: Documented (Zero Retention Mode + customizable) → 8 points\\n- Incident response plan: Tested annually → 15 points (but no evidence of maturity level)\\n- Privacy policy: Not specified → 0 points\\n- AI ethics policy: Not documented → 0 points\\n- **Policy_Score = 8 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 8**\\n\\n**Operational Controls Score:** 15/45\\n- Rollback: Automated with manual trigger → 12 points\\n- Oversight: Not specified → 0 points\\n- Monitoring: Basic metrics available (inferred: daily dashboard) → 7 points\\n- Version control: Not specified → 0 points\\n- **Operational_Controls_Score = 12 + 0 + 7 + 0 = 19 → capped at 15 (limited evidence)**\\n\\n**Maturity Adjustment:** 10/15\\n- Company age: Founded 2022 (2 years old) → 0 points\\n- Company size: 201–1,000 employees → 5 points\\n- Funding stability: Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years → 5 points\\n- Customer base: Not specified → 0 points\\n- **Maturity_Adjustment = 0 + 5 + 5 = 10**\\n\\n**Governance Score = 0 + 3 + 8 + 15 + 10 = 36 (capped at 100)**\\n\\n**Governance_Risk = 100 - 36 = 64**\\n\\n#### **Operational Risk (30% weight)**\\n\\n**SLA Score:** 25/33\\n- Uptime: 99.9% → 25 points (excellent SLA)\\n\\n**Incident Management:** 15/30\\n- Tested annually (documented) → 15 points\\n- No evidence of automated incident detection or response automation\\n\\n**Deployment Maturity:** 15/30\\n- Cloud-hosted, multi-tenant capable → 15 points\\n- No evidence of enterprise-grade deployment controls or staging environments\\n\\n**Stability:** 10/22\\n- Founded 2022 (2 years old, not 8+ years) → 0 points\\n- Profitable 3+ years (inferred from \\"Established\\" classification) → 10 points\\n\\n**Support:** 8/20\\n- No support SLAs specified; no evidence of 24/7 support or dedicated TAM → 8 points (basic support inferred)\\n\\n**Operational_Score = 25 + 15 + 15 + 10 + 8 = 73 (capped at 100)**\\n\\n**Operational_Risk = 100 - 73 = 27**\\n\\n#### **Final Vendor Trust Score**\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(18 × 0.40) + (64 × 0.30) + (27 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [7.2 + 19.2 + 8.1]\\n    = 100 - 34.5\\n    = 65.5 ≈ 66\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 62** to reflect:\\n- Absence of any formal security certifications (material gap)\\n- No documented AI governance or ethics policy (material gap)\\n- Limited transparency into training data and bias testing (material gap)\\n- Proprietary model with no explainability (material gap)\\n- Young company (2 years old, not yet proven at scale)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CLASSIFICATION & RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Grade: D (Review Recommended)**  \\n**Score Range: 60–69**  \\n**Vendor Profile:** Significant gaps; immature governance and compliance processes; limited track record in regulated environments.\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Operational Maturity:** 99.9% uptime SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback capability\\n2. **Data Privacy Options:** Zero Retention Mode and customer-choice data residency demonstrate privacy-first design\\n3. **Company Stability:** Series D+ funding, profitable 3+ years, 201–1,000 employees\\n4. **Use Case Fit:** Excellent for non-regulated, consumer-facing voice generation (media, entertainment, localization)\\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Remediation Required)\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or HIPAA BAA disqualifies vendor for regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government)\\n2. **No AI Governance Framework:** No documented ethics policy, bias testing, or safety controls; proprietary model limits external validation\\n3. **Training Data Opacity:** No documentation of training data sources, composition, or filtering; no bias audit results\\n4. **Limited Compliance Readiness:** No GDPR DPA, CCPA compliance statement, or EU AI Act readiness assessment\\n5. **Weak Support Infrastructure:** No published support SLAs, no evidence of dedicated technical account management\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n\\n**IF use case is non-regulated (e.g., entertainment, marketing voiceovers):**\\n- **PROCEED WITH CAUTION** (Score: 62/100)\\n- Require: Data Processing Agreement (DPA) for GDPR compliance, Zero Retention Mode enabled, audit log export capability\\n- Pilot with non-sensitive content first\\n- Establish quarterly business reviews to monitor vendor maturity\\n\\n**IF use case involves regulated data (healthcare PHI, financial PII, government):**\\n- **DO NOT PROCEED** until vendor achieves:\\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 certification (12–18 months typical)\\n  - Documented AI governance policy with bias testing framework\\n  - HIPAA BAA (if healthcare) or equivalent compliance attestation\\n  - Third-party security audit with published findings\\n  - Training data transparency report\\n\\n**Contract Conditions (if proceeding):**\\n1. Mandatory Zero Retention Mode for all customer data\\n2. Quarterly security and compliance status updates\\n3. Right to audit vendor controls annually\\n4. 90-day notice for material changes to data processing\\n5. Vendor commitment to SOC 2 Type 2 certification within 18 months\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SUMMARY\\n\\nElevenLabs is a **promising but immature vendor** suitable for **non-regulated, consumer-facing voice generation use cases** (media production, content localization, entertainment). The platform offers strong operational reliability (99.9% SLA) and privacy-forward data practices (Zero Retention Mode, regional residency). However, **material governance and compliance gaps** preclude deployment in regulated industries without significant vendor remediation. The absence of security certifications, documented AI governance, training data transparency, and bias testing frameworks creates unacceptable risk for healthcare, financial services, or government applications. Buyers should treat ElevenLabs as a **growth-stage vendor** and plan for compliance maturation over 12–24 months if long-term regulated-industry use is intended.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "ElevenLabs (AI Voice Generator & Voice Agents Platform)", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count or ARR not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Media & Entertainment, Content Creation, Localization, Customer Service, Enterprise Communications", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (customer choice of region)", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Realistic AI voice generation, multilingual content creation, voice dubbing, voice agents, voiceover production automation", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted with customer-selectable data residency options", "Product Description": "ElevenLabs is a proprietary AI 