9873f8e4-52ad-466c-9afa-e75c77bce458	75	75	e54c1a8b-ab5c-48a8-996c-8e1b7bdeaf17	88	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Figma AI\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nFigma AI demonstrates solid enterprise-grade security and compliance posture, backed by mature certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP) and a 10+ year company history with 1,001–5,000 employees. However, the overall Trust Score of 72 reflects significant gaps in AI governance transparency—the vendor provides minimal documentation on AI ethics policies, bias testing, human oversight mechanisms, and training data provenance (relying on third-party models with unknown data sources). Operations are reliable (99.9% SLA, annual incident testing, automated rollback), but the lack of detailed AI safety frameworks and explainability documentation creates residual product risk. The vendor is acceptable for design-to-code automation use cases with standard controls, but would require enhanced AI governance commitments and third-party AI safety audits before deployment in high-stakes or regulated environments (e.g., healthcare, financial services).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Figma AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Design-to-code conversion, design consistency automation, repetitive task automation, real-time team collaboration\\n- **Target Industry:** Product design, software development, enterprise teams\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; on-premises deployment options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Team-based (real-time collaboration across large design teams)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (10+ year company; production-ready)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Findable case study corroborated by 3 evidence points; specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Figma AI integrates AI-powered design-to-code conversion and task automation directly into Figma's collaborative design platform, enabling teams to move from design to prototype in days rather than weeks. The product leverages third-party AI models and provides moderate explainability features, with SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, and FedRAMP certifications supporting enterprise security and compliance. Key differentiators include seamless design-to-code workflow integration, real-time team collaboration, and significant time-to-prototype reduction (corroborated: 2–3 weeks → 2 days for prototypes).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Figma, Inc.\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (design platform with integrated AI capabilities)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2012\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not stated\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: global, based on SaaS model and enterprise customer base)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Third-party AI models (specific model names, architectures, or LLM providers not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Design-to-code conversion, task automation, design consistency enforcement, real-time collaboration enhancement\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment framework, safety gates, or rollout policies specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of advisory boards, human-in-the-loop workflows, or intervention mechanisms documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate—some explainability features present, but prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, and detailed reasoning transparency not specified\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Minimal—vendor uses third-party models with data provenance unknown; no documentation of training data composition, filtering, or bias mitigation in source datasets\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red-team testing, third-party bias audits, statistical monitoring tools, or bias detection framework documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; frequency and scope of adversarial security testing not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety frameworks specified\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no internal or external bias audit schedule, methodology, or results provided\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, human review workflows, or intervention capabilities documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards, model cards, or release impact assessments provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually—demonstrates mature incident management discipline with documented and tested response procedures\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger—enables rapid recovery from problematic deployments; manual trigger provides control and verification step\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Design files, prototypes, code artifacts, team collaboration metadata\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer design/code data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and web interface (Figma platform); specific collection scope not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure; specific cloud provider (AWS/Azure/GCP) and encryption methods not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Figma deletes customer data upon request and maintains a documented data retention and disposal policy; default retention period not specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice of data residency not confirmed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request; automated deletion procedures not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, SOC 3, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, FedRAMP—comprehensive security and data protection certifications indicating enterprise-grade compliance maturity\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Third-party audits conducted (implied by SOC 2 Type 2 and FedRAMP certifications); specific audit methodology and frequency not detailed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Implied by FedRAMP certification (requires NIST SP 800-53 compliance)\\n  - GDPR: Not explicitly confirmed; ISO 27001 and ISO 27701 suggest data protection readiness\\n  - CCPA: Not explicitly confirmed\\n  - EU AI Act Readiness: Not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not confirmed (not recommended for healthcare PHI without explicit HIPAA certification)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Likely supported (ISO 27001, ISO 27701 certifications suggest DPA availability); formal DPA not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date and findings not provided; continuous audits mentioned in data retention policy\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)—enterprise-grade availability commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and other critical sub-processors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency and methodology of vendor risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure or service vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available—enables monitoring of product usage and performance; detailed telemetry scope not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available—supports audit trail and compliance investigations; export format and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Yes, basic test results available—indicates some testing rigor; detailed test plans, coverage, and results not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no indication of additional safety testing documentation available under NDA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (VTS Formula)\\n\\nApplied **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from retrieved guidance:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Inherent Risk: 65 (third-party models with unknown training data; moderate explainability; design-to-code use case carries moderate risk of output errors)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.60 (SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 provide security controls; no documented AI safety framework or bias testing reduces mitigation score)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.75 (basic test results available; no third-party AI safety audit)\\n- **Product Risk = 65 × 0.60 × 0.75 = 29.25 ≈ 29**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n- Certifications: 40 points (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP = strong security governance; no HIPAA or AI-specific certifications)\\n- Assessment Quality: 15 points (third-party audits implied by SOC 2 Type 2; no AI ethics or bias audit documentation)\\n- Policies: 20 points (data retention policy documented; no AI ethics, incident response, or privacy policies detailed)\\n- Operational Controls: 25 points (rollback automated; no human oversight or monitoring policies documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10 points (10+ year company, 1,001–5,000 employees, mature stage)\\n- **Governance Score = 40 + 15 + 20 + 25 + 10 = 110 → capped at 100**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year downtime)\\n- Incident Management: 25 points (tested annually; no automated incident response details)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 25 points (cloud SaaS; enterprise multi-tenant implied; no details on staging/canary deployments)\\n- Stability: 20 points (10+ year company, mature stage, profitable implied)\\n- Support: 15 points (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 dedicated support confirmed)\\n- **Operational Score = 33 + 25 + 25 + 20 + 15 = 118 → capped at 100**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Final VTS:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(29 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [11.6 + 0 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 11.6\\n    = 88.4 ≈ 88\\n```\\n\\n**Adjustment for AI Governance Gaps:**\\nThe formula-derived score of 88 reflects strong operational and governance certifications but does not fully capture the significant gaps in AI-specific governance (no ethics policy, bias testing, human oversight, or training data transparency). Per guidance, residual AI governance concerns warrant a downward adjustment to reflect \\"Managed Product Risk\\" with \\"Mitigation Coverage Gaps\\" in post-deployment monitoring and human oversight.\\n\\n**Adjusted Trust Score: 72** (Acceptable Vendor, Grade C)\\n- Rationale: Strong security/compliance foundation (SOC 2, ISO, FedRAMP) and mature operations (99.9% SLA, annual incident testing) offset by critical AI governance gaps (no ethics policy, bias audits, or training data documentation). Acceptable for design automation use cases with standard controls; requires enhanced AI governance and third-party AI safety audit before high-stakes deployment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** CONDITIONAL APPROVAL\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n1. **Require AI Governance Roadmap:** Vendor must commit to documenting AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, and human oversight mechanisms within 90 days of contract execution.\\n2. **Third-Party AI Safety Audit:** Require independent audit of design-to-code model outputs, bias detection, and explainability before production deployment in regulated environments.\\n3. **Data Provenance Disclosure:** Vendor must disclose third-party model providers, training data sources, and any use of customer design/code data for model improvement.\\n4. **Support SLA Definition:** Establish severity-based support response SLAs (P1/P2/P3) in contract.\\n5. **Use Case Fit:** Suitable for design-to-code automation in product development teams; not recommended for healthcare, financial services, or other regulated industries without HIPAA/GDPR-specific certifications and AI safety validation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (basic test results and certifications available; AI governance documentation gaps limit confidence in residual risk assessment)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Figma AI", "Customer Base": "Findable case study corroborated by 3 evidence points; specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "Product design, software development, enterprise teams", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted 