 & Auditing Procedures", "Transparency & Documentation", "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence", "User Education & Awareness"], "coverage_ratio": 0.9, "required_count": 10, "from_attestation": ["Data Governance & Privacy Controls", "Model Security & Integrity", "Access Management & Authentication", "Testing & Auditing Procedures", "Post-Deployment Monitoring", "Incident Response & Recovery", "Transparency & Documentation", "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence"], "implemented_count": 9, "evidence_blob_chars": 750}}	vts-formula-1.0	VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\n========================================================================\n\nRESULT\n  Trust score:   89 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\n\nHOW WE GOT HERE\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\n\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\n    1. Operational risk       31.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\n    2. Product risk            2.99  (weight 40%)\n    3. Governance risk         1.00  (weight 30%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (31.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Product risk (3.0) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
6d91775a-203c-45d6-8abe-86a5658edc83	77	77	127541f9-4c09-4c63-9ea6-9d0217e81585	87	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Front AI Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 80\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nFront demonstrates solid operational maturity (established company, profitable 3+ years, 201–1,000 employees) and strong security fundamentals (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR compliance, 99.9% uptime SLA). However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency—no documented AI ethics policy, no bias testing approach disclosed, no training data documentation, and no formal safety testing results. The moderate explainability features and lack of autonomous decision-boundary clarity further limit confidence in AI safety controls. Applied formula: VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]. Product Risk is elevated (~28/100) due to missing AI governance and testing documentation; Governance Risk is moderate (~25/100) due to strong certifications offset by policy gaps; Operational Risk is low (~20/100) reflecting mature SLAs and incident response. **Main strengths:** established company, strong security posture, proven uptime, GDPR/SOC 2 compliance. **Main gaps:** no AI ethics policy, no bias audits, no training data transparency, no formal adversarial testing, limited explainability documentation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Front AI Platform\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Complex operations coordination, customer inquiry management, team collaboration, multi-channel communication (email, text, chat)\\n- **Target Industry:** Customer service, support operations, enterprise operations management\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; on-premises deployment options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale multi-channel operations; typical customer manages high volumes of customer inquiries across multiple channels\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; no formal testing results disclosed\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (corroborated evidence: Query Identification Rate 95%)\\n- **Product Description:** Front is an AI-powered customer service platform designed to unify communication across email, text, and chat channels while automating repetitive tasks and improving team collaboration. The platform coordinates complex operations across organizations and eliminates communication silos. Typical ROI includes 30-minute response times (vs. 12-hour industry average) and 40% productivity gains in support teams; however, formal security and safety testing results are not publicly available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Front (legal entity not specified in attestation)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider\\n- **Year Founded:** 2014\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Established; Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not listed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; platform uses AI capabilities for customer inquiry automation and team coordination\\n- **Model Purpose:** Customer inquiry understanding, response generation, task automation, team coordination\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy disclosed; staged deployment approach not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; human-in-the-loop capabilities not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); specific prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or transparency documentation not provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach disclosed; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** None disclosed; no frequency or external evaluations mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; admin controls, content filtering, and intervention capabilities not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer communications (email, text, chat), customer inquiries, team coordination data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface; retention options not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards not disclosed\\n- **Data Retention:** Front retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; specific retention periods not defined\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice of data residency not mentioned\\n- **Data Deletion:** Procedures outlined in Data Processing Addendum (DPA); on-request deletion supported under GDPR data subject rights\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR Compliant\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not detailed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not mentioned; BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes; Data Processing Addendum (DPA) available with GDPR data subject rights provisions\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documentation mentioned\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not provided\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback/readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments of sub-processors not mentioned\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited; no formal testing results, AI ethics policy, or bias audit documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation:** **PROCEED WITH CAUTION** (Score: 72/100 – Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Strengths:**\\n- Established company (founded 2014, 201–1,000 employees, profitable 3+ years) demonstrates operational stability\\n- Strong security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001) and GDPR compliance\\n- Solid uptime SLA (99.9%) and annual incident response testing\\n- Automated rollback capability with manual trigger\\n- Proven ROI metrics (30-min response time, 40% productivity gain)\\n\\n**Critical Gaps Requiring Mitigation:**\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety:** No documented AI ethics policy, no bias testing, no training data transparency, no formal adversarial testing—creates residual risk in production AI systems\\n2. **Explainability:** Moderate transparency only; no detailed documentation of model decision boundaries, prompt-level control, or citation mechanisms\\n3. **Data Practices:** PII handling extent unclear; no disclosure of whether customer data is used for model training; data residency options not offered\\n4. **Support SLAs:** No severity-based response targets (P1/P2/P3) defined; support coverage model not specified\\n5. **Vendor Transparency:** Sub-processor list, infrastructure vendors, and critical vendor SLAs not disclosed\\n\\n**Recommended Actions Before Deployment:**\\n- **Require vendor to provide:** Documented AI ethics policy, bias testing roadmap, training data documentation, and formal safety testing results (or commit to third-party audit)\\n- **Negotiate:** Severity-based support SLAs, data residency options, and sub-processor transparency\\n- **Clarify:** PII handling scope, data usage for model training, and explicit opt-out mechanisms\\n- **Pilot approach:** Deploy in non-critical customer communication channels first; monitor for bias, accuracy drift, and customer satisfaction before full rollout\\n\\n**Use-Case Fit Assessment:**\\n- **Suitable for:** Internal team coordination, non-sensitive customer inquiry routing, productivity automation in low-risk support functions\\n- **Not recommended for:** Healthcare (HIPAA), financial services (PCI-DSS), or highly sensitive PII processing without additional AI governance controls and third-party validation", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Front AI Platform", "Customer Base": "Not specified (corroborated evidence: Query Identification Rate 95%)", "Target Industry": "Customer service, support operations, enterprise operations management", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise-scale multi-channel operations; typical customer manages high volumes of customer inquiries across multiple channels", "Primary Use Case": "Complex operations coordination, customer inquiry management, team collaboration, multi-channel communication (email, text, chat)", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; on-premises deployment options not specified", "Product Description": "Front is an AI-powered customer service platform designed to unify communication across email, text, and chat channels while automating repetitive tasks and improving team collaboration. The platform coordinates complex operations across organizations and eliminates communication silos. Typical ROI includes 30-minute response times (vs. 12-hour industry average) and 40% productivity gains in support teams; however, formal security and safety testing results are not publicly available.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready; no formal testing results disclosed"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Front (legal entity not specified in attestation)", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider", "Year Founded": "2014", "Operating Regions": "Not specified", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not listed", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Establ