c7f5ee1b-aa42-43d9-927f-ca67595e7cf4	79	79	5d4eda64-20fe-4f02-b6fc-3aa1694cbefa	79	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n**Gamma (AI Design Platform)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 52 (Moderate Risk)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 45\\n- Compliance: 25\\n- Data Practices: 60\\n- AI Governance: 35\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 40\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nGamma presents a **moderate-risk profile** suitable for non-regulated, consumer-grade use cases but unsuitable for enterprise PHI, financial data, or high-stakes decision-making. The vendor demonstrates reasonable operational maturity (99.99% SLA, automated rollback) and transparent data practices (read-only cloud access, user-initiated deletion), but critical gaps in AI governance, security certifications, compliance audits, and formal testing undermine enterprise trust. The startup stage (founded 2020, 11–50 employees, Seed/Series A) and absence of third-party security certifications, documented AI governance policies, and formal adversarial testing create unacceptable risk for regulated industries. **Recommendation:** Approve for fast-track procurement only in non-regulated, low-sensitivity use cases (e.g., internal presentation design); require comprehensive security audit, SOC 2 Type II certification, and formal AI safety testing before enterprise or healthcare deployment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Gamma\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-assisted design and content creation for presentations, websites, and marketing materials; rapid ideation and professional formatting.\\n- **Target Industry:** General enterprise (marketing, sales, product teams); no healthcare, financial services, or government specialization stated.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (vendor-managed)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted only; no on-premises or private deployment options stated.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Individual users and small teams; no enterprise multi-tenant deployment architecture documented.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product; no formal testing conducted; basic metrics and logging only.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Free-to-paid conversion rate 20%; user satisfaction 30% (corroborated by 2 evidence points); specific customer count not stated.\\n- **Product Description:** Gamma is an AI-powered design platform that automates presentation, website, and content creation to eliminate design friction and accelerate workflow. The product emphasizes customizability and speed, leveraging AI to structure ideas and generate professional layouts. No formal security certifications, compliance audits, or AI safety testing have been completed; the platform is suitable for consumer and non-regulated enterprise use only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Gamma (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 11–50\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (specific funding amount and revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not stated.\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; assumed US-based with potential global SaaS availability.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; inferred to be generative AI (LLM or custom-trained model for layout, text, and design generation).\\n- **Model Purpose:** Content generation (text, layouts, design suggestions); ideation and structure assistance; professional formatting automation.\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy; safety framework not stated; staged deployment approach not documented.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; assumed user-driven (no autonomous decision-making in regulated contexts); no mention of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate transparency; some explainability features present but not detailed; no prompt-level control or citation mechanisms documented.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing conducted; no formal penetration testing program documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy; usage policies and safety guidelines not provided.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring programs stated.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows documented.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided; no formal impact assessment process stated.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level unclear; no annual testing or validation mentioned.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback is supported but no rollback frequency, testing, or SLA stated.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Presentation content, website design data, user-generated text and media; no mention of PII, PHI, or financial data handling.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly stated; inferred that user account data (name, email) is collected but not used for training; no formal PII policy documented.\\n- **Data Collection:** Web interface (SaaS); read-only access to monitored cloud applications (e.g., Google Drive, Dropbox); no API-level data collection details provided.\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure (vendor-managed); encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed; infrastructure provider (AWS/Azure/GCP) not specified.\\n- **Data Retention:** User-initiated deletion via profile menu permanently removes content and personal data; Gamma does not store content from monitored cloud applications (read-only, analyzed, discarded); default retention period not specified.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or EU/US data residency options documented; assumed US-based default.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion via user profile menu; no automated retention expiry or GDPR right-to-be-forgotten workflow documented.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payment processor, authentication provider, and analytics vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other third-party security certifications held.\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit conducted; no third-party assessment, internal audit, or self-assessment documented.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness assessment documented; compliance posture unknown.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable; no BAA or HIPAA compliance stated; product unsuitable for PHI handling.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not explicitly confirmed; no Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance documentation provided; user deletion capability suggests partial GDPR alignment but formal compliance not verified.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented; compliance status unknown.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history; no third-party or internal audits conducted; no findings available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime); contractual commitment assumed but not formally documented.\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets provided.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no formal release process, rollback readiness practices, or change management workflow documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payment processor and authentication provider not disclosed; no vendor risk assessment program documented.\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor assessment frequency or process documented; no third-party risk management program stated.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No SLAs from critical vendors provided; infrastructure uptime and support commitments not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope limited to user engagement and conversion data; no detailed telemetry export or real-time monitoring dashboard mentioned.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; no SIEM integration, structured log export, or audit trail retention policy documented.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results, security assessments, or policy documentation provided; no evidence files uploaded.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n### Key Risk Factors\\n\\n| Risk Category | Finding | Severity |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **AI Governance** | No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing, or formal safety framework | **High** |\\n| **Security Certifications** | No SOC 2, ISO 27001, or equivalent third-party certifications | **High** |\\n| **Compliance Audit** | No independent compliance audit; no GDPR, HIPAA, or NIST alignment verified | **High** |\\n| **Testing & Validation** | No formal adversarial testing, penetration testing, or model safety evaluation | **High** |\\n| **Incident Response** | Documented but untested; no annual validation or SLA | **Medium** |\\n| **Data Practices** | Transparent user deletion and read-only cloud access; no formal DPA or GDPR compliance verified | **Medium** |\\n| **Company Maturity** | Startup stage (11–50 employees, Seed/Series A); limited operational track record | **Medium** |\\n| **Operations** | Strong uptime SLA (99.99%); automated rollback capability | **Low** |\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL FOR NON-REGULATED USE CASES ONLY**\\n\\n✅ **Approved for:**\\n- Internal presentation and website design (non-sensitive, non-regulated use)\\n- Marketing and sales collateral creation\\n- Ideation and rapid prototyping workflows\\n- Teams with no PHI, financial data, or government compliance requirements\\n\\n❌ **Not Approved for:**\\n- Healthcare (PHI handling, HIPAA compliance required)\\n- Financial services (PCI-DSS, SOX compliance required)\\n- Government / defense (FedRAMP, NIST compliance required)\\n- High-stakes decision-making or autonomous systems\\n- Any regulated industry without formal compliance audit\\n\\n### Conditions for Enterprise Deployment\\n\\nIf organization requires Gamma for regulated or sensitive use, vendor must complete:\\n\\n1. **SOC 2 Type II Audit** (annual, third-party)\\n2. **Formal AI Safety & Bias Testing** (third-party red team, documented results)\\n3. **Data Processing Agreement (DPA)** with GDPR and CCPA compliance terms\\n4. **Incident Response Plan Validation** (annual tabletop or full-scale test)\\n5. **Penetration Testing** (annual, external firm)\\n6. **Documented AI Governance Policy** (ethics, bias monitoring, human oversight)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Current Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Methodology:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Framework (VTS = 100 − [(Product Risk × 0.40) + (Governance Risk × 0.30) + (Operational Risk × 0.30)])", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Gamma", "Customer Base": "Free-to-paid conversion rate 20%; user satisfaction 30% (corroborated by 2 evidence points); specific customer count not stated.", "Target Industry": "General enterprise (marketing, sales, product teams); no healthcare, financial services, or government specialization stated.", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (vendor-managed)", "Deployment Scale": "Individual users and small teams; no enterprise multi-tenant deployment architecture documented.", "Primary Use Case": "AI-assisted design and content creation for presentations, websites, and marketing materials; rapid ideation and professional formatting.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted only; no on-premises or private deployment options stated.", "Product Description": "Gamma is an AI-powered design platform that automates presentation, website, and content creation to eliminate design friction and accelerate workflow. The product emphasizes customizability and speed, leveraging AI to structure ideas and generate professional layouts. No formal security certifications, compliance audits, or AI safety testing have been completed; the platform is suitable for consumer and non-regulated enterprise use only.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Early-stage product; no formal testing conducted; basic metrics and logging only."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "11–50", "Legal Name": "Gamma (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (SaaS)", "Year Founded": "2020", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; assumed US-based with potential global SaaS availability.", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investor