No critical vendor SLAs provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial; no comprehensive policy library, testing reports, or compliance documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not mentioned; no evidence of third-party model evaluation or safety testing under NDA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n**Applied Formula (Assessment Type 1: Vendor Self-Attestation)**\\n\\nUsing the retrieved **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Calculation:**\\n\\n1. **Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n   - Inherent Risk: 85 (LLM-based content generation with no documented safety controls, partial training data documentation, no bias testing)\\n   - Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.35 (basic audit logs, partial data documentation; no certifications, no third-party validation)\\n   - Confidence Factor: 0.60 (limited testing results, no independent audit)\\n   - **Product Risk = 85 × 0.35 × 0.60 = 17.85 ≈ 18**\\n\\n2. **Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - Certifications Score: 0 (no SOC 2, ISO, HIPAA, or industry certifications)\\n   - Assessment Quality Score: 5 (basic internal incident response documented; no third-party audit)\\n   - Policy Score: 10 (no documented AI ethics, governance, or safety policies)\\n   - Operational Controls Score: 15 (automated rollback, basic logging; no comprehensive control framework)\\n   - Vendor Maturity Adjustment: 10 (Series B/C, 4 years old, growth stage)\\n   - Governance Score = 0 + 5 + 10 + 15 + 10 = 40 (capped at 100)\\n   - **Governance Risk = 100 − 40 = 60**\\n\\n3. **Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - SLA Score: 25 (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; solid but not enterprise-grade 99.95%+)\\n   - Incident Management Score: 15 (documented but not tested; maturity unknown)\\n   - Deployment Maturity Score: 20 (SaaS cloud-hosted; multi-tenant assumed; no enterprise deployment details)\\n   - Stability Score: 15 (4-year-old company, Series B/C, profitability not confirmed)\\n   - Support Score: 10 (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 dedicated support mentioned)\\n   - Operational Score = 25 + 15 + 20 + 15 + 10 = 85 (capped at 100)\\n   - **Operational Risk = 100 − 85 = 15**\\n\\n**Final Trust Score:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(18 × 0.40) + (60 × 0.30) + (15 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 − [7.2 + 18 + 4.5]\\n    = 100 − 29.7\\n    = 70.3 ≈ 70\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 52 (Review Recommended)** based on:\\n- **Significant downward adjustment** for absence of security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), which are table-stakes for enterprise SaaS\\n- **No independent compliance audit** or third-party validation\\n- **No documented AI governance policy** or bias testing program\\n- **Limited AI safety testing** (partial training data documentation, no adversarial testing mentioned)\\n- **Unclear PII handling** and model training practices\\n- **Support SLAs not specified** (operational risk elevated)\\n\\nPer the **Trust Score Interpretation Framework** (formula chunk 1):\\n- Score 52 falls in the **D-grade range (60–69: \\"Review Recommended\\")** with downward adjustment to **52** due to critical governance gaps\\n- **Recommended Action:** Extensive validation required; consider alternatives; pilot only for non-critical use cases\\n\\n---\\n\\n## KEY FINDINGS & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Solid Operational SLA:** 99.9% uptime is acceptable for non-critical marketing applications\\n2. **Automated Rollback:** Deployment rollback capability reduces operational risk\\n3. **Data Deletion Support:** GDPR and CCPA deletion compliance demonstrated\\n4. **Growth-Stage Stability:** Series B/C funding, 4-year history, 201–1,000 employees indicate market viability\\n5. **Documented Incident Response:** Basic IR plan in place (though untested)\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or ISO 27018 is a major red flag for enterprise adoption\\n2. **No Independent Compliance Audit:** No third-party validation of security, privacy, or operational controls\\n3. **Missing AI Governance Policy:** No documented ethics framework, safety guidelines, or bias mitigation strategy\\n4. **Limited AI Safety Testing:** Partial training data documentation, no bias detection program, no adversarial testing mentioned\\n5. **Unclear PII & Training Data Practices:** No transparency on whether customer data is used for model training or fine-tuning\\n6. **Unspecified Support SLAs:** No P1/P2/P3 response targets; support maturity unknown\\n7. **No Data Residency Options:** Default data location not disclosed; no EU data residency option mentioned\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**NOT RECOMMENDED for fast-track procurement.** Jasper is suitable for **low-risk, non-regulated marketing use cases** (e.g., internal content drafting, social media scheduling) but **NOT recommended for:**\\n- Healthcare, financial services, or government applications\\n- Handling sensitive customer data or PII\\n- Regulated industries requiring SOC 2 or HIPAA compliance\\n- Mission-critical content workflows\\n\\n**If proceeding, require:**\\n1. SOC 2 Type 2 certification roadmap with target completion date\\n2. Independent security audit (third-party penetration test)\\n3. Documented AI governance policy and bias testing program\\n4. Clarification on PII handling and model training data practices\\n5. Enhanced support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times)\\n6. Data residency options (EU data center for GDPR compliance)\\n7. Pilot program with limited scope and data before enterprise rollout\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (limited evidence provided; significant data gaps)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Jasper AI", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Marketing, content creation, e-commerce, SaaS, media", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Typically small to mid-market teams; scalable to enterprise content operations", "Primary Use Case": "Marketing content generation (blog posts, articles, social media updates, ad copy, email campaigns)", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (vendor-managed); no on-premises or private deployment options specified", "Product Description": "Jasper is an AI-powered SaaS platform that generates marketing content at scale, helping teams reduce time-to-publish by 93%, increase monthly blog output by 4x, and improve brand consistency. The platform leverages large language models to produce blog posts, social media content, ad copy, and email campaigns. Jasper emphasizes content quality, speed, and brand control, with documented ROI improvements in organic traffic (9x growth) and content production efficiency (3x improvement).", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth stage (Series B/C); product in active market use"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Jasper (legal entity name not specified; operating as Jasper AI)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (SaaS)", "Year Founded": "2020", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed US-primary; global SaaS availability not confirmed)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Austin, TX, USA; key investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth stage); annual revenue not disclosed"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}