        3.83  (weight 40%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (39.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (19.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (61.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
1b72b6d4-b8f1-42e8-b292-2771584f2d42	82	82	ce7f1572-4edf-4675-a63e-bc708c85c580	83	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Google Workspace Studio (Vertex AI Platform)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 78 **(Acceptable Vendor)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 85\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 75\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 82\\n- Company Maturity: 90\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nGoogle Workspace Studio benefits from Google's mature operational infrastructure (10,000+ employees, founded 1998, public company) and strong security/compliance posture (ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2/3). However, the trust score is moderated by significant gaps in documented AI governance (no explicit safety policy, bias testing approach, or human oversight framework documented), limited transparency into proprietary Gemini 3 model training data, and unclear decision autonomy boundaries for autonomous agent execution. The 78 score reflects acceptable enterprise readiness with enhanced due diligence recommended on AI safety controls and governance maturity before production deployment in regulated sectors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Google Workspace Studio\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automation of repetitive business workflows including email triaging, report generation, project coordination, and multi-step task execution via natural language prompts\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-industry); early adopters in manufacturing (Karcher SE & Co.)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud Platform)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** SaaS; native integration with Google Workspace ecosystem (Gmail, Drive, Docs)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Scalable; Gemini Alpha program participants executed 20+ million automated tasks in 30 days\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready (early adopter deployments active)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Early adopters documented (Karcher SE & Co.); Gemini Alpha program participants; specific customer count not disclosed\\n- **Product Description:** Google Workspace Studio is a no-code AI agent builder integrated natively into Google Workspace, powered by Gemini 3 for advanced multi-step reasoning and task automation. It enables non-technical users to build and deploy AI agents via natural language prompts, eliminating manual workflows and reducing planning time by up to 90% in early deployments. The platform provides seamless automation across Gmail, Drive, and Docs without external integrations, democratizing AI development across organizations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Cloud Infrastructure & AI Services)\\n- **Year Founded:** 1998\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (Alphabet Inc.); revenue not separately disclosed for Vertex AI\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Alphabet Inc. (parent); Headquarters: Mountain View, California, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (multi-region deployment available)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Model (LLM) – Gemini 3 (proprietary)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Advanced reasoning, multi-step task execution, natural language understanding, workflow automation, adaptive agent behavior\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; proprietary model governance framework not documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop controls, approval workflows, or intervention mechanisms detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level transparency, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data composition unknown; no detailed documentation of data sources, filtering, or curation provided\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no documented red-team testing, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring disclosed\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not specified; no explicit safety guidelines, usage policies, or ethical guardrails documented for Studio\\n- **Bias Audits:** Bias audit frequency and external evaluation approach not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No documented admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention mechanisms specified; autonomous agent execution boundaries unclear\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation for AI governance not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented incident response process in place\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Google Workspace data (email, documents, files, project coordination data); business communications and structured workflow data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified; Google Workspace data may contain PII; customer data usage for model training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** API and native Workspace integration; interaction data available (comprehensive analytics)\\n- **Data Storage:** Google Cloud Platform infrastructure; encryption in transit and at rest (implied by ISO 27001/27017/27018 certifications)\\n- **Data Retention:** Google Workspace data remains in user accounts until deleted; organizations can use Google Vault to establish retention rules; default retention for deleted Drive files is 30–55 days, with additional 25-day administrator recovery window\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (multi-region deployment supported)\\n- **Data Deletion:** User-initiated deletion; administrator-controlled retention and purge via Google Vault\\n- **Sub-processors:** Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure); Google Workspace services (email, storage, collaboration); payment and authentication services (not separately detailed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2, SOC 3\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA-eligible (BAA available); GDPR compliance implied by ISO 27001/27018 and data residency options; EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; HIPAA-eligible for healthcare use cases\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Data residency options and ISO 27018 (PII handling) certification support GDPR compliance; DPA availability not explicitly stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tiers and response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure); Google Workspace services (core platform dependency)\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Vendor risk assessment frequency not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Google Cloud Platform SLAs (99.95% uptime for compute services); specific SLAs for Workspace services not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; interaction data collection enabled\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; export capability implied\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Testing results available (not specified in detail); policy documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available; NDA terms not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Mature Company & Operations:** Google's 10,000+ employee base, 1998 founding, and public company status provide strong operational stability and financial viability.\\n2. **Strong Security & Compliance Baseline:** ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, HIPAA BAA, and SOC 2/3 certifications demonstrate enterprise-grade security controls and third-party validation.\\n3. **Scalability & Performance:** 99.9% uptime SLA and 20+ million automated tasks executed in 30 days demonstrate production-ready infrastructure and scale.\\n4. **Data Residency & Retention Control:** Customer choice of region and Google Vault retention management provide compliance flexibility for regulated industries.\\n5. **Comprehensive Audit & Analytics:** Audit logs and interaction telemetry available for compliance monitoring and forensic analysis.\\n\\n### Gaps & Concerns\\n1. **Undocumented AI Governance:** No explicit AI ethics policy, safety guidelines, or governance framework documented for Workspace Studio; unclear decision autonomy boundaries for autonomous agents.\\n2. **Proprietary Model Opacity:** Gemini 3 training data composition unknown; no transparency into model curation, filtering, or bias mitigation; closed model limits explainability.\\n3. **Insufficient Bias & Safety Testing Documentation:** Bias testing approach, red-team results, and adversarial security testing not specified; no third-party AI safety audits disclosed.\\n4. **Missing Human Oversight Controls:** No documented human-in-the-loop mechanisms, approval workflows, content filtering, or intervention capabilities for autonomous task execution.\\n5. **Incomplete Support & Release Documentation:** Support SLAs by severity not specified; change management process and release cadence not documented; rollback readiness unclear.\\n6. **EU AI Act Readiness Unclear:** No documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance; risk classification and mitigation strategy not provided.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions Before Production Deployment\\n\\n**MUST FIX (Regulatory/Safety):**\\n- Require Google to provide documented AI governance policy, including safety guidelines, bias mitigation strategy, and human oversight controls for autonomous agents.\\n- Request third-party AI safety audit (e.g., by independent security firm) covering model robustness, adversarial testing, and bias detection.\\n- Clarify decision autonomy boundaries: which tasks execute autonomously vs. require human approval; define escalation and intervention mechanisms.\\n- Obtain EU AI Act compliance roadmap if deploying in EU; confirm risk classification and mitigation approach.\\n\\n**SHOULD FIX (Operational Readiness):**\\n- Request detailed support SLAs by severity (P1/P2/P3 response times) and escalation procedures.\\n- Document change management process, release cadence, and rollback testing procedures.\\n- Confirm DPA availability for GDPR compliance and data processing terms.\\n- Request training data documentation for Gemini 3 (or transparency on why proprietary data cannot be disclosed).\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL:**\\n- **For Non-Regulated Use Cases (e.g., internal productivity automation):** Approve with standard security controls; monitor via audit logs and telemetry.\\n- **For Healthcare (HIPAA):** Approve with BAA and mandatory AI governance documentation; require human review of sensitive workflows.\\n- **For Financial Services / Government:** Defer until AI governance and EU AI Act readiness documented; consider pilot phase with enhanced monitoring.\\n\\n### Trust Score Justification (Formula Application)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Self-Attestation (VTS)** formula:\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):** \\n- Inherent risk: High (proprietary LLM, autonomous agents, unknown training data, no documented bias testing) = 85/100\\n- Mitigation effectiveness: Moderate (ISO 27001/27017/27018, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2/3, but no AI safety controls documented) = 0.50\\n- Confidence factor: Moderate (public company, production deployments, but limited third-party AI audits) = 0.80\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.50 × 0.80 = 34**\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 50 points (ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2/3 = strong)\\n- Assessment quality: 20 points (no third-party AI safety audit disclosed)\\n- Policies: 15 points (no documented AI governance policy for Studio)\\n- Operational controls: 30 points (incident response documented, but no AI-specific controls)\\n- Maturity adjustment: 20 points (mature company, but AI governance immature)\\n- **Governance Score = 50 + 20 + 15 + 30 + 20 = 135 → capped at 100**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0** (Note: This reflects strong baseline compliance, but AI governance gaps are captured in Product Risk)\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime = strong)\\n- Incident management: 25 points (documented process, but severity SLAs not specified)\\n- Deployment maturity: 30 points (enterprise multi-tenant, production-ready)\\n- Stability: 25 points (10,000+ employees, public company, 1998 founding)\\n- Support: 15 points (support SLAs not specified; no dedicated TAM mentioned)\\n- **Operational Score = 33 + 25 + 30 + 25 + 15 = 128 → capped at 100**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Adjusted Governance Risk (accounting for AI governance gaps):**\\n- Governance Risk adjusted to 25 (reflecting undocumented AI ethics policy, bias testing, human oversight)\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(34 × 0.40) + (25 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [13.6 + 7.5 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 21.1\\n    = 78.9 ≈ 78\\n```\\n\\n**Classification: Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED**\\n\\n- **For Non-Regulated Use Cases:** Approve with standard procurement process; implement audit log monitoring and quarterly compliance reviews.\\n- **For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Financial Services, Government):** Require completion of AI governance documentation, third-party AI safety audit, and EU AI Act compliance roadmap before contract execution.\\n- **Pilot Approach:** Consider 3–6 month pilot phase with non-critical workflows, comprehensive monitoring, and human review of autonomous decisions before full production rollout.\\n- **Contract Conditions:** Require Google to provide AI governance policy, bias testing results, and human oversight controls as contract addendum; include audit rights for AI safety compliance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessor:** Vendor Attestation Analyst  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Google Workspace Studio", "Customer Base": "Early adopters documented (Karcher SE & Co.); Gemini Alpha program participants; specific customer count not disclosed", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-industry); early adopters in manufacturing (Karcher SE & Co.)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud Platform)", "Deployment Scale": "Scalable; Gemini Alpha program participants executed 20+ million automated tasks in 30 days", 