30%  |  Operational risk 30%\n\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\n    2. Governance risk        16.00  (weight 30%)\n    3. Product risk            3.07  (weight 40%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (16.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
112c7475-91d6-4351-aa85-31ad5a26a30f	82	82	1c3b7cec-dbe1-47c7-a9f7-5b2cca37e0b0	83	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Google NotebookLM\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 78 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 88\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 72\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 82\\n- Company Maturity: 95\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nGoogle NotebookLM achieves a Trust Score of 78, placing it in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" category (70–79 range). The vendor demonstrates strong operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications (ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, SOC 1/2/3, HIPAA BAA), and excellent company stability (10,000+ employees, founded 1998, public company). However, the score is moderated by gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, or adversarial security testing details provided), incomplete data practices documentation (training data sourcing from third-party models with unknown provenance, extended data retention on backups up to 6 months), and missing support SLA details. The source-grounded architecture and automated rollback capability are significant strengths. **Recommendation:** Enhanced due diligence required; suitable for non-critical use cases; require mitigation roadmap for AI governance and training data transparency before high-stakes deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** NotebookLM\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Research synthesis, document analysis, note-taking automation, compliance audit acceleration, decision-ready insight generation\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-sector); Globe Telecom case study indicates telecommunications applicability; compliance-heavy industries (finance, healthcare, legal)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud Platform)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** SaaS (cloud-hosted); NotebookLM Enterprise option with customer Google Cloud project deployment\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-grade; supports up to 25 million words in sandbox; suitable for large-scale document ingestion\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (general availability); comprehensive analytics and audit logs available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Globe Telecom case study published; 83% user satisfaction on note-taking clarity; 3–4 hours/week productivity savings reported\\n- **Product Description:** NotebookLM is a source-grounded AI research and note-taking platform that synthesizes information from user-uploaded documents with citations, eliminating hallucinations. It ingests multiple formats (documents, PDFs, URLs, audio) and generates multimedia outputs (Audio Overviews, Mind Maps). Enterprise deployments offer data residency within customer Google Cloud projects, with HIPAA BAA eligibility and comprehensive audit logging.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (multinational technology company)\\n- **Year Founded:** 1998\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (Nasdaq: GOOGL/GOOG); not specified for NotebookLM product line\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Publicly traded; Headquarters: Mountain View, CA, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (multi-region deployment options available)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Third-party models (underlying model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Document understanding, information synthesis, summarization, cross-format analysis, multimedia generation (audio, mind maps)\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no documented staged deployment or safety framework provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** User-controlled (users upload documents and direct analysis); no autonomous decision-making described; admin controls available for Enterprise deployments\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate transparency; responses include citations to source documents; source-grounding architecture reduces hallucinations; prompt-level control available\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; underlying training data provenance unknown; no documentation of data filtering, deduplication, or bias mitigation in training corpus\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools described\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type of adversarial security testing documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified; no documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluation process documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** User-directed (users control document selection and analysis queries); admin controls available in Enterprise deployments; no automated content filtering or intervention mechanisms described\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; demonstrates mature incident management capability\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated instant rollback; enables rapid recovery from deployment issues\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Documents (text, PDF), URLs, audio files, user notes, analysis outputs (Audio Overviews, Mind Maps)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no explicit policy on PII detection, masking, or handling; HIPAA BAA available suggests PII-capable infrastructure\\n- **Data Collection:** User-uploaded documents via web interface; API integration available (implied by Enterprise deployment model); user-directed analysis queries\\n- **Data Storage:** Google Cloud Platform infrastructure; encrypted in transit and at rest (implied by ISO 27001/27017/27018 certifications); Enterprise deployments stored within customer's Google Cloud project\\n- **Data Retention:** User-controlled deletion; uploaded materials, saved notes, and audio overviews retained until user deletion. For Enterprise: deleted when notebook or project deleted. Google general policy: deletion processes take ~2 months; data may remain on backup systems for up to 6 months\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (multi-region support); Enterprise deployments within customer Google Cloud project\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion; automated deletion upon notebook/project removal (Enterprise); extended backup retention (up to 6 months) noted\\n- **Sub-processors:** Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure, storage, compute); third-party model providers (underlying AI models); payment processors (not specified); authentication (Google identity services implied)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security Controls)\\n  - ISO 27018 (Personal Data Protection in Cloud)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - SOC 1 (Financial Controls)\\n  - SOC 2 (Security, Availability, Processing Integrity, Confidentiality, Privacy)\\n  - SOC 3 (General Controls)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (eligible for healthcare PHI handling)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit body and methodology not documented; frequency of re-certification not stated\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - HIPAA: BAA available\\n  - GDPR: Implied compliance (ISO 27701, data residency options); DPA availability not explicitly stated\\n  - CCPA: Not explicitly addressed\\n  - EU AI Act: No readiness statement provided\\n  - NIST: Not explicitly addressed\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligible; suitable for healthcare PHI handling with appropriate contract terms\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Data residency options and ISO 27701 certification suggest GDPR readiness; DPA availability not confirmed\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed; no statement on compliance preparation or risk classification\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Incident response plan tested annually\\n  - Certification audit frequency not specified\\n  - Last audit date not provided\\n  - Audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response time commitments documented\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** \\n  - Not specified; no documented release process, frequency, or rollback readiness practices provided\\n  - Automated instant rollback capability available (suggests mature deployment infrastructure)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** \\n  - Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure, storage, compute)\\n  - Third-party AI model providers (underlying model sourcing)\\n  - Payment processors (not specified)\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no documented frequency of vendor risk assessments\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** \\n  - Google Cloud Platform SLAs typically 99.95% uptime (standard GCP commitment); specific NotebookLM SLA is 99.9%\\n  - Third-party model provider SLAs not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; enables usage monitoring and performance tracking\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; supports compliance auditing and forensic investigation\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** \\n  - Incident response plan (tested annually)\\n  - Automated rollback capability documented\\n  - Certifications (ISO, SOC, HIPAA) available\\n  - Security and compliance documentation implied by certifications\\n  - AI safety testing results not specified\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available; specific details and NDA terms not provided in attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Exceptional Company Maturity:** Google's 10,000+ employee base, 25+ year operating history, and public company status provide strong financial stability and operational continuity.\\n2. **Comprehensive Security Certifications:** ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701 and SOC 1/2/3 demonstrate mature security and privacy controls; HIPAA BAA eligibility enables healthcare deployments.\\n3. **Source-Grounded Architecture:** Citation-based responses and document-grounded analysis reduce hallucination risk, a key differentiator for research and compliance use cases.\\n4. **Operational Maturity:** 99.9% uptime SLA, automated instant rollback, annual incident response testing, and comprehensive audit logging indicate production-ready infrastructure.\\n5. **Data Residency Flexibility:** Customer choice of region and Enterprise deployment within customer Google Cloud projects support data sovereignty requirements.\\n\\n### Gaps & Concerns\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency (Critical Gap):** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, adversarial security testing, or training data provenance. Third-party model sourcing with unknown training data raises hallucination and bias risks.\\n2. **Data Retention & Backup Exposure:** Extended backup retention (up to 6 months) and ~2-month deletion latency create compliance and privacy risks for sensitive data; not suitable for zero-retention requirements.\\n3. **Missing Support SLAs:** No severity-based response time commitments; unclear support availability for production incidents.\\n4. **Incomplete Regulatory Readiness:** No explicit GDPR DPA, CCPA compliance statement, or EU AI Act readiness documentation; limits applicability in regulated markets.\\n5. **Training Data Opacity:** Reliance on third-party models without disclosed training data filtering, deduplication, or bias mitigation creates risk for high-stakes use cases (healthcare, finance, legal).\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n- **For Non-Critical Use Cases:** Approved for productivity and research workflows (e.g., internal document synthesis, note-taking automation).\\n- **For Healthcare/Compliance Use Cases:** Require vendor to provide:\\n  - Documented AI ethics policy and bias testing roadmap\\n  - Training data provenance and filtering methodology\\n  - GDPR DPA and CCPA compliance confirmation\\n  - Support SLA commitments (P1/P2/P3 response times)\\n  - Zero-retention or shorter backup retention options\\n- **For High-Stakes Deployments:** Conduct independent security assessment and bias audit before production use; implement human-in-the-loop review for critical decisions.\\n- **Contract Conditions:** Require annual third-party AI safety audit, documented incident response testing results, and explicit data deletion SLA (< 30 days).\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Classification:** Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range) — Standard procurement process recommended with enhanced due diligence on AI governance and data practices.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "NotebookLM", "Customer Base": "Globe Telecom case study published; 83% user satisfaction on note-taking clarity; 3–4 hours/week productivity savings reported", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-sector); Globe Telecom case study indicates telecommunications applicability; compliance-heavy industries (finance, healthcare, legal)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud Platform)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise-grade; supports up to 25 million words i