re)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (16.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	2026-07-28 15:36:42.620682+05:30	** Google NotebookLM achieves a Trust Score of 78, placing it in the "Acceptable Vendor" category (70–79 range). The vendor demonstrates strong operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications (ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, SOC 1/2/3, HIPAA BAA), and excellent company stability (10,000+ employees, founded 1998, public company). However, the score is moderated by gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, or adversarial security testing details provided), incomplete data practices documentation (training data sourcing from third-party models with unknown provenance, extended data retention on backups up to 6 months), and missing support SLA details. The source-grounded architecture and automated rollback capability are significant strengths. **Recommendation:** Enhanced due diligence required; suitable for non-critical use cases; require mitigation roadmap for AI governance and training data transparency before high-stakes deployments. ---	2.9653	16	36	16.7861	B	Trusted Vendor	{"llm": {"error": null, "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Google NotebookLM achieves a Trust Score of 78, placing it in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" category (70–79 range). The vendor demonstrates strong operational maturity, comprehensive security c