of Testing Data:** Product stage not specified; no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not quantified; 8 corroborating evidence points (repeat Slack questions: 30%, announcements sent: 173, agent comments/month: 200)\\n- **Product Description:** Guru AI is an AI-driven knowledge management platform that centralizes company information and delivers real-time cited answers to reduce information search time and improve decision-making accuracy. The platform integrates with enterprise tools and offers moderate explainability features. However, it lacks formal security certifications, documented AI safety testing, and compliance frameworks required for regulated industries.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Guru.com (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 1998\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Pittsburgh, PA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-based; global reach not documented)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (inferred: LLM-based or custom NLP for knowledge retrieval and Q&A)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Knowledge retrieval, real-time answer generation with citations, decision support\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows mentioned\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); real-time citations provided; prompt-level control not documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team or third-party audits mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal testing conducted; adversarial security testing not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Not specified; inferred: documents, Slack messages, enterprise communications, knowledge base content\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no documented policy on PII collection, use, or restrictions\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (inferred from product description); retention options not specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** \\"Data stored as long as necessary to provide products and services; account data retained until account deletion unless no longer needed\\"—vague and non-compliant with GDPR/CCPA standards\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or residency options documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied); automated deletion not documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently** (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other third-party certifications)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No documented alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable; no BAA eligibility stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not documented; no DPA availability mentioned\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime/year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, frequency, or rollback/readiness practices\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payment processor not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No documented vendor risk assessment frequency\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No critical vendor SLAs documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (908 active AI users/month, 1M+ card views, 30% repeat Slack questions, 173 announcements, 200 agent comments/month)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Minimal; no formal testing results, no AI governance policy, no security certifications\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n### Scoring Rationale (Applied Formula Guidance)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS) formula** from the vector database:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85/100 (AI system with undocumented training data, no formal testing, moderate explainability)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.35 (basic audit logs, incident response plan not tested, no certifications)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.60 (no third-party validation, basic metrics only)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.35 × 0.60 = 17.85 → 18**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 0 points (none currently)\\n- Assessment Quality: 5 points (basic metrics; no third-party audit)\\n- Policies: 5 points (data retention policy only; no AI ethics, no security policy)\\n- Operational Controls: 10 points (incident response documented but untested; rollback capability present)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 15 points (10+ year company, established)\\n- **Governance Score = 35 → Governance Risk = 100 − 35 = 65**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year downtime)\\n- Incident Management: 10 points (documented but untested)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 15 points (SaaS, multi-tenant assumed; no enterprise deployment details)\\n- Stability: 20 points (mature company, 25+ years operating)\\n- Support: 5 points (support SLAs not specified)\\n- **Operational Score = 75 → Operational Risk = 100 − 75 = 25**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\nVTS = 100 − [(18 × 0.40) + (65 × 0.30) + (25 × 0.30)]\\nVTS = 100 − [7.2 + 19.5 + 7.5]\\nVTS = 100 − 34.2\\n**VTS = 65.8 → 66 (Rounded)**\\n\\n**Adjusted to 52 (Moderate Risk)** due to:\\n- **Critical gaps not fully captured in formula:** No security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), no formal AI safety testing, undocumented training data, vague data retention policy, unspecified support SLAs, no GDPR/HIPAA alignment\\n- **Regulatory industry unsuitability:** Vendor is not suitable for healthcare, financial services, or government without substantial remediation\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Classification & Recommendation\\n\\n**Grade: D (Review Recommended)**\\n- **Score Range:** 60–69 (Significant gaps; immature processes; limited track record for regulated use)\\n- **Vendor Profile:** Mature company with reasonable operational SLA but critical compliance and AI governance gaps; suitable for **non-regulated, internal knowledge management only**\\n- **Recommended Action:** **Extended validation required; pilot only; not recommended for production in regulated industries**\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Conditional Approval Criteria (If Proceeding)\\n\\n**MUST FIX (Before Production Deployment):**\\n1. **Security Certifications:** Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 audit (minimum 6 months)\\n2. **AI Governance:** Document AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, and human-in-the-loop controls\\n3. **Training Data:** Provide documentation of training data sources, curation, and bias mitigation\\n4. **Data Practices:** Clarify PII handling, data residency options, and GDPR/CCPA compliance\\n5. **Support SLAs:** Define P1/P2/P3 response targets and escalation procedures\\n6. **Formal Testing:** Conduct adversarial security testing and bias audits (third-party recommended)\\n\\n**SHOULD FIX (Reduces Residual Risk):**\\n7. Test incident response plan end-to-end\\n8. Provide sub-processor list and vendor SLAs\\n9. Clarify infrastructure provider and data location options\\n10. Document change management and release cadence\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Use Case Suitability\\n\\n| Use Case | Suitability | Rationale |\\n|----------|------------|-----------|\\n| **Internal Knowledge Management (Non-Regulated)** | ✅ Suitable | Mature company, reasonable SLA, basic audit logs |\\n| **Healthcare / Clinical Decision Support** | ❌ Not Suitable | No HIPAA, no formal AI testing, no certifications |\\n| **Financial Services** | ❌ Not Suitable | No SOC 2, no GDPR, no compliance framework |\\n| **Government / Public Sector** | ❌ Not Suitable | No FedRAMP, no security certifications |\\n| **Pilot / Proof-of-Concept** | ⚠️ Conditional | Acceptable for non-sensitive internal use only |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nGuru.com is a **mature, operationally stable vendor** suitable for **non-regulated internal knowledge management use cases**. However, it presents **unacceptable risk for regulated industries** due to the absence of security certifications, formal AI safety testing, documented governance policies, and compliance frameworks. The vendor should be considered only for **pilot deployments in low-risk, non-sensitive environments** and only after remediation of critical gaps (SOC 2 audit, AI governance documentation, formal testing, and GDPR/HIPAA alignment).", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Guru AI", "Customer Base": "Not quantified; 8 corroborating evidence points (repeat Slack questions: 30%, announcements sent: 173, agent comments/month: 200)", "Target Industry": "General enterprise (cross-sector); not specialized for regulated industries", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified; typical customer engagement metrics: 908 active AI users/month, 1M+ card views", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise knowledge management, real-time cited answers, information retrieval, decision support", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "Guru AI is an AI-driven knowledge management platform that centralizes company information and delivers real-time cited answers to reduce information search time and improve decision-making accuracy. The platform integrates with enterprise tools and offers moderate explainability features. However, it lacks formal security certifications, documented AI safety testing, and compliance frameworks required for regulated industries.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Product stage not specified; no formal testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Guru.com (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "1998", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed US-based; global reach not documented)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Pitts