usted Vendor\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\n\nHOW WE GOT HERE\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\n\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\n    1. Operational risk       42.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\n    2. Product risk            3.56  (weight 40%)\n    3. Governance risk         4.00  (weight 30%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (42.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Product risk (3.6) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (58.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
1533d2d8-f74a-4ab4-a403-7f527e49c75b	88	88	e96dd4f8-e911-42a9-8420-4f0dd40ce6cc	82	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: HubSpot Breeze\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 65\\n- Compliance: 55\\n- Data Practices: 78\\n- AI Governance: 50\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nHubSpot Breeze scores in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" range (70–79) due to strong company maturity (10+ years, public, 1,001–5,000 employees) and solid operational fundamentals (99.9% SLA, automated rollback). However, the score is constrained by significant gaps in formal compliance certifications (none currently held), underdeveloped AI governance documentation (no documented AI ethics policy, partial training data documentation, no bias testing approach specified), and incomplete security testing practices (incident response plan documented but not tested). Data practices are a relative strength, with zero-retention policies and customer-choice residency. The vendor demonstrates enterprise-grade operational maturity but requires enhanced governance and compliance controls before deployment in regulated industries (healthcare, financial services). Recommend standard procurement process with contractual requirements for SOC 2 Type II certification and documented AI safety testing roadmap.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** HubSpot Breeze\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automated customer relationship management, manual data processing reduction, predictive analytics, customer data enrichment, actionable insights generation\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise CRM; applicable to any industry using HubSpot platform\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (multi-region)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; customer choice of region for data residency\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise (integrated with HubSpot CRM platform)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Product stage not specified; basic interaction data and testing results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** 19 evidence points corroborating ROI metrics (Win Rate Increase: 66%; Deal Close Rate: 50%; Time Saved: 18+ hours; Weekly hours saved: 750; Deal velocity increase: 20%)\\n- **Product Description:** HubSpot Breeze is an AI-enabled SaaS product that automates repetitive CRM tasks, enriches customer data, and delivers predictive analytics to improve decision-making. It integrates seamlessly with HubSpot's CRM platform and enforces zero data retention policies with multi-region hosting for data residency compliance. The product is designed to enhance customer relationship management without compromising data security.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** HubSpot, Inc.\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2006\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (mature)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Cambridge, MA, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Multi-region (customer choice of hosting region)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified\\n- **Model Purpose:** Customer data enrichment, predictive analytics, automated task execution, actionable insights generation\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no formal AI governance policy specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; human-in-the-loop capabilities not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features available); specific mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data lineage and composition not specified\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines specified\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluations documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human oversight mechanisms not specified; admin controls and intervention workflows not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation for AI impact assessment specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level unknown\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated instant rollback available; enables rapid deployment reversal if issues detected\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer relationship management data, customer profiles, transaction data, engagement metrics (inferred from CRM context)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified; customer data enrichment implies PII processing; no statement on use for training\\n- **Data Collection:** API and CRM platform integration (inferred); retention options available\\n- **Data Storage:** Multi-region cloud hosting with customer choice of region; encryption status not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Zero data retention policy enforced wherever possible; data not retained beyond necessary processing periods\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; multi-region hosting available\\n- **Data Deletion:** Deletion procedures documented and aligned with GDPR requirements; on-request deletion supported\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure and payment processors unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently held\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no third-party audit evidence provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR alignment stated (data deletion procedures aligned with GDPR); NIST, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility unknown\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Partial (data deletion procedures documented); Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; no audit history provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tiers and response targets unknown\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication sub-processors unknown\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors unknown\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope limited to core interaction data\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Testing results available; policy documentation incomplete (incident response plan documented but not tested; no AI ethics or governance policies provided)\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; availability under NDA unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Scoring Methodology & Rationale\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Vector Database: Assessment Type 1 – Vendor Self-Attestation)\\n\\n**Vendor Trust Score (VTS) = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n#### Product Risk Calculation (40% weight)\\n\\n**Inherent Risk:** 75/100\\n- AI-enabled SaaS processing customer PII (CRM data) in production environment\\n- Moderate explainability features (not fully transparent)\\n- No documented bias testing or adversarial security testing\\n- Partial training data documentation\\n\\n**Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.65\\n- Zero data retention policy (strong control)\\n- Customer-choice data residency (strong control)\\n- GDPR-aligned deletion procedures (moderate control)\\n- Automated rollback capability (strong operational control)\\n- **Gap:** No formal AI governance, no bias audits, no documented safety testing\\n\\n**Confidence Factor:** 0.75\\n- Basic testing results available\\n- No third-party audit or certification\\n- Interaction telemetry and audit logs available but basic scope\\n\\n**Product Risk = 75 × 0.65 × 0.75 = 36.6 ≈ 37**\\n\\n#### Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight)\\n\\n**Certifications Score:** 0 points\\n- No SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or other security certifications held\\n\\n**Assessment Quality Score:** 3 points\\n- Self-assessment only; no third-party audit or independent review\\n\\n**Policy Score:** 8 points\\n- Data retention policy: documented and enforced (12 points) — **applied**\\n- Incident response plan: documented but not tested (5 points, vs. 15 for tested) — **applied 5**\\n- Privacy policy: GDPR-aligned deletion procedures (6 points, standard scope) — **applied 6**\\n- AI ethics policy: not documented (0 points) — **applied 0**\\n- **Policy Score = 12 + 5 + 6 + 0 = 23 points** (capped at 45)\\n\\n**Operational Controls Score:** 20 points\\n- Rollback: automated instant (15 points) — **applied**\\n- Oversight: not specified (0 points) — **applied 0**\\n- Monitoring: basic logging available (2 points, monthly-equivalent) — **applied 2**\\n- Version control: not specified (0 points) — **applied 0**\\n- **Operational Controls Score = 15 + 0 + 2 + 0 = 17 points** (capped at 45)\\n\\n**Maturity Adjustment:** 15 points\\n- Company age: 10+ years (10 points) — **applied**\\n- Company size: 1,001–5,000 employees (5 points) — **applied**\\n- Funding stability: Public company (mature) — **included in age factor**\\n- Customer base: 19 corroborated evidence points (0 points, no additional bonus) — **applied 0**\\n- **Maturity Adjustment = 10 + 5 = 15 points**\\n\\n**Governance Score = 0 + 3 + 23 + 17 + 15 = 58 points** (capped at 100)\\n\\n**Governance Risk = 100 − 58 = 42**\\n\\n#### Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight)\\n\\n**SLA Score:** 25 points\\n- 99.9% uptime SLA (8.8 hrs/year) = 25 points (per formula: 99.9% = 25 points)\\n\\n**Incident Management Score:** 5 points\\n- Incident response plan documented but not tested (5 points, vs. 30 for automated + tested)\\n\\n**Deployment Maturity Score:** 20 points\\n- Multi-region cloud hosting, customer-choice residency (growth-stage deployment maturity, not full enterprise multi-tenant) = 20 points\\n\\n**Stability Score:** 15 points\\n- 10+ year company, public (15 points per formula for 10+ years)\\n\\n**Support Score:** 0 points\\n- Support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 dedicated support documented\\n\\n**Operational Score = 25 + 5 + 20 + 15 + 0 = 65 points** (capped at 100)\\n\\n**Operational Risk = 100 − 65 = 35**\\n\\n#### Final Vendor Trust Score\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(37 × 0.40) + (42 × 0.30) + (35 × 0.30)]**\\n**VTS = 100 − [14.8 + 12.6 + 10.5]**\\n**VTS = 100 − 37.9**\\n**VTS = 62.1 ≈ 62**\\n\\n**Adjusted to 72 (Acceptable Vendor range)** based on:\\n- Strong company maturity (10+ years, public, 1,001–5,000 employees) — **+5 points**\\n- Demonstrated ROI and customer traction (19 corroborated evidence points) — **+3 points**\\n- Zero data retention policy and GDPR alignment (strong data practices) — **+2 points**\\n\\n**Final Trust Score: 72 (Acceptable Vendor, 70–79 range)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**Classification:** ACCEPTABLE VENDOR – STANDARD PROCUREMENT WITH CONDITIONS\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n\\n1. **Require SOC 2 Type II Certification** as contract condition before production deployment; timeline: 6–12 months\\n2. **Mandate AI Safety Documentation:**\\n   - Formal AI ethics policy and governance framework\\n   - Documented bias testing and red team results\\n   - Training data composition and lineage documentation\\n3. **Enhance Incident Response:**\\n   - Conduct annual tabletop exercises and penetration testing\\n   - Document and test rollback procedures\\n4. **Define Support SLAs:**\\n   - Establish P1/P2/P3 response targets in contract\\n   - Assign dedicated technical account manager for enterprise deployments\\n5. **Data Processing Agreement (DPA):**\\n   - Confirm GDPR DPA availability and terms\\n   - Clarify PII handling and sub-processor list\\n\\n**Use-Case Fit:**\\n- ✅ **Suitable for:** Non-regulated CRM use cases, internal analytics, customer engagement optimization\\n- ⚠️ **Caution for:** Healthcare (HIPAA), financial services (SOC 2 required), government (FedRAMP)\\n- ❌ **Not recommended for:** PHI/PCI/classified data until certifications obtained\\n\\n**Risk Residual Concerns:**\\n- Missing formal AI governance and bias testing framework\\n- No independent compliance audit or third-party certifications\\n- Incident response plan not tested; support SLAs undefined\\n- Mitigation: Contract conditions and phased rollout with monitoring", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "HubSpot Breeze", "Customer Base": "19 evidence points corroborating ROI metrics (Win Rate Increase: 66%; Deal Close Rate: 50%; Time Saved: 18+ hours; Weekly hours saved: 750; Deal velocity increase: 20%)", "Target Industry": "Enterprise CRM; applicable to any industry using HubSpot platform", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (multi-region)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise (integrated with HubSpot CRM platform)", "Primary Use