VE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Product risk (2.9) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
efd806b2-06e3-4878-95cc-43e2d283f7f4	94	94	d6235914-4105-4a6d-93ad-1e6a6d3eb4c7	84	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Microsoft 365 Copilot\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 82 (Trusted Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 92\\n- Compliance: 90\\n- Data Practices: 78\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 95\\n- Company Maturity: 95\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nMicrosoft 365 Copilot achieves a Trusted Vendor classification (80–89 range) driven by exceptional operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications, and proven company stability. The vendor demonstrates market-leading infrastructure reliability (99.99% SLA, automated rollback) and extensive compliance credentials (SOC 2/3, FedRAMP, HITRUST, ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, ISO 42001). However, the score is tempered by significant gaps in AI governance transparency—no documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, or training data documentation are specified—and moderate data practice concerns around limited residency options (EU only) and unclear PII handling specifics. The proprietary/closed model transparency and lack of human oversight documentation further constrain the AI Governance category. Strengths in operational excellence and compliance posture support fast-track procurement for non-healthcare, non-regulated use cases; healthcare deployments require explicit mitigation of governance gaps before contract execution.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Microsoft 365 Copilot\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-powered productivity enhancement across Microsoft 365 applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams); manual data processing automation, task efficiency, decision-making support, compliance and security maintenance.\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise; cross-industry (healthcare, financial services, government, technology, e-commerce)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (Microsoft infrastructure); SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted only; on-premises deployment not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-wide; typical deployment across organizational Microsoft 365 tenant\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product with basic test results available\\n- **Pricing:** Add-on license required for Microsoft 365 Copilot; Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat available without additional license\\n- **Customer Base:** 21 evidence points corroborating ROI metrics; average monthly usage 83%; 39,000 hours saved annually across customer base\\n- **Product Description:** Microsoft 365 Copilot is a proprietary AI assistant integrated into Microsoft 365 productivity applications, leveraging organizational data and web sources to automate manual tasks and enhance decision-making. The product delivers documented ROI (30% reduction in manual processing, 2x task automation efficiency improvement) and operates under comprehensive security and compliance frameworks (SOC 2/3, FedRAMP, HITRUST, ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, ISO 42001). However, training data documentation and bias testing methodologies are not publicly disclosed, and AI governance policies lack transparency.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Microsoft Corporation\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (subsidiary/division of Microsoft Corporation)\\n- **Year Founded:** 1975\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+ (Microsoft total; Copilot division not separately specified)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Microsoft FY2024 revenue ~$245B (public company); Copilot product revenue not separately disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Public company (NASDAQ: MSFT); Headquarters: Redmond, WA, USA; Strategic partnerships with OpenAI\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global; data residency options limited to EU only (per attestation)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary; specific model architecture not disclosed (likely LLM-based given Microsoft-OpenAI partnership and Copilot positioning)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding and generation; task automation; document analysis; meeting summarization; data synthesis across Microsoft 365 applications\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no documented staged deployment framework or safety governance policy provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop, monitoring, or intervention capabilities disclosed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation specified\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and filtering methodologies not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework specified\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluation program documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No documented admin controls, content filtering, intervention mechanisms, or clinical/expert review workflows specified\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for impact assessment specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested quarterly; demonstrates mature incident management capability\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated instant rollback; enables rapid remediation of failed deployments or security incidents\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Microsoft 365 organizational data (documents, spreadsheets, presentations, emails, chat messages, meeting recordings); web data; user-provided organizational data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified; Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat allows user-provided organizational data; extent of PII processing and customer data usage for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API integration with Microsoft 365 applications; chat interface; organizational data ingestion\\n- **Data Storage:** Microsoft cloud infrastructure (Azure); encryption standards not explicitly specified (inferred: AES-256 per ISO 27001/27017/27018 compliance)\\n- **Data Retention:** Customer data retained per organizational policies and Microsoft 365 existing data retention commitments; deleted per Microsoft procedures aligned with GDPR and regulatory requirements\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** EU only (per attestation); no US, GCP, or customer-choice residency options documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion per Microsoft procedures; on-request deletion capability not explicitly specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Microsoft Azure (infrastructure); OpenAI (potential model partnership); payment processors and authentication providers not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security Controls)\\n  - ISO 27018 (PII Protection in Cloud)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management Systems)\\n  - SOC 1, SOC 2, SOC 3 (Service Organization Controls)\\n  - FedRAMP (Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program)\\n  - NIST CSF (Cybersecurity Framework)\\n  - HITRUST (Healthcare Information and Management Systems Security)\\n  - PCI DSS (Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard)\\n  - GDPR Compliant\\n  - CSA STAR Level 1 & Level 2 (Cloud Security Alliance)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (third-party vs. internal) not disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST CSF, GDPR, CCPA (implied via GDPR compliance), EU AI Act readiness not explicitly stated\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HITRUST certification indicates healthcare compliance capability; BAA eligibility not explicitly confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR compliant; DPA availability not explicitly stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no documented engagement or preparation roadmap\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes downtime per year); enterprise-grade availability commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, and change notification procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Microsoft Azure (infrastructure); OpenAI (potential model partnership); sub-processors not fully enumerated\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Vendor risk assessment frequency not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Azure SLAs (99.99% uptime) inherited; OpenAI partnership terms not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; 21 evidence points corroborating ROI (83% average monthly usage, 6 hours monthly time savings, 5 hours info-gathering savings, 1.4 hours meeting minutes savings, 39,000 hours annual savings)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; export capability and format not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; detailed policy documentation (AI governance, bias testing, training data) not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no indication of NDA-protected testing results or safety validation data\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (VTS Formula)\\n\\nPer the retrieved **Vendor Self-Attestation** formula:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Inherent Risk: 65 (proprietary model, no training data documentation, no bias testing, no human oversight documented)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.60 (comprehensive security certifications, but AI governance gaps limit mitigation)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.85 (SOC 2/3, FedRAMP, HITRUST, but no third-party AI safety audit)\\n- **Product Risk = 65 × 0.60 × 0.85 = 33.15 ≈ 33**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n- Certifications: 50 points (SOC 2/3, FedRAMP, HITRUST, ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, ISO 42001)\\n- Assessment Quality: 15 points (third-party audit implied by SOC/FedRAMP, but frequency and recency not specified)\\n- Policies: 20 points (data retention policy documented; AI ethics, incident response, privacy policies partially documented)\\n- Operational Controls: 35 points (automated rollback, quarterly incident testing; human oversight and monitoring not documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 15 points (10+ years, public company, profitable, large customer base)\\n- **Governance Score = MIN(100, 50 + 15 + 20 + 35 + 15) = 100 (capped)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 0**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.99% uptime = 52 min/year downtime)\\n- Incident Management: 30 points (tested quarterly)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 30 points (enterprise multi-tenant, cloud-hosted)\\n- Stability: 22 points (10+ years, public company, profitable)\\n- Support: 15 points (support SLAs not specified; no dedicated TAM documented)\\n- **Operational Score = MIN(100, 33 + 30 + 30 + 22 + 15) = 100 (capped)**\\n- **Operational Risk = 0**\\n\\n**Final VTS:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(33 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [13.2 + 0 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 13.2\\n    = 86.8 ≈ 87\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 82 (Trusted Vendor, 80–89 range)** to account for:\\n- AI governance transparency gaps (no documented ethics policy, bias testing, training data documentation, human oversight)\\n- Limited data residency (EU only; no US or customer-choice options)\\n- Proprietary/closed model (no explainability or prompt-level control)\\n- Unspecified support SLAs and change management processes\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Classification:** **TRUSTED VENDOR (Grade B: 80–89)**\\n\\n**Recommended Action:** Standard procurement process with governance enhancement requirements\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Exceptional Operations (0 risk):** 99.99% SLA, automated rollback, quarterly incident testing, enterprise-scale deployment\\n2. **Exceptional Compliance (0 risk):** Comprehensive certifications (SOC 2/3, FedRAMP, HITRUST, ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, ISO 42001)\\n3. **Company Maturity:** 10+ years, public company, 10,000+ employees, global operations\\n4. **Proven ROI:** 21 evidence points, 30% manual processing reduction, 2x task automation efficiency\\n\\n### Gaps & Mitigation Requirements\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency (Critical):** \\n   - Require vendor to provide documented AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, and training data composition\\n   - Require third-party AI safety audit or equivalent validation before deployment\\n   - Implement continuous model drift monitoring and user feedback review workflow\\n\\n2. **Data Residency Constraints (Moderate):**\\n   - EU-only residency may conflict with US/APAC deployments\\n   - Clarify residency options and data localization roadmap\\n\\n3. **Human Oversight (Moderate):**\\n   - Require documentation of admin controls, content filtering, and intervention mechanisms\\n   - Implement organizational review workflows for high-stakes outputs (healthcare, finance, legal)\\n\\n4. **Support SLAs (Moderate):**\\n   - Require explicit P1/P2/P3 response time commitments\\n   - Negotiate dedicated technical account manager for enterprise deployments\\n\\n### Conditional Approval Criteria\\n- **For Non-Regulated Use Cases (e.g., productivity, general enterprise):** Approve with standard procurement; implement organizational governance controls\\n- **For Healthcare/Financial/Government:** Require mitigation gap closure (AI governance documentation, bias testing, human oversight) as contract condition before production deployment\\n- **For EU-Only Deployments:** Approve as-is; residency constraints aligned with GDPR\\n- **For US/APAC Deployments:** Clarify residency options and data localization roadmap before contract execution\\n\\n### Contract Conditions\\n1. Vendor to deliver AI ethics policy and bias testing methodology within 30 days of contract signature\\n2. Third-party AI safety audit or equivalent validation required before healthcare/financial deployment\\n3. Continuous model drift monitoring and organizational review workflow implementation required\\n4. Explicit P1/P2/P3 support SLAs and change management procedures required\\n5. Data residency options and localization roadmap clarification required for non-EU deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK SUMMARY TABLE\\n\\n| Risk Category | Score | Status | Mitigation |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Product Risk** | 33 | Managed | Require AI governance documentation, bias testing, training data transparency |\\n| **Governance Risk** | 0 | Exceptional | Comprehensive certifications; enhance AI ethics policy documentation |\\n| **Operational Risk** | 0 | Exceptional | Maintain current SLA and incident management practices |\\n| **Data Practices Risk** | 22 | Managed | Clarify PII handling, residency options, data deletion procedures |\\n| **AI Governance Risk** | 35 | Moderate | Require ethics policy, bias audits, human oversight 