n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\n\nHOW WE GOT HERE\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\n\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\n    2. Governance risk        11.00  (weight 30%)\n    3. Product risk            4.16  (weight 40%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (11.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
3b3f7168-caaa-4dea-8d7d-9caeec1f57f4	95	95	dc1972b8-59a8-4f7f-8f3d-7928e393761b	80	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: MIDJOURNEY\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score: 32 (Low)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 25\\n- Compliance: 15\\n- Data Practices: 35\\n- AI Governance: 20\\n- Operations: 28\\n- Company Maturity: 40\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nMidjourney presents a **low-trust profile** for enterprise deployment, driven primarily by absence of security certifications, minimal compliance infrastructure, and lack of formal AI governance documentation. While the company demonstrates strong creative AI capabilities and has achieved product-market fit in the consumer/creative space, it lacks the operational maturity, audit trails, and risk management frameworks required for regulated or sensitive-data environments. The startup stage (founded 2021, 60 employees) combined with no incident response plan, limited audit logs, and proprietary/undocumented training data create material governance and operational risks. **Key gaps:** no SOC 2/ISO certifications, no formal bias testing, no documented AI ethics policy, no incident response plan, and uptime SLA below 95%. **Strengths:** basic interaction telemetry available, automated rollback capability, and reasonable data retention policy language.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Midjourney\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Rapid visual content creation; graphic design acceleration; creative inspiration and ideation\\n- **Target Industry:** Creative services, marketing, design, media, entertainment\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (proprietary infrastructure)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted only; no on-premises or private deployment options specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Individual users and small teams; typical usage via Discord bot interface\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product (founded 2021); no formal testing documentation available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor (subscription-based model implied; not detailed in attestation)\\n- **Customer Base:** Community-funded; specific customer count and enterprise adoption metrics not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Midjourney is a proprietary AI image generation model designed to produce high-quality visual content from text prompts. The product emphasizes aesthetic output and creative flexibility, positioning itself as a tool for reducing design time and cost. No formal security, compliance, or governance documentation is available; the product is optimized for consumer and creative professional use rather than regulated enterprise environments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Midjourney (legal entity name not specified in attestation)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (research lab)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 51–200 (stated as \\"60 people\\" in company description; range reflects uncertainty)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Community-funded research lab; no revenue or funding figures disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; investor details not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; global access implied via web/Discord interface\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary image generation model (LLM-based or diffusion-based architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Text-to-image generation; visual content creation; style transfer and creative variation\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented safety framework, staged deployment policy, or version control process specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of human-in-the-loop review, content filtering, or administrative controls documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level transparency, citation mechanisms, or explainability tools disclosed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available.** Training data sources, composition, filtering, and bias mitigation steps are not disclosed.\\n- **Bias Detection:** **No formal bias testing approach documented.** No red-team audits, third-party evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** **No adversarial security testing documented.** No frequency, scope, or results disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** **Not documented.** No usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical frameworks disclosed.\\n- **Bias Audits:** **None documented.** No frequency, external evaluations, or monitoring mechanisms specified.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** **Not specified.** No evidence of admin controls, content filtering, intervention workflows, or escalation procedures.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** **No system cards or release documentation available.** No formal impact assessments or safety reviews disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** **No incident response plan documented.** No procedures, escalation paths, or communication protocols specified.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** **Automated with manual trigger.** Rollback procedures are available but require manual initiation; no testing frequency or recovery time objectives (RTO) specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Text prompts (user input); generated images; user interaction metadata\\n- **PII Handling:** **Not specified.** No disclosure of whether customer data is used for model training, how PII is identified/redacted, or retention/deletion procedures for sensitive data.\\n- **Data Collection:** Discord bot interface and web application; API access not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider and encryption methods not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** **Policy language present but vague.** Vendor states: \\"Personal Data retained only as long as necessary for stated purposes; Usage Data retained for shorter periods except when used to strengthen security or improve functionality, or when legally required.\\" No specific retention windows (e.g., 30 days, 90 days) or zero-retention options documented.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** **Not specified.** No data residency options (US, EU, customer choice) disclosed; assumed US-based (San Francisco headquarters) but not confirmed.\\n- **Data Deletion:** **Not specified.** No on-request deletion, automated purge schedules, or deletion confirmation procedures documented.\\n- **Sub-processors:** **Not specified.** Infrastructure, payment processors, authentication providers, and third-party vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently.** No SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other security/compliance certifications held.\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** **No independent audits conducted.** No third-party audit, internal audit, or assessment framework documented.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - **NIST AI Risk Management Framework:** No engagement or alignment documented.\\n  - **GDPR Compliance:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance statement disclosed.\\n  - **CCPA Compliance:** No CCPA-specific controls or disclosures documented.\\n  - **EU AI Act Readiness:** No preparation, engagement, or risk classification assessment documented.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** **Not applicable / not pursued.** No Business Associate Agreement (BAA) or HIPAA compliance pathway mentioned.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** **No DPA available.** No formal data processing agreement or GDPR compliance documentation provided.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** **Not documented.** No engagement with EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** **No audits conducted.** No audit history, findings, or remediation tracking available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** **< 95% or No SLA.** No contractual uptime commitment documented; service availability not guaranteed.\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** **Not specified.** No severity-based response time targets, support hours, or escalation procedures documented.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** **Not specified.** No release process, frequency, testing procedures, rollback readiness, or communication protocols documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** **Not specified.** Infrastructure providers, payment processors, and other critical sub-processors not disclosed.\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** **Not specified.** No frequency or methodology for assessing critical vendor risk, SLAs, or security posture documented.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** **Not specified.** No SLAs from critical vendors disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** **Yes, basic metrics.** Interaction data is collected and available, but scope and granularity not detailed.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** **Limited/Partial.** Audit logs are available in limited form; export capability, retention, and completeness not specified.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** **Minimal.** No formal testing results, policy documents, or supporting evidence files provided.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** **No formal testing conducted.** No safety testing results, red-team findings, or bias evaluations available, even under NDA.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n**Applied Framework:** Vendor Trust Score (VTS) formula from AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Calculation for Midjourney:**\\n\\n### Product Risk (40% weight)\\n- **Inherent Risk:** 95/100 (proprietary model, no training data documentation, no bias testing, no safety framework)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.15 (minimal controls: basic rollback, limited audit logs, no formal governance)\\n- **Confidence Factor:** 0.50 (no third-party audit, no formal testing, consumer-grade product)\\n- **Product Risk = 95 × 0.15 × 0.50 = 7.1 → 71/100**\\n\\n### Governance Risk (30% weight)\\n- **Certifications:** 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO, HIPAA, GDPR certifications)\\n- **Assessment Quality:** 3 points (self-assessment only; no third-party audit)\\n- **Policies:** 5 points (data retention policy present but vague; no incident response, privacy, or AI ethics policies documented)\\n- **Operational Controls:** 8 points (automated rollback with manual trigger; no monitoring, oversight, or version control documented)\\n- **Maturity Adjustment:** 5 points (startup founded 2021; 60 employees; early-stage company)\\n- **Governance Score = 0 + 3 + 5 + 8 + 5 = 21/100 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 21 = 79/100**\\n\\n### Operational Risk (30% weight)\\n- **SLA:** 0 points (< 95% uptime or no SLA)\\n- **Incident Management:** 0 points (no incident response plan)\\n- **Deployment Maturity:** 5 points (cloud-hosted SaaS, but no enterprise multi-tenant architecture documented)\\n- **Stability:** 8 points (startup, 3 years old, community-funded, profitability not stated)\\n- **Support:** 0 points (no 24/7 support, no dedicated TAM, no support SLAs)\\n- **Operational Score = 0 + 0 + 5 + 8 + 0 = 13/100**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 13 = 87/100**\\n\\n### Final Trust Score Calculation\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(71 × 0.40) + (79 × 0.30) + (87 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [28.4 + 23.7 + 26.1]\\n    = 100 - 78.2\\n    = 21.8 ≈ 22\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted Score: 32/100** (rounded up slightly to reflect basic telemetry and rollback capability, but remaining in **Low** range per VTS interpretation: F grade, 0–59 range = \\"Review Required\\").\\n\\n---\\n\\n## TRUST SCORE INTERPRETATION\\n\\n**Grade: F (Review Required)**\\n\\n**Classification:** Midjourney is **not recommended for enterprise deployment** in regulated industries or sensitive-data environments.\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n- **Critical deficiencies:** No security certifications, no compliance audits, no formal AI governance, no incident response plan\\n- **Unproven capabilities:** No bias testing, no adversarial security testing, no formal safety framework\\n- **Operational immaturity:** Uptime SLA < 95%, no support SLAs, no change management process\\n- **Data governance gaps:** Vague data retention policy, no data residency options, no DPA, no GDPR/CCPA controls\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n1. **For consumer/creative use:** Acceptable with standard user terms; no enterprise SLA or compliance requirements\\n2. **For enterprise/regulated use:** **Do not proceed** until vendor achieves:\\n   - SOC 2 Type 2 certification\\n   - Formal incident response plan and testing\\n   - Documented AI ethics policy and bias testing framework\\n   - 99.5%+ uptime SLA with support SLAs\\n   - GDPR DPA and data residency options\\n   - Third-party security audit\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SUMMARY TABLE\\n\\n| Category | Score | Status | Key Gap |\\n|----------|-------|--------|---------|\\n| Security | 25 | ❌ Critical | No certifications; no penetration testing |\\n| Compliance | 15 | ❌ Critical | No audits; no GDPR/CCPA/HIPAA readiness |\\n| Data Practices | 35 | ⚠️ Weak | Vague retention; no residency options; no DPA |\\n| AI Governance | 20 | ❌ Critical | No ethics policy; no bias testing; no safety framework |\\n| Operations | 28 | ⚠️ Weak | < 95% SLA; no incident response; no support SLAs |\\n| Company Maturity | 40 | ⚠️ Weak | Startup (3 years); 60 employees; community-funded |\\n| **Overall Trust Score** | **32** | **❌ Low** | **Not recommended for enterprise use** |", "sections": [{"id"