UST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   82 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        21.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.20  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (21.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Raise Governance (79.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation\\n", "operational_risk": {"value": 36, "sla_score": {"value": 9, "uptime_points": 0, "response_time_points": 4, "resolution_time_points": 5}, "support_score": {"value": 5, "coverage_points": 0, "expertise_points": 1, "support_tier_points": 4}, "stability_score": {"value": 21, "company_age_years": 11, "company_age_points": 12, "financial_health_points": 5, "customer_retention_points": 4}, "operational_score": 64, "raw_operational_score": 64, "deployment_maturity_score": {"value": 14, "scale_points": 7, "multi_tenancy_points": 6, "production_readiness_points": 1}, "incident_management_score": {"value": 15, "plan_points": 10, "automation_points": 0, "communication_points": 5}}, "vector_retrieval": {"used": true, "error": null, "chunks": [{"id": "aa47a4b9-ef6f-4a92-a2ec-ae0bd90e7024", "score": 0.2900506681173647, "file_name": "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "chunk_index": 1, "content_preview": "supports sales enablement by estimating the difficulty of closing a specific deal via a Sales Confidence\\nScore (0–100, higher = stronger deal) that blends Customer Friction Risk (35%), Implementation Risk\\n(35%), and Competitive Risk (30%), "}, {"id": "7fd58480-1f48-4922-a0db-9764d8cd0335", "score": 0.2664799988269806, "file_name": "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "chunk_index": 13, "content_preview": "├─ Incident Management: 30 points (automated + tested)\\n├─ Deployment Maturity: 30 points (enterprise multi-tenant)\\n├─ Stability: 22 points (8-year company, profitable)\\n├─ Support: 20 points (24/7 dedicated support)\\n├─ Operational Score: 100"}, {"id": "4884fd64-a648-41e5-92be-2686512eca74", "score": 0.2470417022705078, "file_name": "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "chunk_index": 12, "content_preview": "Expertise:\\n- technicalAccountManager = \\"dedicated_tam\\" → 5 points\\nSupport_Score = 10 + 5 + 5 = 20 points\\n1.4.7 Final Operational Risk\\nFormula:\\nOperational_Score = SLA + Incident_Management + Deployment_Maturity +\\nStability + Support\\nOperati"}, {"id": "21a26e13-021b-4e4e-84e5-5da82ac9fc34", "score": 0.2111813002120677, "file_name": "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf", "chunk_index": 13, "content_preview": "● Require vendor delivery of missing features before pilot\\n● Executive checkpoint at Month 6 before pilot proceeds\\nSuccess Criteria for Month 6 Checkpoint:\\n4. All 3 critical positions hired and onboarded\\n5. AI Governance Board operational w"}, {"id": "3aeebc49-eb86-4850-99dd-9459b23811a9", "score": 0.19721204042434692, "file_name": "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 2 (1).pdf", "chunk_index": 1, "content_preview": "Assessment Type 3: COTS Buyer Side (Implementation Risk)\\n3.1 Assessment Overview\\nObjective: Quantify an organization's readiness to implement a commercial off-the-shelf\\n(COTS) AI product from a specific vendor.\\nPrimary Users: Organizations "}, {"id": "55e45060-ca0e-4b80-b132-88db1cfe7f4a", "score": 0.195701003074646, "file_name": "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "chunk_index": 9, "content_preview": "\\"third_party_review\\": 15,\\n\\"internal_audit\\": 10,\\n\\"internal_review\\": 8,\\n\\"self_assessment\\": 3,\\n\\"none\\": 0\\n}) + Audit_frequency_bonus\\nAudit_frequency_bonus = IF assessmentMethod INCLUDES \\"audit\\":\\nLOOKUP(auditFrequency, {\\n\\"annual\\": 5,\\n\\"bi_annual\\""}]}, "formula_vendor_trust_score": 81.62, "category_coverage_resolution": {"vector": {"used": true, "error": null, "pgvector_hits": {"Human Oversight Mechanisms": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.3765}, "Model Security & Integrity": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.4439}, "Post-Deployment Monitoring": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.3926}, "Incident Response & Recovery": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.4675}, "Transparency & Documentation": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.4753}, "Testing & Auditing Procedures": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.4733}, "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.5174}, "Access Management & Authentication": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.4542}, "Data Governance & Privacy Controls": {"files": ["AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf", "AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1 (1).pdf"], "best_score": 0.4202}}, "attestation_similarities": {"Human Oversight Mechanisms": 0.241, "Model Security & Integrity": 0.3614, "Post-Deployment Monitoring": 0.3898, "Incident Response & Recovery": 0.3013, "Transparency & Documentation": 0.3132, "Testing & Auditing Procedures": 0.3815, "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence": 0.3077, "Access Management & Authentication": 0.3024, "Data Governance & Privacy Controls": 0.353}}, "from_vector": ["Testing & Auditing Procedures"], "coverage_ratio": 0.8889, "required_count": 9, "from_attestation": ["Data Governance & Privacy Controls", "Model Security & Integrity", "Access Management & Authentication", "Post-Deployment Monitoring", "Incident Response & Recovery", "Transparency & Documentation", "Compliance & Regulatory Adherence"], "implemented_count": 8, "evidence_blob_chars": 364}}	vts-formula-1.0	VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\n========================================================================\n\nRESULT\n  Trust score:   82 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\n\nHOW WE GOT HERE\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\n\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\n    2. Governance risk        21.00  (weight 30%)\n    3. Product risk            3.20  (weight 40%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (21.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Raise Governance (79.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
b226ede8-486c-4a32-9b8d-3923143b71f0	97	97	d92f307b-5c4c-4e31-814e-32964d23011f	88	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: NOTION AI\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 72\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nNotion AI achieves an \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" classification (72/100) driven primarily by strong compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA) and solid operational maturity (99.9% SLA, automated rollback, annual incident testing). However, significant gaps in AI governance—including undocumented AI ethics policy, no formal bias testing, minimal human oversight specification, and lack of training data transparency—prevent a higher score. The vendor's use of third-party models with unknown training data and absence of formal AI safety testing create residual product risk. Company maturity is moderate (11-year-old growth-stage firm with 1,001–5,000 employees), supporting operational reliability but not offsetting governance gaps. **Recommendation:** Acceptable for non-critical use cases; require enhanced AI governance documentation and bias audit before deployment in regulated or high-stakes contexts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Notion AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Knowledge management, document collaboration, content creation, summarization, and workspace automation for distributed teams.\\n- **Target Industry:** General enterprise (small teams to large organizations); no industry-specific hardening documented.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (vendor-managed); on-premises deployment not mentioned.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Small teams to large organizations; typical deployment size not specified.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product; no formal AI safety testing conducted.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (revenue metrics not disclosed); corroborated ROI evidence from 14 sales activity data points.\\n- **Product Description:** Notion AI is a SaaS-based workspace platform integrating document management, project tracking, and AI-assisted content creation in a single interface. The product leverages third-party AI models (training data unknown) to reduce manual content generation by up to 50% and consolidates functionality of Google Docs, Trello, Dropbox Paper, Guru, and Confluence. Security posture includes SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, and HIPAA BAA certifications; however, AI governance and bias testing are not formally documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Notion Labs, Inc. (inferred from notion.com)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS platform)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2013\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (Growth stage); annual revenue not disclosed.\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not listed.\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; assumed global SaaS availability.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Third-party AI models (specific model names and architectures not disclosed).\\n- **Model Purpose:** Content generation, summarization, document assistance, and workspace automation.\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not specified.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no mention of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability mechanisms documented.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data provenance unknown and not documented.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits, third-party evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing documented; frequency and scope not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical guardrails specified.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; frequency and external evaluation mechanisms not mentioned.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities documented.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, release documentation, or impact assessments provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually. Maturity level: documented and tested (meets baseline enterprise standard).\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments or model updates.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Documents, projects, wikis, collaborative content, and user-submitted workspace data.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified; workspace owners control customer data and user data deletion rights. No statement on whether customer data is used for training third-party models.\\n- **Data Collection:** API and workspace interface; retention options controlled by workspace owner.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards not detailed beyond ISO 27001 compliance.\\n- **Data Retention:** Workspace owner controls retention; customers may request deletion upon subscription termination or user departure. No default zero-retention option documented.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no explicit US, EU, or customer-choice residency options mentioned.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (workspace owner or customer-initiated); automated deletion timelines not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - ISO 27001 ✓\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy) ✓\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security) ✓\\n  - ISO 27018 (PII in Cloud) ✓\\n  - HIPAA BAA ✓\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not documented.\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Not explicitly addressed.\\n  - GDPR: Implied by ISO 27701 compliance; no DPA explicitly mentioned.\\n  - CCPA: Not explicitly addressed.\\n  - EU AI Act Readiness: Not addressed.\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; indicates healthcare data handling capability.\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Implied by ISO 27701 certification; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed.\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed.\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO certifications imply regular audits, but frequency and last audit date not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowed); meets enterprise baseline.\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tier response times not documented.\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication sub-processors not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not documented.\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure or payment vendors not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope not specified.\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and log retention not detailed.\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal AI safety testing conducted; policy documentation gaps noted (AI governance, bias testing, human oversight).\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Formula Application (Vector Database Guidance)\\n\\nPer the **Vendor Self-Attestation Assessment Type 1** formula:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 75 (third-party models with unknown training data, no formal bias testing, no documented safety framework)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.50 (SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO certifications provide baseline security; no AI-specific controls)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.70 (basic audit logs and telemetry available; no formal AI testing)\\n- **Product Risk = 75 × 0.50 × 0.70 = 26.25 ≈ 26**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 50 points (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA = strong security baseline; no AI ethics certifications)\\n- Assessment Quality: 10 points (basic audit logs; no third-party AI governance audit)\\n- Policies: 15 points (data retention policy documented; AI ethics policy absent; incident response tested annually)\\n- Operational Controls: 20 points (rollback automated; no human oversight or monitoring controls documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10 points (11-year-old company, 1,001–5,000 employees, growth stage)\\n- Governance Score: 50 + 10 + 15 + 20 + 10 = 105 → capped at 100\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0** (strong compliance posture offsets governance gaps)\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime = enterprise-grade)\\n- Incident Management: 20 points (tested annually; automation level not specified)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 25 points (cloud SaaS, multi-tenant; enterprise-ready)\\n- Stability: 15 points (11-year-old company, profitable implied by growth stage)\\n- Support: 10 points (support SLAs not specified; basic support assumed)\\n- Operational Score: 33 + 20 + 25 + 15 + 10 = 103 → capped at 100\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 100 = 0** (mature operations)\\n\\n**Final Vendor Trust Score:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(26 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [10.4 + 0 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 10.4\\n    = 89.6 ≈ 90\\n```\\n\\n**Adjustment for AI Governance Gaps:**\\nThe formula-derived score of 90 reflects strong compliance and operations but underweights documented AI governance deficiencies (no ethics policy, no bias testing, no human oversight specification, unknown training data). Per the rubric's **Residual Concerns** guidance, missing post-deployment monitoring and human oversight categories warrant a downward adjustment.\\n\\n**Adjusted Trust Score: 72** (Acceptable Vendor, C-grade)\\n\\nThis reflects:\\n- Strong compliance and operations (+90 baseline)\\n- Significant AI governance gaps (-18 adjustment for missing ethics policy, bias testing, training data transparency, human oversight)\\n- Acceptable for general enterprise use; requires enhanced AI governance before regulated/high-stakes deployment\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** CONDITIONAL APPROVAL\\n\\n**Suitable For:**\\n- General knowledge management and document collaboration (non-critical use cases)\\n- Teams without strict AI governance or bias audit requirements\\n- Organizations with internal AI governance oversight capability\\n\\n**Not Suitable For (Without Remediation):**\\n- Healthcare PHI processing (despite HIPAA BAA; AI governance gaps create residual risk)\\n- Financial services or high-stakes decision support\\n- Regulated industries requiring formal AI bias audits and ethics governance\\n\\n**Required Conditions for Deployment:**\\n1. **AI Governance Documentation:** Vendor must provide or commit to developing:\\n   - Formal AI ethics policy and usage guidelines\\n   - Bias detection and monitoring framework\\n   - Training data provenance and documentation for third-party models\\n   - Human oversight and intervention workflows\\n\\n2. **Bias Audit:** Independent third-party bias audit of AI capabilities before production deployment in regulated contexts.\\n\\n3. **Data Processing Agreement (DPA):** Explicit GDPR DPA and confirmation of EU data residency options.\\n\\n4. **Support SLA Clarification:** Define P1/P2/P3 response times and escalation procedures.\\n\\n**Timeline:** 3–6 months for governance remediation before regulated deployment.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Notion AI", "Customer Base": "Not specified (revenue metrics not disclosed); corroborated ROI evidence from 14 sales activity data points.", "Target Industry": "General enterprise (small teams to large organizations); no industry-specific hardening documented.", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Small teams to large organizations; typical deployment size not specified.", "Primary Use Case": "Knowledge management, document collaboration, content creation, summarization, and workspace automation for distributed teams.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (vendor-managed); on-premises deployment not mentioned.", "Product Description": "Notion AI is a SaaS-based workspace platform integrating document management, project tracking, and AI-assisted content creation in a single interface. The product leverages third-party AI models (training data unknown) to reduce manual content generation by up to 50% and consolidates functionality of Google Docs, Trello, Dropbox Paper, Guru, and Confluence. Security posture includes SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, and HIPAA BAA certifications; however, AI governance and bias testing are not formally documented.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product; no formal AI safety testing conducted."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Notion Labs, Inc. (inferred from notion.com)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (SaaS platform)", "Year Founded": "2013", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; assumed global SaaS availability.", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not listed.", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (Growth stage); annual revenue not disclosed."}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Third-party AI models (specific model names and architectures not disclosed).", "Model Purpose": "Content generation, summarization, document assistance, and workspace automation.", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no mention of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows.", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not specified.", "Update Frequency": "Not specified.", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability mechanisms documented."}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No formal bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits, third-party evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned.", "Penetration Testing": "No adversarial security testing documented; frequency and scope not specified.", "Training Data Documentation": "Using third-party models; training data provenance unknown and not documented."}, "title": "AI Governance",