mplete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
7268818f-47de-4012-ae23-70bcaa403d56	98	98	363e6a8b-3da7-481d-a9ca-1e4270a191a0	89	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## OpenAI – ChatGPT Business\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 78 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 85\\n- Compliance: 88\\n- Data Practices: 82\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 80\\n- Company Maturity: 90\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nOpenAI's ChatGPT Business demonstrates strong compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, GDPR/CCPA) and mature company operations (established 2015, 5,001–10,000 employees, Series D+ profitable). Security controls are comprehensive (AES-256 encryption at rest, TLS 1.2+ in transit, no training on customer data). However, the Trust Score is moderated by gaps in AI governance transparency: the vendor provides only partial training data documentation, does not specify bias testing methodology, adversarial security testing approach, or human oversight mechanisms. The 99.9% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability support operational reliability, but missing detail on support response SLAs by severity and change management cadence introduces moderate operational risk. Applied formula: **VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]** with Product_Risk ≈ 22 (strong mitigations offset by governance documentation gaps), Governance_Risk ≈ 12 (excellent certifications, incomplete policies), Operational_Risk ≈ 20 (strong SLA and rollback, incomplete support detail) → VTS ≈ 78.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** ChatGPT Business\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise secure collaboration, research acceleration, compliance-enabled AI assistance for teams\\n- **Target Industry:** Technology, Telecom, Banking/Finance, Professional Services\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (OpenAI infrastructure); customer choice of data residency region\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Team/enterprise (unlimited high-speed access, longer context windows)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; established product with documented incident response and automated rollback\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Includes Asana, BBVA, and other enterprise customers across Tech, Telecom, Banking, and Professional Services sectors; reported ROI 83–88%\\n- **Product Description:** ChatGPT Business is an enterprise-grade AI collaboration platform built on GPT models, offering secure team access with no training on customer data, AES-256 encryption at rest, TLS 1.2+ in transit, and compliance with SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, GDPR, and CCPA. It reduces manual research time by up to 1 hour per person per day and provides customizable data retention controls for regulatory compliance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** OpenAI (legal entity not specified; assume OpenAI, Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (AI research organization)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 5,001–10,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable (3+ years)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; key investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (data residency options available by customer choice)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Models (LLM); GPT-4 and related proprietary models\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding, generation, research assistance, collaborative problem-solving, content creation\\n- **Model Governance:** Proprietary/closed model; staged deployment not explicitly documented; no public safety framework specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented advisory vs. autonomous decision framework or monitoring/alert mechanisms provided\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; prompt-level control available; citations and explainability level not specified\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data provenance and composition not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no red team results, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified; documented AI governance policy not provided in attestation\\n- **Bias Audits:** Frequency and external evaluation methodology not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms provided\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; formal incident response procedures in place\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated instant rollback; production-ready deployment safety mechanism\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Text input/output (chat, prompts, responses); documents and research materials\\n- **PII Handling:** No training on customer data; PII handling specifics (extent of processing, masking, tokenization) not detailed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface; comprehensive analytics and interaction data available\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure (OpenAI); encryption at rest (AES-256) and in transit (TLS 1.2+)\\n- **Data Retention:** Customizable retention controls; ChatGPT Enterprise users have control over retention duration; HIPAA audit logs retained 6 years; SOC 2 auditors require minimum 12 months; consumer accounts follow separate retention policies\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (data residency options available)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied by customizable retention controls); automated deletion upon retention policy expiration\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure (OpenAI cloud), payments (not specified), authentication (not specified)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, SOC 3, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, ISO 42001 (AI Management), FedRAMP, PCI DSS, GDPR Compliant, CCPA Compliant, CSA STAR Level 1\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST (not explicitly stated), GDPR (compliant), CCPA (compliant), EU AI Act (readiness not specified)\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not explicitly stated; BAA eligibility not confirmed (note: HIPAA audit log retention requirement mentioned, suggesting potential BAA availability; recommend clarification)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR Compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; vendor engagement or preparation status unknown\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, and change notification procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure (OpenAI cloud platform); payments and authentication sub-processors not specified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; interaction data collection and export scope not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, audit logs available; export capability and format not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full policy library and testing results not provided in attestation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available; scope and NDA terms not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Classification:** **ACCEPTABLE VENDOR (Grade C, 70–79 range; Trust Score 78)**\\n\\n**Recommendation:** **STANDARD PROCUREMENT WITH ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE**\\n\\n### Strengths\\n- **Exceptional Compliance:** Comprehensive certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, GDPR, CCPA, ISO 42001 AI Management) demonstrate mature compliance infrastructure.\\n- **Strong Security Controls:** AES-256 encryption at rest, TLS 1.2+ in transit, no training on customer data, automated rollback, and documented incident response.\\n- **Established Company:** 2015 founding, 5,001–10,000 employees, Series D+ profitable status indicate operational maturity and financial stability.\\n- **Proven ROI:** Documented customer success (Asana, BBVA) with 83–88% ROI across multiple sectors.\\n- **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA and automated instant rollback support production readiness.\\n- **Data Residency Flexibility:** Customer choice of region supports regulatory requirements.\\n\\n### Gaps & Risks\\n- **AI Governance Transparency (Primary Gap):** Documented AI governance policy, bias testing methodology, adversarial security testing approach, and human oversight mechanisms not specified. Partial training data documentation limits transparency into model safety and fairness.\\n- **Support SLA Gaps:** Severity-based response targets (P1/P2/P3) not documented; support maturity unclear.\\n- **Change Management Opacity:** Release cadence, change notification procedures, and rollback readiness practices not specified.\\n- **HIPAA/BAA Clarity:** HIPAA compliance mentioned (audit log retention) but BAA eligibility not explicitly confirmed.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Vendor engagement or preparation status for EU AI Act compliance not documented.\\n- **Audit Detail:** Audit frequency, last audit date, and findings not disclosed.\\n\\n### Required Actions Before Procurement\\n1. **Obtain AI Governance Documentation:** Request formal AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology (including red team results or third-party audits), adversarial security testing scope, and human oversight procedures.\\n2. **Clarify Support SLAs:** Confirm P1/P2/P3 response targets and escalation procedures.\\n3. **Confirm HIPAA/BAA Eligibility:** Obtain explicit confirmation of BAA availability and HIPAA compliance scope.\\n4. **Document Change Management:** Request release cadence, change notification procedures, and rollback testing frequency.\\n5. **Assess EU AI Act Readiness:** Confirm vendor's engagement with EU AI Act compliance roadmap.\\n6. **Request Recent Audit Report:** Obtain summary of most recent SOC 2 Type 2 or ISO 27001 audit (within 12 months).\\n\\n### Conditional Approval Path\\n- **Proceed with vendor** for non-regulated use cases (e.g., general enterprise productivity, research acceleration).\\n- **Proceed with caution** for regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government) pending clarification of HIPAA/BAA, audit findings, and AI governance documentation.\\n- **Require contract conditions:** Mandatory delivery of AI governance documentation, support SLA confirmation, and audit report summary before go-live.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Applied:** Vendor Trust Score (VTS) = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "ChatGPT Business", "Customer Base": "Includes Asana, BBVA, and other enterprise customers across Tech, Telecom, Banking, and Professional Services sectors; reported ROI 83–88%", "Target Industry": "Technology, Telecom, Banking/Finance, Professional Services", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Team/enterprise (unlimited high-speed access, longer context windows)", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise secure collaboration, research acceleration, compliance-enabled AI assistance for teams", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (OpenAI infrastructure); customer choice of data residency region", "Product Description": "ChatGPT Business is an enterprise-grade AI collaboration platform built on GPT models, offering secure team access with no training on customer data, AES-256 encryption at rest, TLS 1.2+ in transit, and compliance with SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, GDPR, and CCPA. It reduces manual research time by up to 1 hour per person per day and provides customizable data retention controls for regulatory compliance.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready; established product with documented incident response and automated rollback"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "5,001–10,000", "Legal Name": "OpenAI (legal entity not specified; assume OpenAI, Inc.)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (AI research organization)", "Year Founded": "2015", "Operating Regions": "Global (data residency options available by customer choice)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; key investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable (3+ years)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Type