  (weight 40%)\n\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (31.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\n  2. Governance risk (16.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
67a334b1-b1b8-4193-a8f3-58cf86e7e6de	98	98	31e9f643-dca5-44cb-8f65-c4443443cb67	89	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## OpenAI – ChatGPT Enterprise\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 82 (Trusted Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 88\\n- Compliance: 90\\n- Data Practices: 85\\n- AI Governance: 68\\n- Operations: 88\\n- Company Maturity: 92\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nOpenAI demonstrates strong enterprise readiness through comprehensive security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, GDPR/CCPA compliance) and mature operational infrastructure (99.9% uptime SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback). The vendor's established market position (founded 2015, 5,001–10,000 employees, profitable 3+ years) and proven customer ROI (93% monthly active usage, 25–40% productivity gains) support a \\"Trusted Vendor\\" classification. Primary gaps are limited AI governance transparency (no documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, or adversarial security testing details provided) and moderate model explainability, which create residual product risk in regulated environments. The vendor's data residency flexibility and zero-retention options address compliance friction, but governance maturity lags operational excellence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** ChatGPT Enterprise\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Secure, compliant AI adoption for enterprises; productivity acceleration (customer success, consulting, knowledge work); workflow automation; custom GPT creation\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-sector); healthcare, financial services, and government sectors supported via compliance options\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (regional data residency options)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted with customer choice of data residency region\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-wide (unlimited high-speed model access per workspace)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (market-proven, high adoption)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** 93% monthly active usage among enterprise customers; corroborated by 6 evidence points including productivity metrics and cost impact analysis\\n- **Product Description:** ChatGPT Enterprise provides unlimited access to the latest GPT models with SOC 2 Type 2 compliance, data encryption, and regional data residency options to meet global compliance requirements. Advanced admin controls enable governance at scale, while custom GPT creation capabilities support tailored AI solutions. The product delivers measurable ROI: customer success teams save 30–40% time on routine tasks, and consultants complete work 25.1% faster with 40% higher quality output.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** OpenAI (legal entity not specified; operating as OpenAI)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (AI research and deployment)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 5,001–10,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Profitable 3+ years (Series D+ or later)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; major investors include Microsoft (strategic partnership); specific investor list not provided\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (US, EU, and other regions supported via data residency options)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Models (LLM); latest GPT models (specific version not specified)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding, generation, reasoning, code analysis, content creation, workflow automation\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; governance framework not documented in attestation\\n- **Human Oversight:** Admin controls available for workspace governance; specific monitoring, alerting, and audit log capabilities confirmed as available\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features available); prompt-level control and citations not explicitly detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified; latest GPT models available to enterprise customers\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available (full transparency not provided)\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no third-party bias audit frequency or methodology disclosed\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified; documented AI governance policy not provided in attestation\\n- **Bias Audits:** Frequency and external evaluation methodology not disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Admin controls available for content filtering and workspace governance; specific intervention workflows and escalation procedures not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation not mentioned; governance maturity level not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually (mature incident response capability)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (enterprise-grade deployment safety)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Conversations, documents, code, and other text-based inputs (specific data types not exhaustively listed)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified whether customer data is used for model training; PII handling procedures not detailed\\n- **Data Collection:** Chat interface and API; workspace administrators control data collection and retention settings\\n- **Data Storage:** Encrypted (encryption standard not specified); regional data residency options available per customer choice\\n- **Data Retention:** Default: deleted conversations removed within 30 days; zero-retention (ZDR) policy available for eligible endpoints on API platform; workspace administrators control retention configuration\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (US, EU, and other regions supported)\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion within 30 days of conversation removal; on-request deletion supported\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers (AWS/Azure/GCP) not explicitly named; payment and authentication processors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - SOC 3 ✓\\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management) ✓\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security) ✓\\n  - ISO 27018 (PII Protection in Cloud) ✓\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management) ✓\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management) ✓\\n  - FedRAMP ✓\\n  - PCI DSS ✓\\n  - GDPR Compliant ✓\\n  - CCPA Compliant ✓\\n  - CSA STAR Level 1 ✓\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Third-party audit (SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO certifications indicate annual or bi-annual independent audits); specific audit frequency and last audit date not provided\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Not explicitly stated; FedRAMP certification implies NIST alignment\\n  - GDPR: Compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly confirmed\\n  - CCPA: Compliant\\n  - EU AI Act Readiness: Not specified; engagement or preparation level not documented\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not explicitly stated; BAA eligibility not confirmed (healthcare use case supported but HIPAA BAA not mentioned)\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes, GDPR compliant; DPA availability not explicitly confirmed\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year maximum downtime)\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tier response times not documented\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication sub-processors not disclosed\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key vendor SLAs not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available (93% monthly active usage, productivity metrics, cost impact data corroborated by 6 evidence points)\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, audit logs available (export capability and format not specified)\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Partial documentation available; specific policy documents and testing reports not listed\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available (scope and NDA terms not specified)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (VTS Formula)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from the vector database:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Inherent Risk: 65 (LLM with moderate explainability, partial training data documentation, no disclosed bias testing or adversarial security testing)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.70 (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, data residency options, admin controls, but limited AI governance transparency)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.90 (comprehensive certifications, proven market adoption, 93% active usage)\\n- **Product Risk = 65 × (1 − 0.70) × 0.90 = 17.55 ≈ 18**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n- Certifications: 50 points (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017/27018/27701, ISO 42001, FedRAMP, PCI DSS, GDPR/CCPA)\\n- Assessment Quality: 20 points (third-party audit implied by SOC 2 Type 2; audit frequency not specified)\\n- Policies: 30 points (data retention policy documented, incident response plan tested annually; AI ethics policy not documented)\\n- Operational Controls: 35 points (rollback automated, audit logs available, admin controls; human oversight details limited)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 15 points (established company, 5,001–10,000 employees, profitable 3+ years)\\n- **Governance Score = MIN(100, 50 + 20 + 30 + 35 + 15) = 100 (capped)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 0**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year downtime)\\n- Incident Management: 30 points (tested annually)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 30 points (enterprise SaaS, multi-region, proven scale)\\n- Stability: 22 points (established company, 8+ years, profitable)\\n- Support: 20 points (support SLAs not specified; assume standard enterprise support)\\n- **Operational Score = MIN(100, 33 + 30 + 30 + 22 + 20) = 100 (capped)**\\n- **Operational Risk = 0**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(18 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [7.2 + 0 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 7.2\\n    = 92.8 ≈ 93\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted Trust Score: 82** (conservative adjustment for AI governance gaps)\\n\\nThe calculated VTS of 93 is adjusted downward to **82** to reflect:\\n1. **Missing AI Governance Documentation:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, or adversarial security testing details\\n2. **Partial Training Data Transparency:** Training data documentation is partial, not comprehensive\\n3. **Limited Model Explainability:** Moderate explainability features; prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed\\n4. **Unspecified Support SLAs:** Enterprise support assumed but not contractually detailed\\n\\nThis adjustment places the vendor in the **\\"Trusted Vendor\\" (B grade, 80–89 range)** classification, reflecting strong operational and compliance maturity offset by governance transparency gaps typical of large LLM providers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT (with conditions)\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n- ✓ Market-leading AI capabilities with proven enterprise adoption (93% active usage)\\n- ✓ Comprehensive security and compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, GDPR/CCPA)\\n- ✓ Strong operational reliability (99.9% uptime SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback)\\n- ✓ Flexible data residency and zero-retention options address compliance requirements\\n- ✓ Established company maturity (founded 2015, 5,001–10,000 employees, profitable 3+ years)\\n\\n**Conditions for Deployment:**\\n1. **AI Governance Documentation:** Require vendor to provide documented AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, and adversarial security testing frequency before contract execution\\n2. **Training Data Transparency:** Request comprehensive training data documentation and cutoff date for model training\\n3. **Support SLAs:** Negotiate and document P1/P2/P3 response time SLAs aligned with enterprise requirements\\n4. **HIPAA/BAA Confirmation:** If healthcare use case applies, confirm HIPAA BAA eligibility and execute BAA prior to PHI processing\\n5. **DPA Execution:** Execute GDPR Data Processing Agreement before EU data processing begins\\n6. **Audit Access:** Require contractual right to audit logs and SIEM export for compliance monitoring\\n\\n**Risk Mitigation:**\\n- Implement admin controls and content filtering policies at workspace level\\n- Establish governance board for ChatGPT Enterprise usage policies\\n- Monitor model outputs and user interactions via available telemetry and audit logs\\n- Schedule quarterly compliance reviews aligned with SOC 2 Type 2 audit cycle\\n\\n**Timeline:** Standard procurement (4–6 weeks) with governance documentation review\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SUMMARY ASSESSMENT\\n\\nOpenAI's ChatGPT Enterprise represents a **mature, market-proven AI product** with exceptional operational and compliance credentials. The vendor's comprehensive certification portfolio (12+ certifications including SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, GDPR/CCPA) and proven customer ROI (25–40% productivity gains, 93% active usage) position it as a trusted enterprise AI platform. \\n\\n**Key Strengths:**\\n- Enterprise-grade security and compliance infrastructure\\n- Flexible data residency and zero-retention options\\n- Proven operational reliability and incident response maturity\\n- Strong company stability and market leadership\\n\\n**Key Gaps:**\\n- Limited AI governance transparency (no documented ethics policy or bias testing methodology)\\n- Partial training data documentation\\n- Moderate model explainability (not full transparency)\\n- Unspecified support SLAs and vendor sub-processor details\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Proceed with standard procurement contingent on vendor providing AI governance documentation, training data transparency, and negotiated support SLAs. Suitable for enterprise deployment across regulated industries with appropriate contractual safeguards (BAA, DPA, audit rights).", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "ChatGPT Enterprise", "Customer Base": "93% monthly active usage among enterprise customers; corroborated by 6 evidence points including productivity metrics and cost impact analysis", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-sector); healthcare, financial services, and government sectors supported via compliance options", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (regional data residency options)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise-wide (unlimited high-speed model access per workspace)", "Primary Use Case": "Secure, compliant AI adoption for enterprises; productivity acceleration (customer success, consulting, knowledge work); workflow automation; custom GPT creation", "