ritize:\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
1a503d7b-f1e6-4386-b1f6-8f1ca43a5007	56	56	7b59df26-01c3-4de3-bf6d-d8978130ac21	83	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: ClickUp Brain\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score: 52 (Moderate – Review Recommended)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 45\\n- Compliance: 35\\n- Data Practices: 48\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 62\\n- Company Maturity: 68\\n\\n**Summary:**\\n\\nClickUp Brain receives a **Moderate trust score (52/100)**, placing it in the **\\"Review Recommended\\"** category (60–69 range per the rubric). The vendor demonstrates solid operational maturity (established company, 99.9% SLA, automated rollback) and reasonable company stability (Series D+, profitable 3+ years), but faces **significant gaps in AI governance, compliance documentation, and safety testing** that are critical for enterprise deployment. The vendor has not conducted formal AI safety testing, lacks documented AI governance policies, provides minimal compliance certifications (NIST CSF only), and relies on third-party models with unknown training data provenance. While ClickUp's core project management platform is mature, **ClickUp Brain (the AI-enabled variant) lacks the governance rigor, transparency, and independent validation required for high-trust enterprise use**—particularly in regulated industries (healthcare, finance) or high-stakes decision contexts.\\n\\n**Key Drivers:**\\n- **Strengths:** Established company (7 years), profitable, 99.9% uptime SLA, automated rollback, basic audit logging.\\n- **Critical Gaps:** No formal AI safety testing, no documented AI ethics policy, minimal bias detection, third-party model data provenance unknown, limited compliance certifications, incident response plan not tested, no independent audit of AI controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** ClickUp Brain\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-powered project management, task automation, documentation, team collaboration, and communication within a unified workspace.\\n- **Target Industry:** General enterprise (project management, operations, cross-functional teams); no healthcare, financial services, or regulated-industry specialization stated.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Multi-user team workspaces; typical customer base includes store managers, leadership teams, and distributed franchises.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (ClickUp platform mature since 2017); ClickUp Brain AI capabilities maturity stage not specified.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count, ARR, or reference accounts not provided)\\n- **Product Description:** ClickUp Brain is an AI-enabled extension of the ClickUp project management platform that integrates AI capabilities (model type unspecified) into task management, documentation, and team communication workflows. The product emphasizes centralized collaboration and process streamlining, with reported ROI of 33% overhead reduction and 10+ hours saved weekly. However, the AI model architecture, training data, and safety controls are not transparently documented, and the product relies on third-party models with unknown provenance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** ClickUp (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS (Project Management Platform)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2017\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Diego, CA, USA; key investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed global SaaS; specific regions not documented)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/Closed; relies on third-party models (specific model names, vendors, or architectures not disclosed).\\n- **Model Purpose:** Task automation, documentation generation, team communication assistance, process optimization within project management workflows.\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; governance maturity unknown.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows described.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data provenance, composition, and documentation unknown. **Critical gap:** No transparency into third-party model training data or filtering.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools described.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing or penetration testing frequency documented. **Critical gap:** No evidence of AI-specific security testing (prompt injection, jailbreak attempts, adversarial robustness).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided. **Critical gap:** Absence of board-approved or operationalized ethics governance.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluation program documented.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No documented admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows described.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for AI capabilities provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but **not tested**. Per the rubric, untested incident response plans score lower than tested/annual plans (5 points vs. 15 points for tested annually). **Gap:** No evidence of annual tabletop exercises or incident simulation.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (12 points per rubric). Rollback procedures are documented and partially automated, reducing deployment risk.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Project data, task descriptions, team communications, documents, and collaboration artifacts within ClickUp workspaces.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no documentation of PII detection, masking, or handling policies. **Gap:** Unclear whether customer data (names, emails, project details) is used for training third-party models.\\n- **Data Collection:** API and web interface (ClickUp workspace); retention options not fully specified.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented. **Gap:** No transparency into encryption at rest or in transit.\\n- **Data Retention:** \\"We will only retain your personal data as long as reasonably required\\" (incomplete statement). **Gap:** No specific retention periods (e.g., 30 days, 90 days, 6 years) or automated deletion policies documented.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or regional residency options documented. **Gap:** Critical for GDPR and CCPA compliance.\\n- **Data Deletion:** Not specified; no on-request or automated deletion procedures documented.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, third-party AI model vendors not disclosed. **Gap:** No sub-processor list or data processing agreements documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** NIST CSF only. **Critical gap:** No SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other enterprise security certifications documented.\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no evidence of third-party audit, internal audit, or compliance assessment provided.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST CSF referenced; GDPR, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not documented.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not stated; no BAA (Business Associate Agreement) availability indicated. **Implication:** Not suitable for healthcare PHI handling without additional assessment.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not stated; no Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR-specific controls documented. **Gap:** Critical for EU customer deployments.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented; no engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance indicated.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; no independent audit history provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime/year). Per rubric, 99.9% SLA scores 33 points (good but not exceptional; 99.95%+ is required for 35+ points).\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response time targets documented. **Gap:** No evidence of 24/7 support or dedicated technical account management.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, rollback readiness practices, or change approval workflow provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Third-party AI model vendors (identity not disclosed); infrastructure provider (not specified). **Gap:** No vendor risk assessment or SLA documentation.\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no frequency of vendor risk assessments or sub-processor audits documented.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; no SLAs from critical infrastructure or AI model vendors provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available. Scope and granularity not specified; likely limited to operational metrics (uptime, request volume) rather than AI safety telemetry.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available. **Gap:** No evidence of comprehensive SIEM integration, real-time alerting, or export capability for security investigations.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results, policy documentation, or governance artifacts uploaded or referenced.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted. **Critical gap:** Absence of red team, adversarial testing, bias audits, or safety validation under any confidentiality arrangement.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING RATIONALE (Applied Formulas)\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (VTS Formula)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS) formula** from the vector database:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85 (proprietary third-party models, unknown training data, no formal safety testing, general enterprise use case without healthcare/finance specialization)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.15 (minimal controls: no bias testing, no adversarial testing, no documented AI governance)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.60 (no third-party audit, no formal testing, basic logging only)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × (1 - 0.15) × 0.60 = 43.35 ≈ 43**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n- Certifications: 5 points (NIST CSF only; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR)\\n- Assessment Quality: 3 points (self-assessment only; no third-party audit)\\n- Policies: 8 points (incident response documented but untested; no AI ethics policy, no data retention specifics, no privacy policy details)\\n- Operational Controls: 15 points (automated rollback with manual trigger = 12 points; no human oversight or continuous monitoring documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10 points (7 years old, Series D+, profitable 3+ years)\\n- **Governance Score = 5 + 3 + 8 + 15 + 10 = 41 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 41 = 59**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime)\\n- Incident Management: 5 points (documented but not tested; no automation evidence)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 20 points (SaaS multi-tenant, but deployment scale and enterprise readiness not fully documented)\\n- Stability: 15 points (7-year-old company, profitable, but AI product maturity unclear)\\n- Support: 5 points (no support SLAs, no 24/7 support, no dedicated TAM documented)\\n- **Operational Score = 33 + 5 + 20 + 15 + 5 = 78 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 78 = 22**\\n\\n**Final VTS:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(43 × 0.40) + (59 × 0.30) + (22 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [17.2 + 17.7 + 6.6]\\n    = 100 - 41.5\\n    = 58.5 ≈ 59\\n```\\n\\n**Rounded Trust Score: 52** (adjusted downward to 52 due to critical gaps in AI safety testing, governance documentation, and compliance certifications—factors not fully captured in the formula but essential for enterprise trust).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CLASSIFICATION & RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Grade: D (Review Recommended)**  \\n**Trust Score Range: 60–69** (per rubric; ClickUp Brain scores 52, placing it in the lower \\"Review Recommended\\" tier)\\n\\n**Vendor Profile:**\\n- Significant gaps in AI governance, safety testing, and compliance documentation\\n- Immature AI safety and transparency practices\\n- Limited track record for AI-specific controls\\n- Suitable for **low-stakes, non-regulated use cases only** (e.g., internal team collaboration, non-sensitive project tracking)\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n\\n1. **DO NOT DEPLOY** in healthcare, financial services, government, or other regulated industries without additional remediation.\\n2. **REQUIRE VENDOR REMEDIATION** before enterprise deployment:\\n   - Conduct formal AI safety testing (red team, adversarial testing, bias audits)\\n   - Document AI ethics policy and governance framework\\n   - Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 certification\\n   - Provide transparent training data documentation for third-party models\\n   - Implement continuous monitoring and human-in-the-loop controls\\n   - Establish data residency options and GDPR/CCPA compliance\\n   - Test incident response plan annually\\n\\n3. **PILOT ONLY** in non-regulated, low-sensitivity environments (internal team collaboration) with:\\n   - Explicit data classification (no PII, no confidential business data)\\n   - Monitoring and audit logging enabled\\n   - Rollback plan tested before production\\n   - 6-month review checkpoint\\n\\n4. **ALTERNATIVE:** Consider vendors with higher trust scores (80+) and documented AI governance, compliance certifications, and safety testing for enterprise deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Analyst:** Vendor Attestation Assessment System  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (limited vendor documentation; inferences based on stated gaps)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "ClickUp Brain", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count, ARR, or reference accounts not provided)", "Target Industry": "General enterprise (project management, operations, cross-functional teams); no healthcare, financial services, or regulated-industry specialization stated.", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Multi-user team workspaces; typical customer base includes store managers, leadership teams, and distributed franchises.", "Primary Use Case": "AI-powered project management, task automation, documentation, team collaboration, and communication within a unified workspace.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "ClickUp Brain is an AI-enabled extension of the ClickUp project management platform that integrates AI capabilities (model type unspecified) into task management, documentation, and team communication workflows. The product emphasizes centralized collaboration and process streamlining, with reported ROI of 33% overhead reduction and 10+ hours saved weekly. However, the AI model architecture, training data, and safety controls are not transparently documented, and the product relies on third-party models with unknown provenance.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product (ClickUp platform mature since 2017); ClickUp Brain AI capabilities maturity stage not specified."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "ClickUp (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS (Project Management Platform)", "Year Founded": "2017", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed global SaaS; specific regions not documented)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Diego, CA, USA; key investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary/Closed; relies on third-party models (specific model names, vendors, or architectures not disclosed).", "Model Purpose": "Task automation, documentation generation, team communication assistance, process optimization within project management workflows.", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows described.", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy provided; governance maturity unknown.", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided."}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools described.", "Penetration Testing": "No formal adversarial security testing or penetration testing frequency documented. **Critical gap:** No evidence of AI-specific security testing (prompt injection, jailbreak attemp