+ points).", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; no documented release process, rollback readiness practices, or change approval workflow provided.", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; no severity-based response time targets documented. **Gap:** No evidence of 24/7 support or dedicated technical account management."}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; no SLAs from critical infrastructure or AI model vendors provided.", "Critical Vendors": "Third-party AI model vendors (identity not disclosed); infrastructure provider (not specified). **Gap:** No vendor risk assessment or SLA documentation.", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; no frequency of vendor risk assessments or sub-processor audits documented."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available. **Gap:** No evidence of comprehensive SIEM integration, real-time alerting, or export capability for security investigations.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available. Scope and granularity not specified; likely limited to operational metrics (uptime, request volume) rather than AI safety telemetry.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted. **Critical gap:** Absence of red team, adversarial testing, bias audits, or safety validation under any confidentiality arrangement.", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "No formal testing results, policy documentation, or governance artifacts uploaded or referenced."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** ClickUp Brain receives a **Moderate trust score (52/100)**, placing it in the **\\"Review Recommended\\"** category (60–69 range per the rubric). The vendor demonstrates solid operational maturity (established company, 99.9% S