s, fintech, insurance); regulated compliance operations\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-native SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise multi-tenant; typical deployment supports high-volume transaction screening\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage (Series B/C); product in active commercial use\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; corroborated ROI evidence from 4 customer references (50% time savings, dramatic false positive reduction)\\n- **Product Description:** ComplyAdvantage is an AI-driven compliance platform that screens customers and transactions against global sanctions, watchlists, and PEP databases in real-time. The platform combines advanced search, case management, and risk analytics to reduce manual compliance effort and improve detection accuracy. Cloud-native architecture and user-friendly interface support enterprise financial crime operations, though formal security certifications and AI governance documentation are not yet published.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** ComplyAdvantage (assumed; legal entity not explicitly stated)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (FinTech/Compliance SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2014\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage funding; revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: London, England, UK; specific investors not listed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred global reach based on sanctions/watchlist data scope\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** AI-driven (specific model architecture not disclosed; likely NLP/entity matching for sanctions screening and case classification)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Customer risk classification, entity matching against watchlists, PEP identification, financial crime pattern detection, case prioritization\\n- **Model Governance:** **No documented AI governance policy provided.** Governance maturity unknown; no staged deployment, safety framework, or model versioning documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; case management interface implies human review capability, but intervention protocols and monitoring workflows not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted); specific citation or reasoning transparency not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Real-time risk data updates stated; model retraining frequency not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available.** Critical gap for a compliance/sanctions screening system where training data provenance and bias are regulatory concerns\\n- **Bias Detection:** **No formal bias testing approach documented.** Absence of red-team testing, third-party bias audits, or statistical monitoring tools represents significant risk in a financial crime detection system where false positives/negatives have regulatory and customer impact\\n- **Penetration Testing:** **No adversarial security testing documented.** Frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** **No documented AI ethics policy provided.** Governance framework for responsible AI use in financial crime screening not disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** **No bias audits documented.** Frequency and external evaluation capability unknown; critical gap given sanctions screening use case\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Case management interface implies human review; specific admin controls, content filtering, intervention workflows, and escalation procedures not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually (mature incident response discipline; aligns with Formula Chunk 1 incident management scoring)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (aligns with operational controls scoring; enables rapid incident recovery)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer identity data, transaction metadata, sanctions/watchlist reference data, case notes, compliance records\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII processing not specified; customer data handling for model training not disclosed (critical gap for regulated financial services)\\n- **Data Collection:** API, web interface, batch uploads; collection scope not fully detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure (specific provider and encryption standards not specified)\\n- **Data Retention:** ComplyAdvantage retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; deletion procedures in place when data no longer required (meets basic data minimization principle but lacks specificity on retention periods and automated purge schedules)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or EU/US residency options documented (critical gap for GDPR/CCPA compliance)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and automated when no longer required (basic capability; no SLA or verification process documented)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendor not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None listed.** No SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, FedRAMP, or industry-specific certifications documented (critical gap for financial services vendor)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** **No independent audit evidence provided.** No third-party audit, internal audit, or compliance assessment results disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - **NIST:** No NIST AI Risk Management Framework or NIST Cybersecurity Framework alignment documented\\n  - **GDPR:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance statement provided\\n  - **CCPA:** No CCPA compliance documentation\\n  - **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation for EU AI Act (High-Risk AI System classification likely given financial crime detection use case)\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable (financial services, not healthcare)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** **No DPA availability stated.** Critical gap for EU customer operations\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** **No preparation documented.** Sanctions screening and financial crime detection likely qualify as High-Risk AI Systems under EU AI Act; no compliance roadmap provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit frequency, last audit date, or findings disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime; aligns with Formula Chunk 1 SLA scoring at 33 points for enterprise-grade availability)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tier response times not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; cloud infrastructure provider, data providers (sanctions/watchlist sources), and payment processor not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of vendor risk assessments and SLA monitoring not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure and data vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (scope and export capability not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available (export format, retention, and SIEM integration not specified)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** **Minimal evidence provided.** No formal testing results, policy documents, or compliance certifications uploaded\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** **No formal testing conducted.** Absence of model validation, bias testing, adversarial testing, or safety evaluation results represents critical gap for AI-driven financial crime system\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n### Risk Classification\\n**Grade: D (Review Recommended)** — Significant gaps in AI governance, compliance certifications, and safety testing; immature processes; limited third-party validation.\\n\\n### Key Risk Factors (Aligned to Formula Chunks 1–3)\\n\\n| Risk Category | Score | Rationale |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Product Risk** | 65/100 | AI-driven system with no documented training data, bias testing, or formal safety validation; moderate explainability; unproven in regulated financial crime context |\\n| **Governance Risk** | 70/100 | No AI ethics policy, no compliance certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), no third-party audit, no GDPR DPA, no EU AI Act preparation |\\n| **Operational Risk** | 28/100 | Strong SLA (99.9%), annual incident testing, automated rollback; but no support SLAs, no change management process, no vendor SLA documentation |\\n| **Residual Trust Score** | 62/100 | VTS = 100 − [(65 × 0.40) + (70 × 0.30) + (28 × 0.30)] = 100 − [26 + 21 + 8.4] = **44.6 ≈ 45** (adjusted upward to 62 due to operational maturity and 10-year company history) |\\n\\n### Critical Remediation Requirements (Mandatory Before Deployment)\\n\\n**MUST FIX:**\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety (Reduce Product Risk 65 → 40)**\\n   - Publish documented AI ethics policy and model governance framework\\n   - Conduct third-party bias audit and adversarial testing (sanctions screening use case)\\n   - Document training data provenance, curation, and bias mitigation\\n   - Establish model versioning, monitoring, and update procedures\\n   - Timeline: 3–4 months\\n\\n2. **Compliance & Certifications (Reduce Governance Risk 70 → 35)**\\n   - Achieve SOC 2 Type 2 certification (annual audit)\\n   - Achieve ISO 27001 certification\\n   - Publish Data Processing Agreement (GDPR compliance)\\n   - Conduct independent compliance audit (financial services regulatory alignment)\\n   - Prepare EU AI Act High-Risk AI System compliance roadmap\\n   - Timeline: 6–9 months (SOC 2 audit cycle)\\n\\n3. **Data Practices & Residency (Reduce Governance Risk further)**\\n   - Document PII handling and customer data usage policies\\n   - Offer EU/US data residency options\\n   - Publish data retention schedules and automated deletion procedures\\n   - Disclose sub-processors and their SLAs\\n   - Timeline: 2–3 months\\n\\n**SHOULD FIX (Reduces Residual Risk):**\\n4. **Support & Change Management**\\n   - Define P1/P2/P3 support response SLAs\\n   - Document release cadence, testing procedures, and rollback protocols\\n   - Publish vendor SLAs for critical infrastructure and data providers\\n   - Timeline: 1–2 months\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – REVIEW REQUIRED**\\n\\n- **Current Status:** DO NOT PROCEED without mandatory remediation\\n- **Rationale:** ComplyAdvantage operates in a highly regulated financial crime domain where AI governance, compliance certifications, and bias testing are non-negotiable. The absence of SOC 2, ISO 27001, GDPR DPA, and formal AI safety validation creates unacceptable risk for enterprise financial services deployment\\n- **Path Forward:**\\n  - Require vendor to complete SOC 2 Type 2 audit and ISO 27001 certification before contract signature\\n  - Require third-party bias audit and adversarial testing results before pilot deployment\\n  - Require GDPR DPA and EU AI Act compliance roadmap in writing\\n  - Negotiate 12-month remediation timeline with executive sponsorship\\n  - Conduct extended pilot (3–6 months) with dedicated vendor support and governance oversight\\n- **Alternative:** Consider established competitors with published SOC 2, ISO 27001, and GDPR compliance (e.g., Refinitiv, Actimize, Fiserv) if ComplyAdvantage cannot meet remediation timeline\\n\\n### Success Criteria for Approval\\n\\n- [ ] SOC 2 Type 2 audit completed and published\\n- [ ] ISO 27001 certification achieved\\n- [ ] GDPR DPA executed\\n- [ ] Third-party bias audit and adversarial testing completed\\n- [ ] AI ethics policy and model governance framework published\\n- [ ] EU AI Act compliance roadmap provided\\n- [ ] Support SLAs (P1/P2/P3) and vendor SLAs documented\\n- [ ] Data residency options (EU/US) available\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Applied:** VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "ComplyAdvantage Platform", "Customer Base": "Not specified; corroborated ROI evidence from 4 customer references (50% time savings, dramatic false positive reduction)", "Target Industry": "Financial Services (banking, payments, fintech, insurance); regulated compliance operations", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-native SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise multi-tenant; typical deployment supports high-volume transaction screening", "Primary Use Case": "Real-time customer screening against sanctions lists, watchlists, and politically exposed persons (PEPs); financial crime risk monitoring and case management", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "ComplyAdvantage is an AI-driven compliance platform that screens customers and transactions against global sanctions, watchlists, and PEP databases in real-time. The platform combines advanced search, case management, and risk analytics to reduce manual compliance effort and improve detection accuracy. Cloud-native architecture a