df01cd91-09da-4a24-909c-aa50d01a0098	106	106	5020a831-9a7a-45c3-90ce-94d067675b0c	87	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n**Rev – AI-Powered Transcription & Multi-File Insights Platform**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 **(Acceptable Vendor)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 80\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nRev demonstrates solid foundational compliance and operational maturity as an established company (founded 2010, Series D+, profitable 3+ years) with relevant certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, GDPR compliant) and a strong 99.9% uptime SLA. However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency—no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing, and no training data documentation—which limits confidence in the safety and explainability of its AI-powered transcription and multi-file search capabilities. Data practices are moderate; while automated deletion and 30-day retention are reasonable, US-only residency and limited transparency on PII handling reduce the score. The vendor's moderate model transparency and lack of formal testing results further constrain the overall assessment. **Primary gaps:** AI safety documentation, bias/adversarial testing, and training data provenance. **Strengths:** Established company, strong compliance posture, reliable operations, and proven ROI in legal/media/healthcare sectors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Rev (Multi-File Insights)\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Multi-file search and analysis across audio/video transcripts, PDFs, and text files; case preparation, evidence review, and theme/contradiction detection in legal, media, education, and healthcare contexts.\\n- **Target Industry:** Legal, media, education, healthcare\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; data residency US only\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (company founded 2010); no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Rev provides human transcription, captions, subtitles, and AI-powered transcription services with a Multi-File Insights feature enabling simultaneous search across audio, video, PDFs, and text files. The platform is designed to accelerate case preparation and evidence review, with documented ROI of up to 30 hours saved per case (90% time savings on caption QC, 90% critical facts found). Security posture includes SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, and GDPR compliance; however, formal AI safety testing and bias audits are not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Rev (legal entity not explicitly stated; operating as Rev)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2010\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Austin, TX, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** US (primary); data residency US only\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** AI-powered transcription (model type not specified; likely speech-to-text and NLP for multi-file search)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Speech transcription, caption generation, multi-file search, theme detection, contradiction identification\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of advisory boards, human-in-the-loop workflows, or intervention mechanisms\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); specific mechanisms (e.g., citation, confidence scores, prompt-level control) not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing documented; incident response plan exists but is not tested\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Audio files, video files, PDFs, text files, transcripts, captions, subtitles\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified; likely includes PII in transcripts and legal documents; extent of customer data use for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and web interface (Multi-File Insights platform)\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); encryption status not detailed\\n- **Data Retention:** Rev retains customer data for the period necessary to fulfill service purposes, typically up to 30 days post-service completion\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion procedures following strict compliance guidelines\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payment and authentication sub-processors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, SOC 3, HIPAA BAA, GDPR Compliant\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified (SOC 2 Type 2 implies annual third-party audit; specific audit firm and methodology not disclosed)\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA, GDPR; NIST and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available (HIPAA BAA certification confirmed)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR Compliant (DPA availability not explicitly stated)\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, rollback readiness practices, or change notification procedures\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payment and authentication sub-processors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; AI governance policy, bias testing results, and training data documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established Company & Maturity:** Founded 2010, Series D+, profitable 3+ years; demonstrates long-term viability and operational stability.\\n2. **Strong Compliance Posture:** SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, and GDPR compliance certifications indicate commitment to security and regulatory standards.\\n3. **Reliable Operations:** 99.9% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability support production-grade reliability.\\n4. **Proven ROI:** Documented case studies showing 30-hour time savings and 90% critical facts discovery rate in legal/media/healthcare use cases.\\n5. **Data Retention Discipline:** 30-day post-service retention and automated deletion align with privacy best practices.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety:** No documented AI governance policy, bias testing, adversarial security testing, or training data documentation. This is a significant risk for healthcare and legal use cases involving sensitive data.\\n2. **Model Transparency:** Moderate explainability features lack specificity; no evidence of confidence scores, citations, or prompt-level control mechanisms.\\n3. **Testing & Validation:** No formal AI safety testing conducted; incident response plan documented but not tested.\\n4. **PII Handling Clarity:** Extent of PII processing and customer data use for model training not disclosed.\\n5. **Support SLAs:** No severity-based response SLAs documented; support responsiveness unclear.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT** (with conditions)\\n\\n**Conditions:**\\n1. **Pre-Deployment:** Require vendor to provide:\\n   - Documented AI governance policy and bias testing roadmap\\n   - Training data provenance and composition summary\\n   - Formal penetration testing and incident response plan validation\\n   - Detailed PII handling and data use policies\\n\\n2. **Contract Requirements:**\\n   - Severity-based support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times)\\n   - Annual SOC 2 Type 2 audit confirmation and findings summary\\n   - Incident notification SLA (e.g., 24 hours for security incidents)\\n   - Right to audit AI model performance and bias metrics\\n\\n3. **Monitoring & Governance:**\\n   - Establish quarterly compliance reviews\\n   - Monitor audit logs for anomalies; configure SIEM export\\n   - Implement internal bias monitoring for transcription accuracy across demographic groups\\n\\n**Use Case Fit:**\\n- **Recommended:** Legal discovery, media asset management, educational content analysis (non-PHI)\\n- **Conditional:** Healthcare use cases (requires additional AI governance documentation and bias testing before deployment with PHI)\\n\\n**Risk Classification:** **Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range)** — Moderate capabilities with some governance gaps; suitable for standard procurement with enhanced due diligence and contract-level risk mitigation.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Rev (Multi-File Insights)", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Legal, media, education, healthcare", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Multi-file search and analysis across audio/video transcripts, PDFs, and text files; case preparation, evidence review, and theme/contradiction detection in legal, media, education, and healthcare contexts.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; data residency US only", "Product Description": "Rev provides human transcription, captions, subtitles, and AI-powered transcription services with a Multi-File Insights feature enabling simultaneous search across audio, video, PDFs, and text files. The platform is designed to accelerate case preparation and evidence review, with documented ROI of up to 30 hours saved per case (90% time savings on caption QC, 90% critical facts found). Security posture includes SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, and GDPR compliance; however, formal AI safety testing and bias audits are not documented.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product (company founded 2010); no formal testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Rev (legal entity not 