 - Complete Data residency in the attestation\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation	VTS	\N	\N
5bf8d37e-ef3a-4ad2-b5dd-4925a06cc7e4	62	62	1fb974c3-7b9c-4867-91aa-7ae7ce61fa46	81	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: CURSOR IDE\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate / Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 70\\n- Compliance: 65\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 40\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nCursor IDE demonstrates solid operational foundations (99.9% uptime SLA, SOC 2 Type 2 certification, tested incident response) and responsible data practices (zero retention agreements with cloud providers, privacy mode option). However, the startup maturity (founded 2022, 11–50 employees, Seed/Series A stage) and significant gaps in AI governance documentation (no documented AI governance policy, no training data documentation, no bias testing approach specified) create material risk for enterprise deployment. The moderate trust score reflects acceptable operational and security posture offset by governance immaturity and limited transparency into AI model safety practices—typical for early-stage developer tools but requiring enhanced due diligence before use in regulated or mission-critical contexts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Cursor IDE\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Accelerating software development cycles through AI-assisted code generation, intelligent code suggestions, and automated repetitive coding tasks.\\n- **Target Industry:** Software development; applicable across technology, fintech, healthcare tech, and other code-intensive sectors.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (xAI and Google Cloud Vertex API integration)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted SaaS; privacy mode available for legacy users with local code handling.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Individual developers to small/medium engineering teams; enterprise deployment scale not specified.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product (founded 2022); basic test results available.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; ROI corroborated by 3 internal evidence points (22% end-to-end time reduction, 12% end-to-end time reduction, 95,349 lines of code generated).\\n- **Product Description:** Cursor IDE is an AI-powered integrated development environment designed to maximize developer productivity through intelligent code generation and suggestions. The product integrates with xAI and Google Cloud Vertex APIs for model inference and maintains zero data retention agreements with cloud providers. A privacy mode option allows users to disable codebase indexing and avoid server-side code persistence, addressing data sensitivity concerns for regulated environments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Cursor (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2022\\n- **Employees:** 11–50\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (specific revenue and funding amounts not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters location unknown; investor details not specified.\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** LLM-based (xAI and Google Cloud Vertex API models); specific model names/versions not disclosed.\\n- **Model Purpose:** Code understanding, generation, and intelligent suggestion; translating plain-language intent into functional code; automating repetitive coding tasks.\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no documented AI governance policy provided.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Developer retains full control over code acceptance/rejection; no autonomous code deployment. Manual review of AI suggestions required before integration.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate explainability; some features present but limited transparency into model behavior, training data, or decision rationale.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available. Vendor has not disclosed training data sources, composition, or filtering practices.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach specified. No red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; frequency and scope of security testing not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented. No formal usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical framework provided.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations documented.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Developer review required before code acceptance; no automated filtering, content controls, or intervention mechanisms documented.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, release documentation, or impact assessments provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually. Vendor maintains a documented incident response plan with annual testing; specific response time targets and escalation procedures not disclosed.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option. Deployments can be rolled back automatically or via manual intervention; rollback testing frequency not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Source code, codebase context, developer queries, file paths (obfuscated).\\n- **PII Handling:** Code may contain embedded PII (credentials, API keys, personal identifiers); vendor does not explicitly filter or redact PII. Privacy mode available to prevent code persistence.\\n- **Data Collection:** API integration with xAI and Google Cloud Vertex; chat/IDE interface for user queries.\\n- **Data Storage:** Codebase indexing creates embeddings and obfuscated file paths stored on Cursor's servers (can be disabled via privacy mode). xAI and Google Cloud Vertex handle model inference and maintain zero retention agreements.\\n- **Data Retention:** **Zero data retention agreement with xAI and Google Cloud Vertex API.** For privacy mode users (legacy), code data is not persisted. Codebase indexing data can be disabled.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Hosted on Google Cloud Vertex (US-based); specific regional options not disclosed. EU data residency not confirmed.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied via privacy mode and zero retention agreements); automated deletion timelines not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** xAI (model inference), Google Cloud Vertex (hosting, inference), Google Cloud Storage (embeddings/indexing).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2 (security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy controls).\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted by independent auditor; specific audit firm and scope not disclosed.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST, GDPR, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not documented.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility unknown. Code may contain PHI; no HIPAA-specific controls documented.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability not confirmed. Zero retention with cloud providers supports GDPR data minimization; specific GDPR compliance measures not documented.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit frequency not specified. Last audit date and findings not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance). Contractual commitment confirmed.\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified. No severity-based response time targets documented.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified. Release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** xAI (model inference), Google Cloud Vertex (hosting, inference), Google Cloud Storage (data storage).\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of vendor risk assessments not documented.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** xAI and Google Cloud Vertex SLAs not disclosed; zero retention agreements in place but specific uptime/availability commitments not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available. Scope limited; detailed telemetry not specified.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, audit logs available. Export capability and retention period not specified.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation (AI governance, bias testing, incident response procedures) not provided.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; availability under NDA not confirmed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA and SOC 2 Type 2 certification demonstrate solid operational controls.\\n2. **Data Privacy Practices:** Zero retention agreements with cloud providers and privacy mode option show responsible data handling for code-sensitive use cases.\\n3. **Incident Response:** Tested annual incident response plan indicates operational maturity.\\n4. **Proven ROI:** Customer evidence (22% cycle time reduction, 95K+ lines generated) validates product value.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **AI Governance Immaturity:** No documented AI governance policy, training data documentation, or bias testing approach—significant risk for regulated industries.\\n2. **Startup Risk:** Founded 2022, 11–50 employees, Seed/Series A stage creates financial stability and long-term support uncertainty.\\n3. **Limited Transparency:** Model types, training data sources, and safety testing results not disclosed; moderate explainability insufficient for high-stakes deployments.\\n4. **Regulatory Readiness:** HIPAA, GDPR, and EU AI Act compliance not documented; no DPA or BAA availability confirmed.\\n5. **Support SLAs:** No severity-based support response targets; enterprise support maturity unclear.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n\\n**For Non-Regulated Use Cases (e.g., internal development tools):**\\n- **APPROVED WITH CONDITIONS:** Suitable for individual developers and small engineering teams in non-regulated sectors.\\n- Require: Privacy mode enabled for code containing sensitive data; annual SOC 2 audit review; incident response plan access.\\n\\n**For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Finance, Government):**\\n- **REVIEW RECOMMENDED / CONDITIONAL APPROVAL PENDING REMEDIATION:**\\n  1. Vendor must provide: Documented AI governance policy, training data transparency report, bias testing methodology.\\n  2. Vendor must achieve: HIPAA BAA eligibility (if healthcare use case), GDPR DPA, EU AI Act compliance roadmap.\\n  3. Buyer must implement: Enhanced code review workflows, PII/credential scanning, audit logging integration.\\n  4. Pilot phase required: 3–6 months with limited code scope before production rollout.\\n\\n**For Enterprise Deployment:**\\n- **PROCEED WITH CAUTION:** Negotiate dedicated support SLAs, executive escalation procedures, and multi-year financial commitments to mitigate startup risk.\\n- Require: Vendor roadmap for AI governance maturity, third-party bias audit (within 12 months), and GDPR/HIPAA compliance timeline.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Methodology:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification (VTS formula applied; Product Risk 40%, Governance Risk 30%, Operational Risk 30%)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified",