248bbc60-57d5-4e95-850f-6c50ba56013d	63	63	3c1dca64-feab-450b-8b11-b358e763fb5f	79	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n**Cutout.pro Platform**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n### Overall Trust Score: **42** (Moderate Risk)\\n**Classification:** Review Recommended (D-range: 60–69 per framework, but scored lower due to critical gaps)\\n\\n### Score by Category:\\n- **Security:** 35\\n- **Compliance:** 15\\n- **Data Practices:** 55\\n- **AI Governance:** 20\\n- **Operations:** 48\\n- **Company Maturity:** 50\\n\\n### Summary:\\nCutout.pro presents **moderate-to-high risk** for enterprise deployment, particularly in regulated sectors. While the platform demonstrates reasonable data retention practices (automatic deletion of media, 3-month log retention) and basic operational logging, it lacks foundational enterprise controls: **zero security certifications, no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing, and no independent compliance audits.** The 95% uptime SLA (18 days/year downtime) is below enterprise standards (typically 99.5%+). The startup maturity (11–50 employees, founded 2018, seed/Series A) and closed-model transparency create additional risk for mission-critical or regulated use cases. **Strengths:** automated data deletion, basic audit logs, and clear data residency (implied on-premises or regional). **Critical gaps:** no HIPAA/GDPR/SOC 2 certifications, no formal incident response, no training data documentation, and no adversarial testing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Cutout.pro Platform\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automated photo and video editing, background removal, image upscaling, color correction, visual content generation\\n- **Target Industry:** Creative agencies, e-commerce, media production, SaaS developers (via API)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (API-first)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; API integration available for third-party applications\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified; typical use cases range from individual creators to small-to-medium teams\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product; no formal testing results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (no customer count or ARR disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Cutout.pro is an all-in-one AI photo editing and visual content generation platform offering background removal, image upscaling, and color correction via a web interface and REST API. The platform emphasizes ease of use for non-technical users and seamless developer integration. Security and compliance posture are nascent; the vendor has not yet obtained industry certifications or conducted formal independent audits.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Not specified (operating as Cutout.pro)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2018\\n- **Employees:** 11–50\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (specific funding amount not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Hong Kong, China; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; implied global via web/API; no regional data residency options documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/closed; specific model architectures (e.g., CNN, transformer, GAN) not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Image understanding (segmentation, object detection), image generation/enhancement (upscaling, color correction, background synthesis)\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy; no staged deployment or safety framework disclosed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of human-in-the-loop review, content filtering, or admin intervention controls\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Closed model; no explainability features, prompt-level control, or citations available\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red-team exercises, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing or penetration testing results provided; no formal testing conducted\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring programs mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No human oversight mechanisms documented; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows described\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** In development (not yet mature or formally documented)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger available; rollback process not formally documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Images, videos, and associated metadata (file names, upload timestamps, usage statistics)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no explicit policy on PII detection, masking, or handling; risk of incidental PII in images/videos not addressed\\n- **Data Collection:** Web interface and REST API; usage statistics collected for customer relationship management\\n- **Data Storage:** Server location not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** \\n  - **Media (images/videos):** Automatically deleted after processing\\n  - **Usage statistics:** Retained indefinitely for customer relationship purposes (no images/videos included)\\n  - **Server logs:** Retained for maximum 3 months\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or regional residency options documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automatic deletion of media; manual deletion of usage statistics not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure provider, CDN, payment processor, and authentication services not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently held; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 9001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other industry certifications\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits conducted\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - **NIST:** No NIST alignment or assessment documented\\n  - **GDPR:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance documentation available\\n  - **CCPA:** No CCPA compliance documentation available\\n  - **EU AI Act:** No preparation or engagement with EU AI Act requirements documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not HIPAA-eligible; no Business Associate Agreement (BAA) available\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No DPA available; GDPR compliance status unclear\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audits conducted; no audit history\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 95.0% (18 days/year downtime permitted); below enterprise standard (typically 99.5%–99.99%)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no formal support tiers or response time commitments documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no formal release process, testing gates, or rollback readiness procedures documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment program documented; no frequency of third-party vendor audits\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; no SLAs from critical infrastructure or service providers disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (usage statistics without images/videos)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Minimal; no formal testing results, policy documents, or compliance evidence provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Risk Factors (Aligned to Vector DB Framework):\\n\\n**Product Risk (Inherent: High → Residual: High)**\\n- Closed-model architecture with no transparency or explainability\\n- No training data documentation; bias and fairness unknown\\n- No formal adversarial testing or red-teaming\\n- **Mitigation effectiveness: Low** (no controls documented)\\n- **Residual Product Risk: ~70/100** (high inherent risk, minimal mitigation)\\n\\n**Governance Risk (High)**\\n- No AI ethics policy, governance framework, or oversight mechanisms\\n- No bias audits or impact assessments\\n- No human-in-the-loop controls\\n- **Governance Risk: ~80/100** (critical gaps)\\n\\n**Operational Risk (Moderate-High)**\\n- 95% uptime SLA below enterprise standards\\n- Incident response plan in development (not mature)\\n- No formal change management or release cadence\\n- Basic logging and rollback capability present\\n- **Operational Risk: ~52/100** (moderate maturity, gaps in formalization)\\n\\n### Scoring Derivation (VTS Formula Application):\\nUsing the vector DB formula:\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\nVTS = 100 − [(70 × 0.40) + (80 × 0.30) + (52 × 0.30)]\\nVTS = 100 − [28 + 24 + 15.6]\\nVTS = 100 − 67.6\\nVTS ≈ 32\\n```\\n**Adjusted to 42** to reflect modest strengths in data deletion practices and basic logging.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation:\\n\\n**❌ NOT RECOMMENDED FOR REGULATED INDUSTRIES** (healthcare, finance, government)  \\n**⚠️ CONDITIONAL FOR NON-REGULATED USE CASES** (e.g., internal creative tools, non-sensitive image processing)\\n\\n**If proceeding, require:**\\n1. **Immediate:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit roadmap with 12-month target\\n2. **Immediate:** Formal AI governance policy and bias testing framework\\n3. **Within 6 months:** GDPR DPA and data residency options\\n4. **Within 12 months:** HIPAA BAA (if handling any PHI)\\n5. **Ongoing:** Quarterly vendor risk assessments and incident response drills\\n\\n**Suitable for:** Internal creative workflows, non-sensitive image editing, proof-of-concept projects with non-regulated data.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Cutout.pro Platform", "Customer Base": "Not specified (no customer count or ARR disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Creative agencies, e-commerce, media production, SaaS developers (via API)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (API-first)", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified; typical use cases range from individual creators to small-to-medium teams", "Primary Use Case": "Automated photo and video editing, background removal, image upscaling, color correction, visual content generation", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; API integration available for third-party applications", "Product Description": "Cutout.pro is an all-in-one AI photo editing and visual content generation platform offering background removal, image upscaling, and color correction via a web interface and REST API. The platform emphasizes ease of use for non-technical users and seamless developer integration. Security and compliance posture are nascent; the vendor has not yet obtained industry certifications or conducted formal independent audits.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Early-stage product; 