adiness": "Not addressed; no evidence of risk classification, transparency documentation, or compliance roadmap", "Regulatory Frameworks": "- NIST AI RMF: No documented alignment or assessment", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified. SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certifications imply third-party audit; audit frequency, scope, and most recent audit date not disclosed.", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "- Audit frequency: Not specified"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)—acceptable for non-critical workflows; does not meet 99.95%+ standards typical for mission-critical healthcare systems", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified. No documented release process, testing gates, rollback readiness procedures, or communication cadence disclosed. Given healthcare context, absence of formal change management is a gap.", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified. No documented severity levels, response targets, or escalation procedures disclosed."}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified. No SLA documentation from Epic, LLM provider, or infrastructure vendor disclosed.", "Critical Vendors": "- Epic (EHR integration partner)", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified. No documented frequency or methodology for assessing critical vendor risk, SLA compliance, or security posture."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available. Audit log scope (user actions, API calls, model decisions, data access) and export format/frequency not detailed.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available. Vendor reports operational metrics (93.8% coding accuracy, 98% call abandonment reduction, 11% visit increase); detailed telemetry schema and export capability not specified.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Limited/Partial. No bias testing results, adversarial testing reports, or model safety evaluations disclosed (even under NDA). Training data composition and third-party model selection rationale not documented.", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Limited/Partial. No uploaded evidence files, policy documents, or testing reports provided. Vendor claims SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 but certificates not attached; incident response plan documented but not provided for review."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Sully.ai presents a **moderate-risk profile** appropriate for a 2023-stage startup entering healthcare operations. The vendor demonstrates solid foundational security (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA) and operational stability (99.9% SLA, automated rollback), but critical gaps in AI governance, transparency, and data practices create material risk for healthcare deployment. The company's early maturity (seed/Series A, <50 employees, 1 year old) and limited testing evidence (incident response documented but untested, bias testing approach not specified, training data sourced from third-party models with unknown provenance) elevate governance and product risk. **Recommendation: Acceptable for pilot deployment in non-critical workflows with enhanced due diligence, contractual mitigation roadmap, and continuous monitoring requirements.** ---", "overallScore": 84, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 97.13, "Governance": 89, "Operational": 63}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   84 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\