6b07106b-fadd-481e-975f-d13676d8b2ce	118	118	fa21f4e4-b0db-44f7-9f43-5c8d5892d669	80	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n**VEED AI Video Creation Platform**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n### Overall Trust Score: **52** (Moderate Risk)\\n\\n**Score by Category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 25\\n- Data Practices: 45\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 60\\n\\n### Summary:\\nVEED demonstrates moderate operational maturity (99.9% uptime SLA, automated rollback capability) and reasonable company stability (Series B/C, 51–200 employees, founded 2018), but exhibits significant gaps in governance, compliance, and security posture that elevate overall risk. The vendor lacks formal security certifications, documented AI governance policies, bias testing frameworks, and formal security testing—critical requirements for enterprise deployment. While data retention practices are intentionally limited and basic audit logging is available, the absence of independent compliance audits, no formal testing results, and undocumented training data create residual concerns. The product is suitable for non-regulated, general-purpose video creation but requires substantial governance and security enhancements before deployment in regulated industries (healthcare, finance) or handling sensitive data.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** VEED\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Team-based video creation, editing, and content production; social media content generation\\n- **Target Industry:** Media & Entertainment, Marketing, Content Creation, SaaS (general)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Team/group collaboration; typical users are content creators and marketing teams\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage; no formal security or AI testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (evidence suggests active usage with social media integration)\\n- **Product Description:** VEED is an AI-powered video creation platform that simplifies video production through user-friendly tools, real-time collaboration, and AI-assisted editing. The platform reduces video production time by up to 50% and integrates with social media platforms. However, the product lacks formal security certifications, documented AI governance, and independent compliance validation, limiting its suitability for regulated or high-sensitivity use cases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** VEED (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2018\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (Growth stage)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: London, United Kingdom; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (presumed global via SaaS platform)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; inferred to include video processing, editing automation, and possibly speech/text recognition for captions\\n- **Model Purpose:** Video creation assistance, automated editing, content optimization, real-time collaboration support\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy; safety framework not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; presumed user-driven (no autonomous decision-making described)\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted); specific mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team or third-party audits mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing conducted; no formal security testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted or planned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; presumed user-controlled (no automated content filtering or intervention mechanisms described)\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level unclear\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (moderate maturity)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Video files, user-generated content, metadata, collaboration data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; presumed minimal for general video creation use case, but no explicit policy provided\\n- **Data Collection:** Web interface and API; retention options available\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** VEED aims to limit data collection and storage; specific retention periods detailed in privacy policy (policy not provided in attestation)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or residency options documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** Not specified; presumed on-request deletion available (standard SaaS practice)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not identified; payment processors and authentication services not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently** (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other formal certifications)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits conducted\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No documented alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable; no BAA available\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; no DPA documented\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No formal audits conducted\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, rollback readiness, or change management procedures\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not identified; payment processors and authentication services not specified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment frequency documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No critical vendor SLAs documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (DevOps FTE: 1; Data Handled Monthly: 3+; Storage Costs Savings: 50%+; Social Media Profile: Boosted; Content Creation Speed: Quickly produce content)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results; governance and compliance policies not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA demonstrates solid infrastructure maturity\\n2. **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger provides deployment safety\\n3. **Company Stability:** Series B/C funding and 51–200 employees indicate sustainable operations\\n4. **Data Minimization:** Intentional limits on data collection and storage reduce privacy risk\\n5. **Basic Observability:** Audit logs and interaction telemetry available for monitoring\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2, ISO 27001, or equivalent certifications is a major red flag for enterprise deployment\\n2. **Untested Incident Response:** Documented but not tested incident response plan provides limited assurance\\n3. **No AI Governance:** Absence of documented AI ethics policy, bias testing, or safety frameworks\\n4. **No Independent Audits:** No third-party compliance validation or security assessments\\n5. **Training Data Undocumented:** No transparency on model training data sources, quality, or bias mitigation\\n6. **No Formal Testing:** No adversarial security testing, penetration testing, or formal AI safety testing conducted\\n7. **Incomplete Vendor Management:** Critical infrastructure and sub-processor details not documented\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n\\n**For General (Non-Regulated) Use:**\\n- VEED is suitable for general-purpose video creation and marketing content production\\n- Implement internal monitoring and incident response procedures\\n- Establish data handling agreements and retention schedules\\n\\n**For Regulated or Sensitive Use (Healthcare, Finance, Government):**\\n- **Do not deploy** without substantial security and governance enhancements\\n- Require vendor to obtain SOC 2 Type 2 certification (minimum 6–12 months)\\n- Mandate documented AI governance policy, bias testing framework, and formal security testing\\n- Conduct independent penetration testing and compliance audit before production use\\n- Establish contractual SLAs for support response, incident notification, and breach disclosure\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation:** **CONDITIONAL APPROVAL** for non-regulated, general-purpose use only. Require vendor roadmap and timeline for SOC 2 certification and AI governance documentation as a condition of enterprise contract. **REJECT** for regulated industries or sensitive data handling until certifications and governance frameworks are in place.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Versi