as Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no evidence of red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not specified; formal ethics framework not evident in attestation\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluation program documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Supervision capabilities referenced (\\"supervise AI agents\\"); specific admin controls, content filtering, and intervention mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation not specified; impact assessment process not evident\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually — demonstrates mature incident management discipline\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option — supports rapid incident recovery and deployment safety\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Documents, enterprise data (structured and unstructured); specific data categories not enumerated\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and customer data usage for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface; specific collection mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed\\n- **Data Retention:** **Zero data retention approach** — data stored only as long as needed for platform operation; this is a strong privacy-protective practice\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Geographic residency options not specified; default storage location not disclosed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion capability implied by zero-retention policy; automated deletion mechanics not detailed\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - ISO 27001 ✓\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Management) ✓\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management) ✓\\n  - HIPAA BAA ✓\\n  - PCI DSS ✓\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (e.g., Big 4 firm, frequency, scope) not disclosed\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST AI Risk Management Framework: Readiness not specified\\n  - GDPR: DPA availability not confirmed\\n  - CCPA: Compliance not explicitly stated\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness not specified\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available ✓\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability not specified; GDPR compliance posture not detailed\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Audit frequency not specified\\n  - Last audit date not disclosed\\n  - Audit findings not available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime) — enterprise-grade reliability commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not disclosed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key vendor SLAs not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available — limited scope\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available — supports compliance and forensic investigation\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited evidence provided; formal policy documentation and testing results not comprehensively disclosed\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial availability — suggests testing has occurred but results are not broadly accessible\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Compliance & Security Certifications:** Comprehensive portfolio (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001/27701, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA, PCI DSS) demonstrates enterprise-ready security posture.\\n2. **Data Privacy:** Zero-retention policy is a strong privacy-protective practice; aligns with privacy-by-design principles.\\n3. **Operational Reliability:** 99.99% uptime SLA and tested incident response plan indicate mature operations.\\n4. **Audit Logs & Telemetry:** Comprehensive audit logs and basic interaction metrics support compliance and monitoring.\\n\\n### Material Gaps\\n1. **AI Governance Documentation:** No formal AI ethics policy, training data documentation, or bias testing methodology disclosed—a critical gap for regulated industries (healthcare, finance).\\n2. **Bias & Safety Testing:** No evidence of red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or adversarial testing; bias detection approach not specified.\\n3. **Support SLAs:** Response time commitments by severity not disclosed; limits buyer confidence in support responsiveness.\\n4. **Regulatory Readiness:** GDPR DPA, CCPA compliance, and EU AI Act readiness not specified; limits international deployment confidence.\\n5. **Vendor Transparency:** Sub-processor identities, infrastructure provider, and change management process not disclosed.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT** with mandatory conditions:\\n\\n- **Condition 1:** Vendor must provide formal AI governance policy, training data documentation, and bias testing methodology before contract execution.\\n- **Condition 2:** Vendor must disclose support respon