cations (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA, FedRAMP High), and strong compliance posture. The score is tempered by gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing disclosed), limited data practices clarity (third-party model data unknown, basic audit logging only), and unspecified operational SLAs. The vendor's position as a managed AWS service providing access to third-party foundation models creates inherent governance complexity that is not fully addressed in the attestation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Amazon Bedrock\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise generative AI application development, customization via fine-tuning and RAG, deployment of AI agents and applications at production scale\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-industry)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (AWS SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** AWS-managed serverless; integrates with broader AWS ecosystem\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Production-scale enterprise deployments\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; no formal testing results disclosed\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified\\n- **Product Description:** Amazon Bedrock is a fully managed AWS service providing unified API access to foundation models from multiple third-party providers, enabling organizations to experiment, customize, and deploy generative AI applications without managing underlying infrastructure. The service integrates with AWS security, governance, and responsible AI frameworks, offering serverless deployment and RAG/fine-tuning capabilities within the enterprise's existing cloud environment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Amazon Web Services, Inc. (subsidiary of Amazon.com, Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Cloud Infrastructure & Managed Services)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2006 (AWS division; parent company Amazon founded 1994)\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+ (AWS; Amazon total ~1.5M)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company; AWS revenue ~$90B+ annually (2023)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Public; Headquarters: Seattle, Washington, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (AWS operates in 30+ regions worldwide)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Access to third-party foundation models (LLMs, multimodal models); specific model architectures depend on selected provider\\n- **Model Purpose:** Text generation, code generation, image generation, multimodal understanding, analysis, and agent-based reasoning\\n- **Model Governance:** Bedrock provides access to models; governance of individual models deferred to model providers; AWS provides responsible AI guardrails at the platform level\\n- **Human Oversight:** Customer-configurable; supports content filtering, user-defined safety policies, and integration with AWS governance tools; specific oversight mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Model transparency is provider-dependent (proprietary/closed for most foundation models); Bedrock does not provide prompt-level explainability or citation mechanisms\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified; model updates managed by individual model providers through Bedrock\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Third-party models; training data documentation not available (vendor does not control training data)\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach disclosed; relies on model provider bias mitigation\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing disclosed; incident response plan documented but not tested\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI governance policy disclosed in attestation\\n- **Bias Audits:** No formal bias audit frequency or external evaluations disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Content filtering and safety policies configurable by customer; specific intervention workflows not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation disclosed; governance deferred to model providers\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; supports rapid deployment recovery\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Text, code, images, and multimodal inputs (customer-provided)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; AWS privacy policy applies; customer responsible for PII classification and handling\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based; interaction data available (basic metrics)\\n- **Data Storage:** AWS-managed infrastructure; encryption in transit and at rest (standard AWS practices)\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published AWS privacy policy; specific retention windows not detailed in attestation\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** AWS region selection available; customer can choose region for data residency\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request via AWS data deletion mechanisms; automated deletion timelines not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** AWS infrastructure (compute, storage, networking); third-party model providers (data flows to model provider APIs); AWS payment and identity services\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 1, SOC 2 Type 2, SOC 3, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, CSA STAR Level 2, HIPAA, FedRAMP High\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 and FedRAMP High indicate third-party audit; audit frequency and last audit date not specified\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA-compliant; FedRAMP High approval indicates NIST compliance; ISO 27001 and ISO 42001 indicate information security and AI management system maturity\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA-eligible (HIPAA certification held)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability not explicitly stated; AWS standard DPA applies (inferred from EU operations)\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no explicit engagement or preparation disclosed\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified in attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified in attestation; AWS typically publishes regional SLAs (commonly 99.99% for managed services)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified in attestation; AWS support tiers available (Premium, Business, Developer)\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; AWS typically releases updates continuously with backward compatibility; rollback capability available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Third-party foundation model providers (e.g., Anthropic, Cohere, Meta, Mistral, Stability AI); AWS infrastructure (compute, storage, networking)\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; AWS conducts vendor risk assessments for third-party integrations (standard practice, not detailed)\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Third-party model provider SLAs not disclosed; AWS infrastructure SLAs apply\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available via AWS CloudWatch and Bedrock console\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; AWS CloudTrail integration for API audit logs\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results disclosed; incident response plan documented but not tested\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not available; model safety testing deferred to individual model providers\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Exceptional Company Maturity:** AWS is a mature, publicly traded company with 10,000+ employees and 18+ years of operational history, providing strong financial stability and operational continuity.\\n2. **Comprehensive Security & Compliance Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA, and FedRAMP High certifications demonstrate rigorous third-party audit and regulatory alignment.\\n3. **Broad Model Access:** Unified API access to multiple foundation models reduces vendor lock-in and provides flexibility for enterprise use cases.\\n4. **AWS Ecosystem Integration:** Serverless architecture and integration with AWS security, governance, and monitoring tools simplify enterprise deployment.\\n\\n### Gaps & Concerns\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency:** No documented AI governance policy, bias testing approach, or formal safety testing disclosed. Governance responsibility is deferred to third-party model providers, creating potential accountability gaps.\\n2. **Third-Party Model Data Unknown:** Training data for accessed foundation models is not documented; Bedrock does not control model training or bias mitigation, limiting vendor accountability for model safety.\\n3. **Operational SLAs Not Specified:** Uptime SLA, support response SLAs, and change management cadence not disclosed in attestation; AWS typically provides these via separate agreements.\\n4. **Limited Audit Transparency:** Incident response plan documented but not tested; audit frequency and last audit date not specified; basic logging only (not enterprise-grade SIEM export).\\n5. **EU AI Act Readiness Unknown:** No explicit engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance disclosed.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions for Procurement\\n1. **Clarify Operational SLAs:** Request AWS service-level agreements (SLAs) for Bedrock uptime, support response times, and change management processes.\\n2. **Obtain AI Governance Documentation:** Request Bedrock's documented AI governance policy, including bias testing, adversarial security testing, and model safety monitoring practices.\\n3. **Verify Third-Party Model Governance:** Request documentation of how Bedrock vets and monitors third-party model providers for safety, bias, and compliance.\\n4. **Confirm Data Handling for Sensitive Use Cases:** For HIPAA or GDPR-regulated workloads, obtain explicit confirmation of data residency, retention, and deletion practices via BAA or DPA.\\n5. **Test Incident Response:** Request evidence of incident response plan testing (e.g., tabletop exercises, penetration test results).\\n6. **EU AI Act Alignment:** If deploying in EU, request Bedrock's EU AI Act compliance roadmap and risk classification for high-risk AI applications.\\n\\n### Classification\\n**Grade: B (Trusted Vendor)**  \\nAmazon Bedrock qualifies as a trusted vendor with strong governance, mature operations, and comprehensive compliance certifications. Procurement can proceed with standard due diligence focused on operational SLA confirmation, AI governance transparency, and third-party model vetting for regulated use cases.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Amazon Bedrock", "Customer Base": "Not specified", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-industry)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (AWS SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Production-scale enterprise deployments", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise generative AI application development, customization via fine-tuning and RAG, deployment of AI agents and applications at production scale", "Hosted / Deployed": "AWS-managed serverless; integrates with broader AWS ecosystem", "Product Description": "Amazon Bedrock is a fully managed AWS service providing unified API access to foundation models from multiple third-party providers, enabling organizations to experiment, customize, and deploy generative AI applications without managing underlying infrastructure. The service integrates with AWS security, governance, and responsible AI frameworks, offering serverless deployment and RAG/fine-tuning capabilities within the enterprise'