mpliance but no explicit residency options documented"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "SOC 2 Type 2, GDPR", "GDPR Compliance": "Yes, GDPR certified; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly confirmed", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not mentioned; BAA eligibility not stated", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; no documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance", "Regulatory Frameworks": "GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not specified", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted by third party (standard practice); GDPR compliance assessed", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "Not published; no contractual uptime commitment documented", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Continuous community contributions and library updates; formal release process for official libraries (Transformers, Diffusers) not detailed; rollback/readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; no published support response time commitments by severity"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; critical vendor SLAs not provided", "Critical Vendors": "Not specified; infrastructure providers, CDN, and payment processors not documented", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; no documented vendor risk assessment or SLA monitoring program"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Conditional": "Production deployments with formal governance, safety testing, and SLA commitments in place", "Recommended": "Research, experimentation, model discovery, internal ML development, non-production prototyping", "Not Recommended": "Regulated industries (healthcare, finance) without additional safety validation and compliance controls", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability and log retention not specified", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope not specified", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Limited; no formal testing results, AI ethics policy, or impact assessments provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "A", "label": "Exceptional Vendor", "summary": "** Hugging Face demonstrates moderate trustworthiness as an established open-source AI platform provider (founded 2016, Series D+, 201–1,000 employees). Strengths include SOC 2 Type 2 and GDPR certifications, full model transparency with open weights, comprehensive training data documentation, and a large enterprise customer base (50,000+ organizations). However, significant gaps limit the score: no formal AI safety testing or bias audits documented, incident response plan is documented but untested, no published uptime SLA or support response commitments, limited evidence of human-in-the-loop controls, and no formal AI ethics policy or impact assessments. The platform's open-source nature and community-driven model sharing create inherent governance challenges around model provenance and safety validation. Hugging Face is suitable for collaborative ML development and research but requires enhanced operational maturity, formal safety testing, and clearer support commitments for enterprise production deployments handling sensitive data. ---", "overallScore": 94, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.73, "Governance": 100, "Operational": 84}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n=================================