n- Compliance: 78\\n- Data Practices: 65\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 68\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nScale AI demonstrates strong foundational trust through established company maturity (Series D+, profitable, $29B valuation post-Meta investment), robust security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP High, DoD IL4), and significant government/enterprise backing. However, the trust score is constrained by material gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing), limited data practice specificity (PII handling and data residency options not specified), and absence of formal safety testing results. The score reflects a vendor with strong operational and compliance infrastructure but incomplete transparency in AI safety and governance—typical of infrastructure-layer AI providers focused on data annotation and model evaluation rather than autonomous decision systems. Recommended action: **Standard procurement process with enhanced due diligence on data governance and bias testing practices before deployment.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Scale Data Engine\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** High-quality training data generation, model annotation, RLHF (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback) data pipelines, model evaluation, and red-teaming for enterprise and government AI applications\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise AI, Government (DoD, federal agencies), Technology, Financial Services, Healthcare\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS / Cloud-hosted (infrastructure details not specified)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; on-premise or hybrid options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale; typical customer deployment size not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready (established product with government certifications including FedRAMP High and DoD IL4)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not publicly disclosed; government and enterprise customers implied by FedRAMP/DoD certifications\\n- **Product Description:** Scale Data Engine is a full-stack AI data and infrastructure platform that provides high-quality labeled training data, RLHF annotations, model evaluation, and red-teaming services to enable enterprises and governments to build and deploy reliable AI applications. The platform is backed by SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP High, and DoD IL4 certifications, positioning it for regulated and government use cases. Scale's infrastructure supports both proprietary annotation workflows and third-party model evaluation, with data retention and residency governed by customer contracts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Scale AI (legal entity details not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (data annotation, model evaluation, and infrastructure)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Profitable 3+ years; Series D+ (private); $29B post-money valuation (June 2025, following Meta's ~$14.3B investment for ~49% non-voting stake)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Meta (~49% non-voting stake, June 2025); Headquarters: San Francisco, California, USA; remains independent private company\\n- **Operating Regions:** United States (primary); international operations not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Scale Data Engine does not deploy proprietary AI models; instead, it provides infrastructure and annotation services for customer-owned and third-party models (e.g., LLM evaluation, custom model training data)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Model evaluation, red-teaming, training data generation, RLHF pipeline orchestration, bias detection support\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; governance applies to customer models evaluated/trained on the platform, not Scale's own models\\n- **Human Oversight:** Human-in-the-loop annotation and RLHF workflows; Scale manages quality control for annotation tasks; customer models subject to customer governance\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Model transparency is proprietary/closed for Scale's annotation and evaluation algorithms; customer models retain their own explainability properties\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; Scale provides training data services but does not publish documentation of its own training data or annotation methodologies\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; Scale offers bias detection as a service (red-teaming, model evaluation) but does not publish internal bias audit results or methodology\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not documented; no frequency or scope specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI governance policy provided; Scale's ethics framework for annotation and evaluation services not publicly specified\\n- **Bias Audits:** No formal bias audit frequency or external evaluation results disclosed; Scale provides bias detection services to customers but does not publish internal audits\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human annotators and reviewers embedded in RLHF and annotation workflows; customer-side human oversight depends on customer implementation\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release impact documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; formal incident response procedures exist but no evidence of tabletop exercises, simulations, or third-party validation\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback is supported but rollback testing frequency and procedures not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Training data (text, code, images, audio), annotations, RLHF feedback, model evaluation results, customer proprietary datasets\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer PII is used for training or service improvement not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based ingestion, web interface, batch uploads; collection scope and telemetry practices not fully specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud infrastructure (specific providers not named); encryption status not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period not specified; zero-retention options not documented\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice or default US residency not confirmed; FedRAMP High and DoD IL4 certifications suggest US government data handling but commercial customer residency options unclear\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied by contract-based retention); automated deletion procedures not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication services not named; sub-processor list not publicly available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 (security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy)\\n  - ISO 27001 (information security management)\\n  - FedRAMP High (federal cloud security baseline)\\n  - DoD IL4 Provisional Authorization (Department of Defense Impact Level 4)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 imply annual third-party audits; audit scope and most recent audit date not specified\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Compliance implied by FedRAMP High authorization\\n  - GDPR: Not explicitly addressed; EU data residency or DPA availability not specified\\n  - CCPA: Not explicitly addressed\\n  - EU AI Act: No stated readiness or engagement\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not stated; BAA eligibility not confirmed (healthcare use case not explicitly supported)\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not stated; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation roadmap disclosed\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Audit frequency: Annual (implied by SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 standards)\\n  - Last audit date: Not specified\\n  - Audit findings: Not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment disclosed\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response times by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, change notification procedures, and readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication services not named; sub-processor dependencies not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope and customer access not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability, retention, and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; supporting policy documents (incident response, data governance, bias testing) not provided or uploaded\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Vendor Classification:** Acceptable Vendor (Grade C, 70–79 range; actual score 72)\\n\\n**Key Strengths:**\\n1. **Established company maturity** (founded 2016, 1,001–5,000 employees, profitable 3+ years, $29B valuation)\\n2. **Strong security and compliance posture** (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP High, DoD IL4 Provisional Authorization)\\n3. **Government and enterprise backing** (Meta $14.3B investment; federal certifications indicate trusted infrastructure)\\n4. **Documented incident response and rollback capability** (automated rollback with manual trigger)\\n\\n**Material Gaps:**\\n1. **AI governance transparency** (no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing)\\n2. **Data practice specificity** (PII handling, data residency options, and sub-processor list not disclosed)\\n3. **Absence of formal safety testing** (no formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available)\\n4. **Limited operational transparency** (uptime SLA, support SLAs, and release cadence not specified)\\n5. **EU/GDPR readiness unclear** (no DPA, GDPR compliance, or EU AI Act engagement stated)\\n\\n**Recommended Action:** **STANDARD PROCUREMENT WITH ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE**\\n\\n- **Proceed with vendor evaluation** for enterprise and government use cases requiring high-quality training data, model evaluation, and RLHF infrastructure\\n- **Before contract signature, require:**\\n  - Written AI governance policy and bias testing methodology\\n  - Data residency and PII handling addendum (especially for regulated industries)\\n  - Uptime SLA and support response SLA commitments\\n  - Sub-processor list and vendor assessment frequency\\n  - GDPR DPA (if EU customers or data processing involved)\\n- **For healthcare or financial services use cases:** Confirm HIPAA BAA eligibility and SOC 2 Type 2 audit findings before proceeding\\n- **For EU customers:** Clarify GDPR compliance roadmap and EU AI Act engagement before deployment\\n\\n**