 Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 82\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 88\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nUiPath demonstrates strong foundational trust through mature company status (19 years, public, 1,001–5,000 employees), comprehensive security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HITRUST, FedRAMP), and robust compliance posture across multiple regulatory frameworks. However, the Trust Score is constrained by significant gaps in AI governance transparency—notably the absence of documented AI ethics policy, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing, and lack of training data documentation—which elevate product risk despite strong operational and governance infrastructure. The platform's moderate model transparency and undocumented decision autonomy create residual uncertainty about AI safety controls. Operations and data practices are adequate but lack specificity (no published uptime SLA, support SLAs, or explicit data residency options stated). Applying the vendor self-attestation formula (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]), the score reflects manageable product risk (mitigated by certifications) offset by governance and operational gaps requiring contractual clarification before enterprise deployment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** UiPath Platform for Agentic Automation\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** End-to-end business process automation; unification of AI agents, software robots, and human decision-making on a single orchestration system\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise; multi-sector (back-office operations, finance, HR, supply chain)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (specific cloud providers not specified)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; on-premises deployment options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-grade; typical deployments involve orchestration of multiple robots and agents across distributed workflows\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (company founded 2005, public since 2021); formal testing results not available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; UiPath is a recognized market leader in RPA/automation\\n- **Product Description:** UiPath Platform for Agentic Automation is an enterprise-grade orchestration system that unifies AI agents, robotic process automation (RPA) robots, and human decision-makers to automate end-to-end business processes. The platform addresses manual repetitive back-office processes, operational cost reduction, and process cycle time acceleration. Security is underpinned by SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HITRUST, and FedRAMP certifications, enabling deployment in regulated environments including healthcare and government.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** UiPath (Romanian-American enterprise software company)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider; Robotic Process Automation (RPA) / Agentic Automation Leader\\n- **Year Founded:** 2005\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (NYSE: PATH, IPO 2021); revenue not specified in attestation\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: New York, New York, USA; publicly traded on NYSE\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not enumerated; website: https://www.uipath.com)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; platform integrates AI agents with RPA robots; underlying model architectures not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Process automation, decision support, end-to-end workflow orchestration; capabilities include understanding, generation, and autonomous task execution\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no formal AI governance policy provided in attestation\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not fully specified; platform design includes human decision-making integration, but extent of monitoring, alerts, and intervention workflows not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); specific prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or transparency tools not described\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring not specified\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing not specified; frequency and scope of penetration testing not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits documented; frequency and external evaluation mechanisms not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Platform design includes human decision-making integration; specific admin controls, content filtering, intervention workflows, and escalation procedures not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or formal impact assessments documented for releases\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented; however, plan has not been tested (no test frequency or results provided)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments or model updates\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Business process data (documents, structured records, communications); specific data types not enumerated\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of personally identifiable information (PII) processing and whether customer data is used for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** Via platform APIs and orchestration workflows; specific collection mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure and encryption standards not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certifications imply encryption in transit and at rest, but specifics not provided\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period and options for zero retention not specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice or regional residency options not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (inferred from privacy policy reference); automated deletion workflows not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication vendors not enumerated\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 1 Type 2, SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 9001, HITRUST, FedRAMP, StateRAMP, C5, ENS, IRAP\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Certifications indicate readiness for NIST, GDPR, CCPA, and EU regulatory requirements; specific framework engagement not detailed\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HITRUST certification indicates healthcare compliance capability; BAA (Business Associate Agreement) eligibility not explicitly stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** ISO 27001 and data protection certifications (ISO 27017, ISO 27018) indicate GDPR readiness; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; vendor engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance not documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit schedule and most recent audit results not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; contractual uptime commitment not provided\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, and change notification procedures not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers (cloud, hosting), payment processors, and authentication vendors not enumerated\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency and methodology for assessing critical vendor risk not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure or service vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity of telemetry not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability, retention, and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; policy documentation (AI ethics, bias testing, incident response testing) not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not available; no formal testing results disclosed even under NDA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Mature Company & Public Status:** 19-year operating history, NYSE-listed, 1,001–5,000 employees provide operational stability and financial transparency.\\n2. **Comprehensive Security & Compliance Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HITRUST, FedRAMP, and multi-regional compliance frameworks (C5, ENS, IRAP, StateRAMP) demonstrate enterprise-grade security controls and regulatory readiness.\\n3. **Documented Incident Response & Rollback:** Incident response plan and automated rollback capability with manual trigger support rapid incident recovery.\\n4. **Audit Logs & Telemetry:** Basic interaction telemetry and audit logging available for operational monitoring and compliance auditing.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety Documentation:** Absence of documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, adversarial security testing, and training data documentation creates significant product risk in regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government).\\n2. **Model Transparency & Autonomy:** Moderate explainability and undocumented decision autonomy lack clarity on how AI agents make autonomous decisions and how humans can intervene or override.\\n3. **Operational SLAs & Support:** No published uptime SLA, support response SLAs, or change management cadence limit ability to assess operational reliability and support responsiveness.\\n4. **Data Practices Specificity:** PII handling, data residency options, and sub-processor details not specified; limits compliance assessment for regulated data processing.\\n5. **Testing & Validation:** No formal testing conducted; absence of bias audits, penetration testing results, and incident response plan testing creates residual uncertainty about safety and security controls.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions Before Deployment\\n\\n**MUST COMPLETE (Contract Conditions):**\\n1. **AI Governance Documentation:** Require vendor to provide documented AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, and training data documentation before production deployment.\\n2. **Incident Response Testing:** Require annual incident response plan testing with results provided to customer; document test frequency and remediation timelines.\\n3. **Operational SLAs:** Negotiate and document uptime SLA (recommended: 99.5% or higher for enterprise), support response SLAs (P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours), and change management procedures.\\n4. **Data Residency & PII Handling:** Clarify data residency options (US, EU, customer choice), PII handling practices, and whether customer data is used for model training or improvement.\\n\\n**SHOULD COMPLETE (Risk Mitigation):**\\n5. **Bias & Adversarial Testing:** Request results of formal bias testing and penetration testing; if not available, require vendor to conduct before production.\\n6. **Model Transparency:** Request explainability documentation for AI agent decision-making; clarify human oversight and intervention workflows.\\n7. **Vendor Assessment:** Request list of critical infrastructure vendors and their SLAs; verify vendor assessment frequency and risk management practices.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT**\\n\\nUiPath Platform for Agentic Automation is acceptable for enterprise deployment in regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government) **contingent upon:**\\n- Execution of contract amendments addressing AI governance, operational SLAs, and data practices gaps (Section 11 recommendations)\\n- Completion of incident response plan testing and bias testing before production cutover\\n- Establishment of data processing agreement (DPA) for GDPR compliance and Business Associate Agreement (BAA) for HIPAA compliance\\n\\n**Estimated Risk Mitigation Timeline:** 2–3 months (documentation, testing, contract negotiation)\\n\\n**Residual Risk Assessment:** After gap remediation, residual risk is acceptable (estimated 25–30/100) for enterprise automation use cases with appropriate human oversight and monitoring controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Methodology:** VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "UiPath Platform for Agentic Automation", "Customer Base": "Not specified; UiPath is a recognized market leader in RPA/automation", "Target Industry": "Enterprise; multi-sector (back-office operations, finance, HR, supply chain)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (specific cloud prov