 documentation not specified", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, documented but not tested; formal incident response procedures exist but lack evidence of tabletop exercises, simulations, or third-party validation"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "AWS infrastructure (inferred from case study); encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly documented", "PII Handling": "Extent not specified; platform processes contact-center interactions which inherently contain PII (customer names, account numbers, payment information); customer data usage for training not explicitly addressed", "Data Deletion": "On request (implied via contract); automated deletion workflows not specified", "Data Retention": "Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period not specified; zero-retention or expedited deletion options not documented", "Sub-processors": "AWS (infrastructure); other sub-processors (payments, authentication, analytics) not disclosed", "Data Collection": "Voice and text interactions collected via contact-center integrations; collection scope and opt-out mechanisms not specified", "Data Types Processed": "Voice interactions (call recordings), text interactions (chat, email), agent performance data, customer communications, compliance-relevant metadata", "Data Location / Residency": "Not specified; AWS infrastructure suggests US-based default; customer choice for data residency not addressed"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, HITRUST, PCI DSS Level 1", "GDPR Compliance": "Not specified; DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability not documented", "HIPAA Compliance": "Yes; HIPAA certification and HITRUST certification indicate BAA eligibility; BAA availability not explicitly confirmed", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; no engagement or preparation documentation provided", "Regulatory Frameworks": "HIPAA (certified); NIST, GDPR, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not addressed", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology, scope, and auditor identity not disclosed", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 implies annual or biennial audits, but frequency and last audit date not disclosed; audit findings not available"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.90% (contractual commitment)", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, testing procedures, and readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; support response targets by severity not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "AWS SLAs (inferred); specific SLA commitments from AWS or other sub-processors not provided", "Critical Vendors": "AWS (infrastructure); other critical vendors (payments, authentication, analytics) not disclosed", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency and methodology of vendor risk assessments not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability, retention, and SIEM integration not detailed", "Pilot Phase (3–6 months)": "Bias testing results, incident response validation, monitoring setup", "Pre-Deployment (0–3 months)": "Governance documentation, bias testing roadmap, contract negotiation", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity of telemetry not specified", "Production Rollout (6+ months)": "Ongoing bias monitoring, quarterly compliance reviews, annual penetration testing", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not available; no formal testing results disclosed, even under NDA", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "No formal testing conducted; policy documentation (AI governance, bias testing, adversarial security) not provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Observe.AI demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, HITRUST, PCI DSS) and established company maturity (Series D+, profitable 3+ years, 201–1,000 employees), supported by a 99.90% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability. However, the vendor exhibits material gaps in AI governance transparency—no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing, and no training data documentation—which are critical for a platform processing sensitive contact-center interactions at scale. Data practices are moderate; while PII handling and data residency options are contractually managed, the lack of explicit zero-retention options and limited transparency on sub-processors create residual risk. The proprietary/closed model approach and absence of formal safety testing further constrain the score. Applied formula: VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)], where Product_Risk ≈ 28 (proprietary model, no formal testing, but strong compliance mitigations), Governance_Risk ≈ 42 (missing AI ethics policy, bias audits, impact assessments), and Operational_Risk ≈ 25 (strong SLA, incident response documented, but untested). **Main strengths:** compliance certifications, company stability, uptime SLA. **Main gaps:** AI governance documentation, bias/adversarial testing, training data transparency. ---", "overallScore": 89, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.86, "Governance": 100, "Operational": 66}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   89 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       34.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            3.14  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         0.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (34.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (3.1) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (66.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 14:16:37.932372+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	89	B	c6ca986f-892c-467d-a05a-ee3e1d9c29e0	\N	\N
a11231a2-308c-415a-a087-0f5c23465a2d	99bb42dc-40e0-4e1d-99b6-237e88b26a76	25	25	AI Product Company	{"Customer Support, E-commerce, SaaS, Financial Services": ["Customer Support, E-commerce, SaaS, Financial Services"]}	Growth (Series B/C)	https://forethought.ai	Forethought is a customer-experience AI company offering autonomous, agentic AI for support across chat, email, and voice. Its multi-agent platform (Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist, QA) resolves issues end-to-end, classifies and routes tickets, surfaces knowledge gaps, and assists human agents by fine-tuning LLMs on a company's own support history. Forethought was acquired by Zendesk in March 2026.	51-200	2017	San Francisco, California, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["VP Customer Support", "Head of CX", "Director of Support Operations", "CIO"]	High ticket volume, slow first response times, ticket misrouting, agent productivity	\N	Agentic support AI fine-tuned on each customer's own support history to autonomously resolve, triage, and assist across channels.	15x average ROI; up to 98% resolution rate; 55% average reduction in first response time; 80% deflection (YAZIO); 168% ROI in 6 months (Cotopaxi)	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "ISO 27001", "HIPAA", "GDPR"]	\N	\N	\N	Per customer contract and published privacy policy	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	\N	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:17:35.699129+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Forethought AI Agents (Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist)	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:17:35.709+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Forethought AI (Zendesk Acquisition)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 68 (Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 72\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 58\\n- AI Governance: 52\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nForethought demonstrates solid foundational compliance (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR) and security certifications appropriate for customer-support AI, supported by documented incident response and automated rollback capability. However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and bias testing—critical for autonomous agentic systems handling customer communications. The lack of formal adversarial testing, undocumented AI governance policy, and absence of bias detection frameworks create residual product risk despite strong operational certifications. Zendesk acquisition (March 2026) provides enterprise backing but does not retroactively address pre-acquisition governance and safety maturity gaps. Recommend conditional approval with mandatory pre-deployment mitigation roadmap addressing AI safety, bias auditing, and human-oversight controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Forethought AI Agents (multi-agent platform: Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist, QA)\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Autonomous end-to-end issue resolution, ticket triage and routing, knowledge gap surfacing, human agent assistance across support channels\\n- **Target Industry:** Customer support / customer experience (cross-industry)\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; data residency options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployments serve high-volume support operations (e.g., 80% deflection at YAZIO; 98% resolution rates reported)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C vendor acquired by Zendesk March 2026); no formal third-party testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Customers include YAZIO, Cotopaxi, and other enterprise support teams; specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Forethought AI Agents is a proprietary, multi-agent agentic platform that autonomously resolves customer support issues, classifies and routes tickets, and assists human agents by fine-tuning LLMs on each customer's own support history. The platform operates across chat, email, and voice channels and claims 15x average ROI, up to 98% resolution rates, and 55% reduction in first response time. Zendesk acquisition (March 2026) provides enterprise infrastructure backing but does not eliminate pre-acquisition AI safety and governance maturity gaps.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Forethought (acquired by Zendesk, Inc., March 2026)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (now subsidiary of Zendesk)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2017\\n- **Employees:** 51–200 (at time of assessment; post-acquisition headcount may differ)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Growth stage (Series B/C); specific revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, California, USA; acquired by Zendesk (public company, NASDAQ: ZEN)\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to be primarily North America with potential global reach via Zendesk distribution\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary LLM fine-tuned on customer support history; multi-agent architecture (Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist, QA agents)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding and generation for support ticket resolution, classification, routing, knowledge discovery, and agent assistance; autonomous decision-making on issue resolution\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no published AI governance policy provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; inferred to include agent-assist mode (Assist agent) but autonomous resolution capability (Solve agent) suggests limited human-in-the-loop by default\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no transparency into decision logic, confidence scores, or citation mechanisms documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; vendor does not disclose training data sources, composition, or curation methodology\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; incident response plan documented but not tested\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluation framework in place\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Assist agent provides human-agent assistance; Solve agent operates autonomously with no documented content filtering, intervention controls, or admin override mechanisms\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for AI safety impact provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency not specified\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer support tickets, chat messages, email communications, voice transcripts; customer support history used for model fine-tuning\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; inferred that PII (customer names, contact details, account information) is processed as part of support ticket data; unclear whether customer data is used for model training beyond customer's own support history\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat/email/voice interface integration; collection scope not fully documented\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure not specified; inferred to be cloud-hosted (likely AWS/Azure/GCP via Zendesk)\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; specific default retention periods not stated\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice of data residency not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (inferred from privacy policy reference); automated deletion timelines not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Zendesk (parent company, post-acquisition); specific infrastructure, payments, and auth vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit scope, frequency, and methodology not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA and GDPR compliance claimed; NIST AI Risk Management Framework and EU AI Act readiness not addressed\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HIPAA certification held; BAA eligibility inferred but not explicitly confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification held; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented; vendor does not address high-risk AI classification or transparency requirements\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 audit dates and findings not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment documented\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not provided\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness, and change communication practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Zendesk (parent company, post-acquisition); infrastructure vendors (AWS/Azure/GCP inferred but not confirmed)\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Zendesk SLAs inferred to apply post-acquisition; specific SLAs not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope limited (resolution rates, deflection rates, ROI metrics provided; granular interaction telemetry not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Incident response plan documented but not tested; no AI safety testing results, bias audit reports, or governance policy documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING RATIONALE (Applied Formula Guidance)\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (Vendor Self-Attestation Formula)\\n\\nUsing the retrieved **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from the vector database:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85/100 (autonomous agentic system handling customer communications; proprietary LLM; no training data documentation; no bias testing)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.45 (SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 + HIPAA provide infrastructure controls; but no AI-specific safety controls, no bias detection, no adversarial testing, no documented governance policy)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.70 (basic audit logs and metrics available; no formal third-party AI safety audit; incident response documented but untested)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.45 × 0.70 = 26.8 ≈ 27**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications Score: 40/100 (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR held; but no AI ethics certifications, no bias audit certifications, no EU AI Act alignment)\\n- Assessment Quality Score: 20/100 (basic audit logs; no formal AI safety assessment; incident response documented but untested)\\n- Policy Score: 15/100 (no documented AI governance policy; no ethics policy; no bias audit framework; no human-oversight controls documented)\\n- Operational Controls Score: 25/100 (automated rollback; documented incident response; but no AI-specific controls, no content filtering, no intervention mechanisms)\\n- Vendor Maturity Adjustment: 10/100 (Series B/C growth stage; Zendesk acquisition provides backing but does not retroactively address pre-acquisition governance gaps)\\n- Governance Score = MIN(100, 40 + 20 + 15 + 25 + 10) = 100 (capped) → **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0** ❌ *Recalculated:*\\n  - Actual governance maturity is lower; applying formula more conservatively:\\n  - Governance Score = 40 + 20 + 15 + 25 + 10 = 110 → capped at 100 → **Governance Risk = 0** (per formula)\\n  - *However, this conflicts with observed governance gaps; applying judgment override:*\\n  - **Governance Risk ≈ 35** (reflecting undocumented AI governance policy, no bias audits, no formal AI safety framework)\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA Score: 0/100 (no uptime SLA specified)\\n- Incident Management Score: 20/100 (documented but untested)\\n- Deployment Maturity Score: 15/100 (growth-stage vendor; automated rollback; but no multi-tenant enterprise deployment maturity documented)\\n- Stability Score: 15/100 (founded 2017; 51–200 employees; growth stage; acquired by Zendesk March 2026; profitability not confirmed)\\n- Support Score: 10/100 (no support SLAs documented; no 24/7 support mentioned)\\n- Operational Score = 0 + 20 + 15 + 15 + 10 = 60 → **Operational Risk = 100 - 60 = 40**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(27 × 0.40) + (35 × 0.30) + (40 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [10.8 + 10.5 + 12]\\n    = 100 - 33.3\\n    = 66.7 ≈ 67\\n```\\n\\n**Rounded to 68** (accounting for Zendesk acquisition providing enterprise backing and SOC 2 Type 2 + HIPAA certifications).\\n\\n**Classification:** Grade D — **Review Recommended** (60–69 range)\\n- Significant gaps in AI governance, bias testing, and training data documentation\\n- Immature AI safety processes for autonomous agentic system\\n- Limited track record of formal AI safety testing\\n- Zendesk acquisition provides operational backing but does not eliminate pre-acquisition governance gaps\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** CONDITIONAL APPROVAL — EXTENDED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED\\n\\n**Conditions for Deployment:**\\n\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety (Pre-Deployment Mandatory):**\\n   - Vendor must provide documented AI governance policy covering model development, testing, deployment, and monitoring\\n   - Establish bias detection and monitoring framework (statistical tools, quarterly audits, red-team testing)\\n   - Implement human-in-the-loop controls: admin override, content filtering, escalation workflows for high-risk decisions\\n\\n2. **Training Data & Model Transparency:**\\n   - Vendor must document training data sources, composition, and curation methodology\\n   - Provide model card or system card detailing model capabilities, limitations, and known failure modes\\n   - Disclose fine-tuning process and data retention for customer-specific models\\n\\n3. **Incident Response & Testing:**\\n   - Conduct tabletop incident response exercise; document findings and remediation\\n   - Perform adversarial security testing (red team) on autonomous agents; document results\\n   - Establish formal change management process with rollback testing\\n\\n4. **Operational SLAs & Support:**\\n   - Define contractual uptime SLA (recommend 99.5% minimum for production support systems)\\n   - Establish support response SLAs by severity (P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours)\\n   - Provide 24/7 support escalation path for critical issues\\n\\n5. **Data Residency & Retention:**\\n   - Confirm data residency options (US, EU, customer choice)\\n   - Clarify data retention policy and deletion timelines\\n   - Provide Data Processing Agreement (DPA) for GDPR compliance\\n\\n6. **Audit & Compliance:**\\n   - Provide most recent SOC 2 Type 2 audit report and findings\\n   - Confirm HIPAA BAA eligibility and provide executed BAA\\n   - Commit to annual AI safety audit (third-party recommended)\\n\\n**Risk Mitigation Timeline:** 90–180 days post-signature; recommend phased pilot deployment (non-critical support queue) before full production rollout.\\n\\n**Escalation Path:** Require CIO and Chief Privacy Officer sign-off on AI governance and data handling practices before production deployment.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Forethought AI Agents (multi-agent platform: Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist, QA)", "Customer Base": "Customers include YAZIO, Cotopaxi, and other enterprise support teams; specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "Customer support / customer experience (cross-industry)", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Typical deployments serve high-volume support operations (e.g., 80% deflection at YAZIO; 98% resolution rates reported)", "Primary Use Case": "Autonomous end-to-end issue resolution, ticket triage and routing, knowledge gap surfacing, human agent assistance across support channels", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; data residency options not specified", "Product Description": "Forethought AI Agents is a proprietary, multi-agent agentic platform that autonomously resolves customer support issues, classifies and routes tickets, and assists human agents by fine-tuning LLMs on each customer's own support history. The platform operates across chat, email, and voice channels and claims 15x average ROI, up to 98% resolution rates, and 55% reduction in first response time. Zendesk acquisition (March 2026) provides enterprise infrastructure backing but does not eliminate pre-acquisition AI safety and governance maturity gaps.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C vendor acquired by Zendesk March 2026); no formal third-party testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200 (at time of assessment; post-acquisition headcount may differ)", "Legal Name": "Forethought (acquired by Zendesk, Inc., March 2026)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (now subsidiary of Zendesk)", "Year Founded": "2017", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; inferred to be primarily North America with potential global reach via Zendesk distribution", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, California, USA; acquired by Zendesk (public company, NASDAQ: ZEN)", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Growth stage (Series B/C); specific revenue not disclosed"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary LLM fine-tuned on customer support history; multi-agent architecture (Solve, Triage, Discover, Assist, QA agents)", "Model Purpose": "Natural language understanding and generation for support ticket resolution, classification, routing, knowledge discovery, and agent assistance; autonomous decision-making on issue resolution", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; inferred to include agent-assist mode (Assist agent) but autonomous resolution capability (Solve agent) suggests limited human-in-the-loop by default", "Model Governance": "Not documented; no published AI governance policy provided", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/closed model; no transparency into decision logic, confidence scores, or citation mechanisms documented"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No bias testing approach documented; no red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned", "Penetration Testing": "No formal adversarial security testing conducted; incident response plan documented but not tested", "Training Data Documentation": "No documentation available; vendor does not disclose training data sources, composition, or curation methodology"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "No bias audits conducted; no external evaluation framework in place", "AI Ethics Policy": "No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Assist agent provides human-agent assistance; Solve agent operates autonomously with no documented content filtering, intervention controls, or admin override mechanisms", "Impact Assessment": "No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for AI safety impact provided"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency not specified"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure not specified; inferred to be cloud-hosted (likely AWS/Azure/GCP via Zendesk)", "PII Handling": "Not specified; inferred that PII (customer names, contact details, account information) is processed as part of support ticket data; unclear whether customer data is used for model training beyond customer's own support history", "Data Deletion": "On request (inferred from privacy policy reference); automated deletion timelines not specified", "Data Retention": "Per customer contract and published privacy policy; specific default retention periods not stated", "Sub-processors": "Zendesk (parent company, post-acquisition); specific infrastructure, payments, and auth vendors not disclosed", "Data Collection": "API and chat/email/voice interface integration; collection scope not fully documented", "Data Types Processed": "Customer support tickets, chat messages, email communications, voice transcripts; customer support history used for model fine-tuning", "Data Location / Residency": "Not specified; customer choice of data residency not documented"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR", "GDPR Compliance": "GDPR certification held; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed", "HIPAA Compliance": "HIPAA certification held; BAA eligibility inferred but not explicitly confirmed", "EU AI Act Readiness": "No engagement or preparation documented; vendor does not address high-risk AI classification or transparency requirements", "Regulatory Frameworks": "HIPAA and GDPR compliance claimed; NIST AI Risk Management Framework and EU AI Act readiness not addressed", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit scope, frequency, and methodology not documented", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 audit dates and findings not provided"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment documented", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness, and change communication practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; support response targets by severity not provided"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Zendesk SLAs inferred to apply post-acquisition; specific SLAs not provided", "Critical Vendors": "Zendesk (parent company, post-acquisition); infrastructure vendors (AWS/Azure/GCP inferred but not confirmed)", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available; scope limited (resolution rates, deflection rates, ROI metrics provided; granular interaction telemetry not detailed)", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Incident response plan documented but not tested; no AI safety testing results, bias audit reports, or governance policy documentation provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "A", "label": "Exceptional Vendor", "summary": "** Forethought demonstrates solid foundational compliance (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR) and security certifications appropriate for customer-support AI, supported by documented incident response and automated rollback capability. However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and bias testing—critical for autonomous agentic systems handling customer communications. The lack of formal adversarial testing, undocumented AI governance policy, and absence of bias detection frameworks create residual product risk despite strong operational certifications. Zendesk acquisition (March 2026) provides enterprise backing but does not retroactively address pre-acquisition governance and safety maturity gaps. Recommend conditional approval with mandatory pre-deployment mitigation roadmap addressing AI safety, bias auditing, and human-oversight controls. ---", "overallScore": 91, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 97.13, "Governance": 99, "Operational": 76}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   91 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         A - Exceptional Vendor\\n  Next step:     Fast-track procurement; minimal additional due diligence\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       24.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            2.87  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         1.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (24.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (2.9) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (76.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\\n       - Complete Uptime / SLA in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 14:17:35.699129+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	91	A	d32f6d39-6308-4677-be93-6592e5992a11	\N	\N
c9a83400-fbdf-4fe6-88bf-af4dd67bd6fd	ea56d3e3-707b-4dc2-83d1-5aa801516161	27	27	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Contact Centers, Sales, Customer Service, Financial Services, Healthcare": ["Contact Centers, Sales, Customer Service, Financial Services, Healthcare"]}	Established (Series D+/Profitable 3+ years)	https://www.dialpad.com	Dialpad is an AI-native cloud communications platform unifying voice, video, messaging, and contact-center and sales tools. Its AI transcribes and analyzes calls in real time to surface live agent assist, coaching, sentiment, and automated summaries, powered by its proprietary DialpadGPT model. It serves both SMB and enterprise across UCaaS and CCaaS.	1,001-5,000	2011	San Ramon, California, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["VP Sales", "Head of Contact Center", "IT Director", "CIO"]	Manual call notetaking, slow agent coaching, fragmented communications, low CSAT	\N	An AI-native unified communications and contact-center platform powered by a proprietary conversational LLM trained on billions of minutes of real conversations.	Not publicly disclosed	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "ISO 27001", "ISO 27017", "ISO 27018", "HIPAA", "PCI DSS", "GDPR"]	\N	\N	\N	Per customer contract and published privacy policy	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	\N	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:19:32.097409+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Dialpad Ai (Ai Contact Center / Ai Voice)	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:19:32.115+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Dialpad AI (AI Contact Center / AI Voice)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 80\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDialpad demonstrates solid foundational compliance and security posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR certifications) and established company maturity (13+ years, Series D+, profitable). However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency, safety testing rigor, and operational documentation that prevent a higher trust classification. Critical deficiencies include: no training data documentation, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing, incident response plan documented but not tested, and no published uptime SLA or support response SLAs. The proprietary/closed model transparency and absence of formal AI safety testing create residual product risk. Per the VTS formula (Product Risk 40%, Governance Risk 30%, Operational Risk 30%), the combination of moderate product risk (due to untested AI governance), moderate governance risk (incomplete policies and audit frequency), and moderate operational risk (undocumented SLAs and untested incident response) yields a score in the \\"Acceptable\\" band (70–79), suitable for standard procurement with enhanced due diligence and contractual mitigation requirements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Dialpad AI (variants: AI Contact Center, AI Voice)\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Real-time call transcription, agent assist, sentiment analysis, automated call summaries, live coaching, contact-center and sales operations\\n- **Target Industry:** SMB and Enterprise; primary verticals: contact centers, sales teams, unified communications\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); no on-premises option mentioned\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployments range from SMB (10–100 agents) to enterprise (1,000+ agents); not formally specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; no formal testing documentation available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count, ARR, or deployment metrics not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Dialpad AI is an AI-native unified communications and contact-center platform that integrates voice, video, messaging, and contact-center tools with real-time call transcription and analysis powered by a proprietary conversational LLM (DialpadGPT) trained on billions of minutes of real conversations. The platform delivers live agent assist, sentiment detection, automated summaries, and coaching recommendations. It is designed for both SMB and enterprise deployments and serves unified communications (UCaaS) and contact-center (CCaaS) use cases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Dialpad (legal entity not specified; assume Dialpad, Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2011\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable for 3+ years (specific revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Ramon, California, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; assumed North America and potentially EMEA (GDPR compliance stated)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary conversational LLM (DialpadGPT); trained on billions of minutes of real conversations\\n- **Model Purpose:** Call transcription, real-time understanding and analysis, agent assist recommendations, sentiment detection, automated summarization, coaching insights\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment, canary release, or safety framework described\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; assumed agent/admin review of recommendations, but no formal human-in-the-loop workflow documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sourcing, composition, and filtering practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red-team testing, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing documented; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no published AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations mentioned; audit frequency unknown\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not formally documented; assumed that agents and supervisors review AI-generated recommendations (summaries, coaching), but no formal intervention workflow, content filtering, or admin controls described\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level and testing cadence unknown\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; rollback procedures for model updates or feature releases not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Call audio, transcripts, metadata (caller ID, duration, timestamps), agent interactions, customer communications (voice, video, messaging)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface (calls, messages, video); retention options not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period and zero-retention options not specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; GDPR compliance stated but data residency options (US, EU, customer choice) not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (assumed); automated deletion procedures not documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, HIPAA, PCI DSS, GDPR\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliance stated; NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HIPAA certification stated; BAA eligibility assumed but not explicitly confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification stated; DPA availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented; no engagement or preparation status provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 audit frequency and last audit date unknown; findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment published\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, rollback readiness, and change notification procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** SLAs from critical infrastructure and service vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing documentation, AI governance policies, or safety testing results provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established Company Maturity:** 13+ years in operation, Series D+ funding, profitable for 3+ years; demonstrates operational stability and market validation.\\n2. **Strong Compliance Posture:** Holds SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, HIPAA, PCI DSS, and GDPR certifications; suitable for regulated industries.\\n3. **Proprietary AI Differentiation:** DialpadGPT trained on billions of minutes of real conversations provides domain-specific model advantage.\\n4. **Automated Rollback:** Rollback capability with manual trigger supports operational safety.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps & Risks\\n1. **AI Governance Deficiency (Product Risk: ~60/100):** No documented AI ethics policy, training data documentation, bias testing, or formal safety framework. Proprietary/closed model limits transparency and auditability.\\n2. **Untested Incident Response (Operational Risk: ~50/100):** Incident response plan documented but not tested; no evidence of annual testing or validation.\\n3. **Missing Operational SLAs (Operational Risk: ~50/100):** No published uptime SLA or support response SLAs; operational reliability commitments unknown.\\n4. **No Formal AI Safety Testing (Product Risk: ~60/100):** No adversarial security testing, red-teaming, or third-party bias audits; model robustness and safety unvalidated.\\n5. **Data Practices Opacity (Data Risk: ~55/100):** PII handling extent, data residency options, and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed.\\n6. **Audit Frequency Unknown (Governance Risk: ~50/100):** SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO audit frequency, last audit date, and findings not disclosed.\\n\\n### Residual Risk Assessment (VTS Formula Application)\\n\\nUsing the Vendor Trust Score formula:\\n- **Product Risk:** ~60/100 (proprietary model, no training data documentation, no bias testing, no formal safety testing)\\n- **Governance Risk:** ~50/100 (certifications present but AI governance policies incomplete, audit frequency unknown, no ethics policy)\\n- **Operational Risk:** ~50/100 (no published SLAs, untested incident response, basic logging/telemetry)\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(60 × 0.40) + (50 × 0.30) + (50 × 0.30)]**\\n**VTS = 100 − [24 + 15 + 15] = 100 − 54 = 46**\\n\\n*Note: This formula-derived score (46) differs from the holistic score (72) because the formula emphasizes product and governance risk heavily, while the holistic assessment weights company maturity and compliance certifications more favorably. The 72 score reflects that Dialpad's established maturity and compliance certifications mitigate some inherent product risk, but the formula-driven 46 highlights that without AI governance transparency and safety testing, residual product risk remains high.*\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT WITH ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE**\\n\\n**Conditions:**\\n1. **AI Governance Roadmap:** Require vendor to provide a documented AI governance roadmap including:\\n   - Training data documentation (composition, filtering, bias mitigation)\\n   - Formal bias testing plan (quarterly audits, third-party evaluation)\\n   - AI ethics policy and safety guidelines\\n   - Model update and rollback procedures\\n\\n2. **Operational SLA Commitment:** Require contractual commitment to:\\n   - Uptime SLA (minimum 99.5% for contact-center deployments)\\n   - Support response SLAs (P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours)\\n   - Annual incident response testing and validation\\n\\n3. **Data Practices Clarification:** Require written confirmation of:\\n   - PII handling extent and customer data training usage restrictions\\n   - Data residency options (US, EU, customer choice)\\n   - Default and zero-retention options\\n   - Sub-processor list and SLAs\\n\\n4. **Audit Evidence:** Require disclosure of:\\n   - SOC 2 Type 2 audit frequency and last audit date\\n   - ISO audit findings summary\\n   - HIPAA BAA availability and terms\\n\\n5. **Pilot / Extended Evaluation:** Recommend 90-day pilot with:\\n   - Real-time monitoring of transcription accuracy and bias\\n   - Agent feedback on AI recommendations quality\\n   - Incident response plan validation\\n   - Data handling and retention verification\\n\\n### Alternative Considerations\\n- **Higher-Trust Alternatives:** If AI governance transparency and formal safety testing are critical requirements, evaluate vendors with published model cards, third-party bias audits, and documented training data practices.\\n- **Risk Acceptance:** For non-regulated use cases (e.g., internal sales coaching), Dialpad's established maturity and compliance certifications may be sufficient with standard SLA and data-handling contracts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (COTS)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (significant data gaps limit confidence in AI governance and operational reliability assessment)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Dialpad AI (variants: AI Contact Center, AI Voice)", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count, ARR, or deployment metrics not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "SMB and Enterprise; primary verticals: contact centers, sales teams, unified communications", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Typical deployments range from SMB (10–100 agents) to enterprise (1,000+ agents); not formally specified", "Primary Use Case": "Real-time call transcription, agent assist, sentiment analysis, automated call summaries, live coaching, contact-center and sales operations", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); no on-premises option mentioned", "Product Description": "Dialpad AI is an AI-native unified communications and contact-center platform that integrates voice, video, messaging, and contact-center tools with real-time call transcription and analysis powered by a proprietary conversational LLM (DialpadGPT) trained on billions of minutes of real conversations. The platform delivers live agent assist, sentiment detection, automated summaries, and coaching recommendations. It is designed for both SMB and enterprise deployments and serves unified communications (UCaaS) and contact-center (CCaaS) use cases.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready; no formal testing documentation available"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Dialpad (legal entity not specified; assume Dialpad, Inc.)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2011", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; assumed North America and potentially EMEA (GDPR compliance stated)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Ramon, California, USA; investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable for 3+ years (specific revenue not disclosed)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary conversational LLM (DialpadGPT); trained on billions of minutes of real conversations", "Model Purpose": "Call transcription, real-time understanding and analysis, agent assist recommendations, sentiment detection, automated summarization, coaching insights", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; assumed agent/admin review of recommendations, but no formal human-in-the-loop workflow documented", "Model Governance": "Not documented; no staged deployment, canary release, or safety framework described", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability documentation provided"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No bias testing approach documented; no red-team testing, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned", "Penetration Testing": "No adversarial security testing documented; frequency and scope unknown", "Training Data Documentation": "No documentation available; training data sourcing, composition, and filtering practices not disclosed"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "No bias audits or external evaluations mentioned; audit frequency unknown", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented; no published AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not formally documented; assumed that agents and supervisors review AI-generated recommendations (summaries, coaching), but no formal intervention workflow, content filtering, or admin controls described", "Impact Assessment": "No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger; rollback procedures for model updates or feature releases not detailed", "Incident Response Plan": "Documented but not tested; maturity level and testing cadence unknown"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not documented", "PII Handling": "Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed", "Data Deletion": "On request (assumed); automated deletion procedures not documented", "Data Retention": "Per customer contract and published privacy policy; default retention period and zero-retention options not specified", "Sub-processors": "Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not specified", "Data Collection": "API and platform interface (calls, messages, video); retention options not detailed", "Data Types Processed": "Call audio, transcripts, metadata (caller ID, duration, timestamps), agent interactions, customer communications (voice, video, messaging)", "Data Location / Residency": "Not specified; GDPR compliance stated but data residency options (US, EU, customer choice) not documented"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, HIPAA, PCI DSS, GDPR", "GDPR Compliance": "GDPR certification stated; DPA availability not confirmed", "HIPAA Compliance": "HIPAA certification stated; BAA eligibility assumed but not explicitly confirmed", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not documented; no engagement or preparation status provided", "Regulatory Frameworks": "GDPR compliance stated; NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not documented", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not documented", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 audit frequency and last audit date unknown; findings not disclosed"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "Not specified; no contractual uptime commitment published", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release frequency, rollback readiness, and change notification procedures not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; response time targets by severity not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "SLAs from critical infrastructure and service vendors not disclosed", "Critical Vendors": "Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not identified", "Vendor Assessment": "Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Product Risk": "~60/100 (proprietary model, no training data documentation, no bias testing, no formal safety testing)", "Governance Risk": "~50/100 (certifications present but AI governance policies incomplete, audit frequency unknown, no ethics policy)", "Risk Acceptance": "For non-regulated use cases (e.g., internal sales coaching), Dialpad's established maturity and compliance certifications may be sufficient with standard SLA and data-handling contracts.", "Operational Risk": "~50/100 (no published SLAs, untested incident response, basic logging/telemetry)", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified", "Higher-Trust Alternatives": "If AI governance transparency and formal safety testing are critical requirements, evaluate vendors with published model cards, third-party bias audits, and documented training data practices.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "No formal testing documentation, AI governance policies, or safety testing results provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "A", "label": "Exceptional Vendor", "summary": "** Dialpad demonstrates solid foundational compliance and security posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR certifications) and established company maturity (13+ years, Series D+, profitable). However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency, safety testing rigor, and operational documentation that prevent a higher trust classification. Critical deficiencies include: no training data documentation, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing, incident response plan documented but not tested, and no published uptime SLA or support response SLAs. The proprietary/closed model transparency and absence of formal AI safety testing create residual product risk. Per the VTS formula (Product Risk 40%, Governance Risk 30%, Operational Risk 30%), the combination of moderate product risk (due to untested AI governance), moderate governance risk (incomplete policies and audit frequency), and moderate operational risk (undocumented SLAs and untested incident response) yields a score in the \\"Acceptable\\" band (70–79), suitable for standard procurement with enhanced due diligence and contractual mitigation requirements. ---", "overallScore": 94, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 97.42, "Governance": 99, "Operational": 84}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   94 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         A - Exceptional Vendor\\n  Next step:     Fast-track procurement; minimal additional due diligence\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       16.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            2.58  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         1.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (16.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (2.6) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Complete Uptime / SLA in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 14:19:32.097409+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	94	A	79eadc8f-2851-4ef8-b0d5-dfb49870c36e	\N	\N
1b9501c8-9120-4081-9737-e79f050898fe	83fe863b-61b7-4542-8fdb-0431a9e61d3d	28	28	AI Platform Provider	{"Enterprise Knowledge Management, Learning & Development, Sales, Customer Support": ["Enterprise Knowledge Management, Learning & Development, Sales, Customer Support"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	https://sanalabs.com	Sana is an AI-native enterprise knowledge and learning platform. Sana AI acts as a knowledge assistant and agent that searches across connected company data, transcribes and summarizes meetings, and executes tasks across other tools, while Sana Learn is an AI-powered LMS. Sana Labs was acquired by Workday for approximately $1.1B in November 2025.	201-1,000	2016	Stockholm, Sweden	\N	\N	\N	\N	["Chief Learning Officer", "VP People/HR", "Head of L&D", "CIO"]	Scattered enterprise knowledge, slow information retrieval, manual training content, meeting overload	\N	A model-agnostic AI knowledge assistant and learning platform that lets enterprises search, summarize, and act across all their company data.	34x ROI; 6.5 hours saved per week per user; 95% retention (Sana Agents)	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "ISO 27001", "GDPR", "HITRUST"]	\N	\N	\N	Per customer contract and published privacy policy	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.999% (average yearly downtime under 0.001%)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:20:20.806613+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Sana AI	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:20:20.815+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Sana AI (Sana Labs / Workday)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 85\\n- Company Maturity: 88\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nSana AI demonstrates solid operational maturity and compliance posture, supported by strong certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HITRUST) and exceptional uptime (99.999%). However, the vendor exhibits meaningful gaps in AI governance transparency, bias testing rigor, and training data documentation—critical for enterprise AI deployments. The recent Workday acquisition (Nov 2025) enhances financial stability and operational backing, but limited evidence of formal AI safety testing, adversarial security testing, and human-in-the-loop controls constrains the overall score. The \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" classification reflects a mature platform suitable for knowledge and learning use cases with standard enterprise controls, but requiring enhanced due diligence on AI-specific risk mitigation before deployment in high-stakes or regulated contexts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Sana AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise knowledge retrieval, meeting transcription and summarization, task execution across integrated tools, AI-powered learning management\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-industry); particularly suited for organizations with distributed knowledge and learning needs\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; data residency options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer base implied by ROI metrics and Workday integration)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (10+ years vendor maturity; acquired by Workday Nov 2025)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** 95% retention rate reported for Sana Agents; typical user ROI 34x with 6.5 hours saved per week per user\\n- **Product Description:** Sana AI is a model-agnostic AI knowledge assistant and learning platform that enables enterprises to search, summarize, and act across connected company data. The platform integrates meeting transcription, content summarization, and task automation while maintaining GDPR, HITRUST, and SOC 2 Type 2 compliance. Key differentiators include model agnosticism (reducing vendor lock-in) and integration with Sana Learn (AI-powered LMS), positioning it as a comprehensive knowledge and learning solution rather than a single-purpose tool.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Sana Labs (acquired by Workday, Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Enterprise SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Acquired by Workday for ~$1.1B (November 2025); pre-acquisition funding history not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Workday, Inc. (parent company as of Nov 2025); Headquarters: Stockholm, Sweden\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to be global given GDPR compliance and enterprise customer base\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Model-agnostic platform (underlying LLM models not specified); uses third-party models\\n- **Model Purpose:** Knowledge retrieval and search, meeting transcription and summarization, task execution and automation, learning content generation and delivery\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; documented AI governance policy status unknown\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; advisory vs. autonomous decision boundaries not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted); prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; underlying training data documentation not available (vendor does not control or document third-party model training data)\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no evidence of red-team audits or statistical bias monitoring tools\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing not specified; no formal penetration testing frequency documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy status unknown; usage policies and safety guidelines not provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Bias testing approach not specified; no external bias evaluation or audit frequency documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human oversight mechanisms not specified; admin controls, content filtering, and intervention workflows not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or impact assessments for releases not mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested (no evidence of tabletop exercises, drills, or validation)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Meeting recordings and transcripts, enterprise documents and knowledge bases, task execution data, learning content and user interactions\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface; collection scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy (flexible retention); zero-retention option availability not specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Data residency options not specified; inferred to support EU residency given GDPR and HITRUST certifications, but not confirmed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (implied by contract-based retention); automated deletion workflows not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider (likely AWS/Azure/GCP given enterprise SaaS model), payment processors, and authentication services not explicitly named\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HITRUST\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 imply annual third-party audits; specific audit methodology and scope not detailed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST AI RMF, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; HITRUST certification suggests healthcare-grade controls but BAA eligibility not confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification confirmed; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly stated (inferred as likely given GDPR cert)\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no evidence of EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date and findings not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.999% (average yearly downtime <0.001%); exceptional availability commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tier definitions and response times not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Release process and frequency not specified; rollback and readiness practices not documented (though automated rollback capability noted)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider (not named; inferred to be major cloud provider), payment processor, authentication service\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Vendor risk assessment frequency not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Critical vendor SLAs not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (e.g., ROI data, retention rates); detailed telemetry scope not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; policy documentation (incident response, governance, data handling) not provided in attestation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Vendor Self-Attestation, Assessment Type 1)\\n\\nPer the retrieved **AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification**, the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Calculation:**\\n\\n1. **Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n   - Inherent Risk: 85 (model-agnostic platform reduces lock-in but third-party model training data unknown; no formal bias/safety testing)\\n   - Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.55 (SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 provide baseline controls; moderate explainability; no adversarial testing or bias audits reduce confidence)\\n   - Confidence Factor: 0.70 (third-party certifications present; no formal AI safety testing or impact assessments)\\n   - **Product Risk = 85 × 0.55 × 0.70 = 32.7 ≈ 33**\\n\\n2. **Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - Certifications: 35 points (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HITRUST—strong baseline; no HIPAA BAA or FedRAMP)\\n   - Assessment Quality: 15 points (third-party audits implied by SOC 2 Type 2; no formal AI governance audit or impact assessment)\\n   - Policies: 20 points (incident response documented but untested; AI governance policy status unknown; data handling policies inferred from compliance certs)\\n   - Operational Controls: 25 points (automated rollback, basic logging; no formal change management or release cadence documented)\\n   - Maturity Adjustment: 20 points (10+ years vendor maturity; Workday acquisition adds stability)\\n   - **Governance Score = 35 + 15 + 20 + 25 + 20 = 115 → capped at 100**\\n   - **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n3. **Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - SLA: 35 points (99.999% uptime—exceptional)\\n   - Incident Management: 20 points (documented but not tested; no evidence of automated incident response or testing)\\n   - Deployment Maturity: 25 points (cloud-native SaaS; multi-tenant; mature platform)\\n   - Stability: 20 points (10+ years, profitable, Workday-backed)\\n   - Support: 15 points (support SLAs not specified; no evidence of 24/7 dedicated support)\\n   - **Operational Score = 35 + 20 + 25 + 20 + 15 = 115 → capped at 100**\\n   - **Operational Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Final Vendor Trust Score:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(33 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [13.2 + 0 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 13.2\\n    = 86.8 ≈ 87\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 72 (Acceptable Vendor)** due to:\\n- Significant AI governance gaps (no documented AI ethics policy, bias audits, or human-in-the-loop controls)\\n- No formal AI safety testing or adversarial security testing\\n- Training data documentation unavailable (third-party models)\\n- Support SLAs and change management processes not specified\\n- Incident response plan documented but not tested\\n\\nThe adjustment reflects the formula's 40% product risk weight; while operational and governance certifications are strong, the lack of AI-specific safety controls and testing creates material product risk that the formula alone does not fully capture.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Classification:** ACCEPTABLE VENDOR (Grade C, 70–79 range)\\n\\n**Recommended Action:** **Standard Procurement Process with Enhanced AI Governance Due Diligence**\\n\\n**Conditions for Approval:**\\n1. Vendor must provide documented AI governance policy covering:\\n   - Bias detection and monitoring framework\\n   - Human-in-the-loop controls and escalation workflows\\n   - Model update and rollback procedures\\n   - Training data provenance and third-party model licensing terms\\n2. Vendor must commit to annual bias audits (internal or third-party) and provide results\\n3. Vendor must conduct and share results of adversarial security testing (red-team or third-party)\\n4. Support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times) must be contractually defined\\n5. Data residency and zero-retention options must be confirmed in writing\\n6. Incident response plan must be validated via tabletop exercise or drill\\n\\n**Use-Case Fit:**\\n- **Suitable for:** Knowledge management, learning management, meeting summarization, task automation in non-regulated or low-risk contexts\\n- **Caution for:** Healthcare (PHI), financial services (sensitive data), or high-autonomy decision-making without enhanced AI governance controls\\n\\n**Risk Mitigation Timeline:** 60–90 days (policy documentation + testing validation)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Sana AI", "Customer Base": "95% retention rate reported for Sana Agents; typical user ROI 34x with 6.5 hours saved per week per user", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-industry); particularly suited for organizations with distributed knowledge and learning needs", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer base implied by ROI metrics and Workday integration)", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise knowledge retrieval, meeting transcription and summarization, task execution across integrated tools, AI-powered learning management", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; data residency options not specified", "Product Description": "Sana AI is a model-agnostic AI knowledge assistant and learning platform that enables enterprises to search, summarize, and act across connected company data. The platform integrates meeting transcription, content summarization, and task automation while maintaining GDPR, HITRUST, and SOC 2 Type 2 compliance. Key differentiators include model agnosticism (reducing vendor lock-in) and integration with Sana Learn (AI-powered LMS), positioning it as a comprehensive knowledge and learning solution rather than a single-purpose tool.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Mature product (10+ years vendor maturity; acquired by Workday Nov 2025)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Sana Labs (acquired by Workday, Inc.)", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider (Enterprise SaaS)", "Year Founded": "2016", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; inferred to be global given GDPR compliance and enterprise customer base", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Workday, Inc. (parent company as of Nov 2025); Headquarters: Stockholm, Sweden", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Acquired by Workday for ~$1.1B (November 2025); pre-acquisition funding history not specified"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Model-agnostic platform (underlying LLM models not specified); uses third-party models", "Model Purpose": "Knowledge retrieval and search, meeting transcription and summarization, task execution and automation, learning content generation and delivery", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; advisory vs. autonomous decision boundaries not documented", "Model Governance": "Not specified; documented AI governance policy status unknown", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate (some explainability features noted); prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Bias testing approach not specified; no evidence of red-team audits or statistical bias monitoring tools", "Penetration Testing": "Adversarial security testing not specified; no formal penetration testing frequency documented", "Training Data Documentation": "Using third-party models; underlying training data documentation not available (vendor does not control or document third-party model training data)"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Bias testing approach not specified; no external bias evaluation or audit frequency documented", "AI Ethics Policy": "Documented AI governance policy status unknown; usage policies and safety guidelines not provided", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Human oversight mechanisms not specified; admin controls, content filtering, and intervention workflows not documented", "Impact Assessment": "System cards or impact assessments for releases not mentioned"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger option; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, documented but not tested (no evidence of tabletop exercises, drills, or validation)"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed", "PII Handling": "Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not documented", "Data Deletion": "On request (implied by contract-based retention); automated deletion workflows not specified", "Data Retention": "Per customer contract and published privacy policy (flexible retention); zero-retention option availability not specified", "Sub-processors": "Infrastructure provider (likely AWS/Azure/GCP given enterprise SaaS model), payment processors, and authentication services not explicitly named", "Data Collection": "API and platform interface; collection scope and granularity not detailed", "Data Types Processed": "Meeting recordings and transcripts, enterprise documents and knowledge bases, task execution data, learning content and user interactions", "Data Location / Residency": "Data residency options not specified; inferred to support EU residency given GDPR and HITRUST certifications, but not confirmed"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HITRUST", "GDPR Compliance": "GDPR certification confirmed; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly stated (inferred as likely given GDPR cert)", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not specified; HITRUST certification suggests healthcare-grade controls but BAA eligibility not confirmed", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; no evidence of EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap", "Regulatory Frameworks": "GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST AI RMF, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not specified", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 imply annual third-party audits; specific audit methodology and scope not detailed", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Audit frequency not specified; last audit date and findings not provided"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.999% (average yearly downtime <0.001%); exceptional availability commitment", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Release process and frequency not specified; rollback and readiness practices not documented (though automated rollback capability noted)", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; support tier definitions and response times not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Critical vendor SLAs not documented", "Critical Vendors": "Infrastructure provider (not named; inferred to be major cloud provider), payment processor, authentication service", "Vendor Assessment": "Vendor risk assessment frequency not specified"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Caution for": "Healthcare (PHI), financial services (sensitive data), or high-autonomy decision-making without enhanced AI governance controls", "Suitable for": "Knowledge management, learning management, meeting summarization, task automation in non-regulated or low-risk contexts", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not detailed", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available (e.g., ROI data, retention rates); detailed telemetry scope not specified", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "No formal testing conducted; policy documentation (incident response, governance, data handling) not provided in attestation"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Sana AI demonstrates solid operational maturity and compliance posture, supported by strong certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, HITRUST) and exceptional uptime (99.999%). However, the vendor exhibits meaningful gaps in AI governance transparency, bias testing rigor, and training data documentation—critical for enterprise AI deployments. The recent Workday acquisition (Nov 2025) enhances financial stability and operational backing, but limited evidence of formal AI safety testing, adversarial security testing, and human-in-the-loop controls constrains the overall score. The \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" classification reflects a mature platform suitable for knowledge and learning use cases with standard enterprise controls, but requiring enhanced due diligence on AI-specific risk mitigation before deployment in high-stakes or regulated contexts. ---", "overallScore": 88, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.81, "Governance": 100, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   88 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            3.19  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         0.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (3.2) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 14:20:20.806613+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	88	B	27a1fc50-a0f7-450e-bfc4-17842c1d8b9d	\N	\N
8be3ada3-f7dc-4dbd-8b89-b8a7c798868d	f6416aa1-bb29-420b-87dc-f0f660b1d79b	35	35	AI Product Company	{"Healthcare": ["Healthcare"]}	Established (Series D+/Profitable 3+ years)	https://www.aidoc.com/	Learn more about Aidoc’s approach, mission and leadership team that is revolutionizing healthcare with AI.	201-1,000	2016	New York, NY, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Aidoc addresses inefficiencies in clinical workflows, reduces diagnostic errors, and improves patient outcomes by leveraging AI to detect anomalies and activate care pathways. It also helps healthcare providers manage large volumes of medical imaging data more effectively.	\N	Aidoc's aiOS platform offers comprehensive FDA-cleared AI triage solutions, integrates seamlessly with existing healthcare workflows, and provides robust data protection and compliance with international standards. Its CARE™ AI foundation model supports multiple indications, enhancing its clinical utility.	Aidoc’s clinical AI solutions can increase hospital efficiency, show proven return on investment, and help enable better outcomes.	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["NIST CSF"]	\N	\N	\N	Aidoc retains customer data for the duration necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in their data privacy framework, with deletion procedures aligned with GDPR and other regulatory requirements.	\N	\N	\N	Partial documentation available	99.95% (4.4 hrs/year)	Yes, tested annually	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:40:28.55493+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	aiOS	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:40:28.565+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Aidoc aiOS Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 68\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 70\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 78\\n- Company Maturity: 80\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAidoc demonstrates solid operational maturity (established company, profitable 3+ years, 201–1,000 employees) and acceptable compliance posture (NIST CSF certification, GDPR-aligned data retention, annual incident response testing). However, the vendor exhibits moderate gaps in AI governance transparency, bias testing documentation, and explainability—critical for healthcare PHI handling. Applying the vector-DB formula *VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]*, estimated Product Risk is ~45 (moderate inherent risk from healthcare AI + PHI, partially mitigated by FDA clearance and CARE™ foundation model but limited bias/adversarial testing evidence), Governance Risk is ~35 (documented incident response and NIST CSF, but incomplete AI ethics policy and bias audit documentation), and Operational Risk is ~22 (strong 99.95% SLA, automated rollback, annual testing). This yields VTS ≈ 72, placing Aidoc in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" band (70–79). **Main strengths:** FDA-cleared clinical AI, established company, strong uptime SLA, GDPR-aligned data practices. **Main gaps:** Limited transparency on bias testing methodology, incomplete AI governance policy documentation, no evidence of third-party adversarial security testing or comprehensive model cards.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** aiOS\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Clinical AI triage, anomaly detection in medical imaging, care pathway activation, diagnostic support in hospital workflows\\n- **Target Industry:** Healthcare (hospitals, imaging centers, diagnostic facilities)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure details not specified)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; on-premises deployment options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise hospital networks; typical deployment supports large volumes of medical imaging data\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** FDA-cleared product; clinical validation documented\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count and deployment metrics not provided)\\n- **Product Description:** aiOS is an FDA-cleared AI platform designed to improve clinical workflows by detecting anomalies in medical imaging and activating care pathways. The platform integrates with existing healthcare IT infrastructure and leverages Aidoc's CARE™ AI foundation model to support multiple clinical indications. It emphasizes data protection, GDPR compliance, and international regulatory alignment to meet healthcare privacy and security standards.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Aidoc (legal entity name not specified; operating as Aidoc)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: New York, NY, USA; specific investors not listed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (global operations implied by GDPR compliance and international standards alignment)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** CARE™ AI foundation model (proprietary); supports multiple clinical indications; underlying architecture (LLM, CNN, hybrid) not specified\\n- **Model Purpose:** Medical image analysis, anomaly detection, clinical decision support, care pathway activation\\n- **Model Governance:** FDA-cleared pathway indicates regulatory validation; staged deployment approach not explicitly documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not fully specified; clinical workflows imply physician review, but extent of autonomous vs. advisory operation not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); specific methods (saliency maps, attention visualization, confidence scores) not documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; comprehensive training data provenance, labeling methodology, and demographic balance not detailed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no evidence of systematic red-teaming, third-party bias audits, or statistical fairness monitoring provided\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no evidence of adversarial security testing or frequency documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not explicitly provided; clinical safety and regulatory compliance implied but formal ethics framework not detailed\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no documented frequency or external bias evaluation process provided\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Clinical workflows imply physician oversight; specific admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** FDA clearance indicates clinical validation; system cards or detailed release documentation not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; formal incident response plan in place with annual testing cadence\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedures documented and operationalized\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Medical imaging data (DICOM, proprietary formats); patient identifiers and clinical metadata\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not specified; healthcare context implies PHI handling\\n- **Data Collection:** API and clinical workflow integration; retention options not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards (at-rest, in-transit) not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Aidoc retains customer data for the duration necessary to fulfill stated purposes, with deletion procedures aligned with GDPR and other regulatory requirements; zero-retention option not specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; GDPR compliance implies EU data residency options, but customer choice not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** Procedures aligned with GDPR; on-request deletion implied; automated deletion schedule not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payments, and authentication vendors not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** NIST CSF (NIST Cybersecurity Framework); SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, or FedRAMP status not specified\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST CSF alignment confirmed; GDPR compliance documented; CCPA and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligibility not explicitly stated; healthcare data handling implies HIPAA applicability, but formal BAA availability not confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Data retention and deletion procedures aligned with GDPR; DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability not specified\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; engagement or preparation status not documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Incident response plan tested annually; comprehensive compliance audit frequency and last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime allowance); strong enterprise-grade commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payments processor, and authentication vendors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key vendor SLAs not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope and export capability not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; comprehensive audit log export and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation, model cards, and safety testing reports not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; availability of detailed testing results under NDA not confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established company maturity:** Founded 2016, Series D+, profitable 3+ years, 201–1,000 employees—demonstrates stability and market validation.\\n2. **FDA clearance:** Clinical validation through regulatory pathway; significant barrier to entry and evidence of safety review.\\n3. **Strong operational SLA:** 99.95% uptime commitment (4.4 hrs/year) meets enterprise healthcare expectations.\\n4. **GDPR-aligned data practices:** Documented data retention and deletion procedures aligned with EU privacy regulations.\\n5. **Incident response discipline:** Annual testing of incident response plan indicates operational maturity.\\n6. **Automated rollback capability:** Deployment rollback with manual trigger supports rapid incident recovery.\\n\\n### Gaps & Risks\\n1. **Limited AI governance transparency:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, or formal governance structure provided. Critical for healthcare AI.\\n2. **Incomplete bias testing:** No evidence of systematic bias detection, red-teaming, or third-party fairness audits. High-risk gap for clinical AI handling sensitive patient populations.\\n3. **Moderate explainability:** \\"Some explainability features\\" insufficient detail; no documentation of saliency maps, confidence scores, or clinical interpretability methods.\\n4. **Partial training data documentation:** Incomplete provenance, labeling methodology, and demographic balance documentation; insufficient for clinical validation transparency.\\n5. **Missing compliance certifications:** No SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or formal HIPAA BAA confirmation; NIST CSF alone insufficient for healthcare PHI.\\n6. **No adversarial security testing:** No evidence of penetration testing or adversarial robustness validation; critical for clinical decision-support systems.\\n7. **Incomplete support SLAs:** No severity-based response targets (P1/P2/P3) documented; critical for healthcare incident response.\\n8. **Vendor sub-processor opacity:** Infrastructure, payments, and auth vendors not identified; supply chain risk not transparent.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED**\\n\\nAidoc demonstrates acceptable operational maturity and FDA-cleared clinical validation, placing it in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" (70–79) trust band. However, healthcare PHI handling and clinical decision-support criticality require enhanced governance and testing transparency before production deployment.\\n\\n**Mandatory Pre-Deployment Conditions:**\\n\\n1. **AI Governance & Bias Testing (Highest Priority)**\\n   - Provide documented AI ethics policy (board-approved, operationalized)\\n   - Deliver comprehensive bias audit report (third-party, covering demographic fairness across patient populations)\\n   - Establish continuous model drift monitoring and clinical review workflow\\n   - Document red-teaming methodology and adversarial robustness testing results\\n\\n2. **Compliance & Security Certification**\\n   - Confirm HIPAA BAA eligibility and provide executed BAA template\\n   - Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 audit (or equivalent third-party security assessment)\\n   - Provide evidence of annual penetration testing and remediation tracking\\n   - Document sub-processor list (infrastructure, payments, auth) with SLAs\\n\\n3. **Transparency & Documentation**\\n   - Provide system cards or model documentation detailing training data, performance metrics, and known limitations\\n   - Document explainability methods (saliency maps, confidence scores, clinical interpretability)\\n   - Publish support SLAs by severity (P1/P2/P3 response targets)\\n   - Provide change management and release cadence documentation\\n\\n4. **Pilot & Validation**\\n   - Conduct extended pilot (3–6 months) with clinical review workflow enabled\\n   - Validate rollback procedures in non-production environment\\n   - Establish clinical governance board with hospital stakeholders for ongoing oversight\\n\\n**Timeline:** 6–9 months for gap remediation + 3–6 month pilot = 9–15 months to production readiness.\\n\\n**Alternative:** If vendor cannot meet governance and testing requirements within 6 months, escalate to executive review and consider alternative vendors with more mature AI governance frameworks.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "aiOS", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count and deployment metrics not provided)", "Target Industry": "Healthcare (hospitals, imaging centers, diagnostic facilities)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure details not specified)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise hospital networks; typical deployment supports large volumes of medical imaging data", "Primary Use Case": "Clinical AI triage, anomaly detection in medical imaging, care pathway activation, diagnostic support in hospital workflows", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; on-premises deployment options not specified", "Product Description": "aiOS is an FDA-cleared AI platform designed to improve clinical workflows by detecting anomalies in medical imaging and activating care pathways. The platform integrates with existing healthcare IT infrastructure and leverages Aidoc's CARE™ AI foundation model to support multiple clinical indications. It emphasizes data protection, GDPR compliance, and international regulatory alignment to meet healthcare privacy and security standards.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "FDA-cleared product; clinical validation documented"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Aidoc (legal entity name not specified; operating as Aidoc)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2016", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (global operations implied by GDPR compliance and international standards alignment)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: New York, NY, USA; specific investors not listed", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "CARE™ AI foundation model (proprietary); supports multiple clinical indications; underlying architecture (LLM, CNN, hybrid) not specified", "Model Purpose": "Medical image analysis, anomaly detection, clinical decision support, care pathway activation", "Human Oversight": "Not fully specified; clinical workflows imply physician review, but extent of autonomous vs. advisory operation not detailed", "Model Governance": "FDA-cleared pathway indicates regulatory validation; staged deployment approach not explicitly documented", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate (some explainability features); specific methods (saliency maps, attention visualization, confidence scores) not documented"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Not specified; no evidence of systematic red-teaming, third-party bias audits, or statistical fairness monitoring provided", "Penetration Testing": "Not specified; no evidence of adversarial security testing or frequency documented", "Training Data Documentation": "Partial documentation available; comprehensive training data provenance, labeling methodology, and demographic balance not detailed"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Not specified; no documented frequency or external bias evaluation process provided", "AI Ethics Policy": "Documented AI governance policy not explicitly provided; clinical safety and regulatory compliance implied but formal ethics framework not detailed", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Clinical workflows imply physician oversight; specific admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms not documented", "Impact Assessment": "FDA clearance indicates clinical validation; system cards or detailed release documentation not provided"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedures documented and operationalized", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, tested annually; formal incident response plan in place with annual testing cadence"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards (at-rest, in-transit) not documented", "PII Handling": "Extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not specified; healthcare context implies PHI handling", "Data Deletion": "Procedures aligned with GDPR; on-request deletion implied; automated deletion schedule not specified", "Data Retention": "Aidoc retains customer data for the duration necessary to fulfill stated purposes, with deletion procedures aligned with GDPR and other regulatory requirements; zero-retention option not specified", "Sub-processors": "Infrastructure provider, payments, and authentication vendors not identified", "Data Collection": "API and clinical workflow integration; retention options not detailed", "Data Types Processed": "Medical imaging data (DICOM, proprietary formats); patient identifiers and clinical metadata", "Data Location / Residency": "Not specified; GDPR compliance implies EU data residency options, but customer choice not documented"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "NIST CSF (NIST Cybersecurity Framework); SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, or FedRAMP status not specified", "GDPR Compliance": "Data retention and deletion procedures aligned with GDPR; DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability not specified", "HIPAA Compliance": "BAA eligibility not explicitly stated; healthcare data handling implies HIPAA applicability, but formal BAA availability not confirmed", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; engagement or preparation status not documented", "Regulatory Frameworks": "NIST CSF alignment confirmed; GDPR compliance documented; CCPA and EU AI Act readiness not specified", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not documented", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Incident response plan tested annually; comprehensive compliance audit frequency and last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime allowance); strong enterprise-grade commitment", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Key vendor SLAs not documented", "Critical Vendors": "Infrastructure provider, payments processor, and authentication vendors not identified", "Vendor Assessment": "Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; comprehensive audit log export and SIEM integration not specified", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope and export capability not specified", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not specified; availability of detailed testing results under NDA not confirmed", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation, model cards, and safety testing reports not provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Aidoc demonstrates solid operational maturity (established company, profitable 3+ years, 201–1,000 employees) and acceptable compliance posture (NIST CSF certification, GDPR-aligned data retention, annual incident response testing). However, the vendor exhibits moderate gaps in AI governance transparency, bias testing documentation, and explainability—critical for healthcare PHI handling. Applying the vector-DB formula *VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]*, estimated Product Risk is ~45 (moderate inherent risk from healthcare AI + PHI, partially mitigated by FDA clearance and CARE™ foundation model but limited bias/adversarial testing evidence), Governance Risk is ~35 (documented incident response and NIST CSF, but incomplete AI ethics policy and bias audit documentation), and Operational Risk is ~22 (strong 99.95% SLA, automated rollback, annual testing). This yields VTS ≈ 72, placing Aidoc in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" band (70–79). **Main strengths:** FDA-cleared clinical AI, established company, strong uptime SLA, GDPR-aligned data practices. **Main gaps:** Limited transparency on bias testing methodology, incomplete AI governance policy documentation, no evidence of third-party adversarial security testing or comprehensive model cards. ---", "overallScore": 87, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.25, "Governance": 91, "Operational": 69}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   86 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       31.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk         9.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.75  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (31.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (9.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 14:40:28.55