be7ba807-bd33-4b4b-aaee-7abe17026701	a455e3a9-358b-4729-a2ea-6967d6fe56a2	33	33	AI Product Company	{"Healthcare": ["Healthcare"]}	Growth (Series B/C)	https://abridge.com/	Our mission is to power deeper understanding in healthcare through purpose-built AI.	201-1,000	2018	San Francisco, California, United States	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "Chief Risk Officer"]	“When documentation burden pushes clinicians toward burnout and early retirement, our communities feel it directly. Abridge is helping our clinicians stay focused on patients instead of paperwork.”	\N	Abridge offers deep native integration into Epic and expanding support for athenahealth, ensuring seamless workflow integration. The platform automatically deletes audio recordings and transcripts after 30 days, enhancing data privacy. Abridge's AI transforms patient-clinician conversations into structured clinical notes in real-time, significantly reducing documentation burden.	“Abridge is expanding access to care. The freed-up time has increased efficiency for the entire care team to where we've dropped responses to patient calls down to seconds.” [Corroborated by 26 evidence point(s): Professional Fulfillment Improvement: 53%; Decrease in After-Hours Documentation: 60%; Decrease in Cognitive Load: 51%; wRVU Increase: 11%; HCC Diagnoses Increase: 14%]	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "SOC 2 Type 1", "HIPAA BAA", "CCPA Compliant"]	\N	\N	["US only"]	Audio recordings and transcripts are automatically deleted after 30 days. The final clinical note remains in the medical record.	\N	\N	\N	Partial documentation available	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:38:29.965654+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Abridge Ambient Documentation	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:38:29.972+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Abridge Ambient Documentation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 75\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 68\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAbridge demonstrates solid compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 1/2, HIPAA BAA, CCPA) and strong data privacy practices (30-day auto-deletion of recordings/transcripts), positioning it as an acceptable vendor for healthcare PHI handling. However, the score is constrained by moderate AI governance maturity (undocumented bias testing, no third-party AI ethics audit, incident response plan not tested), growth-stage company profile (Series B/C, 6 years old), and operational gaps (no published P1/P2/P3 support SLAs, limited incident management evidence). The vendor's core strength—seamless Epic integration and documented ROI—is offset by incomplete AI safety documentation and testing transparency. Recommendation: **Acceptable for deployment with contractual conditions requiring documented bias testing, annual third-party AI audit, and tested incident response plan before go-live.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Abridge Ambient Documentation\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Real-time clinical documentation automation; transforms patient-clinician conversations into structured clinical notes; reduces clinician documentation burden\\n- **Target Industry:** Healthcare (ambulatory care, primary care, specialty practices)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (Epic and athenahealth integration)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; native Epic integration; expanding athenahealth support\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployment: ambulatory care settings (clinician-facing, patient-clinician interaction capture)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C company); production-deployed with 26 corroborated evidence points on clinical outcomes\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (evidence of multiple healthcare system deployments with documented ROI metrics)\\n- **Product Description:** Abridge Ambient Documentation is a purpose-built healthcare AI platform that captures and transcribes patient-clinician conversations in real-time, automatically generating structured clinical notes integrated directly into Epic and athenahealth EHRs. The platform prioritizes data privacy by automatically deleting audio recordings and transcripts after 30 days while retaining final clinical notes in the medical record. Documented clinical outcomes include 53% improvement in professional fulfillment, 60% reduction in after-hours documentation, and 11% wRVU increase, demonstrating measurable ROI for healthcare organizations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Abridge (legal entity name not specified; operating as Abridge)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (healthcare-focused)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2018\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, California, United States; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** United States (primary); data residency: US only\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Custom-trained healthcare AI model (specific architecture not disclosed); optimized for clinical conversation understanding and note generation\\n- **Model Purpose:** Speech-to-text transcription, clinical entity extraction, structured note generation (understanding + generation); real-time processing of patient-clinician conversations\\n- **Model Governance:** Not fully documented; no published staged deployment framework or formal AI governance policy disclosed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Clinician review of generated notes (implicit in EHR workflow); no explicit monitoring alerts or audit trail for AI decision confidence disclosed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate transparency; some explainability features present (note generation rationale not detailed); no published prompt-level control or citation mechanism disclosed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; specific training dataset composition, size, and healthcare domain coverage not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no evidence of red-team testing, third-party bias audits, or statistical fairness monitoring disclosed; no published bias testing results\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not disclosed; mission statement emphasizes clinician focus and patient care, but formal ethics framework not published\\n- **Bias Audits:** No evidence of formal bias audit program; frequency and external evaluation not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Clinician review of generated notes embedded in EHR workflow; no explicit admin controls for content filtering, confidence thresholds, or intervention workflows disclosed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No published system cards or release impact assessments disclosed; clinical outcome metrics available (ROI evidence) but formal AI impact documentation not evident\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level unclear (basic runbook vs. annual testing unknown)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (moderate maturity; not instant automated rollback)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Audio recordings of patient-clinician conversations; transcripts; clinical notes; patient identifiers (name, MRN, demographics embedded in conversations)\\n- **PII Handling:** High-sensitivity data (PHI under HIPAA); audio and transcripts contain patient identifiers; no explicit statement on whether customer data is used for model training or improvement\\n- **Data Collection:** Real-time capture via ambient microphone/audio interface integrated into clinical workflow; API integration with Epic and athenahealth\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure (specific provider not disclosed); encryption status not explicitly stated\\n- **Data Retention:** **Audio recordings and transcripts automatically deleted after 30 days** (strong privacy practice); final clinical note retained in medical record per standard EHR retention policies\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only; no EU or customer-choice residency options\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion of recordings/transcripts after 30 days; on-request deletion capability not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not disclosed; Epic and athenahealth are integration partners (not sub-processors); payment processor not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - SOC 2 Type 1 ✓\\n  - HIPAA BAA eligible ✓\\n  - CCPA Compliant ✓\\n  \\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit (third-party audit implied by certification); audit frequency and last audit date not disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - HIPAA: BAA available\\n  - CCPA: Compliant\\n  - GDPR: No explicit compliance statement; US-only data residency limits GDPR applicability\\n  - NIST: No explicit NIST alignment disclosed\\n  - EU AI Act: No readiness statement disclosed\\n  \\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; 30-day auto-deletion of recordings/transcripts aligns with HIPAA minimum necessary principle\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not explicitly addressed; US-only data residency may limit GDPR compliance for EU customer data\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation statement disclosed\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Audit frequency: Not specified (SOC 2 Type 2 typically annual; frequency not confirmed)\\n  - Last audit date: Not disclosed\\n  - Audit findings: Not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance); contractual commitment status not explicitly confirmed\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support structure and response targets unknown\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing process, and rollback readiness practices not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** \\n  - Infrastructure provider: Not disclosed\\n  - EHR integration partners: Epic, athenahealth (integration partners, not sub-processors)\\n  - Payment processor: Not disclosed\\n  \\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of sub-processors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Epic and athenahealth SLAs not specified; infrastructure provider SLAs unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope limited (specific metrics not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** \\n  - Clinical outcome evidence: 26 corroborated evidence points (Professional Fulfillment +53%, After-Hours Documentation -60%, Cognitive Load -51%, wRVU +11%, HCC Diagnoses +14%)\\n  - Testing results available: Yes (specific results not disclosed; likely under NDA)\\n  - Policy documentation: Partial (data retention policy clear; AI governance policy not published)\\n  \\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, available under NDA; bias testing, adversarial testing, and clinical validation results not publicly disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (Vendor Self-Attestation Formula)\\n\\nApplied **VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85 (high due to PHI + real-time clinical decision support + audio capture)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.68 (strong data retention policy, SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA; gaps in bias testing and AI governance documentation)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.75 (SOC 2 audit + clinical outcome evidence; limited AI safety transparency)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.68) × 0.75 = 20.4 ≈ 20**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n- Certifications: 35 points (SOC 2 Type 1/2 + HIPAA BAA + CCPA; no ISO 27001, no FedRAMP)\\n- Assessment Quality: 15 points (SOC 2 Type 2 audit; frequency unknown; no third-party AI ethics audit)\\n- Policies: 28 points (data retention policy documented and enforced; incident response plan documented but not tested; AI ethics policy not published; privacy policy implied via CCPA compliance)\\n- Operational Controls: 22 points (automated rollback with manual trigger; human oversight embedded in workflow; no explicit monitoring alerts; basic audit logging)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 8 points (6 years old, Series B/C, 201–1,000 employees; growth-stage, not enterprise-established)\\n- **Governance Score = 35 + 15 + 28 + 22 + 8 = 108 → Capped at 100**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 − 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime; contractual status not confirmed; no P1/P2/P3 support SLAs disclosed)\\n- Incident Management: 12 points (documented plan, not tested; maturity unclear)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 18 points (SaaS cloud-hosted; Epic integration mature; athenahealth expanding; not enterprise multi-tenant scale)\\n- Stability: 15 points (6-year-old company, Series B/C; profitable status unknown; customer retention not disclosed)\\n- Support: 8 points (support structure not detailed; no 24/7 dedicated support confirmed)\\n- **Operational Score = 25 + 12 + 18 + 15 + 8 = 78**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 − 78 = 22**\\n\\n**Final VTS:**\\nVTS = 100 − [(20 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (22 × 0.30)]\\n= 100 − [8 + 0 + 6.6]\\n= 100 − 14.6\\n= **85.4 ≈ 85**\\n\\n**Adjustment for AI Governance Gaps:**\\nVector guidance notes: \\"Mitigation Coverage Gaps: Missing Post-Deployment Monitoring and Human Oversight categories\\" and \\"Recommendation: Require vendor to implement continuous model drift monitoring and clinical review workflow before deployment.\\"\\n\\nAbridge exhibits similar gaps:\\n- No published continuous model drift monitoring\\n- No explicit clinical review workflow for high-confidence vs. low-confidence notes\\n- Bias testing not disclosed\\n\\n**Adjusted Trust Score: 72** (applying −13 point penalty for AI governance transparency gaps and untested incident response)\\n\\n**Classification: Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Category Scores (Derived from Vendor Data)\\n\\n| Category | Score | Rationale |\\n|----------|-------|-----------|\\n| **Security** | 78 | SOC 2 Type 1/2 + HIPAA BAA + CCPA; rollback capability present; incident response plan documented but untested; no penetration testing frequency disclosed. |\\n| **Compliance** | 82 | Strong: SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, CCPA. Gaps: No ISO 27001, no FedRAMP, no GDPR explicit statement, no EU AI Act readiness. |\\n| **Data Practices** | 75 | Strong: 30-day auto-deletion of recordings/transcripts, US data residency, HIPAA-aligned retention. Gaps: No explicit statement on training data usage, no customer data deletion on request, no EU residency option. |\\n| **AI Governance** | 58 | Weak: No published AI ethics policy, no bias audit program, no third-party AI safety audit, training data documentation partial, no explainability framework published. Strength: Clinical outcome evidence (26 corroborated points). |\\n| **Operations** | 70 | 99.9% uptime SLA; basic telemetry and audit logging; no P1/P2/P3 support SLAs; change management not specified; incident response not tested. |\\n| **Company Maturity** | 68 | 6 years old (growth-stage); 201–1,000 employees; Series B/C funding; no revenue/profitability disclosure; customer base not quantified. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status: CONDITIONAL APPROVAL**\\n\\n**Recommended Action:** Proceed with vendor **with mandatory contractual conditions** before production deployment.\\n\\n**Must-Fix (Contract Conditions):**\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety:**\\n   - Vendor must provide documented bias testing results (fairness metrics across demographic groups, clinical subpopulations) within 60 days\\n   - Vendor must commit to annual third-party AI ethics audit (starting within 12 months of contract execution)\\n   - Vendor must document continuous model drift monitoring and alert thresholds for clinical note quality degradation\\n\\n2. **Incident Response:**\\n   - Vendor must conduct and document annual incident response plan testing (tabletop or simulation) with results provided to customer\\n\\n3. **Transparency:**\\n   - Vendor must publish AI model card or system card detailing training data composition, known limitations, and clinical validation scope\\n   - Vendor must disclose infrastructure provider and confirm infrastructure provider SLAs meet customer uptime requirements\\n\\n**Should-Fix (Recommended Enhancements):**\\n- Negotiate explicit P1/P2/P3 support response SLAs (e.g., P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours)\\n- Request quarterly business reviews with clinical outcome tracking\\n- Establish escalation path to CTO/VP Engineering for critical issues\\n\\n**Risk Mitigation Strategy:**\\n- Pilot deployment: 1–2 clinical departments (4–8 weeks) before enterprise rollout\\n- Establish clinical governance board to review high-impact note generation errors\\n- Require vendor to maintain rollback capability and test rollback procedure quarterly\\n\\n**Residual Concerns:**\\n- Growth-stage vendor (Series B/C); long-term viability dependent on funding/profitability (not disclosed)\\n- Limited AI governance transparency may pose regulatory risk in future EU AI Act enforcement\\n- US-only data residency limits international expansion\\n\\n**Success Criteria for Go-Live:**\\n- ✓ Bias testing results provided and acceptable (fairness metrics ≥0.95 across demographic groups)\\n- ✓ Incident response plan tested and documented\\n- ✓ AI model card published\\n- ✓ Infrastructure provider SLAs confirmed\\n- ✓ Pilot deployment demonstrates ", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Abridge Ambient Documentation", "Customer Base": "Not specified (evidence of multiple healthcare system deployments with documented ROI metrics)", "Target Industry": "Healthcare (ambulatory care, primary care, specialty practices)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (Epic and athenahealth integration)", "Deployment Scale": "Typical deployment: ambulatory care settings (clinician-facing, patient-clinician interaction capture)", "Primary Use Case": "Real-time clinical documentation automation; transforms patient-clinician conversations into structured clinical notes; reduces clinician documentation burden", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; native Epic integration; expanding athenahealth support", "Product Description": "Abridge Ambient Documentation is a purpose-built healthcare AI platform that captures and transcribes patient-clinician conversations in real-time, automatically generating structured clinical notes integrated directly into Epic and athenahealth EHRs. The platform prioritizes data privacy by automatically deleting audio recordings and transcripts after 30 days while retaining final clinical notes in the medical record. Documented clinical outcomes include 53% improvement in professional fulfillment, 60% reduction in after-hours documentation, and 11% wRVU increase, demonstrating measurable ROI for healthcare organizations.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C company); production-deployed with 26 corroborated evidence points on clinical outcomes"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Abridge (legal entity name not specified; operating as Abridge)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (healthcare-focused)", "Year Founded": "2018", "Operating Regions": "United States (primary); data residency: US only", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, California, United States; specific investors not disclosed", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not disclosed"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Custom-trained healthcare AI model (specific architecture not disclosed); optimized for clinical conversation understanding and note generation", "Model Purpose": "Speech-to-text transcription, clinical entity extraction, structured note generation (understanding + generation); real-time processing of patient-clinician conversations", "Human Oversight": "Clinician review of generated notes (implicit in EHR workflow); no explicit monitoring alerts or audit trail for AI decision confidence disclosed", "Model Governance": "Not fully documented; no published staged deployment framework or formal AI governance policy disclosed", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate transparency; some explainability features present (note generation rationale not detailed); no published prompt-level control or citation mechanism disclosed"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Bias testing approach not specified; no evidence of red-team testing, third-pa