frastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no frequency of risk assessments or vendor SLA reviews documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; no SLAs from critical vendors provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Available; scope and export capability not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Available; export format and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Not provided in attestation; governance policies and testing results not uploaded\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Available; specific results and NDA terms not disclosed in attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Classification:** **ACCEPTABLE VENDOR – Standard Procurement with Enhanced Due Diligence**\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\nAnthropic's Claude Team scores in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" range (70–79) due to solid compliance foundations (HIPAA BAA, flexible data residency) and documented security capabilities (automated rollback, incident response plan). However, the vendor exhibits material gaps in:\\n\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency** (65/100): No documented governance policy, bias audit schedule, or detailed training data lineage\\n2. **Operational Maturity** (68/100): 99.0% SLA is below enterprise standard; incident response untested\\n3. **Adversarial Testing** (not scored): No evidence of red-teaming or penetration testing\\n4. **Regulatory Readiness** (partial): HIPAA BAA confirmed, but GDPR, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n\\n**Recommended Actions Before Deployment:**\\n\\n1. **Require vendor to provide:**\\n   - Documented AI governance policy with bias audit schedule and methodology\\n   - Evidence of incident response plan testing (tabletop or full-scale exercise)\\n   - Training data composition summary and bias testing results (under NDA if necessary)\\n   - GDPR Data Processing Agreement (DPA) and EU AI Act compliance roadmap\\n\\n2. **Negotiate contract conditions:**\\n   - Upgrade SLA to 99.5% minimum (or 99.95% for production use cases)\\n   - Define support response SLAs by severity (P1/P2/P3)\\n   - Require quarterly compliance attestations and annual third-party audit\\n\\n3. **Pilot approach:**\\n   - Deploy in non-production environment first (e.g., legal document review, non-PHI use cases)\\n   - Monitor for 60 days; validate data retention and deletion processes\\n   - Escalate to production only after governance gaps are closed\\n\\n**Pass/Fail Criteria:**\\n- **PASS:** Vendor provides tested incident response plan, documented bias audit schedule, and GDPR DPA within 30 days\\n- **FAIL:** Vendor unable to provide governance documentation or refuses to upgrade SLA; consider alternative vendors (e.g., OpenAI, Google Vertex AI) with higher operational maturity\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessor Notes:** This assessment is based on vendor self-attestation data. Independent verification of compliance certifications, audit results, and security controls is recommended before contract execution.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Claude Team", "Customer Base": "Not specified", "Target Industry": "Legal services, financial advisory, software development, enterprise operations, sales", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Team-based collaboration; supports shared projects and workplace connectors", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise collaboration, legal workflows, M&A advisory, AI-powered agent building, bug fixing, enterprise operations automation, sales enablement", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; customer choice of data residency region", "Product Description": "Claude Team is an AI-powered collaboration platform featuring a 200K context window for processing long documents, an \\"Artifacts\\" feature for generating stand