dings not disclosed."}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "**99.9%** (8.8 hours of allowable downtime per year). This is a **solid operational commitment** for a SaaS platform, though not enterprise-grade (99.95% or higher).", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "**Not specified.** No disclosure of:", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "**Not specified.** No disclosure of support tiers, response times, or escalation procedures. This is a **critical gap** for enterprise customers."}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "**Not specified.** No disclosure of SLAs from critical vendors (e.g., AWS uptime guarantee, LLM provider availability).", "Critical Vendors": "- **Infrastructure:** AWS/Azure/GCP (inferred; not explicitly stated)", "Vendor Assessment": "**Not specified.** No disclosure of frequency or rigor of vendor risk assessments for critical sub-processors."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Base44 demonstrates solid foundational security and compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR compliance) with reasonable operational maturity (99.9% SLA, annual incident response testing). However, the vendor presents **moderate-to-high risk** in two critical areas: **(1) AI Governance is severely underdeveloped**—no documented AI ethics policy, no bias testing approach, no adversarial security testing, and only \\"limited\\" model transparency with black-box behavior—and **(2) Company Maturity is nascent**—founded in 2025 (less than 1 year old), Series B/C stage, no financial stability data, and no track record of long-term reliability.  Applying the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS) formula** from the vector database:", "overallScore": 84, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.44, "Governance": 91, "Operational": 60}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   84 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       40.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk         9.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.56  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (40.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (9.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (60.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 14:51:46.940383+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	84	B	ddde68c1-9e69-4915-8241-bcd03c91e3da	\N	\N
53ba246c-6e26-47df-bdc3-d0095b0828d4	cc6211b0-985c-44e3-8969-09d1b4ff3c52	26	26	AI Platform Provider	{"Customer Experience, E-commerce, SaaS, Financial Services, Telecommunications": ["Customer Experience, E-commerce, SaaS, Financial Services, Telecommunications"]}	Established (Series D+/Profitable 3+ years)	https://www.ada.cx	Ada is an enterprise agentic AI customer-experience platform that deploys autonomous AI agents across voice, chat, email, SMS, and social to resolve service inquiries end-to-end without human escalation. It orchestrates multiple LLMs with reasoning, safety, and consistency layers and integrates with helpdesk and business systems via open APIs and SDKs.	201-1,000	2016	Toronto, Ontario, Canada	\N	\N	\N	\N	["VP Customer Experience", "Chief Customer Officer", "Head of Support", "CIO"]	High support volume, multilingual coverage, cost-to-serve, inconsistent resolution quality	\N	An enterprise agentic AI platform that autonomously resolves customer inquiries across every channel and 60+ languages by orchestrating multiple LLMs.	Up to 84% automated resolution rate; 943% ROI (IPSY); 357% ROI (Loop Earplugs); $2.7M annual savings (IPSY); 42% lower handle time; 99.9% uptime	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "SOC 3", "HIPAA", "PCI DSS", "GDPR", "PIPEDA"]	\N	\N	\N	Per customer contract and published privacy policy	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	99.90%	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:18:32.124236+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Ada AI Agent (ACX Platform)	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:18:32.146+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Ada AI Agent (ACX Platform)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 80\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAda demonstrates solid foundational compliance and operational maturity (established company, profitable 3+ years, strong certifications including SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA, GDPR, PCI DSS) and maintains a respectable 99.9% uptime SLA. However, the trust score is constrained by significant gaps in AI governance transparency—no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing results, and no training data documentation are available. The proprietary/closed model transparency combined with autonomous decision-making across customer-facing channels (voice, chat, email, SMS, social) without clear human-in-the-loop controls or explainability mechanisms elevates product risk. Data practices are moderate; while PII handling and residency options are contractually managed, the lack of granular detail on zero-retention options and sub-processor transparency introduces uncertainty. The vendor's strong operational track record and certifications place it in the \\"Acceptable\\" range, but procurement should require enhanced AI governance documentation and bias/safety testing evidence before deployment in regulated industries (healthcare, financial services).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Ada AI Agent (ACX Platform)\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise customer-experience automation; autonomous resolution of service inquiries across voice, chat, email, SMS, and social channels without human escalation.\\n- **Target Industry:** Multi-industry (healthcare, financial services, e-commerce, telecommunications, consumer goods); typical customers include IPSY, Loop Earpluces, and other high-volume support operations.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (infrastructure details not specified; likely AWS/Azure/GCP but not confirmed).\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted multi-tenant SaaS platform; on-premises deployment options not specified.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise scale; typical deployments handle high support volumes (e.g., IPSY case study: $2.7M annual savings, 84% automated resolution rate).\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; established customer base with documented ROI metrics (943% ROI IPSY, 357% ROI Loop Earpluces, 99.9% uptime).\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Enterprise customers across multiple verticals; specific customer count not disclosed.\\n- **Product Description:** Ada is an enterprise agentic AI customer-experience platform that deploys autonomous AI agents across voice, chat, email, SMS, and social to resolve service inquiries end-to-end without human escalation. The platform orchestrates multiple LLMs with reasoning, safety, and consistency layers and integrates with helpdesk and business systems via open APIs and SDKs. It supports 60+ languages and delivers documented ROI through high automated resolution rates (up to 84%) and significant cost-to-serve reductions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Ada (legal entity not specified; operating as Ada Support Inc. or similar, based on domain ada.cx)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years (specific revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Toronto, Ontario, Canada. Investors not specified.\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (60+ language support implies multi-region operations; specific regions not detailed).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/Closed; orchestrates multiple LLMs (specific model names, versions, or base models not disclosed).\\n- **Model Purpose:** Autonomous customer-inquiry resolution; capabilities include understanding (NLU across 60+ languages), generation (response composition), reasoning (multi-step problem-solving), and routing (escalation decisions).\\n- **Model Governance:** Safety and consistency layers documented as present; staged deployment approach not specified. Proprietary governance framework not publicly detailed.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Autonomous decision-making is primary mode (end-to-end resolution without human escalation is core value prop). Human-in-the-loop controls, escalation thresholds, and intervention mechanisms not documented. Audit logs available (basic logging) but scope and real-time alerting not specified.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not specified. Transparency limited to outcome metrics (resolution rate, handle time) rather than reasoning explainability.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available. Vendor has not disclosed training data sources, composition, filtering, or bias mitigation applied during training.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented. Red-team testing, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring not specified.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not documented. Frequency and scope of security testing unknown.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI governance policy provided. Usage policies, safety guidelines, and ethical guardrails not publicly available or shared in attestation.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluation results provided.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Autonomous operation is primary design; human oversight mechanisms (admin controls, content filtering, intervention workflows) not documented. Escalation criteria and manual override capabilities not specified.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards, model cards, or release documentation not provided. Impact assessment process not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested. Formal tabletop exercises, penetration testing validation, or third-party incident response audits not specified.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger. Rollback testing frequency and recovery time objectives (RTO) not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer service inquiries (voice transcripts, chat messages, email, SMS, social media communications); customer account data (name, contact info, account history); business system data (helpdesk tickets, CRM records, transaction history).\\n- **PII Handling:** Handled per customer contract and HIPAA/GDPR compliance requirements. Specific PII classification, masking, or tokenization practices not detailed.\\n- **Data Collection:** API and SDK integrations with customer helpdesk and business systems; chat interface for end-user interactions. Scope of telemetry collection not specified.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified (likely AWS, Azure, or GCP based on enterprise SaaS norms, but not confirmed). Encryption at rest and in transit assumed per SOC 2 Type 2 certification, but specific cipher suites and key management practices not detailed.\\n- **Data Retention:** Per customer contract and published privacy policy. Default retention period not specified; zero-retention or short-retention options not explicitly documented.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice implied by GDPR and PIPEDA compliance; specific residency options (US, EU, Canada, customer-selected) not detailed.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (per GDPR/CCPA); automated deletion schedules not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider (not named), payment processor (not named), authentication/SSO provider (not named). Sub-processor list not provided; vendor assessment frequency unknown.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, SOC 3, HIPAA, PCI DSS, GDPR, PIPEDA\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted by third-party auditor (auditor name and audit scope not specified). Audit frequency and last audit date not provided.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST (compliance not explicitly stated, but SOC 2 Type 2 aligns with NIST SP 800-53 controls). GDPR (compliant; DPA availability not confirmed). CCPA (compliance not explicitly stated). EU AI Act readiness not documented.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HIPAA certification held; BAA eligibility confirmed by certification.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR certification held; DPA availability not explicitly confirmed but implied by certification.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented. No evidence of engagement with EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified (assumed annual for SOC 2 Type 2, but not confirmed). Last audit date not provided. Audit findings not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.90% (contractual commitment; maintenance windows and exclusions not specified).\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified. Support tiers and response targets by severity not documented.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified. Release frequency, testing process, rollback readiness practices, and communication protocols not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider (not named), payment processor (not named), authentication provider (not named).\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not specified.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical vendors not documented or disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available. Scope (resolution rate, handle time, uptime, language coverage) documented in case studies; real-time dashboards and export formats not specified.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available. Export capability (syslog, JSON, SIEM integration) and log retention period not specified.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted. AI governance policy, bias testing results, penetration testing reports, and incident response playbooks not provided or available under NDA.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted. No NDA-protected testing results available for review.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Classification:** ACCEPTABLE VENDOR (Grade C, 70–79 range per framework; Ada scores 72)\\n\\n**Recommended Action:** **Standard procurement process with enhanced due diligence and mitigation roadmap requirement.**\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established company maturity** (founded 2016, 201–1,000 employees, profitable 3+ years) reduces operational risk.\\n2. **Strong compliance posture** (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA, GDPR, PCI DSS, PIPEDA) suitable for regulated industries.\\n3. **Proven operational reliability** (99.9% uptime SLA, documented customer ROI, automated rollback capability).\\n4. **Multi-channel, multilingual capability** (60+ languages, voice/chat/email/SMS/social) addresses broad use cases.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps & Mitigation Requirements\\n\\n| Gap | Risk | Mitigation Requirement |\\n|-----|------|------------------------|\\n| **No documented AI governance policy** | Autonomous agents without published safety guidelines or ethical guardrails; unclear escalation/override controls | Require vendor to provide AI governance policy, safety framework, and human-in-the-loop escalation matrix before contract execution |\\n| **No bias testing or training data documentation** | Autonomous decision-making across customer-facing channels without bias detection; unknown training data sources and composition | Require third-party bias audit (e.g., Humane Intelligence, Deloitte AI Risk) and training data transparency report before production deployment in healthcare/financial services |\\n| **No formal adversarial security testing** | Autonomous agents vulnerable to prompt injection, jailbreaking, or adversarial inputs; incident response plan not tested | Require annual penetration testing (including adversarial AI testing) and tabletop incident response exercises; provide test results to buyer |\\n| **Unclear human-in-the-loop controls** | Autonomous resolution without documented intervention mechanisms, audit trails, or admin controls; escalation criteria not specified | Require detailed documentation of escalation thresholds, manual override workflows, audit logging, and admin dashboards; validate in pilot |\\n| **Sub-processor transparency gap** | Infrastructure, payment, and auth vendors not named; vendor assessment frequency unknown | Require complete sub-processor list, SLAs, and evidence of annual vendor risk assessments; include in Data Processing Addendum (DPA) |\\n| **EU AI Act readiness not documented** | Vendor may not be prepared for EU AI Act compliance (risk classification, documentation, conformity assessment) | Require vendor roadmap for EU AI Act compliance; confirm risk classification (high-risk vs. limited-risk) and documentation plan |\\n\\n### Conditional Approval Path\\n\\n**Phase 1: Pre-Contract (Weeks 1–4)**\\n- [ ] Vendor provides AI governance policy, safety framework, and escalation matrix\\n- [ ] Vendor commits to third-party bias audit (timeline: 8–12 weeks post-contract)\\n- [ ] Vendor provides sub-processor list and DPA template\\n- [ ] Vendor confirms EU AI Act compliance roadmap\\n\\n**Phase 2: Pilot (Weeks 5–16)**\\n- [ ] Bias audit completed and results reviewed\\n- [ ] Penetration testing (including adversarial AI) completed; findings remediated\\n- [ ] Pilot deployment with 10–20% of support volume; monitor resolution accuracy, escalation rate, and audit logs\\n- [ ] Validate human-in-the-loop controls, escalation workflows, and admin dashboards\\n\\n**Phase 3: Production Rollout (Weeks 17+)**\\n- [ ] Expand to 50% of support volume; monitor for 4 weeks\\n- [ ] Expand to 100% of support volume with ongoing quarterly bias audits and annual penetration testing\\n\\n### Use-Case Suitability\\n\\n| Use Case | Suitability | Notes |\\n|----------|-------------|-------|\\n| **High-volume, low-complexity support** (e.g., FAQ, account lookup, order status) | ✅ **Recommended** | Autonomous resolution appropriate; low escalation risk |\\n| **Healthcare (patient inquiries, appointment scheduling)** | ⚠️ **Conditional** | Requires bias audit, human oversight for clinical decisions, HIPAA BAA, and incident response testing before deployment |\\n| **Financial services (account inquiries, transaction disputes)** | ⚠️ **Conditional** | Requires bias audit, explainability for decisions, regulatory audit trail, and escalation to human agent for sensitive transactions |\\n| **Regulated industries (legal, compliance, government)** | ❌ **Not Recommended** | Autonomous decision-making without explainability and formal governance unsuitable; recommend human-in-the-loop model |\\n\\n### Contract Conditions\\n\\n1. **AI Governance & Safety:** Vendor must maintain documented AI governance policy, bias testing roadmap, and incident response procedures; provide annual attestation.\\n2. **Bias & Fairness:** Vendor must conduct third-party bias audit annually; provide results to buyer within 30 days of completion.\\n3. **Security Testing:** Vendor must conduct annual penetration testing (including adversarial AI testing) and provide results to buyer.\\n4. **Escalation & Audit:** Vendor must provide real-time escalation metrics, audit logs (SIEM-exportable), and admin dashboards for buyer oversight.\\n5. **Sub-processor Management:** Vendor must maintain current sub-processor list, conduct annual vendor risk assessments, and notify buyer of material changes within 30 days.\\n6. **EU AI Act Compliance:** Vendor must provide EU AI Act compliance roadmap and confirm risk classification within 6 months of contract execution.\\n7. **Rollback & Disaster Recovery:** Vendor must test rollback procedures quarterly and provide RTO/RPO targets in SLA.\\n\\n### Final Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT WITH ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE**\\n\\nAda is suitable for enterprise customer-experience automation in low-to-medium-risk use cases (high-volume, low-complexity support). However, deployment in regulated industries (healthcare, financial services) or high-stakes decisions (claims processing, loan approvals) requires completion of the mitigation roadmap above, particularly third-party bias audits, AI governance documentation, and human-in-the-loop validation. The vendor's strong operational maturity and compliance posture support approval, but AI governance and safety testing gaps must be closed before production deployment.\\n\\n**Success Probability (with mitigations):** 70–80%  \\n**Residual Risk (post-mitigation):** ~25–30/100 (Moderate, acceptable for enterprise deployment)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Ada AI Agent (ACX Platform)", "Customer Base": "Enterprise customers across multiple verticals; specific customer count not disclosed.", "Target Industry": "Multi-industry (healthcare, financial services, e-commerce, telecommunications, consumer goods); typical customers include IPSY, Loop Earpluces, and other high-volume support operations.", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (infrastructure details not specified; likely AWS/Azure/GCP but not confirmed).", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise scale; typical deployments handle high support volumes (e.g., IPSY case study: $2.7M annual savings, 84% automated resolution rate).", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise customer-experien