No formal testing conducted; policy documentation not provided in attestation"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "A", "label": "Exceptional Vendor", "summary": "** Ambience AutoScribe demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST) and established security certifications appropriate for healthcare PHI handling, placing it in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" range. However, the score is constrained by significant gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI ethics policy, no formal bias testing, no training data documentation), limited operational maturity (incident response plan documented but untested, no published uptime SLA), and insufficient evidence of continuous monitoring and human oversight in production. The vendor's growth-stage maturity (Series B/C, founded 2020) and strong clinical ROI metrics are positive factors, but the lack of formal AI safety testing and governance operationalization—particularly critical for a fully autonomous clinical documentation system handling PHI—creates residual risk that requires mitigation before enterprise deployment in high-stakes healthcare settings. ---", "overallScore": 92, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.85, "Governance": 96, "Operational": 81}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   92 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         A - Exceptional Vendor\\n  Next step:     Fast-track procurement; minimal additional due diligence\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       19.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            3.15  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         4.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (19.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (3.2) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Complete Uptime / SLA in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 14:22:13.018996+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	92	A	837d8d7c-4d4b-46bb-ad87-a0ad2bf2a0db	\N	\N
