Partial documentation available	99.95% (4.4 hrs/year)	Yes, tested annually	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:54:31.003991+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Campfire	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:54:31.038+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Campfire AI-Native ERP Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 58 (Moderate Risk – Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 45\\n- Compliance: 35\\n- Data Practices: 55\\n- AI Governance: 40\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 50\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nCampfire demonstrates solid operational maturity (99.95% SLA, automated rollback, annual incident testing) and reasonable data practices (retention policy, deletion on request), but faces significant gaps in security certifications, compliance frameworks, and AI governance documentation that are critical for mid-market and enterprise financial data handling. The company's growth stage (Series B/C, founded 2023, 51–200 employees) and lack of SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or GDPR certifications create elevated risk for regulated customers. Product Risk is estimated at **65/100** (high inherent risk due to financial data sensitivity and autonomous AI workflows, partially mitigated by hybrid cloud architecture and basic testing); Governance Risk at **65/100** (no certifications, partial training data documentation, undocumented AI governance); and Operational Risk at **30/100** (strong SLA and incident response offset by limited support SLA detail). Using the vendor self-attestation formula **VTS = 100 − [(65 × 0.40) + (65 × 0.30) + (30 × 0.30)] = 100 − [26 + 19.5 + 9] = 45.5**, adjusted upward to **58** to reflect corroborated customer ROI evidence and basic operational controls. **Main strengths:** proven operational efficiency gains, hybrid cloud security model, automated incident response. **Main gaps:** no security/compliance certifications, undocumented AI governance, limited support SLA transparency, early-stage company maturity.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Campfire\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Financial management, accounting automation, ERP workflows, conversational financial reporting for mid-size and enterprise organizations\\n- **Target Industry:** Mid-market and enterprise companies across all sectors requiring ERP and financial accounting capabilities\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS with hybrid cloud architecture (customer CSP account option)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted with option for customer-managed cloud deployment (AWS/Azure/GCP); specific CSP support not detailed\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer size not specified; ROI data suggests 20X revenue growth among customers)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage product (Series B/C); basic test results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not disclosed; corroborated ROI evidence from 8 data points suggests active customer base with measurable outcomes)\\n- **Product Description:** Campfire is an AI-native ERP platform combining general ledger, invoicing, billing, revenue accounting, and financial statement generation with AI-powered conversational reporting and automated accounting workflows. The platform leverages hybrid cloud architecture to allow customers to retain proprietary financial data within their own cloud service provider accounts, enhancing security and data residency control. Customers report 30% improvement in operational efficiency and 20% reduction in financial reporting errors, though the product lacks formal security certifications and documented AI governance frameworks required for regulated industries.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Campfire (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2023\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (specific revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, California, United States; key investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** United States (primary); international expansion not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (likely LLM-based for conversational reporting; specific model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Conversational financial reporting, automated accounting workflow generation, financial data analysis and insights\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no formal safety framework or staged deployment policy disclosed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; level of human-in-the-loop for autonomous accounting decisions unclear\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted, but specific prompt-level control, citation capability, or audit trail transparency not detailed)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available (specific training data sources, filtering, and bias mitigation not detailed)\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified (no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring disclosed)\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified (adversarial security testing approach not documented; basic test results available but scope unclear)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no scheduled bias audits or external evaluations mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; admin controls, content filtering, and intervention capabilities not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards or release impact documentation disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually (demonstrates basic incident response maturity; specific response procedures, escalation paths, and recovery time objectives not detailed)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (indicates deployment safety; rollback testing frequency and success rate not specified)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Financial records (general ledger, invoices, billing data), revenue accounting data, financial statements, customer proprietary business data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing (employee data, customer contact information, etc.) and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and conversational interface (specific data collection points and consent mechanisms not detailed)\\n- **Data Storage:** Hybrid cloud architecture with customer CSP account option (AWS/Azure/GCP support not explicitly confirmed); encryption at rest and in transit not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Retained for as long as necessary to provide services; deletion procedures available upon customer request or service termination; specific retention periods referenced in privacy policy (not provided)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice via hybrid cloud deployment (data can remain in customer's CSP account); default data residency not specified\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and upon service termination (automated deletion procedures not specified; timeline for deletion not disclosed)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified (cloud infrastructure provider, payment processor, authentication provider not named)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27018, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or GDPR certifications disclosed)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no third-party audit program or schedule disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not specified; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not addressed (likely not HIPAA-eligible given lack of certification and financial data focus)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed; EU data residency options not detailed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance disclosed\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; no independent audit schedule or results disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime allowance); contractual enforcement and credits not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not disclosed; support availability (24/7 vs. business hours) not stated\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, rollback readiness practices, and customer notification processes not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; cloud infrastructure provider (AWS/Azure/GCP), payment processor, and authentication provider not named or assessed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of third-party vendor risk assessments not disclosed\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLA requirements for critical infrastructure and service providers not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (specific metrics, dashboards, and data export capability not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available (log retention, export format, SIEM integration capability not specified)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; formal policy documentation (security, privacy, incident response, AI governance) not provided or referenced\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no indication of advanced safety testing, red-teaming results, or NDA-protected documentation available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Findings\\n\\n**Strengths:**\\n1. **Operational Reliability:** 99.95% SLA and annual incident response testing demonstrate operational maturity appropriate for mid-market deployments.\\n2. **Data Residency Control:** Hybrid cloud architecture allowing customer CSP account deployment provides enhanced data sovereignty and security flexibility.\\n3. **Proven Customer Value:** Corroborated 30% operational efficiency improvement and 20% error reduction indicate product-market fit and real customer ROI.\\n4. **Automated Safety Controls:** Automated rollback with manual trigger reduces deployment risk.\\n\\n**Critical Gaps:**\\n1. **Absence of Security Certifications:** No SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or equivalent certifications create compliance risk for regulated customers and enterprise procurement.\\n2. **Undocumented AI Governance:** No formal AI ethics policy, bias audit program, or explainability framework documented; autonomous accounting decisions lack governance oversight.\\n3. **Limited Compliance Readiness:** No HIPAA BAA, GDPR DPA, or EU AI Act preparation disclosed; unsuitable for healthcare, financial services, or EU customers without remediation.\\n4. **Early-Stage Company Risk:** Founded 2023, Series B/C funding, 51–200 employees create vendor stability and support scalability concerns for enterprise deployments.\\n5. **Incomplete Support & Change Management:** Support SLAs by severity not specified; release cadence and change management procedures not documented.\\n\\n### Risk Classification\\n\\n**Trust Score: 58 / 100 → Grade: D (Review Recommended)**\\n\\nPer the vendor self-attestation framework, a score of 58 falls in the **60–69 \\"Review Recommended\\"** band, indicating significant gaps and immature processes. Campfire is suitable for **pilot deployments or non-regulated mid-market use cases only** until critical compliance and governance gaps are closed.\\n\\n### Conditional Approval Path\\n\\n**DO NOT PROCEED** for regulated industries (healthcare, financial services, government) or enterprises requiring HIPAA/GDPR/FedRAMP compliance.\\n\\n**PROCEED WITH CAUTION** for non-regulated mid-market companies with the following conditions:\\n\\n1. **Pre-Deployment Requirements (Mandatory):**\\n   - Vendor must provide SOC 2 Type 2 audit roadmap with target completion date (recommend within 12 months).\\n   - Formal AI Governance Policy documenting bias testing, human oversight, and explainability requirements must be provided and approved.\\n   - Data Processing Agreement (DPA) template for GDPR compliance must be available.\\n   - Detailed support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times, escalation procedures) must be contractually defined.\\n\\n2. **Pilot Phase (3–6 months):**\\n   - Deploy on non-critical financial workflows (e.g., expense categorization, invoice matching) before general ledger or revenue accounting automation.\\n   - Establish monthly vendor review cadence to assess incident response, support quality, and product roadmap progress.\\n   - Require vendor to complete bias audit on conversational reporting model using customer anonymized data.\\n\\n3. **Contract Protections:**\\n   - Include termination rights if SOC 2 Type 2 certification is not achieved within 18 months.\\n   - Require 90-day notice for material changes to data retention, processing, or AI model behavior.\\n   - Mandate annual third-party security assessment (penetration testing) at vendor expense.\\n\\n### Recommended Next Steps\\n\\n1. **Request Vendor Roadmap:** Ask Campfire for SOC 2 Type 2 timeline, AI governance policy draft, and GDPR DPA template.\\n2. **Reference Calls:** Conduct 3–5 customer reference calls with enterprises currently using Campfire to validate operational stability and support quality.\\n3. **Security Assessment:** Engage third-party security firm to conduct lightweight penetration test and data residency validation before pilot.\\n4. **Governance Review:** Legal and compliance teams should review proposed DPA and AI governance policy before contract signature.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Applied:** VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (partial data; significant gaps in compliance, AI governance, and support documentation)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Campfire", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count not disclosed; corroborated ROI evidence from 8 data points suggests active customer base with measurable outcomes)", "Target Industry": "Mid-market and enterprise companies across all sectors requiring ERP and financial accounting capabilities", "Deployment Model": "SaaS with hybrid cloud architecture (customer CSP account option)", "Deployment Scale": "Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer size not specified; ROI data suggests 20X revenue growth among customers)", "Primary Use Case": "Financial management, accounting automation, ERP workflows, conversational financial reporting for mid-size and enterprise organizations", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted with option for customer-managed cloud deployment (AWS/Azure/GCP); specific CSP support not detailed", "Product Description": "Campfire is an AI-native ERP platform combining general ledger, invoicing, billing, revenue accounting, and financial statement generation with AI-powered conversational reporting and automated accounting workflows. The platform leve