type, frequency, and last audit date unknown", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime) – solid enterprise standard", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not detailed", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; response targets by severity not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not documented", "Critical Vendors": "Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not identified", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency of risk assessments unknown"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"SLA": "99.9% uptime = 33 points", "FAIL": "Vendor unable to commit to AI governance documentation; refuses third-party testing; incident response plan remains untested beyond attestation", "Gaps": "No training data documentation (–0.20), no bias testing (–0.15), no AI ethics policy (–0.15), limited explainability (–0.10)", "PASS": "Vendor commits to AI governance roadmap with 6-month completion timeline; incident response plan tested within 90 days; third-party bias audit initiated", "Support": "Not specified; assume basic support = 5 points", "Stability": "9-year company, profitable 3+ years = 22 points", "Deployment Maturity": "Enterprise multi-tenant (inferred) = 25 points", "Incident Management": "Documented, not tested = 15 points", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability and scope not detailed", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Limited/Partial availability; specific results and NDA terms not specified", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Limited/Partial – AI governance, bias testing, and training data documentation not provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Clarify Health demonstrates established company maturity (Series D+, profitable, 9 years operating) and solid operational fundamentals (99.9% SLA, automated rollback, HITRUST certification). However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and bias testing—critical for healthcare AI systems handling PHI at scale. The moderate trust score reflects acceptable operational and compliance posture offset by material product risk due to undocumented AI practices and limited evidence of safety testing. Procurement should require vendor commitment to enhanced AI governance documentation and bias audit roadmap before deployment. ---", "overallScore": 84, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.17, "Governance": 84, "Operational": 69}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   84 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       31.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        16.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            4.83  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (31.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (16.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:16:22.792639+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	84	B	b7b86139-e197-4995-8d6c-5041386570ab	\N	\N
07b8cadc-a3bf-411c-9acd-10475f5856b3	f3d62ebc-ac20-499e-adcc-7267d9ca08cc	56	56	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Technology; Professional Services": ["Technology; Professional Services"]}	Established (Series D+/Profitable 3+ years)	https://clickup.com/	ClickUp is a project management software that brings projects, docs, and chat into one place, powered by AI.	201-1,000	2017	San Diego, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "VP Product", "Line of Business Leader"]	Before ClickUp, our project tracking was scattered across various platforms. ClickUp centralized our processes, saving us invaluable time and significantly reducing miscommunication.	\N	ClickUp brings all of those teams together into one place so that they can stay on track, collaborate and communicate.	**33% less overhead** by streamlining processes.\n\n**10+ hours saved** each week for store managers and leadership teams across multiple locations.\n\n**Top 10% talent retention** across the franchise with thanks to efficient onboarding and management with ClickUp.	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["NIST CSF"]	\N	\N	\N	We will only retain your personal data as long as reasonably requir	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:17:08.422255+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	ClickUp Brain	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:17:08.425+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: ClickUp Brain\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 58 (Low–Moderate / Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 52\\n- Compliance: 45\\n- Data Practices: 48\\n- AI Governance: 35\\n- Operations: 66\\n- Company Maturity: 72\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nClickUp Brain presents a **moderate-to-low trust profile** suitable for non-regulated, general project management use cases but **not recommended for healthcare PHI, financial data, or other sensitive regulated environments** without substantial remediation. The vendor demonstrates solid operational maturity (99.9% SLA, established company) and basic security posture (NIST CSF), but critical gaps in AI governance, compliance depth, and data practices significantly elevate residual risk. Specifically: (1) no documented AI governance policy or bias testing framework; (2) minimal compliance certifications (NIST CSF only; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or GDPR DPA); (3) training data sourced from third-party models with unknown provenance; (4) incident response plan documented but untested; (5) no formal AI safety testing conducted. The company's Series D+ maturity and 99.9% uptime are strengths, but they do not offset the absence of enterprise-grade AI controls and compliance infrastructure required for regulated industries.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** ClickUp Brain\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-powered project management, task automation, documentation, team collaboration, and process optimization within a unified workspace.\\n- **Target Industry:** General enterprise (project teams, operations, franchise management); not positioned for healthcare, financial services, or government.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Multi-user team collaboration (store managers, leadership teams, cross-functional project groups)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production; no formal AI safety testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Franchise operations, multi-location retail, project-driven teams; typical ROI: 33% overhead reduction, 10+ hours/week saved, top 10% talent retention\\n- **Product Description:** ClickUp Brain is an AI-enabled project management platform that centralizes projects, documentation, and team chat into a single workspace. It leverages third-party AI models (data provenance unknown) to automate task tracking, reduce process overhead, and improve team collaboration. The product is positioned for general enterprise use and does not appear to have been designed or tested for regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** ClickUp (legal entity not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2017\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Diego, CA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-centric; global reach not confirmed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Third-party models (specific model names, architectures, and versions not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Task automation, documentation generation, process optimization, team collaboration enhancement; specific capabilities (NLP, code generation, summarization) not detailed\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; staged deployment approach not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level transparency, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data provenance unknown; no documentation of data sources, filtering, or bias mitigation in training sets\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red-team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; frequency and scope not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations mentioned; no audit frequency or schedule\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No human oversight capabilities documented; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows specified\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, release documentation, or impact assessments provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but **not tested**; maturity level unclear; no evidence of annual testing, tabletop exercises, or validation\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; capability appears functional but not independently validated\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Project data, task information, documentation, team communications (chat); specific data categories not detailed\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no evidence of PII classification, handling procedures, or customer data usage restrictions\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (assumed); retention options not specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status (in transit / at rest) not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** \\"We will only retain your personal data as long as reasonably required\\" (generic policy language; no specific retention periods, deletion schedules, or zero-retention options documented)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no evidence of customer choice, EU data residency, or regional compliance options\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion capability not explicitly confirmed; automated deletion not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** NIST CSF only; **no SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or GDPR certifications**\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no evidence of third-party audit, internal audit, or assessment\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST CSF alignment claimed; GDPR, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** No BAA or HIPAA compliance mentioned; product not positioned for healthcare\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance documentation provided\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; no audit history provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime/year); contractual commitment level not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, or change notification procedures documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment frequency or process documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No SLAs from critical vendors provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability, retention, and SIEM integration not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results, policy documentation, or evidence files provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n### Scoring Rationale (Applied Formula Guidance)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS) formula** from the vector database:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85/100 (third-party models with unknown training data, no bias testing, no formal safety testing, proprietary/closed)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.25 (minimal controls: no AI governance policy, no bias audits, no human oversight documented)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.60 (no third-party audit, no formal testing, basic telemetry only)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.25) × 0.60 = 38.25 ≈ 38**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n- Certifications: 8 points (NIST CSF only; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR)\\n- Assessment Quality: 3 points (self-assessment only; no third-party audit)\\n- Policies: 12 points (incident response documented but untested; no AI ethics policy, no data retention specifics, no privacy framework)\\n- Operational Controls: 15 points (rollback automated; no human oversight, no continuous monitoring, no version control documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10 points (established company, 7 years old, Series D+, profitable)\\n- **Governance Score = 8 + 3 + 12 + 15 + 10 = 48 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 − 48 = 52**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; strong but not enterprise-grade 99.95%)\\n- Incident Management: 8 points (documented but untested; no automation evidence)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 15 points (cloud SaaS, multi-tenant assumed; infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- Stability: 18 points (7-year-old company, Series D+, profitable)\\n- Support: 8 points (no 24/7 support SLAs documented; no dedicated TAM mentioned)\\n- **Operational Score = 25 + 8 + 15 + 18 + 8 = 74 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 − 74 = 26**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n- VTS = 100 − [(38 × 0.40) + (52 × 0.30) + (26 × 0.30)]\\n- VTS = 100 − [15.2 + 15.6 + 7.8]\\n- VTS = 100 − 38.6\\n- **VTS = 61.4 ≈ 61**\\n\\n**Adjusted to 58** after accounting for: (1) no formal AI safety testing, (2) training data provenance unknown, (3) no documented AI ethics policy, (4) incident response untested, (5) minimal compliance certifications.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Classification & Recommendation\\n\\n**Grade: D (Review Recommended)**  \\n**Score Range: 60–69** (per vector database rubric: \\"Significant gaps; immature processes; limited track record\\")\\n\\n**Recommended Action:**\\n- ✅ **APPROVED FOR:** General project management, non-regulated team collaboration, internal operations\\n- ❌ **NOT APPROVED FOR:** Healthcare (PHI), financial services, government, legal, or any regulated industry without major remediation\\n\\n**Conditional Approval Path (if regulated use case required):**\\n\\n| Remediation Item | Current State | Target State | Effort |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| AI Governance Policy | None | Board-approved, operationalized | High |\\n| Bias Testing & Audits | None | Annual third-party audit | High |\\n| Compliance Certifications | NIST CSF only | SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 + HIPAA/GDPR | Very High |\\n| Incident Response Testing | Documented, untested | Tested annually | Medium |\\n| Training Data Documentation | Unknown | Fully documented with filtering/bias mitigation | High |\\n| Human Oversight Framework | None | Admin controls + monitoring + intervention | High |\\n| Support SLAs | Not specified | 24/7 P1 response + dedicated TAM | Medium |\\n\\n**Timeline for Remediation:** 12–18 months  \\n**Estimated Cost:** $500K–$1M (compliance, audits, policy development, testing)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Summary for Procurement\\n\\n**ClickUp Brain is a mature, operationally reliable project management platform suitable for general enterprise use.** However, it **lacks the AI governance, compliance infrastructure, and safety testing required for regulated industries or sensitive data handling.** The vendor should be considered for:\\n\\n- ✅ Internal team collaboration, task management, documentation\\n- ✅ Non-regulated business operations\\n- ❌ Healthcare, finance, government, or any PHI/PII-intensive use case\\n\\n**For regulated use cases, require vendor commitment to:** (1) SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 certification, (2) documented AI ethics policy + annual bias audits, (3) HIPAA BAA / GDPR DPA, (4) formal AI safety testing roadmap, (5) enhanced support SLAs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Analyst:** Vendor Attestation Assessment System  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (limited vendor-provided documentation; inferences based on industry standards)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "ClickUp Brain", "Customer Base": "Franchise operations, multi-location retail, project-driven teams; typical ROI: 33% overhead reduction, 10+ hours/week saved, top 10% talent retention", "Target Industry": "General enterprise (project teams, operations, franchise management); not positioned for healthcare, financial services, or government.", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Multi-user team collaboration (store managers, leadership teams, cross-functional project groups)", "Primary Use Case": "AI-powered project management, task automation, documentation, team collaboration, and process optimization within a unified workspace.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "ClickUp Brain is an AI-enabled project management platform that centralizes projects, documentation, and team chat into a single workspace. It leverages third-party AI models (data provenance unknown) to automate task tracking, reduce process overhead, and improve team collaboration. The product is positioned for general enterprise use and does not appear to have been designed or tested for regulated industries (healthcare, finance, government).", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production; no formal AI safety testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "ClickUp (legal entity not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2017", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed US-centric; global reach not confirmed)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Diego, CA, USA; investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Third-party models (specific model names, architectures, and versions not disclosed)", "Model Purpose": "Task automation, documentation generation, process optimization, team collaboration enhancement; specific capabilities (NLP, code generation, summarization) not detailed", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy provided; staged deployment approach not specified", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level transparency, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No bias testing approach documented; no red-team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned", "Penetration Testing": "No formal adversarial security testing conducted; frequency and scope not specified", "Training Data Documentation": "Using third-party models; training data provenance unknown; no documentation of data sources, filtering, or bias mitigation in training sets"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "No bias audits or external evaluations mentioned; no audit frequency or sch