t"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** ClickUp Brain presents a **moderate-to-low trust profile** suitable for non-regulated, general project management use cases but **not recommended for healthcare PHI, financial data, or other sensitive regulated environments** without substantial remediation. The vendor demonstrates solid operational maturity (99.9% SLA, established company) and basic security posture (NIST CSF), but critical gaps in AI governance, compliance depth, and data practices significantly elevate residual risk. Specifically: (1) no documented AI governance policy or bias testing framework; (2) minimal compliance certifications (NIST CSF only; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or GDPR DPA); (3) training data sourced from third-party models with unknown provenance; (4) incident response plan documented but untested; (5) no formal AI safety testing conducted. The company's Series D+ maturity and 99.9% uptime are strengths, but they do not offset the absence of enterprise-grade AI controls and compliance infrastructure required for regulated industries. ---", "overallScore": 83, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.11, "Governance": 86, "Operational": 61}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   83 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       39.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        14.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.89  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (39.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (14.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (61.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:17:08.422255+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	83	B	bfba3f4a-4e89-41e8-adaf-1d1d6d572c33	\N	\N
