the API, data is explicitly not used for training. Standard data retention for enterprise accounts is 30 days, and Zero Data Retention (ZDR) is available for qualifying Enterprise customers. Effective September 15, 2025, standard API log retention was reduced to 7 days, though organizations can opt for a 30-day retention period via a Data Processing Addendum for auditing purposes.	\N	\N	\N	Partial documentation available	No SLA	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes	Yes	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:43:12.108309+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Claude Cowork	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:43:12.121+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Anthropic – Claude Cowork\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 60\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAnthropic demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type I/II, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA) and a growth-stage company profile (founded 2021, 1,001–5,000 employees) that support enterprise readiness. However, the trust score is moderated by significant gaps in operational maturity (no contractual uptime SLA, untested incident response, undocumented support SLAs), limited AI governance transparency (no documented AI governance policy, partial training data documentation), and data practices constraints (US-only residency, indefinite consumer data retention). The product's autonomous desktop execution model and emphasis on AI safety (Claude constitution) are strengths, but the lack of operational SLAs and governance documentation creates material risk for regulated industries. **Recommendation:** Acceptable for pilot or non-critical workloads; require contractual SLA commitments and enhanced governance documentation before production deployment in healthcare or financial services.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Claude Cowork\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Autonomous multi-step knowledge work automation; document processing, data analysis, report generation; marketing and engineering workflow automation\\n- **Target Industry:** Marketing, Engineering, General Enterprise\\n- **Deployment Model:** Desktop AI agent (local execution)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Desktop-hosted (local files and applications); no cloud upload required\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Individual or team-level (typical early-adopter deployment)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C vendor)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Early adopters reported; specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Claude Cowork is a desktop AI agent that autonomously executes multi-step knowledge work tasks directly on a user's local machine, integrating with local files and applications without requiring cloud data uploads. The product emphasizes AI safety and transparency, guided by Anthropic's Claude constitution framework. It is designed to free knowledge workers from routine tasks, enabling focus on strategic work.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Anthropic (assumed; legal entity not explicitly stated)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not stated\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (implied: US-based; global reach not documented)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary Claude model (closed); agentic behavior for non-developers\\n- **Model Purpose:** Multi-step task execution, document processing, data analysis, report generation, workflow automation\\n- **Model Governance:** Guided by Anthropic's \\"Claude constitution\\" framework; emphasis on AI safety and transparency; autonomous execution with local-only data handling\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; autonomous desktop execution implies limited real-time human intervention by design\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary model with emphasis on transparency; specific explainability features (citations, prompt-level control) not documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data composition and sources not fully disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no documented red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Claude constitution framework documented; specific usage policies and safety guidelines not detailed in attestation\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluation schedule documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Autonomous execution model; admin controls, content filtering, and intervention mechanisms not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards or release documentation mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level unclear\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; deployment rollback process documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Local files, documents, structured data, application data (desktop-local execution)\\n- **PII Handling:** Enterprise accounts (Claude for Work, API) explicitly exclude training use; consumer versions (indefinite retention) may pose PII risk if user data is retained\\n- **Data Collection:** Desktop-local collection (no cloud upload); API and chat interface available for enterprise\\n- **Data Storage:** Local desktop storage (Claude Cowork); enterprise accounts use Anthropic infrastructure with encryption (not specified)\\n- **Data Retention:** \\n  - Consumer: Indefinite retention unless deleted (30-day deletion lag)\\n  - Enterprise (Claude for Work, API): 30 days standard; **Zero Data Retention (ZDR) available** for qualifying enterprise customers\\n  - API logs: 7 days (effective Sept 15, 2025); 30-day option via Data Processing Addendum\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** **US only** (no EU or customer-choice options documented)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion with 30-day lag for consumer; enterprise deletion policies not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 1 ✓\\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - ISO 27001 ✓\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management) ✓\\n  - HIPAA BAA ✓\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Not specified\\n  - GDPR: Not specified; no DPA mentioned (US-only residency suggests limited GDPR readiness)\\n  - CCPA: Not specified\\n  - EU AI Act: Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; enterprise accounts exclude training use of customer data\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not documented; US-only data residency and indefinite consumer retention suggest gaps\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no preparation or engagement documented\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit schedule and findings not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** **No SLA** (material gap for enterprise production use)\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not documented; no severity-based response targets provided\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication sub-processors not documented\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, available; scope and export capability not detailed\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, available; export capability and format not specified\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Testing results available; specific documentation files not listed\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, available under NDA; scope and findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Compliance posture:** SOC 2 Type I/II, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, and HIPAA BAA demonstrate mature security and AI management frameworks.\\n2. **Data privacy (enterprise):** Explicit exclusion of enterprise customer data from training; Zero Data Retention option for qualifying customers.\\n3. **AI safety emphasis:** Claude constitution framework and transparency commitment align with responsible AI principles.\\n4. **Local execution model:** Desktop-only deployment reduces cloud data exposure and residency concerns for non-regulated use cases.\\n5. **Company maturity:** Growth-stage vendor (Series B/C, 1,001–5,000 employees) with established funding and market presence.\\n\\n### Gaps & Risks\\n1. **No uptime SLA:** Absence of contractual uptime commitment is a critical gap for production enterprise workloads; unacceptable for mission-critical systems.\\n2. **Untested incident response:** Documented but not tested incident response plan creates uncertainty about operational resilience.\\n3. **Limited AI governance transparency:** No documented AI governance policy, bias audit schedule, or human-in-the-loop controls; partial training data documentation.\\n4. **Data residency constraints:** US-only residency incompatible with GDPR, CCPA, or multi-region enterprise requirements.\\n5. **Consumer data retention risk:** Indefinite retention for consumer versions poses PII exposure if product is used with sensitive data.\\n6. **No support SLAs:** Absence of severity-based support response targets; unclear support maturity.\\n7. **Incomplete sub-processor documentation:** Critical vendors and SLAs not disclosed; vendor risk assessment frequency not specified.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**APPROVED FOR PILOT / NON-CRITICAL WORKLOADS; CONDITIONAL FOR PRODUCTION**\\n\\n**Conditions for Production Deployment:**\\n- Require written uptime SLA commitment (minimum 99.5% for enterprise tier)\\n- Obtain tested incident response plan with third-party validation\\n- Provide documented AI governance policy, bias audit schedule, and human-in-the-loop control specifications\\n- Clarify support response SLAs by severity level\\n- For regulated industries (healthcare, finance): Require EU data residency option or explicit GDPR/CCPA compliance roadmap\\n- For healthcare: Require BAA execution and confirmation of enterprise data exclusion from training\\n- Obtain sub-processor list and SLA commitments from critical vendors\\n\\n**Use Case Fit:**\\n- ✓ **Suitable:** Non-regulated knowledge work automation, internal document processing, engineering team workflows, marketing automation\\n- ✗ **Not suitable (without conditions):** Healthcare PHI processing, financial services regulated data, EU customer data, mission-critical production systems\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (partial data; several operational and governance details not specified)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Claude Cowork", "Customer Base": "Early adopters reported; specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "Marketing, Engineering, General Enterprise", "Deployment Model": "Desktop AI agent (local execution)", "Deployment Scale": "Individual or team-level (typical early-adopter deployment)", "Primary Use Case": "Autonomous multi-step knowledge work automation; document processing, data analysis, report generation; marketing and engineering workflow automation", "Hosted / Deployed": "Desktop-hosted (local files and applications); no cloud upload required", "Product Description": "Claude Cowork is a desktop AI agent that autonomously executes multi-step knowledge work tasks directly on a user's local machine, integrating with local files and applications without requiring cloud data uploads. The product emphasizes AI safety and transparency, guided by Anthropic's Claude constitution framework. It is designed to free knowledge workers from routine tasks, enabling focus on strategic work.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C vendor)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Anthropic (assumed; legal entity not explicitly stated)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2021", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (implied: US-based; global reach not documented)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not stated", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not specified"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary Claude model (closed); agentic behavior for non-deve