nt deletion. For API customers, the default log retention was reduced to 7 days as of September 14, 2025, though a 30-day retention period can be opted into via a Data Processing Addendum. Zero Data Retention (ZDR) agreements are available for qualifying enterprise API customers.	\N	\N	\N	Summary only (no detailed lineage)	99.99% (52 min/year downtime)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, comprehensive analytics	Yes	Yes, comprehensive test reports	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:43:56.583401+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Claude Design	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:43:56.596+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Anthropic – Claude Design\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 82 **(Trusted Vendor)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 88\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 78\\n- AI Governance: 72\\n- Operations: 90\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nAnthropic demonstrates strong operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications (SOC 2 Type I/II, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA, FedRAMP), and excellent uptime (99.99% SLA). However, the Trust Score reflects moderate gaps in AI governance transparency (proprietary model, limited documented governance policy) and data practices (consumer data retention on backend systems for 30 days post-deletion, limited bias testing documentation). The vendor's established stage (Series D+, 1,001–5,000 employees, founded 2021) and strong compliance posture support a \\"Trusted Vendor\\" classification suitable for standard procurement with enhanced due diligence on AI safety and governance practices.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Claude Design\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Efficient and consistent visual content creation; design system integration; brand guideline automation; conversational design iteration\\n- **Target Industry:** Design, product development, marketing, enterprise creative teams\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS); Hybrid (Cloud + On-prem) options available\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted primary; customer choice of region; on-premises deployment supported\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise; typical deployment supports design teams and product organizations\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; early adopters reporting significant time savings (20+ prompt iterations reduced to 2; working prototypes in single conversation)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Early adopter base with documented ROI; specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Claude Design is a conversational AI-powered design tool that integrates with existing design systems to automatically apply brand guidelines and enable natural language refinement of visual content. It supports multi-modal input (text, voice, video, shaders, 3D components) and frontier design capabilities, reducing design iteration cycles and maintaining brand consistency across projects. The product leverages Anthropic's Claude LLM family for complex reasoning and generation tasks.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Anthropic (legal entity name not specified; operating as Anthropic)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not stated\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not enumerated; customer choice of data residency supported)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Models (LLM family: Claude); multi-modal capabilities (text, voice, video, 3D components)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Problem-solving, complex task execution (data analysis, code writing, design generation, product descriptions); conversational iteration; design system reasoning\\n- **Model Governance:** Proprietary/Closed model; governance policy documented but not detailed in attestation; frontier capabilities (voice, video, shaders, 3D) indicate staged capability rollout\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; inferred: design system integration and brand guideline application suggest rule-based constraints; conversational interface implies user-driven iteration and control\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary model; transparency level not specified; conversational interface enables user refinement and feedback loops\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Summary only (no detailed lineage); training data sources and composition not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no documented red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; comprehensive test reports available but methodology not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy exists but details not provided in attestation; company description emphasizes \\"reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems\\"\\n- **Bias Audits:** Frequency and external evaluation approach not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Conversational design iteration implies user control; design system integration and brand guideline automation suggest rule-based constraints; specific admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation not mentioned; comprehensive test reports available but scope not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; formal incident response procedures exist but lack evidence of tabletop exercises or real-world validation\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback is supported and can be executed manually when needed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Design inputs (text, voice, video, 3D components); conversation history; design artifacts; brand guidelines; design system data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; inferred: design content may contain PII depending on customer use case; no explicit statement on PII filtering or redaction\\n- **Data Collection:** API, chat interface, design tool interface; interaction data collected for analytics\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud infrastructure (customer choice of region); on-premises deployment option available; encryption not explicitly stated\\n- **Data Retention:** \\n  - **Consumer accounts:** Conversations saved until user deletion; retained on backend for up to 30 days post-deletion before permanent removal\\n  - **API customers:** Default 7-day log retention (as of September 14, 2025); 30-day retention available via Data Processing Addendum\\n  - **Enterprise API customers:** Zero Data Retention (ZDR) agreements available for qualifying customers\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; hybrid (Cloud + On-prem) deployment supported\\n- **Data Deletion:** User-initiated deletion for consumer accounts; automated deletion after retention period; on-request deletion for enterprise customers under ZDR agreements\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; inferred: cloud infrastructure providers (likely AWS/Azure/GCP), payment processors, authentication services\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 1\\n  - SOC 2 Type 2\\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n  - FedRAMP (Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type I/II and ISO certifications imply third-party audit; audit methodology and frequency not detailed\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Implied compliance via FedRAMP authorization\\n  - GDPR: Not explicitly stated; Data Processing Addendum available for API customers suggests GDPR readiness\\n  - CCPA: Not explicitly stated\\n  - EU AI Act: Not explicitly stated; ISO 42001 (AI Management) certification suggests alignment with AI governance frameworks\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** HIPAA BAA available; vendor is eligible to sign Business Associate Agreements for healthcare data processing\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Data Processing Addendum available for API customers; customer choice of data residency and Zero Data Retention options support GDPR compliance\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not explicitly stated; ISO 42001 certification indicates AI governance maturity; specific EU AI Act compliance roadmap not provided\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Audit frequency: Not specified\\n  - Last audit date: Not specified\\n  - Audit findings: Not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year maximum downtime); contractual commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tier structure and response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not detailed; automated rollback with manual trigger capability indicates mature deployment practices\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; inferred: cloud infrastructure providers (AWS/Azure/GCP), payment processors, authentication services\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key vendor SLAs not documented; cloud infrastructure SLAs inferred from 99.99% uptime commitment\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; interaction data collected and available for monitoring and optimization\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, audit logs available; export capability and format not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Comprehensive test reports available; detailed policy documentation not provided in attestation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, comprehensive test reports available; testing methodology and scope not detailed; availability under NDA not explicitly stated\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Exceptional Compliance & Security Posture:** SOC 2 Type I/II, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA, and FedRAMP certifications demonstrate enterprise-grade security and regulatory alignment.\\n2. **Strong Operational Reliability:** 99.99% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability indicate mature production operations.\\n3. **Data Privacy Options:** Zero Data Retention agreements, customer choice of region, and hybrid deployment support GDPR and enterprise privacy requirements.\\n4. **Established Company Maturity:** Series D+ funding, 1,001–5,000 employees, and 3+ years profitability indicate financial stability and operational scale.\\n\\n### Gaps & Mitigation Recommendations\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency (Gap: Moderate):** Proprietary model with limited documented governance policy; no detailed bias testing, red team results, or explainability framework disclosed.\\n   - **Mitigation:** Request detailed AI governance policy, bias testing methodology, and adversarial testing results under NDA before production deployment.\\n\\n2. **Training Data Lineage (Gap: Moderate):** Summary-only documentation of training data; no detailed composition, sources, or filtering practices disclosed.\\n   - **Mitigation:** Request detailed training data documentation and filtering practices for sensitive use cases (e.g., healthcare, financial).\\n\\n3. **Support SLA Documentation (Gap: Minor):** Support response SLAs by severity not specified; support structure and escalation procedures not documented.\\n   - **Mitigation:** Request detailed support SLA documentation and escalation procedures in contract negotiation.\\n\\n4. **Incident Response Validation (Gap: Minor):** Incident response plan documented but not tested; no evidence of tabletop exercises or real-world validation.\\n   - **Mitigation:** Request evidence of incident response testing (tabletop exercises, post-incident reviews) or require vendor to conduct testing within 6 months of contract execution.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT** with enhanced due diligence on AI governance and safety practices. Suitable for enterprise deployment with:\\n- Requirement to provide detailed AI governance policy, bias testing results, and training data documentation under NDA\\n- Incident response testing validation within 6 months of contract execution\\n- Support SLA documentation and escalation procedures in contract terms\\n- For healthcare/regulated use cases: Require HIPAA BAA execution and Zero Data Retention agreement\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Methodology:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Framework (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)])", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Claude Design", "Customer Base": "Early adopter base with documented ROI; specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "Design, product development, marketing, enterprise creative teams", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS); Hybrid (Cloud + On-prem) options available", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise; typical deployment suppo