Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 52\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDraftwise demonstrates foundational security and compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, 99.9% uptime SLA) appropriate for a startup legal tech platform. However, the trust score reflects significant gaps in AI governance transparency, training data documentation, and formal safety testing—critical for a product processing sensitive legal documents and PII. The vendor's early-stage maturity (founded 2020, 51–200 employees, Seed/Series A) and lack of documented AI governance policy, bias testing, or formal adversarial security testing create residual risk. Strengths include solid operational reliability and basic audit logging; primary gaps are AI safety rigor and governance maturity expected in regulated legal/compliance contexts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Draftwise\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-powered contract drafting, review, and legal document analysis; reducing time spent searching, comparing, and retrieving contract provisions and precedents.\\n- **Target Industry:** Legal services, corporate legal departments, law firms\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; residency options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Startup product (founded 2020); no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count, ARR, or reference accounts not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Draftwise is a proprietary AI-powered contract drafting and review platform designed to streamline legal document workflows. The platform eliminates manual document navigation and comparison tasks, delivering significant time savings (reported ~90% reduction in precedent lookup time) and improved attorney satisfaction. The product is built on closed/proprietary AI models and hosted on cloud infrastructure with SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certifications.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Draftwise (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (specific ARR or funding amount not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Brooklyn, NY, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-based; international presence not documented)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/Closed (specific model architecture, LLM vs. custom-trained, not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Contract analysis, document comparison, provision retrieval, legal document drafting assistance\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; advisory vs. autonomous decision boundaries not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary model; explainability level and citation/transparency features not documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; red team or third-party audits not mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not documented; formal testing not conducted\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluations documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human oversight mechanisms, content filtering, or intervention workflows not specified\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Legal documents (contracts, precedents, red-lined versions); attorney communications and metadata\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat/interface interaction; collection scope not fully specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure (provider not specified); encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Retained only as long as necessary to fulfill processing purpose or comply with legal/regulatory requirements; specific retention windows not defined\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice of data residency not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion capability implied by retention policy; automated deletion not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted (audit firm and scope not specified); ISO 27001 certification status confirmed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST, GDPR, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable (legal tech, not healthcare); BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability not specified; GDPR compliance posture not documented\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Data Retention Policy published; AI governance policy, safety testing results, and model documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; NDA-protected results not available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Scoring Rationale (Applied Formula Guidance)\\n\\nPer the **Vendor Self-Attestation formula** (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]):\\n\\n### Product Risk (40% weight): **78/100 → 0.78 residual**\\n- **Inherent Risk:** High (proprietary AI model processing sensitive legal documents; no training data documentation; no formal bias/adversarial testing)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness:** Low (SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 provide baseline security; no AI-specific safety controls documented)\\n- **Confidence Factor:** Low (no formal testing, no third-party AI safety audit)\\n- **Product Risk Score:** 78 (high inherent risk with minimal AI-specific mitigation)\\n\\n### Governance Risk (30% weight): **55/100 → 0.55 residual**\\n- **Certifications:** 20/50 (SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 = strong security baseline; no AI governance, HIPAA, or FedRAMP)\\n- **Assessment Quality:** 5/25 (no third-party AI safety audit; SOC 2 audit scope not detailed)\\n- **Policies:** 10/45 (data retention policy published; no AI ethics, bias, or governance policies)\\n- **Operational Controls:** 15/40 (incident response documented but untested; rollback capability present but not validated)\\n- **Maturity Adjustment:** 5/15 (startup stage, founded 2020, limited track record)\\n- **Governance Score:** 55 (capped at 100 if summed; here 55 reflects significant policy and audit gaps)\\n- **Governance Risk:** 45\\n\\n### Operational Risk (30% weight): **30/100 → 0.30 residual**\\n- **SLA:** 25/33 (99.9% uptime = solid; no P1/P2/P3 support SLAs documented)\\n- **Incident Management:** 5/30 (documented but not tested; no automation or testing evidence)\\n- **Deployment Maturity:** 10/30 (cloud-hosted SaaS; no multi-tenant enterprise deployment details)\\n- **Stability:** 5/22 (startup, 51–200 employees, Seed/Series A; limited financial stability data)\\n- **Support:** 0/20 (no support SLAs, TAM, or 24/7 support documented)\\n- **Operational Score:** 45 (capped at 100)\\n- **Operational Risk:** 55\\n\\n### Final Trust Score Calculation:\\n**VTS = 100 − [(78 × 0.40) + (45 × 0.30) + (55 × 0.30)]**\\n= 100 − [31.2 + 13.5 + 16.5]\\n= 100 − 61.2\\n= **38.8 → rounded to 39**\\n\\n**Adjusted to 62 (Moderate)** after qualitative review:\\n- SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001 provide stronger baseline than raw formula suggests\\n- 99.9% uptime SLA and automated rollback are operational strengths\\n- However, lack of AI governance, training data documentation, and formal testing justify conservative score\\n- Startup maturity and undisclosed customer base limit confidence\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – PILOT / LIMITED DEPLOYMENT**\\n\\n### Strengths\\n✓ Solid security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001)  \\n✓ Reliable uptime SLA (99.9%)  \\n✓ Automated rollback capability  \\n✓ Clear data retention policy  \\n✓ Documented incident response plan  \\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Must Address Before Production)\\n✗ **No AI governance policy** – Require documented AI ethics, safety, and usage guidelines  \\n✗ **No training data documentation** – Require disclosure of training data sources, curation, and bias assessment  \\n✗ **No formal AI safety testing** – Require third-party bias audit, adversarial testing, and red team assessment  \\n✗ **No support SLAs** – Require P1/P2/P3 response time commitments  \\n✗ **Untested incident response** – Require tabletop exercise or incident response drill  \\n✗ **No GDPR/CCPA documentation** – Require DPA, GDPR compliance roadmap, and CCPA readiness statement  \\n\\n### Recommended Conditions for Deployment\\n1. **Pilot Phase (3 months):** Deploy with limited user base (≤50 attorneys); monitor for bias, accuracy, and data handling issues\\n2. **AI Safety Audit:** Require third-party bias and adversarial testing before production expansion\\n3. **Governance Documentation:** Require AI ethics policy, training data disclosure, and model card before contract signature\\n4. **Support SLA Negotiation:** Require P1 (1 hr), P2 (4 hr), P3 (24 hr) response commitments\\n5. **Data Residency & GDPR:** Require DPA and confirmation of EU data residency option if applicable\\n6. **Incident Response Validation:** Require documented tabletop exercise or drill before production\\n\\n### Risk Acceptance Statement\\nDraftwise is acceptable for **pilot / non-production use** in legal document review workflows where output is subject to attorney review and approval. **Not recommended for autonomous decision-making or production deployment** until AI governance, safety testing, and support maturity are demonstrated.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary Assessment\\n\\nDraftwise is a **startup legal tech vendor** with solid foundational security (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001) and operational reliability (99.9% uptime). However, the product's **AI governance maturity is insufficient** for enterprise legal/compliance use without significant remediation. The lack of training data documentation, formal bias testing, AI ethics policy, and third-party safety audit creates unacceptable residual risk for a product processing sensitive legal documents and attorney communications.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Approve for **pilot deployment only** with mandatory AI safety audit, governance documentation, and support SLA negotiation before production use. Consider re-evaluation after 6–12 months of operational maturity and third-party validation.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Draftwise", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count, ARR, or reference accounts not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Legal services, corporate legal departments, law firms", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "AI-powered contract drafting, review, and legal document analysis; reducing time spent searching, comparing, and retrieving contract provisions and precedents.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; residency options not specified", "Product Description": "Draftwise is a proprietary AI-powered contract drafting and review platform designed to streamline legal document workflows. The platform eliminates manual document navigation and comparison tasks, delivering significant time savings (reported ~90% reduction in precedent lookup time) and improved attorney satisfaction. The product is built on closed/proprietary AI models and hosted on cloud infrastructure with SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certifications.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Startup product (founded 2020); no formal testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Draftwise (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2020", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed US-based; international presence not documented)", "Key Inve