turity that outweigh moderate operational capabilities. The vendor is a newly founded (August 2024) growth-stage company with minimal security certifications, no documented AI governance policy, and no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing. While the product demonstrates a strong operational SLA (99.95% uptime) and basic audit logging, the absence of SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA eligibility, or third-party compliance audits—combined with undocumented training data and no bias detection framework—creates unacceptable residual risk for healthcare PHI handling. The vendor's early maturity stage, lack of independent compliance validation, and absence of formal AI safety testing are the primary drivers of the low trust score. ---", "overallScore": 75, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.32, "Governance": 69, "Operational": 55}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   75 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         C - Acceptable Vendor\\n  Next step:     Enhanced due diligence; require mitigation roadmap\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       45.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        31.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            4.68  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (45.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (31.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (55.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Raise Governance (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:20:44.665586+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	75	C	6bb566d9-5e81-455c-8214-8690c5bacd04	\N	\N
94d22bd4-fe4a-446d-a896-019a65634e63	42fcbc96-eaa6-4240-be91-d29ccd0aa488	39	39	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Technology": ["Technology"]}	Established (Series D+/Profitable 3+ years)	https://www.apollo.io	Apollo is a leading data intelligence and sales engagement platform trusted by 40,000 paying customers, from rapidly growing startups to some of the largest global enterprises. Its community-based approach to crowdsourcing data gives users maximum coverage while ensuring data accuracy.	201-1,000	2015	San Francisco, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "VP Product", "Line of Business Leader"]	Apollo.io addresses the challenges of inefficient sales pipeline generation, lack of accurate data for decision-making, and suboptimal team performance. By leveraging AI-driven insights and community-based data crowdsourcing, it helps businesses streamline their go-to-market strategies and improve sales outcomes.	\N	Apollo.io's community-based approach to crowdsourcing data ensures maximum coverage and accuracy, while its AI-driven GTM guidance helps teams optimize their sales strategies. The platform's integration with third-party AI providers enhances functionality and provides advanced insights.	Apollo.io customers experience a significant reduction in manual data entry and improved sales pipeline generation, leading to faster deal closures and higher team productivity.	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["GDPR Compliant"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region"]	Apollo.io retains customer data for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law. Data deletion procedures are in place to ensure that data is securely erased when no longer needed.	\N	\N	\N	Partial documentation available	99.95% (4.4 hrs/year)	Yes, tested quarterly	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:46:24.435589+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Apollo AI	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:46:24.445+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Apollo AI (Apollo.io)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 75\\n- Compliance: 68\\n- Data Practices: 70\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 80\\n- Company Maturity: 78\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nApollo scores in the \\"Acceptable\\" range (70–79) with solid operational maturity (99.95% SLA, quarterly incident testing, automated rollback) and established company credentials (Series D+, 8+ years, 40,000 customers). However, the score is constrained by moderate AI governance transparency, partial training data documentation, and limited evidence of bias testing or adversarial security testing. The vendor demonstrates reasonable data practices (customer choice of residency, deletion procedures) and GDPR compliance, but lacks deeper certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA) and detailed AI safety frameworks that would elevate trust in regulated or high-stakes use cases. Strengths include proven operational reliability and community-driven data accuracy; gaps include AI explainability depth and comprehensive security/compliance posture.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Apollo AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Sales pipeline generation, data-driven GTM guidance, sales team performance optimization, lead intelligence and engagement\\n- **Target Industry:** B2B sales, enterprise go-to-market; applicable across verticals (startups to Fortune 500)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (region selection available per customer choice)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale; 40,000 paying customers ranging from startups to large global enterprises\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product with basic test results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** 40,000 paying customers (mix of rapidly growing startups and large global enterprises)\\n- **Product Description:** Apollo AI is a data intelligence and sales engagement platform that combines community-based data crowdsourcing with AI-driven insights to streamline sales pipeline generation and GTM strategy. The platform integrates third-party AI providers to enhance functionality and decision-making. It emphasizes data accuracy through crowdsourcing while offering moderate explainability features and customer choice of data residency.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Apollo (trading as Apollo.io)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not detailed; customer choice of data residency supported)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (vendor integrates third-party AI providers; internal model types not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Sales pipeline generation, lead scoring, GTM guidance, team performance insights, data enrichment\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; documented AI governance policy not provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; human-in-the-loop controls and intervention mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features available; depth and scope not specified)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available (full scope and lineage not disclosed)\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no mention of red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; adversarial security testing approach not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified; documented AI governance policy not provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; frequency and external evaluations not disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; admin controls, content filtering, and intervention workflows not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; system cards or release documentation not mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested quarterly (demonstrates active incident management maturity)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option (supports rapid recovery from failed deployments)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Business contact data, sales pipeline records, lead intelligence, team performance metrics (specific data types not exhaustively listed)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and customer data usage for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface (specific collection mechanisms not detailed)\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure (specific encryption standards not specified)\\n- **Data Retention:** Retained for as long as necessary to fulfill collection purposes; longer retention permitted by law; deletion procedures in place\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (specific regions available not listed)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and automated per retention policy; procedures documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Third-party AI providers integrated; specific infrastructure, payment, and auth vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** GDPR Compliant (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, FedRAMP, or other security certifications not mentioned)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; vendor engagement or preparation not documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; independent audit frequency and findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours downtime per year; enterprise-grade availability)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity not disclosed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Third-party AI providers integrated; specific infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of vendor risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical sub-processors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (scope and granularity not specified)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available (export capability and retention not specified)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; availability under NDA not confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Formula Applied\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from the retrieved vector database (Assessment Type 1):\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n### Component Calculations\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n- **Inherent Risk:** 65 (moderate; sales/GTM data is business-sensitive but not life-safety or national security; third-party AI integration introduces model governance uncertainty)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.60 (partial training data documentation, moderate explainability, but no documented bias testing or adversarial security testing)\\n- **Confidence Factor:** 0.75 (basic test results and audit logs available; no independent third-party security audit mentioned)\\n- **Product Risk = 65 × 0.60 × 0.75 = 29.25 ≈ 29**\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n- **Certifications:** 20 points (GDPR compliant only; lacks SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP)\\n- **Assessment Quality:** 15 points (basic audit logs and test results; no independent compliance audit methodology disclosed)\\n- **Policies:** 10 points (data retention and deletion procedures documented; AI governance policy not specified)\\n- **Operational Controls:** 15 points (quarterly incident testing, automated rollback; limited detail on change management and release controls)\\n- **Maturity Adjustment:** 20 points (Series D+, 8+ years, 40,000 customers, profitable 3+ years)\\n- **Governance Score = 20 + 15 + 10 + 15 + 20 = 80 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 80 = 20**\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n- **SLA:** 25 points (99.95% uptime = enterprise-grade; 4.4 hrs/year downtime)\\n- **Incident Management:** 20 points (tested quarterly; mature but not fully automated end-to-end)\\n- **Deployment Maturity:** 22 points (cloud SaaS, multi-tenant, customer choice of region; established platform)\\n- **Stability:** 20 points (Series D+, 8+ years, profitable 3+ years, 40,000 customers)\\n- **Support:** 10 points (support SLAs by severity not specified; basic support assumed)\\n- **Operational Score = 25 + 20 + 22 + 20 + 10 = 97 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 97 = 3**\\n\\n### Final Trust Score Calculation\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(29 × 0.40) + (20 × 0.30) + (3 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [11.6 + 6.0 + 0.9]\\n    = 100 - 18.5\\n    = 81.5 ≈ 82\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 72 (Acceptable range)** after accounting for:\\n- Lack of documented AI governance policy (−5 points)\\n- Absence of bias testing and adversarial security testing (−3 points)\\n- Limited third-party AI provider transparency (−2 points)\\n\\n**Classification: Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RECOMMENDED ACTIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Operational Maturity:** 99.95% SLA, quarterly incident testing, automated rollback, and 8+ years of profitable operations demonstrate production-ready reliability.\\n2. **Scale & Customer Base:** 40,000 paying customers (startups to Fortune 500) validate market fit and operational capability.\\n3. **Data Practices:** Customer choice of data residency, documented deletion procedures, and GDPR compliance support data governance.\\n\\n### Gaps Requiring Attention\\n1. **AI Governance:** Documented AI governance policy, bias audit framework, and adversarial testing roadmap needed before high-stakes deployments.\\n2. **Security Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certifications would strengthen trust; HIPAA BAA eligibility should be clarified if handling healthcare data.\\n3. **Training Data & Model Transparency:** Full training data documentation and third-party AI provider SLAs should be disclosed or contractually required.\\n4. **Support SLAs:** Severity-based response time targets (P1/P2/P3) should be formalized in service agreements.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**STANDARD PROCUREMENT** — Acceptable for general B2B sales and GTM use cases with moderate data sensitivity. For regulated industries (healthcare, financial services) or high-stakes decision-making, require:\\n- SOC 2 Type 2 or ISO 27001 certification roadmap\\n- Documented AI governance policy and bias audit schedule\\n- Third-party AI provider SLA transparency\\n- Enhanced support SLA commitments (P1/P2/P3 response times)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Source:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification Part 1", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Apollo AI", "Customer Base": "40,000 paying customers (mix of rapidly growing startups and large global enterprises)", "Target Industry": "B2B sales, enterprise go-to-market; applicable across verticals (startups to Fortune 500)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise-scale; 40,000 paying customers ranging from startups to large global enterprises", "Primary Use Case": "Sales pipeline generation, data-driven GTM guidance, sales team performance optimization, lead intelligence and engagement", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (region selection available per customer choice)", "Product Description": "Apollo AI is a data intelligence and sales engagement platform that combines community-based data crowdsourcing with AI-driven insights to streamline sales pipeline generation and GTM strategy. The platform integrates third-party AI providers to enhance functionality and decision-making. It emphasizes data accuracy through crowdsourcing while offering moderate explainability features and customer choice of data residency.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product with basic test results available"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Apollo (trading as Apollo.io)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2015", "Operating Regions": "Global (specific regions not detailed; customer choice of data residency supported)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable 3