ified)", "PII Handling": "Not specified; extent of PII processing and customer data usage for training not disclosed", "Data Deletion": "On request and automated per retention policy; procedures documented", "Data Retention": "Retained for as long as necessary to fulfill collection purposes; longer retention permitted by law; deletion procedures in place", "Sub-processors": "Third-party AI providers integrated; specific infrastructure, payment, and auth vendors not disclosed", "Data Collection": "API and platform interface (specific collection mechanisms not detailed)", "Data Types Processed": "Business contact data, sales pipeline records, lead intelligence, team performance metrics (specific data types not exhaustively listed)", "Data Location / Residency": "Customer choice of region (specific regions available not listed)"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "GDPR Compliant (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, FedRAMP, or other security certifications not mentioned)", "GDPR Compliance": "GDPR compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly stated", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not specified; BAA eligibility not confirmed", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; vendor engagement or preparation not documented", "Regulatory Frameworks": "GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST, CCPA, EU AI Act readiness not specified", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology and scope not disclosed", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified; independent audit frequency and findings not disclosed"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.95% (4.4 hours downtime per year; enterprise-grade availability)", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, and readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; response time targets by severity not disclosed"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; SLAs from critical sub-processors not provided", "Critical Vendors": "Third-party AI providers integrated; specific infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not disclosed", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency of vendor risk assessments not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"SLA": "25 points (99.95% uptime = enterprise-grade; 4.4 hrs/year downtime)", "Support": "10 points (support SLAs by severity not specified; basic support assumed)", "Policies": "10 points (data retention and deletion procedures documented; AI governance policy not specified)", "Stability": "20 points (Series D+, 8+ years, profitable 3+ years, 40,000 customers)", "Inherent Risk": "65 (moderate; sales/GTM data is business-sensitive but not life-safety or national security; third-party AI integration introduces model governance uncertainty)", "Certifications": "20 points (GDPR compliant only; lacks SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP)", "Confidence Factor": "0.75 (basic test results and audit logs available; no independent third-party security audit mentioned)", "Assessment Quality": "15 points (basic audit logs and test results; no independent compliance audit methodology disclosed)", "Deployment Maturity": "22 points (cloud SaaS, multi-tenant, customer choice of region; established platform)", "Incident Management": "20 points (tested quarterly; mature but not fully automated end-to-end)", "Maturity Adjustment": "20 points (Series D+, 8+ years, 40,000 customers, profitable 3+ years)", "Operational Controls": "15 points (quarterly incident testing, automated rollback; limited detail on change management and release controls)", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available (export capability and retention not specified)", "Mitigation Effectiveness": "0.60 (partial training data documentation, moderate explainability, but no documented bias testing or adversarial security testing)", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available (scope and granularity not specified)", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not specified; availability under NDA not confirmed", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation not provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Apollo scores in the \\"Acceptable\\" range (70–79) with solid operational maturity (99.95% SLA, quarterly incident testing, automated rollback) and established company credentials (Series D+, 8+ years, 40,000 customers). However, the score is constrained by moderate AI governance transparency, partial training data documentation, and limited evidence of bias testing or adversarial security testing. The vendor demonstrates reasonable data practices (customer choice of residency, deletion procedures) and GDPR compliance, but lacks deeper certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA) and detailed AI safety frameworks that would elevate trust in regulated or high-stakes use cases. Strengths include proven operational reliability and community-driven data accuracy; gaps include AI explainability depth and comprehensive security/compliance posture. ---", "overallScore": 83, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.17, "Governance": 86, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   83 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        14.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.83  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (14.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 14:46:24.435589+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	83	B	d6a24e10-7d69-4eec-b23e-cb51229518d8	\N	\N
aaa369c3-651b-4084-b87f-91519363d38d	0a7a69dd-0a07-4bbc-a015-f29f709b4eae	40	40	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Technology, Professional Services, Retail & E-commerce": ["Technology, Professional Services, Retail & E-commerce"]}	Startup (Seed/Series A)	https://artisan.co/	Artisan AI develops AI agents called 'Artisans' to automate business functions. Their first AI worker, Ava, is a business development representative (BDR) that automates outbound sales processes, including lead discovery, personalized email drafting, and meeting scheduling.	51-200	2023	San Francisco, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "VP Product", "Line of Business Leader"]	Ava addresses the inefficiencies in outbound sales processes, such as time-consuming lead discovery and manual email drafting. It also helps businesses scale their sales operations without increasing headcount, reducing the cost per lead and improving response times.	\N	Ava is a fully autonomous AI BDR, unlike traditional sales tools that require manual input. It also offers personalized email drafting at scale, leveraging advanced NLP capabilities. Additionally, Artisan AI's focus on compliance and security (SOC 2 Type 2) makes it a trusted choice for enterprises.	Businesses using Ava can expect a significant reduction in time spent on manual sales tasks, such as lead discovery and email drafting, leading to faster response times and higher conversion rates. The automation also reduces the need for additional sales staff, lowering operational costs.	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region"]	Artisan AI's data retention policies are not explicitly stated, but as a SOC 2 Type 2 compliant company, they likely follow industry best practices for data retention and deletion, including periodic reviews and secure deletion procedures.	\N	\N	\N	Partial documentation available	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Limited/Partial	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:47:24.501065+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Ava	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:47:24.515+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n**Artisan AI – Ava (AI Business Development Representative)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score: 58** (Moderate Risk – Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 72\\n- Compliance: 65\\n- Data Practices: 55\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 40\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nArtisan AI demonstrates foundational security and operational controls (SOC 2 Type 2, 99.9% SLA, documented incident response) but exhibits significant gaps in AI governance maturity, transparency, and data practices documentation that are critical for enterprise deployment. As a 2023-founded startup (51–200 employees) with seed/Series A funding, the vendor lacks the operational track record and governance infrastructure expected for autonomous AI agents handling business-critical sales functions. The moderate trust score reflects acceptable compliance posture offset by immature AI safety practices, incomplete training data documentation, and limited third-party validation of bias/adversarial testing.\\n\\n**Formula Application (Vendor Self-Attestation, Assessment Type 1):**\\nUsing the vector-DB formula:\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n- **Product Risk (~68/100):** Autonomous decision-making (lead discovery, email drafting, meeting scheduling) on business-critical processes with partial training data documentation, moderate explainability, and limited bias/adversarial testing evidence → inherent risk elevated; mitigation effectiveness moderate due to SOC 2 compliance but gaps in AI-specific controls.\\n- **Governance Risk (~70/100):** SOC 2 Type 2 certification present; AI ethics policy and bias audit frequency not documented; human-in-the-loop controls not specified; impact assessments not mentioned → governance score capped by missing AI governance framework.\\n- **Operational Risk (~30/100):** 99.9% SLA, documented incident response (untested), automated rollback capability, basic audit logging → operational maturity acceptable for startup stage but limited support SLA detail and no 24/7 support confirmation.\\n\\n**Calculated VTS:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(68 × 0.40) + (70 × 0.30) + (30 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 − [27.2 + 21.0 + 9.0]\\n    = 100 − 57.2\\n    ≈ 58\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Ava\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Autonomous outbound sales process automation (lead discovery, personalized email drafting, meeting scheduling)\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise sales/business development (sector-agnostic)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; customer choice of data residency region\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified (typical deployment size not documented)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product (company founded 2023); limited/partial testing results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified\\n- **Product Description:** Ava is a fully autonomous AI business development representative that automates outbound sales workflows including lead discovery, personalized email generation at scale, and meeting scheduling. Unlike traditional sales tools requiring manual input, Ava operates autonomously with advanced NLP capabilities and SOC 2 Type 2 compliance. The product emphasizes enterprise-grade security and compliance posture, though AI governance and bias testing documentation remain limited.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Artisan AI (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS startup\\n- **Year Founded:** 2023\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (specific funding amount not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; key investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not explicitly stated; inferred to be US-based with global SaaS availability\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Model (LLM) with NLP capabilities; specific model architecture (proprietary vs. third-party base) not documented\\n- **Model Purpose:** Lead discovery (data retrieval/analysis), personalized email generation (text generation), meeting scheduling (decision/action automation)\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment framework, canary release process, or safety gates mentioned\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no explicit mention of admin controls, content filtering, or human-in-the-loop intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); specific mechanisms (e.g., prompt-level control, decision citations, confidence scores) not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; specific data sources, composition, and filtering criteria not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not documented; no evidence of red-team testing, third-party bias audits, or statistical monitoring tools\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not documented; no frequency or scope specified; adversarial security testing approach not described\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; usage policies and safety guidelines for autonomous agent behavior not provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not documented; audit frequency and external evaluation partners not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not documented; no mention of admin override capabilities, content review workflows, or escalation procedures for high-risk decisions (e.g., email tone, lead targeting)\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not documented; no system cards, model cards, or release impact assessments mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; formal IRP exists but no evidence of tabletop exercises, incident simulation, or third-party validation\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedure documented but not independently verified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Business contact data (leads), email communications (drafts and sent), meeting scheduling data, customer business context\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly documented; extent of PII processing (email addresses, names, phone numbers, company data) and whether customer data is used for model training not specified\\n- **Data Collection:** API and SaaS interface; collection scope and opt-out mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure; encryption method (at-rest and in-transit) not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Default and optional retention policies not explicitly stated; inferred to follow SOC 2 Type 2 best practices (periodic reviews, secure deletion) but not confirmed\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; specific regions supported not listed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (inferred from SOC 2 compliance); automated deletion schedules not documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not named; payment processor, authentication provider, and other critical sub-processors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2 (primary certification)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted by third-party auditor; specific audit firm and scope not named\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Not mentioned\\n  - GDPR: Not explicitly addressed; DPA availability not confirmed\\n  - CCPA: Not mentioned\\n  - EU AI Act: Not mentioned\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not mentioned; BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not confirmed; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not specified\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not mentioned; no engagement or preparation roadmap documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tier definitions and response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not documented; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not described\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not named; payment processor and authentication provider not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of sub-processors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical infrastructure/payment vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; specific metrics (e.g., email send rates, lead quality, meeting booking success) and export capability not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export format, retention period, and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/partial; AI safety testing results, bias audit reports, and governance policies not provided or available under NDA\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/partial; no indication of third-party model evaluation, adversarial testing reports, or safety validation under NDA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Gaps & Recommendations\\n\\n| Category | Gap | Severity | Recommendation |\\n|----------|-----|----------|-----------------|\\n| AI Governance | No documented AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, or human-in-the-loop controls | **High** | Require vendor to provide AI governance charter, bias audit roadmap, and human override procedures before enterprise deployment |\\n| Training Data | Partial documentation; sources and filtering criteria not disclosed | **High** | Request full training data documentation including sources, composition, filtering, and deduplication procedures |\\n| Bias & Safety Testing | No red-team, third-party audits, or adversarial testing evidence | **High** | Require third-party bias audit and adversarial security testing before production use |\\n| GDPR / Data Privacy | DPA not confirmed; GDPR compliance not explicitly addressed | **Medium** | Confirm DPA availability and GDPR compliance roadmap; clarify data residency options for EU customers |\\n| Support SLAs | P1/P2/P3 response targets not defined | **Medium** | Define support SLAs by severity; confirm 24/7 availability for critical issues |\\n| Sub-processor Disclosure | Infrastructure, payment, and auth vendors not named | **Medium** | Provide complete sub-processor list with SLAs and security certifications |\\n| Incident Response Testing | IRP documented but not tested | **Low** | Conduct annual tabletop exercises and publish incident response metrics |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – PILOT ONLY**\\n\\nArtisan AI demonstrates acceptable foundational security (SOC 2 Type 2, 99.9% SLA) and operational maturity for a 2023-founded startup, but **critical AI governance and safety gaps preclude immediate enterprise production deployment**. \\n\\n**Recommended Path:**\\n\\n1. **Pre-Pilot Gate (Weeks 1–4):**\\n   - Vendor must provide: AI ethics policy, bias audit roadmap, human-in-the-loop control specification\\n   - Require third-party bias audit (independent firm) covering lead targeting, email tone, and scheduling decisions\\n   - Confirm GDPR DPA availability and data residency options\\n\\n2. **Pilot Phase (Months 1–3):**\\n   - Limited deployment: 100–500 leads/week with full human review of Ava-generated emails and meeting scheduling decisions\\n   - Continuous monitoring: track email open rates, reply rates, meeting booking accuracy, and false-positive lead targeting\\n   - Weekly governance reviews with vendor and internal stakeholders\\n\\n3. **Production Gate (Month 4):**\\n   - Successful pilot completion (>80% email quality, <5% scheduling errors)\\n   - Vendor completion of third-party bias audit with acceptable findings\\n   - Execution of Data Processing Agreement (GDPR) and support SLA amendment\\n\\n**Risk Acceptance:** Proceed with pilot only if organization accepts residual risk of immature AI governance and limited third-party validation. Do not deploy to production without bias audit completion and documented human-in-the-loop controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Used:** VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Ava", "Customer Base": "Not specified", "Target Industry": "Enterprise sales/business development (sector-agnostic)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified (typical deployment size not documented)", "Primary Use Case": "Autonomous outbound sales process automation (lead discovery, personalized email drafting, meeting scheduling)", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; customer choice of data residency region", "Product Description": "Ava is a fully autonomous AI business development representative that automates outbound sales workflows including lead discovery, personalized email generation at scale, and meeting scheduling. Unlike traditional sales tool