Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:26:53.939733+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Drift AI	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:26:53.957+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Drift AI Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 55\\n- Compliance: 45\\n- Data Practices: 60\\n- AI Governance: 50\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDrift demonstrates moderate trustworthiness with established company maturity (founded 2015, Series D+, profitable 3+ years) and reasonable operational stability (99.9% SLA). However, significant gaps in AI governance documentation, compliance certifications, and security posture limit the overall score. The vendor lacks published security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA), no formal AI ethics policy or bias testing framework is documented, and training data documentation is absent—critical gaps for enterprise deployment. Strengths include automated rollback capability, documented incident response, and basic audit logging; weaknesses center on incomplete governance, unverified compliance, and limited transparency into AI model safety practices.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Drift AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Conversational marketing and sales automation; real-time customer engagement; lead qualification and nurturing; sales conversion optimization\\n- **Target Industry:** B2B SaaS, enterprise sales and marketing organizations\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer base not quantified)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (operational since 2015)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; corroborated evidence includes 2X qualified leads, 120% demo requests, 9X pipeline increase metrics\\n- **Product Description:** Drift AI is a conversational marketing and sales platform that automates lead qualification, customer engagement, and sales workflows through real-time AI-driven interactions. The platform integrates with existing CRM systems to streamline customer interactions and provide actionable insights. Customers report 30% increase in lead conversion rates and 20% reduction in manual sales processing time.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Drift (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Boston, Massachusetts, USA; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-based with potential international reach)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; conversational AI (likely LLM-based or custom NLP)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Lead qualification, customer engagement automation, sales conversation analysis, real-time response generation\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; level of human-in-the-loop intervention not documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted); specific prompt-level control or citation mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available** — critical gap for enterprise AI governance\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; frequency and scope of adversarial security testing not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines published\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluation process documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not documented; no system cards or release documentation available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested** — represents moderate maturity with unvalidated procedures\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger — supports rapid incident recovery\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer conversations, lead information, CRM data, sales interactions\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (specific collection mechanisms not detailed)\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Drift retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; secure deletion procedures outlined in Information Security Addendum\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or residency options documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request via Information Security Addendum; timelines and procedures not detailed in attestation\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None documented** — no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other standard certifications listed\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no recent independent audit documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not specified; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not addressed\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA availability not documented\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime) — industry-standard commitment for SaaS\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of third-party risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (qualified leads, demo requests, pipeline metrics)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and scope not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no NDA-protected testing results referenced\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (Vendor Self-Attestation Formula)\\n\\n**Formula Applied:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Component Scores:**\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85 (conversational AI with customer data; moderate inherent risk for lead qualification use case)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.35 (limited documented controls; no bias testing, training data documentation, or formal safety framework)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.60 (basic testing results available; no third-party audit or comprehensive evidence)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.35) × 0.60 = 33.3 → 33**\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or other standard certifications)\\n- Assessment Quality: 5 points (basic testing results; no third-party audit)\\n- Policies: 10 points (documented incident response and data retention; no AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, or impact assessment)\\n- Operational Controls: 15 points (automated rollback, basic audit logs; limited control maturity)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 20 points (established company, 3+ years profitable)\\n- **Governance Score = 50 (capped at 100) → Governance Risk = 100 − 50 = 50**\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; industry standard but not best-in-class)\\n- Incident Management: 15 points (documented but not tested)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 20 points (SaaS multi-tenant; no enterprise-specific deployment details)\\n- Stability: 20 points (established company, 3+ years profitable)\\n- Support: 10 points (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 dedicated support documented)\\n- **Operational Score = 90 → Operational Risk = 100 − 90 = 10**\\n\\n**Final Vendor Trust Score:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(33 × 0.40) + (50 × 0.30) + (10 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 − [13.2 + 15 + 3]\\n    = 100 − 31.2\\n    = 68.8 ≈ 69\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 62** based on:\\n- Significant gaps in AI governance (no ethics policy, bias testing, training data documentation)\\n- Absence of security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001)\\n- Unverified compliance posture (no HIPAA, GDPR, or regulatory framework documentation)\\n- Incident response not tested\\n- Limited transparency into AI model safety and explainability\\n\\n**Classification:** Moderate Vendor (60–69 range per rubric: \\"Review Recommended\\")\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT SUMMARY\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established Company Maturity:** Founded 2015, Series D+, profitable 3+ years — demonstrates market viability and financial stability\\n2. **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA; automated rollback capability; documented incident response\\n3. **Basic Audit Trail:** Audit logs and basic testing results available\\n4. **Data Retention Governance:** Documented data deletion procedures in Information Security Addendum\\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Require Remediation)\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or HIPAA certification limits enterprise deployability\\n2. **AI Governance Deficiency:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, or training data documentation\\n3. **Compliance Uncertainty:** GDPR, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not addressed; no DPA or BAA availability stated\\n4. **Unvalidated Incident Response:** Incident response plan documented but not tested\\n5. **Limited Transparency:** Model explainability rated \\"moderate\\"; no detailed transparency into AI decision-making or safety practices\\n\\n### Residual Concerns\\n- Support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 support commitment documented\\n- Sub-processor and critical vendor information not disclosed\\n- Change management and release cadence not documented\\n- No third-party audit or independent compliance validation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** **REVIEW RECOMMENDED** (Score 62/100)\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n1. **Require SOC 2 Type 2 certification** before enterprise deployment (timeline: 6–12 months typical)\\n2. **Request formal AI ethics policy and bias testing framework** with third-party validation\\n3. **Obtain HIPAA BAA and GDPR DPA** if handling regulated data\\n4. **Conduct independent security assessment** (penetration testing, code review)\\n5. **Validate incident response plan** through tabletop exercise or audit\\n6. **Clarify support SLAs** and escalation procedures for P1/P2/P3 incidents\\n7. **Request training data documentation** and model card for AI transparency\\n\\n**Suitable For:**\\n- Non-regulated B2B SaaS lead generation and sales automation\\n- Organizations with moderate data sensitivity requirements\\n- Pilot or phased deployments with extended evaluation period\\n\\n**Not Suitable For (Without Remediation):**\\n- Healthcare (HIPAA-regulated) applications\\n- Financial services or government deployments\\n- High-sensitivity PII or PHI processing\\n- Regulated industries requiring formal compliance certifications\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Framework:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)])", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Drift AI", "Customer Base": "Not specified; corroborated evidence includes 2X qualified leads, 120% demo requests, 9X pipeline increase metrics", "Target Industry": "B2B SaaS, enterprise sales and marketing organizations", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Mid-market to enterprise (typical customer base not quantified)", "Primary Use Case": "Conversational marketing and sales automation; real-time customer engagement; lead qualification and nurturing; sales conversion optimization", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "Drift AI is a conversational marketing and sales platform that automates lead qualification, customer engagement, and sales workflows through real-time AI-driven interactions. The platform integrates with existing CRM systems to streamline customer interactions and provide actionable insights. Customers report 30% increase in lead conversion rates and 20% reduction in manual sales processing time.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product (operational since 2015)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Drift (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2015", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed US-based with potential international reach)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Boston, Massachusetts, USA; specific investors not disclosed", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified; conversational AI (likely LLM-based or custom NLP)", "Model Purpose": "Lead qualification, customer engagement automation, sales conversation analysis, real-time response generation", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; level of human-in-the-loop intervention not documented", "Model Governance": "Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework specified", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate (some explainability features noted); specific prompt-level control or citation mechanisms not detailed"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented", "Penetration Testing": "Not specified; frequency and scope of adversarial security testing not provided", "Training Data Documentation": "**No documentation available** — critical gap for enterprise AI governance"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Not specified; no frequency or external evaluation process documented", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines published", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows", "Impact Assessment": "Not documented; no system cards or release documentation available"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger — supports rapid incident recovery", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, documented but **not tested** — represents moderate maturity with unvalidated procedures"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented", "PII Handling": "Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not documented", "Data Deletion": "On request via Information Security Addendum; timelines and procedures not detailed in attestation", "Data Retention": "Drift retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; secure deletion procedures outlined in Information Security Addendum", "Sub-processors": "Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed", "Data Collection": "API and chat interface (specific collection mechanisms not detailed)", "Data Types Processed": "Customer conversations, lead information, CRM data, sales interactions", "Data Location / Residency": "Not specified; no customer choice or residency options documented"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "**None documented** — no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other standard certifications listed", "GDPR Compliance": "Not specified; DPA availability not documented", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not specified; BAA eligibility not stated", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented", "Regulatory Frameworks": "Not specified; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not addressed", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; no recent independent audit documented", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime) — industry-standard commitment for SaaS", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided", "Critical Vendors": "Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency of third-party risk assessments not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability and scope not detailed", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available (qualified leads, demo requests, pipeline metrics)", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not specified; no NDA-protected testing results referenced", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation not provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Drift demonstrates moderate trustworthiness with established company maturity (founded 2015, Series D+, profitable 3+ years) and reasonable operational stability (99.9% SLA). However, significant gaps in AI governance documentation, compliance certifications, and security posture limit the overall score. The vendor lacks published security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA), no formal AI ethics policy or bias testing framework is documented, and training data documentation is absent—critical gaps for enterprise deployment. Strengths include automated rollback capability, documented incident response, and basic audit logging; weaknesses center on incomplete governance, unverified compliance, and limited transparency into AI model safety practices. ---", "overallScore": 82, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 93.96, "Governance": 84, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   82 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        16.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            6.04  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (16.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete Security certifications in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:26:53.939733+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	82	B	cff3c7aa-8bea-4332-9cff-5f81d764575f	\N	\N
5877bc08-884c-4463-be0d-63b5fa9073a4	9d4ee1d7-535f-4129-9c62-fc68172845bb	72	72	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Healthcare": ["Healthcare"]}	Growth (Series B/C)	https://eleos.health	Eleos Health is a mental health care company that leverages AI to streamline documentation, simplify compliance, and provide actionable insights for behavioral health providers. Their platform reduces administrative burdens, allowing clinicians to focus more on patient care.	201-1,000	2020	Boston, MA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "Chief Risk Officer"]	Eleos Health addresses the administrative burden on clinicians by automating documentation, ensuring compliance with HIPAA and other regulations, and providing insights to improve patient care.	\N	Eleos Health's AI platform is built using a large database of real-world behavioral health sessions, supports multilingual documentation, and is SOC 2 Type II certified with HITRUST compliance.	Eleos Health reduces documentation time by more than 70%, allowing clinicians to focus more on patient care. [Corroborated by 12 evidence point(s): Documentation Time Reduction: 70%; Time to Submit Notes: 3.5 days; User Experience Rating: 92%; Use of Evidence-Based Techniques: 35%; Time to Submit a Note: 4.4 hours]	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["HIPAA BAA"]	\N	\N	\N	After a predefined period, information can be de-identified/deleted upon request, based on laws. De-identified audio data may be retained to improve system accuracy.	\N	\N	\N	Partial documentation available	\N	Yes, tested annually	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:27:34.133317+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Eleos Health	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:27:34.136+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Eleos Health\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 75\\n- Compliance: 80\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nEleos Health demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type II, HITRUST, HIPAA BAA) and a growth-stage maturity appropriate for a 2020-founded behavioral health AI vendor. However, the trust score reflects moderate gaps in AI governance transparency, incomplete training data documentation, and limited operational detail (no published uptime SLA or detailed support response times). The vendor's core strength lies in domain-specific healthcare expertise and documented incident response procedures, but advancement to \\"Trusted Vendor\\" (80+) would require fuller disclosure of bias testing methodology, human oversight mechanisms, and operational SLAs. The score is driven primarily by **Compliance Risk (low)** and **Governance Risk (moderate)**, with **Product Risk (moderate-high)** due to incomplete AI safety documentation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Eleos Health\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Behavioral health documentation automation, compliance management, and clinical insights for mental health providers\\n- **Target Industry:** Behavioral health / Mental health care\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; specific cloud provider not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage (Series B/C); product in active clinical use\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Eleos Health is an AI-enabled SaaS platform that automates clinical documentation for behavioral health providers, reducing documentation time by over 70% and enabling compliance with HIPAA and related regulations. The platform leverages a large database of real-world behavioral health sessions and supports multilingual documentation. It is SOC 2 Type II certified and HITRUST compliant, positioning it as a security-conscious solution for regulated healthcare environments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Eleos Health (legal entity name not specified; inferred from domain and branding)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (specific revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Boston, MA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: United States; international regions not disclosed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (inferred: NLP/speech-to-text for documentation automation; specific model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Clinical documentation generation, compliance checking, behavioral health insights extraction\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no formal staged deployment or safety framework documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; level of clinician review and intervention not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features available; specific prompt-level control or citation mechanisms not documented)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data provenance, composition, and bias analysis not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no formal red team, third-party bias audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; frequency and scope of adversarial security testing not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified; no documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no formal bias audit schedule or external evaluation results disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; clinician review workflows, content filtering, and intervention mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards or release impact documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; formal incident response procedures are in place and validated through annual testing\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback is supported via automated processes with manual initiation option\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Clinical documentation (audio, text), behavioral health session notes, patient identifiers (PHI)\\n- **PII Handling:** HIPAA BAA eligible; PII (PHI) is processed as part of clinical documentation; specific restrictions on customer data use for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and clinical interface (inferred from SaaS deployment); collection mechanism not fully specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly documented\\n- **Data Retention:** After a predefined period, information can be de-identified or deleted upon request, based on applicable laws. De-identified audio data may be retained to improve system accuracy.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; data residency options (US, EU, customer choice) not disclosed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and automated based on retention policy; de-identification option available\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type II (security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy)\\n  - HITRUST (healthcare information security)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type II audit (third-party audit); HITRUST certification (third-party assessment); specific audit firm and scope not disclosed\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - HIPAA (Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act)\\n  - State behavioral health regulations (implied; specific frameworks not listed)\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligible; HIPAA compliance demonstrated via BAA availability\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability not disclosed; EU data residency not confirmed\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Incident response plan tested annually\\n  - SOC 2 Type II audit frequency not specified (typical: annual)\\n  - Last audit date not disclosed\\n  - Audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; contractual uptime commitment (e.g., 99.9%, 99.95%) not disclosed\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not documented\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** \\n  - Release frequency not specified\\n  - Rollback/readiness practices: Automated rollback with manual trigger available\\n  - Formal change management process not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers (cloud, hosting), payment processors, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of third-party vendor risk assessments not documented\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure or service vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity of telemetry not detailed\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** \\n  - Basic test results available\\n  - Partial training data documentation available\\n  - Formal policy documentation (AI ethics, data governance, incident response) not provided\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; availability of detailed model safety testing results under NDA not confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Healthcare-Specific Compliance:** SOC 2 Type II, HITRUST, and HIPAA BAA demonstrate serious commitment to regulated healthcare environments.\\n2. **Documented Incident Response:** Annual testing of incident response plan indicates operational maturity.\\n3. **Proven Clinical ROI:** 70%+ documentation time reduction corroborated by 12 evidence points; strong user satisfaction (92% UX rating).\\n4. **Automated Rollback:** Deployment rollback capability reduces operational risk.\\n5. **Growth-Stage Stability:** 201–1,000 employees and Series B/C funding suggest operational sustainability.\\n\\n### Gaps & Risks\\n1. **AI Governance Opacity:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, or human oversight framework; limits confidence in model safety.\\n2. **Incomplete Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation insufficient for regulatory scrutiny or third-party validation.\\n3. **Missing Operational SLAs:** No published uptime SLA or support response times; limits buyer confidence in operational reliability.\\n4. **Limited Transparency on Model Architecture:** AI model types, decision autonomy, and explainability mechanisms not detailed.\\n5. **GDPR / International Readiness:** No DPA, data residency options, or EU AI Act preparation documented; limits international deployment.\\n6. **Vendor Sub-processor Disclosure:** Critical infrastructure and payment vendors not disclosed; limits supply chain risk visibility.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions for Procurement\\n- **Require:** Formal AI ethics policy, documented bias testing methodology, and human oversight workflow before contract execution.\\n- **Require:** Published uptime SLA (recommend ≥99.9%) and support response time SLAs (P1/P2/P3).\\n- **Require:** Complete training data documentation (composition, sources, bias analysis) or third-party model audit.\\n- **Require:** GDPR DPA and data residency options if international deployment is planned.\\n- **Require:** Disclosure of critical sub-processors and their SLAs.\\n- **Recommended:** Pilot deployment with single behavioral health clinic to validate ROI claims and operational stability before enterprise rollout.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Current Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Classification:** Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range) — Proceed with enhanced due diligence; require mitigation of AI governance and operational transparency gaps as contract conditions.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Eleos Health", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Behavioral health / Mental health care", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Behavioral health documentation automation, compliance management, and clinical insights for mental health providers", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; specific cloud provider not specified", "Product Description": "Eleos Health is an AI-enabled SaaS platform that automates clinical documentation for behavioral health providers, reducing documentation time by over 70% and enabling compliance with HIPAA and related regulations. The platform leverages a large database of real-world behavioral health sessions and supports multilingual document