(Low)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 42\\n- Compliance: 25\\n- Data Practices: 45\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 55\\n- Company Maturity: 20\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nEntangl is a newly founded (2024) startup with a compelling mission to prevent infrastructure outages, but exhibits significant gaps across governance, compliance, and operational maturity that are typical of early-stage AI vendors. The company lacks documented AI governance policies, security certifications, bias testing frameworks, and formal compliance audits—critical requirements for enterprise deployment in regulated or mission-critical environments. While the vendor demonstrates basic operational infrastructure (99.9% SLA, automated rollback, incident response plan), the absence of third-party certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), formal bias audits, and comprehensive training data documentation creates unacceptable residual risk for customers handling sensitive infrastructure data. The startup stage (founded October 2024, ~10 employees) and lack of independent compliance validation further constrain trust. **Recommendation: Not suitable for fast-track procurement; extensive due diligence and pilot-only deployment required.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Entangl\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Preventing configuration mistakes and operational errors in critical infrastructure (data centers, aerospace systems); helping teams avoid outages.\\n- **Target Industry:** Data centers, aerospace, critical infrastructure, cloud operations\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (US-based)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product (company founded October 2024); basic test results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (no customer count or reference accounts disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Entangl is an AI platform designed to help infrastructure teams (data centers, aerospace) avoid mistakes that cause outages. Built by aerospace engineers (\\"rocket scientists\\"), the platform leverages AI to detect and prevent configuration errors and operational failures. The vendor claims $100B+ in cost reduction and 2 months of time savings corroborated by evidence, though customer references and deployment scale remain undisclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Entangl (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (Startup)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2024 (October)\\n- **Employees:** ~10 (stated as \\"01-Oct,\\" interpreted as October 2024 founding with minimal team)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (funding amount not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** US only (data residency: US only)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (no details on LLM, custom-trained, NLP, or other model architecture)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Infrastructure error detection and prevention; operational decision support (specific capabilities not detailed)\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy available\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no details on advisory vs. autonomous decision-making, monitoring, or alerts\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted, but no details on prompt-level control, citations, or transparency mechanisms)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools disclosed\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type of adversarial security testing disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines available\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations disclosed; no frequency specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no details on admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, release documentation, or impact assessments disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested** (represents a significant gap; untested plans carry high failure risk in production)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (acceptable for early-stage deployment, but no testing evidence provided)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Infrastructure configuration data, operational logs, system telemetry (inferred from use case; specific data types not formally documented)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no disclosure of whether customer infrastructure data or PII is used for model training or improvement\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface (inferred); specific collection mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** US-based infrastructure (provider not specified; likely AWS/Azure/GCP but unconfirmed)\\n- **Data Retention:** Standard retention: \\"as long as necessary for stated purposes\\"; usage data retained for security/functionality improvements or legal compliance; no zero-retention option disclosed\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only (no EU, customer-choice, or multi-region options)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (inferred from privacy policy language; no automated deletion or SLA specified)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not disclosed; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None disclosed (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other third-party certifications)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits conducted or disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No formal alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not addressed; BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) disclosed; EU compliance status unclear\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audits conducted; company founded October 2024 (too early for formal audit history)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime) — acceptable for non-critical workloads, but below enterprise standards for mission-critical infrastructure (typically 99.95%–99.99%)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets disclosed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no documented release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, or change approval workflow\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not disclosed; infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment program disclosed\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No SLAs from critical vendors disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, available (scope and export capability not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available (no details on completeness, retention, or export format)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no indication of advanced testing or NDA-protected results\\n\\n---\\n\\n## TRUST SCORE DERIVATION (Applied Formula)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from the vector database:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n### Product Risk Calculation (40% weight)\\n- **Inherent Risk:** 85/100 (early-stage AI product, no training data documentation, no bias testing, moderate explainability only)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.35 (basic incident response plan, automated rollback, but untested and no formal governance)\\n- **Confidence Factor:** 0.50 (no third-party audit, basic test results only, no certifications)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.35 × 0.50 = 14.875 ≈ 15**\\n\\n### Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight)\\n- **Certifications:** 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or other certifications)\\n- **Assessment Quality:** 5 points (basic test results, no third-party audit)\\n- **Policies:** 5 points (no documented AI governance, ethics, or safety policies)\\n- **Operational Controls:** 10 points (basic incident response plan, not tested)\\n- **Maturity Adjustment:** 0 points (startup founded October 2024)\\n- **Governance Score = 20 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 20 = 80**\\n\\n### Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight)\\n- **SLA:** 25 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; acceptable but below enterprise standard)\\n- **Incident Management:** 10 points (documented but not tested)\\n- **Deployment Maturity:** 5 points (early-stage, no multi-tenant enterprise deployment evidence)\\n- **Stability:** 5 points (startup, ~10 employees, no profitability or track record)\\n- **Support:** 5 points (no support SLAs by severity disclosed)\\n- **Operational Score = 50 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 50 = 50**\\n\\n### Final VTS Calculation\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(15 × 0.40) + (80 × 0.30) + (50 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [6 + 24 + 15]\\n    = 100 - 45\\n    = 55\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 38** to reflect:\\n- No independent compliance audits (penalty: -10)\\n- No bias testing or adversarial security testing (penalty: -7)\\n- Untested incident response plan (penalty: -5)\\n- US-only data residency (penalty: -3)\\n- No customer references or deployment scale disclosed (penalty: -2)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK CLASSIFICATION & RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Grade: F (Review Required)**\\n- **Score Range:** 0–59 (Critical deficiencies; unproven capabilities; high risk)\\n- **Vendor Profile:** Newly founded startup with compelling mission but significant gaps in governance, compliance, and operational maturity; unsuitable for enterprise or regulated deployments without extensive remediation.\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation: REJECT FOR FAST-TRACK PROCUREMENT**\\n\\n**Conditions for Future Consideration:**\\n1. **Achieve SOC 2 Type 2 certification** (minimum 6-month audit cycle)\\n2. **Implement and document formal AI governance policy** including bias testing, explainability standards, and human oversight requirements\\n3. **Conduct third-party bias audit** and adversarial security testing\\n4. **Test incident response plan** with documented results\\n5. **Disclose customer references** and deployment scale\\n6. **Establish support SLAs** by severity (P1/P2/P3)\\n7. **Provide Data Processing Agreement (DPA)** for GDPR compliance\\n8. **Expand data residency options** to include EU and customer-choice deployments\\n\\n**Suitable Use Cases (Current State):**\\n- Non-critical, internal pilot projects only\\n- Proof-of-concept deployments with limited scope\\n- Development/testing environments (not production)\\n\\n**Not Suitable For:**\\n- Mission-critical infrastructure deployments\\n- Healthcare, financial services, or regulated industries\\n- Handling sensitive customer data or PII\\n- Enterprise procurement without pilot validation", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Entangl", "Customer Base": "Not specifie