 available	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 14:55:25.317283+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Canva AI	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 14:55:25.322+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: CANVA AI\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nCanva AI demonstrates solid foundational trust driven by mature company operations (10+ years, 1,001–5,000 employees), strong compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, CCPA), and enterprise-grade security posture. However, the score is constrained by significant gaps in AI governance transparency—no documented AI ethics policy, no bias testing approach disclosed, and no training data documentation—which elevates product risk despite operational maturity. The 72 score reflects acceptable but not exceptional vendor readiness; Canva is suitable for design and visual content use cases with standard controls, but organizations handling sensitive data or requiring deep AI safety assurance should require enhanced due diligence and contractual mitigation commitments (e.g., bias audits, model transparency roadmap) before deployment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Canva AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise visual content creation, design collaboration, brand-consistent asset generation, social media, presentations, videos, posters, logos, and websites\\n- **Target Industry:** Multi-sector (demonstrated: logistics/FedEx); applicable to marketing, communications, creative services, and any organization requiring visual content at scale\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise teams and global organizations\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (10+ years company history; AI capabilities integrated into established platform)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Global user base; enterprise customers include FedEx; 77% reduction in brand review times and 30% increase in content output reported\\n- **Product Description:** Canva AI is a cloud-hosted, drag-and-drop visual design platform with AI-powered capabilities for rapid content creation and collaboration. It offers enterprise-grade security (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR/CCPA compliant) and AI indemnification for enterprise customers. The platform enables teams to create professional visual content in minutes, maintaining brand consistency at scale while reducing design approval cycles.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Canva (legal entity details not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS platform)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2012\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Surry Hills, New South Wales, Australia; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not enumerated; Australia-based with international reach)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (proprietary/closed models)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Visual content generation, design assistance, template recommendation, asset library integration\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment framework disclosed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no advisory vs. autonomous classification provided\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citation, or explainability documentation disclosed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach disclosed\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; adversarial security testing approach not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluation program disclosed\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested (maturity level: basic/undocumented runbook equivalent)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (moderate maturity; enables rapid recovery but requires human intervention)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Visual design assets, user-generated content, templates, fonts, stock photography metadata, collaboration and project data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** Web interface (drag-and-drop platform); API not explicitly mentioned\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); encryption standard not disclosed\\n- **Data Retention:** Canva retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; data deletion available upon request\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no explicit customer choice or residency options documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (manual process)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payment processors and authentication services not enumerated\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, GDPR Compliant, CCPA Compliant\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR and CCPA compliance stated; NIST and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not stated; BAA eligibility not confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes, compliant; DPA availability not explicitly confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit frequency and last audit date not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider not specified; payment processors and authentication services not enumerated\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments for sub-processors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (Post Interactions: 45%; Return Viewers: 30%; Design Time: Reduced; Content Output: 30%; Design Requests: 42%)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Not uploaded; no policy documents or testing results provided in attestation\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available; scope and NDA terms not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING RATIONALE & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Assessment Type 1: Vendor Self-Attestation)\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n#### Product Risk Calculation (40% weight)\\n\\n**Inherent Risk:** 85/100\\n- Use case: Visual content generation (lower inherent risk than healthcare/financial)\\n- Data sensitivity: Medium (customer design assets, no explicit PHI/PII handling disclosed)\\n- Production autonomy: Moderate (AI assists design; human review typical)\\n- Sector modifier: Design/Creative (lower regulatory burden than healthcare/finance)\\n\\n**Mitigation Effectiveness:** 0.50 (50%)\\n- Control coverage: 3/7 required categories (Data Practices, Security, Incident Response documented; AI Governance, Bias Testing, Training Data Documentation, Human Oversight gaps)\\n- Evidence quality: Low (no training data documentation, no bias testing, no AI ethics policy)\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness = (0.43 × 0.60) + (0.40 × 0.40) = 0.26 + 0.16 = 0.42**\\n\\n**Confidence Factor:** 0.75 (third-party audit: SOC 2 Type 2 + ISO 27001; no AI-specific third-party review)\\n\\n**Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.42) × 0.75 = 85 × 0.58 × 0.75 = 37.0**\\n\\n#### Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight)\\n\\n**Certifications Score:** 40/50\\n- SOC 2 Type 2: 15 points\\n- ISO 27001: 15 points\\n- PCI DSS: 5 points\\n- GDPR/CCPA: 5 points\\n- (No HIPAA, FedRAMP, or AI-specific certifications)\\n\\n**Assessment Quality Score:** 10/25\\n- Third-party audit (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001): 15 points\\n- Audit frequency: Not specified; assume ad-hoc: 0 points\\n- **Assessment Quality = 15 points**\\n\\n**Policy Score:** 15/45\\n- Data retention policy: Documented, not enforced (informal): 3 points\\n- Incident response plan: Documented, not tested: 5 points\\n- Privacy policy: Standard (GDPR/CCPA): 6 points\\n- AI ethics policy: Not documented: 0 points\\n- **Policy Score = 14 points**\\n\\n**Operational Controls Score:** 20/45\\n- Rollback: Automated with manual trigger: 12 points\\n- Oversight: Not specified; assume minimal: 3 points\\n- Monitoring: Not specified; assume weekly reports: 4 points\\n- Version control: Not specified: 0 points\\n- **Operational Controls = 19 points**\\n\\n**Maturity Adjustment:** 10/15\\n- Company age (10+ years): 10 points\\n- Company size (1,001–5,000): 0 points\\n- Funding stability: Not specified: 0 points\\n- Customer base: Established (FedEx, global): 0 points\\n- **Maturity Adjustment = 10 points**\\n\\n**Governance Score = 40 + 10 + 14 + 19 + 10 = 93 (capped at 100)**\\n**Governance Risk = 100 − 93 = 7**\\n\\n#### Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight)\\n\\n**SLA Score:** 33/33\\n- Uptime: 99.9% (8.8 hrs/year): 33 points\\n\\n**Incident Management Score:** 15/30\\n- Incident response: Documented, not tested: 10 points\\n- Automation: Not specified; assume basic: 5 points\\n- **Incident Management = 15 points**\\n\\n**Deployment Maturity Score:** 25/30\\n- Multi-tenant cloud: 20 points\\n- Enterprise scale: 5 points\\n- **Deployment Maturity = 25 points**\\n\\n**Stability Score:** 15/22\\n- Company age (10+ years): 10 points\\n- Profitability: Not specified; assume stable: 5 points\\n- **Stability = 15 points**\\n\\n**Support Score:** 10/20\\n- SLA response times: Not specified: 0 points\\n- Dedicated support: Not specified; assume standard: 5 points\\n- Technical account manager: Not specified: 0 points\\n- **Support = 5 points**\\n\\n**Operational Score = 33 + 15 + 25 + 15 + 5 = 93 (capped at 100)**\\n**Operational Risk = 100 − 93 = 7**\\n\\n#### Final Vendor Trust Score\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(37.0 × 0.40) + (7 × 0.30) + (7 × 0.30)]**\\n**VTS = 100 − [14.8 + 2.1 + 2.1]**\\n**VTS = 100 − 19.0**\\n**VTS = 81.0 ≈ 81**\\n\\n**Adjusted to 72 (Acceptable Vendor range 70–79)** to reflect:\\n- Significant AI governance gaps (no ethics policy, no bias testing, no training data documentation)\\n- Lack of AI-specific third-party audit or certification\\n- Undocumented human oversight and explainability\\n- Basic (untested) incident response\\n- Design/creative use case lower inherent risk than healthcare/finance, but governance gaps warrant conservative scoring\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** ACCEPTABLE VENDOR — PROCEED WITH CAUTION\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\nCanva AI is a mature, operationally sound platform suitable for enterprise visual content creation with standard controls. Strong compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, CCPA) and 99.9% uptime SLA support production deployment. However, significant AI governance transparency gaps—no documented ethics policy, bias testing, training data documentation, or human oversight framework—require contractual mitigation before deployment.\\n\\n**Conditions for Approval:**\\n1. **AI Governance Roadmap:** Vendor commits to third-party AI safety audit (e.g., bias testing, model card documentation) within 6 months of contract execution.\\n2. **Training Data Transparency:** Vendor discloses training data sources, filtering practices, and whether customer design assets are used for model improvement.\\n3. **Bias Testing & Monitoring:** Vendor implements and reports quarterly bias audits for AI-generated design recommendations.\\n4. **Incident Response Testing:** Vendor conducts annual tabletop exercises and documents rollback procedures.\\n5. **Data Residency & Deletion:** Vendor confirms GDPR-compliant data residency options and automated deletion workflows.\\n6. **AI Indemnification Scope:** Clarify indemnification coverage limits, exclusions, and claim procedures in enterprise agreement.\\n\\n**Use Case Fit:**\\n- ✅ **Recommended:** Brand-consistent visual content, design acceleration, team collaboration, marketing asset generation\\n- ⚠️ **Caution:** Sensitive customer data (PII, PHI) should not be embedded in designs without explicit data handling agreement\\n- ❌ **Not Recommended:** Regulated industries (healthcare, finance) without enhanced AI governance validation\\n\\n**Risk Mitigation Timeline:**\\n- **Pre-Deployment (0–3 months):** Vendor completes AI governance roadmap and training data disclosure; buyer conducts reference checks with similar-scale customers.\\n- **Pilot Phase (3–6 months):** Limited deployment with audit logging enabled; monitor for bias, data leakage, or compliance drift.\\n- **Production (6+ months):** Full deployment with quarterly compliance reviews and incident response drills.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## KEY STRENGTHS\\n\\n1. **Mature Operations:** 10+ year company history, 1,001–5,000 employees, global reach, proven enterprise customer base (FedEx)\\n2. **Strong Compliance:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, GDPR, CCPA certifications demonstrate security and privacy maturity\\n3. **Reliable Uptime:** 99.9% SLA (8.8 hrs/year downtime) suitable for production design workflows\\n4. **Rapid ROI:** Documented 77% reduction in brand review times and 30% increase in content output\\n5. **Enterprise Security:** AI indemnification for enterprise customers reduces legal risk\\n6. **Automated Rollback:** Enables rapid incident recovery with manual trigger option\\n\\n---\\n\\n## KEY GAPS & RISKS\\n\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing, or training data documentation; elevates product risk despite operational maturity\\n2. **Untested Incident Response:** Incident response plan documented but not tested; limits confidence in crisis response\\n3. **Limited AI-Specific Audit:** No third-party AI safety or bias audit; SOC 2 Type 2 covers security but not AI governance\\n4. **Undocumented Human Oversight:** No disclosure of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms for AI-generated outputs\\n5. **Data Handling Ambiguity:** PII handling extent and whether customer design assets are used for model training not specified\\n6. **Support SLA Gaps:** P1/P2/P3 response targets not documented; support maturity unclear\\n7. **Sub-processor Transparency:** Infrastructure provider, payment processors, and authentication services not enumerated; vendor risk assessment frequency not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RECOMMENDED NEXT STEPS\\n\\n1. **Reference Calls:** Contact 2–3 enterprise customers (similar scale/industry) to validate support quality, incident response, and data handling practices\\n2. **Security Assessment:** Request detailed SOC 2 Type 2 audit report (last 12 months) and confirm audit scope includes AI components\\n3. **AI Governance Deep Dive:** Schedule vendor call to discuss:", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Canva AI", "Customer Base": "Global user base; enterprise customers include FedEx; 77% reduction in brand review times and 30% increase in content output reported", "Target Industry": "Multi-sector (demonstrated: logistics/FedEx); applicable to marketing, communications, creative services, and any organization requiring visual content at scale", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise teams and global organizations", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise visual content creation, design collaboration, brand-consistent asset generation, social media, presentations, videos, posters, logos, and websites", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "Canva AI is a cloud-hosted, drag-and-drop visual design platform with AI-powered capabilities for rapid content creation and collaboration. It offers enterprise-grade security (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR/CCPA compliant) and AI indemnification for enterprise customers. The platform enables teams to create professional visual content in minutes, maintaining brand consistency at scale while reducing design approval cycles.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Mature product (10+ years company history; AI capabilities integrated into established platform)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Canva (legal entity details not specif