	f	2026-07-28 14:56:24.545+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Canva Magic Design\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nCanva Magic Design achieves an \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" trust score of 72, reflecting strong compliance posture and operational maturity offset by significant gaps in AI governance transparency and training data documentation. The vendor demonstrates enterprise-grade security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS) and regulatory compliance (GDPR, CCPA), supported by an established company profile (founded 2012, 5,001–10,000 employees, profitable 3+ years). However, critical weaknesses include: no documented AI governance policy, no training data documentation, no bias testing approach disclosed, and incident response plan not tested annually. The 99.9% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability provide operational confidence, but the lack of transparency around AI model governance, safety testing, and human oversight mechanisms creates residual product risk that limits the score to the \\"Acceptable\\" band (70–79). Recommendation: Require vendor to provide documented AI ethics policy, bias audit results, and annual incident response testing before production deployment in regulated environments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Canva Magic Design\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Rapid design creation for enterprise teams; brand consistency maintenance at scale; design and approval workflow acceleration\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-industry); demonstrated use case: FedEx (logistics/enterprise operations)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (vendor-managed infrastructure)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise multi-team collaboration; typical customer: 5,000+ user organization\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-grade (established product with corroborated ROI metrics)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Enterprise customers including FedEx; 77% reduction in brand review times documented across customer base\\n- **Product Description:** Canva Magic Design is an AI-powered design automation tool integrated into the Canva platform that enables rapid visual content creation without professional design expertise. The product leverages proprietary AI models to accelerate design workflows, maintain brand consistency across large-scale projects, and reduce approval cycle times by 77% on average. Deployment is cloud-hosted SaaS with SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, and PCI DSS certifications; GDPR and CCPA compliance is documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Canva Pty Ltd (or Canva Inc., depending on entity)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS design platform with embedded AI capabilities)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2012\\n- **Employees:** 5,001–10,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Profitable 3+ years; Series D+ funding (private company)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Surry Hills, New South Wales, Australia\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (multi-region SaaS operations implied by enterprise customer base)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/Closed (specific model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Design generation and automation; visual content creation; brand consistency enforcement\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no documented AI governance policy provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no human-in-the-loop controls or intervention mechanisms documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary model; no transparency into design decision rationale or model behavior provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach disclosed; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type of adversarial security testing disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines for AI model behavior provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation for AI model changes provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; no annual testing or validation of incident response procedures provided\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedures are in place but testing frequency not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Design projects, visual content, brand assets, user collaboration data, design metadata\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** Web interface and API; interaction data available (basic metrics)\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure and encryption details not specified; hosted on vendor-managed cloud infrastructure\\n- **Data Retention:** Canva retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and fulfill purposes outlined in privacy policy; data deletion procedures in place upon request or account termination\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice of data residency not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and automated upon account termination\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR Compliant, CCPA Compliant (stated); NIST and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not stated; BAA eligibility not documented\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Compliant (stated); Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documentation provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit frequency and last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response time targets documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication sub-processors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Testing results available (not detailed); policy documentation incomplete (no AI governance, bias testing, or incident response test results)\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no NDA-protected testing results or safety validation data provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT NOTES & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Established Company Maturity:** Founded 2012, 5,001–10,000 employees, profitable 3+ years—demonstrates operational stability and market viability.\\n2. **Strong Compliance & Security Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, GDPR, and CCPA compliance provide baseline enterprise security posture.\\n3. **Documented Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability support production-grade deployment.\\n4. **Corroborated Business Value:** 77% reduction in brand review times and 30–45 minute to 5–10 minute content creation time savings validated across customer base.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **No AI Governance Documentation:** Absence of documented AI ethics policy, safety guidelines, or model governance framework creates significant product risk for regulated industries.\\n2. **No Training Data Documentation:** No transparency into training data sources, composition, or potential bias vectors.\\n3. **No Bias Testing or Audits:** No red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools disclosed; no bias detection mechanisms documented.\\n4. **Incident Response Not Tested:** Incident response plan documented but not tested annually; no validation of response effectiveness.\\n5. **Limited AI Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model with no explainability, model cards, or transparency into design decision rationale.\\n6. **No Human Oversight Mechanisms:** No documented human-in-the-loop controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**PROCEED WITH CAUTION** (Acceptable Vendor, score 72)\\n\\n- **Suitable for:** Non-regulated design automation use cases (marketing, creative teams, general enterprise design workflows)\\n- **Not suitable for:** Healthcare (PHI), financial services (PII), government, or other regulated industries without additional AI governance and safety validation\\n- **Conditions for approval:**\\n  1. Require vendor to provide documented AI ethics policy and safety guidelines before contract execution\\n  2. Request third-party bias audit results or commitment to annual bias testing with results disclosure\\n  3. Require annual incident response plan testing with results provided to customer\\n  4. Obtain training data documentation or commitment to transparency roadmap\\n  5. Clarify PII handling practices and confirm customer data is not used for model training\\n  6. Establish SLAs for P1/P2/P3 support response times\\n  7. Confirm data residency options and DPA availability for GDPR compliance\\n\\n### Risk Mitigation Actions\\n- Implement customer-side monitoring for design output quality and bias detection\\n- Establish internal review workflows for AI-generated designs before publication\\n- Conduct periodic audits of design output for brand consistency and appropriateness\\n- Maintain rollback procedures and test quarterly\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Framework:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Methodology (Vector Database Formula Guidance Applied)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Canva Magic Design", "Customer Base": "Enterprise customers including FedEx; 77% reduction in brand review times documented across customer base", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-industry); demonstrated use case: FedEx (logistics/enterprise operations)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise multi-team collaboration; typical customer: 5,000+ user organization", "Primary Use Case": "Rapid design creation for enterprise teams; 