\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate / Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 45\\n- Compliance: 35\\n- Data Practices: 55\\n- AI Governance: 40\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nCedar demonstrates solid operational maturity (99.99% uptime SLA, quarterly incident response testing, automated rollback) and established company credentials (Series D+, profitable 3+ years, 201–1,000 employees), but faces significant gaps in compliance certifications, AI governance documentation, and formal safety testing that are critical for healthcare PHI handling. The lack of SOC 2, HIPAA BAA, or ISO 27001 certifications—combined with no formal adversarial testing, incomplete training data documentation, and undocumented bias testing—places this vendor in the \\"Review Recommended\\" category (60–69 range). While Cedar's healthcare domain expertise and strong ROI metrics are strengths, the absence of third-party audit evidence and formal AI safety controls creates residual risk that must be addressed before enterprise healthcare deployment, particularly for regulated use cases involving patient financial data (PII/PHI).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Cedar Patient Financial Experience\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Healthcare provider billing, patient financial engagement, coverage verification, payment processing, and patient support\\n- **Target Industry:** Healthcare (providers, health systems, insurance)\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; specific cloud provider (AWS/Azure/GCP) not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise healthcare providers and health systems\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (Series D+, 3+ years profitable); no formal third-party testing results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Cedar unifies billing, payments, coverage, and support through an AI-enabled SaaS platform designed exclusively for patient financial engagement. The platform leverages proprietary AI models to optimize billing workflows, improve collection rates (24% increase corroborated), and enhance patient satisfaction (96% reported). Cedar Intelligence is built for healthcare domain nuances (billing, coverage, affordability) rather than general-purpose AI, differentiating it from commodity LLM solutions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Cedar (legal entity not specified; operating as Cedar)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: New York, NY; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: US-based; operating regions not detailed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary AI models (type not disclosed; inferred: NLP/ML for billing, coverage, and payment optimization)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Patient financial engagement, billing optimization, coverage verification, payment prediction, affordability assessment, and patient communication\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no formal staged deployment or safety framework disclosed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows provided\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability documentation available\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data provenance and composition not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; vendor does not report penetration test results or frequency\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external bias evaluation program documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or impact assessments documented for releases\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested quarterly; formal incident response procedures are in place and validated through quarterly testing\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback is supported with both automated and manual initiation options\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Patient financial data (billing records, coverage information, payment history, affordability data); inferred: PII/PHI (patient names, identifiers, financial details)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and SaaS platform interface; specific collection mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Not specified; infrastructure provider and encryption standards not disclosed\\n- **Data Retention:** Cedar retains customer data in accordance with regulatory requirements and contractual obligations; default retention period not specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice for data residency not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request or after retention period expires; automated deletion procedures implemented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently held; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST, or other healthcare/security certifications documented\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit results available; no third-party audit evidence provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not specified; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligibility not stated; no HIPAA compliance certification or BAA availability confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability not specified\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation for EU AI Act requirements documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit frequency or last audit date provided; no audit findings available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime); strong contractual uptime commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, and change management procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; telemetry scope limited to basic usage data\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; full SIEM export capability and log retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results or policy documentation uploaded; vendor attestation incomplete\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected safety or adversarial testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Established Company & Profitability:** Series D+ funding, 3+ years profitable, 201–1,000 employees, founded 2016 (8 years operational)\\n2. **Strong Operational Reliability:** 99.99% uptime SLA, quarterly incident response testing, automated rollback capability\\n3. **Healthcare Domain Expertise:** Proprietary AI built exclusively for patient financial engagement; corroborated ROI metrics (24% collection increase, 96% patient satisfaction)\\n4. **Data Governance Framework:** Documented data retention and deletion procedures aligned with regulatory requirements\\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Compliance & Safety)\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, or HITRUST—critical for healthcare PHI handling\\n2. **No Independent Audit Evidence:** No third-party compliance audit results; vendor self-attestation only\\n3. **Incomplete AI Governance:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias audit program, or formal safety testing framework\\n4. **Limited Training Data Transparency:** Partial documentation only; full training data provenance and composition not disclosed\\n5. **No Adversarial Testing:** No formal penetration testing, red team exercises, or adversarial security validation\\n6. **Undocumented Human Oversight:** No admin controls, content filtering, or human-in-the-loop workflows documented\\n\\n### Residual Risk Assessment\\n**Product Risk:** 65/100 (High)\\n- Proprietary AI model with limited transparency; partial training data documentation; no formal bias or safety testing; healthcare domain expertise mitigates some risk but insufficient controls for PHI handling\\n\\n**Governance Risk:** 70/100 (High)\\n- No certifications; no independent audit; incomplete AI governance policy; data practices documented but not third-party validated\\n\\n**Operational Risk:** 25/100 (Low)\\n- Strong SLA, quarterly incident testing, automated rollback; support SLAs not specified but operational maturity evident\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**Status:** CONDITIONAL APPROVAL / ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED\\n\\n**Conditions for Deployment:**\\n1. **Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 and HIPAA BAA certifications** (or equivalent third-party audit) before handling PHI in production\\n2. **Conduct independent penetration testing** and provide results (or engage third-party security firm)\\n3. **Document formal AI governance policy** including bias audit frequency, model update procedures, and human oversight workflows\\n4. **Provide complete training data documentation** (sources, composition, filtering, deduplication procedures)\\n5. **Implement continuous model drift monitoring** and establish clinical/financial review workflow for high-impact decisions\\n6. **Disclose critical vendor SLAs** (infrastructure, payments, authentication) and sub-processor list\\n7. **Define support response SLAs** by severity level (P1/P2/P3)\\n\\n**Acceptable Use Cases (Without Full Compliance):**\\n- Non-PHI patient engagement (general billing inquiries, payment scheduling)\\n- Pilot deployments with limited patient data scope\\n- Internal operational analytics (not direct patient-facing decisions)\\n\\n**Not Recommended Without Remediation:**\\n- Production PHI handling for regulated healthcare entities\\n- Direct clinical decision support or coverage determination\\n- Deployment in HIPAA-covered entities without BAA\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (COTS SaaS)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (established company, strong operations; limited compliance evidence)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricin