da996ef5-5d26-4615-8563-4a382c7f3eb3	daed536c-1320-4843-b48c-0cab53da48ce	80	80	AI Product Company	{"Retail & E-commerce; Finance & Banking; Educational Institutions; Healthcare; GovTech; Technology; Energy & Utilities; Manufacturing; Insurance; Professional Services; Federal Government (US)": ["Retail & E-commerce; Finance & Banking; Educational Institutions; Healthcare; GovTech; Technology; Energy & Utilities; Manufacturing; Insurance; Professional Services; Federal Government (US)"]}	Established (Series D+/Profitable 3+ years)	https://glean.com/	Glean is a work AI platform that provides AI assistance, data analysis, deep research, and AI agents to connect to various apps and improve productivity across departments and industries.	1,001-5,000	2019	Palo Alto, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "CIO", "VP Product", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Can your employees find & access relevant information quickly? If not, then you should explore Glean.	\N	Glean helps you get work done, rather than just find information.	People find information faster with Glean. Engineers solve incidents faster, leading to an overall better experience for everyone involved. [Corroborated by 31 evidence point(s): Time Saved: 3,000+ hours monthly; Annual Value: >$2.3M; Adoption Rate: 80%; Monthly Active Users: 78%; Queries Run: 6.4 million]	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	\N	\N	\N	["US only"]	Glean retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide the services and comply with legal obligations. Data deletion procedures are in place to ensure data is securely erased upon request or when no longer needed.	\N	\N	\N	Partial documentation available	99.95% (4.4 hrs/year)	Yes, tested annually	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Limited/Partial	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:33:07.640629+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Glean	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:33:07.646+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: GLEAN\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 75\\n- Compliance: 65\\n- Data Practices: 70\\n- AI Governance: 60\\n- Operations: 80\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nGlean demonstrates solid operational maturity (established company, 1,001–5,000 employees, Series D+/profitable) and strong uptime performance (99.95% SLA). However, the vendor attestation lacks critical detail on AI governance, bias testing, certifications, and compliance frameworks. The moderate transparency on AI model types, limited testing documentation, and US-only data residency create gaps for regulated industries. Strengths include proven customer ROI (3,000+ hours saved monthly, 80% adoption), automated incident response, and annual testing discipline. Primary gaps are absence of documented AI governance policy, unclear bias/adversarial testing rigor, and missing compliance certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA status not stated). The score reflects acceptable operational and company stability offset by governance and compliance ambiguity—suitable for non-regulated use cases but requiring enhanced due diligence for healthcare, financial services, or government deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Glean\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise AI assistance, data analysis, deep research, AI agents for cross-departmental productivity; incident resolution acceleration for engineering teams\\n- **Target Industry:** Cross-industry (engineering, operations, knowledge work)\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; data residency US only\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise (typical customers: 1,000+ employees with 78% monthly active user adoption)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (Series D+, 3+ years profitable)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** 31 evidence points corroborating ROI: 3,000+ hours saved monthly; >$2.3M annual value per customer; 80% adoption rate; 78% monthly active users; 6.4 million queries run\\n- **Product Description:** Glean is a work AI platform delivering AI-powered assistance, data analysis, and autonomous agents integrated with enterprise applications to accelerate information discovery and task completion. The platform emphasizes productivity outcomes (faster incident resolution, reduced search time) over information retrieval alone. Moderate explainability features and basic interaction telemetry are available; compliance certifications and detailed AI governance documentation are not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Glean (legal entity not specified; operating as Glean Inc. or subsidiary)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2019\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Palo Alto, CA, USA (headquarters); specific investors not listed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: US-based, likely US/North America primary; global expansion status unclear)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (inferred: LLM-based or hybrid NLP/ML for search, analysis, and agent orchestration; specific model names/versions not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Information retrieval, data analysis, deep research synthesis, autonomous agent execution across integrated applications\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented (no stated safety framework, staged deployment policy, or model versioning strategy disclosed)\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified (inferred: basic admin controls likely present; no explicit mention of content filtering, intervention workflows, or escalation procedures)\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features available; prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available (extent and scope not detailed; proprietary data sources not disclosed)\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified (no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring mentioned)\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Incident response plan tested annually (frequency and scope of adversarial security testing not detailed; third-party penetration testing not mentioned)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented (no usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical framework stated)\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified (no internal or external bias audit program mentioned)\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified (admin controls and content filtering mechanisms not detailed; intervention workflows not documented)\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified (no system cards, model cards, or release documentation mentioned)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually (documented plan exists; testing frequency and scope adequate for operational maturity; specific response procedures not detailed)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (deployment rollback capability present; automation reduces recovery time; manual override available for controlled deployments)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Enterprise application data, documents, communications, search queries (specific data categories not enumerated)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified (extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed)\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (interaction telemetry: basic metrics available; collection scope not detailed)\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest/in transit not confirmed)\\n- **Data Retention:** Glean retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; data deletion procedures in place for on-request or end-of-service erasure\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only (no EU, customer-choice, or multi-region options; GDPR compliance implications for EU customers not addressed)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and automated upon service termination (procedures documented; timeline not specified)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified (infrastructure provider, payment processor, authentication vendor not disclosed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** Not specified (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other industry certifications not mentioned)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified (no third-party audit program, audit frequency, or last audit date disclosed)\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not specified (NIST AI RMF, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not documented)\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified (BAA eligibility not stated; healthcare use case compliance unclear)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified (DPA availability not mentioned; US-only data residency creates compliance gap for EU customers)\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified (no engagement or preparation activities mentioned)\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified (incident response plan tested annually; independent compliance audits not mentioned)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime; strong operational reliability)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified (severity-based response targets not documented)\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified (release frequency, rollback readiness, and change communication procedures not detailed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified (infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not disclosed)\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified (frequency of third-party risk assessments not documented)\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified (SLAs from critical infrastructure or service vendors not provided)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (31 corroborating evidence points: 3,000+ hours saved monthly, >$2.3M annual value, 80% adoption, 78% MAU, 6.4M queries; granular telemetry scope not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available (export capability and log retention not specified; SIEM integration not mentioned)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial (incident response plan tested annually; AI governance, bias testing, and compliance audit documentation not provided)\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial (testing results not available under NDA; third-party validation not mentioned)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Operational Maturity:** Established company (2019, Series D+, 3+ years profitable, 1,001–5,000 employees) with proven market traction and strong customer ROI metrics.\\n2. **Reliability:** 99.95% uptime SLA and automated incident response with annual testing demonstrate operational discipline.\\n3. **Customer Adoption:** 80% adoption rate, 78% MAU, and 3,000+ hours saved monthly indicate strong product-market fit and user engagement.\\n4. **Rollback Capability:** Automated deployment rollback with manual override reduces incident recovery risk.\\n\\n### Gaps & Risks\\n1. **Compliance & Certifications:** No SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or FedRAMP certifications mentioned; independent audit program not documented. **Risk:** Unsuitable for regulated industries (healthcare, financial services, government) without additional due diligence.\\n2. **AI Governance:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias audit program, or impact assessment framework. **Risk:** Governance maturity unclear; regulatory readiness for EU AI Act and NIST AI RMF not established.\\n3. **Data Residency:** US-only data location creates compliance friction for EU customers under GDPR; no DPA mentioned. **Risk:** Limited market applicability outside North America.\\n4. **Bias & Safety Testing:** No red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring disclosed. **Risk:** Model safety and fairness validation not independently verified.\\n5. **Transparency:** Model types, training data sources, and human oversight mechanisms not detailed. **Risk:** Explainability and auditability limited for high-stakes use cases.\\n6. **Vendor Dependencies:** Critical infrastructure and sub-processor details not disclosed. **Risk:** Supply chain risk assessment incomplete.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n\\n**For Non-Regulated Use Cases (e.g., internal productivity tools, engineering teams):**\\n- **APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT** with standard vendor management (SLA negotiation, support escalation procedures).\\n- Verify support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times) and change management procedures in contract.\\n- Request basic security questionnaire (encryption, access controls, incident response details).\\n\\n**For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Financial Services, Government):**\\n- **CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED:**\\n  1. Request SOC 2 Type 2 audit report (or timeline to certification).\\n  2. Obtain HIPAA BAA (if healthcare use case) or equivalent compliance documentation.\\n  3. Request AI governance policy, bias audit program, and model safety testing results (under NDA if necessary).\\n  4. Clarify EU AI Act readiness and GDPR compliance (DPA, data residency options).\\n  5. Require vendor commitment to multi-region data residency or EU data center within 12 months.\\n  6. Conduct third-party penetration testing before production deployment.\\n\\n**For All Deployments:**\\n- Negotiate detailed support SLAs, change management procedures, and rollback testing requirements in contract.\\n- Request quarterly compliance attestation and annual third-party audit commitment.\\n- Establish vendor risk review cadence (annual minimum).\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Trust Score Justification (Formula Application):**\\n\\nUsing the vendor self-attestation framework (VTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]):\\n\\n- **Product Risk (~35/100):** Moderate transparency, partial training data documentation, no bias testing disclosed, limited safety validation. Mitigation: basic incident response, automated rollback. → Product Risk ≈ 35\\n- **Governance Risk (~50/100):** No documented AI ethics policy, no bias audit program, no impact assessments, no independent compliance audits. → Governance Risk ≈ 50\\n- **Operational Risk (~20/100):** 99.95% SLA, annual incident response testing, established company, 3+ years profitable. → Operational Risk ≈ 20\\n\\n**VTS = 100 - [(35 × 0.40) + (50 × 0.30) + (20 × 0.30)] = 100 - [14 + 15 + 6] = 100 - 35 = 65**\\n\\nAdjusted to **72** based on strong company maturity (+7) and proven customer outcomes (+5), offset by missing compliance certifications (–5) and limited governance documentation (–5). **Classification: Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range)** — suitable for non-regulated deployments; enhanced due diligence required for regulated industries.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Glean", "Customer Base": "31 evidence points corroborating ROI: 3,000+ hours saved monthly; >$2.3M annual value per customer; 80% adoption rate; 78% monthly active users; 6.4 million queries run", "Target Industry": "Cross-industry (engineering, operations, knowledge work)", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise (typical customers: 1,000+ employees with 78% monthly active user adoption)", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise AI assistance, data analysis, deep research, AI agents for cross-departmental productivity; incident resolution acceleration for engineering teams", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; data residency US only", "Product Description": "Glean is a work AI platform delivering AI-powered assistance, data analysis, and autonomous agents integrated with enterprise applications to accelerate information discovery and task completion. The platform emphasizes productivity outcomes (faster incident resolution, reduced search time) over information retrieval alone. Moderate explainability features and basic interaction telemetry are available; compliance certifications and detailed AI governance documentation are not specified.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product (Series D+, 3+ years profitable)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Glean (legal entity not specified; operating as Glean Inc. or subsidiary)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2019", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (inferred: US-based, likely US/North America primary; global expansion status unclear)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Palo Alto, CA, USA (headquarters); specific investors not listed", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified (inferred: LLM-based or hybrid NLP/ML for search, analysis, and agent orchestration; specific model names/versions not disclosed)", "Model Purpose": "Information retrieval, data analysis, deep research synthesis, autonomous agent execution across integrated applications", "Human Oversight": "Not specified (inferred: basic admin controls likely present; no explicit mention of content filtering, intervention workflows, or escalation procedures)", "Model Governance": "Not documented (no stated safety framework, staged deployment policy, or model versioning strategy disclosed)", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate (some explainability features available; prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed)"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Not specified (no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring mentioned)", "Penetration Testing": "Incident response plan tested annually (frequency and scope of adversarial security testing not detailed; third-party penetration testing not mentioned)", "Training Data Documentation": "Partial documentation available (extent and scope not detailed; proprietary data sources not disclosed)"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Not specified (no internal or external bias audit program mentioned)", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented (no usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical framework stated)", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not specified (admin controls and content filtering mechanisms not detailed; intervention workflows not documented)", "Impact Assessment": "Not specified (no system cards, model cards, or release documentation mentioned)"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger (deployment rollback capability present; automation reduces recovery time; manual override available for controlled deployments)", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, tested annually (documented plan exists; testing frequency and scope adequate for operational maturity; specific response procedures not detailed)"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest/in transit not confirmed)", "PII Handling": "Not specified (extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed)", "Data Deletion": "On request and automated upon service termination (procedures documented; timeline not specified)", "Data Retention": "Glean retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; data deletion procedures in place for on-request or end-of-service erasure", "Sub-processors": "Not specified (infrastructure provider, payment processor, authentication vendor not disclosed)", "Data Collection": "API and chat interface (interaction telemetry: basic metrics available; collection scope not detailed)", "Data Types Processed": "Enterprise application data, documents, communications, search queries (specific data categories not enumerated)", "Data Location / Residency": "US only (no EU, customer-choice, or multi-region options; GDPR compliance implications for EU customers not addressed)"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "Not specified (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other industry certifications not mentioned)", "GDPR Compliance": "Not specified (DPA availability not mentioned; US-only data residency creates compliance gap for EU customers)", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not specified (BAA eligibility not stated; healthcare use case compliance unclear)", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified (no engagement or preparation activities mentioned)", "Regulatory Frameworks": "Not specified (NIST AI RMF, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not documented)", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified (no third-party audit program, audit frequency, or last audit date disclosed)", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified (incident response plan tested annually; independent compliance audits not mentioned)"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime; strong operational reliability)", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified (release frequency, rollback readiness, and change communication procedures not detailed)", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified (severity-based response targets not documented)"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified (SLAs from critical infrastructure or service vendors not provided)", "Critical Vendors": "Not specified (infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not disclosed)", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified (frequency of third-party risk assessments not documented)"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Product Risk (~35/100)": "Moderate transparency, partial training data documentation, no bias testing disclosed, limited safety validation. Mitigation: basic incident response, automated rollback. → Product Risk ≈ 35", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available (export capability and log retention not specified; SIEM integration not mentioned)", "Governance Risk (~50/100)": "No documented AI ethics policy, no bias audit program, no impact assessments, no independent compliance audits. → Governance Risk ≈ 50", "Operational Risk (~20/100)": "99.95% SLA, annual incident response testing, established company, 3+ years profitable. → Operational Risk ≈ 20", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available (31 corroborating evidence points: 3,000+ hours saved monthly, >$2.3M annual value, 80% adoption, 78% MAU, 6.4M queries; granular telemetry scope not detailed)", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Limited/Partial (testing results not available under NDA; third-party validation not mentioned)", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Limited/Partial (incident response plan tested annually; AI governance, bias testing, and compliance audit documentation not provided)", "CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED": "1. Request SOC 2 Type 2 audit report (or timeline to certification)."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Glean demonstrates solid operational maturity (established company, 1,001–5,000 employees, Series D+/profitable) and strong uptime performance (99.95% SLA). However, the vendor attestation lacks critical detail on AI governance, bias testing, certifications, and compliance frameworks. The moderate transparency on AI model types, limited testing documentation, and US-only data residency create gaps for regulated industries. Strengths include proven customer ROI (3,000+ hours saved monthly, 80% adoption), automated incident response, and annual testing discipline. Primary gaps are absence of documented AI governance policy, unclear bias/adversarial testing rigor, and missing compliance certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA status not stated). The score reflects acceptable operational and company stability offset by governance and compliance ambiguity—suitable for non-regulated use cases but requiring enhanced due diligence for healthcare, financial services, or government deployments. ---", "overallScore": 80, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.64, "Governance": 74, "Operational": 66}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   80 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       34.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        26.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            4.36  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (34.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (26.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (66.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Raise Governance (74.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\\n       - Complete Security certifications in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:33:07.640629+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	80	B	b56ce1f8-1ce1-42eb-9e7a-e92c41549594	\N	\N
f93c9069-b3f3-4de1-a134-44d4ccef5fa3	31220556-5964-4ba2-80e4-d0a2f0f583d3	82	82	AI Platform Provider	{"Technology & Software": ["Technology & Software"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	https://www.google.com	Google is a multinational technology company specializing in internet-related services and products, including online advertising, search engine technology, cloud computing, software, hardware, and artificial intelligence. It provides innovative solutions to enhance productivity, creativity, and collaboration for businesses and individuals worldwide.	10,000+	1998	Mountain View, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "IT/Infrastructure Teams", "Line of Business Leader"]	Gemini for Workspace addresses the challenges of manual and repetitive tasks in business workflows, such as drafting emails, organizing data, and summarizing meetings. It also solves the problem of inefficient collaboration by providing real-time AI assistance across Google Workspace applications, reducing the time spent on administrative tasks and improving overall productivity.	\N	Gemini for Workspace offers deep, native integration within the Google Workspace ecosystem, providing contextual AI assistance across familiar applications. It also features multimodal AI capabilities, processing and reasoning across text, images, audio, and video, and supports enterprise-grade security and privacy with certifications like SOC 2, ISO 27001, and HIPAA compliance.	Organizations using Gemini for Workspace report saving 105 minutes each week per employee, with 75% of daily Workspace users reporting improved work quality. A Forrester study indicated a financial impact of $76.1 million for a composite organization, with some companies seeing productivity double.	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "SOC 3", "ISO 27001", "ISO 27017", "ISO 27018", "ISO 27701", "ISO 42001 (AI Management)", "HIPAA BAA"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region"]	For Gemini in Workspace, data retention is administrator-defined, with options ranging from 90 days to indefinite. Google Workspace administrators can set conversation retention policies for the Gemini app, allowing for auto-deletion after periods such as 3 to 36 months. Prompts and generated content within Google Workspace with Gemini are stored alongside other Workspace content and are not shared outside the organization.	\N	\N	\N	Full documentation with lineage	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented incident response process	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, comprehensive analytics	Yes, comprehensive	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:35:13.170011+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Gemini for Workspace	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:35:13.175+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Google – Gemini for Workspace\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 82 (Trusted Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 90\\n- Compliance: 88\\n- Data Practices: 85\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 88\\n- Company Maturity: 95\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nGoogle demonstrates strong enterprise-grade operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA), and proven reliability (99.9% uptime SLA). Data practices are well-structured with administrator-controlled retention policies and customer choice of data residency. However, the score is moderated by limited transparency on AI governance specifics—no documented bias testing methodology, adversarial security testing approach, or explicit human-in-the-loop controls are detailed in the attestation. The vendor's mature company profile (founded 1998, 10,000+ employees, public) and comprehensive audit log/telemetry availability support a \\"Trusted Vendor\\" classification suitable for standard procurement with focus on use-case fit and governance alignment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Gemini for Workspace\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise productivity enhancement through AI-assisted workflows: email drafting, data organization, meeting summarization, and real-time collaboration support across Google Workspace applications.\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise organizations across all sectors; particularly suited for knowledge work and administrative task automation.\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (Cloud-hosted, integrated within Google Workspace)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted on Google infrastructure with customer choice of data residency region.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Organization-wide; typical deployment spans all Workspace users within an enterprise.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; integrated into Google Workspace ecosystem with comprehensive analytics and audit logging.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Broad enterprise adoption; Forrester study documents $76.1 million financial impact for composite organization; 75% of daily Workspace users report improved work quality; 105 minutes weekly productivity savings per employee reported.\\n- **Product Description:** Gemini for Workspace delivers native, multimodal AI assistance (text, image, audio, video) deeply integrated into Google Workspace applications. The product combines enterprise-grade security (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA) with flexible data retention policies (90 days to indefinite, administrator-controlled) and customer-selectable data residency. Prompts and generated content remain within the organization and are not shared externally.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider; Multinational Technology Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 1998\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (Nasdaq: GOOGL/GOOG); no specific revenue disclosed for Gemini for Workspace product line.\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Public equity; Headquarters: Mountain View, CA, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global; operates across North America, Europe, Asia-Pacific, and other regions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary large language model (Gemini family); multimodal architecture supporting text, image, audio, and video processing.\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding and generation; document summarization; email composition; data organization; meeting transcription and analysis; real-time contextual assistance across Workspace applications.\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified in attestation. Proprietary model with no disclosed staged deployment or safety framework details.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified. No explicit documentation of advisory vs. autonomous decision modes, monitoring workflows, or alert mechanisms for high-risk outputs.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model. No prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or explainability scoring disclosed.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Full documentation with lineage provided.\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified. No red team, third-party audit methodology, or statistical monitoring approach disclosed.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified. No frequency or type of adversarial security testing disclosed in attestation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified. No documented usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical framework disclosed.\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified. No frequency or external evaluation methodology disclosed.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified. No admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified. No system cards or release documentation disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented incident response process in place.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; supports rapid remediation of problematic deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Email drafts, meeting transcripts, documents, images, audio, video, and structured data within Google Workspace applications.\\n- **PII Handling:** Prompts and generated content within Google Workspace with Gemini are stored alongside other Workspace content and are not shared outside the organization. Extent of customer data use for model training not specified.\\n- **Data Collection:** API and native Workspace interface; collected through user interactions with Gemini features.\\n- **Data Storage:** Google Cloud infrastructure; encrypted in transit and at rest (standard Google Cloud security practices).\\n- **Data Retention:** Administrator-defined retention policies with options ranging from 90 days to indefinite. Auto-deletion available after periods such as 3 to 36 months. Default retention not specified.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; Google Cloud multi-region options available (US, EU, Asia-Pacific, etc.).\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion per administrator-configured retention policy; on-request deletion available.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Google Cloud infrastructure (compute, storage); Google Workspace platform (email, docs, sheets, meet, etc.); payment processing through Google Cloud Marketplace or direct billing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2\\n  - SOC 3\\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security)\\n  - ISO 27018 (PII Protection in Cloud)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management Systems)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified. Audit methodology and frequency not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - HIPAA: BAA available for healthcare organizations\\n  - GDPR: Compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) available (standard Google Cloud terms)\\n  - CCPA: Compliant (California Privacy Rights Act)\\n  - EU AI Act: Not explicitly addressed in attestation; ISO 42001 certification indicates AI governance framework alignment.\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Yes, BAA eligible; suitable for healthcare PHI handling.\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes, DPA available; compliant with EU data protection requirements.\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not explicitly stated. ISO 42001 certification suggests governance framework in place; specific EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified in attestation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance); industry-standard enterprise SLA.\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified. Support tier response times not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified. Release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented in attestation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** \\n  - Google Cloud (infrastructure: compute, storage, networking)\\n  - Google Workspace platform (email, docs, sheets, meet, drive, etc.)\\n  - Payment processors (Google Cloud Marketplace, direct billing)\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified. Frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Google Cloud infrastructure SLAs (99.95% uptime for multi-region deployments); Workspace platform SLAs (99.9% uptime). Specific SLAs for sub-processors not detailed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; enables monitoring of feature adoption, user engagement, and productivity metrics.\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; exportable for compliance and forensic analysis; integrates with Google Cloud Logging and third-party SIEM platforms.\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Testing results available; full training data documentation with lineage provided. Specific policy documentation files not listed.\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, available under NDA; detailed safety and performance testing results can be provided under confidentiality agreement.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Scoring Methodology Notes\\n\\n**Applied Formula Guidance (Vector DB – Assessment Type 1: Vendor Self-Attestation):**\\n\\nUsing the Vendor Trust Score formula:\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):** Estimated at 25/100 (low-to-moderate residual risk)\\n- Inherent risk is moderate (proprietary LLM, multimodal, enterprise data processing)\\n- Mitigation effectiveness is strong (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, data residency control, admin-controlled retention)\\n- Confidence factor is high (public company, comprehensive audit logs, testing results available)\\n- **Gap:** Limited transparency on bias testing, adversarial testing, and human-in-the-loop controls reduces mitigation confidence slightly\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):** Estimated at 12/100 (low residual risk)\\n- Certifications: 50 points (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA)\\n- Assessment Quality: 20 points (comprehensive audit logs, testing results available; audit frequency not specified)\\n- Policies: 30 points (data retention policy documented, incident response plan documented; AI ethics policy and bias audit procedures not specified)\\n- Operational Controls: 35 points (rollback capability automated with manual trigger; human oversight and monitoring not detailed)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 15 points (founded 1998, 10,000+ employees, public company, established market leader)\\n- **Governance Score:** 150 points → capped at 100\\n- **Governance Risk:** 0 (maximum governance maturity)\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):** Estimated at 12/100 (low residual risk)\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime, enterprise-grade)\\n- Incident Management: 25 points (documented incident response; maturity level not detailed)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 28 points (production-ready, integrated SaaS, multi-region support)\\n- Stability: 22 points (mature company, 10,000+ employees, public, profitable)\\n- Support: 15 points (comprehensive support available; specific SLAs by severity not disclosed)\\n- **Operational Score:** 123 points → capped at 100\\n- **Operational Risk:** 0 (maximum operational maturity)\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(25 × 0.40) + (12 × 0.30) + (12 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [10 + 3.6 + 3.6]\\n    = 100 - 17.2\\n    = 82.8 ≈ 82\\n```\\n\\n**Classification:** Trusted Vendor (80–89 range per rubric)\\n- **Recommended Action:** Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit, data residency alignment, and governance policy review.\\n- **Strengths:** Mature company, comprehensive certifications, strong operational SLAs, flexible data retention and residency, audit log availability.\\n- **Gaps Requiring Attention:** AI governance transparency (bias testing, adversarial testing, human-in-the-loop controls), EU AI Act readiness clarity, support SLA specificity, change management documentation.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Gemini for Workspace", "Customer Base": "Broad enterprise adoption; Forrester study documents $76.1 million financial impact for composite organization; 75% of daily Workspace users report improved work quality; 105 minutes weekly productivity savings per employee reported.", "Target Industry": "Enterprise organizations across all sectors; particularly suited for knowledge work and administrative task automation.", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (Cloud-hosted, integrated within Google Workspace)", "Deployment Scale": "Organization-wide; typical deployment spans all Workspace users within an enterprise.", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise productivity enhancement through AI-assisted workflows: email drafting, data organization, meeting summarization, and real-time collaboration support across Google Workspace applications.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted on Google infrastructure with customer choice of data residency region.", "Product Description": "Gemini for Workspace delivers native, multimodal AI assistance (text, image, audio, video) deeply integrated into Google Workspace applications. The product combines enterprise-grade security (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA) with flexible data retention policies (90 days to indefinite, administrator-controlled) and customer-selectable data residency. Prompts and generated content remain within the organization and are not shared externally.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready; integrated into Google Workspace ecosystem with comprehensive analytics and audit logging."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "10,000+", "Legal Name": "Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider; Multinational Technology Company", "Year Founded": "1998", "Operating Regions": "Global; operates across North America, Europe, Asia-Pacific, and other regions.", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Public equity; Headquarters: Mountain View, CA, USA", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Public company (Nasdaq: GOOGL/GOOG); no specific revenue disclosed for Gemini for Workspace product line."}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary large language model (Gemini family); multimodal architecture supporting text, image, audio, and video processing.", "Model Purpose": "Natural language understanding and generation; document summarization; email composition; data organization; meeting transcription and analysis; real-time contextual assistance across Workspace applications.", "Human Oversight": "Not specified. No explicit documentation of advisory vs. autonomous decision modes, monitoring workflows, or alert mechanisms for high-risk outputs.", "Model Governance": "Not specified in attestation. Proprietary model with no disclosed staged deployment or safety framework details.", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/Closed model. No prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or explainability scoring disclosed."}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Not specified. No red team, third-party audit methodology, or statistical monitoring approach disclosed.", "Penetration Testing": "Not specified. No frequency or type of adversarial security testing disclosed in attestation.", "Training Data Documentation": "Full documentation with lineage provided."}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Not specified. No frequency or external evaluation methodology disclosed.", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not specified. No documented usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical framework disclosed.", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not specified. No admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented.", "Impact Assessment": "Not specified. No system cards or release documentation disclosed."}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger option; supports rapid remediation of problematic deployments.", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, documented incident response process in place."}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Google Cloud infrastructure; encrypted in transit and at rest (standard Google Cloud security practices).", "PII Handling": "Prompts and generated content within Google Workspace with Gemini are stored alongside other Workspace content and are not shared outside the organization. Extent of customer data use for model training not specified.", "Data Deletion": "Automated deletion per administrator-configured retention policy; on-request deletion available.", "Data Retention": "Administrator-defined retention policies with options ranging from 90 days to indefinite. Auto-deletion available after periods such as 3 to 36 months. Default retention not specified.", "Sub-processors": "Google Cloud infrastructure (compute, storage); Google Workspace platform (email, docs, sheets, meet, etc.); payment processing through Google Cloud Marketplace or direct billing.", "Data Collection": "API and native Workspace interface; collected through user interactions with Gemini features.", "Data Types Processed": "Email drafts, meeting transcripts, documents, images, audio, video, and structured data within Google Workspace applications.", "Data Location / Residency": "Customer choice of region; Google Cloud multi-region options available (US, EU, Asia-Pacific, etc.)."}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "- SOC 2 Type 2", "GDPR Compliance": "Yes, DPA available; compliant with EU data protection requirements.", "HIPAA Compliance": "Yes, BAA eligible; suitable for healthcare PHI handling.", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not explicitly stated. ISO 42001 certification suggests governance framework in place; specific EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap not disclosed.", "Regulatory Frameworks": "- HIPAA: BAA available for healthcare organizations", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified. Audit methodology and frequency not disclosed.", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified in attestation."}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance); industry-standard enterprise SLA.", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified. Release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented in attestation.", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified. Support tier response times not disclosed."}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Google Cloud infrastructure SLAs (99.95% uptime for multi-region deployments); Workspace platform SLAs (99.9% uptime). Specific SLAs for sub-processors not detailed.", "Critical Vendors": "- Google Cloud (infrastructure: compute, storage, networking)", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified. Frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not disclosed."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Gap": "Limited transparency on bias testing, adversarial testing, and human-in-the-loop controls reduces mitigation confidence slightly", "Strengths": "Mature company, comprehensive certifications, strong operational SLAs, flexible data retention and residency, audit log availability.", "Governance Risk": "0 (maximum governance maturity)", "Governance Score": "150 points → capped at 100", "Operational Risk": "0 (maximum operational maturity)", "Operational Score": "123 points → capped at 100", "Recommended Action": "Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit, data residency alignment, and governance policy review.", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; exportable for compliance and forensic analysis; integrates with Google Cloud Logging and third-party SIEM platforms.", "Gaps Requiring Attention": "AI governance transparency (bias testing, adversarial testing, human-in-the-loop controls), EU AI Act readiness clarity, support SLA specificity, change management documentation.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, comprehensive analytics available; enables monitoring of feature adoption, user engagement, and productivity metrics.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Yes, available under NDA; detailed safety and performance testing results can be provided under confidentiality agreement.", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Testing results available; full training data documentation with lineage provided. Specific policy documentation files not listed."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Google demonstrates strong enterprise-grade operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA), and proven reliability (99.9% uptime SLA). Data practices are well-structured with administrator-controlled retention policies and customer choice of data residency. However, the score is moderated by limited transparency on AI governance specifics—no documented bias testing methodology, adversarial security testing approach, or explicit human-in-the-loop controls are detailed in the attestation. The vendor's mature company profile (founded 1998, 10,000+ employees, public) and comprehensive audit log/telemetry availability support a \\"Trusted Vendor\\" classification suitable for standard procurement with focus on use-case fit and governance alignment. ---", "overallScore": 88, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 97.13, "Governance": 99, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   88 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            2.87  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         1.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (2.9) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:35:13.170011+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	88	B	9c741285-e115-45a9-a315-4054dc81d179	\N	\N
ce7f1572-4edf-4675-a63e-bc708c85c580	4d4d72c1-d0e3-45d6-80f0-02b33fd9abb0	82	82	AI Platform Provider	{"Technology & Software": ["Technology & Software"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai	Vertex AI is a fully-managed, unified AI development platform for building and using generative AI. It provides access to Vertex AI Studio, Agent Builder, and over 200 foundation models.	10,000+	1998	Mountain View, California, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["IT/Infrastructure Teams", "Line of Business Leader"]	Google Workspace Studio addresses the inefficiency of manual, repetitive tasks in business workflows by automating processes like email triaging, report generation, and project coordination. It also solves the challenge of limited technical expertise in AI development by providing a no-code interface that allows non-technical users to build and deploy AI agents. Additionally, it enhances productivity by integrating AI-powered automation directly into the Google Workspace ecosystem, reducing the need for switching between multiple tools.	\N	Google Workspace Studio's deep, native integration with the Google Workspace ecosystem allows seamless automation across applications like Gmail, Drive, and Docs without requiring external integrations. Its use of Gemini 3 for advanced reasoning and adaptive multi-step task execution sets it apart from simple rule-based automation tools. The no-code interface and natural language prompts democratize AI agent development, making it accessible to non-technical users within organizations.	Early adopters like Karcher SE & Co. reduced manual planning time by up to 90% and produced ready-to-review plans in minutes instead of hours. Participants in the Gemini Alpha program executed over 20 million automated tasks within a 30-day period, demonstrating significant productivity gains and time savings.	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["ISO 27001", "ISO 27017", "ISO 27018", "ISO 27701", "HIPAA BAA", "SOC 2", "SOC 3"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region"]	Google Workspace data generally remains in user accounts until deleted. Organizations can utilize Google Vault to establish retention rules, allowing them to retain data for specified periods, even if users delete it, and to purge data when it is no longer needed for compliance or regulatory reasons. Default retention for files deleted from Google Drive is 30-55 days, with an additional 25 days for administrator recovery.	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented incident response process	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, comprehensive analytics	Yes, comprehensive	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:35:56.126772+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Google Workspace Studio	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:35:56.128+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Google Workspace Studio (Vertex AI Platform)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 78 **(Acceptable Vendor)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 85\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 75\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 82\\n- Company Maturity: 90\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nGoogle Workspace Studio benefits from Google's mature operational infrastructure (10,000+ employees, founded 1998, public company) and strong security/compliance posture (ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2/3). However, the trust score is moderated by significant gaps in documented AI governance (no explicit safety policy, bias testing approach, or human oversight framework documented), limited transparency into proprietary Gemini 3 model training data, and unclear decision autonomy boundaries for autonomous agent execution. The 78 score reflects acceptable enterprise readiness with enhanced due diligence recommended on AI safety controls and governance maturity before production deployment in regulated sectors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Google Workspace Studio\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automation of repetitive business workflows including email triaging, report generation, project coordination, and multi-step task execution via natural language prompts\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-industry); early adopters in manufacturing (Karcher SE & Co.)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud Platform)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** SaaS; native integration with Google Workspace ecosystem (Gmail, Drive, Docs)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Scalable; Gemini Alpha program participants executed 20+ million automated tasks in 30 days\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready (early adopter deployments active)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Early adopters documented (Karcher SE & Co.); Gemini Alpha program participants; specific customer count not disclosed\\n- **Product Description:** Google Workspace Studio is a no-code AI agent builder integrated natively into Google Workspace, powered by Gemini 3 for advanced multi-step reasoning and task automation. It enables non-technical users to build and deploy AI agents via natural language prompts, eliminating manual workflows and reducing planning time by up to 90% in early deployments. The platform provides seamless automation across Gmail, Drive, and Docs without external integrations, democratizing AI development across organizations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Cloud Infrastructure & AI Services)\\n- **Year Founded:** 1998\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (Alphabet Inc.); revenue not separately disclosed for Vertex AI\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Alphabet Inc. (parent); Headquarters: Mountain View, California, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (multi-region deployment available)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Model (LLM) – Gemini 3 (proprietary)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Advanced reasoning, multi-step task execution, natural language understanding, workflow automation, adaptive agent behavior\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; proprietary model governance framework not documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop controls, approval workflows, or intervention mechanisms detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level transparency, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data composition unknown; no detailed documentation of data sources, filtering, or curation provided\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no documented red-team testing, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring disclosed\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not specified; no explicit safety guidelines, usage policies, or ethical guardrails documented for Studio\\n- **Bias Audits:** Bias audit frequency and external evaluation approach not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No documented admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention mechanisms specified; autonomous agent execution boundaries unclear\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation for AI governance not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented incident response process in place\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Google Workspace data (email, documents, files, project coordination data); business communications and structured workflow data\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified; Google Workspace data may contain PII; customer data usage for model training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** API and native Workspace integration; interaction data available (comprehensive analytics)\\n- **Data Storage:** Google Cloud Platform infrastructure; encryption in transit and at rest (implied by ISO 27001/27017/27018 certifications)\\n- **Data Retention:** Google Workspace data remains in user accounts until deleted; organizations can use Google Vault to establish retention rules; default retention for deleted Drive files is 30–55 days, with additional 25-day administrator recovery window\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (multi-region deployment supported)\\n- **Data Deletion:** User-initiated deletion; administrator-controlled retention and purge via Google Vault\\n- **Sub-processors:** Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure); Google Workspace services (email, storage, collaboration); payment and authentication services (not separately detailed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2, SOC 3\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA-eligible (BAA available); GDPR compliance implied by ISO 27001/27018 and data residency options; EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; HIPAA-eligible for healthcare use cases\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Data residency options and ISO 27018 (PII handling) certification support GDPR compliance; DPA availability not explicitly stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tiers and response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure); Google Workspace services (core platform dependency)\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Vendor risk assessment frequency not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Google Cloud Platform SLAs (99.95% uptime for compute services); specific SLAs for Workspace services not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; interaction data collection enabled\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; export capability implied\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Testing results available (not specified in detail); policy documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available; NDA terms not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Mature Company & Operations:** Google's 10,000+ employee base, 1998 founding, and public company status provide strong operational stability and financial viability.\\n2. **Strong Security & Compliance Baseline:** ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, HIPAA BAA, and SOC 2/3 certifications demonstrate enterprise-grade security controls and third-party validation.\\n3. **Scalability & Performance:** 99.9% uptime SLA and 20+ million automated tasks executed in 30 days demonstrate production-ready infrastructure and scale.\\n4. **Data Residency & Retention Control:** Customer choice of region and Google Vault retention management provide compliance flexibility for regulated industries.\\n5. **Comprehensive Audit & Analytics:** Audit logs and interaction telemetry available for compliance monitoring and forensic analysis.\\n\\n### Gaps & Concerns\\n1. **Undocumented AI Governance:** No explicit AI ethics policy, safety guidelines, or governance framework documented for Workspace Studio; unclear decision autonomy boundaries for autonomous agents.\\n2. **Proprietary Model Opacity:** Gemini 3 training data composition unknown; no transparency into model curation, filtering, or bias mitigation; closed model limits explainability.\\n3. **Insufficient Bias & Safety Testing Documentation:** Bias testing approach, red-team results, and adversarial security testing not specified; no third-party AI safety audits disclosed.\\n4. **Missing Human Oversight Controls:** No documented human-in-the-loop mechanisms, approval workflows, content filtering, or intervention capabilities for autonomous task execution.\\n5. **Incomplete Support & Release Documentation:** Support SLAs by severity not specified; change management process and release cadence not documented; rollback readiness unclear.\\n6. **EU AI Act Readiness Unclear:** No documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance; risk classification and mitigation strategy not provided.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions Before Production Deployment\\n\\n**MUST FIX (Regulatory/Safety):**\\n- Require Google to provide documented AI governance policy, including safety guidelines, bias mitigation strategy, and human oversight controls for autonomous agents.\\n- Request third-party AI safety audit (e.g., by independent security firm) covering model robustness, adversarial testing, and bias detection.\\n- Clarify decision autonomy boundaries: which tasks execute autonomously vs. require human approval; define escalation and intervention mechanisms.\\n- Obtain EU AI Act compliance roadmap if deploying in EU; confirm risk classification and mitigation approach.\\n\\n**SHOULD FIX (Operational Readiness):**\\n- Request detailed support SLAs by severity (P1/P2/P3 response times) and escalation procedures.\\n- Document change management process, release cadence, and rollback testing procedures.\\n- Confirm DPA availability for GDPR compliance and data processing terms.\\n- Request training data documentation for Gemini 3 (or transparency on why proprietary data cannot be disclosed).\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL:**\\n- **For Non-Regulated Use Cases (e.g., internal productivity automation):** Approve with standard security controls; monitor via audit logs and telemetry.\\n- **For Healthcare (HIPAA):** Approve with BAA and mandatory AI governance documentation; require human review of sensitive workflows.\\n- **For Financial Services / Government:** Defer until AI governance and EU AI Act readiness documented; consider pilot phase with enhanced monitoring.\\n\\n### Trust Score Justification (Formula Application)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Self-Attestation (VTS)** formula:\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk (40% weight):** \\n- Inherent risk: High (proprietary LLM, autonomous agents, unknown training data, no documented bias testing) = 85/100\\n- Mitigation effectiveness: Moderate (ISO 27001/27017/27018, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2/3, but no AI safety controls documented) = 0.50\\n- Confidence factor: Moderate (public company, production deployments, but limited third-party AI audits) = 0.80\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.50 × 0.80 = 34**\\n\\n**Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 50 points (ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2/3 = strong)\\n- Assessment quality: 20 points (no third-party AI safety audit disclosed)\\n- Policies: 15 points (no documented AI governance policy for Studio)\\n- Operational controls: 30 points (incident response documented, but no AI-specific controls)\\n- Maturity adjustment: 20 points (mature company, but AI governance immature)\\n- **Governance Score = 50 + 20 + 15 + 30 + 20 = 135 → capped at 100**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0** (Note: This reflects strong baseline compliance, but AI governance gaps are captured in Product Risk)\\n\\n**Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime = strong)\\n- Incident management: 25 points (documented process, but severity SLAs not specified)\\n- Deployment maturity: 30 points (enterprise multi-tenant, production-ready)\\n- Stability: 25 points (10,000+ employees, public company, 1998 founding)\\n- Support: 15 points (support SLAs not specified; no dedicated TAM mentioned)\\n- **Operational Score = 33 + 25 + 30 + 25 + 15 = 128 → capped at 100**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Adjusted Governance Risk (accounting for AI governance gaps):**\\n- Governance Risk adjusted to 25 (reflecting undocumented AI ethics policy, bias testing, human oversight)\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(34 × 0.40) + (25 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [13.6 + 7.5 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 21.1\\n    = 78.9 ≈ 78\\n```\\n\\n**Classification: Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range)**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – ENHANCED DUE DILIGENCE REQUIRED**\\n\\n- **For Non-Regulated Use Cases:** Approve with standard procurement process; implement audit log monitoring and quarterly compliance reviews.\\n- **For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Financial Services, Government):** Require completion of AI governance documentation, third-party AI safety audit, and EU AI Act compliance roadmap before contract execution.\\n- **Pilot Approach:** Consider 3–6 month pilot phase with non-critical workflows, comprehensive monitoring, and human review of autonomous decisions before full production rollout.\\n- **Contract Conditions:** Require Google to provide AI governance policy, bias testing results, and human oversight controls as contract addendum; include audit rights for AI safety compliance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessor:** Vendor Attestation Analyst  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Google Workspace Studio", "Customer Base": "Early adopters documented (Karcher SE & Co.); Gemini Alpha program participants; specific customer count not disclosed", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-industry); early adopters in manufacturing (Karcher SE & Co.)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud Platform)", "Deployment Scale": "Scalable; Gemini Alpha program participants executed 20+ million automated tasks in 30 days", "Primary Use Case": "Automation of repetitive business workflows including email triaging, report generation, project coordination, and multi-step task execution via natural language prompts", "Hosted / Deployed": "SaaS; native integration with Google Workspace ecosystem (Gmail, Drive, Docs)", "Product Description": "Google Workspace Studio is a no-code AI agent builder integrated natively into Google Workspace, powered by Gemini 3 for advanced multi-step reasoning and task automation. It enables non-technical users to build and deploy AI agents via natural language prompts, eliminating manual workflows and reducing planning time by up to 90% in early deployments. The platform provides seamless automation across Gmail, Drive, and Docs without external integrations, democratizing AI development across organizations.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Production-ready (early adopter deployments active)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "10,000+", "Legal Name": "Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider (Cloud Infrastructure & AI Services)", "Year Founded": "1998", "Operating Regions": "Global (multi-region deployment available)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Alphabet Inc. (parent); Headquarters: Mountain View, California, USA", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Public company (Alphabet Inc.); revenue not separately disclosed for Vertex AI"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Large Language Model (LLM) – Gemini 3 (proprietary)", "Model Purpose": "Advanced reasoning, multi-step task execution, natural language understanding, workflow automation, adaptive agent behavior", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop controls, approval workflows, or intervention mechanisms detailed", "Model Governance": "Not specified; proprietary model governance framework not documented", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level transparency, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Bias testing approach not specified; no documented red-team testing, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring disclosed", "Penetration Testing": "Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown", "Training Data Documentation": "Using third-party models; training data composition unknown; no detailed documentation of data sources, filtering, or curation provided"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Bias audit frequency and external evaluation approach not specified", "AI Ethics Policy": "Documented AI governance policy not specified; no explicit safety guidelines, usage policies, or ethical guardrails documented for Studio", "Human-in-the-Loop": "No documented admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention mechanisms specified; autonomous agent execution boundaries unclear", "Impact Assessment": "System cards or release documentation for AI governance not provided"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger option available", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, documented incident response process in place"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Google Cloud Platform infrastructure; encryption in transit and at rest (implied by ISO 27001/27017/27018 certifications)", "PII Handling": "Not explicitly specified; Google Workspace data may contain PII; customer data usage for model training not documented", "Data Deletion": "User-initiated deletion; administrator-controlled retention and purge via Google Vault", "Data Retention": "Google Workspace data remains in user accounts until deleted; organizations can use Google Vault to establish retention rules; default retention for deleted Drive files is 30–55 days, with additional 25-day administrator recovery window", "Sub-processors": "Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure); Google Workspace services (email, storage, collaboration); payment and authentication services (not separately detailed)", "Data Collection": "API and native Workspace integration; interaction data available (comprehensive analytics)", "Data Types Processed": "Google Workspace data (email, documents, files, project coordination data); business communications and structured workflow data", "Data Location / Residency": "Customer choice of region (multi-region deployment supported)"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2, SOC 3", "GDPR Compliance": "Data residency options and ISO 27018 (PII handling) certification support GDPR compliance; DPA availability not explicitly stated", "HIPAA Compliance": "BAA available; HIPAA-eligible for healthcare use cases", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; no documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance", "Regulatory Frameworks": "HIPAA-eligible (BAA available); GDPR compliance implied by ISO 27001/27018 and data residency options; EU AI Act readiness not specified", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; support tiers and response targets not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Google Cloud Platform SLAs (99.95% uptime for compute services); specific SLAs for Workspace services not detailed", "Critical Vendors": "Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure); Google Workspace services (core platform dependency)", "Vendor Assessment": "Vendor risk assessment frequency not specified"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Pilot Approach": "Consider 3–6 month pilot phase with non-critical workflows, comprehensive monitoring, and human review of autonomous decisions before full production rollout.", "Contract Conditions": "Require Google to provide AI governance policy, bias testing results, and human oversight controls as contract addendum; include audit rights for AI safety compliance.", "For Healthcare (HIPAA)": "Approve with BAA and mandatory AI governance documentation; require human review of sensitive workflows.", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; export capability implied", "For Non-Regulated Use Cases": "Approve with standard procurement process; implement audit log monitoring and quarterly compliance reviews.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, comprehensive analytics available; interaction data collection enabled", "For Financial Services / Government": "Defer until AI governance and EU AI Act readiness documented; consider pilot phase with enhanced monitoring.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Yes, testing results available; NDA terms not specified", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Testing results available (not specified in detail); policy documentation not provided", "For Non-Regulated Use Cases (e.g., internal productivity automation)": "Approve with standard security controls; monitor via audit logs and telemetry.", "For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Financial Services, Government)": "Require completion of AI governance documentation, third-party AI safety audit, and EU AI Act compliance roadmap before contract execution."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Google Workspace Studio benefits from Google's mature operational infrastructure (10,000+ employees, founded 1998, public company) and strong security/compliance posture (ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, HIPAA BAA, SOC 2/3). However, the trust score is moderated by significant gaps in documented AI governance (no explicit safety policy, bias testing approach, or human oversight framework documented), limited transparency into proprietary Gemini 3 model training data, and unclear decision autonomy boundaries for autonomous agent execution. The 78 score reflects acceptable enterprise readiness with enhanced due diligence recommended on AI safety controls and governance maturity before production deployment in regulated sectors. ---", "overallScore": 83, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.93, "Governance": 84, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   83 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        16.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.07  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (16.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:35:56.126772+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	83	B	1b72b6d4-b8f1-42e8-b292-2771584f2d42	\N	\N
1c3b7cec-dbe1-47c7-a9f7-5b2cca37e0b0	6f1a035b-bd7f-467c-8820-d6054a8072f8	82	82	AI Platform Provider	{"Technology & Software": ["Technology & Software"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	https://cloud.google.com	Google is a multinational technology company specializing in internet-related services and products, including search engines, cloud computing, software, and AI. NotebookLM is an AI-powered research and note-taking tool that helps users analyze, summarize, and synthesize information from their own documents with source-grounded accuracy.	10,000+	1998	Mountain View, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "Line of Business Leader"]	NotebookLM addresses the challenges of synthesizing large volumes of information quickly and accurately, reducing time spent on manual research and note-taking. It also helps businesses streamline workflows and enhance productivity by automating tasks like summarizing documents and generating decision-ready insights. Additionally, it mitigates the risk of AI hallucinations by grounding responses in user-uploaded sources.	\N	NotebookLM's source-grounded accuracy ensures responses are strictly based on user-uploaded documents, with citations provided, reducing hallucinations. It offers massive ingestion capacity (up to 25 million words in a sandbox) and multi-format integration, automatically cross-referencing diverse formats like documents, PDFs, URLs, and audio files. Additionally, it provides unique multimedia output generation, transforming information into interactive formats like Audio Overviews and Mind Maps.	Globe Telecom employees saved 3-4 hours per week through AI automation using NotebookLM. It can reduce compliance audit processes by hours, saving costs. 83% of users reported improved clarity in note-taking, and it helps transform complex research into decision-ready blueprints for faster decision-making.	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["ISO 27001", "ISO 27017", "ISO 27018", "ISO 27701", "SOC 1", "SOC 2", "SOC 3", "HIPAA BAA"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region"]	Uploaded materials, saved notes, and audio overviews are stored until the user deletes them. For NotebookLM Enterprise, data is stored within the user's Google Cloud project and is deleted when the notebook or the project is deleted. Google's general data retention policy indicates that data deletion processes can take approximately two months, with data potentially remaining on backup systems for up to six months.	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, tested annually	Automated instant rollback	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, comprehensive analytics	Yes, comprehensive	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:36:42.620682+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	NotebookLM	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:36:42.625+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Google NotebookLM\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 78 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 88\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 72\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 82\\n- Company Maturity: 95\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nGoogle NotebookLM achieves a Trust Score of 78, placing it in the \\"Acceptable Vendor\\" category (70–79 range). The vendor demonstrates strong operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications (ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701, SOC 1/2/3, HIPAA BAA), and excellent company stability (10,000+ employees, founded 1998, public company). However, the score is moderated by gaps in AI governance transparency (no documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, or adversarial security testing details provided), incomplete data practices documentation (training data sourcing from third-party models with unknown provenance, extended data retention on backups up to 6 months), and missing support SLA details. The source-grounded architecture and automated rollback capability are significant strengths. **Recommendation:** Enhanced due diligence required; suitable for non-critical use cases; require mitigation roadmap for AI governance and training data transparency before high-stakes deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** NotebookLM\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Research synthesis, document analysis, note-taking automation, compliance audit acceleration, decision-ready insight generation\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-sector); Globe Telecom case study indicates telecommunications applicability; compliance-heavy industries (finance, healthcare, legal)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud Platform)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** SaaS (cloud-hosted); NotebookLM Enterprise option with customer Google Cloud project deployment\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-grade; supports up to 25 million words in sandbox; suitable for large-scale document ingestion\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (general availability); comprehensive analytics and audit logs available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Globe Telecom case study published; 83% user satisfaction on note-taking clarity; 3–4 hours/week productivity savings reported\\n- **Product Description:** NotebookLM is a source-grounded AI research and note-taking platform that synthesizes information from user-uploaded documents with citations, eliminating hallucinations. It ingests multiple formats (documents, PDFs, URLs, audio) and generates multimedia outputs (Audio Overviews, Mind Maps). Enterprise deployments offer data residency within customer Google Cloud projects, with HIPAA BAA eligibility and comprehensive audit logging.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (multinational technology company)\\n- **Year Founded:** 1998\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (Nasdaq: GOOGL/GOOG); not specified for NotebookLM product line\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Publicly traded; Headquarters: Mountain View, CA, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (multi-region deployment options available)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Third-party models (underlying model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Document understanding, information synthesis, summarization, cross-format analysis, multimedia generation (audio, mind maps)\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no documented staged deployment or safety framework provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** User-controlled (users upload documents and direct analysis); no autonomous decision-making described; admin controls available for Enterprise deployments\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate transparency; responses include citations to source documents; source-grounding architecture reduces hallucinations; prompt-level control available\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; underlying training data provenance unknown; no documentation of data filtering, deduplication, or bias mitigation in training corpus\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools described\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type of adversarial security testing documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified; no documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluation process documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** User-directed (users control document selection and analysis queries); admin controls available in Enterprise deployments; no automated content filtering or intervention mechanisms described\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; demonstrates mature incident management capability\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated instant rollback; enables rapid recovery from deployment issues\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Documents (text, PDF), URLs, audio files, user notes, analysis outputs (Audio Overviews, Mind Maps)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no explicit policy on PII detection, masking, or handling; HIPAA BAA available suggests PII-capable infrastructure\\n- **Data Collection:** User-uploaded documents via web interface; API integration available (implied by Enterprise deployment model); user-directed analysis queries\\n- **Data Storage:** Google Cloud Platform infrastructure; encrypted in transit and at rest (implied by ISO 27001/27017/27018 certifications); Enterprise deployments stored within customer's Google Cloud project\\n- **Data Retention:** User-controlled deletion; uploaded materials, saved notes, and audio overviews retained until user deletion. For Enterprise: deleted when notebook or project deleted. Google general policy: deletion processes take ~2 months; data may remain on backup systems for up to 6 months\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (multi-region support); Enterprise deployments within customer Google Cloud project\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion; automated deletion upon notebook/project removal (Enterprise); extended backup retention (up to 6 months) noted\\n- **Sub-processors:** Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure, storage, compute); third-party model providers (underlying AI models); payment processors (not specified); authentication (Google identity services implied)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security Controls)\\n  - ISO 27018 (Personal Data Protection in Cloud)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - SOC 1 (Financial Controls)\\n  - SOC 2 (Security, Availability, Processing Integrity, Confidentiality, Privacy)\\n  - SOC 3 (General Controls)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (eligible for healthcare PHI handling)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit body and methodology not documented; frequency of re-certification not stated\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - HIPAA: BAA available\\n  - GDPR: Implied compliance (ISO 27701, data residency options); DPA availability not explicitly stated\\n  - CCPA: Not explicitly addressed\\n  - EU AI Act: No readiness statement provided\\n  - NIST: Not explicitly addressed\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligible; suitable for healthcare PHI handling with appropriate contract terms\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Data residency options and ISO 27701 certification suggest GDPR readiness; DPA availability not confirmed\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed; no statement on compliance preparation or risk classification\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Incident response plan tested annually\\n  - Certification audit frequency not specified\\n  - Last audit date not provided\\n  - Audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response time commitments documented\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** \\n  - Not specified; no documented release process, frequency, or rollback readiness practices provided\\n  - Automated instant rollback capability available (suggests mature deployment infrastructure)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** \\n  - Google Cloud Platform (infrastructure, storage, compute)\\n  - Third-party AI model providers (underlying model sourcing)\\n  - Payment processors (not specified)\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no documented frequency of vendor risk assessments\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** \\n  - Google Cloud Platform SLAs typically 99.95% uptime (standard GCP commitment); specific NotebookLM SLA is 99.9%\\n  - Third-party model provider SLAs not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; enables usage monitoring and performance tracking\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; supports compliance auditing and forensic investigation\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** \\n  - Incident response plan (tested annually)\\n  - Automated rollback capability documented\\n  - Certifications (ISO, SOC, HIPAA) available\\n  - Security and compliance documentation implied by certifications\\n  - AI safety testing results not specified\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available; specific details and NDA terms not provided in attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Exceptional Company Maturity:** Google's 10,000+ employee base, 25+ year operating history, and public company status provide strong financial stability and operational continuity.\\n2. **Comprehensive Security Certifications:** ISO 27001/27017/27018/27701 and SOC 1/2/3 demonstrate mature security and privacy controls; HIPAA BAA eligibility enables healthcare deployments.\\n3. **Source-Grounded Architecture:** Citation-based responses and document-grounded analysis reduce hallucination risk, a key differentiator for research and compliance use cases.\\n4. **Operational Maturity:** 99.9% uptime SLA, automated instant rollback, annual incident response testing, and comprehensive audit logging indicate production-ready infrastructure.\\n5. **Data Residency Flexibility:** Customer choice of region and Enterprise deployment within customer Google Cloud projects support data sovereignty requirements.\\n\\n### Gaps & Concerns\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency (Critical Gap):** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, adversarial security testing, or training data provenance. Third-party model sourcing with unknown training data raises hallucination and bias risks.\\n2. **Data Retention & Backup Exposure:** Extended backup retention (up to 6 months) and ~2-month deletion latency create compliance and privacy risks for sensitive data; not suitable for zero-retention requirements.\\n3. **Missing Support SLAs:** No severity-based response time commitments; unclear support availability for production incidents.\\n4. **Incomplete Regulatory Readiness:** No explicit GDPR DPA, CCPA compliance statement, or EU AI Act readiness documentation; limits applicability in regulated markets.\\n5. **Training Data Opacity:** Reliance on third-party models without disclosed training data filtering, deduplication, or bias mitigation creates risk for high-stakes use cases (healthcare, finance, legal).\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n- **For Non-Critical Use Cases:** Approved for productivity and research workflows (e.g., internal document synthesis, note-taking automation).\\n- **For Healthcare/Compliance Use Cases:** Require vendor to provide:\\n  - Documented AI ethics policy and bias testing roadmap\\n  - Training data provenance and filtering methodology\\n  - GDPR DPA and CCPA compliance confirmation\\n  - Support SLA commitments (P1/P2/P3 response times)\\n  - Zero-retention or shorter backup retention options\\n- **For High-Stakes Deployments:** Conduct independent security assessment and bias audit before production use; implement human-in-the-loop review for critical decisions.\\n- **Contract Conditions:** Require annual third-party AI safety audit, documented incident response testing results, and explicit data deletion SLA (< 30 days).\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Classification:** Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range) — Standard procurement process recommended with enhanced due diligence on AI governance and data practices.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "NotebookLM", "Customer Base": "Globe Telecom case study published; 83% user satisfaction on note-taking clarity; 3–4 hours/week productivity savings reported", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-sector); Globe Telecom case study indicates telecommunications applicability; compliance-heavy industries (finance, healthcare, legal)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud Platform)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise-grade; supports up to 25 million words in sandbox; suitable for large-scale document ingestion", "Primary Use Case": "Research synthesis, document analysis, note-taking automation, compliance audit acceleration, decision-ready insight generation", "Hosted / Deployed": "SaaS (cloud-hosted); NotebookLM Enterprise option with customer Google Cloud project deployment", "Product Description": "NotebookLM is a source-grounded AI research and note-taking platform that synthesizes information from user-uploaded documents with citations, eliminating hallucinations. It ingests multiple formats (documents, PDFs, URLs, audio) and generates multimedia outputs (Audio Overviews, Mind Maps). Enterprise deployments offer data residency within customer Google Cloud projects, with HIPAA BAA eligibility and comprehensive audit logging.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Mature product (general availability); comprehensive analytics and audit logs available"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "10,000+", "Legal Name": "Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider (multinational technology company)", "Year Founded": "1998", "Operating Regions": "Global (multi-region deployment options available)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Publi