hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise multi-tenant (typical customer deployment size not specified)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage; no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count and verticals not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** ComplyAdvantage is a cloud-native AI-driven compliance platform that screens customers and transactions against sanctions, watchlists, and PEP databases in real time. The platform combines advanced search and case management capabilities with AI-powered risk detection to reduce manual effort, lower false positive rates, and improve accuracy in identifying financial crime risks. Customers report 50% reduction in manual processing time and dramatic false positive reduction, though formal independent validation is not available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** ComplyAdvantage (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2014\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage funding; revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: London, England, UK; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (global operations implied by website presence; specific regions not documented)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (AI model architecture, LLM vs. custom-trained, not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Financial crime risk detection, customer screening, watchlist matching, PEP identification, and case prioritization via advanced search\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy; governance framework not disclosed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified (advisory vs. autonomous decision-making not documented; case management interface implies human review capability, but formal oversight procedures not stated)\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features available; specific explainability mechanisms, citation capability, or decision transparency level not detailed)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified (real-time data updates mentioned for risk data, but model retraining and update cadence not documented)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available (training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed)\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools disclosed\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing documented; frequency and scope not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy disclosed; usage policies and safety guidelines not available\\n- **Bias Audits:** No formal bias audit program; frequency and external evaluation not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Case management interface implies human review; specific admin controls, content filtering, or intervention procedures not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or formal impact assessments for releases documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually (incident response plan exists and is validated through annual testing; specific procedures and escalation paths not detailed)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (deployment rollback is available; rollback testing frequency and success criteria not specified)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer identity data, transaction records, sanctions and watchlist data, PEP information, case management records\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII processing not specified; customer data usage for model training or improvement not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface (specific collection mechanisms and consent workflows not detailed)\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure (specific cloud provider, encryption standards, and storage architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Data Retention:** ComplyAdvantage retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; deletion procedures are in place when data is no longer required (specific retention periods and automated deletion timelines not specified)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified (customer choice or fixed residency not documented; EU/US data residency options not disclosed)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and when legally required (automated deletion timelines and verification procedures not specified)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified (infrastructure provider, payment processor, authentication vendor, and other critical sub-processors not disclosed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None disclosed (SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other security/compliance certifications not mentioned)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified (no independent audit program documented; audit methodology not disclosed)\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not specified (NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not documented)\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable (product is not marketed for healthcare; BAA eligibility not stated)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified (Data Processing Agreement availability, GDPR compliance controls, or adequacy not documented)\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified (engagement with EU AI Act requirements or preparation status not disclosed)\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No independent audit program disclosed; audit frequency and findings not available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance; contractual commitment and exclusions not specified)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified (severity-based response time targets not documented)\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified (release frequency, change approval process, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified (infrastructure, payments, authentication, and other critical sub-processor relationships not disclosed)\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified (frequency and scope of vendor risk assessments not documented)\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified (SLA commitments from critical infrastructure or service vendors not disclosed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics (telemetry scope, granularity, and availability for audit not detailed)\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging (log retention, export capability, and SIEM integration not specified)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; policy documentation not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not available (no formal testing results disclosed; NDA-protected results not mentioned)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Classification:** Review Recommended (D-grade, 60–69 range per vector-database rubric)\\n\\n**Key Findings:**\\n\\n1. **Operational Strengths:**\\n   - Established company (10-year history) with growth-stage funding and 201–1,000 employees\\n   - Acceptable uptime SLA (99.9%) and annual incident response testing\\n   - Automated rollback capability with manual trigger\\n   - Basic audit logging and interaction telemetry available\\n\\n2. **Critical Gaps Requiring Remediation:**\\n   - **No security certifications disclosed** (SOC 2, ISO 27001 not mentioned)\\n   - **No AI governance policy** documented; governance framework absent\\n   - **No formal bias testing or adversarial security testing** conducted\\n   - **No training data documentation** available\\n   - **No independent compliance audit program** disclosed\\n   - **GDPR/CCPA/EU AI Act readiness not documented**\\n   - **Sub-processor relationships not disclosed** (infrastructure, payments, auth)\\n   - **Support SLAs by severity not specified**\\n   - **Change management and release cadence not documented**\\n\\n3. **Residual Risk Assessment:**\\n   - **Product Risk (Moderate-High):** Moderate explainability, no formal safety testing, and undocumented training data create uncertainty about model accuracy, fairness, and robustness in financial crime detection\\n   - **Governance Risk (High):** Absence of documented AI ethics policy, bias audits, and impact assessments limits confidence in long-term compliance and risk management\\n   - **Operational Risk (Moderate):** Basic SLA and support structure acceptable for growth-stage vendor, but lack of detailed change management and support escalation procedures creates deployment risk\\n\\n**Recommended Actions Before Procurement:**\\n\\n1. **Mandatory Pre-Deployment Requirements:**\\n   - Require vendor to obtain SOC 2 Type 2 certification (or equivalent security audit) within 12 months\\n   - Demand documented AI governance policy covering model development, testing, bias detection, and human oversight\\n   - Require formal bias audit by independent third party (e.g., algorithmic auditor) covering sanctions/watchlist matching accuracy across demographic groups\\n   - Obtain complete training data documentation (sources, composition, curation practices, and update frequency)\\n\\n2. **Enhanced Due Diligence:**\\n   - Request GDPR Data Processing Agreement and CCPA compliance documentation\\n   - Obtain detailed sub-processor list (infrastructure, payments, authentication, analytics)\\n   - Request support SLAs by severity (P1/P2/P3 response times) and escalation procedures\\n   - Obtain change management and release cadence documentation with rollback testing evidence\\n\\n3. **Contractual Conditions:**\\n   - Require annual independent security audit (SOC 2 Type 2 or equivalent)\\n   - Mandate quarterly bias monitoring and annual bias audit reports\\n   - Include model explainability and decision transparency requirements in contract\\n   - Require 30-day notice and testing window for material model updates\\n\\n4. **Pilot / Phased Deployment:**\\n   - Recommend 3–6 month extended pilot with limited transaction volume (e.g., 10% of production volume)\\n   - Validate false positive rates, accuracy, and explainability against internal benchmarks\\n   - Conduct rollback testing during pilot phase\\n   - Establish governance board with vendor participation for ongoing oversight\\n\\n**Decision Framework:**\\n- **IF** vendor commits to SOC 2 certification, AI governance policy, and independent bias audit within 6 months: **CONDITIONAL APPROVAL** for pilot with mandatory gap closure before production\\n- **IF** vendor declines or delays remediation: **DEFER PROCUREMENT** and re-evaluate in 12 months or consider alternative vendors\\n\\n**Estimated Remediation Timeline:** 6–12 months (certifications, governance documentation, bias audits)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "ComplyAdvantage Platform", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count and verticals not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Financial Services (banking, insurance, fintech, payments)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-native SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise multi-tenant (typical customer deployment size not specified)", "Primary Use Case": "Real-time customer screening against sanctions lists, watchlists, and politically exposed persons (PEPs); advanced search and case management for financial crime risk detection and mitigation", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "ComplyAdvantage is a cloud-native AI-driven compliance platform that screens customers and transactions against sanctions, watchlists, and PEP databases in real time. The platform combines advanced search and case management capabilities with AI-powered risk detection to reduce manual effort, lower false positive rates, and improve accuracy in identifying financial crime risks. Customers report 50% reduction in manual processing time and dramatic false positive reduction, though formal independent validation is not available.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth stage; no formal testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "ComplyAdvantage (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2014", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (global operations implied by website presence; specific regions not documented)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: London, England, UK; specific investors not disclosed", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth-stage funding; revenue not disclosed)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified (AI model architecture, LLM vs. custom-trained, not disclosed)", "Model Purpose": "Financial crime risk detection, customer screening, watchlist matching, PEP identification, and case prioritization via advanced search", "Human Oversight": "Not specified (advisory vs. autonomous decision-making not documented; case management interface implies human review capability, but formal oversight procedures not stated)", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy; governance framework not disclosed", "Update Frequency": "Not specified (real-time data updates mentioned for risk data, but model retraining and update cadence not documented)", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate (some explainability features available; specific explainability mechanisms, citation capability, or decision transparency level not detailed)"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No formal bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools disclosed", "Penetration Testing": "No adversarial security testing documented; frequency and scope not specified", "Training Data Documentation": "No documentation available (training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed)"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "No formal bias audit program; frequency and external evaluation not specified", "AI Ethics Policy": "No documented AI ethics policy disclosed; usage policies and safety guidelines not available", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Case management interface implies human review; specific admin controls, content filtering, or intervention procedures not documented", "Impact Assessment": "No system cards or formal impact assessments for releases documented"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger (deployment rollback is available; rollback testing frequency and success criteria not specified)", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, tested annually (incident response plan exists and is validated through annual testing; specific procedures and escalation paths not detailed)"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Cloud-hosted infrastructure (specific cloud provider, encryption standards, and storage architecture not disclosed)", "PII Handling": "Extent of PII processing not specified; customer data usage for model training or improvement not disclosed", "Data Deletion": "On request and when legally required (automated deletion timelines and verification procedures not specified)", "Data Retention": "ComplyAdvantage retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; deletion procedures are in place when data is no longer required (specific retention periods and automated deletion timelines not specified)", "Sub-processors": "Not specified (infrastructure provider, payment processor, authentication vendor, and other critical sub-processors not disclosed)", "Data Collection": "API and platform interface (specific collection mechanisms and consent workflows not detailed)", "Data Types Processed": "Customer identity data, transaction records, sanctions and watchlist data, PEP information, case management records", "Data Location / Residency": "Not specified (customer choice or fixed residency not documented; EU/US data residency options not disclosed)"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "None disclosed (SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other security/compliance certifications not mentioned)", "GDPR Compliance": "Not specified (Data Processing Agreement availability, GDPR compliance controls, or adequacy not documented)", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not applicable (product is not marketed for healthcare; BAA eligibility not stated)", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified (engagement with EU AI Act requirements or preparation status not disclosed)", "Regulatory Frameworks": "Not specified (NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not documented)", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified (no independent audit program documented; audit methodology not disclosed)", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "No independent audit program disclosed; audit frequency and findings not available"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance; contractual commitment and exclusions not specified)", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified (release frequency, change approval process, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented)", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified (severity-based response time targets not documented)"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified (SLA commitments from critical infrastructure or service vendors not disclosed)", "Critical Vendors": "Not specified (infrastructure, payments, authentication, and other critical sub-processor relationships not disclosed)", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified (frequency and scope of vendor risk assessments not documented)"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging (log retention, export capability, and SIEM integration not specified)", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics (telemetry scope, granularity, and availability for audit not detailed)", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not available (no formal testing results disclosed; NDA-protected results not mentioned)", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "No formal testing conducted; policy documentation not provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** ComplyAdvantage demonstrates moderate operational maturity (99.9% SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback) and reasonable company stability (10-year history, 201–1,000 employees, Series B/C funding). However, the vendor exhibits significant governance and transparency gaps that limit trust: no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing or adversarial security testing, minimal training data documentation, no security certifications disclosed, and only basic audit logging and interaction telemetry. The moderate explainability level and absence of formal AI safety testing create residual product risk, particularly for financial crime detection where accuracy and fairness are critical. While operations and company maturity are acceptable, the lack of rigorous AI controls, compliance certifications, and governance frameworks places this vendor in the \\"Review Recommended\\" category (D-grade equivalent, 60–69 range) per the vector-database rubric. Procurement should require enhanced due diligence, formal bias audits, and documented AI governance before deployment in regulated financial services environments. ---", "overallScore": 82, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 93.4, "Governance": 86, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   82 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        14.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            6.60  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (14.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete Security certifications in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:19:21.329088+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	82	B	ebaea603-d5b0-4999-a4ac-0c8f73c29aff	\N	\N
c76ac759-baad-4852-8578-e24ae3b8737b	98e2d12f-6649-49cb-add5-d047148ed331	60	60	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Finance & Banking; Technology; Legal & Compliance": ["Finance & Banking; Technology; Legal & Compliance"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	https://www.confluence.com/	Confluence Technologies Inc. is a global technology solutions provider that helps the investment management industry solve complex investment data challenges. Their AI product, Rovo, integrates into Confluence to provide AI-powered search, content creation, and editing capabilities, enhancing team productivity and content quality.	201-1,000	1991	Pittsburgh, PA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "VP Product", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Rovo addresses the challenges of inefficient content creation and knowledge management by providing AI-powered tools that streamline content generation and improve search capabilities. It also helps teams overcome the difficulty of integrating knowledge across multiple enterprise applications.	\N	Rovo’s integration with Atlassian’s ecosystem, including Confluence and Jira, provides a seamless experience for users already within the Atlassian environment. Its ability to connect knowledge across multiple enterprise apps enhances productivity and collaboration. Additionally, Rovo’s adherence to ISO 27001 and SOC 2 compliance ensures robust security and privacy.	Evidence from use cases: Productivity & Quality Boost: Significant reduction; Reduced Cycle Time: Accelerated; Improved Accuracy: Minimized; Time Saved: Minutes; Faster Knowledge Review: 83%	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["None Currently"]	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	\N	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:20:01.739641+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Rovo	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:20:01.742+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Confluence Technologies Inc. – Rovo\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate / Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 45\\n- Compliance: 50\\n- Data Practices: 40\\n- AI Governance: 35\\n- Operations: 55\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nConfluence Technologies is a mature, established vendor (founded 1991, 201–1,000 employees) with strong company fundamentals and basic operational infrastructure. However, Rovo's trust profile is significantly constrained by critical gaps in AI governance, data practices transparency, and formal compliance certifications. While the vendor claims ISO 27001 and SOC 2 compliance in marketing materials, no certifications are currently held, and formal AI safety testing, bias audits, and training data documentation are absent. The product exhibits moderate operational maturity (documented incident response, automated rollback) but lacks the governance rigor, transparency, and independent validation required for enterprise deployment in regulated or sensitive contexts. Recommendation: **Proceed with caution for non-regulated use cases only; require substantial gap remediation (formal certifications, AI governance policy, bias testing, data residency options) before deployment in healthcare, financial services, or government sectors.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Rovo\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-powered search, content creation, and editing within Confluence; knowledge management and team productivity enhancement\\n- **Target Industry:** Investment management (primary); general enterprise (secondary)\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted, integrated with Atlassian ecosystem)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; deployment within Atlassian Confluence environment\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Team to enterprise (typical deployment within Confluence workspaces)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Product stage not specified; basic interaction telemetry available; no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count or deployment metrics not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Rovo is an AI-enabled SaaS product that integrates natively with Atlassian Confluence and Jira to deliver AI-powered search, content generation, and editing capabilities. The product enhances team productivity by streamlining content creation and enabling knowledge discovery across enterprise applications. Rovo claims adherence to ISO 27001 and SOC 2 standards, though formal certifications are not currently held; the product's closed, proprietary model limits transparency into model behavior and training data provenance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Confluence Technologies Inc.\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 1991\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Pittsburgh, PA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed global based on website and Atlassian ecosystem reach)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (proprietary/closed model; type—LLM, custom-trained, or hybrid—not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Content understanding, search ranking, content generation, editing assistance, knowledge synthesis across enterprise applications\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not specified; staged deployment approach not described\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of advisory boards, content filtering, or intervention workflows documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and filtering practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools described\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; frequency and scope not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring frameworks described\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency not specified\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; rollback testing and validation procedures not described\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Documents (Confluence pages, attachments), structured content (Jira metadata), communications (team interactions within Atlassian ecosystem); specific data types not formally enumerated\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (Rovo integration within Confluence); collection scope and opt-out mechanisms not specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards (in-transit, at-rest) not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Default and optional retention policies not specified; zero-retention option availability not confirmed\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice for data residency not offered; geographic storage location not disclosed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion capability not confirmed; automated deletion workflows not described\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider (likely AWS/Azure/GCP via Atlassian), payment processors, and authentication services not formally listed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently held.** Vendor claims ISO 27001 and SOC 2 compliance in marketing materials but provides no evidence of formal certification; certifications appear aspirational rather than current\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit conducted or documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST, GDPR, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not addressed; no compliance roadmap provided\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not addressed; BAA eligibility not confirmed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not addressed; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed; no engagement or preparation activities described\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history provided; no audit findings or remediation tracking available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not specified; contractual uptime commitment not documented\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity not provided\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Release frequency and process not specified; rollback/readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Atlassian (platform dependency); infrastructure provider (AWS/Azure/GCP assumed but not confirmed); payment processors and authentication services not formally identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Atlassian platform SLAs assumed to apply; explicit SLA commitments from Rovo not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope (user activity, feature usage, performance metrics) not detailed; data export and analysis capabilities not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; log retention, export format, and SIEM integration capabilities not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results, policy documents, or governance frameworks provided; vendor attestation incomplete\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Company Maturity:** Established vendor (33+ years in operation) with 201–1,000 employees provides operational stability and longevity\\n2. **Operational Infrastructure:** Documented incident response plan and automated rollback capability indicate basic operational readiness\\n3. **Ecosystem Integration:** Native integration with Atlassian Confluence and Jira provides seamless user experience for existing customers\\n4. **Telemetry & Logging:** Basic interaction telemetry and audit logging available for operational monitoring\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **Compliance Vacuum:** No active certifications (ISO 27001, SOC 2 claimed but not held); no independent audit history; HIPAA, GDPR, and EU AI Act readiness not addressed\\n2. **AI Governance Absence:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing, training data documentation, or safety framework; model is proprietary/closed with no transparency\\n3. **Data Practices Opacity:** PII handling, data residency options, retention policies, and sub-processor list not disclosed; customer data usage for training not clarified\\n4. **Safety Testing Gaps:** No formal adversarial testing, bias audits, or red-team activities; incident response plan documented but not tested\\n5. **Support & SLA Gaps:** Uptime SLA and support response SLAs not specified; change management and release cadence not documented\\n\\n### Risk Classification (per NIST AI RMF & EU AI Act)\\n- **Product Risk:** High (proprietary model, no transparency, no formal testing, no governance policy)\\n- **Governance Risk:** High (no certifications, no audit history, no ethics framework)\\n- **Operational Risk:** Moderate (basic incident response and rollback, but SLAs not specified)\\n- **Residual Risk:** **High** — Suitable for non-regulated, low-sensitivity use cases only (e.g., general team productivity, content creation in non-sensitive contexts)\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – NON-REGULATED USE CASES ONLY**\\n\\n**Proceed with Rovo for:**\\n- General enterprise content creation and knowledge management (non-regulated industries)\\n- Teams already embedded in Atlassian ecosystem seeking productivity gains\\n- Pilot deployments with limited scope and non-sensitive data\\n\\n**DO NOT PROCEED without substantial remediation for:**\\n- Healthcare (HIPAA-regulated) environments\\n- Financial services (SOX, GLBA-regulated) environments\\n- Government (FedRAMP, FISMA) deployments\\n- Any use case involving PHI, PII, or regulated data\\n\\n### Mandatory Remediation Roadmap (Before Regulated Deployment)\\n\\n| Remediation Item | Timeline | Priority |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Obtain ISO 27001 and SOC 2 Type 2 certifications | 6–12 months | **CRITICAL** |\\n| Conduct independent third-party AI safety audit (bias, adversarial testing, training data review) | 3–6 months | **CRITICAL** |\\n| Document and publish AI governance policy (ethics, safety, bias monitoring, human oversight) | 1–2 months | **CRITICAL** |\\n| Publish data residency options (EU, US, customer choice) and DPA/BAA templates | 1–2 months | **CRITICAL** |\\n| Test and document incident response plan with tabletop exercise | 1 month | **HIGH** |\\n| Publish support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times) and uptime SLA | 1 month | **HIGH** |\\n| Conduct GDPR and HIPAA compliance gap analysis; publish roadmap | 2–3 months | **HIGH** |\\n| Document training data sources, composition, and filtering practices | 1–2 months | **MEDIUM** |\\n| Implement bias monitoring and continuous testing framework | 3–6 months | **MEDIUM** |\\n\\n### Contract Conditions (If Proceeding)\\n\\n1. **Scope Limitation:** Restrict deployment to non-regulated, non-sensitive data only; prohibit PHI, PII, and financial data processing without explicit written approval\\n2. **Data Residency:** Require vendor to confirm data storage location and offer customer choice for residency (US, EU, or other)\\n3. **Audit Rights:** Include right to conduct independent security and AI safety audits; require vendor cooperation with third-party assessments\\n4. **Certification Roadmap:** Require vendor to commit to ISO 27001 and SOC 2 Type 2 certification within 12 months; tie renewal to certification achievement\\n5. **Incident Notification:** Require 24-hour breach notification and post-incident reporting; include SLA penalties for non-compliance\\n6. **Termination Clause:** Include termination right if vendor fails to achieve certifications or publish required governance policies within agreed timeline\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Methodology:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Framework (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)])", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Rovo", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count or deployment metrics not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Investment management (primary); general enterprise (secondary)", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted, integrated with Atlassian ecosystem)", "Deployment Scale": "Team to enterprise (typical deployment within Confluence workspaces)", "Primary Use Case": "AI-powered search, content creation, and editing within Confluence; knowledge management and team productivity enhancement", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; deployment within Atlassian Confluence environment", "Product Description": "Rovo is an AI-enabled SaaS product that integrates natively with Atlassian Confluence and Jira to deliver AI-powered search, content generation, and editing capabilities. The product enhances team productivity by streamlining content creation and enabling knowledge discovery across enterprise applications. Rovo claims adherence to ISO 27001 and SOC 2 standards, though formal certifications are not currently held; the product's closed, proprietary model limits transparency into model behavior and training data provenance.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Product stage not specified; basic interaction telemetry available; no formal testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Confluence Technologies Inc.", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "1991", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed global based on website and Atlassian ecosystem reach)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Pittsburgh, PA, USA; investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Not specified"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified (proprietary/closed model; type—LLM, custom-trained, or hybrid—not disclosed)", "Model Purpose": "Content understanding, search ranking, content generation, editing assistance, knowledge synthesis across enterprise applications", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no evidence of advisory boards, content filtering, or intervention workflows documented", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not specified; staged deployment approach not de