 contents); metadata and usage telemetry; customer configuration and integration data", "Data Location / Residency": "US only; no EU or multi-region residency options offered"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "SOC 2 Type I, SOC 2 Type II, HIPAA BAA, GDPR Compliant", "GDPR Compliance": "GDPR compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly stated but implied by compliance claim", "HIPAA Compliance": "BAA available; vendor eligible for healthcare data processing", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not addressed; no engagement or preparation documented", "Regulatory Frameworks": "GDPR compliance stated; HIPAA BAA available; NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not addressed", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology and scope not disclosed", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified; audit frequency, most recent audit date, and findings not disclosed"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release frequency, change management process, and rollback readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; support response times by severity not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not disclosed", "Critical Vendors": "Not specified; cloud infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not disclosed", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency of risk assessments for critical vendors not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not detailed", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope not specified", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not specified; no indication of model safety testing, adversarial testing, or performance validation under NDA", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Testing results available; specific test coverage, methodologies, and policy documents not provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Datafold achieves a moderate trust score of 62, reflecting solid compliance and security foundations (SOC 2 Type I/II, HIPAA BAA, GDPR compliance) but significant gaps in AI governance transparency and early-stage company maturity. The vendor demonstrates acceptable operational reliability (99.9% SLA) and data handling practices aligned with privacy regulations, yet lacks documented AI governance policies, bias testing frameworks, and adversarial security testing—critical for enterprise data quality applications. As a 2020-founded startup (11–50 employees) in the seed/Series A stage, Datafold presents moderate operational risk typical of growth-stage vendors; the absence of formal AI safety documentation and limited transparency into model decision-making processes further constrain the score. Strengths include strong compliance certifications and proven customer ROI; primary gaps are AI governance maturity, training data documentation, and evidence of rigorous model testing. ---", "overallScore": 83, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.01, "Governance": 89, "Operational": 61}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   83 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       39.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        11.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.99  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (39.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (11.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (61.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:24:07.089524+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	83	B	99d64cbf-127e-4891-a806-cea7909c466e	\N	\N
4b6713ca-da76-468f-b10e-c2b74c381433	45815824-8ab8-4b4d-b0a4-de34c8d4ad5f	68	68	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Healthcare": ["Healthcare"]}	Growth (Series B/C)	https://deepscribe.ai/	DeepScribe provides an AI-powered medical scribe that automates medical documentation for doctors, capturing patient visits and writing documentation directly within a clinician’s electronic health record system. This reduces administrative burden and improves efficiency in healthcare settings.	51-200	2017	San Francisco, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "Line of Business Leader"]	DeepScribe addresses the administrative burden on healthcare providers by automating medical documentation, reducing the time spent on paperwork, and improving the accuracy of patient records.	\N	DeepScribe combines AI-powered ambient listening with human quality assurance, ensuring high accuracy in medical documentation. It integrates directly with electronic health record systems, reducing the need for manual data entry.	DeepScribe reduces the time spent on medical documentation by up to 50%, allowing healthcare providers to see more patients and improve overall efficiency. [Corroborated by 3 evidence point(s): Reduced Documentation Time: 75%; Time Saved: 75%; Chart Closure Time: 1.6 minutes]	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "ISO 27001", "HIPAA BAA", "GDPR Compliant"]	\N	\N	["US only"]	DeepScribe retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide its services, with deletion procedures in place to remove data upon customer request or after the termination of the service agreement.	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, tested annually	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:24:45.339589+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	DeepScribe AI Medical Scribe	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:24:45.342+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## DeepScribe AI Medical Scribe\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDeepScribe demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, GDPR compliant) and operational reliability (99.9% SLA, tested incident response), positioning it as an acceptable vendor for healthcare deployment. However, significant gaps in AI governance (no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing, no training data documentation) and data practices (US-only residency, limited transparency on PII handling) create material risk. The vendor's Growth stage maturity (Series B/C, 51-200 employees) and moderate model transparency further constrain the score. Per the vendor self-attestation formula (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]), the primary driver of the 72 score is elevated Product Risk (estimated ~50/100 due to healthcare PHI handling with incomplete mitigation documentation) and Governance Risk (~45/100 due to missing AI ethics policy, bias audits, and training data transparency), partially offset by strong Operational Risk profile (estimated ~25/100 due to certified SLAs and incident response). **Recommendation: Enhanced due diligence required; require mitigation roadmap closure (AI governance policy, bias testing, training data documentation) as contract condition before production deployment.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** DeepScribe AI Medical Scribe\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automated medical documentation capture and EHR integration for clinical encounters; reduces clinician administrative burden by automating chart note generation from ambient voice recordings.\\n- **Target Industry:** Healthcare (primary); applicable to any clinical setting with EHR systems.\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; integrates directly with electronic health record systems.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployment ranges from single-specialty clinics to multi-facility health systems; per vendor, reduces documentation time by up to 50%.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage product (Series B/C); no formal third-party testing results available.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count or revenue metrics not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** DeepScribe combines AI-powered ambient listening with human quality assurance to automate medical documentation directly within EHR systems. The product captures patient visits via voice and generates structured clinical notes, reducing manual documentation time by up to 50% (corroborated by 3 evidence points: 75% reduced documentation time, 75% time saved, 1.6-minute chart closure). The solution integrates natively with major EHR platforms and includes HIPAA BAA eligibility, SOC 2 Type 2, and ISO 27001 certifications.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** DeepScribe (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2017\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (Growth stage); revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** United States (primary); data residency limited to US only\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (ambient voice recognition and clinical note generation inferred; specific model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Automated speech-to-text transcription and clinical documentation generation; capabilities include patient encounter capture, structured note generation, and EHR integration.\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; governance framework not specified.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Human quality assurance component mentioned as part of the product design; specific oversight mechanisms (review workflows, approval gates, audit trails) not detailed.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate transparency; some explainability features present but not fully documented. No information on prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or model decision transparency.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available.** Vendor has not provided training data provenance, composition, or curation methodology. This is a material gap for healthcare PHI handling.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No formal bias testing approach documented. No evidence of red-team exercises, third-party bias audits, or statistical monitoring for demographic or clinical bias in documentation generation.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or scope of adversarial security testing disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy provided. Vendor has not disclosed usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical frameworks governing model deployment and clinical decision support boundaries.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits documented; no frequency or external evaluation process specified.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human quality assurance is mentioned as part of the product; specific admin controls, content filtering, intervention workflows, and escalation procedures not detailed.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided. No evidence of structured impact assessments for clinical safety or fairness.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually. Vendor maintains a documented incident response plan with annual testing; specific response time targets, escalation procedures, and post-incident review processes not detailed.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option. Vendor supports both automated and manual rollback of deployments; specific rollback time objectives and testing frequency not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Patient visit audio recordings (ambient voice), clinical encounter transcripts, structured clinical notes, and EHR-integrated documentation. Likely includes patient demographics, medical history, and clinical assessments.\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII handling not fully specified. Product processes Protected Health Information (PHI) as part of clinical documentation; specific controls for PII de-identification, masking, or segregation not documented.\\n- **Data Collection:** Ambient voice recording via clinical encounter capture; integration with EHR systems for note storage and retrieval. Collection scope and granularity not fully specified.\\n- **Data Storage:** Hosted on cloud infrastructure (specific provider not disclosed); encryption status and key management practices not detailed.\\n- **Data Retention:** DeepScribe retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services. Deletion procedures in place upon customer request or service termination; specific retention periods and automated purge schedules not specified.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only. No multi-region or customer-choice residency options available; this may limit GDPR compliance flexibility for EU customers.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and upon service termination; automated deletion timelines not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider not disclosed; payment processing and authentication vendors not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - ISO 27001 ✓\\n  - HIPAA BAA eligible ✓\\n  - GDPR Compliant (stated; specific DPA or adequacy mechanism not detailed)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology, scope, and auditor identity not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:**\\n  - NIST: Readiness not specified\\n  - GDPR: Stated as compliant; DPA availability not confirmed\\n  - CCPA: Readiness not specified\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness not specified\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligible; specific BAA terms, covered entity obligations, and breach notification procedures not detailed.\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Stated as compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed. US-only data residency may create GDPR compliance friction for EU deployments.\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; vendor has not disclosed engagement with EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap.\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Incident Response Plan: Tested annually\\n  - Compliance Audit Frequency: Not specified\\n  - Last Audit Date: Not specified\\n  - Audit Findings: Not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance). This is a standard enterprise SLA; specific exclusions, remedies, and credit terms not detailed.\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified. Vendor has not disclosed severity-based response time targets or support escalation procedures.\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified. Vendor has not disclosed release frequency, change approval process, testing procedures, or rollback readiness practices.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendor not disclosed.\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not specified.\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available. Specific telemetry scope (e.g., API call volume, error rates, latency, user engagement) not detailed.\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available. Specific log types (authentication, API, data access, configuration changes), retention period, and export format not specified.\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results available. Vendor has not provided third-party security assessments, penetration test reports, or policy documentation beyond certifications.\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted. Vendor has not disclosed model performance benchmarks, safety testing results, or clinical validation studies (even under NDA).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Compliance Credentials:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, and stated GDPR compliance provide foundational trust for regulated healthcare deployment.\\n2. **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% SLA and annually tested incident response demonstrate operational maturity.\\n3. **Clinical Value:** Documented 50% reduction in documentation time with corroborating evidence supports clear ROI.\\n4. **Deployment Integration:** Direct EHR integration and automated rollback capability reduce implementation friction.\\n\\n### Material Gaps & Risks\\n1. **AI Governance Deficiency (Critical):** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing, or training data transparency. For healthcare PHI handling, this is a material gap requiring immediate remediation.\\n2. **Data Practices Opacity:** US-only residency, limited PII handling documentation, and no sub-processor disclosure create compliance and data sovereignty risks.\\n3. **Testing & Validation Gaps:** No formal third-party testing, no clinical validation studies, and no bias audits undermine confidence in model safety and fairness.\\n4. **Transparency Limitations:** Moderate model explainability and no system cards or impact assessments limit clinical governance oversight.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions (Pre-Deployment)\\n1. **Require AI Governance Policy:** Vendor must provide documented AI ethics policy, bias testing roadmap, and training data documentation before contract execution.\\n2. **Conduct Bias Audit:** Engage third-party to perform bias testing on clinical note generation across demographic groups and clinical specialties.\\n3. **Clarify Data Practices:** Obtain detailed PII handling procedures, sub-processor list, and GDPR DPA confirmation.\\n4. **Clinical Validation:** Request clinical validation studies or pilot results demonstrating accuracy and safety across target specialties.\\n5. **Establish Governance Checkpoints:** Include quarterly AI governance reviews and annual bias audits as contract conditions.\\n\\n### Classification\\n**Acceptable Vendor (C-grade, 70–79 range):** Suitable for deployment with enhanced due diligence and mitigation roadmap closure. Recommend pilot phase with dedicated governance oversight before enterprise-wide rollout.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "DeepScribe AI Medical Scribe", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count or revenue metrics not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Healthcare (primary); applicable to any clinical setting with EHR systems.", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Typical deployment ranges from single-specialty clinics to multi-facility health systems; per vendor, reduces documentation time by up to 50%.", "Primary Use Case": "Automated medical documentation capture and EHR integration for clinical encounters; reduces clinician administrative burden by automating chart note generation from ambient voice recordings.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; integrates directly with electronic health record systems.", "Product Description": "DeepScribe combines AI-powered ambient listening with human quality assurance to automate medical documentation directly within EHR systems. The product captures patient visits via voice and generates structured clinical notes, reducing manual documentation time by up to 50% (corroborated by 3 evidence points: 75% reduced documentation time, 75% time saved, 1.6-minute chart closure). The solution integrates natively with major EHR platforms and includes HIPAA BAA eligibility, SOC 2 Type 2, and ISO 27001 certifications.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth stage product (Series B/C); no formal third-party testing results available."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "DeepScribe (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2017", "Operating Regions": "United States (primary); data residency limited to US only", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not disclosed", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (Growth stage); revenue not disclosed"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified (ambient voice recognition and clinical note generation inferred; specific model architecture not disclosed)", "Model Purpose": "Automated speech-to-text transcription and clinical documentation generation; capabilities include patient encounter capture, structured note generation, and EHR integration.", "Human Oversight": "Human quality assurance component mentioned as part of the product design; specific oversight mechanisms (review workflows, approval gates, audit trails) not detailed.", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy provided; governance framework not specified.", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate transparency; some explainability features present but not fully documented. No information on prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or model decision transparency."}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No formal bias testing approach documented. No evidence of red-team exercises, third-party bias audits, or statistical monitoring for demographic or clinical bias in documentation generation.", "Penetration Testing": "Not specified; no frequency or scope of adversarial security testing disclosed.", "Training Data Documentation": "**No documentation available.** Vendor has not provided training data provenance, composition, or curation methodology. This is a material gap for healthcare PHI handling."}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "No bias audits documented; no frequency or external evaluation process specified.", "AI Ethics Policy": "No documented AI ethics policy provided. Vendor has not disclosed usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical frameworks governing model deployment and clinical decision support boundaries.", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Human quality assurance is mentioned as part of the product; specific admin controls, content filtering, intervention workflows, and escalation procedures not detailed.", "Impact Assessment": "No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided. No evidence of structured impact assessments for clinical safety or fairness."}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger option. Vendor supports both automated and manual rollback of deployments; specific rollback time objectives and testing frequency not specified.", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, tested annually. Vendor maintains a documented incident response plan with annual testing; specific response time targets, escalation procedures, and post-incident review processes not detailed."}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Hosted on cloud infrastructure (specific provider not disclosed); encryption status and key management practices not detailed.", "PII Handling": "Extent of PII handling not fully specified. Product processes Protected Health Information (PHI) as part of clinical documentation; specific controls for PII de-identification, masking, or segregation not documented.", "Data Deletion": "On request and upon service termination; automated deletion timelines not specified.", "Data Retention": "DeepScribe retains customer data for as long as necessary to provide services. Deletion procedures in place upon customer request or service termination; specific retention periods and automated purge schedules not specified.", "Sub-processors": "Infrastructure provider not disclosed; payment processing and authentication vendors not specified.", "Data Collection": "Ambient voice recording via clinical encounter capture; integration with EHR systems for note storage and retrieval. Collection scope and granularity not fully specified.", "Data Types Processed": "Patient visit audio recordings (ambient voice), clinical encounter transcripts, structured clinical notes, and EHR-integrated documentation. Likely includes patient demographics, medical history, and clinical assessments.", "Data Location / Residency": "US only. No multi-region or customer-choice residency options available; this may limit GDPR compliance flexibility for EU customers."}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "- SOC 2 Type 2 ✓", "GDPR Compliance": "Stated as compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed. US-only data residency may create GDPR compliance friction for EU deployments.", "HIPAA Compliance": "BAA eligible; specific BAA terms, covered entity obligations, and breach notification procedures not detailed.", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; vendor has not disclosed engagement with EU AI Act risk classification or compliance roadmap.", "Regulatory Frameworks": "- NIST: Readiness not specified", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology, scope, and auditor identity not disclosed.", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "- Incident Response Plan: Tested annually"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance). This is a standard enterprise SLA; specific exclusions, remedies, and credit terms not detailed.", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified. Vendor has not disclosed release frequency, change approval process, testing procedures, or rollback readiness practices.", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified. Vendor has not disclosed severity-based response time targets or support escalation procedures."}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Key SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not disclosed.", "Critical Vendors": "Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendor not disclosed.", "Vendor Assessment": "Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not specified."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available. Specific log types (authentication, API, data access, configuration changes), retention period, and export format not specified.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available. Specific telemetry scope (e.g., API call volume, error rates, latency, user engagement) not detailed.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted. Vendor has not disclosed model performance benchmarks, safety testing results, or clinical validation studies (even under NDA).", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "No formal testing results available. Vendor has not provided third-party security assessments, penetration test reports, or policy documentation beyond certifications."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** DeepScribe demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, GDPR compliant) and operational reliability (99.9% SLA, tested incident response), positioning it as an acceptable vendor for healthcare deployment. However, significant gaps in AI governance (no documented AI governance policy, no formal bias testing, no training data documentation) and data practices (US-only residency, limited transparency on PII handling) create material risk. The vendor's Growth stage maturity (Series B/C, 51-200 employees) and moderate model transparency further constrain the score. Per the vendor self-attestation formula (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]), the primary driver of the 72 score is elevated Product Risk (estimated ~50/100 due to healthcare PHI handling with incomplete mitigation documentation) and Governance Risk (~45/100 due to missing AI ethics policy, bias audits, and training data transparency), partially offset by strong Operational Risk profile (estimated ~25/100 due to certified SLAs and incident response). **Recommendation: Enhanced due diligence required; require mitigation roadmap closure (AI governance policy, bias testing, training data documentation) as contract condition before production deployment.** ---", "overallScore": 88, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.63, "Governance": 99, "Operational": 66}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   88 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       34.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            4.37  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         1.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (34.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (4.4) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (66.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:24:45.339589+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	88	B	ab8a7327-05c3-4c27-a519-57c1c8ee5c23	\N	\N
5c24452b-2607-4c4e-a07e-97af34c0b0db	86da6c8b-d380-4ab0-9660-d0c12a757c1e	69	69	AI Product Company	\N	Startup (Seed/Series A)	https://www.deepseek.com	DeepSeek builds AI models.	51-200	2023	杭州	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "Chief AI Officer"]	DeepSeek Chat addresses the need for cost-effective AI solutions that match or exceed the performance of established AI systems. It also helps businesses reduce operational costs associated with AI deployment and provides an open-source model that enhances transparency and customization.	\N	DeepSeek's models are open-source, providing full transparency and allowing for greater customization. The company's AI solutions are significantly more cost-effective than competitors, offering high performance at lower operational costs. DeepSeek focuses on Artificial General Intelligence (AGI), positioning itself as a leader in advanced AI research and development.	DeepSeek Chat reduces operational costs by up to 40% compared to traditional AI solutions, while maintaining or exceeding performance benchmarks. Customers report a 30% reduction in manual processing time due to the efficiency of DeepSeek's language models.	\N	\N	Full Transparency (Open weights, explainable)	\N	["None Currently"]	\N	\N	\N	Data retention practices are not explicitly defined, and there's ambiguity about how long user data, such as chat logs, is stored. It is noted that user data may be retained indefinitely and could be used to train models unless explicitly deleted by users.	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	< 95% or No SLA	In development	Manual with documented procedures	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Limited/Partial	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:25:27.154771+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	DeepSeek Chat	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:25:27.157+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## DeepSeek Chat\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 42 (Low)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 15\\n- Data Practices: 25\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 40\\n- Company Maturity: 45\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDeepSeek Chat scores in the Low trust range (42/100) due to significant gaps across governance, compliance, and operational maturity. While the vendor demonstrates transparency through open-source models and cost efficiency, critical deficiencies in security certifications, data retention policies, incident response readiness, and formal AI governance frameworks present material risk for enterprise deployment. The startup stage (founded 2023, 51–200 employees) and absence of independent compliance audits, SLA commitments, and documented bias testing further constrain confidence. Strengths include open-model architecture and basic logging capability; primary gaps are lack of formal certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA), undefined data retention practices, and immature operational controls.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** DeepSeek Chat\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Cost-effective AI conversational and analytical tasks; operational cost reduction; high-performance language model inference\\n- **Target Industry:** Technology, Finance, Healthcare (cost-sensitive segments); enterprises seeking AGI-aligned research partnerships\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (vendor-operated); open-source model weights available for self-hosted deployment\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Vendor-hosted cloud platform; self-hosted via open-source weights\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified; typical deployments range from pilot (single team) to enterprise-wide\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product (vendor founded 2023); limited third-party validation\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor (cost-effective positioning; 40% operational cost reduction claimed vs. competitors)\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; metrics not disclosed\\n- **Product Description:** DeepSeek Chat is an open-source AI language model offering full transparency and high customization capability. The platform delivers performance comparable to or exceeding established competitors while reducing operational costs by up to 40% and manual processing time by 30%. Open-source architecture enables on-premises deployment and model fine-tuning; however, data retention practices remain ambiguous and formal security/compliance certifications are absent.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** DeepSeek (registered in 杭州 [Hangzhou], China)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (model developer and SaaS provider)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2023\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Not specified; Seed/Series A stage inferred from employee count and founding date\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: 杭州 (Hangzhou), China; investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** China (primary); global access via web platform; regional data residency options not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Model (LLM); open-source weights; transformer-based architecture (inferred)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Natural language understanding, generation, reasoning, and code analysis; positioned as AGI-research-aligned\\n- **Model Governance:** Focused on AGI research and development; formal safety framework and staged deployment policy not documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop review, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Full transparency via open weights; model architecture and training approach disclosed; prompt-level explainability and citation mechanisms not specified\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified; release cadence and model versioning practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training corpus composition, sources, and filtering practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools not mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not available; usage policies and safety guidelines not disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit program documented; frequency and external evaluation partners not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No documented admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows; autonomous decision-making scope not defined\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards, model documentation, or release impact assessments not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** In development; formal incident response procedures, escalation paths, and communication protocols not yet mature\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Manual rollback with documented procedures available; automated rollback or canary deployment practices not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Chat logs, user prompts, model outputs; code, documents, and structured data via API (inferred from conversational AI use case)\\n- **PII Handling:** Extent of PII processing not specified; no explicit policy on whether customer data is used for model training; significant ambiguity noted\\n- **Data Collection:** Web chat interface and API; collection scope and opt-out mechanisms not documented\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** **Critical Gap:** Data retention practices are not explicitly defined. User data (chat logs) may be retained indefinitely and could be used for model training unless explicitly deleted by users. No default zero-retention option or automated purge policy documented\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Primary operations in China (Hangzhou); customer choice of data residency not specified; EU/US data residency options not available\\n- **Data Deletion:** User-initiated deletion available; automated deletion on request not specified; deletion confirmation and audit trail not documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider(s) not disclosed; payment processor, authentication provider, and third-party analytics vendors not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently held.** No SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, FedRAMP, HIPAA, HITRUST, or equivalent certifications documented\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit conducted; vendor self-assessment only\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST AI Risk Management Framework: Engagement not specified\\n  - GDPR: Compliance status unclear; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) not available\\n  - CCPA: Compliance status not specified\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness and engagement not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not HIPAA-eligible; BAA not available; healthcare data handling not authorized\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA not available; data residency in China creates compliance friction for EU customers; adequacy determination unclear\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No documented engagement with EU AI Act requirements; high-risk classification likely (general-purpose LLM); compliance roadmap not provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No independent audits conducted; vendor maturity (founded 2023) and startup stage preclude established audit history\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** <95% or no formal SLA; uptime commitment not contractually defined; reliability targets not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response times by severity not documented; support availability (24/7 vs. business hours) not stated\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Release process and frequency not documented; rollback readiness practices not specified; change communication procedures not defined\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider(s), payment processor, and authentication services not disclosed; vendor dependencies not transparent\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified; vendor SLA monitoring and audit practices not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** SLAs from critical infrastructure and service vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope (user counts, query volume, latency, error rates) not detailed; export capability not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; log retention period, export format, and SIEM integration not specified; audit trail completeness not documented\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial; formal security policies, compliance documentation, and testing results not provided; evidence files not uploaded\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial; third-party model evaluation results, safety benchmarks, or adversarial robustness testing not available; NDA-protected results not offered\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Critical Gaps (Must Address Before Enterprise Deployment)\\n\\n1. **Compliance & Certifications (Severity: Critical)**\\n   - No SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or equivalent security certifications\\n   - Not HIPAA-eligible; unsuitable for healthcare PHI handling\\n   - GDPR compliance unclear; DPA not available; China data residency creates legal friction\\n   - Recommendation: Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 audit within 12 months; provide GDPR DPA; clarify EU AI Act compliance roadmap\\n\\n2. **Data Retention & PII Handling (Severity: Critical)**\\n   - Indefinite data retention by default; ambiguity on model training use\\n   - No explicit opt-out or zero-retention policy\\n   - Recommendation: Publish explicit data retention policy; offer customer-controlled deletion and zero-retention options; provide audit trail for data handling\\n\\n3. **Incident Response & Operational Maturity (Severity: High)**\\n   - Incident response plan in development; not yet mature\\n   - No formal SLA commitments; uptime <95% or undefined\\n   - Recommendation: Complete and document incident response procedures; commit to 99.5%+ uptime SLA with penalties; establish 24/7 support escalation\\n\\n4. **AI Governance & Safety Testing (Severity: High)**\\n   - No documented bias testing, red-teaming, or adversarial security evaluation\\n   - Training data composition not disclosed; no impact assessments\\n   - Recommendation: Conduct third-party bias audit; publish training data documentation; establish formal AI safety review board\\n\\n### Moderate Gaps (Address Before Production Deployment)\\n\\n5. **Security Certifications & Vendor Transparency**\\n   - Infrastructure providers and sub-processors not disclosed\\n   - Encryption practices (at rest, in transit) not documented\\n   - Recommendation: Disclose critical vendor dependencies; document encryption standards (AES-256, TLS 1.3); provide vendor SLA summaries\\n\\n6. **Support & Change Management**\\n   - Support SLAs by severity not defined\\n   - Release cadence and rollback procedures not documented\\n   - Recommendation: Define P1/P2/P3 response times; publish release notes and rollback procedures; establish change advisory board\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – PILOT ONLY (Not Recommended for Production)**\\n\\n- **Current State:** DeepSeek Chat is suitable for **low-risk, non-regulated pilot use cases only** (e.g., internal R&D, cost-optimization experiments, non-PHI data analysis)\\n- **Restrictions:** Do not deploy with regulated data (healthcare PHI, financial PII, government classified); do not use in customer-facing production until compliance gaps are closed\\n- **Path to Production:**\\n  1. **Months 1–3:** Vendor completes SOC 2 Type 2 audit; publishes GDPR DPA and data retention policy\\n  2. **Months 4–6:** Vendor conducts third-party bias audit; documents training data and AI safety framework\\n  3. **Months 7–9:** Vendor commits to 99.5%+ uptime SLA; establishes 24/7 support with defined response times\\n  4. **Month 10+:** Re-evaluate for production deployment; consider phased rollout with extended monitoring\\n\\n- **Timeline to Production-Ready:** 10–12 months (subject to vendor remediation)\\n- **Residual Risk (Post-Remediation):** Moderate (50–60/100) due to startup stage and China-based operations; ongoing monitoring required\\n\\n### Alternative Considerations\\n\\n- **For Regulated Industries (Healthcare, Finance, Government):** Recommend established vendors with proven compliance track records (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI) until DeepSeek achieves SOC 2 Type 2 and HIPAA eligibility\\n- **For Cost-Sensitive, Non-Regulated Use Cases:** DeepSeek Chat is a strong candidate; leverage open-source model for on-premises deployment to mitigate data residency concerns\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Analyst Assessment Level:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confidence in Score:** Moderate (limited independent verification; reliance on vendor-provided data and public disclosures)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor (cost-effective positioning; 40% operational cost reduction claimed vs. competitors)", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "DeepSeek Chat", "Customer Base": "Not specified; metrics not disclosed", "Target Industry": "Technology, Finance, Healthcare (cost-sensitive segments); enterprises seeki