training not disclosed", "Data Deletion": "On request; automated deletion procedures not specified", "Data Retention": "Figma deletes customer data upon request and maintains a documented data retention and disposal policy; default retention period not specified", "Sub-processors": "Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication vendors not disclosed", "Data Collection": "API and web interface (Figma platform); specific collection scope not detailed", "Data Types Processed": "Design files, prototypes, code artifacts, team collaboration metadata", "Data Location / Residency": "Not specified; customer choice of data residency not confirmed"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "SOC 2 Type 2, SOC 3, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, FedRAMP—comprehensive security and data protection certifications indicating enterprise-grade compliance maturity", "GDPR Compliance": "Likely supported (ISO 27001, ISO 27701 certifications suggest DPA availability); formal DPA not confirmed", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not specified; BAA eligibility not confirmed (not recommended for healthcare PHI without explicit HIPAA certification)", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified", "Regulatory Frameworks": "- NIST: Implied by FedRAMP certification (requires NIST SP 800-53 compliance)", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Third-party audits conducted (implied by SOC 2 Type 2 and FedRAMP certifications); specific audit methodology and frequency not detailed", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Audit frequency not specified; last audit date and findings not provided; continuous audits mentioned in data retention policy"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)—enterprise-grade availability commitment", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure or service vendors not provided", "Critical Vendors": "Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and other critical sub-processors not disclosed", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency and methodology of vendor risk assessments not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available—supports audit trail and compliance investigations; export format and retention not specified", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available—enables monitoring of product usage and performance; detailed telemetry scope not specified", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not specified; no indication of additional safety testing documentation available under NDA", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Yes, basic test results available—indicates some testing rigor; detailed test plans, coverage, and results not provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Figma AI demonstrates solid enterprise-grade security and compliance posture, backed by mature certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP) and a 10+ year company history with 1,001–5,000 employees. However, the overall Trust Score of 72 reflects significant gaps in AI governance transparency—the vendor provides minimal documentation on AI ethics policies, bias testing, human oversight mechanisms, and training data provenance (relying on third-party models with unknown data sources). Operations are reliable (99.9% SLA, annual incident testing, automated rollback), but the lack of detailed AI safety frameworks and explainability documentation creates residual product risk. The vendor is acceptable for design-to-code automation use cases with standard controls, but would require enhanced AI governance commitments and third-party AI safety audits before deployment in high-stakes or regulated environments (e.g., healthcare, financial services). ---", "overallScore": 88, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 97.13, "Governance": 99, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   88 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            2.87  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         1.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (2.9) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:29:37.042918+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	88	B	9873f8e4-52ad-466c-9afa-e75c77bce458	\N	\N
af196403-86e3-4ac6-91c3-469e92f811dc	a546ddff-2caa-45a8-95c0-6f11858ea4f7	76	76	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Technology & Software, Professional Services, Healthcare, Finance & Banking, Retail & E-commerce": ["Technology & Software, Professional Services, Healthcare, Finance & Banking, Retail & E-commerce"]}	Growth (Series B/C)	https://www.fireflies.ai	Fireflies.ai is an AI-powered meeting assistant that automates note-taking, transcription, and summarization of conversations across various meeting platforms. It enhances productivity by providing searchable transcripts, AI-generated summaries, and actionable insights from meetings.	51-200	2016	Miami, FL, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "Line of Business Leader", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Fireflies.ai addresses the time-consuming process of manual note-taking and meeting documentation, which can lead to missed details and inefficiencies. It also solves the challenge of extracting actionable insights from meetings and integrating them into workflows, such as updating CRMs or project management tools.	\N	Fireflies.ai offers enterprise-grade security with SOC 2 Type II, GDPR, and HIPAA compliance, appealing to regulated sectors. It also provides extensive integration options with over 100 business applications and a hybrid approach with 'Self-Hosted Runners' for organizations requiring deployments within their own network boundaries.	Users report significant time savings on documentation and faster insight analysis. The tool is seen as cost-effective compared to more expensive enterprise solutions.	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "GDPR Compliant", "HIPAA BAA"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region", "Hybrid (Cloud + On-prem)"]	Fireflies.ai maintains a strict zero-day retention policy with its AI vendors, meaning customer data is not stored or used for AI training by these third parties. For personal information associated with an account, data is stored as long as the account remains active. Upon account closure, personal information is deleted, though legal obligations may require some data retention. Enterprise clients have options for custom data retention policies.	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes	Yes	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:30:20.423635+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Fireflies.ai	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:30:20.428+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Fireflies.ai\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 75\\n- Compliance: 80\\n- Data Practices: 78\\n- AI Governance: 55\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 65\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nFireflies.ai demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type II, GDPR, HIPAA BAA) and strong data practices with zero-day retention policies and customer choice on residency, positioning it as acceptable for regulated environments. However, the vendor exhibits moderate-to-low maturity in AI governance (limited documented safety frameworks, bias testing, and explainability), combined with growth-stage company risk and an untested incident response plan, which constrains the overall trust score. The 72 score reflects a vendor suitable for standard enterprise deployments with enhanced due diligence on AI safety controls and operational resilience before handling high-risk use cases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Fireflies.ai\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automated meeting transcription, note-taking, summarization, and actionable insight extraction for enterprise teams\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-sector); particularly regulated sectors (healthcare, financial services) given HIPAA and GDPR compliance\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (Cloud-hosted) with hybrid option (Self-Hosted Runners)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud (vendor-managed) or hybrid (customer on-premises with cloud integration)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified; typical deployment size not stated\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage (Series B/C); basic test results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (metrics not provided)\\n- **Product Description:** Fireflies.ai is an AI-powered meeting assistant that automates transcription, note-taking, and summarization across multiple meeting platforms. It integrates with over 100 business applications and offers enterprise-grade security with SOC 2 Type II, GDPR, and HIPAA BAA compliance. The platform supports hybrid deployment via Self-Hosted Runners for organizations requiring on-premises data handling.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Fireflies.ai (legal entity not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth stage); revenue not specified\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Miami, FL, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; global reach implied by multi-platform support and GDPR compliance\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Third-party models (specific model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Speech-to-text transcription, natural language summarization, insight extraction, and meeting analytics\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no mention of advisory controls, monitoring alerts, or audit trails for AI decisions\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted, but specifics not detailed); no mention of prompt-level control or citation mechanisms\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data provenance unknown and not documented\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type of adversarial security testing documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluation process mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level and testing cadence unknown\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Meeting audio/video, transcripts, participant communications, extracted summaries and insights\\n- **PII Handling:** Customer data not used for AI training (zero-day retention policy with third-party AI vendors); personal account information retained during account lifecycle\\n- **Data Collection:** API and meeting platform integrations (100+ applications); collection scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud infrastructure (vendor-managed) or on-premises (hybrid Self-Hosted Runners); encryption method not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Zero-day retention with third-party AI vendors; account-linked personal data retained while account active; custom retention policies available for enterprise clients; legal hold exceptions noted\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; hybrid cloud + on-premises option available\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automatic deletion upon account closure (subject to legal obligations); on-request deletion not explicitly stated\\n- **Sub-processors:** Third-party AI vendors (identity not specified); infrastructure, meeting platform integrations, and business application connectors (100+ integrations); payment and authentication sub-processors not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type II, GDPR Compliant, HIPAA BAA eligible\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope unknown\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR (compliant), HIPAA (BAA available); NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not mentioned\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; eligible for healthcare use cases\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation mentioned\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type II audit frequency and most recent audit date unknown; findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; response time targets by severity level not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness, and change communication practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Third-party AI vendors (identity not disclosed); meeting platform providers (Zoom, Teams, Google Meet, etc.); 100+ business application integrations\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency and rigor of vendor risk assessments unknown\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; SLAs from critical infrastructure and AI vendors not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, available; export format and retention period not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation (AI governance, incident response, change management) not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; availability under NDA not mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Strengths\\n\\n1. **Compliance Posture:** SOC 2 Type II, GDPR, and HIPAA BAA certifications demonstrate commitment to regulated industry standards.\\n2. **Data Privacy:** Zero-day retention policy with third-party AI vendors and customer choice on data residency reduce data misuse risk.\\n3. **Deployment Flexibility:** Hybrid Self-Hosted Runners option enables organizations to maintain data within their own infrastructure.\\n4. **Integration Breadth:** 100+ business application integrations support seamless workflow adoption.\\n5. **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA provides acceptable availability for non-critical meeting documentation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Gaps & Risks\\n\\n1. **AI Governance Deficiency:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias testing, or safety framework; reliance on undisclosed third-party models creates transparency and accountability gaps.\\n2. **Untested Incident Response:** Documented but not tested incident response plan; maturity and effectiveness unknown.\\n3. **Limited Explainability:** Moderate transparency features lack specifics on prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or decision auditability.\\n4. **Growth-Stage Operational Risk:** Series B/C maturity with 51–200 employees presents scaling and support capacity concerns for large enterprise deployments.\\n5. **Incomplete Vendor Management:** Third-party AI vendor identity and SLAs not disclosed; vendor assessment practices not documented.\\n6. **Missing Change Management Documentation:** Release cadence, rollback procedures, and change communication practices not specified.\\n7. **Support SLA Gaps:** No documented response time targets by severity level; support maturity unknown.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recommended Actions for Procurement\\n\\n1. **Require AI Governance Documentation:** Request formal AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, and model governance framework before contract execution.\\n2. **Validate Incident Response:** Conduct tabletop exercise or audit of incident response plan to verify maturity and testing cadence.\\n3. **Clarify Third-Party Model Provenance:** Obtain detailed documentation on third-party AI vendors, model training data, and safety certifications.\\n4. **Negotiate Support SLAs:** Define P1/P2/P3 response time targets and escalation procedures aligned with business criticality.\\n5. **Establish Change Management Expectations:** Document release cadence, rollback procedures, and change notification requirements in contract.\\n6. **Pilot with Non-Critical Data:** Deploy in non-regulated or non-sensitive use case first to validate operational maturity before handling PHI or financial data.\\n7. **Require Audit Log Export Capability:** Confirm SIEM-compatible audit log export format and retention for compliance and forensics.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Assessment Classification\\n\\n**Grade: C (Acceptable Vendor)**\\n\\nFireflies.ai is suitable for standard enterprise meeting documentation use cases in regulated industries, supported by solid compliance certifications and strong data privacy practices. However, the vendor requires enhanced due diligence on AI safety, governance, and operational resilience before deployment in high-risk or mission-critical workflows. A conditional approval with mandatory gap remediation (AI governance documentation, incident response validation, support SLA definition) is recommended.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Fireflies.ai", "Cu