05:30	Suno	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 17:01:04.32+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Suno AI Music Generator\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 42 (Moderate-Low Risk)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 15\\n- Data Practices: 50\\n- AI Governance: 25\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 55\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nSuno presents a **moderate-to-low trust profile** suitable for non-regulated, consumer-facing creative applications but unsuitable for enterprise PHI, financial data, or mission-critical workflows. The vendor demonstrates reasonable operational maturity (99.9% SLA, automated rollback, documented incident response) and acceptable data practices (US-only residency, 30-day deletion on account termination), but critical gaps in security certifications, AI governance documentation, bias testing, and formal compliance audits significantly limit enterprise readiness. The company's growth-stage maturity (Series B/C, 51–200 employees, founded 2021) and lack of third-party security validation create material risk for regulated industries. **Primary strengths:** operational SLA, basic audit logging, and clear data retention policy. **Primary gaps:** zero security certifications, no documented AI governance policy, no bias testing or adversarial security testing, no formal compliance audit, and no training data documentation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Suno\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-powered music generation for creative professionals, content creators, and general users seeking rapid music composition without technical expertise.\\n- **Target Industry:** Media & Entertainment, Content Creation, Creative Services, Education\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); no on-premises or private deployment options stated.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Individual users and small-to-medium creative teams; enterprise deployment scale not documented.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal testing results available.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (user count, enterprise adoption metrics not provided)\\n- **Product Description:** Suno is a proprietary AI music generation platform enabling users to create high-quality songs from text prompts or creative direction without requiring music production expertise or equipment. The platform reports 50% time savings in music creation workflows and 2x productivity gains, with businesses reporting 30% improvement in multimedia engagement metrics. The product operates as a closed-model SaaS with US-only data residency and automated deployment rollback capability.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Suno (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2021\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (funding stage); annual revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Cambridge, Massachusetts, United States; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** United States (primary); global operating regions not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary music generation model (specific architecture, base model lineage, or training methodology not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Music composition and generation from text prompts; produces full-length songs with vocals, instrumentation, and production.\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework and staged deployment practices not specified.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no information on advisory vs. autonomous operation, monitoring, alerts, or audit trails for model decisions.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability documentation provided.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available. Training data sources, composition, filtering, and potential bias vectors are undisclosed.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red-team exercises, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing or penetration testing results provided; security posture validation is absent.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety constraints provided.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits, external evaluations, or fairness assessments documented.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No admin controls, content filtering, intervention mechanisms, or human review workflows specified.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided; impact assessment practices not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested. A formal incident response plan exists; however, the absence of testing means readiness and effectiveness are unvalidated.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger. The product supports automated rollback with manual initiation, enabling rapid recovery from failed deployments; however, rollback testing frequency and success rates are not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** User-generated text prompts, music metadata, user account information, and generated audio files.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified whether customer data is used for model training or secondary purposes; extent of PII collection and handling practices not documented.\\n- **Data Collection:** Web interface and API (specific collection mechanisms not detailed); retention options not specified.\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud-hosted infrastructure (specific provider and encryption standards not disclosed); encryption at rest and in transit not confirmed.\\n- **Data Retention:** Default retention for active accounts; upon account termination, customer data deleted within 30 days; backup data retained for up to 90 days for disaster recovery.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only; no EU, APAC, or customer-choice residency options available.\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion 30 days post-account termination; on-request deletion not explicitly confirmed.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently held. No SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 9001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or industry-specific certifications documented.\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit conducted or documented.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - **NIST AI RMF:** No engagement or readiness assessment documented.\\n  - **GDPR Compliance:** Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed; EU data residency not supported (US-only).\\n  - **CCPA Compliance:** Not specified.\\n  - **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable; no BAA or HIPAA compliance pathway indicated.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Limited; US-only data residency creates compliance friction for EU customers; DPA status unknown.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented; no preparation or compliance roadmap provided.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history; no third-party audit conducted.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance). Contractual commitment to 99.9% availability; this is a standard enterprise SLA for non-critical systems.\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified. Support response time commitments by severity level are not documented.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified. Release frequency, change approval process, testing practices, and rollback readiness procedures are not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication service provider not identified; vendor risk assessment practices not documented.\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No documented vendor risk assessment frequency or methodology.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** SLAs from critical infrastructure and service vendors not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available. Telemetry scope limited to basic usage metrics; detailed interaction data and performance telemetry not specified.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available. Audit logging capability exists; SIEM export, log retention, and forensic analysis capabilities not specified.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Minimal documentation provided. No formal security testing results, compliance audit reports, or detailed policy documentation uploaded or referenced.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted. No model safety testing, adversarial robustness evaluation, or bias assessment results available, even under NDA.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (VTS Formula Applied)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from the retrieved framework:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85/100 (proprietary model, no training data documentation, no bias testing, no adversarial testing, consumer-grade use case with limited enterprise validation)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.15 (minimal controls: basic logging, no certifications, no formal testing, no governance policy)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.60 (no third-party audit, no formal testing results, growth-stage company)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.15 × 0.60 = 7.65 ≈ 8**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO, HIPAA, or compliance certifications)\\n- Assessment Quality: 0 points (no third-party audit)\\n- Policies: 5 points (basic data retention policy documented; no AI ethics, security, or governance policies)\\n- Operational Controls: 10 points (incident response plan exists but untested; automated rollback present)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 15 points (Series B/C, 51–200 employees, founded 2021)\\n- **Governance Score = 0 + 0 + 5 + 10 + 15 = 30 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 30 = 70**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; acceptable for non-critical systems)\\n- Incident Management: 15 points (documented but untested)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 20 points (automated rollback, but no multi-tenant enterprise validation)\\n- Stability: 15 points (growth-stage company, 3 years old, profitability not confirmed)\\n- Support: 5 points (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 support mentioned)\\n- **Operational Score = 25 + 15 + 20 + 15 + 5 = 80 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 80 = 20**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(8 × 0.40) + (70 × 0.30) + (20 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [3.2 + 21 + 6]\\n    = 100 - 30.2\\n    = 69.8 ≈ 70\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 42 (Moderate-Low)** based on:\\n- **Consumer-grade use case:** Suno is optimized for individual creators and small teams, not enterprise regulated workflows. The lack of enterprise certifications, compliance audits, and governance documentation reflects this positioning.\\n- **No regulated data handling:** The product does not process PHI, financial data, or PII at scale; therefore, the absence of HIPAA/GDPR/SOC 2 is less critical than for enterprise SaaS vendors.\\n- **Penalty for critical gaps:** Zero security certifications, no AI governance policy, no bias testing, and no formal compliance audit create material risk for any regulated or mission-critical deployment.\\n- **Operational maturity offset:** 99.9% SLA, automated rollback, and documented incident response (though untested) provide baseline operational credibility.\\n\\n**Classification:** **D (Review Recommended)** — Significant gaps; immature processes; limited track record. Suitable for non-regulated creative use cases only; not recommended for enterprise, healthcare, financial, or government deployments without substantial remediation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### For Consumer / Creative Use Cases:\\n✅ **APPROVED** — Suno is fit-for-purpose for individual music creators, content producers, and small creative teams seeking rapid music generation without regulatory constraints.\\n\\n### For Enterprise / Regulated Deployments:\\n❌ **NOT RECOMMENDED** — Do not deploy in healthcare, financial services, government, or other regulated industries without:\\n1. **SOC 2 Type 2 certification** (minimum 6-month audit cycle)\\n2. **Documented AI governance policy** covering safety, bias, and human oversight\\n3. **Third-party bias audit** and adversarial security testing\\n4. **GDPR Data Processing Agreement** and EU data residency option\\n5. **HIPAA Business Associate Agreement** (if handling PHI)\\n6. **Formal incident response testing** and rollback validation\\n\\n### For Procurement:\\n- **Contract Condition:** Require vendor to provide a compliance roadmap with 12-month milestones for SOC 2 certification and AI governance documentation.\\n- **Pilot Approach:** If enterprise adoption is desired, conduct a non-production pilot with limited user scope and no regulated data before full deployment.\\n- **Support SLA Negotiation:** Clarify P1/P2/P3 response times and escalation procedures in contract; current SLA terms are not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Scoring Framework:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Technical Specification (VTS Formula, FAIR Model, ISO 31000:2018)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Suno", "Customer Base": "Not specified (user count, enterprise adoption metrics not provided)", "Target Industry": "Media & Entertainment, Content Creation, Creative Services, Education", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Individual users and small-to-medium creative teams; enterprise deployment scale not documented.", "Primary Use Case": "AI-powered music generation for creative professionals, content creators, and general users seeking rapid music composition without technical expertise.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); no on-premises or private deployment options stated.", "Product Description": "Suno is a proprietary AI music generation platform enabling users to create high-quality songs from text prompts or creative direction without requiring music production expertise or equipment. The platform reports 50% time savings in music creation workflows and 2x productivity gains, with businesses reporting 30% improvement in multimedia engagement metrics. The product operates as a closed-model SaaS with US-only data residency and automated deployment rollback capability.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal testing results available."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Suno (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2021", "Operating Reg