ial documentation available	99.95% (4.4 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, comprehensive analytics	Yes, comprehensive	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 17:03:09.063364+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Windsurf	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 17:03:09.071+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Windsurf (Codeium)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 72\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 78\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 68\\n- Company Maturity: 35\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nWindsurf demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA) and strong data practices with zero-data retention defaults and flexible deployment options, positioning it well for regulated environments. However, the vendor's startup maturity (founded 2026, seed/series A stage, ~10 employees) and significant gaps in AI governance documentation, bias testing, and adversarial security testing create material risk. The 99.95% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability provide operational confidence, but incomplete incident response testing and limited transparency on AI model governance substantially reduce overall trustworthiness. This vendor is acceptable for non-critical, non-PHI use cases with enhanced due diligence; healthcare and financial services deployments require mandatory gap closure on AI safety and governance before production.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Windsurf\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-assisted code generation, developer productivity automation, secret detection in regulated environments\\n- **Target Industry:** Software development; enterprises in regulated sectors (healthcare, financial services, government)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (SaaS), Hybrid (Cloud + On-prem), On-premise\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Multi-deployment: SaaS cloud, hybrid, and fully on-premise options available\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise (typical customer deployment not specified; inferred from compliance posture)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Basic test results available; product stage not specified\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified; ROI data corroborated by 1 evidence point\\n- **Product Description:** Windsurf is an AI-assisted code generation and developer productivity platform designed for regulated environments. It emphasizes zero-data retention for paid seats, real-time secret detection (via GitGuardian integration), and flexible deployment (cloud, hybrid, on-prem) to meet strict data residency and compliance requirements. The platform reports 30–50% reduction in manual coding time and 90% reduction in security incidents through automation and secret detection.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Not specified (operating as Windsurf)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (Startup)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2026\\n- **Employees:** ~10 (stated as \\"01-Oct\\"; interpreted as October 1st headcount or ~10 FTE)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (stage stated; revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Mountain View, CA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to be US-based with potential global reach via cloud/hybrid deployment\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (proprietary/closed model)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Code generation, code completion, secret detection, developer assistance\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no advisory, monitoring, or alert mechanisms documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data provenance and composition not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type of adversarial security testing documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no frequency or external evaluations documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not documented; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms specified\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not documented; no system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level unclear\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Source code, developer communications, API interactions; secret/credential detection\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly stated; inferred that code may contain PII; no documented policy on PII extraction or handling\\n- **Data Collection:** API and IDE integration (Windsurf interface); retention options configurable by customer\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Defaults to zero-data retention for all paid seats; no data stored beyond immediate session unless customer explicitly configures otherwise\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region, on-premise deployment available, hybrid (cloud + on-prem) supported\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion on session end (default); on-request deletion available\\n- **Sub-processors:** GitGuardian (secret detection); other infrastructure providers not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** HIPAA (BAA eligible); GDPR and CCPA compliance not explicitly stated; EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available; vendor eligible for healthcare PHI handling\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not explicitly stated; DPA availability not documented\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented; no engagement or preparation status provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit frequency and most recent audit date not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback/readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** GitGuardian (secret detection); infrastructure provider(s) not specified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** GitGuardian SLA not specified; other critical vendor SLAs not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; policy documentation incomplete (AI governance, bias testing, adversarial security testing not provided)\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no indication of NDA-protected testing results\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (VTS Formula)\\n\\nApplied **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from vector database (Assessment Type 1):\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85/100 (proprietary model, no bias testing, no adversarial security testing, partial training data documentation, code generation in regulated environments)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.65 (zero-data retention, secret detection, SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, but no AI governance or safety framework)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.70 (basic test results available, but no third-party AI safety audit; startup stage reduces confidence)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × 0.65 × 0.70 = 38.6 ≈ 39**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 20/50 (SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA present; no ISO 27001, no AI-specific certifications)\\n- Assessment Quality: 8/25 (basic test results; no third-party AI safety audit; audit frequency not specified)\\n- Policies: 15/45 (zero-data retention policy documented; no AI ethics policy, no incident response testing, no bias audit policy)\\n- Operational Controls: 12/45 (automated rollback; no human oversight, no continuous monitoring, no version control documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 0/15 (founded 2026, ~10 employees; startup stage, no maturity bonus)\\n- **Governance Score = 20 + 8 + 15 + 12 + 0 = 55/100 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 - 55 = 45**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 25/33 (99.95% uptime SLA documented; no support SLAs by severity)\\n- Incident Management: 12/30 (incident response plan documented but not tested; no automation or testing evidence)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 18/30 (hybrid and on-prem options available; startup stage limits enterprise maturity)\\n- Stability: 5/22 (founded 2026, seed/series A; limited track record, profitability not stated)\\n- Support: 0/20 (no support SLAs or dedicated support documented)\\n- **Operational Score = 25 + 12 + 18 + 5 + 0 = 60/100**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 - 60 = 40**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(39 × 0.40) + (45 × 0.30) + (40 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [15.6 + 13.5 + 12.0]\\n    = 100 - 41.1\\n    = 58.9 ≈ 59\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 62** based on strong data practices (zero-data retention, flexible residency) and solid compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA), which partially offset AI governance and startup maturity gaps.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CLASSIFICATION & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n**Trust Score Grade:** D (60–69 range) — **Review Recommended**\\n\\n**Vendor Profile:** Startup with strong compliance credentials but significant AI governance and maturity gaps; acceptable for non-critical, non-PHI use cases with enhanced due diligence.\\n\\n**Recommended Action:** \\n- **Non-PHI, Non-Critical Use Cases:** Standard procurement process with vendor questionnaire on AI safety and governance\\n- **PHI / Healthcare Use Cases:** Extensive validation required; mandate AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, and adversarial security testing before contract execution\\n- **Financial Services / Government:** Enhanced due diligence; require third-party AI safety audit and incident response testing before pilot\\n- **Production Deployment:** Pilot phase mandatory; require 90-day monitoring period with rollback capability before full rollout\\n\\n**Critical Gaps Requiring Closure:**\\n1. **AI Governance:** Document AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, and human oversight mechanisms\\n2. **Safety Testing:** Conduct third-party bias audit and adversarial security testing; document results\\n3. **Incident Response:** Test incident response plan annually; document findings and remediation\\n4. **Support SLAs:** Define P1/P2/P3 response targets; document escalation procedures\\n5. **Vendor Stability:** Provide evidence of funding runway, customer retention, and path to profitability\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SUMMARY ASSESSMENT\\n\\n**Strengths:**\\n- Zero-data retention default for paid seats; strong data privacy posture\\n- Flexible deployment (cloud, hybrid, on-prem) meets strict residency requirements\\n- SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA certifications demonstrate compliance commitment\\n- 99.95% uptime SLA and automated rollback provide operational confidence\\n- Real-time secret detection (GitGuardian integration) reduces security incident risk\\n\\n**Weaknesses:**\\n- Startup maturity (founded 2026, ~10 employees) creates sustainability and support risk\\n- No documented AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, or adversarial security testing\\n- Incident response plan not tested; maturity unclear\\n- Proprietary/closed model with partial training data documentation limits transparency\\n- No support SLAs or dedicated support documented\\n- No GDPR DPA or EU AI Act readiness stated\\n\\n**Risk Profile:** Moderate (62/100). Acceptable for non-critical, non-PHI use cases with standard controls. Healthcare, financial services, and government deployments require mandatory gap closure on AI safety, governance, and incident response testing before production.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Windsurf", "Customer Base": "Not specified; ROI data corroborated by 1 evidence point", "Target Industry": "Software development; enterprises in regulated sectors (healthcare, financial services, government)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (SaaS), Hybrid (Cloud + On-prem), On-premise", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise (typical customer deployment not specified; inferred from compliance posture)", "Primary Use Case": "AI-assisted code generation, developer productivity automation, secret detection in regulated environments", "Hosted / Deployed": "Multi-deployment: SaaS cloud, hybrid, and fully on-premise options available", "Product Description": "Windsurf is an AI-assisted code generation and developer productivity platform designed for regulated environments. It emphasizes zero-data retention for paid seats, real-time secret detection (via GitGuardian integration), and flexible deployment (cloud, hybrid, on-prem) to meet strict data residency and compliance requirements. The platform reports 30–50% reduction in manual coding time and 90% reduction in security incidents through automation and secret detection.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Basic test results available; product stage not specified"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "~10 (stated as \\"01-Oct\\"; interpreted as October 1st headcount or ~10 FTE)", "Legal Name": "Not specified (operating as Windsurf)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company (Startup)", "Year Founded": "2026", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; inferred to be US-based with potential global reach via cloud/hybrid deployment", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Mountain View, CA, USA; investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Seed/Series A (stage stated; revenue not disclosed)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified (proprietary/closed model)", "Model Purpose": "Code generation, code completion, secret detection, developer assistance", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no advisory, monitoring, or alert mechanisms documented", "Model Governance": "Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework specified", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability documentation provided"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Not specified; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented", "Penetration Testing": "Not specified; no frequency or type of adversarial security testing documented", "Training Data Documentation": "Partial documentation available; full training data provenance and composition not disclosed"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Not specified; no frequency or external evaluations documented", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines provided", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not documented; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms specified", "Impact Assessment": "Not documented; no system cards or release documentation provided"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger; enables rapid recovery from failed deployments", "Incident Response Plan": "Documented but not tested; maturity level unclear"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented", "PII Handling": "Not explicitly stated; inferred that code may contain PII; no documented policy on PII extraction or handling", "Data Deletion": "Automated deletion on session end (default); on-request deletion available", "Data Retention": "Defaults to zero-data retention for all paid seats; no data stored beyond immediate session unless customer explicitly configures otherwise", "Sub-processors": "GitGuardian (secret detection); other infrastructure providers not specified", "Data Collection": "API and IDE integration (Windsurf interface); retention options configurable by customer", "Data Types Processed": "Source code, developer communications, API interactions; secret/credential detection", "Data Location / Residency": "Customer choice of region, on-premise deployment available, hybrid (cloud + on-prem) supported"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA", "GDPR Compliance": "Not explicitly stated; DPA availability not documented", "HIPAA Compliance": "BAA available; vendor eligible for healthcare PHI handling", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not documented; no engagement or preparation status provided", "Regulatory Frameworks": "HIPAA (BAA eligible); GDPR and CCPA compliance not explicitly stated; EU AI Act readiness not documented", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified; audit frequency and most recent audit date not provided"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime allowance)", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback/readiness practices not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; support response targets by severity not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "GitGuardian SLA not specified; other critical vendor SLAs not documented", "Critical Vendors": "GitGuardian (secret detection); infrastructure provider(s) not specified", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Production Deployment": "Pilot phase mandatory; require 90-day monitoring period with rollback capability before full rollout", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, comprehensive audit logs available", "PHI / Healthcare Use Cases": "Extensive validation required; mandate AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, and adversarial security testing before contract execution", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, comprehensive analytics available", "Financial Services / Government": "Enhanced due diligence; require third-party AI safety audit and incident response testing before pilot", "Non-PHI, Non-Critical Use Cases": "Standard procurement process with vendor questionnaire on AI safety and governance", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not specified; no indication of NDA-protected testing results", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Basic test results available; policy documentation incomplete (AI governance, bias testing, adversarial security testing not provided)"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "C", "label": "Acceptable Vendor", "summary": "** Windsurf demonstrates solid compliance credentials (SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA) and strong data practices with zero-data retention defaults and flexible deployment options, positioning it well for regulated environments. However, the vendor's startup maturity (founded 2026, seed/series A stage, ~10 employees) and significant gaps in AI governance documentation, bias testing, and adversarial security testing create material risk. The 99.95% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability provide operational confidence, but incomplete incident response testing and limited transparency on AI model governance substantially reduce overall trustworthiness. This vendor is acceptable for non-critical, non-PHI use cases with enhanced due diligence; healthcare and financial services deployments require mandatory gap closure on AI safety and governance before production. ---", "overallScore": 77, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 97.07, "Governance": 74, "Operational": 52}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   77 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         C - Acceptable Vendor\\n  Next step:     Enhanced due diligence; require mitigation roadmap\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       48.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        26.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            2.93  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (48.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (26.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (52.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Raise Governance (74.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 17:03:09.063364+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	77	C	74a2b0d7-17ab-4147-b832-434c23ff3ee0	\N	\N
a89a2883-7225-46d1-8a2a-1024ed0358ec	f602c575-1952-4445-81b8-8de8d588979d	121	121	AI Product Company	\N	Growth (Series B/C)	https://writer.com/	Writer is a full-stack generative AI platform for enterprises, enabling businesses to integrate AI into their workflows securely. The platform allows teams to build, activate, and supervise AI agents grounded in company data, powered by Writer's enterprise-grade LLMs.	1,001-5,000	2020	San Francisco, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "Chief AI Officer"]	Writer addresses the need for enterprises to integrate AI securely into their workflows, ensuring compliance with privacy and security standards. It also solves the challenge of building and supervising AI agents grounded in company data, enabling businesses to leverage AI-first workflows effectively.	\N	WRITER nailed it: agentic AI that actually works at scale, Knowledge Graphs that unlock real value, UX that users love, and a customer success model that ensures impact. This is what differentiation looks like.	Vizient uses WRITER to accelerate the production of high-quality, personalized, and compliant healthcare assets, achieving 4x ROI within one year. [Corroborated by 16 evidence point(s): Time Savings: 60-80%; Hours Repurposed: 1000s; User Satisfaction: High scores; Productivity Increase: 20%; Time Saved: 1 work day]	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "ISO 27001", "ISO 27701", "ISO 42001 (AI Management)", "HIPAA BAA", "PCI DSS"]	\N	\N	\N	WRITER takes a zero data retention approach, storing data for only as long as is needed for you to build with our platform.	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	99.99% (52 min/year downtime)	Yes, tested annually	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, comprehensive	Limited/Partial	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 17:04:38.39962+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Writer	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 17:04:38.409+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n**Writer – Enterprise Generative AI Platform**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score: 72** (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 82\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 78\\n- AI Governance: 58\\n- Operations: 80\\n- Company Maturity: 68\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nWriter demonstrates solid enterprise-grade security and compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001/27701, HIPAA BAA, PCI DSS) with strong operational reliability (99.99% uptime SLA, tested incident response). However, the vendor exhibits meaningful gaps in AI governance transparency—notably absent documentation of training data provenance, bias testing methodology, and formal AI ethics policies—which constrains the overall score despite strong operational and compliance credentials. The company's Growth stage (Series B/C) and moderate employee count (1,001–5,000) position it as a credible but not yet market-leading vendor; residual risk centers on AI safety maturity and governance documentation rather than operational or security concerns.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Writer\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise AI workflow integration; building, activating, and supervising AI agents grounded in company data\\n- **Target Industry:** Healthcare (corroborated case: Vizient), financial services, and general enterprise\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; on-premises deployment options not specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise multi-tenant; typical customer deployment scale not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C); limited public testing results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Vizient (healthcare) documented as reference customer; total customer count not specified\\n- **Product Description:** Writer is a full-stack generative AI platform enabling enterprises to build and supervise AI agents grounded in proprietary company data. The platform emphasizes secure workflow integration, compliance-ready deployment (HIPAA BAA, SOC 2 Type 2), and knowledge graph capabilities to unlock structured data value. Unique positioning centers on agentic AI scalability, user experience, and customer success model alignment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Writer (legal entity name not specified; operating as \\"Writer\\")\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage funding); annual revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not listed\\n- **Operating Regions:** United States (primary); international regions not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/closed LLM (enterprise-grade); knowledge graph technology\\n- **Model Purpose:** Agentic AI for workflow automation; document generation; data analysis; compliance-aware content production\\n- **Model Governance:** Not formally documented; governance framework not specified in attestation\\n- **Human Oversight:** Supervision and control capabilities implied (\\"supervise AI agents\\"); specific admin controls, content filtering, and intervention workflows not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Model transparency: Proprietary/Closed; prompt-level explainability and citation mechanisms not specified\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available** — a material gap; training data provenance, composition, and filtering practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no evidence of red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or statistical monitoring tools\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not specified; formal ethics framework not evident in attestation\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluation program documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Supervision capabilities referenced (\\"supervise AI agents\\"); specific admin controls, content filtering, and intervention mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation not specified; impact assessment process not evident\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually — demonstrates mature incident management discipline\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option — supports rapid incident recovery and deployment safety\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Documents, enterprise data (structured and unstructured); specific data categories not enumerated\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and customer data usage for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface; specific collection mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed\\n- **Data Retention:** **Zero data retention approach** — data stored only as long as needed for platform operation; this is a strong privacy-protective practice\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Geographic residency options not specified; default storage location not disclosed\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion capability implied by zero-retention policy; automated deletion mechanics not detailed\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - ISO 27001 ✓\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Management) ✓\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management) ✓\\n  - HIPAA BAA ✓\\n  - PCI DSS ✓\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (e.g., Big 4 firm, frequency, scope) not disclosed\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST AI Risk Management Framework: Readiness not specified\\n  - GDPR: DPA availability not confirmed\\n  - CCPA: Compliance not explicitly stated\\n  - EU AI Act: Readiness not specified\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA available ✓\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability not specified; GDPR compliance posture not detailed\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** \\n  - Audit frequency not specified\\n  - Last audit date not disclosed\\n  - Audit findings not available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime) — enterprise-grade reliability commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not disclosed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key vendor SLAs not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available — limited scope\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available — supports compliance and forensic investigation\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited evidence provided; formal policy documentation and testing results not comprehensively disclosed\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial availability — suggests testing has occurred but results are not broadly accessible\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Compliance & Security Certifications:** Comprehensive portfolio (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001/27701, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA, PCI DSS) demonstrates enterprise-ready security posture.\\n2. **Data Privacy:** Zero-retention policy is a strong privacy-protective practice; aligns with privacy-by-design principles.\\n3. **Operational Reliability:** 99.99% uptime SLA and tested incident response plan indicate mature operations.\\n4. **Audit Logs & Telemetry:** Comprehensive audit logs and basic interaction metrics support compliance and monitoring.\\n\\n### Material Gaps\\n1. **AI Governance Documentation:** No formal AI ethics policy, training data documentation, or bias testing methodology disclosed—a critical gap for regulated industries (healthcare, finance).\\n2. **Bias & Safety Testing:** No evidence of red-team audits, third-party bias evaluations, or adversarial testing; bias detection approach not specified.\\n3. **Support SLAs:** Response time commitments by severity not disclosed; limits buyer confidence in support responsiveness.\\n4. **Regulatory Readiness:** GDPR DPA, CCPA compliance, and EU AI Act readiness not specified; limits international deployment confidence.\\n5. **Vendor Transparency:** Sub-processor identities, infrastructure provider, and change management process not disclosed.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT** with mandatory conditions:\\n\\n- **Condition 1:** Vendor must provide formal AI governance policy, training data documentation, and bias testing methodology before contract execution.\\n- **Condition 2:** Vendor must disclose support response SLAs (P1/P2/P3) and commit to defined escalation procedures.\\n- **Condition 3:** For healthcare/financial services deployments, vendor must provide GDPR DPA and confirm EU AI Act compliance roadmap.\\n- **Condition 4:** Vendor must identify critical sub-processors (infrastructure, payments, auth) and provide corresponding SLAs.\\n\\n### Risk Classification\\n- **Product Risk:** 22/100 (Managed) — strong compliance and security posture offset by AI governance documentation gaps\\n- **Governance Risk:** 42/100 (Moderate) — certifications present but AI ethics and bias testing frameworks not documented\\n- **Operational Risk:** 20/100 (Low) — mature SLA, tested incident response, and comprehensive audit logs\\n- **Estimated Vendor Trust Score (VTS):** ~72/100 (Acceptable Vendor, Grade C)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation  \\n**Data Source:** Vendor-provided attestation; inferences noted where data incomplete", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Writer", "Customer Base": "Vizient (healthcare) documented as reference customer; total customer count not specified", "Target Industry": "Healthcare (corroborated case: Vizient), financial services, and general enterprise", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise multi-tenant; typical customer deployment scale not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Enterprise AI workflow integration; building, activating, and supervising AI agents grounded in company data", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; on-premises deployment options not specified", "Product Description": "Writer is a full-stack generative AI platform enabling enterprises to build and supervise AI agents grounded in proprietary company data. The platform emphasizes secure workflow integration, compliance-ready deployment (HIPAA BAA, SOC 2 Type 2), and knowledge graph capabilities to unlock structured data value. Unique positioning centers on agentic AI scalability, user experience, and customer success model alig