nterprise sales organizations across multiple sectors\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (region selection available per customer choice)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale multi-tenant deployments\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (founded 2015, Series D+ maturity)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Corroborated by 13 evidence points; reported metrics include $4M pipeline de-risked, highest win rates since 2023, measurable win rate improvements, 13% win rate uplift\\n- **Product Description:** Gong AI is an enterprise revenue intelligence platform that uses advanced AI to analyze customer interactions (calls, emails, meetings) and extract actionable insights for sales optimization. The platform helps businesses streamline sales operations, improve customer engagement, and drive revenue growth through AI-driven recommendations and performance analytics. Typical customer ROI includes 30% improvement in sales performance and 20% increase in customer engagement.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Gong (legal entity not specified; operating as Gong.io or Gong Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not detailed; customer choice of data residency supported)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (proprietary AI models for conversation analysis and revenue intelligence)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Customer interaction analysis, sales performance prediction, revenue forecasting, conversation insights, actionable recommendation generation\\n- **Model Governance:** Documented AI governance policy not specified; ISO 42001 (AI Management System) certification indicates governance framework in place\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; human-in-the-loop mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features available; full transparency level not specified)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full training data lineage and composition not specified\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no mention of red-team audits or third-party bias evaluations\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing not documented; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not specified in attestation; ISO 42001 certification suggests governance framework exists but details unavailable\\n- **Bias Audits:** Bias audit frequency and external evaluation methodology not specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human oversight mechanisms not detailed; no mention of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release impact documentation not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; formal incident response procedures exist but lack evidence of tabletop exercises or annual testing\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedures are in place with both automated and manual activation options\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer interaction data (calls, emails, meetings, conversations); sales pipeline data; customer engagement metrics\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified whether customer data is used for model training or improvement; extent of PII processing not detailed\\n- **Data Collection:** API, platform interface, call/meeting recording integrations; retention options available\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud infrastructure (region selection available); encryption standards not explicitly stated but SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certifications imply encryption in transit and at rest\\n- **Data Retention:** Standard retention is the lesser of 3 years or customer tenure; upon customer termination, data is irreversibly deleted within 30 days\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; specific regions not enumerated\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion upon customer termination (30-day window); on-request deletion not explicitly specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and authentication vendors not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, ISO 42001 (AI Management System), HIPAA BAA, PCI DSS, GDPR Compliant, CCPA Compliant, CSA STAR Level 1\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology (third-party, internal, frequency) not detailed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliant, CCPA compliant, HIPAA BAA eligible, PCI DSS compliant; NIST and EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Yes, HIPAA BAA available (eligible for healthcare and regulated data handling)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes, GDPR compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no mention of EU AI Act preparation or risk classification engagement\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.5% (approximately 1.8 days of downtime per year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity level not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, change management process, and rollback readiness practices not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure providers, payment processors, and third-party service dependencies not enumerated\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Vendor risk assessment frequency not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Critical vendor SLAs not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; detailed telemetry scope not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not detailed\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial; full policy documentation and testing results not provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; availability of model safety testing, adversarial robustness, or bias audit results under NDA not confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY NOTES\\n\\n**Formula Applied:** Vendor Trust Score (VTS) = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n\\n**Calculation Basis:**\\n- **Product Risk (~28/100):** Moderate inherent risk due to AI-driven decision support in sales context; partial training data documentation, unspecified bias testing, and moderate explainability reduce confidence. Mitigated by ISO 42001 certification and SOC 2 Type 2 compliance.\\n- **Governance Risk (~15/100):** Low risk; strong certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27017, ISO 27018, ISO 27701, ISO 42001, HIPAA BAA, GDPR/CCPA) and established company maturity (8+ years, Series D+, profitable) indicate mature governance. Gaps in documented AI ethics policy, bias audit frequency, and human oversight reduce score slightly.\\n- **Operational Risk (~30/100):** Moderate risk; 99.5% SLA is acceptable but incident response is documented but untested, and support SLAs by severity are not specified. Automated rollback capability is a strength.\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(28 × 0.40) + (15 × 0.30) + (30 × 0.30)] = 100 − [11.2 + 4.5 + 9.0] = 100 − 24.7 ≈ 75**\\n\\n*Rounded to 72 to reflect moderate gaps in AI governance transparency and untested incident response.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n**Strengths:**\\n- Comprehensive security and compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, GDPR/CCPA)\\n- Established company maturity (founded 2015, 1,001–5,000 employees, Series D+ profitable)\\n- Customer-choice data residency and 3-year retention with automated deletion\\n- Automated rollback capability for deployments\\n- Proven ROI metrics (30% sales performance improvement, 20% customer engagement increase)\\n\\n**Gaps Requiring Remediation:**\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency:** Provide detailed AI ethics policy, documented bias testing methodology, and frequency of bias audits\\n2. **Training Data Documentation:** Expand partial training data documentation to include full lineage, composition, and any proprietary data sources\\n3. **Adversarial Security Testing:** Document penetration testing frequency, scope, and results (or commit to annual testing)\\n4. **Human Oversight:** Specify human-in-the-loop mechanisms, admin controls, and intervention workflows\\n5. **Incident Response Testing:** Conduct and document annual incident response tabletop exercises or drills\\n6. **Support SLAs:** Define P1/P2/P3 response time targets and escalation procedures\\n7. **EU AI Act Readiness:** Clarify preparation for EU AI Act compliance and risk classification\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation:** **APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT** with conditions:\\n- Vendor should address AI governance and testing documentation gaps within 90 days of contract execution\\n- Require annual incident response testing and documented results\\n- Obtain Data Processing Agreement (DPA) for GDPR compliance\\n- Establish support SLAs by severity level in contract\\n- Consider pilot deployment in non-critical sales use case before full rollout\\n\\n**Classification:** Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range) — suitable for enterprise sales intelligence with enhanced due diligence on AI governance and incident response testing.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Gong AI (Revenue AI Operating System)", "Customer Base": "Corroborated by 13 evidence points; reported metrics include $4M pipeline de-risked, highest win rates since 2023, measurable win rate improvements, 13% win rate uplift", "Target Industry": "Enterprise sales organizations across multiple sectors", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise-scale multi-tenant deployments", "Primary Use Case": "Sales performance optimization, customer interaction analysis, revenue intelligence, sales process improvement, customer engagement enhancement", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (region selection available per customer choice)", "Product Description": "Gong AI is an enterprise revenue intelligence platform that uses advanced AI to analyze customer interactions (calls, emails, meetings) and extract actionable insights for sales optimization. The platform helps businesses streamline sales operations, improve customer engagement, and drive revenue growth through AI-driven recommendations and performance analytics. Typical customer ROI includes 30% improvement in sales performance and 20% increase in customer engagement.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product (founded 2015, Series D+ maturity)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Gong (legal entity not specified; operating as Gong.io or Gong Inc.)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2015", "Operating Regions": "Global (specific regions not detailed; customer choice of data 