: 99, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   88 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            2.93  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         1.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (2.9) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:33:49.790921+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	88	B	c07e5c7b-35ba-4a25-9b20-1d47a752b6ff	\N	\N
353bfdb5-8dad-4dad-9ee5-043e62ce3b01	613f95e0-c042-418d-bb9f-879327208497	82	82	AI Platform Provider	{"Technology & Software": ["Technology & Software"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	cloud.google.com	Google, through its Vertex AI platform, offers a fully-managed, unified AI development platform for building and using generative AI. It provides access to its latest Gemini models and tools for developers and enterprises to build, scale, and govern AI applications and agents at a global scale, including Gemini Enterprise for secure agent management.	10,000+	1998	Mountain View, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "Chief AI Officer", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Google Cloud and Gemini Enterprise help solve pain points such as low conversion rates in digital sales, inefficient security operations, inaccurate inventory forecasting, high operational costs, difficulty in personalizing customer experiences, challenges in managing large datasets, time-consuming content creation (e.g., video), scalability and reliability issues during peak demand, fragmented management systems, long development times, and the inability to accurately predict risks.	\N	Native integration with Google Search for live grounding, built-in trust through SSO and user-level access, and broad connectivity with enterprise systems like Google Workspace and Microsoft 365.	Customers have achieved: 2.6x boost in conversion rates in digital sales efforts (Millennium BCP), up to 90% improvement in inventory accuracy (Super-Pharm), reduction in video creation time from days to minutes (HeyGen), 37% cut in development time (ComplyAdvantage), sub-90ms latency and 99.99% uptime for voice AI (Cartesia), and processing $14.6B in Black Friday weekend sales without compromising speed and reliability (Shopify).	\N	\N	High (Feature importance, confidence scores)	\N	["SOC 2 Type 2", "SOC 3", "ISO 27001", "ISO 27017", "ISO 27018", "ISO 27701", "ISO 42001 (AI Management)", "HIPAA BAA", "FedRAMP", "PCI DSS", "CSA STAR Level 1", "CSA STAR Level 2"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region", "On-premise deployment available", "Hybrid (Cloud + On-prem)"]	For Gemini Enterprise (Standard and Plus editions), customer data, including prompts, chats, files, and outputs, are not used to train Google models or models for any other customer. All enterprise data remains within the customer's tenant and under their organization's control. Gemini Enterprise deletes user-requested data within 60 days. For the Gemini API, inputs and outputs are retained for up to 55 days for abuse monitoring, but this data is not used for model training.	\N	\N	\N	Full documentation with lineage	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented incident response process	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, comprehensive analytics	Yes, comprehensive	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:34:30.942037+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Gemini Enterprise	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:34:30.946+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Google Gemini Enterprise\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 87 (High)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 92\\n- Compliance: 95\\n- Data Practices: 88\\n- AI Governance: 75\\n- Operations: 90\\n- Company Maturity: 98\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nGoogle Gemini Enterprise demonstrates strong enterprise trustworthiness, driven by exceptional compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, FedRAMP), mature operational infrastructure (99.9% SLA, automated rollback), and robust data isolation practices (no model training on customer data, 60-day deletion). The score reflects the vendor's 25+ year operational maturity and comprehensive security posture. Primary gaps are in documented AI governance policy specifics (bias testing methodology, adversarial testing protocols, and human oversight workflows are not detailed in attestation), which moderately constrains the AI Governance category despite strong transparency and data practices. The formula applied: **VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**, where Product_Risk ≈ 13 (strong data controls, minor governance gaps), Governance_Risk ≈ 5 (comprehensive certifications, incomplete policy documentation), Operational_Risk ≈ 0 (mature SLA, proven incident response). This yields VTS ≈ 87, classified as **Exceptional Vendor** (90–100 range threshold approached; minor governance documentation gaps prevent 90+ score).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Gemini Enterprise\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Enterprise generative AI application development, agent management, secure multi-tenant deployment, digital sales optimization, security operations, inventory forecasting, content creation, risk prediction\\n- **Target Industry:** Retail, financial services, healthcare, technology, e-commerce, logistics, media\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (Google Cloud), SaaS with on-premise and hybrid options\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Google Cloud (multi-region), on-premise deployment available, hybrid (Cloud + on-prem)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale; customers include Shopify ($14.6B Black Friday processing), Millennium BCP, Super-Pharm, HeyGen, ComplyAdvantage, Cartesia\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Production-ready; mature platform with 25+ years of parent company operational history\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Multi-industry enterprise customers with documented ROI metrics (2.6x conversion boost, 90% inventory accuracy, sub-90ms latency, 99.99% uptime for voice AI)\\n- **Product Description:** Gemini Enterprise is a fully-managed, unified AI development platform providing secure access to Google's latest Gemini models with native integration to Google Search for live grounding, built-in SSO and user-level access controls, and broad enterprise system connectivity (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365). The platform enforces strict data isolation—customer data is never used for model training—and supports flexible deployment (cloud, on-premise, hybrid) with comprehensive compliance certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, FedRAMP).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Google LLC (Alphabet Inc. subsidiary)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (Cloud Infrastructure & Generative AI)\\n- **Year Founded:** 1998\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+ (Google Cloud division; Alphabet Inc. ~190,000+ total)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Publicly traded (Alphabet Inc.); Google Cloud revenue ~$33B+ annually (2023)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Publicly traded; Headquarters: Mountain View, CA, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (multi-region cloud infrastructure across North America, Europe, Asia-Pacific, and other regions)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Gemini (large language models); access to latest Gemini model variants\\n- **Model Purpose:** Generative AI capabilities including text understanding, generation, code generation, multimodal analysis, agent orchestration, and real-time grounding via Google Search integration\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified in detail; platform supports staged deployment and multi-tenant isolation; Gemini Enterprise includes secure agent management\\n- **Human Oversight:** Built-in SSO and user-level access controls; comprehensive audit logs available; interaction telemetry available for monitoring\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** High transparency; feature importance and confidence scores provided; native integration with Google Search for live grounding supports citation and source attribution\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Full documentation with lineage provided\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified (bias testing approach not detailed in attestation)\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified (adversarial security testing protocols not detailed in attestation)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not explicitly detailed in attestation; however, platform enforces data isolation and user-level access controls\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified (frequency and external evaluation methodology not provided)\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Built-in SSO and user-level access controls; comprehensive audit logs and interaction telemetry enable monitoring and intervention; specific human-in-the-loop workflows not detailed\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified (system cards or release documentation not mentioned)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented incident response process in place\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger capability; enables rapid remediation of issues\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Prompts, chats, files, outputs; supports integration with enterprise systems (Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, Google Search)\\n- **PII Handling:** Gemini Enterprise enforces strict data isolation; customer data (including PII) is not used for model training or shared with other customers; data remains within customer's tenant under organization's control\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface; comprehensive analytics and interaction telemetry available\\n- **Data Storage:** Google Cloud infrastructure with encryption; customer choice of region; on-premise and hybrid deployment options available\\n- **Data Retention:** \\n  - **Gemini Enterprise (Standard & Plus editions):** Customer data deleted within 60 days upon request; no retention for model training\\n  - **Gemini API:** Inputs and outputs retained for up to 55 days for abuse monitoring only (not used for model training)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; on-premise deployment available; hybrid (Cloud + on-prem) supported\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request (60-day deletion window for Gemini Enterprise)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Google Cloud infrastructure (compute, storage, networking); Google Search integration for grounding; authentication via SSO; payment processing (not specified); third-party integrations with Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2\\n  - SOC 3\\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security)\\n  - ISO 27018 (Personal Data Protection in Cloud)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management Systems)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (eligible for healthcare PHI handling)\\n  - FedRAMP (federal government compliance)\\n  - PCI DSS (payment card data security)\\n  - CSA STAR Level 1 & Level 2 (Cloud Security Alliance)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted by independent third party (standard practice); ISO certifications maintained through independent certification bodies; audit frequency not specified\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:**\\n  - NIST: Compliance with NIST cybersecurity standards via FedRAMP authorization\\n  - GDPR: Data residency options and data deletion capabilities support GDPR compliance\\n  - CCPA: Data isolation and deletion on request support CCPA compliance\\n  - EU AI Act: Not explicitly stated; platform's transparency, data isolation, and governance controls align with EU AI Act requirements for high-risk AI systems\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Yes, HIPAA BAA available; eligible for healthcare PHI handling with appropriate data residency and access controls\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes, supported via customer choice of data residency (EU regions available), data deletion on request (60-day window), and data processor agreements\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not explicitly stated; however, platform's comprehensive certifications (ISO 42001), data isolation, transparency features, and audit capabilities position it favorably for EU AI Act compliance\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; audit findings not disclosed in attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours of acceptable downtime per year)\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified in attestation\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified in attestation; however, automated rollback capability with manual trigger indicates mature release management practices\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** \\n  - Google Cloud infrastructure (compute, storage, networking)\\n  - Google Search (for live grounding integration)\\n  - Microsoft 365 (enterprise integration)\\n  - Google Workspace (enterprise integration)\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified (frequency of risk assessments for sub-processors not provided)\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Google Cloud infrastructure SLAs typically 99.95%+ for compute and storage; specific SLAs for critical sub-processors not detailed in attestation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available; enables monitoring of model behavior, user interactions, and system performance\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available; supports export for security information and event management (SIEM) integration\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Not provided in attestation; however, SOC 2 Type 2 audit reports and ISO certification documentation are available upon request\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available; specific methodologies and findings not disclosed in public attestation (likely available under NDA for enterprise customers)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary Assessment\\n\\n**Strengths:**\\n- Exceptional compliance posture with 11 major certifications including SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, FedRAMP, and ISO 42001 (AI Management)\\n- Mature, proven operational infrastructure (99.9% SLA, automated rollback, documented incident response)\\n- Strong data practices with strict customer data isolation, no model training on customer data, and flexible deployment options (cloud, on-premise, hybrid)\\n- Transparent AI capabilities with feature importance, confidence scores, and live grounding via Google Search\\n- Enterprise-scale customer base with documented ROI metrics across multiple industries\\n- 25+ years of parent company operational maturity and financial stability\\n\\n**Gaps:**\\n- AI governance policy details not explicitly documented in attestation (bias testing methodology, adversarial testing protocols, human-in-the-loop workflows not specified)\\n- Support SLAs by severity level not provided\\n- Change management and release cadence details not specified\\n- Audit frequency and last audit date not disclosed\\n- EU AI Act readiness not explicitly stated (though platform controls suggest alignment)\\n\\n**Recommendation:**\\n**APPROVED FOR FAST-TRACK PROCUREMENT** — Gemini Enterprise demonstrates market-leading compliance, operational maturity, and data governance practices suitable for enterprise and regulated-industry deployments. Recommend requesting detailed AI governance policy documentation, bias testing methodology, and adversarial testing protocols as contract addenda to close governance documentation gaps. Suitable for healthcare (HIPAA), government (FedRAMP), and financial services (PCI DSS) use cases with appropriate data residency and access control configuration.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Gemini Enterprise", "Customer Base": "Multi-industry enterprise customers with documented ROI met