l & Professional Services AI Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 78 (Acceptable Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 82\\n- Compliance: 85\\n- Data Practices: 88\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 80\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nHarvey AI demonstrates strong compliance posture and data privacy practices, with robust certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, ISO 42001) and explicit zero-retention, customer-controlled data policies. Operations are solid with 99.9% uptime SLA and annual incident response testing. However, the Trust Score is moderated by gaps in AI governance transparency—limited documentation on bias testing, adversarial security testing, human oversight mechanisms, and explainability features. The company's Series D+ maturity and 2022 founding provide operational stability, but the relatively recent market entry and moderate transparency on AI safety practices prevent a higher score. Applied formula: VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)], with Product Risk elevated due to incomplete AI safety documentation and Governance Risk moderated by strong compliance certifications.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Harvey AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Contract analysis, due diligence, compliance review, litigation support, document research\\n- **Target Industry:** Legal services, professional services, Fortune 500 enterprises\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; customer choice of data residency region\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise (law firms, Fortune 500 companies)\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product with basic test results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Law firms and Fortune 500 companies; ROI corroborated by 11 evidence points (33% contract processing time reduction, 27% quote generation velocity improvement, 19% data entry accuracy gain, 42% response time improvement to sales inquiries, 10 hours/week time savings)\\n- **Product Description:** Harvey AI is a domain-specific AI platform for legal and professional services, specializing in contract analysis, due diligence, compliance, and litigation support. The platform emphasizes security and privacy through encrypted processing, a secure document vault, and zero data retention for model training. It is built on modern AI capabilities with moderate explainability features and is designed for enterprise deployment with customer-controlled data residency and retention policies.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Harvey (legal entity name not specified; operating as Harvey AI)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2022\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years (inferred from \\"Established\\" maturity classification)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, California, United States; specific investors not disclosed\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: North America primary; customer choice of data residency suggests multi-region capability)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (inferred: Large Language Model or domain-specific transformer-based model for legal document understanding and generation)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Document understanding, contract analysis, compliance assessment, litigation research, query answering, document summarization\\n- **Model Governance:** Not fully specified; documented AI governance policy field incomplete; ISO 42001 (AI Management) certification indicates governance framework in place\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; field incomplete\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate explainability features; some transparency available but not comprehensive\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; does not train AI models on customer data (zero-retention policy enforced)\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; bias testing approach field incomplete\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing field incomplete; no frequency or type documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not specified; documented AI governance policy field incomplete\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no external bias audit frequency or evaluations documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; human oversight mechanisms not documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards or release documentation referenced\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually; demonstrates mature incident response capability\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; enables rapid recovery from problematic deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Legal documents (contracts, compliance materials, litigation files), queries, professional communications\\n- **PII Handling:** Customer data is not used for model training; zero-retention policy ensures PII is not retained for AI improvement\\n- **Data Collection:** API and interface-based; customer-controlled retention and deletion settings available\\n- **Data Storage:** Encrypted processing; secure vault for legal document storage; infrastructure not specified (inferred: cloud-hosted on customer-selected region)\\n- **Data Retention:** Customer-controlled; zero data retention for model training; customers can configure retention and deletion policies\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; multi-region support implied\\n- **Data Deletion:** Customer-initiated deletion available; automated deletion policies configurable\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified (inferred: cloud infrastructure provider, authentication services; specific vendors not disclosed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 (security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy)\\n  - ISO 27001 (information security management)\\n  - ISO 27701 (privacy information management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI management systems)\\n  - GDPR Compliant\\n  - CCPA Compliant\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit frequency and last audit date not provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR, CCPA, ISO standards; EU AI Act readiness not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not stated (likely not HIPAA-certified given legal focus rather than healthcare)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes, certified compliant; DPA availability not explicitly stated but implied by certification\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 implies annual or bi-annual audit cycle, but specific dates and findings not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance); strong enterprise-grade availability commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure and payment processor vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of vendor risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; interaction data available for monitoring and optimization\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; audit log export capability not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available; comprehensive policy documentation not referenced\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified; no indication of advanced safety testing results available under NDA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Strengths\\n\\n1. **Strong Data Privacy & Retention:** Zero-retention policy for model training and customer-controlled data deletion provide exceptional privacy protection for sensitive legal documents.\\n2. **Comprehensive Compliance Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, and ISO 42001 demonstrate mature security and AI governance frameworks.\\n3. **Enterprise Operational Maturity:** 99.9% uptime SLA, annual incident response testing, and automated rollback capability indicate reliable production operations.\\n4. **Proven ROI & Customer Traction:** 11 corroborated evidence points show measurable business impact (33% processing time reduction, 42% response time improvement).\\n5. **Domain-Specific Expertise:** Tailored AI for legal services with secure document vault and encrypted processing reduces domain-specific risks.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Gaps & Recommendations\\n\\n1. **Limited AI Safety Transparency:** Bias testing approach, adversarial security testing, and human oversight mechanisms are not documented. **Recommendation:** Request detailed bias audit results, adversarial testing reports, and human-in-the-loop workflow documentation before enterprise deployment.\\n\\n2. **Incomplete AI Governance Documentation:** Documented AI governance policy, model explainability details, and impact assessments are not provided. **Recommendation:** Require vendor to provide AI ethics policy, model card documentation, and explainability framework before contract execution.\\n\\n3. **Support SLA Gaps:** Response time targets by severity level are not specified. **Recommendation:** Negotiate and document P1/P2/P3 response SLAs aligned with customer criticality requirements.\\n\\n4. **Vendor Risk Assessment Undocumented:** No evidence of third-party vendor assessments or critical vendor SLAs. **Recommendation:** Request vendor risk assessment reports and SLAs from critical infrastructure and payment processors.\\n\\n5. **Limited Audit Transparency:** Specific audit dates, findings, and audit frequency not disclosed. **Recommendation:** Request most recent SOC 2 Type 2 audit report and schedule annual audit reviews as contract condition.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT** with conditions:\\n\\n- ✅ **Proceed:** Strong compliance posture, proven operations, and exceptional data privacy practices support enterprise deployment.\\n- ⚠️ **Conditions:** Require vendor to provide (1) detailed AI safety and bias testing documentation, (2) human oversight and explainability framework, (3) support SLAs by severity, and (4) most recent SOC 2 audit report before contract execution.\\n- 📋 **Contract Terms:** Include annual compliance audit verification, incident response testing attestation, and data residency guarantees as ongoing obligations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Classification Summary\\n\\n| Category | Score | Status |\\n|----------|-------|--------|\\n| **Overall Trust Score** | **78** | **Acceptable Vendor (C Grade)** |\\n| Security | 82 | Strong |\\n| Compliance | 85 | Strong |\\n| Data Practices | 88 | Exceptional |\\n| AI Governance | 65 | Moderate (gaps) |\\n| Operations | 80 | Strong |\\n| Company Maturity | 75 | Acceptable |\\n\\n**Rationale:** Harvey AI qualifies as an Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range) with strong compliance and data privacy practices offsetting moderate gaps in AI safety transparency. The company's Series D+ maturity, 99.9% uptime, and zero-retention policy support enterprise deployment. However, incomplete documentation on bias testing, human oversight, and explainability prevents a higher grade. Enhanced due diligence on AI governance is required before deployment.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Harvey AI", "Customer Base": "Law firms and Fortune 500 companies; ROI corroborated by 11 evidence points (33% contract processing time reduction, 27% quote generation velocity improvement, 19% data entry accuracy gain, 42% response time improvement to sales inquiries, 10 hours/week time savings)", "Target Industry": "Legal services, professional services, Fortune 500 enterprises", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise (law firms, Fortune 500 companies)", "Primary Use Case": "Contract analysis, due diligence, compliance review, litigation support, document research", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; customer choice of data residency region", "Product Description": "Harvey AI is a domain-specific AI platform for legal and professional services, specializing in contract analysis, due diligence, compliance, and litigation support. The platform emphasizes security and privacy through encrypted processing, a secure document vault, and zero data retention for model training. It is built on modern AI capabilities with moderate explainability features and is designed for enterprise deployment with customer-controlled data residency and retention policies.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product with basic test results available"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "201–1,000", "Legal Name": "Harvey (legal entity name not specified; operating as Harvey AI)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2022", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (inferred: North America primary; customer choice of data residency suggests multi-region capability)", "Key Investors / Headquarte