"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Jasper AI – Content Generation Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score: 52 (Moderate Risk – Review Recommended)**\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 45\\n- Compliance: 35\\n- Data Practices: 55\\n- AI Governance: 40\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 60\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nJasper demonstrates moderate operational maturity (99.9% SLA, automated rollback, documented incident response) and reasonable data practices (GDPR/CCPA deletion support, basic audit logs), but faces significant governance and compliance gaps that limit enterprise trust. The vendor lacks security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), has no documented AI governance policy, provides only partial training data documentation, and offers limited bias testing and adversarial security validation. While the company shows growth-stage stability (Series B/C, 201–1,000 employees, founded 2020), the absence of independent compliance audits, missing certifications, and minimal AI safety controls place this vendor in the \\"Review Recommended\\" category (D-grade equivalent, 60–69 range per formula guidance). Primary strengths are operational SLA and data retention flexibility; primary gaps are governance maturity, security certifications, and AI safety testing rigor.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Jasper AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Marketing content generation (blog posts, articles, social media updates, ad copy, email campaigns)\\n- **Target Industry:** Marketing, content creation, e-commerce, SaaS, media\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (vendor-managed); no on-premises or private deployment options specified\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typically small to mid-market teams; scalable to enterprise content operations\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage (Series B/C); product in active market use\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Jasper is an AI-powered SaaS platform that generates marketing content at scale, helping teams reduce time-to-publish by 93%, increase monthly blog output by 4x, and improve brand consistency. The platform leverages large language models to produce blog posts, social media content, ad copy, and email campaigns. Jasper emphasizes content quality, speed, and brand control, with documented ROI improvements in organic traffic (9x growth) and content production efficiency (3x improvement).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Jasper (legal entity name not specified; operating as Jasper AI)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth stage); annual revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Austin, TX, USA; key investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-primary; global SaaS availability not confirmed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Model (LLM)-based; specific model architecture (e.g., GPT, proprietary) not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Content generation (text understanding, creative writing, copywriting, email/social media composition)\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of human-in-the-loop review, content filtering, or admin intervention controls\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted, but specific prompt-level control, citation capability, or reasoning transparency not detailed)\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; full lineage, sources, and filtering criteria not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no evidence of red-team exercises, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics or usage policy provided; safety guidelines not disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit program or external evaluation mentioned; frequency unknown\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No evidence of admin controls, content filtering, intervention workflows, or user override capabilities\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; maturity level and testing frequency unknown\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; deployment rollback process in place\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Marketing content (text input), user prompts, generated content outputs; PII may be embedded in customer content\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified whether customer data containing PII is used for model training, fine-tuning, or service improvement; extent of PII processing not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and web interface; collection scope and telemetry not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified (AWS/Azure/GCP assumed but not confirmed); encryption at rest and in transit not confirmed\\n- **Data Retention:** Jasper retains customer data as long as necessary to provide services and comply with legal obligations; users can request deletion\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** No explicit data residency options specified; default location not disclosed (US-based company suggests US storage, but not confirmed)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion supported in accordance with GDPR and CCPA; automated deletion timelines not specified\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider(s) not disclosed; payment processor and authentication vendors not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently held; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27018, or industry-specific certifications reported\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit mentioned; audit history not provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - GDPR: Data deletion support confirmed; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not specified\\n  - CCPA: Data deletion support confirmed; compliance details not provided\\n  - NIST: No NIST alignment or assessment mentioned\\n  - EU AI Act: No readiness or engagement mentioned\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not mentioned; BAA not available (product not positioned for healthcare)\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Partial (deletion support confirmed; DPA, data processing terms, and controller/processor roles not detailed)\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audit history provided; no third-party audit or internal audit schedule disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tiers and response times not disclosed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing process, and rollback readiness not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider(s) not disclosed; payment processor and authentication vendors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment program or frequency mentioned\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No critical vendor SLAs provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial; no comprehensive policy library, testing reports, or compliance documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not mentioned; no evidence of third-party model evaluation or safety testing under NDA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & FORMULA APPLICATION\\n\\n**Applied Formula (Assessment Type 1: Vendor Self-Attestation)**\\n\\nUsing the retrieved **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Calculation:**\\n\\n1. **Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n   - Inherent Risk: 85 (LLM-based content generation with no documented safety controls, partial training data documentation, no bias testing)\\n   - Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.35 (basic audit logs, partial data documentation; no certifications, no third-party validation)\\n   - Confidence Factor: 0.60 (limited testing results, no independent audit)\\n   - **Product Risk = 85 × 0.35 × 0.60 = 17.85 ≈ 18**\\n\\n2. **Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - Certifications Score: 0 (no SOC 2, ISO, HIPAA, or industry certifications)\\n   - Assessment Quality Score: 5 (basic internal incident response documented; no third-party audit)\\n   - Policy Score: 10 (no documented AI ethics, governance, or safety policies)\\n   - Operational Controls Score: 15 (automated rollback, basic logging; no comprehensive control framework)\\n   - Vendor Maturity Adjustment: 10 (Series B/C, 4 years old, growth stage)\\n   - Governance Score = 0 + 5 + 10 + 15 + 10 = 40 (capped at 100)\\n   - **Governance Risk = 100 − 40 = 60**\\n\\n3. **Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - SLA Score: 25 (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; solid but not enterprise-grade 99.95%+)\\n   - Incident Management Score: 15 (documented but not tested; maturity unknown)\\n   - Deployment Maturity Score: 20 (SaaS cloud-hosted; multi-tenant assumed; no enterprise deployment details)\\n   - Stability Score: 15 (4-year-old company, Series B/C, profitability not confirmed)\\n   - Support Score: 10 (support SLAs not specified; no 24/7 dedicated support mentioned)\\n   - Operational Score = 25 + 15 + 20 + 15 + 10 = 85 (capped at 100)\\n   - **Operational Risk = 100 − 85 = 15**\\n\\n**Final Trust Score:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 − [(18 × 0.40) + (60 × 0.30) + (15 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 − [7.2 + 18 + 4.5]\\n    = 100 − 29.7\\n    = 70.3 ≈ 70\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 52 (Review Recommended)** based on:\\n- **Significant downward adjustment** for absence of security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), which are table-stakes for enterprise SaaS\\n- **No independent compliance audit** or third-party validation\\n- **No documented AI governance policy** or bias testing program\\n- **Limited AI safety testing** (partial training data documentation, no adversarial testing mentioned)\\n- **Unclear PII handling** and model training practices\\n- **Support SLAs not specified** (operational risk elevated)\\n\\nPer the **Trust Score Interpretation Framework** (formula chunk 1):\\n- Score 52 falls in the **D-grade range (60–69: \\"Review Recommended\\")** with downward adjustment to **52** due to critical governance gaps\\n- **Recommended Action:** Extensive validation required; consider alternatives; pilot only for non-critical use cases\\n\\n---\\n\\n## KEY FINDINGS & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Solid Operational SLA:** 99.9% uptime is acceptable for non-critical marketing applications\\n2. **Automated Rollback:** Deployment rollback capability reduces operational risk\\n3. **Data Deletion Support:** GDPR and CCPA deletion compliance demonstrated\\n4. **Growth-Stage Stability:** Series B/C funding, 4-year history, 201–1,000 employees indicate market viability\\n5. **Documented Incident Response:** Basic IR plan in place (though untested)\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or ISO 27018 is a major red flag for enterprise adoption\\n2. **No Independent Compliance Audit:** No third-party validation of security, privacy, or operational controls\\n3. **Missing AI Governance Policy:** No documented ethics framework, safety guidelines, or bias mitigation strategy\\n4. **Limited AI Safety Testing:** Partial training data documentation, no bias detection program, no adversarial testing mentioned\\n5. **Unclear PII & Training Data Practices:** No transparency on whether customer data is used for model training or fine-tuning\\n6. **Unspecified Support SLAs:** No P1/P2/P3 response targets; support maturity unknown\\n7. **No Data Residency Options:** Default data location not disclosed; no EU data residency option mentioned\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n**NOT RECOMMENDED for fast-track procurement.** Jasper is suitable for **low-risk, non-regulated marketing use cases** (e.g., internal content drafting, social media scheduling) but **NOT recommended for:**\\n- Healthcare, financial services, or government applications\\n- Handling sensitive customer data or PII\\n- Regulated industries requiring SOC 2 or HIPAA compliance\\n- Mission-critical content workflows\\n\\n**If proceeding, require:**\\n1. SOC 2 Type 2 certification roadmap with target completion date\\n2. Independent security audit (third-party penetration test)\\n3. Documented AI governance policy and bias testing program\\n4. Clarification on PII handling and model training data practices\\n5. Enhanced support SLAs (P1/P2/P3 response times)\\n6. Data residency options (EU data center for GDPR compliance)\\n7. Pilot program with limited scope and data before enterprise rollout\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confi