 "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Lovable Platform – AI-Powered App & Website Development\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score: 62** (Moderate / Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 72\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 58\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 50\\n- Company Maturity: 55\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nLovable demonstrates solid foundational security and compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR compliance) and has implemented automated security controls (Security Checker 2.0, policy enforcement). However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance maturity, operational transparency, and data practices documentation that limit overall trustworthiness. The company's recent founding (2023), growth-stage maturity, and lack of formal AI testing, bias audits, training data documentation, and disclosed SLAs create material risk for enterprise deployments. The score reflects the formula weighting: **Product Risk (40%) = 55** (moderate inherent risk with partial mitigation), **Governance Risk (30%) = 60** (incomplete policies and audit framework), **Operational Risk (30%) = 50** (undisclosed SLAs and untested incident response). This vendor is acceptable for non-critical use cases but requires enhanced due diligence and contractual commitments before production deployment in regulated industries.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Lovable Platform\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Rapid AI-powered creation of web applications and websites from natural language descriptions; automated security scanning and policy enforcement.\\n- **Target Industry:** Software development, web agencies, enterprises seeking accelerated development cycles.\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); no on-premises deployment option stated.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified; typical customer deployment size not documented.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal AI testing conducted; basic interaction metrics available.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not quantified; ROI corroborated by 7 evidence points indicating adoption and cost savings.\\n- **Product Description:** Lovable is an AI-powered platform enabling rapid development of applications and websites through natural language descriptions, reducing development time by up to 50%. The platform includes automated security scanning (Security Checker 2.0) for exposed secrets and misconfigurations, combined with human-oversight policy enforcement that blocks violations in real-time. Built with SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, and GDPR compliance, the platform mitigates security risks through automated controls rather than manual intervention.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Lovable (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider\\n- **Year Founded:** 2023\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); annual revenue not disclosed.\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Stockholm, Sweden; specific investors not named.\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; global reach assumed based on GDPR compliance and web-based SaaS model.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified; underlying LLM or custom model architecture not disclosed.\\n- **Model Purpose:** Code generation, application design, website creation from natural language input; security policy enforcement and violation detection.\\n- **Model Governance:** Platform safety program with human oversight documented; real-time policy violation blocking implemented. Formal staged deployment or canary release process not specified.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Human oversight integrated into platform safety program; real-time policy enforcement with blocking capability. Monitoring and alert mechanisms not detailed.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate explainability; some features present but comprehensive transparency documentation not provided. Prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not specified.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available. Significant gap for enterprise AI governance.\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools specified.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted. Incident response plan documented but not tested.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not explicitly provided; platform safety program with human oversight and policy enforcement described but formal ethics framework not detailed.\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations documented; no frequency specified.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Real-time policy violation blocking and human oversight integrated into platform safety program; content filtering and intervention mechanisms operational. Admin controls not detailed.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or formal impact assessments documented for releases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested. Maturity level unclear; testing and annual validation not confirmed.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; deployment rollback procedures in place but frequency of testing not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Application code, website designs, natural language descriptions, user input; specific data categories not exhaustively documented.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly specified. GDPR compliance stated but extent of PII processing and safeguards not detailed.\\n- **Data Collection:** API and platform interface; retention options not specified.\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not named; encryption status (in transit and at rest) not confirmed.\\n- **Data Retention:** Not explicitly stated. Vendor notes GDPR compliance likely implies standard retention practices, but default retention period and deletion timelines not documented.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; EU residency likely given Stockholm headquarters and GDPR compliance, but customer choice and multi-region options not confirmed.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request implied by GDPR compliance; automated deletion policies not specified.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not named; sub-processor list not provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR Compliant\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not specified.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not stated; BAA eligibility not confirmed.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Yes, GDPR compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly confirmed.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; vendor engagement or preparation for EU AI Act requirements not documented.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Audit frequency not disclosed; last audit date not provided; audit findings not available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** Not disclosed. Material gap for enterprise commitments.\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response targets by severity not documented.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not detailed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not named.\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not specified.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, audit logs available; export capability and retention not specified.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited documentation; formal AI testing results, bias audits, and comprehensive policy frameworks not provided.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; NDA-protected results not available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Security & Compliance Foundation:** SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, and GDPR compliance demonstrate baseline security controls and third-party validation.\\n2. **Automated Security Controls:** Security Checker 2.0 and real-time policy enforcement reduce manual security burden and provide proactive threat detection.\\n3. **Proven ROI:** Documented cost savings (up to 50% development time reduction, $1M+ annual cost avoidance) and high support ticket reduction (85%) indicate operational value.\\n4. **Human Oversight Integration:** Platform safety program with real-time policy blocking and human oversight reduces autonomous AI risk.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **AI Governance Immaturity:** No documented training data, bias testing, formal ethics policy, or impact assessments. Significant risk for regulated industries.\\n2. **Operational Transparency:** Uptime SLA, support response SLAs, and release cadence not disclosed. Limits ability to assess operational reliability.\\n3. **Data Practices Documentation:** PII handling, data retention policies, storage encryption, and sub-processor list not specified. GDPR compliance inferred but not formally documented.\\n4. **Testing & Validation:** No formal AI testing, adversarial security testing, or annual incident response drills documented. Incident response plan untested.\\n5. **Company Maturity Risk:** Founded 2023 (1 year old), Series B/C stage, 51–200 employees. Limited operational track record and financial stability not confirmed.\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – MODERATE RISK**\\n\\n**Suitable for:**\\n- Non-critical internal development tools and proof-of-concept projects\\n- Organizations with moderate risk tolerance and internal AI governance capability\\n- Use cases not involving regulated data (healthcare PHI, financial PII, government classified)\\n\\n**Not Recommended for:**\\n- Healthcare, financial services, or government deployments without extensive remediation\\n- Production systems requiring 99.9%+ uptime SLAs\\n- Regulated data processing without formal Data Processing Agreement and BAA\\n\\n**Required Contractual Conditions:**\\n1. Explicit uptime SLA (minimum 99.5%) with financial penalties\\n2. Support response SLAs (P1: 4 hours, P2: 8 hours, P3: 24 hours)\\n3. Formal Data Processing Agreement (DPA) with GDPR Annex B sub-processor list\\n4. Annual SOC 2 Type 2 audit with findings disclosure\\n5. Documented incident response plan with annual testing certification\\n6. Training data documentation and bias audit roadmap (12-month delivery)\\n7. 30-day rollback guarantee for production deployments\\n\\n**Recommended Due Diligence:**\\n- Reference calls with 3+ enterprise customers in similar industries\\n- Security architecture review of data storage, encryption, and access controls\\n- Formal vendor financial stability assessment (funding runway, burn rate)\\n- Pilot deployment with non-critical workload (3–6 months) before production commitment\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Current Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Formula Applied:** VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Lovable Platform", "Customer Base": "Not quantified; ROI corroborated by 7 evidence points indicating adoption and cost savings.", "Target Industry": "Software development, web agencies, enterprises seeking accelerated development cycles.", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified; typical customer deployment size not documented.", "Primary Use Case": "Rapid AI-powered creation of web applications and websites from natural language descriptions; automated security scanning and policy enforcement.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified); no on-premises deployment option stated.", "Product Description": "Lovable is an AI-powered platform enabling rapid development of applications and websites through natural language descriptions, reducing development time by up to 50%. The platform includes automated security scanning (Security Checker 2.0) for exposed secrets and misconfigurations, combined with human-oversight policy enforcement that blocks violations in real-time. Built with SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, and GDPR compliance, the platform mitigates security risks through automated controls rather than manual intervention.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C); no formal AI testing conducted; basic interaction metrics available."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Lovable (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider", "Year Founded": "2023", "Operating Regions": "Not specified; global reach assumed based on GDPR compliance and web-based SaaS model.", "Key Inves