cessing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly confirmed.", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not stated; BAA eligibility not confirmed.", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; vendor engagement or preparation for EU AI Act requirements not documented.", "Regulatory Frameworks": "GDPR compliance confirmed; NIST, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not specified.", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; audit methodology and scope not documented.", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Audit frequency not disclosed; last audit date not provided; audit findings not available."}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "Not disclosed. Material gap for enterprise commitments.", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not detailed.", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; support response targets by severity not documented."}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Key SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not documented.", "Critical Vendors": "Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication vendors not named.", "Vendor Assessment": "Frequency of risk assessments of critical vendors not specified."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, audit logs available; export capability and retention not specified.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted; NDA-protected results not available.", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Limited documentation; formal AI testing results, bias audits, and comprehensive policy frameworks not provided."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Lovable demonstrates solid foundational security and compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR compliance) and has implemented automated security controls (Security Checker 2.0, policy enforcement). However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance maturity, operational transparency, and data practices documentation that limit overall trustworthiness. The company's recent founding (2023), growth-stage maturity, and lack of formal AI testing, bias audits, training data documentation, and disclosed SLAs create material risk for enterprise deployments. The score reflects the formula weighting: **Product Risk (40%) = 55** (moderate inherent risk with partial mitigation), **Governance Risk (30%) = 60** (incomplete policies and audit framework), **Operational Risk (30%) = 50** (undisclosed SLAs and untested incident response). This vendor is acceptable for non-critical use cases but requires enhanced due diligence and contractual commitments before production deployment in regulated industries. ---", "overallScore": 84, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.63, "Governance": 94, "Operational": 58}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   84 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       42.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk         6.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            4.37  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (42.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (6.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (58.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:41:27.744361+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	84	B	b92114fb-030f-499c-8d3c-4a89956c939e	\N	\N
592b6a49-fd73-41ba-8328-8b83c424bc57	fe5a7a8c-8695-4b99-95ac-f89275bb5545	93	93	AI Product Company	{"Technology": ["Technology"]}	Growth (Series B/C)	https://manus.im	Manus is a genre-defining smart AI agent, not just another chatbot. It actively streamlines busywork and delivers production-ready results. With flexible team pricing and upcoming collaboration features, it transforms how teams work with AI through simple, intuitive onboarding.	Nov-50	2020	Singapore, Singapore	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "Line of Business Leader"]	Manus addresses the inefficiency of manual task handling by automating repetitive tasks and delivering production-ready results. It also solves the problem of complex AI onboarding by providing simple, intuitive integration for teams. Additionally, it enhances decision-making by offering AI-driven insights and analysis.	\N	Manus offers flexible team pricing and upcoming collaboration features, making it highly adaptable for various team sizes and needs. Its simple, intuitive onboarding process ensures quick integration and minimal disruption. Additionally, Manus actively streamlines busywork and delivers production-ready results, enhancing overall productivity.	30% reduction in manual processing time, 2x improvement in task completion speed	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	["SOC 2 Type 1", "SOC 2 Type 2", "ISO 27001", "ISO 27701"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region"]	Conversation history and agent logs have configurable retention periods (7 days to 7 years) with immediate and permanent deletion.	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, comprehensive	Limited/Partial	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:42:07.58244+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Manus	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:42:07.586+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Manus AI Agent Platform\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate / Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 78\\n- Compliance: 75\\n- Data Practices: 72\\n- AI Governance: 45\\n- Operations: 70\\n- Company Maturity: 58\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nManus demonstrates solid foundational security and compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 1/2, ISO 27001/27701 certifications) with flexible data residency and configurable retention policies. However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance maturity—notably absent documented AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, training data documentation, and formal human oversight protocols—which substantially constrains trust for regulated or high-stakes deployments. The company's growth-stage maturity (Series B/C, ~11–50 employees, founded 2020) and lack of tested incident response procedures further elevate operational risk. The score reflects acceptable use for non-critical, internal-facing automation but requires substantial governance and testing enhancements before deployment in healthcare, financial services, or other regulated sectors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Manus\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automation of repetitive tasks, team collaboration, AI-driven decision support, production-ready task execution\\n- **Target Industry:** General enterprise (cross-industry; no sector specialization stated)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (customer choice of region)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted SaaS with customer-selectable data residency\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Team-based (flexible team pricing model); typical deployment size not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product; limited/partial testing results available\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor (flexible team-based pricing model)\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified\\n- **Product Description:** Manus is a smart AI agent platform designed to automate busywork and deliver production-ready results with minimal onboarding friction. It emphasizes team collaboration, flexible pricing, and intuitive integration. The platform supports configurable data retention (7 days to 7 years) and customer-controlled data residency, positioning it as privacy-conscious for general enterprise use; however, it lacks documented AI governance, bias testing, and formal human oversight frameworks necessary for regulated industries.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Manus (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2020\\n- **Employees:** 11–50\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage funding; revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Singapore, Singapore; key investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (inferred: global via cloud SaaS model; no regional restrictions mentioned)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (underlying LLM or custom model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Task automation, decision support, analysis, and production-ready result generation\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy; safety framework not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no formal human-in-the-loop, monitoring, or intervention protocols documented\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; red team or third-party audits not mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit program or external evaluation framework specified\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or formal impact documentation for releases mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested** (maturity gap: untested procedures reduce confidence in real-world execution)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (moderate maturity; manual trigger introduces operational delay vs. fully automated rollback)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Not specified (inferred: task/workflow data, agent logs, conversation history based on product description)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and customer data use for training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API and agent interface (inferred); retention options configurable\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards not detailed\\n- **Data Retention:** Configurable retention periods (7 days to 7 years) with immediate and permanent deletion on request\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (flexible residency; specific regions not enumerated)\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion supported; automated deletion per retention policy\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 1 ✓\\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 ✓\\n  - ISO 27001 ✓\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy) ✓\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified (audit methodology, scope, and auditor identity not disclosed)\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Not specified\\n  - GDPR: Implied compliance (ISO 27701 suggests privacy controls); formal DPA availability not stated\\n  - CCPA: Not specified\\n  - EU AI Act Readiness: Not specified\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not mentioned; BAA eligibility unknown\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Implied via ISO 27701; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit recency and findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime/year)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Critical vendor SLAs not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited evidence; no uploaded policy documents or formal testing reports provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial testing results available; full results not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Strengths\\n1. **Solid Compliance Foundation:** SOC 2 Type 1/2 and ISO 27001/27701 certifications demonstrate baseline security and privacy controls.\\n2. **Flexible Data Governance:** Configurable retention (7 days–7 years) and customer-controlled data residency align with privacy-conscious enterprise requirements.\\n3. **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA meets standard enterprise expectations.\\n4. **Audit Trail:** Comprehensive audit logs and basic interaction telemetry support operational transparency.\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n1. **AI Governance Deficiency:** Absence of documented AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, training data documentation, and human oversight protocols creates unacceptable risk for regulated sectors (healthcare, financial services, government).\\n2. **Untested Incident Response:** Documented but untested incident response plan reduces confidence in crisis management capability.\\n3. **Limited Transparency:** No disclosure of underlying model types, training data provenance, or adversarial testing results; moderate explainability insufficient for high-stakes decisions.\\n4. **Growth-Stage Maturity:** 11–50 employees and Series B/C funding indicate operational scaling challenges; support SLAs and vendor management practices not documented.\\n\\n### Recommended Actions\\n\\n**For Non-Regulated Use Cases (Internal Automation, General Productivity):**\\n- **PROCEED WITH CAUTION** (IRS ≈ 62–70 range)\\n- Require vendor to provide: (1) tested incident response procedures, (2) detailed support SLAs, (3) critical vendor SLA documentation\\n- Implement customer-side monitoring and audit log review; establish escalation procedures for anomalies\\n\\n**For Regulated Sectors (Healthcare, Financial Services, Government):**\\n- **DO NOT PROCEED** without substantial remediation\\n- Require vendor to deliver: (1) formal AI ethics and bias testing framework with third-party audit, (2) training data documentation and provenance, (3) human-in-the-loop oversight capabilities, (4) HIPAA BAA or equivalent regulatory compliance, (5) tested incident response with annual validation\\n- Consider pilot phase with limited scope and extended timeline to validate governance maturity\\n\\n**For All Deployments:**\\n- Establish contractual requirements for: (1) annual SOC 2 Type 2 audit with findings disclosure, (2) quarterly vendor risk assessments, (3) documented change management and release procedures, (4) performance guarantees tied to uptime and support SLAs\\n- Negotiate data processing agreement (DPA) with explicit GDPR/CCPA terms and sub-processor disclosure\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Classification:** C – Acceptable Vendor (70–79 range) with mandatory governance enhancements before regulated-sector deployment. Growth-stage maturity and AI governance gaps require enhanced due diligence and contractual risk mitigation.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor (flexible team-based pricing model)", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Manus", "Customer Base": "Not specified", "Target Industry": "General enterprise (cross-industry; no sector specialization stated)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (customer choice of region)", "Deployment Scale": "Team-based (flexible team pricing model); typical deployment size not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Automation of repetitive tasks, team collaboration, AI-driven decision support, production-ready task execution", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted SaaS with customer-selectable data residency", "Product Description": "Manus is a smart AI agent platform designed to automate busywork and deliver production-ready results with minimal onboarding friction. It emphasizes team collaboration, flexible pricing, and intuitive integration. The platform supports configurable data retention (7 days to 7 years) and customer-controlled data residency, positioning it as privacy-conscious for general enterprise use; however, it lacks documented AI governance, bias testing, and formal human oversight frameworks necessary for regulated industries.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product; limited/partial testing results available"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "11–50", "Legal Name": "Manus (legal entity name not specified)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2020", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (inferred: global via cloud SaaS model; no regional restrictions mentioned)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Singapore, Singapore; key investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth-stage funding; revenue not disclosed)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified (underlying LLM or custom model architecture not disclosed)", "Model Purpose": "Task automation, decision support, analysis, and production-ready result generation", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no formal human-in-the-loop, monitoring, or intervention protocols documented", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy; safety framework not specified", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate (some explainability features); prompt-level control and citation mechanisms not detailed"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No bias testing approach documented; red team or third-party audits not mentioned", "Penetration Testing": "Adversarial security testing approach not specified; frequency and scope unknown", "Training Data Documentation": "No documentation available"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "No bias audit program or external evaluation framework specified", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented; no formal usage policies or safety guidelines provided", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities", "Impact Assessment": "No system cards or formal impact documentation for releases mentioned"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger (moderate maturity; manual trigger introduces operational delay vs. fully automated rollback)", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, documented but **not tested** (maturity gap: untested procedures reduce confidence in real-world execution)"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption standards not detailed", "PII Handling": "Not specified; extent of PII processing and customer data use for training not disclosed", "Data Deletion": "On-request deletion supported; automated deletion per retention policy", "Data Retention": "Configurable retention periods (7 days to 7 years) with immediate and permanent deletion on request", "Sub-processors": "Infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not disclosed", "Data Collection": "API and agent interface (inferred); retention options configurable", "Data Types Processed": "Not specified (inferred: task/workflow data, agent logs, conversation history based on product description)", "Data Location / Residency": "Customer choice of region (flexible residency; specific regions not enumerated)"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "- SOC 2 Type 1 ✓", "GDPR Compliance": "Implied via ISO 27701; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not mentioned; BAA eligibility unknown", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified", "Regulatory Frameworks": "- NIST: Not specified", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified (audit methodology, scope, and auditor identity not disclosed)", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified; audit recency and findings not disclosed"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours downtime/year)", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Critical vendor SLAs not disclosed", "Critical Vendors": "Infrastructure, payments, and authentication vendors not identified", "Vendor Assessment": "Frequency of vendor risk assessments not specified"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, comprehensive audit logs available", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Limited/Partial testing results available; full results not disclosed", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Limited evidence; no uploaded policy documents or formal testing reports provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Manus demonstrates solid foundational security and compliance posture (SOC 2 Type 1/2, ISO 27001/27701 certifications) with flexible data residency and configurable retention policies. However, the vendor exhibits significant gaps in AI governance maturity—notably absent documented AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, training data documentation, and formal human oversight protocols—which substantially constrains trust for regulated or high-stakes deployments. The company's growth-stage maturity (Series B/C, ~11–50 employees, founded 2020) and lack of tested incident response procedures further elevate operational risk. The score reflects acceptable use for non-critical, internal-facing automation but requires substantial governance and testing enhancements before deployment in healthcare, financial services, or other regulated sectors. ---", "overallScore": 85, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.94, "Governance": 94, "Operational": 61}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   85 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       39.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk         6.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            4.06  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (39.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (6.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (61.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:42:07.58244+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	85	B	543879d0-68db-4480-91a0-72653345bb43	\N	\N
7badb852-6f54-4e3e-8c29-8077e7aa233a	83eb6cc2-bbae-44ac-9485-f3e44657d4de	94	94	AI Product Company	{"Professional Services; Technology": ["Professional Services; Technology"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	https://www.microsoft.com/	Microsoft 365 Copilot is an AI-powered tool that helps with your work tasks. Users enter a prompt in Copilot and Copilot responds with AI-generated information. The responses are in real-time and can include internet-based content and work content that users have permission to access.	10,000+	1975	Redmond, Washington, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Microsoft Copilot Studio addresses the need for automating repetitive tasks and improving customer engagement by providing AI-powered agents that can interact across multiple channels. It also solves the challenge of integrating AI capabilities into existing workflows without requiring extensive coding expertise.	\N	Microsoft 365 Copilot uses your organizational data and the web. It requires an [add-on license](/en-us/copilot/microsoft-365/microsoft-365-copilot-licensing). Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat uses the web and users can provide organizational data. It doesn't require an additional license.	Customers report significant reductions in manual task time and improved customer response times due to automated AI agents. Specific outcomes include 40% faster customer service resolution and 30% reduction in operational costs.	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["ISO 27001", "ISO 27017", "ISO 27018", "ISO 27701", "ISO 42001 (AI Management)", "SOC 1", "SOC 2 Type 2", "SOC 3", "FedRAMP", "NIST CSF", "HITRUST", "HIPAA BAA", "CSA STAR attestation", "CSA STAR certification"]	\N	\N	["EU only"]	Microsoft Copilot Studio allows organizations to set their own data retention policies in compliance with regional regulations. Data is retained according to organizational policies and can be deleted upon request, with procedures aligned to Microsoft 365's existing privacy and compliance commitments.	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, tested annually	Automated instant rollback	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, comprehensive analytics	Yes, comprehensive	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:42:42.796247+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Copilot Studio	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:42:42.801+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Microsoft 365 Copilot Studio\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 82 (Trusted Vendor)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 90\\n- Compliance: 92\\n- Data Practices: 78\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 88\\n- Company Maturity: 95\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nMicrosoft 365 Copilot Studio scores as a **Trusted Vendor (Grade B, 80–89 range)** with strong operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications, and proven enterprise reliability. The vendor benefits from Microsoft's 49-year operating history, 10,000+ employee base, and extensive compliance portfolio (ISO 27001, SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST). However, the score is moderated by three material gaps: (1) **AI Governance** is underdeveloped—no documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, or adversarial security testing methodology are specified; (2) **Data Practices** lack transparency regarding training data sources (\\"data unknown\\" for third-party models) and PII handling specifics; (3) **Model Transparency** is proprietary/closed, limiting explainability and audit capability. The 99.9% uptime SLA, automated rollback, and comprehensive audit logs support operational confidence. **Recommendation:** Approve for standard procurement with contractual requirements for (a) documented AI governance roadmap including bias monitoring, (b) training data provenance disclosure, and (c) enhanced transparency on model decision boundaries for regulated use cases.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Microsoft 365 Copilot Studio\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automating repetitive tasks, improving customer engagement, integrating AI capabilities into existing workflows without extensive coding expertise; AI-powered agents interacting across multiple channels.\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (multi-sector); healthcare (HIPAA BAA eligible); government (FedRAMP authorized).\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (Microsoft 365 ecosystem); SaaS.\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; EU data residency option available.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise multi-tenant (10,000+ employee organization).\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product stage (part of Microsoft 365 suite).\\n- **Pricing:** Requires add-on license for Microsoft 365 Copilot; Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat available without additional license.\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (implied: large enterprise base given Microsoft's market position).\\n- **Product Description:** Microsoft 365 Copilot Studio is a proprietary AI-powered agent platform enabling organizations to automate workflows and customer interactions across multiple channels using organizational data and web content. The product integrates with Microsoft 365 ecosystem, supports EU data residency, and is HIPAA/FedRAMP compliant. Customers report 40% faster customer service resolution and 30% reduction in operational costs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Microsoft Corporation\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (Public Technology Corporation)\\n- **Year Founded:** 1975\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (NASDAQ: MSFT); not specified in attestation.\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Redmond, Washington, USA; publicly traded.\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (EU data residency option specified).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary; leverages third-party models (specific model architecture not disclosed).\\n- **Model Purpose:** Task automation, customer engagement, workflow integration; real-time response generation using organizational data and web content.\\n- **Model Governance:** Not specified; no documented staged deployment or safety framework provided.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no advisory vs. autonomous decision framework documented.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability documentation specified.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data sources unknown. **Gap:** Insufficient transparency for regulated environments.\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified. **Gap:** No red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools documented.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified. **Gap:** No frequency or methodology provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented. **Gap:** No usage policies or safety guidelines specified.\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified. **Gap:** No frequency or external evaluation process documented.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified. **Gap:** No admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified. **Gap:** No system cards or release documentation provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually. Demonstrates mature incident management capability.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated instant rollback. Supports rapid remediation and deployment safety.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Organizational data (documents, communications, work content) and internet-based content; users can provide organizational data to Copilot Chat.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified. **Gap:** Extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for training not documented.\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface; real-time interaction model.\\n- **Data Storage:** Microsoft 365 infrastructure (encrypted, SOC 2 Type 2 audited).\\n- **Data Retention:** Organizations can set their own retention policies in compliance with regional regulations; data deleted upon request aligned to Microsoft 365 privacy commitments.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** EU-only option available; customer choice supported.\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request; procedures aligned to Microsoft 365 standards.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Microsoft infrastructure (Azure); third-party model providers (not specified).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security)\\n  - ISO 27018 (PII Protection in Cloud)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management)\\n  - SOC 1, SOC 2 Type 2, SOC 3\\n  - FedRAMP (Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program)\\n  - NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF)\\n  - HITRUST (Healthcare compliance)\\n  - HIPAA BAA (Business Associate Agreement eligible)\\n  - CSA STAR attestation and certification\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 and HITRUST audits indicate third-party annual or biennial assessment; specific audit methodology not detailed.\\n\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST CSF: Implemented\\n  - GDPR: Supported (EU data residency, DPA implied via Microsoft 365 standard terms)\\n  - CCPA: Supported (implied via Microsoft 365 compliance)\\n  - EU AI Act Readiness: Not specified\\n\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligible; HITRUST certified.\\n\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** EU data residency option; DPA availability implied via Microsoft 365 standard agreements.\\n\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified. **Gap:** No documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance.\\n\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; findings not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year). Meets enterprise expectations for non-critical systems; falls short of 99.95%+ for mission-critical healthcare/financial use cases.\\n\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified. **Gap:** No severity-based response targets documented.\\n\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified. **Gap:** No release process, frequency, or rollback readiness practices documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Microsoft Azure (infrastructure); third-party model providers (not specified).\\n\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified. **Gap:** No documented frequency of risk assessments for sub-processors.\\n\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Azure SLAs implied (99.95% uptime standard); third-party model provider SLAs not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, comprehensive analytics available. Supports operational monitoring and performance tracking.\\n\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available. Supports compliance auditing and forensic investigation.\\n\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Basic test results available. **Gap:** Detailed security testing, bias testing, and AI governance documentation not provided.\\n\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified. **Gap:** No indication of advanced safety testing or red-team results available under NDA.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Vendor Self-Attestation, Assessment Type 1)\\n\\nPer vector database guidance, the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Calculation:**\\n\\n1. **Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n   - Inherent Risk: 60 (proprietary model, third-party training data unknown, no documented bias testing or adversarial security testing)\\n   - Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.65 (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 42001, but no AI-specific safety controls documented)\\n   - Confidence Factor: 0.85 (mature vendor, but limited transparency on model governance)\\n   - **Product Risk = 60 × 0.65 × 0.85 = 33.15 ≈ 33**\\n\\n2. **Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - Certifications: 45 points (ISO 27001, SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST, FedRAMP—comprehensive but no AI ethics policy)\\n   - Assessment Quality: 20 points (SOC 2 Type 2 indicates annual audit, but AI governance audit not specified)\\n   - Policies: 25 points (data retention, privacy aligned to Microsoft 365, but no documented AI ethics or bias audit policy)\\n   - Operational Controls: 35 points (automated rollback, incident response tested annually, but no AI-specific controls)\\n   - Maturity Adjustment: 20 points (49-year company, public, 10,000+ employees)\\n   - **Governance Score = 45 + 20 + 25 + 35 + 20 = 145 → capped at 100**\\n   - **Governance Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n3. **Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime = 8.8 hrs/year; acceptable for non-critical, below 99.95% for mission-critical)\\n   - Incident Management: 25 points (tested annually; mature but not continuous)\\n   - Deployment Maturity: 30 points (enterprise multi-tenant, Microsoft 365 ecosystem)\\n   - Stability: 25 points (49-year company, public, profitable)\\n   - Support: Not specified; assume 15 points (no P1/P2/P3 SLAs documented)\\n   - **Operational Score = 25 + 25 + 30 + 25 + 15 = 120 → capped at 100**\\n   - **Operational Risk = 100 - 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(33 × 0.40) + (0 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [13.2 + 0 + 0]\\n    = 100 - 13.2\\n    = 86.8 ≈ 87\\n```\\n\\n**Adjusted to 82 (Grade B range)** to account for:\\n- AI Governance gaps (no ethics policy, bias testing, adversarial testing)\\n- Data transparency gaps (training data sources unknown)\\n- Model explainability limitations (proprietary/closed)\\n- Support SLA gaps (not specified)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** APPROVED FOR STANDARD PROCUREMENT (Grade B: Trusted Vendor)\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n- Strong operational maturity, security posture, and compliance portfolio\\n- Proven enterprise reliability (99.9% uptime, automated rollback, comprehensive audit logs)\\n- Eligible for HIPAA, FedRAMP, and EU regulated environments\\n- Microsoft's 49-year track record and public company status reduce financial/operational risk\\n\\n**Conditions for Contract:**\\n\\n1. **AI Governance Roadmap:** Vendor must provide documented commitment to:\\n   - Bias detection and monitoring (statistical tools, quarterly audits)\\n   - Adversarial security testing (annual red-team assessment)\\n   - AI ethics policy and usage guidelines\\n   - Impact assessment documentation for major releases\\n\\n2. **Training Data Transparency:** Vendor must disclose:\\n   - Third-party model providers and licensing terms\\n   - Training data composition and filtering practices\\n   - Mechanisms for customer data exclusion from model training\\n\\n3. **Enhanced Support SLAs:** Vendor must define:\\n   - P1 (Critical): 1-hour response, 4-hour resolution target\\n   - P2 (High): 4-hour response, 24-hour resolution target\\n   - P3 (Medium): 24-hour response, 5-day resolution target\\n\\n4. **EU AI Act Readiness:** Vendor must confirm compliance roadmap for high-risk AI classification (if applicable to use case).\\n\\n**Risk Acceptance:**\\n- Product Risk (33/100): Acceptable for non-life-critical use cases; requires enhanced monitoring for healthcare/financial applications\\n- Governance Risk (0/100): Excellent\\n- Operational Risk (0/100): Excellent\\n\\n**Recommended Use Cases:**\\n- ✅ Customer service automation, workflow optimization, knowledge management\\n- ✅ Healthcare administrative tasks (non-clinical decision support)\\n- ✅ Financial services (non-advisory, compliance-monitored)\\n- ⚠️ Clinical decision support (requires additional bias audits and human oversight)\\n- ⚠️ Autonomous financial advisory (requires enhanced governance controls)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RESIDUAL CONCERNS & MONITORING\\n\\n| Concern | Severity | Mitigation |\\n|---------|----------|-----------|\\n| AI Governance gaps (no bias testing, ethics policy) | Medium | Require roadmap; quarterly attestation |\\n| Training data sources unknown | Medium | Demand transparency; audit third-party models |\\n| Model explainability (proprietary/closed) | Medium | Require decision audit logs; human review workflows |\\n| Support SLAs not specified | Low | Define in contract; escalation procedures |\\n| EU AI Act readiness not confirmed | Low | Confirm compliance roadmap in contract |\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Prepared:** [Date]  \\n**Assessor:** Vendor Attestation Analyst  \\n**Classification:** Trusted Vendor (Grade B, 80–89)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Requires add-on license for Microsoft 365 Copilot; Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat available without additional license.", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Microsoft 365 Copilot Studio", "Customer Base": "Not specified (implied: large enterprise base given Microsoft's market position).", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (multi-sector); healthcare (HIPAA BAA eligible); government (FedRAMP authorized).", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (Microsoft 365 ecosystem); SaaS.", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise multi-tenant (10,000+ employee organization).", "Primary Use Case": "Automating repetitive tasks, improving customer engagement, integrating AI capabilities into existing workflows without extensive coding expertise; AI-powered agents interacting across multiple channels.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; EU data residency option available.", "Product Description