ntation": "Using third-party models; training data sources unknown. **Gap:** Insufficient transparency for regulated environments."}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Not specified. **Gap:** No frequency or external evaluation process documented.", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented. **Gap:** No usage policies or safety guidelines specified.", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not specified. **Gap:** No admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented.", "Impact Assessment": "Not specified. **Gap:** No system cards or release documentation provided."}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated instant rollback. Supports rapid remediation and deployment safety.", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, tested annually. Demonstrates mature incident management capability."}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Microsoft 365 infrastructure (encrypted, SOC 2 Type 2 audited).", "PII Handling": "Not specified. **Gap:** Extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for training not documented.", "Data Deletion": "On request; procedures aligned to Microsoft 365 standards.", "Data Retention": "Organizations can set their own retention policies in compliance with regional regulations; data deleted upon request aligned to Microsoft 365 privacy commitments.", "Sub-processors": "Microsoft infrastructure (Azure); third-party model providers (not specified).", "Data Collection": "API and chat interface; real-time interaction model.", "Data Types Processed": "Organizational data (documents, communications, work content) and internet-based content; users can provide organizational data to Copilot Chat.", "Data Location / Residency": "EU-only option available; customer choice supported."}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "- ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)", "GDPR Compliance": "EU data residency option; DPA availability implied via Microsoft 365 standard agreements.", "HIPAA Compliance": "BAA eligible; HITRUST certified.", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified. **Gap:** No documented engagement or preparation for EU AI Act compliance.", "Regulatory Frameworks": "- NIST CSF: Implemented", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "SOC 2 Type 2 and HITRUST audits indicate third-party annual or biennial assessment; specific audit methodology not detailed.", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Frequency not specified; last audit date not provided; findings not disclosed."}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year). Meets enterprise expectations for non-critical systems; falls short of 99.95%+ for mission-critical healthcare/financial use cases.", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified. **Gap:** No release process, frequency, or rollback readiness practices documented.", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified. **Gap:** No severity-based response targets documented."}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Azure SLAs implied (99.95% uptime standard); third-party model provider SLAs not specified.", "Critical Vendors": "Microsoft Azure (infrastructure); third-party model providers (not specified).", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified. **Gap:** No documented frequency of risk assessments for sub-processors."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, comprehensive audit logs available. Supports compliance auditing and forensic investigation.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, comprehensive analytics available. Supports operational monitoring and performance tracking.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not specified. **Gap:** No indication of advanced safety testing or red-team results available under NDA.", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Basic test results available. **Gap:** Detailed security testing, bias testing, and AI governance documentation not provided."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Microsoft 365 Copilot Studio scores as a **Trusted Vendor (Grade B, 80–89 range)** with strong operational maturity, comprehensive security certifications, and proven enterprise reliability. The vendor benefits from Microsoft's 49-year operating history, 10,000+ employee base, and extensive compliance portfolio (ISO 27001, SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, HIPAA BAA, HITRUST). However, the score is moderated by three material gaps: (1) **AI Governance** is underdeveloped—no documented AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, or adversarial security testing methodology are specified; (2) **Data Practices** lack transparency regarding training data sources (\\"data unknown\\" for third-party models) and PII handling specifics; (3) **Model Transparency** is proprietary/closed, limiting explainability and audit capability. The 99.9% uptime SLA, automated rollback, and comprehensive audit logs support operational confidence. **Recommendation:** Approve for standard procurement with contractual requirements for (a) documented AI governance roadmap including bias monitoring, (b) training data provenance disclosure, and (c) enhanced transparency on model decision boundaries for regulated use cases. ---", "overallScore": 88, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 97.12, "Governance": 100, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   88 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Product risk            2.88  (weight 40%)\\n    3. Governance risk         0.00  (weight 30%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Product risk (2.9) - mitigations, domain coverage, evidence quality\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:42:42.796247+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	88	B	de01c87c-0440-4992-b6aa-e0a8fb3228d5	\N	\N
43dd6e8a-cd49-46fa-b6c3-a7d5bcc5af5b	41e1ecaa-0587-4566-b335-94c7b5f6740e	96	96	AI Product Company	{"Technology; Marketing; Professional Services": ["Technology; Marketing; Professional Services"]}	Startup (Seed/Series A)	https://monica.im	All-in-one AI assistant. Personalized, fast and free.\n\nMonica leverages cutting-edge AI models, including GPT-5, Claude 4.5 Sonnet, Gemini 3 Pro, Google Nano-Banana, Sora 2, and GPT o4-mini to enhance your chat, search, writing, image generation, video generation and coding experiences. Available as a browser extension for Chrome and Edge, as well as a mobile and desktop app.	01-Oct	2015	Montreal, Canada	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CDO/Head of Data Science", "VP Product"]	Monica addresses the need for efficient and personalized AI assistance across multiple tasks such as chat, search, writing, and coding. It helps users save time by automating repetitive tasks and enhancing productivity. Additionally, it provides a seamless integration across browser extensions and mobile/desktop apps, ensuring accessibility and convenience.	\N	Monica leverages cutting-edge AI models, including GPT-5, Claude 4.5 Sonnet, Gemini 3 Pro, Google Nano-Banana, Sora 2, and GPT o4-mini to enhance your chat, search, writing, image generation, video generation and coding experiences.	Save 90% of your time by instantly summarizing web pages and videos. [Corroborated by 7 evidence point(s): Time Saved: 2,200+; Snippets Used: 216,000; Cancel Deflection Rate: 2X; Silent Churn: Eliminated; Email Course Conversion Rate: 44%]	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["None Currently"]	\N	\N	["US only"]	Data is securely deleted within 30 days after contract completion or earlier upon request. [monicoai.com](https://monicoai.com/en/security/)	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:45:03.95869+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Monica	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:45:03.962+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: MONICA\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 38 (Low)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 15\\n- Data Practices: 45\\n- AI Governance: 20\\n- Operations: 60\\n- Company Maturity: 25\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nMonica presents a **low-trust profile** suitable only for non-regulated, low-stakes use cases. While the product offers attractive consumer features (multi-model AI access, time savings) and maintains basic operational reliability (99.9% SLA), critical gaps in governance, compliance, and security posture create unacceptable risk for enterprise or regulated deployments. The vendor lacks security certifications, formal AI governance policies, bias testing, adversarial security testing, and any independent compliance audits. The startup maturity (founded 2015 but seed/Series A stage, ~10 employees) and absence of enterprise-grade controls (no SOC 2, no HIPAA BAA, no formal incident response testing) mean this product is fundamentally unsuitable for healthcare, financial services, government, or any data-sensitive workload. Strengths include transparent data retention (30-day deletion) and basic logging; however, these do not offset the absence of foundational security and governance infrastructure required for enterprise trust.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Monica\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-assisted productivity across chat, search, writing, image generation, video generation, and coding tasks; consumer and SMB productivity enhancement.\\n- **Target Industry:** General consumer and SMB; not positioned for regulated industries (healthcare, financial services, government).\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Browser extension (Chrome, Edge), mobile app, desktop app\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Individual/team consumer use; not designed for enterprise multi-tenant deployment\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Early-stage product; no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Free (freemium model implied; premium tiers not detailed)\\n- **Customer Base:** 7 evidence points cited (2,200+ time saved metrics, 216,000 snippets used, 2X cancel deflection, 44% email course conversion); specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Monica is an all-in-one AI assistant available as a browser extension and mobile/desktop app, leveraging multiple third-party AI models (GPT-5, Claude 4.5 Sonnet, Gemini 3 Pro, Sora 2, etc.) to automate writing, coding, search, and content generation tasks. The product emphasizes convenience and time savings but lacks enterprise security controls, compliance certifications, and formal AI governance. Data is retained in the US only and deleted within 30 days of contract completion.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Monica (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (SaaS)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** ~10 (stated as \\"01-Oct,\\" interpreted as 1–10 range)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (specific revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Montreal, Canada; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; data residency limited to US only\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Multi-model architecture: GPT-5, Claude 4.5 Sonnet, Gemini 3 Pro, Google Nano-Banana, Sora 2, GPT o4-mini (third-party models, not proprietary)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Chat, search enhancement, writing assistance, image generation, video generation, coding support\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy; safety framework not specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or human-in-the-loop intervention\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Model transparency is proprietary/closed; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models; training data documentation unknown and not provided by vendor\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No adversarial security testing conducted; no frequency or type specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy; usage policies and safety guidelines not provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring programs mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level unclear and untested plans carry high execution risk\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; capability exists but testing/validation status unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Chat interactions, search queries, writing content, code snippets, image/video generation prompts; scope of data collection not fully detailed\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no documentation on extent of PII processing or whether customer data is used for training\\n- **Data Collection:** API, chat interface, browser extension, mobile/desktop apps; collection scope not fully documented\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Default 30-day deletion after contract completion; earlier deletion on request available\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only; no multi-region or customer-choice options\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated after 30 days or on-request deletion available\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure, payments, authentication providers not identified; third-party model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google) are implicit but not formally listed as sub-processors\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently** (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other security/compliance certifications)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits conducted\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No documented alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act; readiness not assessed\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable; no BAA eligibility\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not documented; no Data Processing Agreement (DPA) mentioned\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; no engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audits conducted; no audit history\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime); contractual commitment level not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no release process, frequency, or rollback/readiness practices documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Third-party AI model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google) are implicit dependencies; infrastructure provider not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment frequency documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No SLAs from critical vendors documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available (2,200+ time saved, 216,000 snippets used, 2X cancel deflection, 44% conversion); scope limited\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and SIEM integration not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; no policy documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing results available; no NDA-protected testing data offered\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n### Key Risk Factors (Applied to Vendor Trust Score Formula)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Self-Attestation (VTS)** formula from the vector database:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 95/100 (third-party models, no training data transparency, no bias testing, no adversarial testing)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.15 (minimal controls; no certifications, no formal governance, no safety testing)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.50 (no independent audits, basic logging only)\\n- **Product Risk: 71/100** (high residual risk due to lack of safety controls and transparency)\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 0 points (none)\\n- Assessment Quality: 0 points (no independent audits)\\n- Policies: 5 points (incident response documented but untested; no ethics, data governance, or AI governance policies)\\n- Operational Controls: 8 points (rollback capability exists; no monitoring, oversight, or version control documented)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 0 points (startup stage, ~10 employees, seed/Series A funding)\\n- **Governance Risk: 85/100** (critical gaps in formal governance infrastructure)\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime = acceptable but not enterprise-grade; 8.8 hrs/year downtime)\\n- Incident Management: 5 points (documented but untested; no automation or testing evidence)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 10 points (consumer/SMB SaaS; not enterprise multi-tenant)\\n- Stability: 8 points (startup, ~10 employees, seed/Series A; limited financial stability evidence)\\n- Support: 0 points (no support SLAs documented)\\n- **Operational Risk: 52/100** (moderate operational maturity; startup instability and lack of enterprise support)\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n- VTS = 100 − [(71 × 0.40) + (85 × 0.30) + (52 × 0.30)]\\n- VTS = 100 − [28.4 + 25.5 + 15.6]\\n- VTS = 100 − 69.5\\n- **VTS = 30.5 ≈ 31** (rounded; **F-grade: Review Required**)\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**REJECT FOR ENTERPRISE / REGULATED USE**\\n\\nMonica is **unsuitable for any regulated industry** (healthcare, financial services, government) or data-sensitive workload. The product is appropriate **only for consumer/SMB productivity use** where data sensitivity is low and regulatory compliance is not required.\\n\\n**Blockers:**\\n1. **No security certifications** (SOC 2, ISO 27001)\\n2. **No compliance certifications** (HIPAA, GDPR, FedRAMP)\\n3. **No formal AI governance** (ethics policy, bias testing, adversarial testing)\\n4. **Untested incident response** (documented but not validated)\\n5. **Startup maturity** (~10 employees, seed/Series A; limited financial stability)\\n6. **No independent audits** (no third-party validation of security or compliance claims)\\n7. **Third-party model dependency** (training data unknown; no transparency on model safety)\\n\\n**Acceptable Use Cases:**\\n- Individual consumer productivity (writing, coding, search assistance)\\n- SMB internal productivity tools (non-regulated, non-sensitive data)\\n- Pilot/proof-of-concept only (with explicit data minimization and no PII)\\n\\n**If Vendor Wishes to Pursue Enterprise Sales:**\\n1. Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 certification (minimum 6-month audit cycle)\\n2. Conduct independent third-party AI safety and bias audit\\n3. Develop and operationalize formal AI governance policy (ethics, bias monitoring, human oversight)\\n4. Implement and test incident response plan (annual testing required)\\n5. Provide HIPAA BAA and GDPR DPA for regulated use cases\\n6. Document training data provenance and bias testing for all third-party models\\n7. Expand support SLAs and incident management capabilities to enterprise grade\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (basic data provided; significant gaps in documentation)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Free (freemium model implied; premium tiers not detailed)", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Monica", "Customer Base": "7 evidence points cited (2,200+ time saved metrics, 216,000 snippets used, 2X cancel deflection, 44% email course conversion); specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "General consumer and SMB; not positioned for regulated industries (healthcare, financial services, government).", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Individual/team consumer use; not designed for enterprise multi-tenant deployment", "Primary Use Case": "AI-assisted productivity across chat, search, writing, image generation, video generation, and coding tasks; consumer and SMB productivity enhancement.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Browser extension (Chrome, Edge), mobile app, desktop app", "Product Description": "Monica is an all-in-one AI assistant available as a browser extension and mobile/desktop app, leveraging multiple third-party AI models (GPT-5, Claude 4.5 Sonnet, Gemini 3 Pro, Sora 2, etc.) to automate writing, coding, search, and content generation tasks. The product emphasizes convenience and time savings but lacks enterprise security controls, compliance certifications, and formal AI governance. Data is retained in the US only and deleted within 30 days of contract completion.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Early-stage product; no formal testing conduc