ring, with automatic deletion after this period unless legally required otherwise. Customers can request earlier deletion or Zero Data Retention (ZDR) for eligible endpoints. For ChatGPT (consumer-facing), conversations are retained by default and may be used for model improvement unless users opt out or delete their chat history.	\N	\N	\N	Partial documentation available	No SLA	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:49:18.419514+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Codex	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:49:18.427+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## OpenAI – Codex\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 72 (Moderate-High)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 85\\n- Compliance: 82\\n- Data Practices: 68\\n- AI Governance: 65\\n- Operations: 60\\n- Company Maturity: 88\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nOpenAI Codex demonstrates strong security certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, PCI DSS) and established company maturity (founded 2015, 5,001–10,000 employees, profitable 3+ years), positioning it as a credible enterprise vendor. However, the trust score is moderated by gaps in operational transparency (no contractual uptime SLA, undocumented support response SLAs, untested incident response), incomplete AI governance documentation (no published ethics policy or bias testing methodology), and data practice constraints (30-day default retention, limited zero-data-retention options, and unclear PII handling for code inputs). The score reflects a vendor with strong foundational security and compliance posture but incomplete operational maturity and governance transparency required for high-trust enterprise deployments in regulated sectors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** OpenAI Codex\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Automated code generation, bug fixes, code review automation, codebase understanding and debugging, multi-agent task orchestration\\n- **Target Industry:** Software development, enterprise engineering teams\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (OpenAI-managed SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted only; no on-premises or customer-hosted deployment options stated\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale; supports parallel task processing and multi-agent orchestration for large development teams\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product with production deployments (customer examples: Cisco, Carlyle)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Notable customers include Cisco and Carlyle; specific customer count not disclosed\\n- **Product Description:** OpenAI Codex is an AI-powered code automation platform that reduces development cycle time by 30–50% through automated bug fixes, code reviews, and multi-agent task orchestration. It features sandboxed execution for secure operations and \\"Computer Use\\" capability for deep desktop application interaction. The product is built on OpenAI's foundation models with full transparency and operates under SOC 2 Type 2, FedRAMP, and ISO 27001 compliance frameworks.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** OpenAI (legal entity not specified; assume OpenAI, Inc. or subsidiary)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company (research and deployment)\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 5,001–10,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Profitable 3+ years (Series D+ or later; specific revenue not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; key investors not specified in attestation\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not enumerated; data residency options available by customer choice)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Foundation models (LLM-based); specific model architecture not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Code understanding, generation, analysis, and autonomous task execution; multi-agent orchestration and parallel processing\\n- **Model Governance:** Sandboxed execution environment for secure operations; staged deployment capability implied but not explicitly documented\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; unclear whether code generation outputs require human review, approval workflows, or audit trails before execution\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Full Transparency (open weights, explainable); model decisions and reasoning available for audit\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Partial documentation available; complete training data lineage, composition, and bias characteristics not fully disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Bias testing approach not specified; no mention of red-team exercises, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring for code generation outputs\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Adversarial security testing approach not documented; frequency and scope unknown\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Documented AI governance policy not specified; no published ethics guidelines, acceptable use policy, or safety guardrails for code generation disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** Bias audit frequency and external evaluation methodology not stated\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Human oversight mechanisms not specified; unclear whether code generation requires approval, review workflows, or intervention capabilities\\n- **Impact Assessment:** System cards or release documentation not mentioned; no evidence of pre-deployment impact assessments for code generation features\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested; formal incident response procedures exist but lack evidence of tabletop exercises, drills, or third-party validation\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedures are in place and can be executed manually when needed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Source code, code snippets, development artifacts, and potentially PII embedded in code comments or strings\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; unclear whether PII detection, masking, or exclusion mechanisms are implemented for code inputs\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based integration; data collected via OpenAI API endpoints for Codex\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure not specified; assumed OpenAI-managed cloud infrastructure (AWS/Azure/GCP not confirmed)\\n- **Data Retention:** Default 30-day retention for API inputs/outputs for abuse monitoring; automatic deletion after 30 days unless legally required; Zero Data Retention (ZDR) available for eligible endpoints (eligibility criteria not specified)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region; specific regions available not enumerated\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automatic deletion after 30-day retention window; on-request deletion available; ZDR option available for eligible use cases\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider(s) not specified; payment processing and authentication providers not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2\\n  - SOC 3\\n  - ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)\\n  - ISO 27017 (Cloud Security)\\n  - ISO 27018 (PII Protection in Cloud)\\n  - ISO 27701 (Privacy Information Management)\\n  - ISO 42001 (AI Management Systems)\\n  - FedRAMP (Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program)\\n  - PCI DSS (Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard)\\n  - GDPR Compliant\\n  - CCPA Compliant\\n  - CSA STAR Level 1 (Cloud Security Alliance)\\n\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; audit methodology, scope, and auditor identity not disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST (implied via FedRAMP); GDPR and CCPA compliance stated; EU AI Act readiness not mentioned\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not stated; no BAA (Business Associate Agreement) mentioned\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** GDPR Compliant stated; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not mentioned; no engagement or preparation status disclosed\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; audit recency and findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** No SLA; no contractual uptime commitment stated\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response times by severity not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, change approval process, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider(s) not specified; payment processing and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Vendor risk assessment frequency not stated\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Critical vendor SLAs not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity of telemetry not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, audit logs available; export capability and retention period not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Testing results available; specific test coverage, methodologies, and policy documents not enumerated\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, available under NDA; scope of testing (bias, adversarial, safety) and NDA terms not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Strengths\\n\\n1. **Enterprise Security & Compliance:** Comprehensive certifications (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, PCI DSS) demonstrate mature security controls and regulatory alignment.\\n2. **Company Maturity & Stability:** Established vendor (founded 2015, 5,001–10,000 employees, profitable 3+ years) with proven market presence and financial stability.\\n3. **Model Transparency:** Full transparency and explainability support auditability and regulatory compliance.\\n4. **Proven ROI:** Customer case studies (Cisco, Carlyle) demonstrate measurable productivity gains (30–50% reduction in development time).\\n5. **Data Residency & Retention Options:** Customer choice of data region and Zero Data Retention (ZDR) option support data sovereignty and privacy requirements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Gaps & Risks\\n\\n1. **No Uptime SLA:** Absence of contractual uptime commitment creates risk for mission-critical development workflows; no recourse for service unavailability.\\n2. **Incomplete AI Governance:** No published ethics policy, bias testing methodology, or human-in-the-loop controls documented; unclear safety guardrails for code generation.\\n3. **Untested Incident Response:** Incident response plan exists but lacks evidence of testing, drills, or third-party validation; response effectiveness unknown.\\n4. **Limited PII Handling Clarity:** No documented PII detection or masking for code inputs; risk of sensitive data exposure in code comments or strings.\\n5. **Partial Training Data Documentation:** Training data composition, bias characteristics, and potential code-specific biases not fully disclosed.\\n6. **No Support SLAs:** Support response times not contractually defined; support quality and responsiveness unknown.\\n7. **HIPAA & EU AI Act Gaps:** No HIPAA BAA or EU AI Act readiness mentioned; limits use in healthcare and regulated EU deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT**\\n\\nOpenAI Codex is suitable for enterprise software development teams in non-regulated sectors with mature security and compliance requirements. Recommended actions:\\n\\n1. **Require SLA Addendum:** Negotiate contractual uptime SLA (minimum 99.5%) and support response SLAs (P1: 1 hour, P2: 4 hours, P3: 24 hours).\\n2. **AI Governance Documentation:** Request published ethics policy, bias testing results, and human-in-the-loop control specifications before deployment.\\n3. **Incident Response Validation:** Request evidence of incident response testing (tabletop exercises, drills) or third-party validation.\\n4. **PII Handling Assessment:** Clarify PII detection, masking, and exclusion mechanisms for code inputs; confirm data residency for sensitive code.\\n5. **Pilot Deployment:** Conduct 90-day pilot with non-critical development workloads to validate performance, support quality, and integration fit.\\n6. **Regulatory Alignment:** If HIPAA or EU AI Act compliance required, defer procurement until vendor confirms BAA eligibility and EU AI Act readiness.\\n\\n**Not Recommended For:**\\n- Healthcare or life-sciences organizations (no HIPAA BAA)\\n- EU-regulated deployments (EU AI Act readiness not confirmed)\\n- Mission-critical systems without uptime SLA", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "OpenAI Codex", "Customer Base": "Notable customers include Cisco and Carlyle; specific customer count not disclosed", "Target Industry": "Software development, enterprise engineering teams", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (OpenAI-managed SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise-scale; supports parallel task processing and multi-agent orchestration for large development teams", "Primary Use Case": "Automated code generation, bug fixes, code review automation, codebase understanding and debugging, multi-agent task orchestration", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted only; no on-premises or customer-hosted deployment options stated", "Product Description": "OpenAI Codex is an AI-powered code automation platform that reduces development cycle time by 30–50% through automated bug fixes, code reviews, and multi-agent task orchestration. It features sandboxed execution for secure operations and \\"Computer Us