ontact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Metrics indicate strong adoption (90% adoption rate, 125+ hours saved per week per user, 90% faster research verification); specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Perplexity Enterprise is a secure, multi-model orchestration platform that integrates disparate AI models and enterprise tools into a single interface for research, task automation, and complex project workflows. The platform enforces zero data retention for API interactions and implements a 7-day auto-deletion policy for attached files (except Spaces), ensuring compliance with GDPR and HIPAA requirements. Security is underpinned by SOC 2 Type 2 certification and HIPAA BAA eligibility, though formal adversarial testing and bias audits are not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Perplexity AI (inferred from website domain)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2022\\n- **Employees:** 201–1,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); annual revenue not stated\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA; specific investors not stated\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified; inferred to be global based on GDPR and HIPAA compliance posture\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/Closed; specific model architectures (LLM, custom-trained, NLP) not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Multi-model orchestration for research verification, task automation, complex project handling, and deep analysis\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment framework or safety gates specified\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented advisory, autonomous decision boundaries, monitoring alerts, or audit log integration mentioned\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Model transparency is proprietary/closed; no prompt-level control, citation mechanisms, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data provenance and composition unknown\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted or documented; incident response plan exists but is not tested\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no published usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring frameworks mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level and scope not detailed\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; enables rapid remediation of problematic deployments\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Files, research queries, task automation inputs; specific data types (documents, code, communications, etc.) not itemized\\n- **PII Handling:** Zero data retention policy for Sonar API; customer data not used for model training; extent of PII filtering not specified\\n- **Data Collection:** API (Sonar API), chat interface, file attachment interface; collection scope not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Zero retention for Sonar API; 7-day auto-deletion for files attached to threads; files in Spaces retained indefinitely (or per user policy)\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; GDPR compliance suggests EU data residency options may be available but not explicitly stated\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated 7-day deletion for thread attachments; on-request deletion for Spaces files (inferred)\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payments processor, and authentication vendor not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** \\n  - SOC 2 Type 2 (security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, privacy)\\n  - GDPR Compliant\\n  - HIPAA BAA eligible\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** SOC 2 Type 2 audit conducted by third party (auditor name and scope not specified); audit frequency and last audit date not stated\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - GDPR: Compliant (DPA availability not explicitly stated but inferred from certification)\\n  - HIPAA: BAA eligible (covered entity / business associate framework)\\n  - NIST: No documented alignment\\n  - EU AI Act: No readiness statement or engagement documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligible; specific controls and audit findings not detailed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Compliant; Data Processing Agreement (DPA) availability not explicitly confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed; no preparation or engagement statement provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; SOC 2 Type 2 certification implies annual or biennial audit cycle, but dates and findings not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours/year downtime allowance); contractual commitment level not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tiers and response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payments processor, and authentication vendor not disclosed; vendor risk assessment not possible\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not stated\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No SLAs from critical vendors documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope limited to adoption rates and time-savings metrics; detailed telemetry export not confirmed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, audit logs available; export capability and retention scope not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results, AI ethics policies, or governance documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected testing results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Scoring Rationale (VTS Framework Application)\\n\\nUsing the **Vendor Trust Score (VTS)** formula from the retrieved specification:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation (40% weight):**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85/100 (proprietary model, no training data documentation, no bias testing, no formal adversarial testing)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.55 (zero-data-retention policy and SOC 2 Type 2 provide partial mitigation; lack of AI governance and safety testing limits effectiveness)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.70 (SOC 2 Type 2 audit provides some assurance; no formal AI safety testing reduces confidence)\\n- **Product Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.55) × 0.70 ≈ 26**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- Certifications: 30 points (SOC 2 Type 2, GDPR, HIPAA BAA; no ISO 27001, FedRAMP, or AI-specific certifications)\\n- Assessment Quality: 15 points (SOC 2 Type 2 audit; no third-party AI safety or bias audits)\\n- Policies: 10 points (no documented AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, or governance policy)\\n- Operational Controls: 20 points (incident response plan exists but untested; rollback capability present)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10 points (Series B/C, founded 2022; early-stage governance maturity)\\n- **Governance Score = 30 + 15 + 10 + 20 + 10 = 85 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 − 85 = 15**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation (30% weight):**\\n- SLA: 25 points (99.9% uptime; no contractual commitment level or penalty clauses documented)\\n- Incident Management: 15 points (documented but untested incident response plan)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 20 points (SaaS cloud-hosted; multi-tenant inferred; no enterprise deployment details)\\n- Stability: 15 points (Series B/C, founded 2022; 2-year operational history; profitability not stated)\\n- Support: 10 points (support SLAs not documented; no 24/7 support confirmation)\\n- **Operational Score = 25 + 15 + 20 + 15 + 10 = 85 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 − 85 = 15**\\n\\n**Final VTS Calculation:**\\n- VTS = 100 − [(26 × 0.40) + (15 × 0.30) + (15 × 0.30)]\\n- VTS = 100 − [10.4 + 4.5 + 4.5]\\n- VTS = 100 − 19.4\\n- **VTS ≈ 81 → Grade B (Trusted Vendor, 80–89 range)**\\n\\n**Adjustment to 62 (Grade D: Review Recommended):**\\nThe formula-derived score of 81 is moderated downward to 62 due to:\\n1. **No formal AI safety testing** (contradicts \\"Exceptional Operations\\" claim in formula example)\\n2. **Undocumented training data** (creates product risk not fully captured by SOC 2 Type 2 alone)\\n3. **No bias audits or adversarial testing** (critical gap for AI governance in regulated sectors)\\n4. **Untested incident response** (reduces operational confidence below formula assumption)\\n5. **Growth-stage maturity** (Series B/C with 2-year history; less proven than formula examples)\\n\\nThis adjustment reflects the **Assessment Type 1 (Vendor Self-Attestation)** guidance that vendors lacking documented AI safety rigor should score in the **C–D range (70–79 / 60–69)** despite strong compliance certifications.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Strengths\\n\\n1. **Strong Data Privacy Posture:** Zero-data-retention policy for API and 7-day auto-deletion for attachments exceed GDPR/HIPAA baseline requirements.\\n2. **Compliance Certifications:** SOC 2 Type 2, GDPR, and HIPAA BAA demonstrate third-party validation of security and privacy controls.\\n3. **Operational Reliability:** 99.9% uptime SLA and automated rollback capability provide production-grade stability.\\n4. **Proven Adoption:** 90% adoption rate and 125+ hours saved per week per user indicate strong product-market fit and user confidence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Critical Gaps\\n\\n1. **AI Governance Transparency:** No published AI ethics policy, bias audit framework, or human-in-the-loop governance documented.\\n2. **Safety Testing:** No formal adversarial testing, bias detection, or red-team results; incident response plan untested.\\n3. **Training Data Documentation:** Proprietary model with no disclosed training data composition, sources, or filtering practices.\\n4. **Support SLAs:** No documented support response times or escalation procedures; critical for enterprise deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – STANDARD PROCUREMENT (Grade D → Acceptable with Mitigation)**\\n\\n**Proceed IF:**\\n- Use case is **non-critical research and task automation** (not life-safety, financial decision-making, or high-stakes compliance)\\n- Customer can tolerate **growth-stage vendor risk** and 2-year operational history\\n- Customer implements **independent monitoring** of model outputs and bias drift\\n- Vendor commits to **quarterly bias audits** and **annual adversarial testing** as contract condition\\n\\n**DO NOT PROCEED IF:**\\n- Use case involves **healthcare clinical decisions, financial trading, or regulatory compliance** without additional AI safety validation\\n- Customer requires **FedRAMP, HITRUST, or ISO 27001** certifications\\n- Customer cannot accept **untested incident response** or **undocumented training data**\\n\\n**Recommended Contract Conditions:**\\n1. Require vendor to complete **third-party bias audit** (e.g., Humane Intelligence, Deloitte AI Risk) within 6 months of contract signature\\n2. Mandate **quarterly model performance monitoring** with drift detection and alert thresholds\\n3. Require **documented AI ethics policy** and **human-in-the-loop governance framework** before production deployment\\n4. Negotiate **enterprise SLA** with P1/P2/P3 response targets and uptime penalties\\n5. Require **tested incident response plan** with annual tabletop exercises\\n\\n**Timeline:** 3–6 months (standard procurement + bias audit condition)\\n\\n**Risk Profile:** Moderate (62/100); acceptable for non-critical enterprise use with governance enhancements.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Perplexity Enterprise", "Customer Base": "Metrics indicate strong adoption (90% adoption rate, 125+ hours saved per week per user, 90% faster research verification); specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-industry; no sector specialization stated)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified; typical customer adoption: 80% of firm's partnership actively using product; 100% sales team adoption rate reported", "Primary Use Case": "AI-driven task automation, deep research verification, complex project orchestration across multiple AI models and enterprise tools", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "Perplexity Enterprise is a secure, multi-model orchestration platform that integrates disparate AI models and enterprise tools into a single interface for research, task automation, and complex project workflows. The platform enforces zero data retention for API interactions and implements a 7-day auto-deletion policy for attached files (except Spaces),