 vendors (identity not disclosed); infrastructure provider (not specified). **Gap:** No vendor risk assessment or SLA documentation.", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; no frequency of vendor risk assessments or sub-processor audits documented."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available. **Gap:** No evidence of comprehensive SIEM integration, real-time alerting, or export capability for security investigations.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available. Scope and granularity not specified; likely limited to operational metrics (uptime, request volume) rather than AI safety telemetry.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "No formal testing conducted. **Critical gap:** Absence of red team, adversarial testing, bias audits, or safety validation under any confidentiality arrangement.", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "No formal testing results, policy documentation, or governance artifacts uploaded or referenced."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** ClickUp Brain receives a **Moderate trust score (52/100)**, placing it in the **\\"Review Recommended\\"** category (60–69 range per the rubric). The vendor demonstrates solid operational maturity (established company, 99.9% SLA, automated rollback) and reasonable company stability (Series D+, profitable 3+ years), but faces **significant gaps in AI governance, compliance documentation, and safety testing** that are critical for enterprise deployment. The vendor has not conducted formal AI safety testing, lacks documented AI governance policies, provides minimal compliance certifications (NIST CSF only), and relies on third-party models with unknown training data provenance. While ClickUp's core project management platform is mature, **ClickUp Brain (the AI-enabled variant) lacks the governance rigor, transparency, and independent validation required for high-trust enterprise use**—particularly in regulated industries (healthcare, finance) or high-stakes decision contexts. **Key Drivers:**", "overallScore": 83, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.11, "Governance": 86, "Operational": 61}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   83 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       39.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        14.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.89  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (39.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (14.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (61.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:48:32.876279+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	83	B	1a503d7b-f1e6-4386-b1f6-8f1ca43a5007	\N	\N
59feaf87-0353-4cea-8dac-32d4a8701abf	e9eca768-acf7-4952-bdfe-5e9c7b64eb74	57	57	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Educational Institutions; Media & Entertainment; Technology": ["Educational Institutions; Media & Entertainment; Technology"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	https://help.clipchamp.com	Clipchamp is a video editing platform with features like trim and cut videos, green screen video editor, auto subtitle generator, special effects and filters, and realistic AI voiceovers for video.	10,000+	2014	Brisbane, Queensland, Australia	\N	\N	\N	\N	["Line of Business Leader", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Clipchamp addresses the need for easy-to-use, professional-grade video editing tools without requiring advanced technical skills. It also solves the problem of high costs associated with traditional video editing software by offering a cloud-based, subscription-free model. Additionally, it provides AI-powered features like auto subtitles and voiceovers to save time and enhance video quality.	\N	Clipchamp stands out with its AI-powered features like auto subtitle generation and realistic AI voiceovers, which are not commonly found in free or low-cost video editors. It also offers a seamless integration with Microsoft 365, making it ideal for enterprise users. Additionally, its web-based platform eliminates the need for high-end hardware, making it accessible to a broader audience.	Users report significant time savings with AI-powered features like auto subtitles, reducing manual editing time by up to 50%. The platform's ease of use also reduces the learning curve, enabling faster video production cycles. [Corroborated by 6 evidence point(s): Cost Savings: $1,500; Lift In Winback: 600%; Time Saved: 20 seconds; Availability: 99.99%; Time Saved: Several hours]	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["None Currently"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region"]	Clipchamp stores video projects on OneDrive or SharePoint for collaboration, and user videos can be synced to the cloud via Google Cloud Platform. Retention policies are likely aligned with Microsoft's and Google's standard practices, but specific durations are not disclosed.	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	99.99% (52 min/year downtime)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:50:05.589117+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Clipchamp	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:50:05.59+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: CLIPCHAMP\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 58 (Moderate – Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 45\\n- Compliance: 25\\n- Data Practices: 52\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 72\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nClipchamp receives a moderate trust score reflecting strong operational maturity (10+ years, 10,000+ employees, 99.99% uptime) and established company stability, offset by significant gaps in AI governance, compliance certifications, and security posture. The vendor lacks formal security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA), documented AI governance policies, bias testing frameworks, and formal penetration testing—critical gaps for enterprise deployments handling user-generated video content and personal data. While the platform demonstrates reliable operations and basic audit logging, the absence of independent compliance audits, formal incident response testing, and transparent AI model documentation creates residual risk. The vendor is suitable for general-purpose video editing but requires substantial governance and security enhancements before deployment in regulated industries (healthcare, finance) or handling sensitive PII at scale.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Clipchamp\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Cloud-based video editing for enterprise and consumer users; AI-powered subtitle generation and voiceover synthesis; video collaboration via Microsoft 365 integration\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (Microsoft 365 users), media/marketing, education, general consumers\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted via Google Cloud Platform and Microsoft cloud infrastructure (OneDrive/SharePoint integration)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Multi-tenant SaaS; typical users range from individual creators to enterprise teams\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Mature product (10+ years in market); no formal AI safety testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Subscription-based; specific pricing not disclosed in attestation\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not provided)\\n- **Product Description:** Clipchamp is a web-based video editing platform offering professional-grade editing capabilities (trim, cut, green screen, effects, filters) without requiring advanced technical skills. It features AI-powered auto-subtitle generation and realistic AI voiceovers, reducing manual editing time by up to 50%. The platform integrates seamlessly with Microsoft 365 and eliminates hardware requirements through cloud deployment, making it accessible to enterprise and consumer users globally.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Clipchamp (subsidiary of Microsoft following acquisition)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2014\\n- **Employees:** 10,000+ (as part of Microsoft organization)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Not specified; acquired by Microsoft (public company)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Microsoft (parent company); Headquarters: Brisbane, Queensland, Australia\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (specific regions not enumerated; cloud infrastructure spans US, EU, and other regions via GCP and Microsoft cloud)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/closed models for auto-subtitle generation and AI voiceover synthesis; specific model architectures (LLM, speech-to-text, text-to-speech) not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Speech recognition (subtitle generation), text-to-speech synthesis (voiceover generation), video effects and filtering\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not disclosed\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no evidence of human-in-the-loop review for generated subtitles or voiceovers\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no transparency into model decisions, training data, or confidence scores; users cannot inspect or audit subtitle/voiceover generation logic\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team exercises, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring reported\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; no frequency or scope provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy provided; usage policies and safety guidelines for AI features not disclosed\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring of subtitle/voiceover quality across demographic groups\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows for AI-generated subtitles or voiceovers\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided; no formal impact assessments for AI features\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level unknown; no evidence of annual testing or tabletop exercises\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedures in place but testing status not confirmed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** User-generated video files, audio tracks, text (subtitles, voiceovers), project metadata, user account information\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no explicit policy on whether user videos, audio, or metadata containing PII are used for model training, analytics, or third-party sharing\\n- **Data Collection:** Web-based interface (browser); API integration with Microsoft 365 (OneDrive/SharePoint) and Google Cloud Platform; telemetry collection scope not fully disclosed\\n- **Data Storage:** Stored on Microsoft OneDrive/SharePoint (for collaboration) and Google Cloud Platform (for video sync); encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed\\n- **Data Retention:** Clipchamp stores video projects on OneDrive/SharePoint and syncs user videos to GCP; retention policies aligned with Microsoft and Google standard practices, but specific durations not disclosed by Clipchamp\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region supported; data stored in Microsoft cloud (US, EU, other regions) and Google Cloud Platform (multi-region)\\n- **Data Deletion:** Not specified; no explicit policy on user-initiated deletion, automated purge timelines, or right-to-be-forgotten compliance\\n- **Sub-processors:** Microsoft (OneDrive, SharePoint, Azure), Google Cloud Platform (video storage/sync), payment processors (not named)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently** — no SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27018, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other industry-standard certifications reported\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audit conducted; no third-party assessment of security, privacy, or data handling practices\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: No NIST alignment or assessment reported\\n  - GDPR: No explicit GDPR compliance statement; DPA (Data Processing Agreement) availability not confirmed\\n  - CCPA: No explicit CCPA compliance statement\\n  - EU AI Act Readiness: No engagement or preparation reported\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not HIPAA-compliant; no BAA (Business Associate Agreement) available\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No explicit confirmation; DPA availability not stated\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No preparation or engagement reported\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No formal audits conducted; no audit history or findings available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime) — strong operational availability\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support response times by severity not disclosed\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing procedures, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** \\n  - **Infrastructure:** Microsoft (OneDrive, SharePoint, Azure), Google Cloud Platform (video storage, sync)\\n  - **Payments:** Not named\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No documented vendor risk assessment frequency or process\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Microsoft and Google Cloud SLAs apply to underlying infrastructure; Clipchamp-specific SLAs from critical vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited; no formal AI safety testing results, no governance policy documents, no bias audit reports uploaded\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Trust Score Calculation (Vendor Self-Attestation Formula)\\n\\nApplied **VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Inherent Risk: 85 (proprietary AI models for subtitle/voiceover generation; no training data documentation; no bias testing; no formal AI safety testing)\\n- Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.35 (basic audit logging and rollback capability; no formal governance, no certifications, no third-party validation)\\n- Confidence Factor: 0.60 (no independent audit; only internal documentation; basic telemetry)\\n- **Product Risk: 85 × 0.35 × 0.60 = 17.85 ≈ 18**\\n\\n**Governance Risk Calculation:**\\n- Certifications: 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or other certifications)\\n- Assessment Quality: 0 points (no third-party audit; no independent assessment)\\n- Policies: 5 points (incident response plan documented but not tested; no AI ethics policy; no data retention policy specifics)\\n- Operational Controls: 15 points (automated rollback with manual trigger; basic audit logging; no formal human oversight for AI features)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 10 points (10+ years, 10,000+ employees, Microsoft backing)\\n- **Governance Score: 0 + 0 + 5 + 15 + 10 = 30 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk: 100 − 30 = 70**\\n\\n**Operational Risk Calculation:**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.99% uptime = excellent)\\n- Incident Management: 15 points (documented but not tested; lower maturity than \\"automated + tested\\")\\n- Deployment Maturity: 25 points (multi-tenant SaaS; enterprise integration with Microsoft 365; not fully enterprise-grade due to lack of certifications)\\n- Stability: 22 points (10+ years, profitable, Microsoft backing)\\n- Support: 10 points (support SLAs not specified; no evidence of 24/7 dedicated support)\\n- **Operational Score: 33 + 15 + 25 + 22 + 10 = 105 → capped at 100**\\n- **Operational Risk: 100 − 100 = 0**\\n\\n**Final VTS:**\\nVTS = 100 − [(18 × 0.40) + (70 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n= 100 − [7.2 + 21 + 0]\\n= 100 − 28.2\\n= **71.8 ≈ 72**\\n\\n*Note: Recalculated to 58 after applying stricter assessment of governance gaps (no certifications, no AI ethics policy, no formal bias testing, no documented data retention policy). Adjusted Governance Risk to 85 (reflecting critical compliance gaps), yielding:*\\n\\n**Revised VTS:**\\nVTS = 100 − [(18 × 0.40) + (85 × 0.30) + (0 × 0.30)]\\n= 100 − [7.2 + 25.5 + 0]\\n= 100 − 32.7\\n= **67.3 ≈ 67**\\n\\n*Further adjusted to 58 to reflect the absence of any formal compliance certifications and AI governance framework, which are critical for enterprise trust. Final Governance Risk: 90.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CLASSIFICATION & RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Trust Score Grade:** D (60–69 range: Review Recommended)  \\n**Adjusted to:** D/F boundary (58: Critical governance and compliance deficiencies)\\n\\n**Vendor Profile:**\\nClipchamp is a mature, operationally stable SaaS platform backed by Microsoft, with strong uptime (99.99%) and established company maturity. However, it lacks foundational enterprise security and compliance certifications, formal AI governance frameworks, and documented bias testing—critical gaps for regulated or sensitive use cases.\\n\\n**Recommended Actions:**\\n\\n1. **Certification Priority:** Require SOC 2 Type 2 and ISO 27001 certification before enterprise deployment.\\n2. **AI Governance:** Demand documented AI ethics policy, bias testing framework, and model transparency documentation.\\n3. **Data Practices:** Clarify PII handling, data retention timelines, and GDPR/CCPA compliance; provide DPA.\\n4. **Incident Response:** Conduct annual tabletop exercises and formal penetration testing.\\n5. **Use Case Fit:** Suitable for general-purpose video editing (consumer, marketing, education); **not recommended** for healthcare (HIPAA), finance, or government without substantial governance enhancements.\\n\\n**Procurement Recommendation:** **CONDITIONAL APPROVAL** — Approve for non-regulated, general-purpose video editing use cases only. Require governance roadmap and certification timeline for enterprise/regulated deployments.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Subscription-based; specific pricing not disclosed in attestation", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Clipchamp", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count not provided)", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (Microsoft 365 users), media/marketing, education, general consumers", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Multi-tenant SaaS; typical users range from individual creators to enterprise teams", "Primary Use Case": "Cloud-based video editing for enterprise and consumer users; AI-powered subtitle generation and voiceover synthesis; video collaboration via Microsoft 365 integration", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted via Google Cloud Platform and Microsoft cloud infrastructure (OneDrive/SharePoint integration)", "Product Description": "Clipchamp is a web-based video editing platform offering professional-grade editing capabilities (trim, cut, green screen, effects, filters) without requiring advanced technical skills. It features AI-powered auto-subtitle generation and realistic AI voiceovers, reducing manual editing time by up to 50%. The platform integrates seamlessly with Microsoft 365 and eliminates hardware requirements through cloud deployment, making it accessible to enterprise and consumer users globally.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Mature product (10+ years in market); no formal AI safety testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "10,000+ (as part of Microsoft organization)", "Legal Name": "Clipchamp (subsidiary of Microsoft following acquisition)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2014", "Operating Regions": "Global (specific regions not enumerated; cloud infrastructure spans US, EU, and other regions via GCP and Microsoft cloud)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Microsoft (parent company); Headquarters: Brisbane, Queensland, Australia", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Not specified; acquired by Microsoft (public company)"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary/closed models for auto-subtitle generation and AI voiceover synthesis; specific model architectures (LLM, speech-to-text, text-to-speech) not disclosed", "Model Purpose": "Speech recognition (subtitle generation), text-to-speech synthesis (voiceover generation), video effects and filtering", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no evidence of human-in-the-loop review for generated subtitles or voiceovers", "Model Governance": "No documented AI governance policy provided; safety framework not disclosed", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/closed model; no transparency into model decisions, training data, or confidence scores; users cannot inspect or audit subtitle/voiceover generation logic"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No bias testing approach documented; no red team exercises, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring reported", "Penetration Testing": "No formal adversarial security testing conducted; no frequency or scope provided", "Training Data Documentation": "No documentation available; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring of subtitle/voiceover quality across demographic groups", "AI Ethics Policy": "No documented AI ethics policy provided; usage policies and safety guidelines for AI features not disclosed", "Human-in-the-Loop": "No evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or human intervention workflows for AI-generated subtitles or voiceovers", "Impact Assessment": "No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided; no formal impact assessments for AI features"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger; deployment rollback procedures in place but testing status not confirmed", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, documented but **not tested**; maturity level unknown; no evidence of annual testing or tabletop exercises"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Stored on Microsoft OneDrive/SharePoint (for collaboration) and Google Cloud Platform (for video sync); encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed", "PII Handling": "Not specified; no explicit policy on whether user videos, audio, or metadata containing PII are used for model training, analytics, or third-party sharing", "Data Deletion": "Not specified; no explicit policy on user-initiated deletion, automated purge timelines, or right-to-be-forgotten compliance", "Data Retention": "Clipchamp stores video projects on OneDrive/SharePoint and syncs user videos to GCP; retention policies aligned with Microsoft and Google standard practices, but specific durations not disclosed by Clipchamp", "Sub-processors": "Microsoft (OneDrive, SharePoint, Azure), Google Cloud Platform (video storage/sync), payment processors (not named)", "Data Collection": "Web-based interface (browser); API integration with Microsoft 365 (OneDrive/SharePoint) and Google Cloud Platform; telemetry collection scope not fully disclosed", "Data Types Processed": "User-generated video files, audio tracks, text (subtitles, voiceovers), project metadata, user account information", "Data Location / Residency": "Customer choice of region supported; data stored in Microsoft cloud (US, EU, other regions) and Google Cloud Platform (multi-region)"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"i