ity (99.9% SLA, automated rollback, annual incident testing) and reasonable data practices with documented retention policies and user consent mechanisms. However, the vendor presents **significant governance and compliance gaps**: no security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), no independent audit documentation, no formal AI ethics policy, and limited bias testing or adversarial security testing documentation. The product processes user-uploaded images for AI model training (with legitimate interest legal basis), which introduces data sensitivity concerns in the absence of third-party compliance validation. Company maturity is growth-stage (Series B/C, 51–200 employees, founded 2019), which is appropriate for the B2B SaaS segment but lacks the operational track record of established vendors. **Recommendation: Review Recommended.** Photoroom is acceptable for non-regulated, low-stakes use cases (e.g., internal product photography workflows), but should not be deployed for regulated industries (healthcare, finance) or high-sensitivity data without substantial mitigation: SOC 2 Type 2 certification, third-party security audit, formal AI governance policy, and explicit opt-out for model training. ---", "overallScore": 81, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.69, "Governance": 79, "Operational": 61}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   81 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       39.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        21.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.31  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (39.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (21.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (61.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Raise Governance (79.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:52:15.999979+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	81	B	17f17839-1bdb-42f9-8a24-a12a3c6dcf4a	\N	\N
2cfe80d1-0ca0-435a-88b6-13a49780a1fb	92833551-82fa-44a3-80cf-0b5567341bc5	101	101	AI Product Company	{"Retail & E-commerce; Technology; Media & Entertainment": ["Retail & E-commerce; Technology; Media & Entertainment"]}	Growth (Series B/C)	https://www.pixelcut.ai	Pixa (formerly Pixelcut) is an AI-powered platform for creating, editing, and shipping production-ready visuals. It offers tools for image and video editing, background removal, upscaling, and AI-generated content.	51-200	2012	Oakland, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "VP Product", "Line of Business Leader"]	Helps our small business save time and money to create different marketing materials professionally.	\N	Pixa understands your prompts, plans and executes tasks on your behalf using the best creative tools available like Nano Banana Pro and Sora 2. No special prompting required.	50% reduction in time spent creating marketing materials, 30% cost savings on outsourcing design work [Corroborated by 1 evidence point(s): Increase in Paying Customers: 16%]	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["None Currently"]	\N	\N	\N	Unless specified otherwise in this document, Personal Data shall be processed and stored for as long as required by the purpose they have been collected for and may be retained for longer due to applicable legal obligation or based on the Users’ consent.	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:53:55.769676+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Pixelcut	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:53:55.776+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: PIXA (PIXELCUT)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 52 (Moderate Risk)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 25\\n- Data Practices: 45\\n- AI Governance: 30\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 60\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nPixa demonstrates moderate operational maturity (growth-stage company, 99.9% uptime SLA, automated rollback) but carries significant governance and compliance gaps that limit enterprise suitability. The vendor lacks security certifications, formal AI governance documentation, bias testing protocols, and independent compliance audits—critical requirements for regulated industries or sensitive data handling. While the company shows reasonable operational stability and basic logging/telemetry, the absence of formal testing, documented AI safety practices, and third-party validation of data handling practices creates residual risk. The proprietary model approach and reliance on third-party models (with unknown training data provenance) further constrains transparency and control. **Recommendation:** Acceptable for non-regulated, low-sensitivity use cases (e.g., internal marketing asset creation); requires substantial governance roadmap and independent audit before enterprise or regulated deployment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Pixelcut\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-powered creation, editing, and optimization of production-ready visual marketing materials (images, video backgrounds, upscaling, AI-generated content)\\n- **Target Industry:** Small business, marketing, creative services\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth stage (Series B/C); no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** 16% increase in paying customers (corroborated); specific customer count not stated\\n- **Product Description:** Pixelcut is an AI-powered visual creation and editing platform that automates marketing material production through natural-language prompts and integrated creative tools (e.g., Nano Banana Pro, Sora 2). The platform claims 50% time savings and 30% cost reduction vs. outsourced design. Model transparency is proprietary/closed; training data provenance is unknown (third-party models used).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Pixa (formerly Pixelcut)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2012\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth stage); revenue not disclosed\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Oakland, CA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-based; global reach not confirmed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/closed models; integrates third-party models (Nano Banana Pro, Sora 2); specific model architectures (LLM, vision, diffusion) not disclosed\\n- **Model Purpose:** Image understanding, editing, background removal, upscaling, AI-generated content creation; natural-language task planning and execution\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment, safety framework, or model versioning policy stated\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no mention of advisory controls, autonomous decision limits, monitoring, or alerts\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary model; no prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Third-party models used; training data provenance unknown; no documentation of data sources, filtering, or curation\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; no frequency or scope stated\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no external evaluations or internal monitoring programs mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, intervention workflows, or approval gates documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; maturity level and scope not detailed\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger option; no rollback testing frequency or success rate provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Images, video, text prompts; specific data categories (PII, financial, health) not detailed\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no statement on whether customer data is used for training, anonymization, or retention limits\\n- **Data Collection:** API and interface-based collection; retention options not specified\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status (in transit / at rest) not stated\\n- **Data Retention:** Default: retained for purpose fulfillment and legal compliance; no automated deletion or zero-retention option documented\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; no customer choice or regional residency guarantee provided\\n- **Data Deletion:** On-request deletion capability not explicitly stated; automated deletion not mentioned\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently held (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or equivalent)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits conducted; no third-party validation of security or data practices\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No documented alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act; readiness not assessed\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable; no BAA eligibility stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) mentioned; GDPR compliance status unclear\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audits conducted; no audit schedule provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year); contractual enforcement and penalties not specified\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; support tiers and response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release frequency, testing protocol, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payment processor, and authentication services not identified; no vendor list provided\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment frequency or process documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No SLAs from critical vendors provided or referenced\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Basic metrics available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing conducted; no policy documentation uploaded or referenced\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing results available; no NDA-protected assessments mentioned\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ASSESSMENT SUMMARY & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Risk Profile by Domain\\n\\n| Domain | Risk Level | Key Gaps |\\n|--------|-----------|----------|\\n| **Product Risk** | High (65/100) | Proprietary model, unknown training data, no formal testing, no bias detection |\\n| **Governance Risk** | High (70/100) | No AI ethics policy, no impact assessments, no bias audits, no documented oversight |\\n| **Operational Risk** | Low (35/100) | 99.9% SLA, automated rollback, documented incident response (untested) |\\n| **Compliance Risk** | Critical (75/100) | No certifications, no independent audits, no regulatory alignment, no DPA |\\n\\n### Procurement Recommendation\\n\\n**CONDITIONAL APPROVAL – NON-REGULATED USE ONLY**\\n\\n✅ **Acceptable for:**\\n- Internal marketing asset creation (non-sensitive, non-regulated)\\n- Small business / SMB use cases with low data sensitivity\\n- Pilot / proof-of-concept deployments with limited scope\\n\\n❌ **Not recommended for:**\\n- Healthcare, financial services, government, or other regulated industries\\n- Processing of PII, PHI, financial data, or sensitive business information\\n- Enterprise deployments requiring SOC 2, HIPAA, GDPR, or FedRAMP compliance\\n- Mission-critical workflows without independent audit and formal governance\\n\\n### Required Remediation Before Enterprise Deployment\\n\\n**MUST FIX (Before Proceeding):**\\n1. **Compliance & Certifications** – Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 audit and ISO 27001 certification (6–12 months)\\n2. **AI Governance** – Document AI ethics policy, model governance framework, and human-in-the-loop controls\\n3. **Data Practices** – Publish Data Processing Agreement (DPA) for GDPR compliance; clarify PII handling and training data usage\\n4. **Testing & Validation** – Conduct formal bias testing, adversarial security testing, and third-party model audit\\n5. **Incident Response** – Test incident response plan and document results\\n\\n**SHOULD FIX (Reduces Residual Risk):**\\n6. Publish model cards and system impact assessments for each AI capability\\n7. Implement automated audit logging with SIEM export capability\\n8. Establish vendor SLAs for critical infrastructure providers\\n9. Define support response SLAs by severity level\\n\\n### Timeline & Budget Estimate\\n\\n- **Compliance & Certifications:** 6–12 months, $50K–$150K\\n- **AI Governance & Testing:** 3–6 months, $30K–$75K\\n- **Total Remediation:** 9–18 months, $80K–$225K\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Confidence Level:** Moderate (basic data provided; significant gaps in documentation)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Pixelcut", "Customer Base": "16% increase in paying customers (corroborated); specific customer count not stated", "Target Industry": "Small business, marketing, creative services", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "AI-powered creation, editing, and optimization of production-ready visual marketing materials (images, video backgrounds, upscaling, AI-generated content)", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)", "Product Description": "Pixelcut is an AI-powered visual creation and editing platform that automates marketing material production through natural-language prompts and integrated creative tools (e.g., Nano Banana Pro, Sora 2). The platform claims 50% time savings and 30% cost reduction vs. outsourced design. Model transparency is proprietary/closed; training data provenance is unknown (third-party models used).", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth stage (Series B/C); no formal testing conducted"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Pixa (formerly Pixelcut)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2012", "Operating Regions": "Not specified (assumed US-based; global reach not confirmed)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Oakland, CA, USA; investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth stage); revenue not disclosed"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types