not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes	Yes, basic logging	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:55:18.374291+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Podium AI Employee	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:55:18.377+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Podium AI Employee\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate – Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 58\\n- Compliance: 45\\n- Data Practices: 65\\n- AI Governance: 40\\n- Operations: 72\\n- Company Maturity: 78\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nPodium demonstrates moderate trustworthiness with established company maturity (founded 2014, 1,001–5,000 employees, Series D+ profitable) and acceptable operational stability (99.9% uptime SLA). However, critical gaps in AI governance, compliance certifications, and security posture significantly limit trust. The vendor lacks documented AI governance policies, bias testing frameworks, formal security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA not stated), and third-party audit evidence. Training data documentation is absent, and incident response procedures are documented but untested. While data retention policies and basic audit logging are in place, the absence of comprehensive compliance certifications and AI safety controls places this vendor in the \\"Review Recommended\\" category (D grade, 60–69 range). Procurement should require enhanced due diligence, formal security/compliance audits, and documented AI governance roadmap before enterprise deployment, particularly for regulated industries or sensitive data handling.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Podium AI Employee\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Lead management, customer communication automation, sales conversion optimization for local businesses\\n- **Target Industry:** Local businesses (SMB focus); applicable to retail, services, professional services\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted (infrastructure provider not specified)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Typical deployment for SMB to mid-market local business operations\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Not specified\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (corroborated by 13 evidence points including ROI metrics: 20% lead conversion increase, 30% reduction in manual communication tasks, 2x lead closing rates)\\n- **Product Description:** Podium AI Employee is an AI-powered platform that integrates messaging, reviews, and payments to help local businesses attract, manage, and convert leads through improved communication and sales tools. The platform streamlines customer interactions and enhances business growth by automating lead response and engagement workflows. Moderate explainability features are available; specific security and compliance certifications are not documented in the attestation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Podium (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2014\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Lehi, Utah, United States; specific investors not stated\\n- **Operating Regions:** Not specified (assumed US-based with potential multi-region support)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (AI capabilities present but model architecture not documented)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Lead management, customer communication automation, message routing, sales conversion optimization\\n- **Model Governance:** No documented AI governance policy provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified (no explicit human-in-the-loop, monitoring, or intervention controls documented)\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate explainability features available; specific prompt-level control or citation mechanisms not documented\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; red team or third-party audits not mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; adversarial security testing approach not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** No documented AI ethics policy or usage guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audit frequency or external evaluations documented\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** No explicit human oversight, content filtering, or intervention controls documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, documented but not tested (maturity gap: untested procedures reduce confidence)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger (moderate maturity; automated component reduces deployment risk)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Customer communications, lead information, review data, payment-related information (inferred from product description)\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (inferred from product capabilities); retention options not explicitly stated\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** Podium retains customer data for as long as necessary to fulfill collection purposes, including legal, accounting, or reporting requirements; deletion procedures implemented upon request or after retention period expires\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Not specified; customer choice for data residency not documented\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request and automated after retention period expiration\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure provider, payments processor, and authentication services not identified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** Not specified (SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA, FedRAMP, or other certifications not documented)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no evidence of third-party audit provided\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** NIST, GDPR, CCPA, and EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** BAA eligibility not stated; not recommended for PHI handling without explicit BAA\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** DPA availability not documented\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documentation provided\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified; no recent audit evidence provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year; acceptable for non-critical systems, below enterprise standard of 99.95%+)\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, and rollback readiness practices not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Infrastructure provider, payments processor, and authentication services not identified\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Frequency of vendor risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, interaction data available\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available (export capability and SIEM integration not specified)\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited; no formal security, compliance, or AI governance documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Yes, testing results available (specific results and NDA terms not detailed in attestation)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** REVIEW RECOMMENDED (D Grade – 60–69 range)\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\nPodium demonstrates established company maturity and acceptable operational uptime but lacks critical enterprise-grade security, compliance, and AI governance controls. The absence of formal certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), documented AI governance policies, bias testing frameworks, and third-party audit evidence creates material risk for regulated industries or sensitive data handling.\\n\\n**Conditions for Approval:**\\n1. **Security & Compliance:** Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 audit report (or equivalent third-party security assessment) and document encryption, access controls, and incident response procedures\\n2. **AI Governance:** Provide documented AI ethics policy, bias testing methodology, and human oversight controls\\n3. **Data Practices:** Clarify PII handling, sub-processor list, data residency options, and training data usage policies\\n4. **Support & Operations:** Define severity-based support SLAs, release cadence, and tested incident response procedures\\n5. **Regulatory Alignment:** For healthcare/financial use cases, obtain HIPAA BAA or equivalent compliance certification before deployment\\n\\n**Recommended Use Cases:**\\n- SMB lead management and customer communication (non-regulated, non-sensitive data)\\n- Pilot deployments with limited data scope pending compliance upgrades\\n- Not recommended for healthcare PHI, financial data, or government use cases without enhanced compliance evidence\\n\\n**Risk Mitigation Timeline:** 90–180 days for compliance gap closure; re-assess after vendor provides audit evidence and governance documentation.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Podium AI Employee", "Customer Base": "Not specified (cor