l trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes, basic test results	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 15:59:58.077073+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Daily	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 15:59:58.082+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Daily (Video Infrastructure Platform)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 55\\n- Compliance: 35\\n- Data Practices: 60\\n- AI Governance: Not enough data\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 70\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nDaily scores in the **Moderate** range (62/100), reflecting solid operational maturity and data handling practices, but significant gaps in compliance certifications and governance documentation. The vendor demonstrates strong operational reliability (99.95% uptime SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback) and reasonable data practices (session-based retention, basic audit logging), which support the operations score of 75. However, the absence of security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA), limited compliance framework documentation, and lack of explicit AI governance policies create material risk for regulated industries—driving compliance and security scores to 35 and 55 respectively. Company maturity is solid for a Series B/C growth-stage vendor (51–200 employees, founded 2016, profitable trajectory implied by customer ROI claims), but the vendor has not yet achieved the governance and certification posture expected of enterprise-grade infrastructure providers. **Recommendation:** Acceptable for non-regulated use cases (e.g., consumer video apps, internal communications); requires enhanced due diligence and contractual SLA/indemnification for healthcare, financial services, or government deployments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Daily\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Video and audio integration into applications; custom video experiences; real-time communication infrastructure.\\n- **Target Industry:** Developer-centric (SaaS, fintech, healthcare, education, enterprise communication platforms).\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS (global video infrastructure).\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted only; no on-premises option stated.\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Supports integration from simple two-line-of-code implementations to custom, low-level API builds; scales to enterprise deployments.\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Growth-stage product (Series B/C); basic test results available.\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor.\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not disclosed; ROI corroborated by 4 evidence points).\\n- **Product Description:** Daily provides end-to-end encrypted video and audio infrastructure with global reach, enabling developers to integrate video calls with minimal code complexity. The platform emphasizes security (no China-based data routing), low-latency performance, and compliance-ready infrastructure. Typical ROI includes 80% reduction in development time and <2-day implementation, with 50% complaint reduction and 44-line code savings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Daily (legal entity name not specified in attestation).\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Platform Provider (video infrastructure and APIs).\\n- **Year Founded:** 2016\\n- **Employees:** 51–200\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not disclosed.\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA. Investors not specified.\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (infrastructure deployed across multiple regions to minimize latency); specific regions not enumerated.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified. Vendor uses third-party models for certain capabilities; internal model architecture not disclosed.\\n- **Model Purpose:** Video/audio codec optimization, real-time quality adaptation, latency minimization. AI-specific capabilities (e.g., noise suppression, speaker detection) not detailed.\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented. No staged deployment, safety framework, or model versioning policy stated.\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified. No advisory board, human-in-the-loop controls, or monitoring alerts documented.\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features noted, but specifics not provided). No prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or detailed explainability documentation available.\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Limited. Vendor uses third-party models; training data provenance and documentation unknown.\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified. No red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools documented.\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified. No frequency or scope of penetration testing disclosed (distinct from incident response testing, which is annual).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented. No published usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical framework stated.\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified. No internal or external bias audit program documented.\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified. No admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented.\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified. No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for AI components available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually. Formal incident response plan exists and is validated through annual testing; specific response time targets and escalation procedures not detailed.\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger. Deployment rollback is available and can be triggered manually; automated rollback conditions not specified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Video and audio streams, session metadata, call logs, user interaction data.\\n- **PII Handling:** Not explicitly stated. Vendor does not disclose whether customer data (including PII within video/audio) is used for training, model improvement, or analytics. End-to-end encryption suggests data is not decrypted server-side for processing, but retention and secondary use policies are unclear.\\n- **Data Collection:** API-based collection; real-time session data ingestion. Scope of telemetry and metadata collection not detailed.\\n- **Data Storage:** Cloud infrastructure (vendor-managed); encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed, though end-to-end encryption is highlighted as a differentiator.\\n- **Data Retention:** Session data retention varies by plan:\\n  - Free: 1 day\\n  - Pay-as-you-go: 3 days\\n  - Advanced Support: 14 days\\n  - Premium Support: 21 days\\n  - Enterprise: 30 days\\n  - No zero-retention option stated; deletion on request not explicitly confirmed.\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Global infrastructure with explicit statement that data does not route through China-based servers. Customer choice of data residency not stated; specific regional options (EU, US, APAC) not enumerated.\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion after retention period expires; on-request deletion not explicitly confirmed.\\n- **Sub-processors:** Infrastructure providers not named. Payment processors, authentication providers, and analytics vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **None currently.** No SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27018, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other industry-standard certifications held.\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified. No third-party audit program or audit schedule documented.\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** \\n  - NIST: Not addressed.\\n  - GDPR: Not explicitly addressed; no DPA or data processing agreement mentioned.\\n  - CCPA: Not addressed.\\n  - EU AI Act: Not addressed.\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** No BAA (Business Associate Agreement) available; HIPAA compliance not claimed.\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance statement provided.\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not addressed.\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No independent audit program; last audit date and findings not available.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime allowance). Strong operational commitment; specific remedies (credits, service level credits) not stated.\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified. Support tiers (Advanced Support, Premium Support, Enterprise) exist but response time targets by severity not documented.\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified. Release frequency, change notification process, and rollback readiness practices not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not disclosed. Infrastructure providers (likely AWS, Azure, or GCP), CDN partners, and payment processors not named.\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified. No documented vendor risk assessment program or frequency.\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified. SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not disclosed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available. Scope limited to basic session and call metrics; detailed telemetry export or custom reporting not confirmed.\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, basic logging available. Audit log export capability and SIEM integration not detailed; log retention and completeness not specified.\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Yes, basic test results available. Comprehensive security, compliance, and governance documentation not provided; policy library not disclosed.\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Not specified. No indication of advanced testing results available under NDA; third-party model testing not documented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## RISK ASSESSMENT & RECOMMENDATIONS\\n\\n### Key Strengths\\n1. **Operational Reliability:** 99.95% uptime SLA with annual incident response testing and automated rollback capability demonstrates mature operations.\\n2. **Data Privacy by Design:** End-to-end encryption and explicit non-routing through China-based infrastructure address key privacy concerns.\\n3. **Developer-Friendly:** Rapid integration (two lines of code) and documented ROI (80% dev time reduction, <2-day implementation) reduce deployment friction.\\n4. **Company Maturity:** Series B/C funding, 51–200 employees, and 8-year operating history suggest financial stability and market traction.\\n\\n### Key Gaps\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, or HIPAA BAA limits enterprise and regulated-industry deployability.\\n2. **Minimal AI Governance:** No documented AI ethics policy, bias audit program, or explainability framework; third-party model provenance unknown.\\n3. **Limited Compliance Documentation:** No GDPR DPA, CCPA statement, or EU AI Act readiness assessment; regulatory alignment unclear.\\n4. **Incomplete Data Practices Transparency:** PII handling, secondary use of data, and sub-processor disclosure not addressed; data residency options limited.\\n\\n### Recommended Use Cases\\n- **Approved:** Consumer video apps, internal team communication, developer-centric SaaS platforms, non-regulated video conferencing.\\n- **Conditional (Enhanced Due Diligence Required):** Healthcare (requires HIPAA BAA and SOC 2 Type 2 audit), financial services (requires SOC 2 and GDPR DPA), government (requires FedRAMP or equivalent).\\n- **Not Recommended:** Highly regulated deployments (e.g., medical imaging, financial transaction recording) until certifications are obtained.\\n\\n### Remediation Path\\nTo improve trust score to 80+, Daily should:\\n1. Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 certification (6–12 months).\\n2. Publish GDPR Data Processing Agreement and CCPA compliance statement.\\n3. Document AI governance policy, bias audit program, and third-party model provenance.\\n4. Expand data residency options (EU, US, APAC customer choice).\\n5. Disclose critical sub-processors and their SLAs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation  \\n**Analyst Notes:** This assessment is based on vendor-provided attestation data and publicly available information. Independent verification of claims (e.g., uptime SLA, incident response testing, ROI metrics) is recommended before enterprise deployment. Vendor should complete a formal SOC 2 Type 2 audit and publish compliance documentation to support regulated-industry use cases.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor.", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Daily", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count not disclosed; ROI corroborated by 4 evidence points).", "Target Industry": "Developer-centric (SaaS, fintech, healthcare, education, enterprise communication platforms).", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS (global video infrastructure).", "Deployment Scale": "Supports integration from simple two-line-of-code implementations to custom, low-level API builds; scales to enterprise deployments.", "Primary Use Case": "Video and audio integration into applications; custom video experiences; real-time communication infrastructure.", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted only; no on-premises option stated.", "Product Description": "Daily provides end-to-end encrypted video and audio infrastructure with global reach, enabling developers to integrate video calls with minimal code complexity. The platform emphasizes security (no China-based data routing), low-latency performance, and compliance-ready infrastructure. Typical ROI includes 80% reduction in development time and <2-day implementation, with 50% complaint reduction and 44-line code savings.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Growth-stage product (Series B/C); basic test results available."}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "51–200", "Legal Name": "Daily (legal entity name not specified in attestation).", "Vendor Type": "AI Platform Provider (video infrastructure and APIs).", "Year Founded": "2016", "Operating Regions": "Global (infrastructure deployed across multiple regions to minimize latency); specific regions not enumerated.", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA. Investors not specified.", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series B/C (growth-stage); revenue not disclosed."}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified. Vendor uses third-party models for certain capabilities; internal model architecture not disclosed.", "Model Purpose": "Video/audio codec optimization, real-time quality adaptation, latency minimization. AI-specific capabilities (e.g., noise suppression, speaker detection) not detailed.", "Human Oversight": "Not specified. No advisory board, human-in-the-loop controls, or monitoring alerts documented.", "Model Governance": "Not documented. No staged deployment, safety framework, or model versioning policy stated.", "Update Frequency": "Not specified.", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate (some explainability features noted, but specifics not provided). No prompt-level control, citation mechanism, or detailed explainability documentation available."}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Not specified. No red team, third-party audits, or statistical bias monitoring tools documented.", "Penetration Testing": "Not specified. No frequency or scope of penetration testing disclosed (distinct from incident response testing, which is annual).", "Training Data Documentation": "Limited. Vendor uses third-party models; training data provenance and documentation unknown."}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Not specified. No internal or external bias audit program documented.", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented. No published usage policies, safety guidelines, or ethical framework stated.", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not specified. No admin controls, content filtering, or intervention mechanisms documented.", "Impact Assessment": "Not specified. No system cards, model cards, or release documentation for AI components available."}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated with manual trigger. Deployment rollback is available and can be triggered manually; automated rollback conditions not specified.", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, tested annually. Formal incident response plan exists and is validated through annual testing; specific response time targets and escalation procedures not detailed."}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Cloud infrastructure (vendor-managed); encryption at rest and in transit not explicitly confirmed, though end-to-end encryption is highlighted as a differentiator.", "PII Handling": "Not explicitly stated. Vendor does not disclose whether customer data (including PII within video/audio) is used for training, model improvement, or analytics. End-to-end encryption suggests data is not decrypted server-side for processing, but retention and secondary use policies are unclear.", "Data Deletion": "Automated deletion after retention period expires; on-request deletion not explicitly confirmed.", "Data Retention": "Session data retention varies by plan:", "Sub-processors": "Infrastructure providers not named. Payment processors, authentication providers, and analytics vendors not disclosed.", "Data Collection": "API-based collection; real-time session data ingestion. Scope of telemetry and metadata collection not detailed.", "Data Types Processed": "Video and audio streams, session metadata, call logs, user interaction data.", "Data Location / Residency": "Global infrastructure with explicit statement that data does not route through China-based servers. Customer choice of data residency not stated; specific regional options (EU, US, APAC) not enumerated."}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "**None currently.** No SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 27018, HIPAA, FedRAMP, or other industry-standard certifications held.", "GDPR Compliance": "No Data Processing Agreement (DPA) or GDPR compliance statement provided.", "HIPAA Compliance": "No BAA (Business Associate Agreement) available; HIPAA compliance not claimed.", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not addressed.", "Regulatory Frameworks": "- NIST: Not addressed.", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified. No third-party audit program or audit schedule documented.", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "No independent audit program; last audit date and findings not available."}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.95% (4.4 hours/year downtime allowance). Strong operational commitment; specific remedies (credits, service level credits) not stated.", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified. Release frequency, change notification process, and rollback readiness practices not documented.", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified. Support tiers (Advanced Support, Premium Support, Enterprise) exist but response time targets by severity not documented."}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified. SLAs from critical infrastructure vendors not disclosed.", "Critical Vendors": "Not disclosed. Infrastructure providers (likely AWS, Azure, or GCP), CDN partners, and payment processors not named.", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified. No documented vendor risk assessment program or frequency."}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Approved": "Consumer video apps, internal team communication, developer-centric SaaS platforms, non-regulated video conferencing.", "Not Recommended": "Highly regulated deployments (e.g., medical imaging, financial transaction recording) until certifications are obtained.", "Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, basic logging available. Audit log export capability and SIEM integration not detailed; log retention and completeness not specified.", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available. Scope limited to basic session and call metrics; detailed telemetry export or custom reporting not confirmed.", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Not specified. No indication of advanced testing results available under NDA; third-party model testing not documented.", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Yes, basic test results available. Comprehensive security, compliance, and governance documentation not provided; policy library not disclosed.", "Conditional (Enhanced Due Diligence Required)": "Healthcare (requires HIPAA BAA and SOC 2 Type 2 audit), financial services (requires SOC 2 and GDPR DPA), government (requires FedRAMP or equivalent)."}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Daily scores in the **Moderate** range (62/100), reflecting solid operational maturity and data handling practices, but significant gaps in compliance certifications and governance documentation. The vendor demonstrates strong operational reliability (99.95% uptime SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback) and reasonable data practices (session-based retention, basic audit logging), which support the operations score of 75. However, the absence of security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA), limited compliance framework documentation, and lack of explicit AI governance policies create material risk for regulated industries—driving compliance and security scores to 35 and 55 respectively. Company maturity is solid for a Series B/C growth-stage vendor (51–200 employees, founded 2016, profitable trajectory implied by customer ROI claims), but the vendor has not yet achieved the governance and certification posture expected of enterprise-grade infrastructure providers. **Recommendation:** Acceptable for non-regulated use cases (e.g., consumer video apps, internal communications); requires enhanced due diligence and contractual SLA/indemnification for healthcare, financial services, or government deployments. ---", "overallScore": 83, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 96.57, "Governance": 84, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   83 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        16.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            3.43  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (16.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Data residency in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 15:59:58.077073+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	83	B	60214a52-2714-41de-9fe8-2d963fc9d200	\N	\N
