b944c68d-ceab-4897-973c-2e49e40453e3	4393b21f-dabc-476d-9da4-0381d44d5a07	113	113	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Manufacturing; Technology; Media & Entertainment; Retail & E-commerce; Finance & Banking; Healthcare; Educational Institutions; Public Sector; Professional Services": ["Manufacturing; Technology; Media & Entertainment; Retail & E-commerce; Finance & Banking; Healthcare; Educational Institutions; Public Sector; Professional Services"]}	Mature (10+ years or Public)	https://slack.com/team-chat	Team Chat & Messaging App	1,001-5,000	2009	San Francisco, CA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "CIO", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Slack AI addresses the challenges of information overload and inefficient communication by providing AI-powered search and message summarization. It also helps automate repetitive tasks, reducing manual effort and improving team productivity.	\N	Slack’s conversational, AI-powered platform because it makes work simpler, more	Slack AI reduces the time spent searching for information by 30% and automates up to 20% of routine tasks, leading to significant productivity gains. [Corroborated by 10 evidence point(s): Increase in upsell bookings: 50%; Time spent generating account plans: 50% less; Increase in upsell win rate: 20%; Time saved with Slack AI summaries: Multiple hours per week, per resource; Upsell Opportunity Volume: Doubled]	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	["None Currently"]	\N	\N	["Customer choice of region"]	Slack offers global retention policies, allowing customers to configure how long their data is retained. Deletion procedures are in place to ensure data is securely removed when no longer needed.	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	99.99% (52 min/year downtime)	Yes, tested annually	Automated instant rollback	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, comprehensive	Limited/Partial	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 16:58:51.359149+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Slack AI	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 16:58:51.372+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT\\n## Slack AI\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate / Review Recommended)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 65\\n- Compliance: 45\\n- Data Practices: 70\\n- AI Governance: 35\\n- Operations: 80\\n- Company Maturity: 85\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nSlack AI receives a moderate trust score reflecting strong operational maturity and company stability (10+ years, public, 1,001–5,000 employees) offset by significant governance and compliance gaps. The vendor demonstrates solid operational infrastructure (99.99% SLA, automated rollback, annual incident testing) and reasonable data practices (customer-choice residency, documented retention/deletion). However, critical deficiencies in AI governance—no documented AI ethics policy, no bias testing approach, no training data documentation, and no security certifications—elevate residual risk. Using the Vendor Trust Score formula (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]), Product Risk is estimated at ~55–60 (high inherent risk from proprietary/closed model with minimal mitigation evidence), Governance Risk at ~70 (missing certifications, policies, and controls), and Operational Risk at ~20 (strong SLA and incident response). This yields VTS ≈ 62, placing Slack AI in the \\"Review Recommended\\" (D-grade, 60–69) band. **Recommendation:** Enhanced due diligence required; suitable for non-regulated use cases or as a pilot; require mitigation roadmap (AI ethics policy, bias audit, security certification) before production deployment in sensitive contexts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Slack AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** AI-powered search, message summarization, task automation, team communication enhancement\\n- **Target Industry:** Enterprise (cross-industry; no sector restrictions stated)\\n- **Deployment Model:** SaaS (cloud-hosted)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; customer choice of region for data residency\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified; typical deployment is team/organization-wide within Slack workspace\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Product stage not explicitly stated; inferred as mature/production (integrated into Slack platform since 2009 base product)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not quantified; Slack is a widely adopted enterprise platform with millions of users globally\\n- **Product Description:** Slack AI is an AI-enabled conversational platform integrated into Slack's team messaging application, providing AI-powered search, message summarization, and task automation to reduce information overload and improve team productivity. The product uses proprietary/closed AI models and claims 30% reduction in information-search time and up to 20% automation of routine tasks. Deployment is SaaS-based with customer-configurable data residency and retention policies.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Slack Technologies, Inc. (or Slack, a Salesforce company)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS\\n- **Year Founded:** 2009\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Public company (acquired by Salesforce); revenue not specified in attestation\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Salesforce (parent company); Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA\\n- **Operating Regions:** Global (not explicitly listed; inferred from \\"customer choice of region\\" data residency)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Proprietary/Closed (specific model architecture not disclosed)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Search enhancement, message summarization, task automation, conversational AI\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework stated\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no advisory vs. autonomous designation provided\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** No documentation available\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; no frequency or type provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits or external evaluations mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities documented\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Yes, tested annually (demonstrates basic maturity)\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated instant rollback (strong operational control)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Team messages, chat history, documents shared in Slack workspace\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII handling and whether customer data is used for training not documented\\n- **Data Collection:** API and chat interface (native to Slack platform)\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure not explicitly named; encryption status not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Slack offers global retention policies with customer configuration; deletion procedures in place\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** Customer choice of region (flexible; specific regions not enumerated)\\n- **Data Deletion:** Automated deletion procedures when data retention policy expires; on-request deletion not explicitly stated\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; Slack's parent company (Salesforce) infrastructure assumed; specific payment/auth processors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None currently (critical gap)\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no third-party audit mentioned\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not documented; no NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness stated\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not stated; BAA eligibility unknown\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not stated; DPA availability unknown\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No independent audit frequency or findings provided; only incident response plan tested annually\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime) — strong operational commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no release process, frequency, or rollback/readiness practices documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Salesforce (parent company); infrastructure and platform dependencies not detailed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; no frequency of risk assessments documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Yes, basic metrics available\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Yes, comprehensive audit logs available\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Limited/Partial (no AI ethics, bias testing, or training data documentation provided)\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** Limited/Partial (no safety testing results disclosed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Scoring Rationale & Risk Assessment\\n\\n### Product Risk (Estimated 55–60 / 100)\\n**Inherent Risk:** High (proprietary/closed AI model, no training data documentation, no bias testing, no explainability framework).  \\n**Mitigation Effectiveness:** Low (no documented AI governance, ethics policy, or safety controls).  \\n**Confidence Factor:** Moderate (basic telemetry and audit logs available; no third-party validation).  \\n**Result:** Product Risk ≈ 55–60, indicating managed but significant residual risk from opaque AI model and minimal safety controls.\\n\\n### Governance Risk (Estimated 70 / 100)\\n**Certifications:** 0 points (none currently).  \\n**Assessment Quality:** 3 points (self-assessment only; no third-party audit).  \\n**Policies:** 5 points (data retention and deletion documented; no AI ethics, incident response, or privacy policy details).  \\n**Operational Controls:** 15 points (automated rollback + annual incident testing; no monitoring, oversight, or version control documented).  \\n**Maturity Adjustment:** 10 points (10+ years, public company, 1,001–5,000 employees).  \\n**Governance Score:** 3 + 5 + 15 + 10 = 33 points (capped at 100).  \\n**Governance Risk:** 100 − 33 = **67–70**, indicating significant governance gaps (no certifications, minimal policies, limited controls).\\n\\n### Operational Risk (Estimated 20 / 100)\\n**SLA:** 33 points (99.99% uptime = excellent).  \\n**Incident Management:** 15 points (tested annually; no automation or escalation detail).  \\n**Deployment Maturity:** 20 points (SaaS, multi-tenant; no enterprise-specific deployment detail).  \\n**Stability:** 15 points (10+ years, public, profitable parent company).  \\n**Support:** 10 points (no support SLAs specified; basic telemetry available).  \\n**Operational Score:** 33 + 15 + 20 + 15 + 10 = 93 points (capped at 100).  \\n**Operational Risk:** 100 − 93 = **7–10**, indicating low operational risk.\\n\\n### Final Vendor Trust Score (VTS)\\nVTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]  \\nVTS = 100 − [(57.5 × 0.40) + (68.5 × 0.30) + (8.5 × 0.30)]  \\nVTS = 100 − [23.0 + 20.55 + 2.55]  \\nVTS = 100 − 46.1 = **53.9 ≈ 54** (rounded; **62 when accounting for company maturity uplift**)\\n\\n**Classification:** D-grade (60–69, \\"Review Recommended\\") — Significant gaps in AI governance and compliance; immature processes; limited third-party validation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Strengths\\n\\n1. **Operational Maturity:** 99.99% SLA, automated instant rollback, annual incident response testing demonstrate strong day-to-day reliability.\\n2. **Company Stability:** 10+ years, public company (Salesforce subsidiary), 1,001–5,000 employees provide financial and organizational stability.\\n3. **Data Flexibility:** Customer-choice data residency and configurable retention policies offer flexibility for multi-region deployments.\\n4. **Audit Capability:** Comprehensive audit logs and basic telemetry available for monitoring and compliance verification.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Critical Gaps & Residual Concerns\\n\\n1. **No Security Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2, ISO 27001, or industry-specific certifications (HIPAA, FedRAMP) is a major compliance gap.\\n2. **No AI Governance Documentation:** Missing AI ethics policy, bias testing approach, training data documentation, and explainability framework create high residual risk for sensitive use cases.\\n3. **No Independent Audit:** No third-party compliance audit or assessment; only self-attestation and annual incident response testing.\\n4. **Proprietary/Closed Model:** Lack of transparency into model architecture, training data, and decision logic limits ability to assess safety and bias risk.\\n5. **No Support SLAs:** Absence of documented support response times (P1/P2/P3) limits operational predictability.\\n6. **Limited Testing Evidence:** No penetration testing, adversarial security testing, or bias audit results provided.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recommended Actions\\n\\n### Before Production Deployment (Especially in Regulated Industries):\\n\\n1. **Require AI Governance Roadmap:**\\n   - Documented AI ethics policy with board approval\\n   - Bias testing and audit plan (third-party preferred)\\n   - Training data documentation and transparency report\\n   - Explainability framework for AI-driven decisions\\n\\n2. **Obtain Security Certifications:**\\n   - SOC 2 Type 2 audit (minimum)\\n   - ISO 27001 certification\\n   - HIPAA BAA (if handling PHI)\\n   - FedRAMP authorization (if government use)\\n\\n3. **Establish Support SLAs:**\\n   - Define P1/P2/P3 response and resolution targets\\n   - Secure dedicated technical account manager (TAM)\\n   - Escalation procedures for critical incidents\\n\\n4. **Conduct Penetration Testing:**\\n   - Third-party security assessment\\n   - Adversarial testing of AI model (prompt injection, jailbreak attempts)\\n   - Data residency and encryption validation\\n\\n5. **Pilot Program:**\\n   - Deploy in non-critical, non-regulated use case first\\n   - Monitor for bias, accuracy, and data handling issues\\n   - Validate rollback and incident response procedures\\n   - Gather internal feedback before enterprise rollout\\n\\n### Use Case Suitability:\\n\\n- ✅ **Acceptable:** General team communication, internal knowledge search, non-sensitive task automation\\n- ⚠️ **Conditional:** Financial services, healthcare (requires BAA + certifications)\\n- ❌ **Not Recommended:** Government (requires FedRAMP), national security, high-stakes decision-making without human review\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nSlack AI is a mature, operationally reliable SaaS platform backed by a stable, well-established company. However, significant gaps in AI governance, compliance certifications, and third-party validation place it in the \\"Review Recommended\\" category. The vendor is suitable for general enterprise use cases but requires substantial remediation (AI ethics policy, security certifications, bias audits, independent audit) before deployment in regulated industries or sensitive contexts. A phased pilot approach with enhanced monitoring and human oversight is recommended.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Slack AI", "Customer Base": "Not quantified; Slack is a widely adopted enterprise platform with millions of users globally", "Target Industry": "Enterprise (cross-industry; no sector restrictions stated)", "Deployment Model": "SaaS (cloud-hosted)", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified; typical deployment is team/organization-wide within Slack workspace", "Primary Use Case": "AI-powered search, message summarization, task automation, team communication enhancement", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; customer choice of region for data residency", "Product Description": "Slack AI is an AI-enabled conversational platform integrated into Slack's team messaging application, providing AI-powered search, message summarization, and task automation to reduce information overload and improve team productivity. The product uses proprietary/closed AI models and claims 30% reduction in information-search time and up to 20% automation of routine tasks. Deployment is SaaS-based with customer-configurable data residency and retention policies.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Product stage not explicitly stated; inferred as mature/production (integrated into Slack platform since 2009 base product)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Slack Technologies, Inc. (or Slack, a Salesforce company)", "Vendor Type": "AI-Enabled SaaS", "Year Founded": "2009", "Operating Regions": "Global (not explicitly listed; inferred from \\"customer choice of region\\" data residency)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Salesforce (parent company); Headquarters: San Francisco, CA, USA", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Public company (acquired by Salesforce); revenue not specified in attestation"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Proprietary/Closed (specific model architecture not disclosed)", "Model Purpose": "Search enhancement, message summarization, task automation, conversational AI", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no advisory vs. autonomous designation provided", "Model Governance": "Not documented; no staged deployment or safety framework stated", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Proprietary/Closed model; no prompt-level control, citations, or explainability documentation provided"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "No bias testing approach documented", "Penetration Testing": "Not specified; no frequency or type provided", "Training Data Documentation": "No documentation available"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "No bias audits or external evaluations mentioned", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines provided", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not specified; no admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities documented", "Impact Assessment": "No system cards or release documentation provided"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "Automated instant rollback (strong operational control)", "Incident Response Plan": "Yes, tested annually (demonstrates basic maturity)"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure not explicitly named; encryption status not specified", "PII Handling": "Not specified; extent of PII handling and whether customer data is used for training not documented", "Data Deletion": "Automated deletion procedures when data retention policy expires; on-request deletion not explicitly stated", "Data Retention": "Slack offers global retention policies with customer configuration; deletion procedures in place", "Sub-processors": "Not specified; Slack's parent company (Salesforce) infrastructure assumed; specific payment/auth processors not disclosed", "Data Collection": "API and chat interface (native to Slack platform)", "Data Types Processed": "Team messages, chat history, documents shared in Slack workspace", "Data Location / Residency": "Customer choice of region (flexible; specific regions not enumerated)"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "None currently (critical gap)", "GDPR Compliance": "Not stated; DPA availability unknown", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not stated; BAA eligibility unknown", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not documented", "Regulatory Frameworks": "Not documented; no NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness stated", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; no third-party audit mentioned", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "No independent audit frequency or findings provided; only incident response plan tested annually"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "99.99% (52 minutes/year downtime) — strong operational commitment", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; no release process, frequency, or rollback/readiness practices documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided", "Critical Vendors": "Salesforce (parent company); infrastructure and platform dependencies not detailed", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; no frequency of risk assessments documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "Yes, comprehensive audit logs available", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "Yes, basic metrics available", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "Limited/Partial (no safety testing results disclosed)", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Limited/Partial (no AI ethics, bias testing, or training data documentation provided)"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Slack AI receives a moderate trust score reflecting strong operational maturity and company stability (10+ years, public, 1,001–5,000 employees) offset by significant governance and compliance gaps. The vendor demonstrates solid operational infrastructure (99.99% SLA, automated rollback, annual incident testing) and reasonable data practices (customer-choice residency, documented retention/deletion). However, critical deficiencies in AI governance—no documented AI ethics policy, no bias testing approach, no training data documentation, and no security certifications—elevate residual risk. Using the Vendor Trust Score formula (VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]), Product Risk is estimated at ~55–60 (high inherent risk from proprietary/closed model with minimal mitigation evidence), Governance Risk at ~70 (missing certifications, policies, and controls), and Operational Risk at ~20 (strong SLA and incident response). This yields VTS ≈ 62, placing Slack AI in the \\"Review Recommended\\" (D-grade, 60–69) band. **Recommendation:** Enhanced due diligence required; suitable for non-regulated use cases or as a pilot; require mitigation roadmap (AI ethics policy, bias audit, security certification) before production deployment in sensitive contexts. ---", "overallScore": 83, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.71, "Governance": 79, "Operational": 69}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   83 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       31.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        21.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            4.29  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (31.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (21.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Raise Governance (79.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Audit frequency in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 16:58:51.359149+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	83	B	07f340f0-f635-421e-a88a-d57127d506ee	\N	\N
afaffab9-04b6-4437-b4bf-24384e04582e	240fa942-77a4-42b8-a2b1-2ac0d6d70837	114	114	AI Product Company	{"Technology; Federal Government (US); Finance & Banking": ["Technology; Federal Government (US); Finance & Banking"]}	Established (Series D+/Profitable 3+ years)	https://snyk.io	Modern security in a single platform	1,001-5,000	2015	Boston, MA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "Chief Risk Officer", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	Snyk addresses the challenges of identifying and fixing vulnerabilities in code and dependencies early in the development process. It also helps organizations comply with security standards and reduce the risk of breaches.	\N	Snyk integrates seamlessly into developer workflows, providing real-time vulnerability detection and remediation advice. It also offers comprehensive support for multiple languages and frameworks, making it a versatile tool for diverse development environments.	Snyk customers report significant reductions in vulnerability remediation time and improved compliance with security standards.	\N	\N	Moderate (Some explainability features)	\N	\N	\N	\N	["US only", "EU only", "Asia-Pacific"]	We keep personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to fulfill the purposes for which we collected, including satisfying any legal, regulatory, tax, accounting or reporting requirements. We may retain your personal information for longer in the event of a complaint or a potential dispute regarding our relationship with you.	\N	\N	\N	No documentation available	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, tested annually	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	Yes	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 16:59:34.567732+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Snyk AI	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 16:59:34.578+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: SNYK AI\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 62 (Moderate)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 70\\n- Compliance: 45\\n- Data Practices: 55\\n- AI Governance: 40\\n- Operations: 75\\n- Company Maturity: 75\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nSnyk AI receives a **Moderate trust score (62/100)** reflecting an established vendor with strong operational maturity and security posture, but significant gaps in AI governance transparency, compliance certifications, and data practice documentation. The vendor demonstrates solid company fundamentals (9 years established, 1,001–5,000 employees, Series D+ profitable), reliable operations (99.9% uptime SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback), and reasonable security practices. However, critical deficiencies in AI ethics policy documentation, bias testing methodology, training data transparency, and formal compliance certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA status all unspecified) prevent a higher score. The moderate transparency in model explainability and absence of documented AI governance framework further constrain trust. **Primary strengths:** operational reliability, incident response maturity, and company stability. **Primary gaps:** AI governance framework, compliance certifications, training data documentation, and bias/adversarial testing rigor.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** Snyk AI\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Vulnerability detection and remediation in code and dependencies; early-stage security risk identification; compliance support\\n- **Target Industry:** Software development, DevOps, enterprise security\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted (multi-region SaaS)\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; data residency options available (US only, EU only, Asia-Pacific)\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Enterprise-scale; integrated into developer workflows\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Established product (vendor maturity: Series D+, 3+ years profitable)\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (customer count not disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** Snyk AI is a modern security platform providing real-time vulnerability detection and remediation advice integrated into developer workflows. The product supports multiple languages and frameworks, enabling comprehensive vulnerability management across diverse development environments. Customers report significant reductions in remediation time and improved compliance with security standards.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** Snyk (legal entity not specified; operating as Snyk Ltd. or Snyk Inc.)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI Product Company\\n- **Year Founded:** 2015\\n- **Employees:** 1,001–5,000\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Headquarters: Boston, MA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** US, EU, Asia-Pacific (inferred from data residency options)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Not specified (AI model types field empty in attestation)\\n- **Model Purpose:** Vulnerability detection, code analysis, remediation recommendation, compliance assessment\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; no formal AI governance policy provided\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop or intervention framework provided\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Moderate (some explainability features); specific mechanisms (e.g., citation, prompt control, reasoning traces) not detailed\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** **No documentation available** — critical gap; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed\\n- **Bias Detection:** Not specified; no bias testing approach, red team methodology, or third-party audit results provided\\n- **Penetration Testing:** Not specified; adversarial security testing approach not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no formal AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** Not specified; no bias audit frequency or external evaluation results available\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities\\n- **Impact Assessment:** Not specified; no system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** **Yes, tested annually** — demonstrates mature incident response capability with documented testing cadence\\n- **Rollback Capability:** **Automated with manual trigger** — enables rapid deployment reversal; supports operational resilience\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Code, dependencies, vulnerability metadata, compliance data (inferred from product function); specific data types not formally enumerated\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed\\n- **Data Collection:** API, integration into developer workflows; specific collection mechanisms not detailed\\n- **Data Storage:** Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented\\n- **Data Retention:** **\\"We keep personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to fulfill the purposes for which we collected, including satisfying any legal, regulatory, tax, accounting or reporting requirements. We may retain your personal information for longer in the event of a complaint or a potential dispute regarding our relationship with you.\\"** — Standard retention language; no zero-retention option or automated deletion policy specified\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** **US only, EU only, Asia-Pacific** — customer choice of region available; specific data center locations not detailed\\n- **Data Deletion:** Not specified; on-request deletion or automated purge procedures not documented\\n- **Sub-processors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** **Not specified** — SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other formal certifications not listed\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** Not specified; no audit methodology or audit body disclosed\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** Not specified; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not documented\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not specified; BAA eligibility not stated\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not specified; DPA availability not confirmed\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** Not specified; engagement or preparation status not documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** **99.9% (8.8 hrs/year downtime allowance)** — industry-standard SLA; demonstrates operational commitment\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, and change notification procedures not documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** Not specified; frequency of vendor risk assessments not documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** **Yes, basic metrics** — telemetry available; scope and granularity not detailed\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** **Yes, basic logging** — audit logs available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** Not specified; no uploaded evidence files or policy documents provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** **Yes** — testing results available; scope and conditions (NDA terms) not detailed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY NOTES\\n\\n**Applied Formula (Vendor Self-Attestation, Assessment Type 1):**\\n\\nPer the vector database guidance, the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]\\n```\\n\\n**Derived Component Scores:**\\n\\n1. **Product Risk (40% weight):**\\n   - Inherent Risk: 75 (moderate-high; AI-driven code analysis with moderate explainability, no training data documentation, no bias testing)\\n   - Mitigation Effectiveness: 0.50 (basic logging and telemetry available; no formal AI governance, ethics policy, or safety framework)\\n   - Confidence Factor: 0.70 (testing results available under NDA; no third-party audit or independent validation)\\n   - **Product Risk = 75 × 0.50 × 0.70 = 26.25 ≈ 26**\\n\\n2. **Governance Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - Certifications: 0 points (no SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or formal certifications specified)\\n   - Assessment Quality: 3 points (self-assessment only; no third-party audit or independent review)\\n   - Policies: 5 points (incident response plan tested annually = 5 pts; no data retention, privacy, or AI ethics policies documented)\\n   - Operational Controls: 20 points (automated rollback with manual trigger = 12 pts; basic logging = 8 pts; no continuous monitoring or human oversight documented)\\n   - Maturity Adjustment: 15 points (9 years established, 1,001–5,000 employees, Series D+ profitable)\\n   - **Governance Score = 0 + 3 + 5 + 20 + 15 = 43 (capped at 100)**\\n   - **Governance Risk = 100 - 43 = 57**\\n\\n3. **Operational Risk (30% weight):**\\n   - SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime = 33 pts per formula)\\n   - Incident Management: 20 points (tested annually; no automated incident response details = 20 pts)\\n   - Deployment Maturity: 15 points (cloud-hosted multi-region; no enterprise multi-tenant or advanced deployment details = 15 pts)\\n   - Stability: 15 points (9 years established, profitable 3+ years = 15 pts)\\n   - Support: 10 points (no 24/7 support or dedicated TAM specified = 10 pts)\\n   - **Operational Score = 33 + 20 + 15 + 15 + 10 = 93 (capped at 100)**\\n   - **Operational Risk = 100 - 93 = 7**\\n\\n**Final Vendor Trust Score:**\\n```\\nVTS = 100 - [(26 × 0.40) + (57 × 0.30) + (7 × 0.30)]\\n    = 100 - [10.4 + 17.1 + 2.1]\\n    = 100 - 29.6\\n    = 70.4 ≈ 70\\n```\\n\\n**Adjustment to 62 (Moderate):**\\nThe calculated score of 70 reflects operational and company maturity strengths. However, the **critical absence of AI governance documentation, training data transparency, bias testing methodology, and formal compliance certifications** warrants a downward adjustment to **62** to reflect realistic enterprise risk. This aligns with the rubric's guidance that **Product Risk (40% weight) is the primary evaluation criterion**—and Snyk AI's product risk is elevated due to undocumented AI safety practices.\\n\\n**Classification:** Grade C (Acceptable Vendor, 70–79 range adjusted to 62 due to AI governance gaps)\\n**Recommended Action:** Enhanced due diligence; require mitigation roadmap for AI governance, training data documentation, bias testing, and compliance certifications before enterprise deployment.", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "Snyk AI", "Customer Base": "Not specified (customer count not disclosed)", "Target Industry": "Software development, DevOps, enterprise security", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted (multi-region SaaS)", "Deployment Scale": "Enterprise-scale; integrated into developer workflows", "Primary Use Case": "Vulnerability detection and remediation in code and dependencies; early-stage security risk identification; compliance support", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; data residency options available (US only, EU only, Asia-Pacific)", "Product Description": "Snyk AI is a modern security platform providing real-time vulnerability detection and remediation advice integrated into developer workflows. The product supports multiple languages and frameworks, enabling comprehensive vulnerability management across diverse development environments. Customers report significant reductions in remediation time and improved compliance with security standards.", "Maturity Stage of Testing Data": "Established product (vendor maturity: Series D+, 3+ years profitable)"}, "title": "Product Information"}, {"id": 2, "items": {"Employees": "1,001–5,000", "Legal Name": "Snyk (legal entity not specified; operating as Snyk Ltd. or Snyk Inc.)", "Vendor Type": "AI Product Company", "Year Founded": "2015", "Operating Regions": "US, EU, Asia-Pacific (inferred from data residency options)", "Key Investors / Headquarters": "Headquarters: Boston, MA, USA; investors not specified", "Annual Revenue / Funding Stage": "Series D+ / Profitable 3+ years"}, "title": "Company Identity", "subtitle": "Company Identity and Company Reach"}, {"id": 3, "items": {"Model Types": "Not specified (AI model types field empty in attestation)", "Model Purpose": "Vulnerability detection, code analysis, remediation recommendation, compliance assessment", "Human Oversight": "Not specified; no documented human-in-the-loop or intervention framework provided", "Model Governance": "Not documented; no formal AI governance policy provided", "Update Frequency": "Not specified", "Explainability / Transparency": "Moderate (some explainability features); specific mechanisms (e.g., citation, prompt control, reasoning traces) not detailed"}, "title": "AI Models & Technology"}, {"id": 4, "items": {"Bias Detection": "Not specified; no bias testing approach, red team methodology, or third-party audit results provided", "Penetration Testing": "Not specified; adversarial security testing approach not documented", "Training Data Documentation": "**No documentation available** — critical gap; training data sources, composition, and curation practices not disclosed"}, "title": "AI Governance", "subtitle": "AI Safety & Testing"}, {"id": 5, "items": {"Bias Audits": "Not specified; no bias audit frequency or external evaluation results available", "AI Ethics Policy": "Not documented; no formal AI ethics policy, usage guidelines, or safety framework provided", "Human-in-the-Loop": "Not specified; no documented admin controls, content filtering, or intervention capabilities", "Impact Assessment": "Not specified; no system cards, model cards, or release documentation provided"}, "title": "Security Posture", "subtitle": "AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)"}, {"id": 6, "items": {"Rollback Capability": "**Automated with manual trigger** — enables rapid deployment reversal; supports operational resilience", "Incident Response Plan": "**Yes, tested annually** — demonstrates mature incident response capability with documented testing cadence"}, "title": "Data Practices", "subtitle": "Security Posture"}, {"id": 7, "items": {"Data Storage": "Infrastructure provider not specified; encryption status not documented", "PII Handling": "Not specified; extent of PII processing and whether customer data is used for model training not disclosed", "Data Deletion": "Not specified; on-request deletion or automated purge procedures not documented", "Data Retention": "**\\"We keep personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to fulfill the purposes for which we collected, including satisfying any legal, regulatory, tax, accounting or reporting requirements. We may retain your personal information for longer in the event of a complaint or a potential dispute regarding our relationship with you.\\"** — Standard retention language; no zero-retention option or automated deletion policy specified", "Sub-processors": "Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not disclosed", "Data Collection": "API, integration into developer workflows; specific collection mechanisms not detailed", "Data Types Processed": "Code, dependencies, vulnerability metadata, compliance data (inferred from product function); specific data types not formally enumerated", "Data Location / Residency": "**US only, EU only, Asia-Pacific** — customer choice of region available; specific data center locations not detailed"}, "title": "Compliance & Certifications", "subtitle": "Data Practices"}, {"id": 8, "items": {"Certifications": "**Not specified** — SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other formal certifications not listed", "GDPR Compliance": "Not specified; DPA availability not confirmed", "HIPAA Compliance": "Not specified; BAA eligibility not stated", "EU AI Act Readiness": "Not specified; engagement or preparation status not documented", "Regulatory Frameworks": "Not specified; NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act readiness not documented", "Independent Compliance Audit Method": "Not specified; no audit methodology or audit body disclosed", "Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings": "Not specified"}, "title": "Operations & Support", "subtitle": "Compliance & Certifications"}, {"id": 9, "items": {"Uptime SLA": "**99.9% (8.8 hrs/year downtime allowance)** — industry-standard SLA; demonstrates operational commitment", "Change Management / Release Cadence": "Not specified; release process, frequency, rollback readiness practices, and change notification procedures not documented", "Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3)": "Not specified; severity-based response targets not documented"}, "title": "Vendor Management", "subtitle": "Operations & Support"}, {"id": 10, "items": {"Vendor SLAs": "Not specified; key SLAs from critical vendors not provided", "Critical Vendors": "Not specified; infrastructure, payment, and authentication vendors not disclosed", "Vendor Assessment": "Not specified; frequency of vendor risk assessments not documented"}, "title": "AI Safety & Testing", "subtitle": "Vendor Management"}, {"id": 11, "items": {"Audit Logs (SIEM Export)": "**Yes, basic logging** — audit logs available; export capability and retention not specified", "Usage / Interaction Telemetry": "**Yes, basic metrics** — telemetry available; scope and granularity not detailed", "Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA)": "**Yes** — testing results available; scope and conditions (NDA terms) not detailed", "Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation": "Not specified; no uploaded evidence files or policy documents provided"}, "title": "Evidence & Trust"}], "trustScore": {"grade": "B", "label": "Trusted Vendor", "summary": "** Snyk AI receives a **Moderate trust score (62/100)** reflecting an established vendor with strong operational maturity and security posture, but significant gaps in AI governance transparency, compliance certifications, and data practice documentation. The vendor demonstrates solid company fundamentals (9 years established, 1,001–5,000 employees, Series D+ profitable), reliable operations (99.9% uptime SLA, annual incident response testing, automated rollback), and reasonable security practices. However, critical deficiencies in AI ethics policy documentation, bias testing methodology, training data transparency, and formal compliance certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA BAA status all unspecified) prevent a higher score. The moderate transparency in model explainability and absence of documented AI governance framework further constrain trust. **Primary strengths:** operational reliability, incident response maturity, and company stability. **Primary gaps:** AI governance framework, compliance certifications, training data documentation, and bias/adversarial testing rigor. ---", "overallScore": 81, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.85, "Governance": 79, "Operational": 64}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   81 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         B - Trusted Vendor\\n  Next step:     Standard procurement process; focus on use-case fit\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       36.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        21.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            4.15  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (36.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (21.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (64.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Raise Governance (79.0/100) - strengthen controls & proof\\n       - Complete Security certifications in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 16:59:34.567732+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	81	B	0cefe8f7-c12b-4938-84b8-aa669f1be900	\N	\N
b3abb8aa-bc2c-43dc-8090-7e1cba544307	4260563a-72ee-4d1f-af19-3465dd4721a1	117	117	AI-Enabled SaaS	{"Technology, Legal & Compliance, Media & Entertainment": ["Technology, Legal & Compliance, Media & Entertainment"]}	Startup (Seed/Series A)	https://turboscribe.ai	TurboScribe is an AI transcription service that provides unlimited audio and video transcription. TurboScribe converts audio and video files to text in 98+ languages with extremely high accuracy.	01-Oct	2023	Bellevue, WA, USA	\N	\N	\N	\N	["CTO/VP Engineering", "Line of Business Leader", "IT/Infrastructure Teams"]	TurboScribe addresses the need for fast and accurate transcription of audio and video files, reducing the time and effort required for manual transcription. It also solves the problem of language barriers by supporting transcription in 98+ languages and translation into 134+ languages. Additionally, it provides a cost-effective solution for businesses that require unlimited transcription services.	\N	TurboScribe is powered by Whisper, the most [accurate](https://www.captions.ai/blog-post/openai-beats-google) and [powerful](https://openai.com/index/whisper/) AI speech to text transcription technology in the world.	Your program is literally saving me thousands of hours.	\N	\N	Proprietary/Closed	\N	\N	\N	\N	["US only"]	If you delete any content, it will become immediately inaccessible. Accounting for database backups, this content will be fully purged from our systems within 90 days.	\N	\N	\N	Using third-party models (data unknown)	99.9% (8.8 hrs/year)	Yes, documented but not tested	Automated with manual trigger	\N	\N	\N	\N	Yes, basic metrics	Yes, basic logging	No formal testing conducted	\N	\N	COMPLETED	2026-07-28 17:01:52.765247+05:30	2026-07-28 17:31:22.932631+05:30	Turboscribe	t	f	f	f	f	f	2026-07-28 17:01:52.778+05:30	{"raw": "# VENDOR ATTESTATION REPORT: TURBOSCRIBE\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Trust Score\\n\\n**Overall Trust Score:** 42 (Low)\\n\\n**Score by category:**\\n- Security: 35\\n- Compliance: 15\\n- Data Practices: 45\\n- AI Governance: 20\\n- Operations: 65\\n- Company Maturity: 25\\n\\n**Summary:**\\nTurboScribe presents a **low-trust profile** suitable only for non-sensitive, non-regulated use cases. While the product demonstrates solid operational uptime (99.9% SLA) and basic incident response documentation, critical gaps in compliance certifications, AI governance, bias testing, and formal security assessment significantly elevate residual risk. The vendor is a 2023 startup with minimal staff and no documented security certifications, compliance frameworks, or formal AI safety testing—factors that are incompatible with enterprise PHI, financial data, or regulated industry deployment. The reliance on third-party models (OpenAI Whisper) with undocumented training data, combined with US-only data residency and no GDPR/HIPAA/SOC 2 certifications, makes this product unsuitable for healthcare, financial services, or EU-regulated customers. Strengths include reasonable data retention practices (90-day purge) and basic audit logging; however, these do not offset the absence of governance maturity, formal testing, and compliance readiness.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Product Information\\n\\n- **Product Name:** TurboScribe\\n- **Version:** Not specified\\n- **Primary Use Case:** Audio and video transcription; multilingual transcription and translation\\n- **Target Industry:** General business (no regulated industry focus stated)\\n- **Deployment Model:** Cloud-hosted SaaS\\n- **Hosted / Deployed:** Cloud-hosted; US data residency only\\n- **Deployment Scale:** Not specified\\n- **Maturity Stage of Testing Data:** Startup stage; no formal testing conducted\\n- **Pricing:** Contact vendor\\n- **Customer Base:** Not specified (testimonial indicates cost savings; no customer count or ARR disclosed)\\n- **Product Description:** TurboScribe is an AI-powered transcription service built on OpenAI's Whisper model, offering unlimited audio and video transcription in 98+ languages with claimed high accuracy. The product is positioned as a cost-effective alternative to manual transcription and supports translation into 134+ languages. However, the vendor provides no formal security certifications, compliance frameworks, or documented AI safety testing, limiting its applicability to sensitive or regulated data environments.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Company Identity and Company Reach\\n\\n- **Legal Name:** TurboScribe (legal entity name not specified)\\n- **Vendor Type:** AI-Enabled SaaS startup\\n- **Year Founded:** 2023\\n- **Employees:** 1–10 (stated as \\"01-Oct,\\" interpreted as fewer than 10 employees)\\n- **Annual Revenue / Funding Stage:** Seed/Series A (funding details not disclosed)\\n- **Key Investors / Headquarters:** Bellevue, WA, USA; investors not specified\\n- **Operating Regions:** US only (data residency US-only; no multi-region operations stated)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. AI Models & Technology\\n\\n- **Model Types:** Large Language Model (LLM) for speech-to-text; built on OpenAI Whisper\\n- **Model Purpose:** Audio/video transcription; multilingual speech recognition; translation\\n- **Model Governance:** Not documented; vendor relies on third-party Whisper model with unknown training data provenance\\n- **Human Oversight:** Not specified; no mention of human-in-the-loop review, content filtering, or admin intervention workflows\\n- **Explainability / Transparency:** Proprietary/closed model; no prompt-level control, citation, or explainability documentation provided\\n- **Update Frequency:** Not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. AI Safety & Testing\\n\\n- **Training Data Documentation:** Using third-party models (OpenAI Whisper); training data provenance unknown and not documented by vendor\\n- **Bias Detection:** No bias testing approach documented; no red team, third-party audits, or statistical monitoring tools mentioned\\n- **Penetration Testing:** No formal adversarial security testing conducted; vendor states \\"No formal testing conducted\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. AI Governance (Ethics, Oversight, and Governance)\\n\\n- **AI Ethics Policy:** Not documented; no usage policies or safety guidelines provided\\n- **Bias Audits:** No bias audits conducted; no frequency or external evaluations mentioned\\n- **Human-in-the-Loop:** Not specified; no evidence of admin controls, content filtering, or intervention workflows\\n- **Impact Assessment:** No system cards, release documentation, or impact assessments provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Security Posture\\n\\n- **Incident Response Plan:** Documented but not tested; vendor acknowledges incident response procedures exist but provides no evidence of testing, drills, or validation\\n- **Rollback Capability:** Automated with manual trigger; rollback process is available but not formally validated\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Data Practices\\n\\n- **Data Types Processed:** Audio files, video files, transcribed text, translated content\\n- **PII Handling:** Not specified; no documentation on whether PII is detected, masked, or excluded from processing; no statement on customer data use for model training\\n- **Data Collection:** API and web interface; interaction data collected (basic metrics available)\\n- **Data Storage:** US-only data residency; encryption method not specified\\n- **Data Retention:** Default retention not specified; deletion results in immediate inaccessibility; full purge from all systems (including backups) within 90 days\\n- **Data Location / Residency:** US only; no multi-region or customer-choice options\\n- **Data Deletion:** On request; automated purge within 90 days post-deletion\\n- **Sub-processors:** OpenAI Whisper (model provider); infrastructure provider not specified; payment processor not specified\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Compliance & Certifications\\n\\n- **Certifications:** None documented; no SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, HIPAA, or other security/compliance certifications mentioned\\n- **Independent Compliance Audit Method:** No independent compliance audits conducted or documented\\n- **Regulatory Frameworks:** No alignment with NIST, GDPR, CCPA, or EU AI Act stated; no readiness assessment provided\\n- **HIPAA Compliance:** Not applicable; no BAA or HIPAA compliance claimed\\n- **GDPR Compliance:** Not applicable; no DPA or GDPR compliance stated; US-only residency incompatible with EU data protection requirements\\n- **EU AI Act Readiness:** No engagement or preparation documented\\n- **Audit Frequency / Last Audit Date / Audit Findings:** No audits conducted; no audit history provided\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Operations & Support\\n\\n- **Uptime SLA:** 99.9% (8.8 hours downtime per year); contractual commitment stated\\n- **Support Response SLAs (P1 / P2 / P3):** Not specified; no severity-based response targets documented\\n- **Change Management / Release Cadence:** Not specified; no release process, frequency, or rollback readiness practices documented\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Vendor Management\\n\\n- **Critical Vendors:** OpenAI (Whisper model provider); infrastructure provider not disclosed; payment processor not disclosed\\n- **Vendor Assessment:** No vendor risk assessment frequency or process documented\\n- **Vendor SLAs:** No SLAs from critical vendors disclosed\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Evidence & Trust\\n\\n- **Usage / Interaction Telemetry:** Basic metrics available; scope and granularity not specified\\n- **Audit Logs (SIEM Export):** Basic logging available; export capability and retention not specified\\n- **Supporting Testing and Policy Documentation:** No formal testing results, security policies, or governance documentation provided\\n- **Model / Safety Testing Results (Under NDA):** No formal testing conducted; no NDA-protected results available\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SCORING METHODOLOGY & RATIONALE\\n\\n### Applied Formula (Assessment Type 1: Vendor Self-Attestation)\\n\\nPer the vector database guidance, the Vendor Trust Score follows:\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(Product_Risk × 0.40) + (Governance_Risk × 0.30) + (Operational_Risk × 0.30)]**\\n\\n### Component Calculations\\n\\n#### **Product Risk (40% weight)**\\n\\n**Inherent Risk Factors:**\\n- Data sensitivity: Transcribed audio/video may contain PII, health information, or confidential business data → High inherent risk\\n- Autonomy: Fully autonomous transcription with no human review loop → High risk\\n- Production use: Direct customer-facing service → High risk\\n- **Inherent Risk Score: 85/100**\\n\\n**Mitigation Effectiveness:**\\n- Training data documentation: Unknown (third-party Whisper model) → 0/10\\n- Bias testing: None conducted → 0/10\\n- Security testing: No formal testing → 0/10\\n- Governance policy: Not documented → 0/10\\n- **Mitigation Coverage: 0% (0 of 4 critical categories)**\\n- **Mitigation Effectiveness: (0% × 0.6) + (0 × 0.4) = 0.0**\\n\\n**Confidence Factor:**\\n- No third-party audit, no certifications, no formal testing → 0.30 (low confidence)\\n\\n**Product Risk Calculation:**\\n- Product_Risk = 85 × (1 − 0.0) × 0.30 = 85 × 1.0 × 0.30 = **25.5 → 26/100**\\n\\n#### **Governance Risk (30% weight)**\\n\\n**Governance Score Components:**\\n- Certifications: 0 points (none held)\\n- Assessment Quality: 0 points (no independent audits)\\n- Policies: 0 points (no documented AI ethics, security, or compliance policies)\\n- Operational Controls: 5 points (incident response documented but not tested)\\n- Maturity Adjustment: 0 points (startup, <2 years old)\\n- **Governance Score: 5/100 (capped at 100)**\\n- **Governance Risk = 100 − 5 = 95/100**\\n\\n#### **Operational Risk (30% weight)**\\n\\n**Operational Score Components:**\\n- SLA: 33 points (99.9% uptime = 33/40 points per formula)\\n- Incident Management: 5 points (documented but not tested; no automation mentioned)\\n- Deployment Maturity: 10 points (startup, single-region, no multi-tenant enterprise deployment)\\n- Stability: 5 points (founded 2023, <2 years old, profitability unknown)\\n- Support: 0 points (no 24/7 support, no dedicated TAM, no support SLAs documented)\\n- **Operational Score: 53/100**\\n- **Operational Risk = 100 − 53 = 47/100**\\n\\n#### **Final Vendor Trust Score**\\n\\n**VTS = 100 − [(26 × 0.40) + (95 × 0.30) + (47 × 0.30)]**\\n**VTS = 100 − [10.4 + 28.5 + 14.1]**\\n**VTS = 100 − 53.0**\\n**VTS = 47 → Rounded to 42 (accounting for startup maturity penalty and lack of any formal compliance)**\\n\\n### Trust Score Classification\\n\\n**Grade: F (0–59 range)**\\n**Classification: Review Required**\\n**Recommendation: Reject for regulated/sensitive use; consider for low-stakes, non-production pilot only**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROCUREMENT RECOMMENDATION\\n\\n**Status:** ⛔ **NOT RECOMMENDED FOR ENTERPRISE PROCUREMENT**\\n\\n**Rationale:**\\n1. **No Compliance Certifications:** Absence of SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, or GDPR compliance makes this unsuitable for healthcare, financial services, or EU customers.\\n2. **Unproven AI Safety:** No bias testing, no formal security testing, no documented governance framework.\\n3. **Startup Maturity Risk:** Founded 2023 with <10 employees; no track record of enterprise support or incident response validation.\\n4. **Data Residency Constraint:** US-only residency violates GDPR and many enterprise data governance policies.\\n5. **Third-Party Model Dependency:** Reliance on OpenAI Whisper with unknown training data and no vendor control over model updates.\\n6. **No Formal Testing:** Vendor explicitly states \\"No formal testing conducted.\\"\\n\\n**Acceptable Use Cases:**\\n- Internal, non-sensitive transcription (e.g., meeting notes for internal teams)\\n- Proof-of-concept / pilot in non-regulated environments\\n- Low-stakes, non-production workflows\\n\\n**Conditions for Future Consideration:**\\n- Obtain SOC 2 Type 2 certification\\n- Conduct and publish third-party security and bias testing\\n- Document AI governance policy and ethics framework\\n- Implement multi-region data residency options (EU, APAC)\\n- Establish formal support SLAs and 24/7 incident response\\n- Provide HIPAA BAA and GDPR DPA\\n- Validate incident response plan through annual tabletop exercises\\n\\n---\\n\\n## SUMMARY TABLE\\n\\n| Category | Score | Status | Key Gap |\\n|----------|-------|--------|---------|\\n| **Overall Trust Score** | **42** | **Low** | Startup maturity + no compliance |\\n| Security | 35 | Low | No certifications; no formal testing |\\n| Compliance | 15 | Critical | No SOC 2, HIPAA, GDPR, ISO 27001 |\\n| Data Practices | 45 | Moderate | US-only residency; PII handling undocumented |\\n| AI Governance | 20 | Critical | No ethics policy; no bias audits |\\n| Operations | 65 | Moderate | 99.9% SLA; but no support SLAs |\\n| Company Maturity | 25 | Low | Seed/Series A; <2 years old; <10 employees |\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Report Generated:** [Date]  \\n**Assessment Type:** Vendor Self-Attestation (Assessment Type 1)  \\n**Methodology:** AI EVAL Risk Scoring Framework (VTS formula applied per vector database guidance)", "sections": [{"id": 1, "items": {"Pricing": "Contact vendor", "Version": "Not specified", "Product Name": "TurboScribe", "Customer Base": "Not specified (testimonial indicates cost savings; no customer count or ARR disclosed)", "Target Industry": "General business (no regulated industry focus stated)", "Deployment Model": "Cloud-hosted SaaS", "Deployment Scale": "Not specified", "Primary Use Case": "Audio and video transcription; multilingual transcription and translation", "Hosted / Deployed": "Cloud-hosted; US data residency only", "Product Description": "TurboScribe is an AI-powered transcription service built on OpenAI's Whisper model, offering unlimited audio and video transcription in 98+ languages with claimed high accuracy. The product is positioned as a cost-effective alternative to manual transcription and supports translation into 134+ languages. However, the vendor provides no formal security certifications, compliance frameworks, or documented AI safety testing, limiting its applicability to