trates solid operational uptime (99.9% SLA) and basic incident response documentation, critical gaps in compliance certifications, AI governance, bias testing, and formal security assessment significantly elevate residual risk. The vendor is a 2023 startup with minimal staff and no documented security certifications, compliance frameworks, or formal AI safety testing—factors that are incompatible with enterprise PHI, financial data, or regulated industry deployment. The reliance on third-party models (OpenAI Whisper) with undocumented training data, combined with US-only data residency and no GDPR/HIPAA/SOC 2 certifications, makes this product unsuitable for healthcare, financial services, or EU-regulated customers. Strengths include reasonable data retention practices (90-day purge) and basic audit logging; however, these do not offset the absence of governance maturity, formal testing, and compliance readiness. ---", "overallScore": 76, "scoreByCategory": {"Product": 95.64, "Governance": 69, "Operational": 58}}, "scoreRationale": "VENDOR TRUST SCORE (Type 1) - EXPLAINED\\n========================================================================\\n\\nRESULT\\n  Trust score:   76 / 100   (higher = more trustworthy)\\n  Grade:         C - Acceptable Vendor\\n  Next step:     Enhanced due diligence; require mitigation roadmap\\n  Source:        formula+llm-narrative\\n\\nHOW WE GOT HERE\\n  Method:   Deterministic trust formula from vendor self-attestation answers\\n  Idea:     Trust = 100 minus weighted Product, Governance, and Operational risk\\n  Weights:  Product risk 40%  |  Governance risk 30%  |  Operational risk 30%\\n\\n  Risk drivers (higher risk lowers trust):\\n    1. Operational risk       42.00  (weight 30%)  << biggest drag\\n    2. Governance risk        31.00  (weight 30%)\\n    3. Product risk            4.36  (weight 40%)\\n\\nWHAT TO IMPROVE (to raise trust score)\\n  1. Biggest drag: Operational risk (42.0) - SLA, incident management, deployment maturity, support\\n  2. Governance risk (31.0) - certs, policies, assessment quality, maturity\\n  3. From attestation evidence, prioritize:\\n       - Raise Operational (58.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Raise Governance (69.0/100) - document policies, certs, testing, or SLAs\\n       - Complete Security certifications in the attestation\\n       - Complete PII handling in the attestation\\n       - Complete Human oversight in the attestation\\n       - Complete AI governance policy in the attestation\\n       - Complete Bias testing in the attestation\\n       - Complete Security / adversarial testing in the attestation"}	f	f	f	f	2026-10-28 17:01:52.765247+05:30	{}	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	76	C	1d6dc2b4-acd8-44e2-97d7-d8e0368dd3ed	\N	\N
